window.AKK_THE_BEAUTIFUL_STEPMOTHER_FROM_THE_EIGHTIES_MARRYING_A_FACTORY_DIRECTOR_TO_RAISE_KIDS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_THE_BEAUTIFUL_STEPMOTHER_FROM_THE_EIGHTIES_MARRYING_A_FACTORY_DIRECTOR_TO_RAISE_KIDS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":401,"title":"Chapter 401: The Thief","paragraphs":["But now it was night...","A mansion by day, a haunted house by night.","The courtyard was quite large, even bigger than their previous one.","There were also many rooms, but Si Nian didn't have much of a mind to slowly appreciate them right now.","Having not showered for two days, she was covered in the smell of the train, sticky and greasy. Jing City was already hot, and she felt uncomfortable all over.","The beds in the rooms were all new, but completely bare.","Si Nian somewhat regretted not listening to her mother and bringing their quilts.","Where was she supposed to buy bedding in the middle of the night?","The children were also very sleepy; Second Child couldn't even stand steady.","His eyelids were drooping.","Fortunately, she had prepared a new four-piece bedding set when she boarded the train. It was originally meant to be used on the train, but it finally came in handy now.","They would just have to make do with it as a mat for the night.","Zhou Yueshen took Yaoyao from her arms, placed her on the bed, held Si Nian's hand, and said, \"It's been hard on you.\"","Si Nian waved her hand to show it was nothing. After all, they had come in a hurry, and having a place to rest their feet was already good enough.","Eldest Child and Second Child fell asleep as soon as they lay down.","Si Nian managed to hold on and took a quick cold shower.","Good thing it was hot here, otherwise she really wouldn't have been able to stand it.","Sleeping on the hard bedboards at night left Si Nian waking up the next day with a sore back and aching waist.","She really had been living too comfortably lately.","She wasn't used to sleeping on hard beds anymore.","Zhou Yueshen had disappeared to who-knows-where early in the morning. When she got up, the weather outside was exceptionally good, cloudless for miles.","There were two crabapple trees in the courtyard, and nothing else.","The ground was paved with stone, so she couldn't dig it up to plant flowers like she did back home.","But the advantage of this was that it was easy to clean.","Si Nian sized up the layout of the courtyard and thought it was quite nice.","With her hands on her hips, she had already figured out how to lay out her garden.","The children walked out with messy, frizzy hair. Yaoyao's little braids had come undone and were skewed to one side.","Looking at the groggy appearance of the three little ones, Si Nian couldn't help but want to laugh.","\"Did you three siblings just flee from a famine?\"","Yaoyao tilted her head, \"Mommy, what is fleeing from a famine?\"","\"Haha, Mommy is just joking with you.\" Si Nian pinched her little cheek.","Second Child was already familiarly picking out his own room.","This time he declared he wanted to be further away from his brother so he wouldn't be seen when secretly working hard.","\"Mommy, Mommy, are we going to live here from now on?\" he asked Si Nian after making his choice.","Si Nian nodded, \"Barring any accidents, yes.\"","She just didn't know if this place was far from the university.","But since Zhou Yueshen had someone buy a place here, he must have thought about it.","Even though she had just gotten up, Si Nian was already hungry. She pulled the little darlings along, ready to go out and buy food.","By the time Zhou Yueshen returned, the house was empty.","He was carrying packed food in his hands.","Turning a corner outside, he saw Si Nian leading the little munchkins, picking out corn at a small vendor's stall. The children probably hadn't even washed their faces yet; their hair was a mess.","After buying the corn, they turned around, one adult and three kids simultaneously gnawing on ears of corn.","Zhou Yueshen watched them, feeling both a pang of sympathy and amusement.","\"Daddy, Mommy look, it's Daddy.\"","\"Daddy is back.\"","Seeing Zhou Yueshen approach, Second Child said loudly.","\"Daddy, look, this corn is so sweet and sticky!\"","He ran over to Zhou Yueshen and held up the corn for him to see.","Zhou Yueshen smiled and rubbed his head, then looked at Si Nian, \"I bought some food, let's head back first.\"","Gnawing on her corn, Si Nian asked, \"Where did you go so early in the morning?\"","The kitchen had absolutely nothing; even the cleverest housewife cannot cook without rice.","She was also helpless. Fortunately, she saw someone selling corn as soon as she walked out.","Zhou Yueshen said, \"I went to buy some furniture.\"","Before he finished speaking, Si Nian already saw several workers moving things into the house.","Sofas, tables, a TV, bedding, and more, they had everything.","Si Nian, \"You... did a great job.\"","Zhou Yueshen was amused by her tone.","After eating breakfast, Si Nian changed clothes and put on an apron, preparing for a thorough deep clean.","The children imitated her by wrapping gauze scarves around their heads and faces. Because the house was too big, there was no telling how long it would take for one person to clean it.","Cleaning together made it go much faster.","Zhou Yueshen moved furniture, while Si Nian and the children wiped tables, mopped the floor, and washed down the large courtyard.","Yaoyao hugged a dustpan to go empty the trash, spilling it as she walked. By the time she reached the trash can, there wasn't much dust left in the dustpan.","In short, with the whole family working together, they finally got a brand-new-looking house.","Zhou Yueshen also changed to new locks.","But this courtyard house had a drawback, the walls were not high at all. Anyone slightly tall could climb up.","Moreover, the tree in the corner of the wall provided a perfect foothold.","So much so that right after Zhou Yueshen brought Da Huang home and tied him under the tree to adapt to the new environment, a foot extended from outside the courtyard and stepped onto the tree.","Da Huang opened his eyes, stood up, and looked upward.","Just then, the thief looked down.","They stared at each other for a moment.","\"Ah!\" The thief's foot slipped, and he tumbled down from the tree.","He fell right in front of Da Huang.","Da Huang was already a bit carsick and was currently panting heavily.","His large mouth full of sharp teeth was wide open, with drool dripping from them.","When the man opened his eyes, he came face-to-face with the dog's mouth.","Another piercing scream rang out.","By the time Zhou Yueshen, Si Nian, and the children rushed out, the man had already fainted from fright.","It was unclear if he hit his head when he fell, but there was blood on his face. Da Huang was pawing at his limp body.","Then he turned around and looked innocently at Si Nian.","Mommy, Mommy, he really didn't do anything.","Si Nian, \"...\"","...","The thief was sent to the police station by Zhou Yueshen for education.","Si Nian stroked Da Huang's head with lingering fear, \"Da Huang, bringing you along was indeed the best choice.\"","With thieves showing up in broad daylight, what would happen at night?","This courtyard house really wasn't easy to live in.","Da Huang lay on the ground; after riding in the vehicle for two days, he had lost a pound.","He indicated that he needed to eat meat to recover.","Si Nian immediately went to buy bones to make food for him.","Someone from next door heard the commotion and came over to ask what happened."]},{"number":402,"title":"Chapter 402: School Enrollment Report","paragraphs":["\"Little sister-in-law, what's wrong? What happened?\"","Si Nian, who was just about to open the door: \"...\"","Little sister-in-law? What kind of address was that?","She looked up at the door, only to see a woman who was actually a bit older than herself.","Calling her little sister-in-law, was it a unique local way of addressing someone?","Si Nian greeted her awkwardly, \"Someone just climbed over the wall and fell down. My husband took him to the hospital.\"","Hearing this, the woman slapped her thigh exaggeratedly. \"Oh my, was it that brat Wang Ergou climbing walls again? Are you alright?\"","Si Nian asked blankly, \"Sister, do you know him?\"","The woman replied, \"Of course. Wang Ergou used to be a petty thief around here all year round. Previously, he accidentally killed someone while stealing and was caught and locked up for ten years before being released. I didn't know where he ran off to, but I didn't expect that a leopard can't change its spots, and he's back to stealing again.\"","After saying that, the woman whispered, \"Little sister-in-law, you need to be careful. That guy is greedy and lecherous. He used to harass pretty young girls a lot in the past.\"","She assumed that Si Nian was targeted because she was too pretty.","Si Nian's heart skipped a beat as she asked, \"He killed someone?\"","\"Yes. We've been locking our doors tight at night these past few days, afraid he might come in the middle of the night. But nothing happened, so we thought he had turned over a new leaf.\"","\"I just heard a scream, which is why I ran over. You guys just moved in, right? I've seen this house empty for a long time.\"","Si Nian nodded.","\"Thank you for the warning, sister. You can just call me Si Nian.\"","\"Oh, my name is Song Zhaodi, you can just call me Sister Zhaodi. I heard earlier that someone was moving in, but I didn't expect it to be so soon. I can tell your family is from out of town, you have a heavy accent. If there's anything you don't understand, just ask me.\"","Si Nian nodded and thanked her.","After returning to the house, her expression became a bit more serious.","The security of this house was simply too poor.","It looked nice, but it wasn't practical.","If Da Huang hadn't come today and happened to bump into him, they probably wouldn't have even known someone broke into the house.","It would have been dangerous if the children had bumped into him.","The more Si Nian thought about it, the more terrifying it seemed.","Suddenly, she didn't yearn for this kind of big courtyard house anymore.","Second Child still didn't realize the severity of the situation. He waved his fist and said, \"Mom, if a thief comes again next time, I'll send him flying with one punch.\"","Si Nian said seriously, \"Xiao Dong, Xiao Han, we are not familiar with this area yet, so you cannot run around outside, understand?\"","The two children exchanged a glance and nodded.","Si Nian rarely spoke to them with such a serious expression. If she did, it must be something very serious.","The thief really did scare their mom, right?","In the evening, the sun set in the west, and the sky gradually darkened.","Si Nian turned on the lights. Because of what happened during the day, she had lost many of her beautiful fantasies about this house.","Zhou Yueshen actually hadn't returned yet. It seemed the thief was probably injured quite badly.","The children were all tired and went back to their rooms to sleep, while Si Nian waited for Zhou Yueshen to come home.","It was almost seven o'clock when Zhou Yueshen finally walked in carrying some things.","Si Nian was dozing off with her head propped on the table. The TV still had no signal and couldn't be watched, which was boring to death. Of course, she wouldn't admit that she was waiting for Zhou Yueshen to come back because she was too scared to go to sleep alone.","\"You're back. How did it go?\"","The children had gone to sleep after dinner, and Da Huang, who was highly adaptable, was also sleeping soundly under the tree.","Only Si Nian was left in the room.","There were still dishes on the table, but they had gotten a bit cold.","Si Nian said, \"I'll go to the kitchen to heat up the food for you, wait a moment.\"","Zhou Yueshen responded, put down the things in his hands, and went into the kitchen to help her carry the dishes.","\"Are you sleepy? Do you want to go to sleep first?\" Zhou Yueshen asked.","Si Nian shook her head, yawning as she watched him eat, and asked about the thief's situation.","Sure enough, Zhou Yueshen's expression became a bit more serious.","\"His injuries were somewhat severe, and he didn't wake up until the afternoon. I contacted the people at the police station and found out that this guy is a repeat offender. He just got out not long ago and has a criminal record.\"","Si Nian initially thought that perhaps what the next-door neighbor Song Zhaodi heard was just a rumor and it wasn't actually that exaggerated.","She didn't expect it to actually be true, and her expression also became a bit more serious: \"Has he killed someone?\"","Zhou Yueshen was slightly taken aback, then nodded, \"Yes, he accidentally killed a woman ten years ago and was just released from prison not long ago. However, since he was discovered before he could steal anything this time, he will probably just get a verbal warning.\"","After saying that, he realized that Si Nian might be scared.","He paused and looked at her. \"Nian Nian.\"","Si Nian subconsciously responded, \"Hmm?\"","Zhou Yueshen put down his chopsticks and said in a gentle voice, \"Don't be afraid, I'm here.\"","Si Nian was slightly stunned. When she reacted, she said awkwardly, \"I'm not afraid. I'm just worried about the kids.\"","Zhou Yueshen reached out, patted her head, and said, \"Don't worry, I'll keep an eye out.\"","Si Nian hummed in agreement.","After he finished eating, the two of them cleared the table, washed up, and returned to the bedroom to rest.","After getting into bed, even though there was a mattress pad, Si Nian still wasn't used to sleeping on this kind of bed. She became fully awake and said, \"Zhou Yueshen, let's change the bed. I'm not used to this kind of bed, it feels weirdly depressing.\"","Zhou Yueshen was slightly taken aback, then nodded.","This kind of wooden bed was still very expensive around here. They were handmade, and people usually only bought them to match the color of the house.","Moreover, it was extremely heavy.","Many older people liked it. Zhou Yueshen didn't really care about where he slept, but Si Nian cared a lot about these details.","So he said, \"Okay, after I take you to school to register tomorrow, we'll go buy one.\"","Si Nian added, \"I thought about it, and the layout of the courtyard is quite depressing too. Also, that wall is too low; any adult could easily climb over it. The tree by the wall can't stay either.\"","Zhou Yueshen listened quietly to her. Even though they might only live here for two or three years, Si Nian had high standards for her living environment, and he couldn't force her to settle.","She would always keep in mind these little things that Zhou Yueshen would never think of.","Zhou Yueshen actually admired Si Nian quite a bit.","Because the details she cared about were what made this house feel more like a home.","\"Oh right, right, right, there's also the bathroom. If the wet and dry areas aren't separated, it will be easy for bacteria to breed in the future, and the smell will be heavy. It's best to separate them.\"","Speaking of this, Si Nian felt a bit helpless.","It wasn't that she was too picky, but every time someone took a shower, the place would get soaking wet, and over time, that wouldn't be good for their health.","Zhou Yueshen raised an eyebrow. Back at their old home, the toilet and the shower room were separated. Si Nian paid great attention to hygiene, and being a neat freak, she couldn't stand it otherwise.","Not to mention she also liked taking baths.","Zhou Yueshen couldn't help but chuckle softly, \"I'll find some workers to fix it up. We'll build another washroom then, so it'll be convenient for washing clothes and bathing.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian was pleasantly surprised. In her excitement, she wrapped her arms around Zhou Yueshen's neck and planted a loud kiss on his cheek. \"Zhou Yueshen, have I ever told you that you are a competent husband!\"","Zhou Yueshen's body tensed, and his eyes darkened. \"No, but this is the second time you've called me husband.\"","Si Nian was surprised. \"Have I called you that before?\"","She was so used to calling the older man by his full name, Zhou Yueshen.","At this moment, she really couldn't remember when she had ever called him that.","Hearing this, Zhou Yueshen gritted his teeth. \"You really can't remember?\"","Si Nian looked at him blankly and said, \"I really, really can't remember.\"","Zhou Yueshen was a bit angry. Did this woman just use him and then forget about it?","Did she forget how she called him 'hubby' just to make another man jealous?","Zhou Yueshen's voice was hoarse as his arms wrapped around Si Nian, pulling her close. \"Then I'll make you remember.\"","With no children sleeping next door, their movements were much louder.","Da Huang raised its head vigilantly, glanced around, and seeing no suspicious movement, closed its eyes and went back to sleep.","On August 30th, Si Nian planned to go to the university to register early.","She didn't plan to live on campus because she found out the university was actually only a ten-minute walk from their place.","It was only two stops away by bus.","Moreover, the road here was very flat. Although it looked a bit creepy at night, during the day, the interlocking ginkgo trees on both sides made for beautiful scenery.","Many people rode bicycles back and forth.","Si Nian was already missing her bicycle.","Zhou Yueshen held her hand. Si Nian's walking posture was still a bit unnatural. Second Child noticed something was wrong, looked up, and asked if she had sprained her ankle.","Si Nian pinched the man's hand while smiling and saying it was just a little sprain.","Second Child immediately supported her and said, \"Then be careful, Mom. I'll hold you.\"","Zhou Zedong held his younger sister's hand. Watching his younger brother flatter their mother made his eyes hurt.","He simply looked away, out of sight, out of mind.","Zhou Yueshen didn't show any other expression despite being pinched; his face remained entirely righteous.","At the main gate of the university, as soon as they walked over, they could see the senior students welcoming the freshmen. Some had Volunteer pasted on their arms. Seeing Si Nian's family, they enthusiastically came over to greet them.","This family had young children and young adults. At first, people didn't quite understand the dynamic, but seeing the man and the young woman with their fingers intertwined, everyone seemed to understand.","To be honest, being married with children in college wasn't considered strange around here.","\"Junior, this way please. I'll take you to register.\"","\"Thank you.\" Si Nian was already feeling hot, but Zhou Yueshen refused to let go no matter what. Helpless, she could only glare at him. The family followed the senior inside. Hearing the other person ask if she was married, she directly replied, \"Yes, I'm married. This is my husband and my three little burdens.\"","Second Child, holding Si Nian's other hand, asked curiously upon hearing this, \"Mom, what is a burden?\"","Si Nian laughed, \"It means someone who holds you back.\"","\"Mom, I didn't hold you back,\" Second Child said blankly.","The senior leading the way originally thought Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan were her younger brothers. After all, the two kids didn't look that young, and Si Nian looked like a seventeen or eighteen-year-old. How could she have kids around ten years old?","Hearing this, he looked at Si Nian in shock. Even though there were married students at their school, this was his first time seeing a situation like this. He even stuttered a bit, \"Ju... Junior, you've been married for so long?\"","Si Nian couldn't help but laugh. \"Haha, did I scare you? I haven't been married for long. No matter how you look at them, they couldn't possibly be my biological children, right? They are my adopted sons and daughter.\"","The senior wiped away his cold sweat. Although he had heard that in some places girls married as young as thirteen or fourteen, it was still quite terrifying to encounter.","Si Nian chatted with him while holding Zhou Yueshen's hand, following him to her major's registration desk.","Handing in the admission notice, filling out her information.","The registration was quite simple. Originally, when dorms were being assigned, Si Nian didn't plan to take one. But thinking she could occasionally rest there and it would be convenient to store things, she applied for a dorm room anyway.","Dormitories from this era were very different from the future. It was just a five-story building with stairs, and the decoration was somewhat old.","It was a building with a lot of history.","Si Nian's dorm was on the third floor, not too high up. Four people lived in the room with bunk beds.","It was cleaned very nicely inside, and Si Nian was the first to arrive.","However, the downside was that there was no independent bathroom.","Fortunately, she would only come over occasionally to rest.","Looking at the dorm room, Si Nian felt like she had returned to her junior high school days.","Back then, when she studied in town, she had a dorm just like this. Going to the toilet meant crossing half the campus, which was extremely inconvenient.","But in this era, having a dorm like this was already pretty good.","One must know that in many schools, eight people shared a single room.","It was better than she had expected.","The bed was made of iron with wooden boards underneath. The bedding on top was distributed by the school, so she didn't have to go out of her way to buy it herself.","Second Child curiously touched the bed and said, \"Mom, Mom, this bed is so small. It's not as big as Mom and Dad's bed.\"","Si Nian smiled and said, \"Of course, because only one person can sleep here.\"","Second Child nodded in disappointment, feeling that this bed wasn't as good as the one at home.","So this was a dormitory? He didn't look forward to it at all anymore.","It was still better at home.","But since Mom said she would go home every night, he stopped worrying.","Although the bed was already set up, Si Nian still planned to clean it up a bit.","Zhou Yueshen fetched water for her and went back and forth wiping the bed and wardrobe.","Eldest Child helped sweep the floor and mopped the entire dorm clean.","When the other people arrived, they saw this family cleaning up.","They were originally a bit surprised, but when they looked up, they froze.","\"Kid Bro?\"","Zhou Zedong looked up in confusion, only to see a young man staring at him in surprise.","He frowned. \"You are?\"","The other party was stunned, then said, not knowing whether to laugh or cry, \"You forgot already? I'm the brother who played Gobang with you on the train.\"","After saying this, he felt surprised. Why was this family at the university? Wasn't today registration day?","How strange.","Could it be that someone in their family was also studying here?","The two girls who were with him earlier also walked over carrying books.","Then they were all dumbfounded. \"You guys are...\"","Before they could finish speaking, the young man slapped his forehead and said, \"Ah, I know! Were you hired by the school to clean up?\"","\"As expected of Jinghua University, the treatment is so good!\"","Si Nian: \"......\"","\"Thanks for your hard work, little brother. Coming out to work with your family at such a young age.\"","\"Here, have some candy from big brother.\"","Zhou Zedong: \".....\""]},{"number":403,"title":"Chapter 403: Researcher","paragraphs":["\"I'm not cleaning up for you, I'm cleaning up for my mom,\" Zhou Zedong said directly, ignoring the candy offered to him.","The group was taken aback for a moment.","Come to think of it, no matter how good the treatment was, they wouldn't go so far as to hire someone to clean for them, right?","Only a rich kid like Xiao Chen would think of such a possibility.","Si Nian looked at the group of four. She really didn't expect such a coincidence—these were the same people from the train who had played chess with her son and even thought about becoming her daughter-in-law.","Seeing the two boys carrying large and small bags, she figured they were probably helping the girls bring their things up.","Si Nian stepped forward and asked, \"Are you in this dorm too?\"","The two girls nodded blankly. Since Si Nian was already married, it was hard for people to associate her with someone who was just starting college.","However, looking around, there were only the old and the young.","There was no one else but her.","\"I'm Zhang Xue, and she is Liu Nana,\" the two introduced themselves.","\"I'm Si Nian. We'll be roommates from now on.\"","The two girls blushed.","After all, back on the train, they had openly said right in front of Si Nian that they had taken a liking to her son.","Even though they had thought he was her younger brother at the time, it was still awkward now.","Si Nian learned from the two girls that the other two boys were named Chen Haoran and Zhu Dong.","Chen Haoran was a local from Jing City, while the other three were from Bai City. They had all met on the train.","It seemed that Chen Haoran had his eye on Zhang Xue and was currently pursuing her.","Before long, the last roommate arrived. She was also a local from Jing City, named Lu Yao.","Everyone exchanged greetings and then started cleaning their own spaces.","\"Sister Si Nian, where are you from?\"","Zhang Xue and Liu Nana were a bit more familiar with Si Nian. As they laid out their new bedsheets, they asked her curiously.","Because Si Nian was married, both of them automatically treated her like an older sister.","Si Nian replied, \"I'm from the Yungui and Sichuan area, very far away.\"","Chen Haoran immediately chimed in, \"I know that place. My dad used to be a soldier there. I heard it was quite backward. But I guess that's not entirely true, seeing as you're quite fashionable, sister.\"","After Chen Haoran spoke, the other three roommates subconsciously glanced at Si Nian's outfit.","She was wearing a simple dress and small leather shoes. She had a lot of hair, styled in waves and draped over her back. Her facial features were bright and elegant, and her skin was fair. No matter how you looked at her, she didn't seem like someone from a remote area.","The style of her dress was also very beautiful. She wore no makeup but had applied a little lipstick, giving her a great complexion.","Even though she was about the same age as them, she was much more fashionable.","They were still wearing ordinary little sailor-collar tops.","Their hair was in ordinary braids.","And they had thick, heavy bangs...","Prompted by Chen Haoran's words, the other three subconsciously felt a sudden wave of inferiority.","Once the men stepped out, they immediately gathered around and asked Si Nian, \"Sister, where did you buy your clothes?\"","Si Nian was slightly taken aback and said, \"I bought them back in my hometown. They have this style in the department stores. If you like it, you can go take a look.\"","Department stores?","They exchanged glances. Wouldn't that be very expensive?","It hadn't been easy for them to get into college. Their family conditions weren't bad, but they weren't exactly wealthy either.","They rarely went to places like department stores to buy clothes; they usually bought them from street stalls.","Hearing Si Nian say this, they thought to themselves that her family must be quite rich.","Who said remote areas were poor? In their eyes, Si Nian was much richer than they were.","Si Nian wouldn't be living in the dorm very often anyway. After finishing the cleaning, she planned to take her older husband and the three children out to eat.","It was a good opportunity to taste how the food in their cafeteria was.","There weren't many people reporting in today, but the cafeteria had started operating long ago.","The students who arrived early didn't have to worry about going hungry.","Si Nian said goodbye to Zhang Xue and the others, then led the children and Zhou Yueshen to the cafeteria.","The cafeteria was huge, and the school itself was astonishingly large.","There was also a library and other facilities.","The children were dazzled by the sights.","\"Big brother, this school is so much bigger than ours.\"","Second Child had a stunned expression on his face.","Zhou Zedong was quite calm and seemed very satisfied with the school's environment.","Although he was still young, he had already made up his mind to study here in the future.","The family of five arrived at the cafeteria. There weren't many people around at the moment.","Some other students had also come with their families, so their group didn't look out of place.","Si Nian ordered two meat dishes—sweet and sour spare ribs and steamed fish—along with scrambled eggs, spare rib soup, and four portions of rice.","It looked quite appetizing.","However, the price wasn't cheap either.","The children held their bowls of rice and ate. They weren't picky eaters and ate everything.","\"Mom, these sweet spare ribs are just as delicious as the ones you make.\"","Si Nian smiled slightly. Back when she was in school, her school also had this dish. Because she loved eating it, she had specifically learned how to make it.","Naturally, the taste was quite similar.","Although Si Nian's cooking skills were quite good, she wasn't so confident as to compare herself to a professional chef.","Her son's words were already the greatest affirmation of her culinary skills.","After eating, the family went to buy some furniture and items that were still missing at home.","Jing City was even hotter than back home, but the courtyard house was actually quite cool. Buying a fan would completely solve the heat problem.","Si Nian also bought new schoolbags for the children.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't gone out to busy himself these past two days. Instead, he hired workers to build a washroom next to the toilet, which would make washing clothes and other chores convenient in the future.","Si Nian also contacted a local primary school, planning to send the two children there to register.","This school was recommended to Zhou Yueshen by Yu Dong's wealthy sister, who lived far away in Jing City.","They had a letter of introduction.","As soon as the school saw the letter, they didn't even look at the children's grades and directly said they just needed to come and register.","Their attitude was incredibly accommodating.","Surprisingly, there was also a kindergarten here. It wasn't like the typical childcare classes in the compounds, but a real preschool.","In the future, all three siblings would be able to attend the same school.","After registering the children, Si Nian couldn't help but ask Zhou Yueshen exactly how wealthy Yu Dong's family was.","Zhou Yueshen didn't know much. He only knew that Yu Dong's family ran a restaurant back in their hometown, and he had occasionally heard him boast about how his grandfather or some older generation had been a royal chef in the palace.","But he had never taken it seriously, assuming Yu Dong was just bragging.","But now, seeing that a single introduction letter from his sister had waived the complicated enrollment procedures for three children and even secured them placements in the best classes, he had to admit that they had some serious backing.","Jiang Jiu was also brought to register by Jiang Wenqing. Jiang Jiu had been staying with his dad in the researchers' dormitory these past few days. He had initially been unhappy about it, but after seeing all the weird and wonderful things at the research institute, he became fascinated.","He had even completely forgotten about his dear second brother.","He only remembered him when it was time for school.","Jiang Jiu's family was very wealthy; he could attend any school he wanted without a problem.","They had called Zhou Yueshen in advance to ask, and knowing they were coming to this primary school, they immediately sent their son over.","When Jiang Jiu saw the two brothers, he happily ran over and said, \"Big brother, second brother! My dad is amazing. He researches a lot of magical things. Look, this is the globe my dad gave me. Dad says the earth is round.\"","He took a mini globe out of his schoolbag to show them.","Second Child touched it, and the globe began to spin.","Even Zhou Zedong, who had been sitting off to the side with no interest in their conversation, couldn't help but have his eyes drawn to the globe.","Second Child asked in confusion, \"Why is the earth round, yet we don't fall off?\"","Zhou Zedong rolled his eyes at his younger brother. \"Because of gravity.\""]},{"number":404,"title":"Chapter 404: Dreams","paragraphs":["Zhou Zehan couldn't understand.","Zhou Zedong also regretted it; saying these things to his younger brother was simply a waste of breath.","His eyes were fixed on the globe, a glint of light flashing in his gaze.","\"Xiao Jiu, can I have a look at this?\"","Jiang Jiu generously handed it over. \"Big Brother, do you like this? If you like it, I'll ask my dad to give you one too.\"","Jiang Wenqing, standing to the side: \"...\"","He only had this one. If it weren't for the fact that his son liked it so much, he would have never been willing to give it to him.","And now his son was just generously offering it to someone else.","What a great son he had.","However, thinking about how highly the team leader thought of Zhou Zedong earlier, his eyes flickered. Perhaps this was a good opportunity.","He said, \"I'll go to the institute and ask. If there are any extras, I'll find one for you.\"","Jiang Jiu immediately said, \"My dad also has a world map and a microscope. Little bugs can become super big!\"","\"Big Brother, if there's anything else you like, just tell me, and I'll have my dad give it to you.\"","Jiang Jiu used to not know exactly what his dad did and felt he had no charm at all.","When others were showing off what their dads did and how amazing they were, he would feel very envious.","But when the teacher asked him what his dad did for a living, he couldn't answer at all.","Now, seeing it with his own eyes, he finally realized that his dad was actually so charming and so amazing!","Zhou Zedong spun the globe, and upon hearing this, his expression shifted again.","Jiang Wenqing: \"...\"","The group talked and laughed as they went to the classroom to register.","Si Nian asked Jiang Wenqing about his situation, \"Is it convenient for you to bring Xiao Jiu to the research institute? If it's too much trouble, he can come to my house. The kids can keep each other company.\"","Jiang Wenqing smiled embarrassedly. \"How could I do that? I wasn't home before and neglected Xiao Jiu. Now that I have him by my side, I want to spend more time with him and make it up to him.\"","Si Nian thought about it and agreed. She had been quite worried at first, but seeing Jiang Jiu excitedly telling the two children about what he saw at the research institute, it seemed things weren't as bad as she had thought.","Today was September 1st, and there were a lot of people coming to register.","Zhou Yueshen took his eldest son to the fifth grade, and Si Nian took Zhou Zehan to the second grade.","Jiang Jiu was in the same class as him, and many parents were currently bringing their children to register.","When the homeroom teacher saw them arrive, she specially came over to greet them. \"I just heard from the director that two new transfer students have arrived. It must be these two little friends, right?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Hello, this is my son, Zhou Zehan. This is Jiang Jiu and his father.\"","The teacher smiled and nodded. \"Hello, little friend Xiao Han, and little friend Xiao Jiu. I am your homeroom teacher, Wang Shuang. Please take care of me from now on.\"","\"Hello, teacher!\"","The two children immediately greeted her loudly.","\"Then I'll take them inside to meet their classmates,\" Teacher Wang said with a smile.","Si Nian and Jiang Wenqing waited outside.","The second-grade children were not very old yet, sitting perfectly straight and proper.","There were two or three other children on the stage, who all looked like new transfer students as well.","Including Jiang Jiu and Zhou Zehan, there were five of them in total.","Teacher Wang clapped the blackboard and said, \"Quiet down. Today we have a few new friends in our class. Let's introduce ourselves to each other and talk about our hobbies and dreams, okay?\"","It was Jiang Wenqing's first time bringing his son to school for registration. Seeing his son standing on the stage preparing to introduce himself, a hint of nervousness flashed in his eyes.","Si Nian, on the other hand, felt a bit awkward, terrified that her second son's dream would be to become a pig slaughterer just like his father.","The three students who went in first took turns introducing themselves.","\"My name is Hao Zhengyi, and I am eight years old this year. My hobby is playing catch the thief. When I grow up, I want to be a police officer and catch thieves for the common people.\"","\"My name is Wang Liting, and I am eight years old. When I grow up, I want to be a doctor and treat the common people for free.\"","\"My name is Liu Yonggui. When I grow up, I want to be a scientist and let the common people fly into the sky...\"","When it was the second son's turn, he found himself at a loss for words. Were everyone's dreams this grand?","He thought hard, and suddenly his eyes lit up as he said loudly, \"My name is Zhou Zehan. When I grow up, I want to be the common people, so they will all serve me.\"","The class immediately erupted into laughter.","Si Nian: \"...\"","The teacher was also amused and looked at Jiang Jiu. Jiang Jiu originally wanted to be a scientist, but his dream had been stolen. He was just wondering what to say when he heard his second brother say this, and he immediately chimed in, \"I also want to be the common people and enjoy their services with my second brother.\"","Jiang Wenqing: \"...\"","The person who brought Xiao Bowen to register was a middle-aged woman. He hadn't expected to run into Zhou Zedong so soon.","His face was full of surprise.","The two of them were now transfer students in Class One of the fifth grade. Both children had been assigned to this class because of their excellent grades.","There was none of the lively atmosphere of the second grade; the scene was even a bit awkward.","The teacher asked the two of them to introduce themselves.","\"My name is Xiao Bowen, and I'm eight years old.\"","\"My name is Zhou Yuedong, and I'm eleven.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Why the sudden awkward silence?","The teacher laughed awkwardly to smooth things over. \"Where are you two students from? Do you have any hobbies, or what do you want to be when you grow up?\"","Fang Bowen frowned and said, \"My hobby is reading and doing homework.\"","Zhou Zedong: \"My hobby is reading books and practicing calligraphy.\"","Everyone: \"...\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","Behind him, a woman stared blankly at Zhou Zedong's face.","Primary school covered a lot of subjects, and the knowledge varied in every city, but it wasn't too difficult. Zhou Zedong knew most of the material.","He really wanted to just skip straight to junior high.","Moreover, he had no interest in these things now; his mind was still on the globe Jiang Jiu had brought back earlier that day.","After returning home, he flipped through a book he now found dull and said to Si Nian, \"Mom, can I go to the library to read?\"","Si Nian knew he had lost interest in what he currently had, which was why he brought this up to her.","In any case, reading more books was always a good thing. She nodded and agreed, \"Of course, but don't stay out too late. You can borrow the books you want from the library and read them at home; otherwise, Mom will worry about you being out alone.\"","Zhou Zedong nodded and agreed.","He planned to go to the library after class tomorrow.","There was a very large library right across from their school. He had seen Fang Bowen—oh, wait, Xiao Bowen—go there with a woman after class.","Actually, he had really wanted to go look too, but he was afraid his mom would worry, so he came home first.","\"Bowen, do you know that boy?\"","Xiao Guifang asked her grandson. Because her son was very busy with the start of the school term these past few days, she was asked to bring the child to school to register.","She hadn't expected to see a boy who looked so much like her eldest son.","Xiao Guifang had been completely stunned at the time.","Only now did she finally react.","Xiao Bowen nodded as he flipped through his book, \"I know him, Grandma. He is Zhou Zedong. When Mom and I went to Yungui-Sichuan City, he lived right next door to me. Even though he always keeps a straight face, he is a very good person.\"","Xiao Guifang's eyes trembled."]},{"number":405,"title":"Chapter 405: Ten Years Ago","paragraphs":["Thinking of everything that had happened before, she had originally thought that Fang Hui taking her grandson over there was just another trick to force her son to marry her. But now, it seemed that was not the case at all.","No longer in the mood to read with her grandson, she hurriedly said, \"Little Bowen, let's go home first, okay? I'll bring you back to read tomorrow.\"","With that, she quickly pulled the confused Xiao Bowen home.","The Xiao family resided in a luxurious courtyard house in the city center.","Xiao Guifang drove home. Aside from a few maids cleaning, the house was empty.","Her youngest son hadn't returned yet.","She asked the maid to take care of her grandson and inquired, \"How is the old master doing today?\"","\"Madam, the old master is the same as usual today.\"","Xiao Guifang gave a sound of acknowledgment, went upstairs, and entered the bedroom.","On the bed lay an elderly man with gray hair, completely motionless.","On the nightstand beside him sat a vase and a family portrait.","Xiao Guifang picked up the photo. Looking at her deceased husband and son in the picture, her eyes filled with agony. \"It's all karma.\"","Meanwhile, a middle-aged man in his thirties or forties led a teenage boy into the alley, carrying gifts in his hands, and found the Zhou family's house.","Looking at the somewhat dilapidated house in front of them, the boy grumbled, \"Dad, what kind of friend requires you to visit in person? Besides, isn't this Beilu Village? People actually still live here?\"","The man scolded him, \"What nonsense are you spouting? Plenty of people live here. Don't you dare say such things in front of your Uncle Zhou.\"","\"Tch, I might not know, but don't you?\"","\"That was ten years ago. So many years have passed, stop blabbering about it.\"","The man made a gesture as if to kick him.","Only then did the boy shut his mouth.","The man straightened his suit, stepped forward with top-tier Maotai liquor and a fruit basket in hand, and knocked on the door.","\"Coming, coming!\"","A child's crisp voice rang out.","\"Who is it?\" Second Child poked his little head through the crack in the door.","His eyes met the gaze of the teenager looking down.","\"Ah, it's you! The big brother who lost to my older brother on the train.\"","Chen Haoran was speechless.","The man was surprised. \"Haoran, you've met?\"","Chen Haoran was also dumbfounded. He never expected fate to play such a trick on him. He said, \"Dad, is this the old friend's house you were talking about?\"","\"Aren't they from out of town?\"","Father Chen replied, \"Yes, they just moved here.\"","\"Haven't I told you before? When I was serving in the military out of town, I made a few friends whom I'd trust with my life.\"","Chen Haoran looked at him suspiciously. \"Are you bragging? If you really trust each other with your lives, why didn't you advise them against living here?\"","\"What's wrong with here?\" Si Nian, who had heard the knock and walked out, frowned upon hearing his words.","\"Mom, it's that big brother who lost to my older brother looking for us.\"","Chen Haoran said, \"Ten years ago, there was a family over there...\"","Before he could finish his sentence, Father Chen kicked him.","Chen Haoran stumbled inside and bumped right into a giant dog.","\"Ah!\" He was nearly scared to death.","\"Da Huang.\" Si Nian called out Da Huang's name, signaling it not to bite.","Only then did Da Huang retract its fangs.","Covered in sweat, Chen Haoran ran back and hid behind Si Nian. \"Damn, sis, your family keeps such a huge dog. It scared the life out of me.\"","Si Nian, on the other hand, was confused. \"You are?\"","She didn't think she was familiar enough with this schoolmate for him to pay a home visit.","Father Chen spoke first. \"Sister-in-law, my name is Chen Nan, and this is my son Haoran. I didn't expect you to have already met, so I won't introduce you much further. I heard from Yueshen that you moved here. I've been too busy to visit, but since I was passing by today, I finally had the time to come see you.\"","Si Nian was slightly surprised. She nodded and called out to Zhou Yueshen, who was still busy inside the house, \"Zhou Yueshen, someone is here to see you.\"","Zhou Yueshen walked out.","He was still holding installation tools in his hands.","Seeing the father and son, he was also slightly taken aback.","\"Old Chen?\"","Chen Nan said, \"I was just passing by. Knowing you moved in, I thought I'd drop by for a visit. Here is a little gift for you.\"","He handed the items to Si Nian. \"Sister-in-law, this modest gift is to celebrate your admission to university. Yueshen told me about your situation over the phone. Congratulations.\"","Si Nian thanked him, \"You're too kind.\"","\"Haha, you're welcome. Now that the gift is delivered and I've seen you, I won't disturb your work any longer.\"","Si Nian originally wanted to invite them to stay for a meal, but unexpectedly, the father and son ran off incredibly fast.","She had wanted to ask what exactly happened in this neighborhood.","This brother of Zhou Yueshen wouldn't lie to him, would he?","Right at this moment, Song Zhaodi walked over carrying a basket and asked curiously, \"Sister, did you have visitors just now?\"","Si Nian nodded and glanced at Song Zhaodi. She was in her late twenties and dressed plainly, but Si Nian hadn't seen anyone else around her these past few days.","Wasn't it a bit unusual to be around thirty and not have children?","She asked casually, \"Sister-in-law, how many years have you lived here?\"","Song Zhaodi smiled. \"Over a decade. I married and moved here when I was eighteen, and I'm almost thirty now. Is there something you want to ask me?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"I just heard someone say that something terrible happened here. Is that true?\"","Song Zhaodi paused for a moment, then let out a sigh. \"It's no secret. I mentioned it to you before. It's about Wang Ergou accidentally killing someone. But it wasn't on our side; it was quite far away. It just got spread around in a mysterious way. The main reason was that the woman was indecent. Being a widow, she couldn't bear the loneliness and seduced many men. After she was accidentally killed by Wang Ergou, everyone said she deserved to die. However, people passing by her house kept hearing noises, so all sorts of bizarre rumors started spreading. You know how it is, there are superstitious things everywhere these days. But it's been ten years, and I can barely remember it.\"","Si Nian nodded thoughtfully.","No wonder Chen Haoran had that tone just now.","Sure enough, no matter the era, terrifying rumors would always spread.","Especially in these older times, when people were still somewhat superstitious.","She now understood even better why Zhou Yueshen's friend couldn't sell his house.","Si Nian sighed.","\"What? Dad, you introduced this house to my schoolmate? How could you be so wicked? Haven't you heard that place is haunted?\"","Chen Nan was speechless. \"Haunted my foot! Those are just rumors spread by superstitious people. If you really want to get into it, there isn't a single place in Beijing where someone hasn't died. During the wars in the past, there were corpses everywhere. It's precisely because of people like you that my house can't be sold.\"","\"Your Uncle Zhou wanted a newer place that was also close to the school. This was the only suitable option. Besides, you don't know what kind of person your Uncle Zhou is. Even if there really was a ghost, it would be scared to death by him. He has slaughtered more pigs than there are ghosts, why would he be afraid?\"","Chen Haoran curled his lips. \"Forget it. At least you have some conscience left by not introducing a murder house to them.\"","Chen Nan: \"...\""]},{"number":406,"title":"Chapter 406: Roommate","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen hired a few workers and spent a few days finishing the washroom. It had a bathtub and a washbasin inside, and was currently being aired out.","He also took the opportunity to build a wooden doghouse for Da Huang, which Si Nian had designed.","Now Da Huang finally had a nest of its own in Jing City.","Since there weren't many people around here, Si Nian didn't have to keep it tied up all day.","Plus, the yard was large, so Da Huang could run around freely.","One of the two trees in the yard had been cut down, leaving only one. This tree was huge, at least several decades old. Beneath it sat a stone table and stools, a perfect spot to cool off when the weather was hot.","Zhou Yueshen found a punching bag from who-knows-where and hung it from the tree. Second Child would go punch it for a while whenever he had nothing to do.","Zhou Yueshen was a man of his word. Since he had decided to train his son, even moving to a new place and starting school didn't stop the early morning training sessions.","Zhou Zehan felt that his father was like two completely different people when facing him versus his mother.","In front of his mom, whatever she said went.","But in front of him, he became the one being bossed around.","With school and daily exercise, Second Child's appetite had not only grown, but his sleep quality was top-notch.","His bad habit of snoring was getting more and more exaggerated.","Zhou Zedong could hear his younger brother's snores just walking past his door. Clutching a biology book he had borrowed from the library, he walked by, secretly glad that he didn't share a room with his brother.","After finishing the chores around the house, Zhou Yueshen went back to leaving early and returning late.","Although he had done business before, now that he was involved in an unfamiliar field, he had to study very seriously.","Recently, Si Nian actually saw this man studying German.","She was a bit dumbfounded. She had a knack for languages and knew a little bit of everything, so seeing Zhou Yueshen learning it surprised her.","The courtyard house originally had a large, antique-style study where Zhou Yueshen usually worked.","Si Nian would occasionally bring him some fruit and tea.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen reading up on German-related materials, she was very curious: What is this for?","Zhou Yueshen was very focused when he worked, and normally Si Nian wouldn't disturb him.","But this time, she was truly curious.","Flipping through the book, Zhou Yueshen replied, Just some German learning materials. The electrical components Lao Chen deals with are imported, so we often need to socialize with these people.","Si Nian was surprised: You can read it?","Zhou Yueshen picked up the cup she brought, took a sip, and frowned.","He set it down without changing his expression.","Back when we were doing literacy campaigns in the army, I took on some diplomatic tasks and had a bit of exposure to it.","Si Nian was impressed. She only knew that this man had beautiful handwriting and figured he must be educated.","But she hadn't expected Zhou Yueshen to know so much more than she imagined.","She sat to the side, picked up a grape, popped it into her mouth, and asked, Are things going smoothly with you and Lao Chen?","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod: Everything is fine.","That is good, Si Nian nodded. By the way, I have a few classes tomorrow, so I might be back a bit late in the afternoon. If you get back early, go pick up the kids.","Zhou Yueshen nodded and agreed.","Si Nian stood up. Noticing the coffee he had only taken one sip of, her eyes flickered as she asked, Is the coffee good? I just bought it today. Seeing you work so late recently, I thought this stuff could help keep you awake.","Zhou Yueshen paused. In truth, he wasn't used to drinking this kind of thing. Just now, he had even thought it was some kind of medicine...","He didn't expect it to actually be coffee.","Seeing Si Nian waiting expectantly for his response, his Adam's apple bobbed, and he let out an Mhm.","It is good.","That is great. Si Nian smiled: Then I will brew a cup for you every day from now on.","Zhou Yueshen: You really don't need to go to so much trouble.","Si Nian said, It is no trouble at all.","After saying that, she walked away happily.","Zhou Yueshen let out a helpless, low chuckle and lowered his head to continue reading.","The school semester had just started, and everyone was still getting used to things.","Si Nian was a foreign language major, and all of her roommates were in the same major.","It really was quite a coincidence.","Every day when Si Nian went to the dorm, the others were either memorizing vocabulary or listening to tapes.","They were incredibly diligent.","In contrast, she seemed a bit too casual.","The truth was, she had grown sick of listening to tapes during her time teaching. Right now, she really had no desire for it; she just wanted to quickly finish her college degree.","Si Nian subconsciously lowered her voice.","She didn't want to disturb them.","All three loved studying, though Zhang Xue and Liu Nana were alright, a bit more easily distracted, whereas Lu Yao was extremely serious.","Word had it that she planned to become a diplomat in the future.","Because of this, she worked exceptionally hard.","Seeing Si Nian arrive, Zhang Xue and Liu Nana instantly lost their mood to study. They hurried over and said, Sister Si Nian, did you hear? There is a mixer dance at the school tonight. They say it is to promote communication and build relationships among the freshmen. Do you want to go?","Si Nian really didn't care much about these things. After all, she went straight home every day after class. There weren't that many major courses in college, and Si Nian had no intention of studying anything else, so after finishing her required classes, she basically didn't stay on campus.","A dance?","Yeah, let's go together.","Lu Yao, are you going?","Lu Yao frowned and said, I don't really want to go to that kind of dance. It feels a bit improper. I would rather just study. You guys too, you shouldn't slack off just because you are in college now. We worked so hard to get in.","After saying that, she looked at Si Nian: Si Nian, you never seem to study at noon. Don't you think that is a bad idea?","Si Nian only came over at noon to take a nap, as she had a habit of napping, and it also conveniently kept her from disturbing her roommates' studies.","Hearing this, she was taken aback for a moment before replying, It is fine. I know what I am doing.","Who knows what part of her words struck a nerve with Lu Yao, but she immediately frowned and said, From the start of the semester until now, I have never seen you study. Not to be a busybody, but I just think it is not good for you to act like this. There are only four of us in the dorm, and you will be the only one failing classes when the time comes.","Si Nian paused slightly and said, I won't fail.","Lu Yao thought she was blindly confident. Remembering how Zhang Xue and Liu Nana discussed every day whether Si Nian's family was very wealthy, she couldn't help but let her imagination run wild.","She couldn't help but say, Even though I know you have money, things bought with money don't give you nearly as much of a sense of achievement as things earned through your own abilities.","Hearing this, Si Nian also felt that something was off.","Lu Yao's tone made it sound as if she had bribed her way into the school through the back door.","Just because she didn't study in the dorm? She came up with this kind of idea?","Wasn't that a bit too ridiculous?","The four girls in the dorm usually didn't interact much, especially since Si Nian basically only came to rest.","So up until now, everyone had been polite and friendly, and no conflicts had broken out.","This was the very first time.","Zhang Xue and Liu Nana didn't dare to speak.","Si Nian asked, What did I do to make you misunderstand that I paid my way into the school?","Confronted so directly, Lu Yao felt a bit uncomfortable: If you are unhappy about it, just pretend I didn't say anything. This is just a kind reminder from someone who scored a 96 on the foreign language exam. I am only doing this for your own good.","Si Nian said in a deep voice, \"Sorry, I cannot just pretend you didn't say that. The fact that you suspect I bought my way in is an insult to me in itself. You were unaware of the truth, and perhaps my behavior really did cause you to misunderstand, so I don't blame you for that. However, I don't think someone with a perfect score in foreign languages needs a reminder from someone who only scored a ninety-six.\""]},{"number":407,"title":"Chapter 407: Almost forgot that I have a husband.","paragraphs":["Lu Yao's breath hitched.","Zhang Xue and Liu Nana had been trying to figure out how to ease the tension, but hearing this, they were both dumbfounded.","\"Si, Sister Si Nian, you got a perfect score in English?\"","\"Are you serious?\"","After her initial shock, Lu Yao's face was filled with suspicion.","Taking it easy every day, eating, drinking, and having fun—in her eyes, Si Nian was just a wealthy young lady who came to college to experience life.","She got a perfect score?","Who would believe that?","There probably weren't even a handful of people in the entire country who could get a perfect score, right?","Si Nian didn't bother to argue, calmly stating, \"You can go ask the counselor.\"","Originally, Si Nian had been invited to give a speech on stage as a freshman, but she found it too troublesome and refused. She didn't want a high profile; she just wanted to quickly finish college and go home.","She never expected that this would lead to misunderstandings.","Although Lu Yao might just be the type of top student who couldn't stand people who didn't like to study, her lecturing tone still made Si Nian quite uncomfortable.","Lu Yao's grip on her pen tightened.","After moving into the dorm, she had asked about the scores of her other two roommates, and neither was as high as hers.","She had never even seen Si Nian study. Hearing Zhang Xue and the others mention that Si Nian must be very rich, she hadn't thought much of it.","She assumed Si Nian was just an ignorant and incompetent rich girl.","But she never expected her to be like this.","Si Nian didn't pay her much more attention and went to her bed to sleep.","After classes in the afternoon, Zhang Xue and Liu Nana insisted on dragging her to a mixer.","They said she was experienced and had a better eye for judging people.","In short, the two were shy and treated Si Nian as their leader.","Si Nian figured she had already told Zhou Yueshen she would be back late today, and since she was a bit curious herself, she agreed.","\"Lu Yao, are you really not going?\"","Seeing that Lu Yao hadn't left the classroom yet, Zhang Xue and the other called out to her again.","Lu Yao looked at the three of them walking arm in arm, her frown deepening as she refused, \"No.\"","Seeing her cold expression, the two didn't say much more.","Lu Yao walked to the counselor's office and found the counselor.","Hearing her mention Si Nian, the counselor was a bit surprised. \"I remember the two of you were assigned to the same dorm. Is something wrong?\"","Their dorm assignments actually followed certain rules; students with good grades were grouped with those with average grades to encourage studying.","Lu Yao was the one with the good grades.","Seeing her come in, the counselor worried that the girls might be having a conflict.","\"Teacher, I wanted to ask about Si Nian's college entrance exam score.\"","Lu Yao still couldn't quite get past it in her heart.","After all, someone she had always considered inferior to herself suddenly claimed to be better than her.","How could she feel comfortable with that?","Lu Yao was too competitive. She had always been like this in class, wanting to be the best at everything.","It wasn't that she couldn't stand Si Nian being better than her; she just felt that someone who never studied or read books had no right to be better than her.","Hearing this, the counselor paused again, surprised. \"You don't know? I thought you all would have known by now.\"","Lu Yao frowned. \"Why do you say that?\"","\"Si Nian is the provincial top scorer whom our school leaders flew a long way to recruit. It caused quite a stir back then. She got perfect scores in several subjects. I thought you would have asked her long ago.\"","The counselor continued, \"She used to be an English teacher at a famous foreign language elementary school. I heard several genius students from her class are being closely observed and cultivated by the school. They'll probably be highly sought after when they grow up. It's a good thing you were assigned with her; you can learn from and exchange ideas with each other.\"","Lu Yao's face looked awful. \"Provincial top scorer...\"","The counselor said, \"Right. I heard you were also a school top scorer. You are both very outstanding talents. You must not have any conflicts, understand?\"","Originally, the special treatment the school offered Si Nian was a single dorm room.","But Si Nian felt it was a waste of school resources and that being singled out for special treatment would draw unwanted attention, so she declined, hoping to keep a low profile.","Therefore, the school didn't mention the matter much.","Seeing her terrible expression, the counselor guessed what was going on and sighed.","There were too many students with good grades, especially at a school like theirs.","Before getting into college, these kids were all the cream of the crop at their respective schools, thinking highly of themselves.","However, after coming to their university, they realized there was always someone better out there, and they took a huge blow to their pride.","It wasn't anything strange.","Si Nian returned to the dorm, and the two girls started getting dressed up.","Zhang Xue changed into several outfits but wasn't satisfied with any of them. Looking at how good Si Nian looked in whatever she threw on, she couldn't help but say, \"Sister Si Nian, I want to discuss something with you.\"","\"What is it?\"","\"Um, could you, could you lend me the dress you wore on registration day? Don't worry, I'll wash it clean for you,\" Zhang Xue said ingratiatingly.","Si Nian frowned. She knew that some good friends and sisters would share clothes, but she was a neat freak. She naturally wouldn't lend out such close-fitting clothes to others, not to mention that those clothes were all bought for her by Zhou Yueshen.","So she refused directly, \"I'm sorry, Zhang Xue, but I don't lend out my personal clothing.\"","Zhang Xue said, \"Oh come on, I'm just going to wear it once, it's no big deal. I'll wash it clean for you afterwards, don't worry. Please, pretty please?\"","Having just arrived at college, she had seen too many beautiful girls and felt terribly inadequate.","Today, she naturally wanted to look beautiful for the dance.","However, no matter how she dressed, it just didn't feel right; she felt she looked tacky.","Si Nian didn't waver in the slightest. \"No. If you want to buy one, I can recommend a place, but my clothes are not for loan.\"","Seeing her absolute and uncompromising tone, a hint of resentment appeared in Zhang Xue's eyes.","She felt that she treated Si Nian as a friend, yet Si Nian was treating her like this.","Feeling somewhat disappointed, she pursed her lips, said nothing, and turned back to getting dressed.","Liu Nana frowned but didn't say anything either.","Before they finished getting ready, Yang Haoran and his group sent someone to call them.","Zhang Xue blushed, hurriedly applied some lip gloss, and anxiously rushed downstairs.","Who would have thought that Chen Haoran wouldn't even glance at her carefully dressed self, but instead ran straight toward Si Nian, enthusiastically calling out, \"Sister, Sister, are you going to the dance too?\"","After saying this, he added in a low voice that only the two of them could hear, \"Does Uncle Zhou know?\"","His dad had told him to call Si Nian 'Auntie' when he saw her.","But Chen Haoran had high emotional intelligence. Besides, Si Nian was as beautiful as a fairy; calling her 'Auntie' would be an absolute insult to her peerless looks.","So he chose to do it his own way and call her 'Sister', which was both polite and sounded nice.","Hearing this, Si Nian paused, slapped her forehead, and suddenly realized, \"Right, how could I forget? As a married woman, it's probably not appropriate for me to go to this kind of dance, is it?\"","Although it was billed as a networking event to get to know each other, bluntly speaking, it was for finding a partner.","Sigh, she had almost forgotten that she had a husband.","She had actually thought of herself as an innocent female college student for a moment.","\"Forget it then, I won't go. You guys go ahead.\"","She waved her hand.","Seeing how familiar the two were with each other left a bitter taste in Zhang Xue's mouth, even though she knew Si Nian was already married and had a child."]},{"number":408,"title":"Chapter 408: The Secret","paragraphs":["But why was Chen Haoran suddenly being so enthusiastic towards her?","Wasn't he just recently acting so... towards her?","She pinched the palm of her hand.","Suddenly, she understood why Lu Yao had a problem with Si Nian.","\"We're already here, let's go, Sis. It won't hurt to take a look. Besides, I have something I want to tell you.\"","Chen Haoran still had his thoughts about Si Nian living in that kind of place.","Right now, his gossiping spirit was burning bright.","He couldn't wait to share it with her immediately.","Si Nian said, \"Are you talking about the accidental murder from ten years ago? I already know about it.\"","\"Accidental? Who told you it was an accident? I heard it was a premeditated murder,\" Chen Haoran said with a frown.","Si Nian was confused. \"Premeditated? Wasn't it a burglar who broke in to rob the place and accidentally killed someone?\"","\"Your version is the original one. What I know is the updated version. At first, everyone thought the same as you, but later word got out that the burglar was just unlucky enough to stumble into a murder scene and ended up taking the blame. Even after he was caught, he refused to confess, and the police couldn't find conclusive evidence to prove he committed the murder. The case became an unsolved mystery. But because the victim's family made a huge fuss, it was eventually closed as manslaughter.\"","\"I also heard that people walking by at night would hear sounds coming from the courtyard where the murder happened. It was extremely terrifying. Later, someone even went missing, so a lot of people moved away from there at the time.\"","\"A lot of houses over there still can't be sold even now.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","She had thought that no matter what, it was a courtyard house, so it shouldn't be that hard to sell.","So this was the reason.","No wonder so few people lived around there.","People in this era were inherently superstitious. With stories like this going around, there probably weren't many who wouldn't be scared.","Si Nian comforted herself: Don't be scared, don't be scared. Even if it's a haunted house, it's a haunted house worth hundreds of millions.","If you aren't afraid of being poor, why be afraid of ghosts?","However, what puzzled Si Nian was that if this story had been updated, why did Song Zhaodi still tell her the original version?","She seemed to believe that the thief, Wang Ergou, was the murderer.","But according to what Chen Haoran said, did that mean the real murderer was someone else?","Based on her past experience of scrolling through short videos watching unsolved mystery cases, the vast majority of these incidents were committed by acquaintances, who likely lived nearby.","If Wang Ergou wasn't the culprit, then it was highly likely that the murderer was still at large.","In this era, there were no surveillance cameras anyway.","There were far too many cases where people murdered someone, dumped the body, and it was treated as a missing person case.","There were also cases that were overturned decades later.","But by then, it would be too late.","Si Nian originally hadn't wanted to pay much attention to this kind of thing; after all, hearing too much of it gave her the creeps.","But she had already bought the house. If this haunting issue wasn't resolved, it would affect the skyrocketing value of her property.","This was one of her assets for her future retirement.","How could she let it be affected by an unfounded rumor?","Judging from the hundreds of unsolved murder cases she had read about, the haunting was very likely a rumor deliberately spread by someone to confuse the public.","Thinking this way, Si Nian lost all interest in going to any dance.","She directly took her leave, saying, \"I still have some things to do at home. You guys go have fun, I'm heading back first.\"","After saying that, without waiting for them to react, she put on her backpack and quickly left the school.","As she was standing at the bus stop waiting for the bus, a black sedan pulled up in front of her.","\"Teacher Si, where are you going? I'll give you a ride.\"","Si Nian looked over in surprise. \"Mr. Xiao?\"","Xiao Yi nodded. \"I heard there's a freshman networking dance tonight. You aren't attending?\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"Forget it, I'm already married, that kind of occasion doesn't suit me. What about you, Mr. Xiao? No, it should be Professor Xiao, have you finished your classes too?\"","\"How is student Fang Bowen doing?\"","\"Little Bowen is doing well, thank you for your concern, Teacher Si.\"","Si Nian smiled and nodded. Seeing the bus arriving, she hurriedly waved goodbye. \"Thank you for the offer, but I can just take the bus back. Goodbye, Professor Xiao.\"","Watching her get on the bus with her backpack, to the point where the male students behind her blushed and made way for her, Xiao Yi's eyes flickered.","If he remembered correctly, that Zhou Yueshen should be thirty years old.","It was quite curious that a young girl like Si Nian would actually marry him.","Xiao Yi drove back home.","He had been busy lately and hadn't been back for a few days.","As soon as he entered the house, his son ran over. \"Dad, you're back! Let me tell you, I saw Zhou Zedong. He and his younger brother both transferred to my school, and they're even in my class. Dad, doesn't this prove that I have a special connection with them?\"","Xiao Bowen hadn't shown it at school, but in reality, he was very excited inside.","Xiao Yi patted his head. When he looked up, his mother was standing at the top of the stairs, looking at him.","Xiao Yi paused and called out, \"Mom.\"","Mother Xiao had a cold and gloomy expression. \"So you still know I'm your mother.\"","After saying that, she realized her grandson was still there, and said in a deep voice, \"Come up, I have something to discuss with you.\"","Xiao Yi paused, then followed her upstairs.","Mother Xiao threw a few photos onto the table, her tone agitated. \"What is the meaning of this? You sent Fang Hui to Yungui City just to look for these kids, didn't you?\"","Xiao Yi glanced at the photos and frowned. \"You had someone secretly take pictures of them?\"","\"If I hadn't had someone take pictures, I wouldn't have known that our Xiao family still has children wandering out there!\"","Hearing this, a trace of mockery flashed in Xiao Yi's eyes. \"Children? Back when my brother wanted to bring them back, have you forgotten how you stopped him? You forced my brother to marry, you threatened him with your life to force him to stay in Beijing, making him abandon his wife and children. And now you're calling them children of the Xiao family?\"","\"You caused the death of their biological father. Their mother died of depression because she was abandoned in the countryside. The children became orphans, and just when they were finally adopted and started living a good life, you can't wait to scheme against them?\"","Hearing about her deceased son, a flash of guilt appeared in Mother Xiao's eyes.","She was actually unable to refute her son's words.","\"If you still feel any guilt towards my brother, I hope you won't disturb their family's life.\"","\"They are much better off there than returning to the Xiao family.\"","Back then, when Xiao Yi was on a business trip, he accidentally saw a newspaper article about Zhou Zedong being called a genius.","When he saw the photo at the time, he was extremely surprised because the child looked exactly like his older brother.","He only investigated out of suspicion.","He didn't expect it to be such a coincidence; the child came from Xingfu Village, the very place where his older brother had stayed when he was sent to the countryside.","Later, he found out that their mother had died early, their father was unknown, and they had been adopted by their uncle.","He was originally very worried that the children might have a hard time living under someone else's roof.","He was afraid that the children appearing in the newspaper was a publicity stunt by their adoptive parents for profit, wanting to use the children to make money.","So he specifically found a reporter to pay them a visit.","But the result was beyond his expectations.","The children's uncle and his wife treated the children very well.","However, before he could investigate further, he had to return to Beijing due to work reasons.","To better understand the children's situation, he sent Fang Hui, who was a reporter, to Yungui City, and even bought the house next door to the Zhou family.","Since then, he had continuously had people looking into the children's situation.","Only then did he know that they were living very well and were very happy.","Naturally, Xiao Yi had no desire to tear their current family apart, which was why he had quietly taken his son and walked away. He had anticipated that his mother might eventually discover his older brother's illegitimate child, but he never expected them to cross paths this soon. As for Xiao Bowen, he had only come upstairs to ask his father a question. Little did he know, he would end up overhearing such an earth-shattering revelation."]},{"number":409,"title":"Chapter 409: Biological Father","paragraphs":["Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan were actually the children of his father's older brother.","How could this be?","He wasn't an ignorant child, and he knew exactly what this meant.","Didn't this mean that he and they were cousins?","Xiao Bowen's mind was a mess.","He wasn't in the right state of mind at school the next day.","He didn't even react when the teacher called on him to answer a question.","This caused his classmates to cast a few extra glances his way.","Zhou Zedong also looked at him and frowned slightly.","How could someone as serious and studious as Xiao Bowen not pay attention in class?","When the bell rang for the end of class, Zhou Zedong took out the book he had borrowed and continued reading.","It contained some experimental procedures.","He had read quite a bit, but he didn't have any of the tools. Just as he was hesitating about where to find these things to do the experiments, he was interrupted by a voice filled with complex emotions.","\"Classmate Zhou Zedong.\"","He looked up; it was Xiao Bowen.","Stopping his reading, he asked, \"Is something the matter?\"","Xiao Bowen carefully scrutinized Zhou Zedong. Previously, when he visited his great-grandfather, he had seen a family portrait on his nightstand.","At the time, he had asked his father who the person standing next to him was and why he had never seen him before.","His father had gently replied that it was his uncle.","He heard that his uncle had gone to a very faraway place.","To put it bluntly, he was already dead.","Xiao Bowen wasn't a three-year-old child; how could he not understand what that meant?","His uncle was very tall and handsome, even better-looking than his father.","His facial features were particularly striking, and his father had also said that his uncle was a genius.","No wonder Zhou Zedong was better than him, and his sister was so amazing too.","As for Zhou Zehan, he had already ruled him out; maybe he was picked up from somewhere, otherwise why would he be so stupid?","Thinking back like this, Xiao Bowen realized that Zhou Zedong looked a lot like his uncle.","He was practically a child version of his uncle.","If that were really the case, wouldn't he have to call him older brother?","A look of refusal flashed across Xiao Bowen's face.","He couldn't help but ask, \"Classmate Zhou Zedong, is Uncle Zhou not your biological father?\"","Zhou Zedong frowned. \"What do you mean?\"","Xiao Bowen said, \"Because you don't look very much like Uncle Zhou.\"","Zhou Zedong's frown deepened. \"How do we not look alike? My mom said I look like my dad.\"","Xiao Bowen: \"I've heard all about it. You were adopted. Since you're not his biological son, how could you look like him?\"","The fact that Zhou Zedong was adopted wasn't a secret. Most people knew about it; after all, Si Nian was only nineteen years old, so there was no way she could have a son as old as him.","However, Zhou Zedong remained quite calm. \"My mom wouldn't lie to me.\"","Xiao Bowen was speechless. Did he just believe whatever his mom said?","Teacher Si was definitely just coaxing him.","\"Then where did your biological father go?\"","Zhou Zedong frowned. \"Why are you asking this?\"","\"I'm just curious. You're so amazing, your dad must be really amazing too, right?\" Xiao Bowen had seen many trophies in the study at home.","Those all belonged to his uncle.","It seemed he was a very powerful and important figure when he was alive.","Thinking about how Zhou Zedong's adoptive father was already so impressive, and now his biological father was amazing too.","He was even more impressive than his own father, and he himself couldn't beat him. This left a bad taste in Xiao Bowen's mouth.","But when he remembered that Zhou Zehan was much stupider than him, he felt better again.","One floor away, the little second brother sneezed twice.","Jiang Jiu asked worriedly, \"Second Brother, what's wrong? Did you catch a cold?\"","Zhou Zehan said with inexplicable confidence, \"Of course not. It must be my mom missing me.\"","Jiang Jiu: \"...\"","Back upstairs.","His father was very amazing?","Zhou Zedong subconsciously tried to recall, but only dug up fragments of memories from the darkest corners of his mind.","However, the memories were very blurry. He only remembered that the man had given him a few books, which he loved reading.","His mother would also become very gentle. He couldn't remember her exact appearance, only that as soon as the man left, his mother would beat him like a madwoman. He would hold his younger brother, who couldn't even speak yet, and hide in the corner, his skin torn and flesh gaping. It hurt so much being beaten, as if he were going to die.","He immediately covered his head, unwilling to think about it anymore.","Xiao Bowen was frightened by his reaction. \"Are... are you okay? If you don't want to talk about it, forget it.\"","After saying that, he turned and ran back to his seat.","...","Si Nian hadn't been to the dorms much these past few days. Because of the incident with Lu Yao, it was quite awkward.","On her way back from buying groceries after class, she purposely sought out the so-called haunted house.","Truth be told, the location of this haunted house was quite good, facing south to north, but it was very dilapidated because it hadn't been cleaned for years.","In Si Nian's eyes, this wasn't a haunted house; this was a future one hundred million.","However, the house had already been sealed off, with paper seals pasted on the outside.","Si Nian looked at it curiously for a while before being interrupted by someone. \"Don't even think about going inside to look, girl. It's really creepy in there.\"","Si Nian turned around and saw a few women who were also carrying groceries.","She asked, \"Creepy?\"","\"Yes, I heard that even though the body was found a long time ago, people can still smell the rotting stench blowing out from inside. Tell me, isn't that scary?\"","\"One look and I can tell you're new here. I heard a few days ago that someone had moved in, but this is the first time I've seen you.\"","Si Nian smiled and nodded. \"Because I have to attend school, I don't have much time to wander around.\"","\"So you're a student! Which university do you go to?\"","\"The nearby Jing University.\"","Hearing that she studied at Jing University, the women looked at her differently.","With faces full of admiration, they said, \"You're so impressive, getting into such a good university.\"","\"If you're scared, take another route in the future. Don't walk this way anymore.\"","\"I heard that the murderer, Wang Ergou, just got released from prison. You need to be careful.\"","Si Nian nodded.","Walking and chatting with the group, she asked, \"I heard someone went missing here before, is it true?\"","\"Of course it's true. The whole thing is very mysterious. The man who went missing was having an affair with that widow. I heard they were always flirting, and he was completely bewitched by her. He even wanted to divorce his wife for her.\"","Si Nian was surprised. \"Is that family still here?\"","\"Of course they are. Oh, I remember her house isn't far from yours. That woman is pitiful too. She married into the family when she was seventeen or eighteen, and because she couldn't have children, she was always despised by her in-laws. Her husband used this as an excuse to fool around outside all day and demand a divorce. In those days, divorced women had no way to survive. If Widow Liu hadn't had an accident, they probably would have divorced long ago. Everyone says he was lured away by Widow Liu.\"","\"If you ask me, he got what he deserved. It's just a pity for his parents. Still, Xiao Song has a good conscience, willing to stay and fulfill her filial duties to them. She hasn't remarried all these years.\"","\"Xiao Song is too honest. If it were any other woman, she would have run away long ago.\"","\"But her husband's family was quite wealthy. They left behind a lot of property. She used the money to open a few shops over the past few years and actually made quite a bit.\"","\"What are you guys talking about?\"","As the women were talking, a voice suddenly sounded from behind them.","Everyone turned around and saw Song Zhaodi standing behind them, carrying a bamboo basket. They didn't know when she had arrived.","Startled, they were just about to say something when Si Nian interrupted, \"I just met these aunties and we were getting to know each other.\""]},{"number":410,"title":"Chapter 410: Business Trip","paragraphs":["The few of them snapped back to reality and quickly smiled, \"Right, right, right, this is our first time meeting Comrade Si. This girl is really beautiful!\"","They thought Si Nian said this because she was afraid of bringing up bad memories for Song Zhaodi, so they couldn't help but praise her for being considerate. If she hadn't said anything, they probably would have blurted it out.","It was all in the past anyway, and it wasn't good to bring up someone's sad affairs.","Song Zhaodi walked over to them. \"I was worried that she was too young and wouldn't have anything to talk about with everyone, but it seems I was overthinking it.\"","Si Nian returned home and frowned.","She didn't know if she had watched too much Detective Conan, which made her overly cautious, but she always felt that the person with the least criminal tendency was the most likely to be the culprit.","But ten years ago, hadn't Song Zhaodi just married into the family for barely two years?","Not having a child after two years of marriage was already a huge taboo in this era.","No wonder her husband wanted a divorce.","And her name, just hearing it made it obvious that her family's situation probably wasn't very good.","Si Nian couldn't ask too much about this kind of thing, nor could she make it too obvious. Otherwise, if the real criminal was right next to her, it would be dangerous.","Si Nian thought that she shouldn't rush this matter. She would wait for Zhou Yueshen to come back and ask him to find someone to investigate it first.","To avoid arousing suspicion, Si Nian didn't ask about this matter again.","Song Zhaodi was quite enthusiastic and would often ask her to go grocery shopping together.","Xiao Bowen couldn't get anything out of Zhou Zedong, so he thought about asking Zhou Zehan about his father.","Zhou Zedong always ignored him and didn't like to talk.","He couldn't ask him anything at all.","But Zhou Zehan was different. He was so talkative; he would definitely tell him everything as soon as he asked.","Xiao Bowen went to Zhou Zehan's class and was dumbfounded when he saw him.","They hadn't seen each other for only two months, and Zhou Zehan was actually taller than him?","He looked in astonishment at Zhou Zehan, who was nearly half a shoulder taller than him, his small face flashing with disbelief.","How could someone grow so tall all of a sudden?","\"Ah, Fang Bowen, are you looking for me?\" Second Child was very excited to see him.","\"My name is Xiao Bowen now, not Fang Bowen,\" Xiao Bowen corrected him.","\"Ah, you changed your surname to your father's?\"","Xiao Bowen nodded.","\"Let me ask you, have you ever met your father?\"","\"Of course I have. I even ran eight kilometers with my dad this morning.\"","After he finished speaking, he shook his legs, which still felt a bit sore.","Xiao Bowen: \"...I'm asking about your biological father.\"","\"Biological father?\" Second Child froze for a moment, a flash of confusion in his eyes. \"Biological father? Do I have a biological father? Didn't my mom say I popped out of a rock?\"","Xiao Bowen: \"...Forget it, pretend I didn't ask.\"","With that, he turned and left.","He now understood why Zhou Zehan had grown so tall.","Because his brains had all gone into his height.","Second Child looked baffled.","When he went home in the afternoon, he was still wondering about this question.","He couldn't help but ask his brother, \"Big brother, did I really pop out of a rock?\"","Zhou Zedong paused while reading his book. \"What do you mean?\"","\"I'm just curious. I asked my classmates, and they were all born to their moms and dads. But I wasn't born to my current mom and dad, so where did my previous mom and dad go?\"","Zhou Zedong withdrew his gaze and said lightly, \"You don't have a mom and dad. You popped right out of a rock. I saw it with my own eyes.\"","Zhou Zehan: \"...\"","When he got home, he found Si Nian and said apologetically, \"Mom, I shouldn't have doubted you. My brother said I really did pop out of a rock.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian couldn't help but laugh. \"That's what your brother said?\"","Second Child: \"Yes, he said he saw it with his own eyes.\"","\"Mom, are my mom and dad really rocks? Doesn't that mean I'm different from my classmates?\"","He thought about the story of Journey to the West that his mom had told him before, where Sun Wukong popped out of a rock.","But Sun Wukong was a monkey. Could it be that he was also a monkey?","Si Nian paused. Why was Second Child suddenly curious about his mom and dad?","She actually didn't know much about his parents either. After all, his mother had died early, and it wasn't described in the novel.","Talking about the deceased would only add to the sadness.","So she said, \"Well... how should I put it? You'll know when you grow up.\"","Second Child nodded. \"No wonder I'm different from my classmates. I run faster than them, and I know how to make Mom happy, while they only know how to make their moms cry.\"","As he spoke, he even started to look smug.","Si Nian smiled and rubbed his head. This optimistic personality was really nice. How did he end up becoming a gangster in the book?","When Zhou Yueshen came back at night, Si Nian told him about the murder case nearby.","Hearing her say that she suspected Wang Ergou might not be the real killer, Zhou Yueshen's expression also grew a bit more solemn.","He was just preparing to go on a business trip with Chen Nan for a few days, and didn't expect to hear about this.","Although ten years had passed, since Si Nian was suspicious, it was a hidden danger for them.","\"How about we move away? The houses we bought before are all empty. We can change places.\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"Wouldn't that be even weirder? We just moved here, and the furniture and everything are just set up. Moving again would be too troublesome.\"","This location was actually very good. It was right near the university, and the surrounding schools were all relatively good.","In the future, this would definitely be a prime school district house.","Right now, it was just because the houses here were old, plus the previous rumors about this kind of thing, some people had moved away, and the houses couldn't be sold. So the rumors spread wider and wider, and not many people moved in, which was why it was so deserted.","Zhou Yueshen naturally knew this too, but he wouldn't feel at ease if he wasn't at home.","This business trip was to discuss business, and he would be gone for several days.","He came back tonight just to hear Si Nian talk about this.","But now he couldn't settle his mind.","He said in a deep voice, \"What you say makes sense. I have to leave in the middle of the night later. Before I go, I'll contact someone to keep an eye on you all. Try to interact with them less during this time.\"","\"How many days will you be gone?\"","Zhou Yueshen replied, \"This collaboration is quite big, so Old Chen handed it over to me. It will probably take three or four days.\"","Si Nian nodded, able to understand. He was already so busy running the breeding farm, and now coming to Beijing to do business, there was no way it would be easy.","Si Nian told him not to worry, she knew what she was doing.","She told him to wake her up when he left.","At four in the morning, Zhou Yueshen got dressed and came to the bedside, but he couldn't bear to wake the sleeping Si Nian.","Even though she had emphasized it repeatedly, it was still early, and she had to go to class later.","Zhou Yueshen brushed aside the hair on Si Nian's cheek, gently kissed her smooth, fair forehead, and then went to his daughter's room.","Unexpectedly, Yaoyao was awake. Rubbing her eyes, she called out groggily, \"Daddy, pee-pee.\" As she spoke, she let out a big yawn. Zhou Yueshen smiled and rubbed her head, picked the child up to go to the toilet, and then directly took her to Si Nian's room. He placed her on the bed, tucked her in, and said in a low voice, \"Be good, don't wake Mommy up.\"","Yaoyao nodded obediently, closed her eyes, and fell back asleep.","Zhou Yueshen closed the door and went to his two sons' room. The two originally had separate rooms, but the Second Child was too scared to get up and use the bathroom at night, so he had stubbornly moved into his older brother's room again.","Right now, he was sleeping sprawled out on his back with one leg draped over his brother, the blanket nowhere to be seen.","Zhou Yueshen pulled the blanket up to cover the two children, walked out, patted Da Huang's head, and left.","...","As soon as he arrived at the factory, he said to Chen Nan, who was on the phone, \"Old Chen, come out here. I need to talk to you about something.\"","Old Chen's heart skipped a beat. He had a bad feeling about this."]},{"number":411,"title":"Chapter 411: Sudden Apology","paragraphs":["At six o'clock in the morning, Si Nian woke up. It was only after she got up that she realized Yaoyao was beside her, and her man was gone. She threw off the quilt and got out of bed.","Zhou Yueshen had already left.","Si Nian ran her fingers through her hair and went to the living room. A delicious aroma was wafting from the kitchen; Zhou Zedong was making breakfast.","Just then, he walked out carrying a dish. Seeing Si Nian, he said, Mom, I made noodles today.","This was the hand-pulled noodles Si Nian had taught him to make, kneading the dough himself.","He had made it a few times before, and the children all loved it.","Now he had learned to do it quite decently. He could even fry an egg in the shape of a heart, sprinkled with chopped green onions. The clear broth noodles with floating oil droplets were coated with rich soup in every bite.","Where is Dad? Usually, Zhou Yueshen got up earlier than Si Nian, but he was nowhere to be seen today.","Si Nian replied, Dad went on a business trip.","Then I made too much. Zhou Zedong frowned.","Having lacked food since childhood, even knowing that their family was well-off now, he would not waste food.","Si Nian cast her eyes down. Because Zhou Yueshen had a big appetite, Little Dong had cooked a huge bowl.","They definitely couldn't finish it. It's a pity for these noodles, let's give them to Da Huang.","That was the only way, otherwise, it wouldn't taste good if kept until the afternoon, and they always ate lunch at the cafeteria.","Si Nian went into the room to wash Yaoyao's face and braid her hair, then changed her clothes, put on her little backpack, and took her downstairs.","The little girl was so sleepy she could barely open her eyes, but Si Nian couldn't let her stay in bed now, as she was a kindergartener after all.","Kindergartens nowadays didn't teach much. Although called kindergartens, they were actually just places where people who couldn't take care of their children at home sent them for the teachers to watch over.","So the things Yaoyao learned there were very boring.","Fortunately, Si Nian would prepare some homework for her in advance, like practicing writing strokes and pinyin, for her to do at school.","No matter how smart she was, she still needed to practice the basics well.","Otherwise, writing characters that looked like chicken scratches wouldn't be good.","Second Child had also started practicing his handwriting now. His handwriting was truly too ugly, to the point where he couldn't even recognize it himself when he looked back at it.","So Si Nian also required him to practice writing for half an hour every day.","These past few days, Zhou Yueshen had told them not to come into contact with outsiders, so Si Nian only went to school and picked up the children.","Because of this, she hadn't been to the dormitory for several days.","With Zhou Yueshen away for a few days, the house was also quieter. The sound of Second Child crying for his parents while being supervised by his dad practicing martial arts could no longer be heard.","At first, Si Nian was just a little unaccustomed to it, but when she went to sleep at night and subconsciously reached out, she touched nothing.","After sleeping in a man's arms for a long time, his sudden disappearance really took some getting used to.","So Si Nian brought Yaoyao to her room to sleep with her daughter.","The fragrant and soft little dumpling was much more comfortable to hold than the old man.","Three days after Zhou Yueshen left, Si Nian heard that Wang Ergou had been released.","Previously, he had failed to steal from their house and instead fell from the wall, breaking his head.","After being taken to the hospital, he stayed for a few days, but then ran off to steal again because he had no money, and was caught once more.","This time he was detained for a few days.","Now that he was out, he was sneaking around in the alley.","Si Nian saw him on her way home.","When the other party turned around and saw her, he shuddered in fear and ran away as fast as his legs could carry him.","Si Nian looked left and right. There was no one around her, what was he afraid of?","Did she look terrifying?","How strange. He was scared unconscious by Da Huang before, and now he ran over again. Couldn't he see such a big dog tied up in her yard?","If you say he wasn't afraid, he fainted from fright the first time he came.","If you say he was afraid, he dared to come again.","She couldn't figure out this thief's thoughts.","Could it be that he came to apologize?","Si Nian was amused by her own thought.","However, she didn't expect that in the afternoon, someone knocked on the door. Comrade Xiao Si, why is there fruit at your door? Who brought it for you?","Why don't you take it in? Otherwise, it would be a loss if someone else took it.","It was a few aunties she had met on the road earlier.","Si Nian confusedly picked up the bag, opened it, and saw a few oranges.","There was also a crumpled piece of paper inside. She opened it and saw a crookedly written sentence.","I'm sorry, I didn't mean to climb your wall on purpose. I just went the wrong way, I hope you don't blame me. — Wang Ergou.","Si Nian was speechless. He really came to apologize?","The women asked curiously, Is it for your family?","Si Nian nodded. Seeing that they looked like they were here for a visit, she quickly asked, Are you aunties looking for me for something?","They smiled and said, Nothing much, just came to take a look. I saw your family moving in a while ago, and there were always cars hauling things over. You must have bought a lot of good things.","Yes, I saw them hauling bricks over too. The road around here was full of potholes, and I saw him hauling sand to fill them. We used to fall when riding our bicycles here, but now it's very flat.","The other person sighed with emotion, Speaking of this, we really have to thank Comrade Xiao Si's man. That road hasn't been repaired for a long time, and no one was willing to spend money on it.","Yes, we just came to thank you, but we don't have anything good at home, so we brought you some rice and eggs.","You're all too polite. That was also because it was hard for us to haul things in, so we filled it up. Who knows when the main road will be fixed.","They were also doing it for their own convenience.","Please come in and sit down.","Since the neighbors had come to visit, Si Nian couldn't let them stand outside talking, so she led them into the house.","As soon as they entered, they saw Da Huang lying under the tree, and almost dropped the eggs in their hands from fright.","Oh my goodness, such a big dog.","Is this raised for eating?","Da Huang was speechless.","Si Nian felt a sweat drop.","No, it's raised to guard the house and yard.","True, if it were me, I wouldn't dare eat such a big dog either.","Entering the house, everyone was stunned. The Zhou family's house was cleaned so well; the floor was shiny, and the cement floor was reflecting light.","Seeing Si Nian changing her shoes, the group didn't know what to do.","They weren't this particular.","Comrade Xiao Si, your house is cleaned too well. Should we also change our shoes?","Another auntie blushed and said, My feet smell a bit, I hope you don't mind.","Si Nian hadn't expected anyone to visit, and hearing this made her feel a bit awkward.","She rubbed her nose and said, It's fine, you don't need to change. My house is mainly this clean because we have a lot of kids who like to play on the floor.","Actually, it was because Second Child, trained by his dad, cleaned the house whenever he had nothing to do, making it this clean.","Cleaning every day, how could it not be clean?","Everyone looked around and saw everything neatly arranged. There were beautiful patterned cushions on the sofa, and the TV cabinet was covered with gauze. The windows also had matching gauze curtains.","It was both beautiful and kept the dust out."]},{"number":412,"title":"Chapter 412: Enjoy Life","paragraphs":["The most unbelievable part was that the house actually smelled incredibly fragrant.","They considered themselves quite hygienic normally, but being this clean was basically impossible.","The little mud monkeys at home would mess everything up in a matter of seconds.","But Si Nian's house was not only clean, it was also exquisite and beautiful.","The natural wood-colored cabinets paired with the white sheer curtains looked premium and gorgeous.","Everyone couldn't take their eyes off it.","A feeling of being unsophisticated country bumpkins, completely out of place, spontaneously arose in their hearts.","Originally, they had just wanted to drop by and say hello, but now they were looking here and touching there, reluctant to leave.","They were all getting on in years, their rough edges long smoothed out by the grind of life.","Seeing a house like this now, they couldn't help but recall their youth, when they too had imagined a beautiful life after marriage.","It would probably be something like this.","So there really were people who could live their lives like a poem.","\"Sister Wang, look quickly, Si's house even has a bathtub!\"","\"Wow, taking a bath in that must be so comfortable.\"","\"Si, you really know how to enjoy life.\"","Everyone clicked their tongues in praise.","\"Aunt Liu, Aunt Wang, you're here too.\"","As they were talking, Song Zhaodi stood at the door and greeted them with a smile.","Seeing her carrying a basket with vegetables inside, she must have just come back from grocery shopping.","She went grocery shopping at this time every day; she was very particular about it.","\"Oh, Xiao Song, you're here. Look, Si's house is so exquisite and beautiful. Just looking at it makes me feel comfortable.\"","\"That's because Si's man is willing to spoil her. A while ago, I saw him running around buying these things. This bathing area must have been built after they moved here. Look at all these things, which one didn't cost a lot of money?\"","\"Yes, yes, the young couple is just so happy.\"","Si Nian just smiled awkwardly. After they finished their tour, she wanted to invite them to stay for a meal, but they all quickly scurried away.","After they left, Song Zhaodi said, \"Sister Si, did you hear? Wang Ergou is out again.\"","Si Nian paused. \"Is that so?\"","\"Yes, I heard he was only locked up for a few days this time before being released. You have to be careful. Last time I saw him get injured at your place, I'm afraid he might come to take revenge on you. Your man isn't home, right?\"","Si Nian's eyes flickered, and she said, \"He should be back in a day or two. Don't worry, Sister Song.\"","Song Zhaodi smiled, \"Then I'll go back to cook first. Remember to lock your doors well when you sleep at night.\"","Si Nian responded with a sound of agreement.","As soon as she turned around, her smile vanished.","Why was Song Zhaodi paying so much attention to Wang Ergou?","If Wang Ergou was really as she described, would there be any need for him to specifically write a little note to apologize?","From a person's words, you can more or less see their true nature.","Wang Ergou looked timid and afraid of trouble at first glance, and he even knew how to apologize?","Would a chronic thief apologize?","Furthermore, Song Zhaodi knew exactly when he went in and when he came out.","Could she be keeping tabs on him privately?","Why would she be paying attention to this person?","Those aunts just now hadn't even mentioned this matter.","As expected, the case from ten years ago must definitely be connected to Song Zhaodi.","...","After Zhou Zedong finished class, he first went to pick up his younger sister, and then waited at the gate for his younger brother.","He didn't wait for his brother, but instead waited for Xiao Bowen.","Xiao Bowen was being led by a woman in her fifties or sixties. He had been seeing this woman often lately. It was because this person would always stare at him with a complicated look in her eyes.","Xiao Bowen stepped forward and said, \"Zhou Zedong, let's go to the library to play Gomoku. We didn't decide a winner last time.\"","Zhou Zedong flatly refused, \"No.\"","Xiao Bowen frowned, \"Why?\"","Zhou Zedong said, \"I'm going home.\"","Their father wasn't home these past few days, and their mother had instructed him to come straight home after class.","Yaoyao was sucking on a fruit candy. Hearing about playing a game, she perked up, tugged at Zhou Zedong's sleeve, and said, \"Brother, I want to play too.\"","\"No, Mom said we have to go home early. If we go back late, Mom will be angry.\"","\"When we get home, I'll play with you.\"","Thinking of her mother, Yaoyao immediately nodded obediently.","Compared to playing a game, she wanted even less for her mother to be angry.","Seeing that neither of the siblings paid attention to him, Xiao Bowen felt a bit hurt.","Even though he was also a younger brother, Zhou Zedong wasn't nice to him at all.","Although they weren't blood brothers, he had looked it up; it was called being cousins, which wasn't much different from being real brothers.","Grandma Xiao, who was standing to the side, walked over and smiled, \"Xiao Bowen wants to play chess with his classmate.\"","Xiao Bowen nodded dejectedly.","He had found many other people to play with since then, but those people were too stupid.","They would lose in just a few minutes.","Only Zhou Zedong could play with him for a long time.","So he wanted to play with him.","\"Isn't that simple? Grandma will take you to his house to play, and then pick you up to go home tonight.\"","\"You guys are good friends, right?\"","Xiao Bowen: \"...\"","It seemed they couldn't even be considered friends.","Zhou Zedong also looked at Grandma Xiao with an odd gaze.","Where did she get the idea that they were good friends?","At this moment, Second Child and Jiang Jiu came skipping out.","\"Brother, brother, Xiao Jiang said he wants to sleep at our house tonight, let's go home! Mom will definitely be happy to see Xiao Jiang.\"","\"Big brother, look, this is the globe model my dad asked me to give you, it's even bigger than mine!\"","Jiang Jiu dug out the globe model from his backpack and handed it to Zhou Zedong.","Zhou Zedong was stunned for a moment, then carefully reached out and took it.","Jiang Jiu seeing how much he liked it, immediately straightened his neck, puffed two breaths out of his nostrils, and started acting smug.","Sure enough, even the hardest-to-get-along-with big brother would fall for his charm.","\"Thank you, Xiao Jiu.\"","\"Big brother, you are my own big brother, don't be so polite with me.\"","Jiang Jiu said very generously.","Zhou Zedong patted his head and said, \"Let's go.\"","Looking at his attitude towards Jiang Jiu, and then thinking about his attitude towards himself.","Xiao Bowen felt a bitter taste in his heart.","He lowered his head in dismay. Even though his grandma said he could go to the Zhou family's house to play.","But he didn't have the courage.","Because it seemed like none of them really liked playing with him.","Just as he didn't know what to do, Zhou Zehan finally noticed him and said loudly, \"Aren't you Fang Bowen? What are you doing here?\"","\"My name is Xiao Bowen,\" Xiao Bowen corrected him patiently.","\"Oh, oh, right, you changed your name. What are you doing here?\"","\"I-I'm not doing anything.\" Xiao Bowen twisted his body away, turning his back to them.","Grandma Xiao looked lovingly at the children with a smile, her eyes slightly red.","\"Little Bowen wants to go to your house and play Gomoku with you all. I wonder if you could take him to play? Auntie will buy you candy.\"","Second Child said, \"Of course he can. I lost to him before, but times have changed, and I won't lose again. Today I must beat him!\"","He waved his fist.","Grandma Xiao smiled and said, \"Alright, Auntie will take you home.\"","After saying that, a luxury car drove over, and the driver got out to open the door for them.","Second Child exaggeratedly opened his mouth wide, \"Wow, Xiao Bowen, you even have a private car to pick you up now?\"","Xiao Bowen felt proud in his heart, but said disdainfully with his mouth, \"It's nothing, my family has too many cars like this.\"","After saying that, he fell silent for a moment, and whispered: \"...You guys have them too.\"","Second Child didn't understand what that meant, and he leaned against the car window with Jiang Jiu.","\"Brother, look! The people outside are all staring at us.\"","Zhou Zedong sat on the other side holding his younger sister, his brows furrowed.","He had originally wanted to refuse, but before the words could leave his mouth, his younger brother and Jiang Jiu had already found their seats and were waving at him. \"Brother, hurry up and get in! You and sister can sit here.\"","Zhou Zedong wished he could give him a good slap.","Right now, he didn't want to pay any attention to him at all.","Hearing the sound of a car, Si Nian thought Zhou Yueshen had returned.","But as soon as she stepped out the door, she saw Zhou Zedong followed by one, two, three, four little munchkins.","Second Child and Yaoyao were one thing, but what was the deal with Jiang Jiu smiling so sweetly beside them, and Xiao Bowen, whose ears were completely red as he tilted his head to look at the sky and the ground, looking everywhere but at her?"]},{"number":413,"title":"Chapter 413: The Little Boss's Experiment","paragraphs":["At this moment, a middle-aged woman dressed in elegant, expensive clothes walked over.","She looked Si Nian up and down, a hint of surprise in her eyes. \"Are you the mother of these children?\"","Si Nian asked, \"And you are?\"","Grandma Xiao replied, \"I'm Bowen's grandmother. Bowen said he wanted to play Gomoku with Little Dong, so I just brought the children back together on my way.\"","Little Dong?","Si Nian looked at her son in surprise.","Zhou Zedong also frowned.","He didn't really like strangers calling his name so affectionately.","Si Nian withdrew her gaze and smiled. \"Sorry for the trouble.\"","\"You're welcome. I heard from my son that when you were in Yunguichuan City, Xiao Bowen was well taken care of by you all.\"","Si Nian's doubts eased. So that was it.","In that case, it wasn't strange for her to help drop the kids off.","She smiled, nodded, and invited Grandma Xiao inside to sit down.","Grandma Xiao shook her head and said, \"I still have things to do, so I'll leave Bowen here to play with you. This is my phone number. If Bowen wants to go home tonight, just give me a call.\"","Si Nian agreed.","She watched the woman get into her car and leave.","Only then did she look down at the children.","Zhou Zedong pursed his lips, worried that Si Nian would blame him. After all, back in their hometown, Xiao Bowen's mother hadn't allowed Bowen to play with them, and their mother had also warned them to minimize contact. Thus, he said, \"Mom, I didn't play with him. He insisted on coming.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Bowen's little face turned bright red.","Si Nian coughed awkwardly. It was true that this child had a high IQ, but his EQ was definitely low.","No wonder he couldn't make friends.","\"It's fine. He can come if he wants to, it's not like you guys don't know each other.\"","\"Hurry up and go inside. I'll cook tonight, you just play with them.\"","The children nodded and followed her into the house.","Although Xiao Bowen had known them for a long time, it was his first time entering the Zhou family's home.","He looked around curiously until Second Child brought out the Gomoku board, which snapped him back to reality.","Under the tree in the courtyard were a stone table and stools. The children gathered around it to play Gomoku.","Zhou Zedong, however, had no interest in Gomoku. He held some tools in his hands, fiddling with something unknown.","After playing two rounds with Second Child, Xiao Bowen lost interest, but Zhou Zedong was ignoring him.","He couldn't help but ask, \"What is your brother doing? Isn't he going to play?\"","Second Child tilted his head to look and saw his brother holding two paper cups, doing who knows what.","He was also a bit puzzled. Just as he was about to ask, Jiang Jiu stared curiously and spoke up, \"Big brother, what are you doing?\"","\"Making a telephone,\" Zhou Zedong replied without looking up, looking very serious.","\"Huh? A telephone?\"","The three children instantly moved over, looking at him curiously and asking, \"Like the telephone we use at home?\"","\"Yeah.\" Zhou Zedong used a pencil to poke a small hole in the bottom of a paper cup. Then, he used scissors to cut open the straws they used to drink milk that morning, threaded one end of a cotton string through the hole in the bottom of the cup, and tied it. After a series of actions, the two paper cups were connected.","Under their curious gazes, he handed a paper cup to Second Child.","\"Try it.\"","\"Huh? How do I try it?\"","\"Take it and walk away, pull the string tight, and then put it to your ear.\"","Second Child dazedly took the paper cup and walked into the house. Seeing the string pulled taut, he placed it against his ear.","Who would have thought that his brother's voice would actually sound from inside the paper cup!","\"Can you hear me?\"","Second Child was so startled he almost threw the paper cup away.","\"Ah, brother, your voice is in the cup!\"","\"Let me listen.\" Jiang Jiu ran over, imitating Zhou Zedong's manner and speaking into the paper cup.","\"Big brother, big brother, can you hear me? Over.\"","Zhou Zedong: \"...\"","When Si Nian came out, she saw the children lying on the ground holding paper cups to their ears, listening to who knows what, occasionally saying \"Over.\"","She raised an eyebrow. Wasn't this the simple telephone experiment the teacher taught when they went to the lab as kids?","Although she had learned how to make it, she hadn't succeeded.","How did these kids manage to make it?","\"Big brother, big brother, Mom has finished cooking. Come in and eat. Over.\"","\"Copy that. Over.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","After eating, the children ran back to the room to hide and play with the simple telephone again.","Zhou Zedong had already lost interest in the thing. He flipped through a book, reading seriously. Occasionally, when he didn't know how to pronounce a few words, he would look them up in the dictionary.","Even though he read relatively slowly, he was very focused.","Xiao Bowen originally wanted to ask Zhou Zedong exactly how that telephone was made, but he didn't know how to bring it up.","Seeing the book he was reading now, it was as if he suddenly understood something.","He made up his mind. He would read too when he got back.","He absolutely could not lose to him.","Going outside, he saw Second Child practicing martial arts in the courtyard, his punches generating wind. Xiao Bowen's little face grew even more serious. It seemed he needed to exercise his body too.","He was no longer interested in Gomoku.","After the children got tired of playing, they cuddled up together and fell asleep.","Si Nian called the Xiao family to let them know, allowing the child to stay the night so they could be taken to school together the next day.","The next day, Si Nian originally planned to take the children to school first, but unexpectedly, the Xiao family's driver came over early in the morning to pick them up.","Since it was on her way, she also got in the car.","After the children entered the school, the driver dropped her off along the way.","As soon as she got out of the car, she bumped into Zhang Xue and Liu Nana.","The two stared at her in astonishment. If they weren't mistaken, that car was a very expensive Santana.","And it even had a Jing City license plate.","Wasn't Si Nian an out-of-towner?","Si Nian also saw the two of them, but she didn't have time to say much and just greeted them, \"Zhang Xue? Why are you guys just standing there? Class is about to start.\"","After saying that, she quickly ran toward the school.","Because there had been a traffic jam on the way over, she had been delayed.","It would take another ten minutes to walk from the school entrance to the classroom.","Therefore, Si Nian didn't notice their surprised gazes.","The two snapped out of it and hurriedly ran after her.","The group rushed anxiously to the classroom, only to find that all the back seats were taken, leaving only the front seats.","If this were the future, everyone would choose the good seats in the front.","But because their major's English teacher had a gap in his teeth, spit would fly everywhere whenever he lectured. Plus, he had a habit of standing right in front of the first row to teach. Word was that a student who sat there before got sprayed with spit all over their head.","The main issue was that they didn't dare complain about it.","So everyone learned their lesson, and no one was willing to sit in the very front.","When the three of them arrived, only the very last spots in the front were left.","Lu Yao had arrived early and was sitting in the row right behind them.","Seeing Lu Yao, Zhang Xue couldn't help but say, \"Lu Yao, why didn't you save seats for us? Aren't we roommates?\"","Lu Yao frowned and said displeasedly, \"Who knew you would come so late? Besides, aren't there still seats in the front?\"","Zhang Xue was a little angry. \"But we saved seats for you before.\"","\"Forget it, forget it,\" Liu Nana tugged at her. Even though Lu Yao lived in the same dorm as them, they didn't hang out together.","She was a loner who loved to study, and she wouldn't even allow them to make a single sound when they were in the dorm.","Otherwise, she would get angry.","So the two felt she was hard to get along with, and didn't interact with her much.","Naturally, their relationship wasn't considered good.","Si Nian didn't mind, casually choosing a seat to sit down.","Lu Yao glanced at her, pursed her lips, and said nothing.","Soon, the major's professor arrived.","The surroundings instantly quieted down.","She placed the cassette player on the desk and began the lecture.","Zhang Xue was unlucky; the teacher stood right next to her.","In no time, she was sprayed with a face full of spit.","When the teacher walked away, she wiped her face with a tissue, saying angrily, \"I'm so mad. Lu Yao is too selfish. I'm never saving a seat for her again.\"","Liu Nana was also a bit embarrassed and didn't know what to say.","Seeing her stay silent, Zhang Xue got even angrier.","She had just gotten her hair done yesterday, and the hairdresser had told her not to get it wet for a few days.","Now that she had been sprayed with spit by the teacher, how could she stand not washing it?","The more she thought about it, the more wronged she felt. Zhang Xue was about to cry.","Liu Nana hurriedly comforted her, telling her to endure it.","Their voices weren't loud, but the teacher still heard them.","She turned around and scolded, \"What are you arguing about? Did you hear everything clearly?\"","\"Zhang Xue, stand up and answer a question about the listening comprehension part we just did.\"","Zhang Xue's face turned pale. She had been too busy being angry to pay attention.","She stammered, unable to speak.","The English teacher sneered, \"Liu Nana, you stand up and translate.\"","Liu Nana blushed and stuttered out two sentences of translation before forgetting the rest.","\"Si Nian, you do it!\"","Si Nian frowned, stood up, and translated the content.","The English teacher glared at her and said, \"Don't think that just because your English is good, you can mess around in my class. You may sit down. You two will stand for the rest of the class.\"","The two girls stood there with flushed faces, wishing they could find a hole to crawl into.","They finally made it to the end of class. The English teacher gathered her books, then suddenly seemed to remember something and said, \"I have a few translation jobs here. The requirements are a bit high. You can do them at home, and they pay. Although it's not easy, it can improve your skills. Si Nian, what do you think?\"","As soon as she finished speaking, Lu Yao snapped her head to look at the English teacher.","She was the class monitor. Usually, the teachers would give her any opportunities first. She had also told the teacher that she wanted to be a diplomat, but the English teacher hadn't mentioned this to her.","What did this mean?","Was the English teacher planning to choose Si Nian and not her?","Lu Yao was full of indignation and clenched her fists.","Then she heard the English teacher say, \"I saw that your spoken English is very good just now. This shouldn't be difficult for you.\"","She knew about Si Nian's grades; the principal had specially mentioned them.","If such a talent was cultivated, she might even become a diplomat in the future.","Hearing her answer the question today, others might not fully understand how good her pronunciation was.","But she knew exactly how outstanding it was.","With this level of proficiency, there was no need for her to even attend class.","Si Nian saw the envious and jealous gazes from the people around her.","The stare from behind her was especially obvious.","It was Lu Yao's.","Actually, this job wasn't important to her.","Translation work was tiring, troublesome, and demanding.","Especially in this era, not many people could do it, and ordinary people couldn't even get this kind of opportunity.","If she did well now, maybe they could have a long-term cooperation in the future.","When teachers selected students, it was mostly to mentor and promote them. Such opportunities were rare.","Someone like Si Nian, who had teaching experience, excellent college entrance exam scores, and a high level of English, could do whatever she wanted in this era—it was something others could only dream of.","However, the English teacher was quite petty.","If she refused, the teacher might hold a grudge against her in the future.","Everyone knew that in college, you could offend anyone, but you absolutely could not offend your major's professor.","Si Nian was someone who hated trouble. To avoid future trouble, she could only agree for now.","\"Teacher, I can give it a try.\"","The English teacher observed Si Nian's expression. Seeing that she didn't look reluctant or arrogant, she finally revealed a smile.","\"Good. Come to my office tomorrow, and I'll give you the assignment.\"","\"But let me make things clear first: if you don't do a good job, or if any accidents happen, you will have to take full responsibility. Even if you are my student, I won't cover for you.\"","The school term had just started, and the English teacher couldn't even remember the names of the students in the major.","Naturally, she didn't know what kind of person Si Nian was.","So she chose to use this matter to test her. If she was merely good at studying but lacked emotional intelligence and diplomatic skills, she certainly wouldn't be suitable to be a diplomat.","Si Nian nodded and agreed, \"I understand. Thank you, Teacher, for giving me this opportunity.\"","\"You're welcome,\" the English teacher said, preparing to leave.","Right then, someone spoke up. \"Teacher, shouldn't such an important opportunity be offered fairly to the other students? If you just give it directly to Si Nian, won't everyone have objections?\"","The English teacher's expression remained indifferent. \"Fairness? When you enter society, will society give you fair choices? In my eyes, only the most outstanding students can get opportunities, and it's the same in the real world. You aren't three-year-olds; don't you understand such a simple principle?\"","Lu Yao bit her lip tightly.","It was clearly the English teacher playing favorites. This was school; what did it have to do with entering society?","If they competed fairly, she didn't think she would lose to Si Nian.","Si Nian only had better college entrance exam scores than her, but that didn't mean she couldn't beat her in college.","If she didn't fight for it, an opportunity like this would never come to her.","\"Teacher, I just think that being outstanding is one thing, but being suitable is another. Who's to say other students couldn't do it better?\"","The English teacher fell silent for a moment. \"By 'other students,' do you mean yourself? Then rest assured, I can easily tell that your level is not as good as Si Nian's. I didn't want to say this because I wanted to save you some face, but you insist on being pretentious and asking for trouble. If you really want a reason, then I'll tell you: that is the reason.\"","Previously, she had more or less selected the more outstanding students in the class to answer questions.","She could see clearly whose level was high and whose was low.","Lu Yao's face turned completely red.","Being told to her face by the teacher that she was inferior to someone else was a tremendous insult to her.","However, the people around her didn't feel sorry for her. The English teacher's sharp tongue was no joke; she had scolded at least eighty, if not a hundred, students to tears.","Lu Yao, relying on her status as class monitor and her good grades, had questioned the teacher's choice, so it was no surprise she got scolded.","The teacher definitely had her reasons for choosing whomever she chose.","\"Of course, if you insist that you are capable, I can give you an opportunity too.\"","\"Come to my office tomorrow afternoon, and I will give you an assignment as well.\"","With that, the teacher left.","Lu Yao clenched her fists. The humiliation from just a moment ago vanished, and she even felt a bit delighted.","Because she had fought for it, she had obtained this opportunity.","She shot Si Nian a provocative look."]},{"number":414,"title":"Chapter 414: Secretly Giving My Heart","paragraphs":["Si Nian: \"...\"","What kind of situation was this? She used to be a teacher, after all, and her previous company required long-term communication with foreigners.","Therefore, her spoken translation skills were rock solid. Being made to compete with a college freshman right now—it wasn't that Si Nian was overly confident, but she genuinely felt it would be an unfair victory and unjust to Lu Yao.","Unfortunately, the English teacher wasn't easy to fool, otherwise Si Nian really wouldn't want this opportunity.","Giving it to Lu Yao would have saved her the trouble.","\"Si Nian, don't worry, you can definitely do it.\"","Seeing her expression, Liu Nana thought she was worried about not doing a good job.","Si Nian sighed.","She wasn't worried about herself; she was worried for Lu Yao.","If Lu Yao didn't get selected, would she come looking for trouble with her?","Interpersonal relationships were truly too complicated.","Watching her head home weighed down by her thoughts, the two roommates exchanged a glance.","\"It really is because of Lu Yao. Si Nian doesn't even come to the dorm anymore,\" Zhang Xue couldn't help but say.","Previously, Lu Yao had been saying in the dorm that Si Nian didn't like studying, but who knew Si Nian would get a perfect score in English, doing even better than her.","After that, the relationship between the two had inexplicably become a bit delicate.","Now, Lu Yao not only refused to save seats for them but also blatantly fought for the opportunity the teacher had given Si Nian.","It was obviously directed at her.","It was only because Si Nian had a good temper. If it were her, she would have been furious.","\"But Sister Si Nian is something else too. She's already so rich, why does she still do this kind of work? It offends people, not to mention it's troublesome.\" Thinking of the car Si Nian had taken that morning, Zhang Xue couldn't help but add.","Liu Nana told her to keep her voice down.","The two had just finished class and were about to head back to the dorm when they ran into an acquaintance.","Seeing it was Chen Haoran, Liu Nana nudged Zhang Xue beside her.","Zhang Xue blushed and hurriedly adjusted her newly styled hair.","She didn't expect such good luck. She had just gotten a new hairstyle, and Chen Haoran had come to find her.","Actually, Chen Haoran wasn't very close to them. They had met on the train. At the time, Chen Haoran saw someone rummaging through their bags and warned them, which was how the group got acquainted.","Chen Haoran dressed fashionably and looked handsome; he was the currently popular \"pretty boy\" type.","They heard he had been out traveling and was getting ready to return to Beijing to report to school. Upon interacting, they realized everyone was a student going to Beijing to enroll.","So they started chatting.","Chen Haoran was a local, familiar with the surroundings, and very enthusiastically helped them.","As they spent time together, a bit of romantic ambiguity developed between the two of them.","He was handsome, came from a wealthy family, and went to the same school as her.","Zhang Xue had no reason not to be smitten.","By now, she had already secretly given him her heart.","All that was left was to officially confirm their relationship.","However, Chen Haoran was handsome, and many girls had their eyes on him.","Just on the day of the mixer dance, several women went up to talk to him.","Zhang Xue was still very panicked inside, which was why she anxiously bought new clothes and got her hair done, just to show her best side to Chen Haoran.","Now, seeing him come to find her, she was naturally incredibly surprised and delighted.","\"Haoran, what brings you here?\"","She stepped forward to greet him, but before she could ask if he was looking for her for something...","She saw Chen Haoran looking left and right, not resting his gaze on her at all. \"Hey, where's Sister Nian? Isn't she with you guys?\"","Zhang Xue's smile froze. \"Si Nian?\"","Chen Haoran said, \"Yeah, isn't she with you?\"","\"She... she went home. Why are you looking for her?\"","Zhang Xue knew Si Nian was too beautiful. In just these few days since school started, many people had already come to ask them if Si Nian had a boyfriend or anything.","Wherever she passed, regardless of gender, people would stare at her.","But those people didn't know Si Nian was married, so it wasn't strange for them to stare.","But Chen Haoran knew! Why was he still paying so much attention to Si Nian?","Zhang Xue felt a bit humiliated.","Chen Haoran said, \"I originally wanted to escort her home, but I didn't expect her to have left already. Sigh, since that's the case, never mind. I'll get going first.\"","He waved his hand, turned around, and quickly walked away.","Zhang Xue's expression became even uglier.","Escort... escort Si Nian home?","Why?","Seeing her terrible expression, Liu Nana, though also a bit confused, felt it shouldn't be like that, so she comforted her, \"Could there be some misunderstanding? After all, Si Nian is already married.\"","\"What misunderstanding could there be? I can see it clearly now. Chen Haoran has definitely taken a fancy to her. He was always trying to strike up conversations with her before. At the last dance, after Si Nian left, he didn't stick around to have fun either. And now he specifically wanted to escort her home. Would he need to do all this if he didn't mean anything by it!\" After saying this, Zhang Xue cried from anger, wiping her tears as she ran upstairs.","Chen Haoran still didn't know that because of this incident, the already strained relationship among the dorm mates had completely fallen apart.","He had received a call from his dad yesterday telling him to help take care of Si Nian and the children of the Zhou family. His dad said the thief who had previously broken into her house to steal things had been released from prison, and he was worried the thief might come looking for trouble while Zhou Yueshen was away from home.","Chen Haoran was also very worried in his heart, so right after class, he hurriedly came over to find her and ask about the situation.","He didn't expect to miss her.","He walked outside and just happened to see Si Nian getting on a public bus.","He hurriedly squeezed his way on.","\"Sister, Sister! It's me.\"","Hearing the familiar voice, Si Nian looked up and saw Chen Haoran in the crowd, his face contorted from being squeezed.","Chen Haoran struggled to push his way over. Sweating profusely, he said, \"Ouch, why are you still suffering like this? Aren't Uncle Zhou and my dad making big money doing business? Yet he still makes you take the bus home. He really doesn't know how to be tender and protective of women.\"","\"Sure enough, older guys are just like this. They want a pretty wife but are reluctant to spend money. He didn't even buy you a car.\"","He complained about Zhou Yueshen.","Although Zhou Yueshen looked to be only thirty-one or thirty-two, in Chen Haoran's eyes, anyone who called his father a brother belonged to the previous generation.","Yet Si Nian, who was his classmate, had actually married someone from his father's generation.","It was a complete case of an older man going after a young girl.","And to make a girl like her take the bus—it was simply too much.","Hearing this, Si Nian laughed. \"Your Uncle Zhou's money is all with me, so what would he use to buy a car? Besides, it's only two stops from here, driving would be a hassle. As for you, please call me Auntie from now on, otherwise I'm going to tell your dad.\"","Chen Haoran looked as if he had been struck by lightning. \"Sister, I was just looking out for you. How can you turn around and blame me? Isn't calling you Auntie so unpleasant to hear? Wouldn't it make you sound so old?\"","Si Nian smiled. \"I don't mind having you as my junior.\"","Chen Haoran curled his lips. He understood now; Si Nian just wanted to pull rank on him.","Could it be because he had just spoken ill of Uncle Zhou and offended her?","What a petty woman.","\"By the way, where are you heading?\" Si Nian asked, not dwelling on the previous issue.","\"It's my dad. He said Uncle Zhou went on a business trip with him. Uncle Zhou was worried about you and the kids, so he asked me to help look after you guys. I figured I'd head over and check on you.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Sorry to trouble you, but we're doing fine.\"","\"Even if everything is fine, we can't let our guard down. I heard the thief who scaled your wall last time was released from prison. My dad did a guilty thing by selling this house to you, so as his son, it's only right that I help make up for it.\"","\"Don't worry, sis. I'll help you teach that thief a lesson so he never dares to climb your wall again.\"","\"I'm definitely not just coming over to mooch a meal off you, I promise.\"","As they spoke, the car arrived.","Not long after they got out, they ran into Wang Ergou again.","Coincidentally, the guy was in the middle of scaling a wall.","\"You little thief, how dare you climb a wall right in front of me!\"","Chen Haoran immediately rushed over and swiftly yanked Wang Ergou down from the wall.","\"Ouch!\" Wang Ergou jumped in fright. Before he could even react, Chen Haoran's heavy fist came crashing down on him.","Si Nian pulled her gaze away from the wall and stopped him. \"Wait, Chen Haoran, this isn't my house.\"","Chen Haoran paused. He looked up and was taken aback.","There, on the dilapidated red wooden door, was a tattered official seal pasted across it."]},{"number":415,"title":"Chapter 415: Climbing the Wall Again","paragraphs":["This house had already been sealed off; no one lived there anymore.","Around here, only houses where murders had occurred would have this kind of seal pasted on them.","Wang Ergou covered his face and howled.","Si Nian coughed awkwardly.","\"Are you alright?\"","Wang Ergou looked to be only twenty-seven or twenty-eight, which meant that before he went to prison, he was just seventeen or eighteen years old.","He was short and skinny, like a monkey.","His hair was very long, covering his eyes.","He had the look of a future gamer geek.","Chen Haoran used a loud voice to cover up his guilty conscience. \"Sis, even though he didn't climb our wall, climbing someone else's wall is still wrong.\"","Si Nian was also puzzled. She looked at the sickly-looking Wang Ergou. \"Your name is Wang Ergou, right?\"","Wang Ergou snapped back to reality and finally noticed Si Nian. He was startled, not expecting it to be her again.","Ever since this family moved here, he had been very unlucky. Not only was he caught every time he climbed the wall, but he also got injured every single time.","Is it really this hard to climb a wall nowadays?","However, meeting Si Nian's bright and beautiful face, he actually blushed shamefully and stammered, \"How, how do you know my name?\"","Si Nian said, \"It was written on the apology letter you wrote before.\"","Wang Ergou's face instantly turned even redder.","\"I... I really didn't mean to climb your wall. I just haven't been back for a long time and went the wrong way.\"","\"What do you mean? How could you climb the wrong wall? Where were you originally planning to go?\" Si Nian asked in return.","Wang Ergou's eyes flickered. \"Anyway, it wasn't your house. I... I'll be leaving first.\"","After saying that, he carefully looked left and right, preparing to leave.","As a result, he was grabbed by the tall and burly Chen Haoran. \"Hey, wait a minute. My sister is asking you a question, and you just try to walk away? Do you have any manners?\"","Si Nian looked at him using his size to bully others and felt a bit helpless, but she had to admit that this kind of behavior was often more intimidating.","Wang Erge turned pale with fright.","\"This family's house is sealed off, and you still climbed in. Could there be gold inside or something?\"","\"Hey, don't tell me this is the house that was haunted ten years ago!\" Chen Haoran was startled by his own guess and immediately distanced himself from the haunted house.","Si Nian broke a sweat, looked at the pale-faced Wang Ergou, and asked in a deep voice, \"I heard that the hostess of this house was accidentally killed by you?\"","Wang Ergou waved his hands in a panic. \"It wasn't me, it wasn't me at all! She was already dead when I went in. It has absolutely nothing to do with me!\"","Si Nian and Chen Haoran exchanged a glance. \"If not you, then who?\"","Wang Erge said angrily, \"If I knew, would I have gone to prison? That's what I'm investigating right now. I definitely have to catch that damn murderer! I need to clear my name.\"","\"If you're investigating, why did you climb my wall?\"","Wang Ergou said, \"I climbed the wrong one. I originally wanted to go to Song Zhaodi's house. I heard her husband also went missing.\"","\"I suspect her husband killed someone, so he ran away and made me take the blame.\"","Si Nian frowned. \"You suspect it's Song Zhaodi's husband?\"","\"That's right, it must be him!\" Wang Ergou said. \"At the time, I was drinking with a few buddies. We passed by the widow's door at night and heard the sound of a man and a woman doing... that thing. I just wanted to get a few friends to come watch a good show, but my friends were all drunk, so I went to look by myself. But when I climbed in, the person was already lying on the ground, dead.\"","\"I definitely didn't hear wrong. They all said I was drunk and lying, but I know it was definitely her man who killed her.\"","Hearing him say this, Si Nian's eyes wandered a bit. She frowned. \"How can you be so sure?\"","\"Because... because...\"","Chen Haoran asked suspiciously, \"Do you often eavesdrop on this kind of thing?\"","Wang Ergou's face instantly flushed red.","Chen Haoran had an 'I knew it' expression.","Si Nian's mouth twitched.","Wang Ergou stiffened his neck and said, \"Who told her to moan so loudly? Even the dogs passing by at night could hear it, let alone people. Over time, I can clearly distinguish whose man it is, so I definitely didn't hear wrong.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"I think I know why you were framed.\"","The two of them immediately looked at her.","Wang Ergou was even more excited. \"You believe me?\"","Si Nian said, \"Looking at your wall-climbing skills, I can tell you don't look like someone who would dare to kill.\"","Wang Ergou: \"...\" As a thief, was it really okay to insult him like this?","However, seeing that someone actually believed him right away, Wang Ergou was still very touched and actually started crying.","Si Nian and Chen Haoran were startled.","\"What are you crying for?\"","Wang Ergou wiped his tears. \"Wuwuwu, it's been so many years, and no one believed me. Only you are willing to believe me, wuwuwu... You're too kind... wuwuwu...\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Chen Haoran looked disgusted. \"Men don't shed tears lightly. Can you not be so embarrassing? But then again, if it really wasn't you, then who was it? Damn, if that's the case, the real murderer is still on the run?\"","Si Nian glanced at him. \"Didn't you say before that it wasn't him?\"","Chen Haoran said, \"I just listened to it as a story. How could I have thought it was true?\"","\"But Sis, how can you be sure this kid didn't do it? I think he looks dishonest.\"","Si Nian said, \"It's a guess. When he passed by the murder scene and saw the body, he must have screamed in fear. This sound was noticed by the murderer. At that time, the murderer hadn't had time to dispose of the body yet, and didn't know when Wang Ergou had shown up. The killer probably suspected he had been seen, but in reality, Wang Ergou didn't see anything. So, the killer found an opportunity to firmly pin it on Wang Ergou. Without having to lift a finger, he sent Wang Ergou to prison.\"","\"So...\" Si Nian glanced at the stunned Wang Ergou and said, \"Now that you're out of prison, the one in danger isn't the murderer, but you.\"","Wang Ergou's face turned pale."]},{"number":416,"title":"Chapter 416: Scared","paragraphs":["That was why he had such guts. Knowing full well he wasn't the murderer, he still loitered around the area all day. For someone like Wang Ergou, even if something really happened to him, probably no one would suspect a thing; they might even think he deserved to die.","Si Nian was genuinely worried for this poor, unlucky guy.","\"Then, then what should I do, sis?\"","Called \"sis\" and receiving a pleading look for help, Si Nian: \"...\"","\"What can you do? Suck it up!\" Chen Haoran rolled his eyes at him, looking utterly disgusted.","However, it did make him sigh in relief. Since Wang Ergou wasn't a bad guy, the things his dad worried about wouldn't happen.","Si Nian said, \"I do have an idea, but it depends on my guess being right. Just do as I say.\"","She whispered to Wang Ergou for a moment, then added, \"From now on, don't come near me. If you see me, pretend you don't know me, understand?\"","Wang Ergou obediently nodded.","After the man ran off, Chen Haoran couldn't hold back his curiosity and asked, \"Sis, what did you say to him?\"","\"It's a secret.\" Si Nian was only guessing and couldn't be sure, so she needed Wang Ergou to test it out.","Seeing that she wouldn't say, Chen Haoran grew even more curious.","Why did he get the feeling that Si Nian was masterminding everything?","It was as if she already knew who the killer was.","Yet she just wouldn't tell him, which was incredibly frustrating.","\"Alright, I'm home. You should go back. Even though you are my junior in terms of generation, you are actually older than me. Your uncle isn't home, and if I let you in and someone sees, they might start rumors.\"","Si Nian didn't let him in the house, speaking bluntly.","Chen Haoran didn't get any answers and had the door shut in his face, so he just rubbed his nose.","Although it sounded heartless, he knew Si Nian had a point.","Thus, he walked away feeling somewhat dejected.","...","The weather in Beijing was much hotter. After finishing their PE class, the children were panting heavily.","The old freezer stall was packed with people.","Second Child squeezed his way in, bought a few ice pops, and squeezed back out.","He handed them out to his older brother and younger sister.","Yaoyao took a lick and said, \"Second brother, it's so sweet!\"","Second Child was also happily sucking on his ice pop, grinning from ear to ear, \"So refreshing~\"","Zhou Zedong looked at the block of ice stuck on the wooden stick, then looked at the booming little stall. He took a bite and immediately frowned.","Wasn't this just frozen sugar water?","It was so simple, yet business was so good.","If Brother Chen and the others were here, he would definitely want to sell these.","Upon returning home, he dove straight into the kitchen, up to who knows what.","Si Nian came out yawning. Seeing that the kids were back from school, she said, \"There's food in the kitchen fridge. Just heat it up and you can eat.\"","\"Mom, it's yummy.\" Yaoyao held up her old ice pop, which had melted down to a small nub, offering it to Si Nian.","Si Nian paused for a moment, then smiled, \"Mom doesn't want any, you eat it.\"","Her room had a fan, and covering up with a blanket while the fan blew was very cool.","But outside, it was truly sweltering, at least over thirty degrees Celsius.","Yaoyao's hair was dripping wet, and her tank top was soaked.","Si Nian wiped her sweat, thinking she would need to give her a bath tonight.","She then looked up to see Second Child holding an ice pop in each hand, stuffing them into his mouth as fast as he could. She frowned and said, \"Xiaohan, don't eat too many. Eating too much cold stuff will give you a stomachache.\"","Second Child was enjoying his treat immensely. Hearing this, he immediately replied, \"This is my brother's. He didn't want it, and I couldn't bear to throw it away.\"","Si Nian sighed helplessly, \"Alright, but you can't have any more after you finish. Don't eat so many in the future, or I won't give you pocket money.\"","Zhou Zehan nodded like a woodpecker.","\"Where is your brother?\" Si Nian asked, not seeing Zhou Zedong.","\"Brother is in the kitchen. I don't know what he's doing,\" Second Child said in confusion.","Hearing this, Si Nian didn't think much of it and took Yaoyao to the bedroom to change clothes.","Seeing his mom leave, Zhou Zehan looked conflictedly at the melting ice pop. He hesitated for a moment; although he really didn't want to waste it, he was also afraid of getting a stomachache.","So he hurried to the door and held the ice pop out to Da Huang. \"Da Huang, eat it quickly, or it'll be bad if Mom sees.\"","Da Huang was lying under the tree, enjoying a cool nap.","Disturbed, the dog didn't even lift an eyelid, just turned its head and went back to sleep.","For anything without the scent of meat, it wouldn't even spare a glance.","Zhou Zehan suddenly felt that Da Huang was really a picky eater; it didn't even look at such a delicious treat.","In the end, it all went into his own stomach anyway.","After finishing it, Zhou Zehan felt his mouth was too numb, so he dug out the beef jerky Jiang Jiu had given him from his schoolbag and started eating.","But it was too spicy. In no time, his little face flushed red from the heat.","When he ran into the kitchen, he happened to see a glass of strangely colored water sitting there. It was somewhat dark and had bubbles rising to the top.","Without thinking much, he assumed it was some kind of fruit juice and gulped it down in one go.","After downing it, his eyes lit up.","What was this? It tingled on the tongue, but it was very sweet. It was so good.","\"What are you doing?\"","Zhou Zedong walked in holding a notebook and a pen.","He immediately saw his younger brother clutching the glass, the liquid inside already more than half gone.","His face instantly drained of color.","\"Brother, this stuff is really good! Did Mom buy it?\" Zhou Zehan asked curiously. After speaking, he raised it to take another drink.","\"You can't drink that!\" Zhou Zedong's voice lost control as he lunged forward and slapped the glass out of his hand.","Zhou Zehan was startled.","The commotion was so loud that it even alarmed Si Nian.","She rushed to the kitchen and saw a panicked Zhou Zedong trying to pry his brother's mouth open.","A shattered glass lay on the floor.","Stunned, she immediately asked, \"Xiaodong, what are you doing? What happened?\"","Zhou Zedong's eyes were red. \"Mom, my brother drank my experimental product.\"","\"Experimental product?\" Si Nian was shocked. \"What is it?\"","Only then did she notice that on the cutting board to the side, there was a lot of cilantro, baking soda, brown sugar, and other things.","Next to them was some green cilantro juice.","She was a bit bewildered.","\"Xiaodong, what did you make?\"","She had thought he went into the kitchen because he was hungry and wanted to make some food.","But what was he making here?","\"Mom, I just wanted to see what I could make by mixing these things together. I didn't expect my brother to drink it.\"","Zhou Zedong's face was etched with anxiety.","He didn't even know what he had created. He had just seen these experiments in a book and tried to alter them a bit himself. He didn't even know if it was drinkable, yet his brother had mistaken it for water and drank it.","Si Nian's nose twitched as she looked at the dark brown liquid spilled all over the floor.","She had smelled something the moment she walked in.","It was very familiar.","Like soda or cola.","Looking again at the things placed on the child's table, an unbelievable thought flashed through Si Nian's mind. \"Don't tell me you made cola?\"","Zhou Zedong was still a bit confused because he had never drunk cola and didn't know what it was.","Because Si Nian had specifically learned how to cook in the past, she had read many recipes.","She had also paid attention to things like cola.","However, she had only noticed the ingredients. In the future, everyone could afford to drink cola, so no one bothered making it themselves, but there were some experiments that could produce it.","Of course, she had never tried it.","She certainly never would have imagined that Zhou Zedong would actually make it.","In this era, there still weren't many people who drank cola.","Judging by Zhou Zedong's expression, it was obvious that the kid's success was just a pure fluke.","Hearing his older brother admit that even he didn't know what he had just made, Zhou Zehan finally started to feel a little scared. \"Mom... I'm not going to die, am I?\""]},{"number":417,"title":"Chapter 417: A Complete Childhood","paragraphs":["After he finished speaking, he clutched his stomach, looking as if the pain was about to hit him. Ah, my stomach hurts so much. Am I going to die...","Si Nian was also a bit worried. Although the smell was somewhat similar, it wasn't necessarily that. Seeing that her son didn't seem to be faking it, she immediately said, Let me take you to the hospital for a check-up.","Xiao Dong, stay at home and watch your sister.","Zhou Zedong's face was deathly pale, and his whole body was trembling.","Was his younger brother going to be killed by him?","It was all his fault!","Why did he have to do this kind of experiment? If anything happened to his brother, he wouldn't want to live anymore.","Fortunately, the hospital was not far away, but even so, Si Nian was sweating profusely by the time she carried Zhou Zehan to the hospital on her back.","Zhou Zehan clutched his stomach and wailed loudly, crying out that he was going to die of pain, which scared the people around them into hurriedly making way.","A doctor quickly walked over and asked what was going on.","Si Nian explained that he had drank something, but she wasn't sure exactly what it was, so she didn't dare to make wild guesses at the moment.","The doctor hurriedly took him inside for an examination.","Si Nian sat outside, feeling anxious and uneasy. She also felt a pang of regret for not keeping a closer eye on the children at home, allowing him to swallow such things by mistake.","If something really happened, how was she going to explain it to Zhou Yueshen?","Thinking of the Second Child's cute and cheerful smiling face, Si Nian's eyes grew red.","The doctor soon came out.","Is Zhou Zehan's family here?","Si Nian hastily wiped her tears and walked over. Yes, I am. Doctor, how is Xiao Han?","The doctor said with a complicated expression, He's fine. He has already been sent to the place he belongs.","Huh?","Si Nian was a bit confused.","He ate something bad and got an upset stomach. He needed to go to the bathroom as soon as he went in. Good thing we have spare bedpans here...","Si Nian: ...That's it?","Yes, that's it. The doctor said speechlessly, Next time this happens, please send him to the toilet, not the hospital.","The people around them burst into laughter.","Si Nian: ...","Even with a thick skin like hers, she couldn't help but blush at this moment.","...","As soon as Zhou Yueshen arrived at the door of his house, he saw his eldest son and daughter sitting on the threshold. Yaoyao seemed oblivious to what had happened and was looking at Zhou Zedong with some fear.","Meanwhile, Zhou Zedong was actually covering his face and wiping away tears.","His usually strong and stoic eldest son was actually crying. Seeing this scene, Zhou Yueshen's expression instantly changed.","He strode forward and asked in a deep voice, Xiao Dong, what happened?","Hearing Zhou Yueshen's voice, Zhou Zedong choked out, D-Dad, I hurt my brother. I'm sorry, boohoo, it's all my fault. I shouldn't have messed with those random things. I was wrong, boohoo...","Before he could finish his sentence, he broke down and cried out loud.","His miserable cries drew the attention of the surrounding neighbors.","Zhou Yueshen's expression tightened. What happened to your brother?","My brother drank my experimental product. I didn't even know if it was drinkable. As soon as he drank it, he cried about his stomach hurting, and Mom took him to the hospital.","Experimental product?","Just hearing that made it obvious it wasn't anything good.","Zhou Yueshen looked grave and said, Stop crying. I'll go take a look.","Dad, I want to go too.","Zhou Zedong hurriedly stood up, but his legs felt as if they had lost all their strength, and he almost fell over.","Seeing that he was truly terrified, Zhou Yueshen maintained a tense expression, took his hand, picked up his daughter, and rushed toward the hospital.","As a result, before they even reached the hospital, they saw Si Nian leading Zhou Zehan by the hand, walking in the direction of their home.","The Second Child was still holding a small bag in his hand.","His little face was completely flushed.","Zhou Yueshen breathed a sigh of relief and strode forward.","Nian Nian.","Si Nian was just feeling depressed. Hearing the man's voice, she was startled. Looking up, she saw Zhou Yueshen holding one child by the hand and carrying the other, walking toward her.","Zhou Zedong also let go of his father's hand and stumbled toward his younger brother.","Xiao Han, how is Xiao Han?","As he spoke, he looked like he wanted to cry again.","Seeing his inability to control his emotions, Si Nian knew the child had been badly frightened. She quickly said, Your brother is fine. He just had diarrhea.","What? Zhou Zedong's worried expression froze.","Zhou Zehan lowered his head guiltily and said, I-I didn't know either. I just felt that my stomach hurt a lot. Of course, it doesn't hurt at all now. I pooped it all out, nothing left at all.","As he spoke, he patted his belly with a very satisfied expression.","Si Nian had dark lines all over her head.","He still had the nerve to say that. She had been thoroughly humiliated at the hospital.","But she couldn't really blame him. After all, the child didn't know any better. Seeing his brother's expression, he probably thought he had ingested poison.","He had already been through something like this once, and this time, accidentally ingesting something again, he was probably scared out of his wits.","As soon as his stomach hurt, he thought he was going to die.","As a result, as soon as he arrived at the hospital, he started having diarrhea. Even the doctor was disgusted and told him to hurry home.","This was the first time in her life that Si Nian had lost so much face.","After hearing Si Nian's words, even Zhou Yueshen paused for a moment.","Zhou Zedong's face turned completely ashen.","Thinking of how he had been scared weak in the knees, he wished he could strangle his brother right then and there.","He knew that the ingredients he used could all be consumed individually, so how could it have been that exaggerated?","Although he thought this way, his tense little face visibly relaxed.","After a moment of silence, he finally said, It's good that you're okay.","You're not allowed to buy those popsicles outside anymore, Si Nian also instructed.","Although old-fashioned popsicles might just be plain sugar water, there was no shortage of unscrupulous vendors who used dirty water or cheap saccharin to make them.","When the child was eating it earlier, she was worried that eating too much would give him a stomachache.","But seeing the Second Child's reluctance to waste food, she didn't have the heart to make him throw it away, thinking that a childhood without eating old-fashioned popsicles was incomplete.","Well, look at him now. His childhood was entirely complete.","Zhou Yueshen patted his son's head. Don't eat random things next time. You scared your brother half to death this time. Apologize to him.","Zhou Yueshen had held his son's hand on the way over, so he could feel his fear and panic.","When he held his hand, his hand was trembling.","Zhou Zedong valued his younger brother and sister more than his own life. If something really happened to him because of his actions, this child would probably never forgive himself for the rest of his life.","Zhou Zehan then looked at his older brother. Seeing that he was still looking at him, his eyes held the same gentle and caring look from when he used to protect him as a toddler.","He instantly felt a warmth in his heart. After growing up, he had once felt that his brother had become cold and didn't like playing with him anymore.","But now he realized that even though his brother had grown up, in his heart, he was still his most beloved younger brother.","Deeply moved, Zhou Zehan suddenly hugged his brother tightly. Brother, I'm sorry. I didn't do it on purpose. I ate some beef jerky at the time, and it was too spicy, so I drank your water. I didn't mean to drink it.","So he had also eaten beef jerky...","Si Nian looked up at the sky in speechlessness.","Zhou Zedong, however, pushed him away in disgust.","You stink!"]},{"number":418,"title":"Chapter 418: The New Assistant","paragraphs":["He reverted to his usual disdain for his younger brother.","It was as if the gentleness from just a moment ago was merely Zhou Zehan's hallucination.","Zhou Zehan didn't feel awkward at all. He just rubbed his head and said, \"But brother, what was that thing you made? It was sweet, bubbly, and super delicious, way better than old popsicles.\"","Zhou Zedong frowned. He didn't know exactly what it was either; he only knew that putting those things together caused a reaction.","At the time, he was about to go back to his room to get a notebook to record it, but when he turned around, he found that his brother had drunk it.","Si Nian was also amazed. If Xiao Han didn't get sick from drinking this stuff, could Xiao Dong have actually created something?","Her eyes flickered with interest. \"Xiao Dong, when we get back, make it for me to see.\"","Zhou Zedong nodded.","...","\"This is cola. Yes, it definitely is. Although the taste is very light, I absolutely couldn't have tasted it wrong.\"","Si Nian smacked her lips, savoring the taste, and confirmed.","However, the children still didn't know what cola actually was.","They had only ever had soda water.","They exchanged a glance.","\"Mom, can we drink it?\"","\"Of course you can, but it's best to drink less of this kind of carbonated beverage.\"","Si Nian reminisced about the taste.","Even though she hadn't had cola in a long time either.","This stuff was even more refreshing when chilled.","She marveled inwardly. How could this child even make cola?","Did he have to be this heaven-defyingly genius?","Si Nian admired Zhou Zedong even more.","Knowing the child truly liked researching these things, she suggested to Zhou Yueshen, \"I see the small storage room in the east wing is unused. How about we clear it out for Xiao Dong to do his experiments? Otherwise, if he stays in the kitchen, things like this are bound to happen again.\"","She knew that in his previous life, Zhou Zedong was a researcher, so of course, she supported him developing in this direction now.","Zhou Yueshen had no objections. He was naturally happy that the child had such imagination and manufacturing ability, so he nodded in agreement.","Si Nian then asked him how his business trip went.","\"It's already signed,\" Zhou Yueshen said. \"This collaboration was delayed for some time due to an accident.\"","But precisely because of this accident, they fortuitously built a good relationship with their partners.","They successfully signed the partnership.","The other party was a large foreign factory.","Signing this long-term cooperation could keep their factory standing for at least ten years!","With a massive influx of capital, Chen Nan planned to make the factory bigger and stronger.","Seeing his expression, Si Nian felt relieved and told him about what had happened over the past few days.","Like the matters concerning Wang Ergou and Song Zhaodi, and things at school.","After finishing, she felt a bit of a headache. \"Interpersonal relationships are really too complicated. We started competing out of nowhere, and I can't just brush off the teacher either.\"","If she deliberately did a bad job to brush off the teacher, who knows how the teacher would view her in the future.","But if Lu Yao lost to her, returning to the dorm would be awkward.","If she had known, she wouldn't have applied for the dorm.","As the two were talking, someone knocked on the door.","Second Child went out to open the door and saw a young, unfamiliar auntie.","He asked in confusion, \"Auntie, who are you looking for?\"","\"Little boy, I'm looking for your dad. Is your dad home?\"","Second Child's innocent little face was full of confusion.","Looking for dad?","It was his first time seeing a strange woman looking for his dad.","\"Mom, an auntie is looking for dad.\"","He trotted back and said to Si Nian.","Si Nian looked up at Zhou Yueshen, only to see a woman wearing a professional suit and high heels walk in.","\"Hello, is CEO Zhou here?\"","Si Nian tilted her head to look.","It was a young woman in her twenties, dressed in a sharp professional suit with her hair styled and down, looking exactly like a professional white-collar worker.","She looked at Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Yueshen frowned slightly and asked in a low voice, \"What is it?\"","\"CEO Zhou, these are the documents CEO Chen asked me to deliver for your signature.\" The woman handed over the documents in her hand. \"You were drunk last night, and I didn't want to disturb you, so I brought them over today.\"","Zhou Yueshen reached out to take them. \"Thanks for the trouble.\"","\"You're too polite, CEO Zhou. I'm your assistant. If there's anything you need in the future, just instruct...\"","\"You can go back first.\"","Zhou Yueshen interrupted her.","His eyes carried a sense of alienation and indifference.","The woman paused, smiled, glanced at Si Nian, and left.","Si Nian looked thoughtfully at her retreating figure.","Graceful, slender, and pretty.","Sure enough, when you're a big boss, the assistants and secretaries around you are never too shabby.","\"Chen Nan arranged it. I told him I didn't need one, but he said an assistant who speaks both German and English is hard to find.\"","Seeing her retract her gaze, Zhou Yueshen began to explain.","Si Nian looked at him. \"Oh, you were drunk last night?\"","Zhou Yueshen paused. \"I was pretending. I wasn't drunk; they were just being endless.\"","Si Nian let out a snort through her nose.","To be honest, no matter the era, there were simply too many bosses who had affairs with their secretaries.","Zhou Yueshen rubbed his nose.","\"After wrapping up the cooperation last night, I left early this morning because I just wanted to come back and see you all.\"","Zhou Yueshen said, \"That's why I didn't get the documents.\"","\"Oh~\" Si Nian dragged out the syllable. A woman's sixth sense is always very accurate. The way the other party looked at Zhou Yueshen carried a hint of fawning.","\"I believe you, but I don't trust others.\"","Of course, Si Nian didn't mean to blame the woman. After all, if they could get together, it would mean neither party was any good.","She said, \"If I find out anything is going on, no matter the reason, we are getting a divorce.\"","She couldn't tolerate a single grain of sand in her eye.","Zhou Yueshen's jaw tightened slightly.","\"Niannian, I won't.\"","Si Nian: \"Won't what?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"That day won't come.\"","He held her hand, took a box out of his bag, and opened it. Inside was a diamond ring.","\"When I was on my business trip, aside from work, it was just you.\"","He hurried back just to show her the gift he bought, but he was delayed by Second Child's matter and almost forgot.","He slipped the diamond ring onto her finger. It fit perfectly, neither too big nor too small.","It looked exceptionally beautiful on her tender hands, which were so delicate that the fine fuzz could be seen under the light.","Zhou Yueshen held her hand and placed a gentle kiss on it.","Si Nian's face flushed red.","This older man was getting bolder and bolder; the kids were still right here.","She instinctively glanced at the children, only to see Eldest Child reading a book, Second Child rummaging through his dad's bag, and Yaoyao drawing and writing with a pen.","Alright, no one was paying attention.","She breathed a sigh of relief and glared at Zhou Yueshen again.","She wasn't joking with him.","Second Child rummaged and rummaged through his dad's bag. \"Mom, look, it's an airplane model! Is it for me?\"","His eyes sparkled as he looked at Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Yueshen, with his arm around Si Nian, took a moment to glance at him and said, \"That's for your brother.\"","\"Then is this for me?\"","Second Child pulled out a cute little backpack.","It was so cute, completely unfitting for his temperament.","But considering it was bought by his dad, it didn't matter even if it was cute.","\"That's for your sister.\"","Zhou Zehan: \"......\"","Refusing to give up, he rummaged some more and pulled out two fist-like objects.","\"What are these?\"","\"Boxing gloves. I bought those for you to wear when you practice boxing in the future.\""]},{"number":419,"title":"Chapter 419: The Disappearing Corpse","paragraphs":["Zhou Zehan: \"...\"","Si Nian withdrew her gaze. It seemed the older man hadn't lied.","He truly did have his family in his heart.","She got up to make dinner for him.","Zhou Yueshen followed her.","Hearing the noise, Si Nian knew it was him. Taking eggs out of the refrigerator, she said, \"It's already dark, let's just eat something simple. The kids haven't eaten either, so how about we have noodles tonight?\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a sound of agreement and rolled up his sleeves to help her.","The figures moved back and forth in the kitchen. His tall, lean silhouette moved methodically, accompanied by her slender, gentle shadow next to him, creating a warm and cozy scene.","After cooking the noodles, Si Nian let the children serve themselves. She picked up her own bowl and walked out.","Yaoyao held her little bowl, took a small portion from her father's large bowl, and began slurping the noodles happily.","She was still wearing her new backpack. She couldn't even bear to take it off while eating.","After all the fuss today, everyone was tired.","Si Nian told the kids to wash up and go to bed after eating, planning to get some early rest herself.","By the time Zhou Yueshen finished washing up and returned to the room, Si Nian was sitting with her back to him at the vanity, wiping her face.","She took off her ring and examined it carefully for a moment.","It looked like a real diamond. That must have cost a lot of money, right?","Just how deep were this man's pockets?","Zhou Yueshen walked over and closed the window. Because of the orientation of their house, if the window wasn't closed, the early morning sun would shine right in and be too bright.","When he turned around, Si Nian had already gotten into bed and was lying flat.","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","For some reason, he had a bad premonition.","The summer blanket was exceptionally thin. In the past, Zhou Yueshen never used a blanket at all, but Si Nian needed one. She insisted on using a summer cooling blanket, which felt nice and cool to the touch.","As she lay there now, the curves of her body were clearly outlined.","Zhou Yueshen looked away, then lay down beside Si Nian, his posture straight and stiff, facing upward.","It was as if they had gone back to when they first got married. Back then, he was still somewhat reserved and always slept in this rigid posture.","Once they became familiar with each other, he would always pull her into his arms as soon as they got into bed.","Si Nian found it somewhat amusing. Her eyes darted around with a hint of craftiness.","She turned her body closer to Zhou Yueshen, resting her hand subconsciously on his chest, lightly tapping it from time to time.","\"Zhou Yueshen, I need to do an inspection.\"","Zhou Yueshen's eyes snapped open. \"Inspect what?\"","\"To check if your chastity is still intact, of course.\"","With the windows closed, the room was very dark.","Si Nian couldn't see Zhou Yueshen's face.","But Zhou Yueshen had excellent night vision. He could clearly see her blinking eyes and her body pressed tightly against his.","Her soft curves were pressed right against his arm.","Zhou Yueshen knew this matter wouldn't end so simply, so he said, \"Alright, go ahead and inspect.\"","Si Nian chuckled softly. This man actually took it seriously, thinking she was really doubting him.","She quickly hid her smile and reached out to turn on the small bedside lamp.","Leaning over to unbutton the man's clothes, her movements were deliberately slow.","It didn't look like an inspection at all; it was more like flirting.","Zhou Yueshen's Adam's apple bobbed unconsciously.","He watched her actions in silence. Si Nian pulled his clothes open, her gaze sweeping wantonly over his body, before she frowned critically. \"How did your muscles get even better?\"","He obviously wasn't butchering pigs anymore, so how come his muscles hadn't softened even a little bit?","Zhou Yueshen's voice was deep. \"I've been working out with Little Han lately.\"","...","Si Nian yawned. \"It seems your chastity is still intact. Let's go to sleep early then.\"","After saying that, she pushed Zhou Yueshen's hand away, turned her back to him, lay down, and closed her eyes to sleep...","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","...","Meanwhile, next door, Song Zhaodi opened her eyes, feeling restless.","Ever since Wang Ergou was released from prison, she hadn't been able to sleep for the past few days.","Thinking back to when Wang Ergou climbed over the wall of Si Nian's house a while ago, she felt a lingering sense of unease.","She couldn't shake the feeling that Wang Ergou hadn't just come to steal things.","Could it be that he really saw something?","The more she thought about it, the more panicked she became, especially after hearing people say during the day that Wang Ergou had been sneaking around the area lately. It made her even more worried.","She climbed out of bed, threw on some clothes, and hurriedly left the house.","In the darkness of the night, she walked to the door of a certain house.","Her flashlight shone on the door. The police seal was still there; although slightly weathered, it remained intact.","Song Zhaodi breathed a small sigh of relief. She had just turned around to leave when she suddenly heard an \"Ouch~\" coming from inside.","Her footsteps abruptly halted. She turned her head to look, her trembling pupils looking especially terrifying in the dead of night.","...","After class the next day, Si Nian went to the English teacher to learn about the work details. It was mostly translating documents and the like. The contents of these documents were confidential and could not be leaked, so the English teacher repeatedly emphasized that she had to do all the work personally.","Lu Yao stood beside her, also listening attentively.","As the two walked out, Lu Yao glanced at her and said, \"Si Nian, I hope you don't misunderstand. I'm not trying to compete with you; I just want to prove that I'm no worse than you.\"","Si Nian: \"...No one has ever said you were worse than me.\"","Lu Yao's grip on the documents tightened.","Si Nian shook her head, too lazy to say more to her.","In college, the competition among students with good grades to get better resources was always fierce.","Everyone wanted the best. She could understand that, so naturally, she didn't think there was anything wrong with what Lu Yao was doing.","However, while Lu Yao claimed it was to prove herself, she was actually afraid that people would think she was fighting Si Nian for the spot, which was why she said such things.","She thought she was proving her innocence, but in reality, it was just self-comfort.","Unfortunately, Si Nian punctured her illusion with a single sentence.","Before she even reached home, she saw police cars parked outside the alley.","Many people by the roadside were talking in hushed tones.","\"Is there really a corpse? That's too scary. Wasn't the body of the previous female homeowner already found? Then whose is it this time?\"","\"Corpse my ass, the police said they didn't find anything. It was Wang Ergou lying...\""]},{"number":420,"title":"Chapter 420: Celebration","paragraphs":["Si Nian's eyes flickered, and she walked toward the crowd.","Up ahead, Wang Ergou looked anxious. Pointing into the house, he said, \"It's true, I really saw it. I saw it with my own eyes, right inside that well.\"","The police officer looked impatient. \"You brat, do you think we're blind? You just saw it last night, and today it disappeared. Did you see a ghost or something?\"","\"Let's go, let's go. What a waste of time.\"","The group of officers prepared to leave.","Wang Ergou had no choice but to watch helplessly as the group walked away.","Si Nian's gaze swept over the crowd and noticed Song Zhaodi standing at the back, carrying a bamboo basket and watching the scene.","A faint smile played on the corners of her lips.","Since no one was paying attention to her, she made no effort to hide it.","Since Wang Ergou had called the police, it must be true, just as she had guessed.","But if he discovered it last night, where did the corpse go?","Was he spotted, and the body moved to another location?","Si Nian turned and went back home.","A short while later, there was a knock on the door.","She opened it to find a pale-faced Wang Ergou.","Si Nian glanced outside and let him in to talk.","She poured him a glass of water and said, \"Tell me, what happened?\"","Wang Ergou said agitatedly, \"Sister, I followed what you said, and I really found the body. It was right inside the well in that courtyard. I was so excited that I went to wait outside the police station late at night for them to open. As soon as I woke up, I notified them to come over, but when we got here, the body was gone.\"","After he finished speaking, even he began to doubt himself. \"Sister, do you think I really saw a ghost last night?\"","Si Nian was speechless.","She originally hadn't wanted to meddle in Wang Ergou's affairs. First, she didn't want to live in the same alley as a murderer. Second, this rumor was indeed affecting the sale of houses nearby.","And Zhou Yueshen had followed her advice and bought the houses from Chen Nan.","For her, this had at least some impact.","She didn't want to expose the murderer herself; after all, such things easily drew hatred.","Now that Wang Ergou had stepped forward wanting to clear his name, and she wanted to solve the problem, it killed two birds with one stone.","That was why Si Nian had tipped him off.","But she hadn't expected the other party to be so vigilant.","She had even specifically reminded Wang Ergou to go look when no one was around.","Because Si Nian herself was only guessing. A person couldn't just vanish inexplicably, especially in the case of Song Zhaodi's husband.","In situations like this, they were almost always murdered and their bodies dumped in the wilderness.","This was especially common in the older eras.","Si Nian also thought that it wouldn't be easy to dispose of a body unnoticed in Beijing, let alone a grown man.","She understood the principle of burying close and dumping far.","Assuming the killer was Wang Zhaodi, it would be even harder for her to move an adult's body.","Therefore, the body was very likely in a nearby place where no one could find it.","And that sealed-off house, which everyone avoided like the plague, was a perfect place to hide a body.","Of course, Si Nian had only been guessing at the time, but she hadn't expected to actually be right.","It was just that Wang Ergou was too stupid. He didn't know to preserve the evidence the moment he saw the body, which gave the killer another chance to escape.","Truly a piece of rotten wood that cannot be carved.","Wang Ergou hadn't expected this either. When he actually saw the body, he was both terrified and thrilled. He rushed to the police station immediately, only to find that they weren't open in the middle of the night.","After his excitement faded, he fell asleep, and by the time he woke up, it was already noon the next day.","Only then did he remember the important matter and hurried to report it.","But when they went over, there was already nothing in the well.","He felt a wave of lingering fear.","Because for the body to disappear, there were only two possibilities: either he had been discovered by the murderer, or he had seen a ghost.","He didn't want either to be true.","\"Sister, what do you think I should do?\"","\"A perfect chance to clear your name was right in front of you, and you couldn't grasp it. What else can you do?\"","Si Nian rolled her eyes at him and said in a low voice, \"You've already been discovered by the killer now. They probably have their eyes on you. Hiding isn't going to solve anything. Now it just depends on whether you have the courage.\"","\"Ah? What do you mean?\"","\"Sneak into the killer's house. It's still early, so the killer definitely hasn't had time to dispose of the body yet. The body must still be nearby, very likely somewhere she can keep an eye on it. So you still have one chance: sneak into the killer's house and look for the body.\"","Wang Ergou's face turned pale.","\"Ah, wouldn't that put me in a lot of danger?\"","Si Nian was speechless. \"You're a man. According to my guess, the killer is very likely a woman. As long as you're careful, could you really be overpowered by a woman?\"","Wang Ergou nodded. \"That makes sense.\"","\"From what I know, she goes out to buy groceries for a while every afternoon, taking about forty minutes. You only have this window of time.\"","She had heard that Song Zhaodi's mother-in-law had passed away a couple of years ago, leaving only her paralyzed father-in-law.","If he was careful, there was still a chance.","Wang Ergou's expression turned serious. \"I understand. Nothing ventured, nothing gained. I'm good at this sort of thing.\"","\"But Sister, I want to ask, why are you willing to help me?\"","Si Nian: \"Do you want to be neighbors with a murderer?\"","Wang Ergou: \"......\"","...","Si Nian sent him away and went into her room to start looking through the documents.","It wasn't difficult, but the workload was quite heavy.","She didn't know how the pay would be. If it was too low, she would just find an excuse to turn it down.","Translating these kinds of documents posed no challenge for her.","However, for college students, it was very useful.","Not only could it improve their skills, but they could also learn a lot of knowledge.","For college students, it was indeed a great way to improve their abilities while making money.","Meanwhile, on the other side, Antarctic Appliance Home had signed a major partnership.","At this moment, the entire company was celebrating.","Chen Nan had even booked a hotel.","The higher-ups sat at one table, and people were lining up to toast Zhou Yueshen.","Everyone knew about the company's newly promoted major shareholder, President Zhou.","Rumor had it that when the boss's startup was on the verge of bankruptcy, he was the only one willing to invest money.","Boss Chen treated him like a blood brother.","This current partnership had been under negotiation for months without success, but the one time he tagged along, it succeeded.","Everyone said that President Zhou was Boss Chen's lucky star.","Boss Chen had even assigned his most prized assistant to him.","It was just that the new President Zhou was tall and burly, with sharp features, and rarely smiled.","He looked very unapproachable.","Everyone was a little afraid of him.","Chen Nan clinked glasses with Zhou Yueshen and asked, \"Old Zhou, why didn't you bring your girl out to play?\"","Zhou Yueshen's brows were cold and stern. He looked up and said, \"She has to go to school.\"","Hearing this, Chen Nan couldn't help but laugh.","\"You call other people wild players, but I don't think anyone is wilder than you. Others find young girls to be their mistresses, but you're something else—you just found one to be your wife.\"","Zhou Yueshen's jaw tightened a fraction.","\"I don't like these kinds of jokes. Don't compare her to others.\"","Chen Nan finally realized he had misspoken. Men will be men, after all—who didn't have a few intimate companions?","These days, among those who made money, how many were truly devoted to one person?","Someone like Zhou Yueshen had been highly sought after even back in the military.","To be able to find such a beautiful and delicate wife out there.","Sometimes, Chen Nan really envied him.","Coming from a grassroots background, yet able to reach this level.","One had to admire his self-control.","He made an \"I know I was wrong\" expression and said to the female assistant in an evening gown next to Zhou Yueshen, \"Assistant Chen, take good care of Mr. Zhou.\"","Then he stood up and went to dance with his female companion.","Chen Mi poured a glass of wine for Zhou Yueshen. Her deep red evening gown accentuated her beautiful curves perfectly.","She wore exquisite, professional makeup, and if one got just a little closer, they could smell her captivating perfume.","People continuously came up to invite her to dance.","But she rejected them all.","Chen Mi looked up at Zhou Yueshen. His sleeves were rolled up, revealing the distinct muscle lines of his arms.","With his bronze skin, one could tell at a glance that he was a man who loved to exercise.","At thirty, there weren't many men who had the self-discipline to work out and maintain their figures.","Take Chen Nan for example. He used to be a famous handsome guy in their circle, but now he already had a beer belly.","And his face was sagging heavily.","\"Mr. Zhou, aren't you going to dance?\"","Zhou Yueshen took a sip of his wine, his expression unchanged.","\"No.\"","Speaking of which, he wondered if Niannian would like this kind of occasion. She came from a good family background, so she had probably attended such dances before.","Zhou Yueshen had never seen her dance.","He lowered his head and took another sip of wine.","With a glass in his hand continuously for the past few days, his temples were throbbing with a dull ache.","Zhou Yueshen reached up and rubbed them.","Then he heard the woman beside him say, \"Mr. Zhou, working with Mr. Chen in the future, there will be many occasions like this. Dancing is basically a necessary skill. If you don't know how, I can teach you.\"","Zhou Yueshen interrupted her, his voice low and cold, \"I said no need. Do you not understand?\"","Chen Mi's expression stiffened, and she didn't dare say anything else.","Zhou Yueshen checked the time. It was about late enough. He grabbed his suit jacket from the side and stood up to leave.","It wasn't an important business dinner anyway, so there was no need for him to stay any longer.","If Chen Nan hadn't insisted he come this time to introduce him to some people, Zhou Yueshen would have gone home long ago.","Whether acting as a behind-the-scenes shareholder or doing business together as partners.","He didn't want to stay out all night anymore.","He would no longer neglect his family for the sake of work.","Zhou Yueshen took a taxi home.","The smell of alcohol on him was very heavy.","He stood outside for a while, waiting for the wind to blow the smell away, before walking into the house.","Si Nian was stewing soup.","After finishing her work in the afternoon, she went and bought a chicken, planning to make soup.","She also bought a lot of medicinal herbs to stew with it, making it nutritious and highly replenishing.","Of course, this was all to nourish the children. Kids needed a nutritional boost from time to time to grow fast.","The fragrance of the herbs blended with the smell of the chicken, creating an indescribably delicious aroma.","Zhou Yueshen suddenly felt a bit hungry.","The food Si Nian cooked was as mouthwatering as always.","He walked into the kitchen and watched Si Nian bustling about, with Eldest Child washing vegetables on the side.","Seeing him come in, the boy called out, \"Dad.\"","Si Nian took a moment to look back at him.","\"You're back.\"","Zhou Yueshen responded, poured a glass of water, and downed it in one gulp.","Si Nian stood on her tiptoes, sniffed him twice, and then fanned her nose with her hand. \"Such a strong smell of alcohol. Did you drink again?\"","\"The company had a celebration banquet today, so I drank a little.\"","Si Nian thought about it and agreed; it was inevitable on such occasions.","But it was still early, and he was already back.","Logically speaking, shouldn't the celebration have just started?","Was it because her words from before had scared him, so he didn't dare to stay out long?","Thinking of this, Si Nian felt a hint of sweetness in her heart. The only man who would take her words to heart and actually act on them was him.","She picked up a fragrant, tender piece of boiled chicken from the pot with her chopsticks, blew on it, and brought it to Zhou Yueshen's mouth. \"Try this. Is it good?\"","Zhou Yueshen opened his mouth and took it. The chicken was soft, tender, and flavorful. The faint herbal fragrance mixed with the rich meaty aroma exploded in his mouth.","It was a hundred times better than the cold food at the hotel.","\"Mhm.\"","\"It's delicious.\"","\"Alright, it's about done. Let's eat.\" Si Nian gave him a gentle smile and called out loudly for Second Child to come in and carry the bowls.","Zhou Yueshen looked at her and the children, his eyes filled with unspeakable tenderness.","After dinner, Si Nian told him about what happened during the day.","\"Actually, I was just guessing, but I didn't expect it to be true. If Wang Ergou really hadn't discovered anything, he wouldn't have gone to the police.\"","\"It's just that this murderer is too cautious and smart, yet they were still discovered.\"","Si Nian sighed. \"If it weren't for the impact of this rumor, there would definitely be more people living here.\"","As she spoke, she watched Zhou Yueshen put down the basin of foot-washing water and put her feet in.","She was scalded slightly. \"It's so hot.\"","Zhou Yueshen sat opposite her, touched the water, and didn't think it was hot.","He took off his shoes and put his feet in.","His feet were so big that they took up the entire basin.","Si Nian immediately stepped on his feet, not forgetting to say, \"If this murderer isn't caught, the rumor will never be broken, and it will affect the housing prices in the future.\"","Zhou Yueshen lowered his head. Her little feet were tender and small.","Stepping on his feet, they looked even whiter.","He didn't move, letting Si Nian do as she pleased.","He only withdrew his gaze after she poked him.","\"Why are you spacing out? I'm talking to you.\"","Si Nian muttered in dissatisfaction.","Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly. \"Don't worry about this matter.\"","\"Then what do you plan to do?\"","\"Chen Nan has connections over there. If that's really the case, I'll have him find someone to investigate. He should be very willing.\"","Si Nian thought about it and agreed. After all, Chen Nan sold the house to them without mentioning this matter beforehand, so he must feel a bit guilty.","Now that there was a chance to make up for it, he would definitely be willing.","Having figured it out, Si Nian couldn't be bothered to focus on this issue anymore.","She dried her feet first and put on her slippers. \"I finished washing first, so you pour out the water.\"","After saying that, she ran into the room.","Like a little kid.","Zhou Yueshen thought that Second Child's personality was probably infected by her.","He chuckled softly, stood up, and poured out the water.","Returning to the room, Si Nian was already lying down.","Although translation work wasn't difficult, it was very mentally draining.","After cooking, Si Nian was actually quite sleepy.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen get into bed, she subconsciously leaned closer to him.","Snuggling against the crook of his arm.","Their skin touched, and they could hear each other's breathing.","\"Niannian, no inspection tonight?\" Zhou Yueshen's deep voice rumbled from his chest, making the ear of the leaning Si Nian tingle.","Si Nian: \"?!\"","\"Why do I need to inspect?\"","\"I drank alcohol today too.\" Zhou Yueshen's Adam's apple bobbed.","Having drank alcohol, being half-drunk, it was the easiest to get aroused.","Si Nian blinked, nodded, and said, \"Alright then.\"","After saying that, she tilted her head up and planted a loud kiss on his cheek.","Seeing her perfunctory attitude, Zhou Yueshen laughed. \"That's it?\"","\"What else?\" Si Nian asked as a matter of fact.","Only this time, Zhou Yueshen wasn't going to indulge her. Sensing danger, Si Nian was about to turn over and pretend to sleep.","But the next second, her hands were pinned down with an undeniable force.","The man's scorching breath drew closer and closer.","\"You... uh...\" Si Nian's hands were pressed against the bedsheets on one side, unable to move an inch.","Before she had time to think, she was pressed down by the man's mountain-like body.","Like the rise and fall of the tide.","Who knows if it was because of the alcohol."]},{"number":421,"title":"Chapter 421: Mom, are you guys fighting","paragraphs":["In her daze, Si Nian could still hear him murmuring in her ear, seemingly asking if she knew how to dance.","When Si Nian answered that she did, he paused for a moment.","When Zhou Yueshen woke up in the morning to call her, she was still a bit sulky and turned her back to him.","\"Niannian, if you don't get up now, you'll be late for class.\" Zhou Yueshen coughed into his fist and reminded her in a low voice.","His voice was deliberately kept low.","It clearly carried a hint of guilt and caution.","Covered by the blanket, Si Nian stiffened, only then remembering that she was still a student.","What a sin, what a sin.","She climbed out of bed, feeling quite disgraced, and even bumped into Zhou Yueshen as she walked past.","\"Ouch!\" Zhou Yueshen didn't budge, but she was bounced back and almost fell flat on her bottom.","What a disaster.","Zhou Yueshen didn't know exactly how angry Si Nian was to actually use her slender little body to ram into him. This was something he hadn't expected.","Seeing her cry out in pain, he quickly reached out to pull her up.","To keep her from falling.","Si Nian, flushed red with anger, glared at him fiercely before heading downstairs.","During breakfast, the children all sensed the off-kilter atmosphere.","\"Mom, did you and Dad have a fight?\"","Second Child asked, looking at the two of them curiously while biting into an egg.","Si Nian's expression stiffened. \"Nothing of the sort.\"","\"Then why are you sitting so far away from Dad? Mom, you're usually not like this.\"","Second Child's face was written all over with confusion.","Usually, Mom and Dad sat together.","But today, Mom sat very far from Dad, and she didn't say a single word.","\"If I'm not usually like this, then what am I like?\"","Second Child said, \"Usually, you sit right up against Dad, and you lean on him, holding hands while you eat, and sometimes you even let Dad feed you.\"","Si Nian was speechless. Was she usually that clingy?","Zhou Yueshen looked at his son, his eyes filled with a smile.","He received another glare from Si Nian.","She coughed, \"Alright, eat your food.\" Why was he observing so carefully?","She had thought their usual interactions were subtle enough that the kids wouldn't notice at all.","How utterly embarrassing.","Si Nian went to school. She didn't plan on handing in the translated documents to the English teacher so quickly. Since the teacher had given them two days, she could just submit them at the last minute.","If she handed in the assignment too quickly, the teacher might think she had it easy, and it wouldn't be good if she was piled with a bunch of work in the future.","Thinking like this, Si Nian went to class with peace of mind.","Unexpectedly, she bumped right into Lu Yao, who had just gone to hand in her documents.","Lu Yao's complexion was not looking good; she had dark bruises under her eyes and two big dark circles.","It seemed she had stayed up late working overtime last night.","She was really giving it her all for this opportunity.","As she walked into the classroom, Liu Nana called out to her, \"Sister Si Nian, over here.\"","Liu Nana had saved a seat for her.","This time, at least, it wasn't in the first row.","Si Nian couldn't bring herself to refuse, so she walked over and sat down.","Only then did she notice Zhang Xue sitting on the other side. Her face looked even worse than Lu Yao's, and her eyes were very red and swollen.","She looked as if she had been crying.","A bit puzzled, she asked, \"What's wrong with Zhang Xue?\"","Liu Nana's expression turned awkward. For a moment, she found it hard to say that Zhang Xue had been miserable all night because Chen Haoran had come looking for Si Nian.","This matter really couldn't be blamed on Si Nian. It wasn't her fault that she was pretty, and if Chen Haoran really liked her, what could be done about it?","Before Liu Nana could speak, Zhang Xue slammed her book onto the desk with a smack, staring coldly at Si Nian.","Si Nian looked baffled.","She didn't have any grudge against Zhang Xue, right?","\"Xiaoxue, don't be like this.\"","Liu Nana hurriedly pulled at her.","But Zhang Xue swatted her hand away.","\"Nana, are you my friend or her friend? You know perfectly well that I'm upset because of her, yet you still save a seat for her. Why are you being so kind? Do you also want to see me make a fool of myself?\"","Zhang Xue said angrily.","She was already unhappy about the situation between Si Nian and Chen Haoran.","Yet here Nana was, talking to Si Nian.","What was the meaning of this?","Could it be that she also wanted to suck up to Si Nian because she had money?","The more she thought about it, the more likely it seemed, and Zhang Xue's gaze toward Liu Nana consequently turned unfriendly.","After her initial shock, Liu Nana felt a chill in her heart. \"Is that really what you think of me?\"","She had been thinking all along that things between Si Nian and Chen Haoran might not be what Zhang Xue imagined.","Seeing her in such distress, Nana only wanted to ask Si Nian what the real reason was.","Yet Zhang Xue actually thought of her this way.","Liu Nana was furious.","A fire sparked in her heart as well.","Just for a man, how many people was she willing to offend before she was satisfied?","Was it really worth it?","\"Then what else did you mean by it?\" Zhang Xue actually regretted her words as soon as she said them.","But unable to swallow her pride at this moment, she still braced herself and spoke.","\"Forget it!\" Liu Nana gave her a glance and withdrew her gaze with a disappointed face.","She didn't want to talk to her anymore.","Looking at the two of them, Si Nian felt a massive headache coming on.","Girls' friendships were just so fragile, falling apart at the drop of a hat.","She didn't even know what had happened.","But she sensitively detected that it probably had something to do with her.","She was just about to ask what was going on when she was interrupted by the teacher's voice.","Class had started.","After class, Zhang Xue ran off first.","Liu Nana stiffened for a moment and remained silent.","Only then did Si Nian get the chance to ask what exactly the situation was.","\"Does it have something to do with me? What happened to Zhang Xue?\"","Liu Nana reluctantly said, \"It's because of Chen Haoran. Yesterday afternoon, Chen Haoran came looking for us, saying he wanted to walk you home. It made Zhang Xue misunderstand that Chen Haoran likes you, and she cried all night.\"","She sighed. She and Zhang Xue had fantasized during high school about working hard together once they got into college, yet their friendship had deteriorated to this state over a man. It truly disappointed her beyond words.","Si Nian was greatly astonished. \"What? I'm already married, and she could still misunderstand?\"","\"Because from our perspective, Chen Haoran really is quite enthusiastic towards you.\"","Si Nian understood now.","Because of his relationship with Chen Nan, Chen Haoran treated her like a relative.","But the others didn't know about this yet and had always thought that they weren't actually familiar with each other.","Chen Haoran taking the initiative to seek her out like that was what caused the misunderstanding.","Si Nian rubbed her temples, feeling that college relationships were truly complicated and bumpy.","However, to avoid trouble, she still said, \"This matter is a misunderstanding.\"","She briefly explained the relationship between the Chen family and her own. Although it was a bit of a coincidence, Si Nian truly wasn't lying.","After hearing this, Liu Nana was also very surprised. \"So that's how it is. I felt something wasn't right and that it wasn't like what Zhang Xue thought. Good thing I didn't misunderstand you.\"","Si Nian nodded and said, \"My husband and I have a very good relationship. He loves me very much, and, um... I also like him a lot. So it's impossible for me to have anything going on with Chen Haoran. In terms of seniority, he should even be calling me Aunt.\"","Liu Nana smiled awkwardly. \"So that's how it is.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Zhang Xue probably misunderstood. I'll have to trouble you to help explain it to her. If I speak to her right now, she probably won't listen. Her emotions are being controlled by love. You two shouldn't fall out over this little thing. After all, there are still four years of college left, and you'll be seeing each other all the time. It will be awkward in the future.\"","Liu Nana said gratefully, \"Thank you, you're such a good person.\"","This whole thing was a misunderstanding to begin with. With Zhang Xue treating her like that, anyone else would have been angry.","But Si Nian wasn't angry; instead, she kindly advised her.","Liu Nana had a very good impression of her.","Si Nian shook her head. She just didn't want to cause trouble for herself. Otherwise, whether other people got along well or not was none of her business.","However, after this incident, she also became clear about the good and bad personality traits of her three roommates.","Liu Nana asked her again, \"Have you finished the work the English teacher gave you? Last night, I saw Lu Yao working all night. She didn't sleep this morning and went to hand it in bright and early.\"","She said this, feeling a bit worried about Si Nian.","\"Don't worry, I have my own plans for this.\"","Si Nian said unhurriedly.","Seeing her expression, Liu Nana didn't ask any more questions.","At the agreed time, Si Nian handed in her work to the English teacher.","In the blink of an eye, it was Saturday, and she finally had a day off.","Si Nian was just thinking about taking Da Huang out for a walk when she encountered a woman screaming, \"Catch the thief! Catch the thief!\"","She looked up and saw a thief rushing toward her, carrying a bag.","Si Nian was startled. Before she could step aside, Da Huang let out a dangerous, low growl.","The man was still looking back smugly. By the time he reacted, a huge dog had suddenly pounced on him.","Terrified, his legs gave way, and he collapsed to the ground.","Half an hour later, the thief was taken away by the police.","The wealthy lady, having gotten her bag back, walked up to Si Nian and thanked her profusely.","\"Sister, thank you so much! If you hadn't helped me catch the thief, I really wouldn't have known what to do. Losing money is a small matter, but losing my ID documents would be a huge hassle.\"","Si Nian withdrew her gaze from the bag the woman was carrying.","Hermes. Authentic at a glance.","Oh my, she had actually run into a rich woman.","The other party was dressed very luxuriously, though her outfit made her look a bit older.","She had big wavy hair, looking incredibly trendy.","However, she looked to be only in her thirties.","Actually, she hadn't thought about helping at all; it was Da Huang who had pounced on his own.","Who would have thought that their Da Huang also had a heart of justice?","It was rare to go out for a stroll, yet she still managed to run into a thief.","\"You're too polite, sis.\"","\"Sis... oh wow, you sure know how to talk. Seeing as you're about the same age as my son, you should really be calling me Auntie.\"","Si Nian looked surprised. \"You look like you're in your twenties. I thought you weren't much older than me.\"","The woman's smile grew even sweeter, unable to contain the grin at the corners of her mouth.","\"Sister, you're really interesting. What's your name? Let's get to know each other.\"","As she spoke, she looked Si Nian up and down, exclaiming in surprise, \"You have a beautiful figure. Would you consider coming to my company to be a model?\"","Seeing her outfit and aura, Si Nian knew she was very likely a modern career woman.","Hearing this now, it was indeed the case.","She said shyly, \"I'm still in school.\"","\"What a pity. Your looks have a very classic domestic charm. You would definitely look beautiful in a qipao.\"","\"Oh my, I've been talking to you for so long, I almost forgot my main business. Sister, do you know where the Zhou family lives?\"","Si Nian blinked. \"The Zhou family? Zhou Yueshen's family?\"","The truth was, there were so few families living in this alley, and hers was the only one with the surname Zhou.","Si Nian was surprised. She was looking for Zhou Yueshen?","Did Zhou Yueshen have such a wealthy relative?","\"Ah, yes, that's the name. Recently, I've been hearing my Lao Chen talking about him. He even said his wife is young, beautiful, and elegant, telling me to learn from her. I wanted to come over and see just how beautiful she is.\"","Lao Chen?","Could it be Chen Nan?","Come to think of it, looking closely, this woman really did look a bit like Chen Haoran.","Si Nian: \"...\" Goodness, the gossip she was enjoying turned out to be about herself.","Seeing her suddenly fall silent, the woman paused. Suddenly, she realized something and stammered, \"I-it couldn't be you, could it...\"","Si Nian: \"...\" You hit the nail on the head.","...","Meanwhile, at the Jing City railway station.","Lin Sisi arrived in Jing City carrying her luggage.","This time, she had taken a special leave of absence to come here.","In her hands, she also carried the five thousand yuan that Zhang Cuimei had given her.","Lin Sisi was here to do business.","It took her a long time to convince Zhang Cuimei to give her pension savings to start a clothing business.","She had finally gotten out of prison and even gotten into university.","Lin Sisi's next plan was to be just like Si Nian in her previous life—to build a booming business.","Si Nian was now busy studying in Jing City, so she definitely wouldn't drop out of school to do business like she did in her last life.","By the time she finished university, the most she would have was a diploma from a prestigious school.","But as for herself, not only would she have a diploma, she would also become a powerful career woman and a big boss.","For this dream, Lin Sisi had traveled thousands of miles alone to Jing City.","Of course, she didn't come all the way to Jing City just to inspect goods.","It was because she remembered that around this time in her previous life, Fu Yang had been transferred to Jing City for a mission.","Because Si Nian wanted to do business, she had tagged along for the trip.","She heard that during her time in Jing City, Si Nian had met a female boss in the clothing industry.","Not only did she collaborate with the other party and secure a co-branding deal, but she also started a major brand business.","That female boss was an investor.","It was said that her husband was an equally wealthy businessman.","In his early years, he had invested in a friend and bought over a dozen courtyard houses. As a result of the friend running away, the dozen or so houses were stuck in his hands, unable to be sold.","Later, he gave these dozen or so houses to his wife.","His wife discovered that the reason the houses couldn't be sold was because a murder had occurred in the alley. Rumors were flying everywhere, scaring the surrounding residents into moving away.","Si Nian accidentally met the female boss, noticed something amiss, and later asked Fu Yang for help. The two worked together to catch the real murderer.","To thank Si Nian for her help, the female boss generously gave her a courtyard house, saying she could come to Jing City to play anytime.","Who would have known that the housing prices for such a courtyard house would skyrocket in the next ten to twenty years.","It would be worth hundreds of millions!","Of course, Lin Sisi knew this because Si Nian had become famous at the time, and many reporters interviewed her about her entrepreneurial experience.","It was reported in the newspapers.","After she found out that Si Nian was a fake heiress, she kept looking up everything about Si Nian.","Therefore, she knew everything that had happened to her like the back of her hand.","That was why she thought of making a special trip to Jing City.","If the person helping out this time was replaced by herself...","Wouldn't she be able to get a house for free?","The more Lin Sisi thought about it, the more excited she became.","That was a courtyard house worth a hundred million!","She suddenly felt full of confidence in the future."]},{"number":422,"title":"Chapter 422: Detente","paragraphs":["...","Meanwhile, at the Zhou family's home.","Si Nian sneezed twice.","She poured a cup of tea for the woman sitting across from her.","From what she had just learned, this woman was Miao Chunhua, 35 years old, and the boss of a clothing factory.","She wasn't from Jing City; she was from Jinhua.","In her early years, she followed her parents in business and met Chen Nan, who had also ventured into business with his parents. They got to know each other and eventually married.","Although she wasn't a local, her family's financial conditions were excellent.","Her parents ran a wholesale clothing factory in Jinhua.","Whether she had inherited her parents' talent or not, she started her own clothing brand after getting married.","A couple of years ago, when Chen Nan's business was struggling, it was her financial support that allowed him to keep his electronics business afloat.","In short, she was a very formidable woman.","Si Nian didn't like doing business; she hated dealing with stressful things.","Perhaps she just didn't have such grand ambitions. Being an ordinary person was fine with her. As long as she had enough money to spend and didn't have to worry about food and clothing, she was satisfied.","But rich people had their own troubles. For example, Sister Miao in front of her was currently looking miserable, crying about her hardships.","\"What's the use of making money? My husband's heart isn't with me. He even despises me for being old and messes around with young people all day long.\"","Si Nian's mouth twitched. \"Actually, you aren't old. Um... it's just that your style of dress makes you look a bit mature.\"","Truth be told, Miao Chunhua's outfit was the most fashionable style for wealthy ladies at the moment.","It certainly gave off a commanding presence.","One look and you could tell she was a rich woman.","It's just that men all prefer young and beautiful women.","That's true in any era.","It was clearly the man's fault, yet the woman had to bear the pain.","If you asked Si Nian, if she were in Miao Chunhua's shoes, wouldn't she just keep half a dozen handsome young boy toys?","Why fixate on that old bald guy?","It wasn't like she lacked money.","\"Sister, then what kind of clothes do you think would suit me?\"","Si Nian felt a headache coming on. You run a clothing business and don't even know what suits you? Is your business success really just because of the Jinhua merchant halo?","She said, \"You could straighten your hair; curly hair makes you look too old. Also, while this outfit is nice, it doesn't suit your skin tone. Your skin is quite fair, and the color of these clothes is too dark. Your lipstick should be a lighter shade too...\"","She spoke based on her own aesthetic sense.","Miao Chunhua listened very earnestly. \"You are so pretty, I trust you.\"","Si Nian thought: Well, thank you very much.","\"By the way, did you come to find me just to see what I look like?\"","Si Nian asked.","Was this big boss really that free?","Miao Chunhua smiled awkwardly. \"Not exactly. Actually, there is another important matter. I heard that a murder took place here ten years ago, causing many people in the neighborhood to move away. Is that right?\"","Si Nian nodded.","\"Lao Chen told me about this. He said it was his fault for selling the house to you without mentioning this issue beforehand. I happen to have a younger cousin who is a deputy director at the local police station. I'll have him get some people to thoroughly investigate it, try to overturn the case, and get this matter resolved so you can live here in peace.\"","\"Actually, I think this location is quite good. It's close to the center and near everything. The way I see it, aside from the ugly rumors, there's no downside at all. Who knows, maybe one day the government will support real estate trading, and when housing prices go up, you guys won't lose out!\"","Miao Chunhua carefully observed her surroundings, growing more fond of the place the longer she looked. \"I don't know why, but walking into your home makes me feel incredibly comfortable. Even the air smells sweet; it has a really good aura. You might not believe it, but in my line of work, we know a bit about feng shui. I'm very accurate when it comes to reading houses and people!\"","Si Nian was impressed. \"You're really amazing!\"","She meant it from the bottom of her heart.","To think that Miao Chunhua could spot the geographical advantages this early on, and even predict the future surge in housing prices. As expected of a businesswoman, she relied on more than just luck!","Miao Chunhua smiled. \"Originally, when I heard Lao Chen say he couldn't sell the house, I thought about telling him to hold onto it and wait and see. He isn't short on money anyway. I didn't expect you guys to buy it.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian felt a bit guilty.","Right now, it might not seem like much, but she knew just how terrifyingly the price of this house would skyrocket in ten or twenty years.","With Miao Chunhua putting it like that, she suddenly felt guilty, as if she had stolen someone else's fortune.","Alas, one really shouldn't do anything with a guilty conscience.","\"But Lao Chen is too busy and hates dealing with the hassle. It's really thanks to you guys that he was able to get rid of this headache. Speaking of which, I should be thanking you and your husband.\"","Si Nian smiled. \"You're too polite.\"","Miao Chunhua pulled her aside to chat some more. Perhaps because Si Nian had helped her catch a thief, she was particularly fond of her.","She even asked if Si Nian wanted to get into business, offering to show her the ropes.","Si Nian hadn't actually thought about it, though investing wasn't entirely out of the question.","Of course, she couldn't rush into it, so she said she would think it over.","Miao Chunhua didn't press the matter and even invited her to go shopping together sometime.","Perhaps because Si Nian herself wasn't exactly young either, she didn't feel any generation gap between them.","Women always had so much to talk about, and before they knew it, the sky had grown dark.","Only then did Miao Chunhua hurry to head home.","Si Nian liked her quite a bit too. She originally wanted to invite her to stay for dinner, but seeing that she was in a rush and had things to do, she walked her out instead.","On her way back, she happened to run into Song Zhaodi from across the street, who was returning from grocery shopping.","Seeing her, Song Zhaodi smiled and greeted, \"Si Nian, are you not having classes today?\"","Si Nian nodded. Just as she was about to turn and leave, she suddenly saw a hand clinging to the wall of Song Zhaodi's house.","Si Nian: \"...\"","She turned back and smiled. \"That's right. Are you not busy today?\"","She had heard that Song Zhaodi ran a few grocery stores and business was good. Since today was Saturday, there should be even more customers.","Because of these stores, Song Zhaodi hadn't needed to go out and work a regular job like everyone else.","Her life could be considered quite comfortable.","\"It's alright, there are people watching the stores, so it's manageable,\" Song Zhaodi said with a smile.","Si Nian struggled to find a topic. Truth be told, although Song Zhaodi seemed friendly to everyone, she usually kept to herself.","She always went grocery shopping alone, and rarely did anyone visit her home.","Even though everyone had a good impression of her and pitied her, she didn't have any close friends.","Si Nian didn't know what else to say and was just trying to find a topic to stall for time when Song Zhaodi took the initiative to speak: \"Has that Wang Ergou been harassing you these past few days?\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"No, we keep such a big dog at home, he wouldn't dare.\"","Song Zhaodi smiled. \"That's true.\"","The two chatted for a few more sentences, and then Song Zhaodi left.","Lin Sisi spent a few days asking around before finally locating the alley that roughly matched the one she had heard about in her previous life.","Shortly after walking inside, she spotted the sealed courtyard house everyone had been talking about.","This was the very place where the incident had occurred.","Seeing that it was still sealed off meant the issue hadn't been resolved yet.","Lin Sisi breathed a sigh of relief; it seemed she still had a chance.","The incident had been heavily reported back then. She had paid special attention to it, so the memories remained fresh in her mind.","After it was resolved, the female boss and Si Nian had specifically demolished the place and built a temple in its stead. They would come to burn incense during festivals, claiming it served to suppress the negative energy.","Businessmen in this era were quite superstitious.","But rumor had it that because the temple was incredibly effective, everyone who moved in later made a fortune.","Therefore, it wouldn't be long before this area became a highly coveted, prime piece of real estate.","...","Si Nian had no idea that Lin Sisi knew about the events of their past life and had rushed to Beijing to pursue her own dreams.","On Monday, Si Nian and Lu Yao were called into the office together.","The English teacher said, I have reviewed both of your translation documents.","Lu Yao's expression tightened. Teacher, how is it? Are there any problems?","Let's start with you, Lu Yao. I told you that you had two days and could take your time. You were too eager for quick success, and there are issues with many of your translations. In official documents, mistranslating professional vocabulary can completely change the meaning. Do you think something like this can be submitted?","Reprimanded so mercilessly, Lu Yao's face flushed bright red.","It was true. Even though she had excellent grades, she was still just a college freshman. Applying her knowledge to real-world scenarios was still quite difficult for her.","Moreover, since she couldn't ask anyone for help, she had stayed up translating by candlelight while constantly flipping through her vocabulary book.","Even so, Lu Yao had thought there wouldn't be any major issues.","Now about Si Nian.","The English teacher shifted her gaze as she spoke.","Si Nian replied, Please go ahead, Teacher.","Your translation has no issues. It is fluent, professional, and precise. It does not look like your first time doing this.","As her words fell, Lu Yao instantly felt her cheeks burn.","It felt as though she had been given a vicious slap across the face.","But why did you wait until the very last minute to hand it in to me?","The English teacher raised an eyebrow in displeasure.","Si Nian answered, Teacher, I am very happy that you were willing to give me this opportunity, but I have several children to take care of myself. I cannot burn the midnight oil like Lu Yao does. I hope you can understand.","My situation is a bit special, which the school is aware of. Secondly, I feel that this translation work doesn't actually help me improve my skills or benefit me much. This job might be better suited for other students; it is not quite right for me.","The English teacher's face darkened. I praise you a little, and you let it go to your head, is that it?","Not at all. I just think that such a precious opportunity is better suited for students who need the help and want to continue improving their skills. Giving it to me seems like a bit of a waste.","The English teacher pondered for a moment, then nodded. You have a point. I mainly gave this to you both to improve your learning abilities. Since it poses no challenge to you, we certainly shouldn't waste it.","With that, she looked at Lu Yao. Lu Yao, your ambition is worth learning from, but you are a bit too competitive. I want you to properly settle down and focus. I gave you plenty of time, so there is no need to be so eager for quick success just for the sake of competition, understand?","Lu Yao didn't expect Si Nian to give up a job she could easily get and hand it over to her instead. After her initial shock, she felt a bit conflicted.","She nodded and said she understood.","The English teacher told the two to go back to class.","Walking out of the office, Lu Yao couldn't help but ask, \"Si Nian, why aren't you angry?\"","Si Nian looked at her in confusion. \"What is there to be angry about?\"","\"I stole your opportunity, and everyone looks down on me. You can't possibly have no feelings about it, right?\" Lu Yao said. \"Why aren't you angry?\"","Si Nian smiled. \"Competition isn't shameful. I should actually thank you. I don't need this job, so your appearance actually did me a favor and gave me a chance to turn the teacher down.\"","\"There's nothing wrong with a girl being a bit ambitious, and there's nothing wrong with studying hard and aiming high. But you have to know that there will always be people in the world who are better than us. If you try to compete and fight with everyone, won't you exhaust yourself to death?\"","After Si Nian finished speaking, she ignored Lu Yao's astonished expression and went back to the dorm.","As soon as she walked to her bed, she found a small gift box on it with a note attached.","It was written by Zhang Xue: \"Sister Si Nian, I'm sorry. I misunderstood you and Chen Haoran. Yesterday, Chen Haoran and Nana explained everything clearly to me. I'm really sorry and too ashamed to face you. These are some pastries I made myself; I hope you can accept them.\"","She reached out to open it and found delicate rose pastries inside.","Si Nian suddenly felt that she was in a pretty good mood.","When she got home, she put the pastries in the fridge.","In the afternoon, Second Child came back crying.","He said he got beaten up.","Si Nian was greatly surprised and almost cut her hand in shock.","She quickly asked him, \"Where did you get hit? Who hit you?\"","Second Child pointed to the dark circles under his eyes and said, \"Here.\"","Si Nian: \"...\" Uh, she thought those were just dark circles from lack of sleep.","Second Child started crying again but absolutely refused to say who had hit him.","It wasn't until Zhou Zedong spoke up: \"He was beaten up by a girl. It was Uncle Yu's niece, the one who went to Mom's college acceptance banquet before. Serves him right for showing off how tough he is at school every day.\"","So he was beaten by a girl—no wonder he wouldn't say.","Second Child now practiced boxing every day in addition to running.","Not only did he throw punches with great vigor, but his stance was also very stable.","However, Zhou Yueshen was currently only training his physical fitness, so his progress wasn't that fast.","She remembered Yu Dong's niece; she seemed to have studied Taekwondo or something since she was little.","It was normal that Second Child couldn't beat her.","What she couldn't understand, though, was why the two of them were fighting.","Zhou Zedong quickly answered this question for her.","\"He and that girl were fighting over who gets to be the boss of the second grade. They said whoever lost would become the other's underling, and then he lost.\"","Si Nian: ...Good heavens. It's no wonder you become a gangster in the future; you already know how to fight for turf and be a boss at such a young age.","Even though it was just a different setting.","The essence remained the same.","Si Nian's head was full of imaginary black lines.","Seeing her son crying with an expression of utter despair, as if life wasn't worth living, she still couldn't help but want to laugh.","\"Alright Xiaohan, you just can't beat her temporarily. When you grow up, maybe you'll be able to win, and then you might get to be the boss.\"","Zhou Zehan sobbed, sniffing back a snot bubble. \"Really, Mom?\"","Si Nian said, feeling a bit at a loss for words, \"Of course, but Mom doesn't want you fighting with girls. That's not right.\"","Second Child protested, \"She was the one who forced me to fight her, and she even wants me to carry her backpack from now on.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","\"It's just carrying a backpack. Just treat it as exercise.\"","\"I know, Mom. I won't fight with her anymore.\"","Comforted by Si Nian, Second Child cheered up again. He felt that carrying a backpack was no big deal. Didn't his older brother carry his younger sister's backpack every day?","He could just treat her like a younger sister, right?","Having figured this out, he ran out briskly. \"Mom, I'm taking Da Huang out for a run.\"","Si Nian nodded.","Second Child would get scared running alone in the morning, so Si Nian told him to take Da Huang along.","Having a dog by his side was also safer.","When Second Child ran back, covered in sweat, he saw a crowd of people gathered at the neighbor's door.","Da Huang also walked over there, as if sniffing something out.","He pulled on the leash but couldn't even hold the dog back."]},{"number":423,"title":"Chapter 423: Lin Sisi's Failed Detective Work","paragraphs":["As he walked over, he realized that there were many police uncles being led by a very familiar-looking woman who was talking to them.","Second Child was very surprised.","Wasn't this that Aunt Sisi or something? Why was she here?","She seemed to be the woman who was originally supposed to marry his dad, but then despised him and ran away.","Second Child squeezed his little head through the crowd.","He heard her say, Comrade police, I am certain that she is the murderer. She definitely hid the corpse in her house.","Song Zhaodi looked at the strange woman in front of her with a shocked expression.","Her eyes carried a hint of coldness and confusion.","Who exactly was this person? From her accent, she could guess that she wasn't a local. She had heard this accent before. Right, it was the same accent as the children from Si Nian's family next door.","But in their neighborhood, the only ones with this accent were Si Nian's family.","Where did this woman pop out from?","Furthermore, she had an expression as if she had known the truth all along, bringing the police straight to her.","Who was she, and what grudge did she have against her?","Song Zhaodi thought hard, but this person did not exist in her memory.","The startled neighbors around them were also surprised when they heard this. What nonsense are you talking about? How could you say Song Zhaodi killed him? Her husband was lured away by the ghost of that widow.","Exactly! A few days ago, that Wang Ergou said the body was in the well. Today, you come running here saying it's in Zhaodi's house. You aren't some scammer hired by Wang Ergou, are you?","Naturally, everyone still believed Song Zhaodi, whom they had lived alongside for over a decade, rather than Lin Sisi, who had appeared out of nowhere.","They also thought about how Wang Ergou previously claimed there was a body in the courtyard where the widow died, but the police ended up finding nothing.","By now, the police surely wouldn't pay any attention to Wang Ergou anymore.","That must be why Wang Ergou found a woman to come over instead.","Lin Sisi, of course, had already looked into this matter.","Hearing their words, she sneered, What era is this, and you are all still so superstitious? There are no ghosts in this world at all. That rumor was deliberately spread by someone to confuse you. If Wang Ergou couldn't find the body, it must be because someone moved it ahead of time. And that person is her!","She pointed at Song Zhaodi.","Everyone looked astonished.","You, you are talking nonsense! What proof do you have? Song Zhaodi said angrily.","Of course I have proof. I heard your husband was entangled with that widow and was clamoring for a divorce. Your family has five sisters in total and only one brother. Your parents favored boys over girls, so they especially disliked you. That's how you got your name, too.","If you got divorced, you wouldn't have anywhere to go. So in a fit of anger, you and your husband killed the widow. But your husband wanted to turn himself in, and you were worried about being ratted out, so you found an opportunity to kill him too! You threw his body into the well of the sealed-off house.","Lin Sisi recalled the contents of this case as narrated by Si Nian during an interview in her previous life.","She confidently raised her chin and accused Song Zhaodi, Then you logically inherited all of his property, didn't you?","Her words greatly shocked the people around them.","In an instant, they all began to harbor some suspicions about Song Zhaodi.","In that era, a divorced woman had no home, not to mention that Song Zhaodi was unable to bear children.","Many who could not withstand the pressure ended up committing suicide.","And at this crucial moment, the widow died, and her husband went missing.","She became the most pitiful person, and no one suspected her.","Hearing this, Song Zhaodi was stunned for a long while before letting out a cold sneer, What proof do you have?","As long as the body is found in your house, it will prove that what I said is right!","Lin Sisi said confidently.","The police comrades were also shocked by Lin Sisi's speech.","Song Zhaodi asked, And what if you can't find it?","If we can't find it, I will kowtow and apologize to you! Lin Sisi immediately replied!","She remembered it was written in the reports that Si Nian had fallen into danger multiple times for this case. At that time, she had said with lingering fear, The other party is a very smart person. She placed the corpse in a place where she could see it, yet no one else could discover it. If I hadn't been certain she was the murderer, I would definitely have been fooled by her superb acting.","The reporter asked, Then where was the body found?","Si Nian answered, Right inside her house.","...","Therefore, Lin Sisi was certain that the body was definitely in Song Yanzhi's house.","Song Zhaodi laughed out of anger. Fine, then I will let you all go in and search!","Saying that, she stepped aside.","Seeing Lin Sisi's firm tone, the police comrades now had no choice but to go in and search.","If this ten-year-old cold case could really be solved, they could also get a bonus. Why not do it?","Thus, the group of people went in and began rummaging around.","Second Child wanted to go home and notify his mother.","However, Da Huang refused to leave no matter what.","He hoisted the arm-thick iron chain onto his shoulder and, with his back to Da Huang, headed toward his own house.","He and Da Huang formed a tug-of-war posture.","Da Huang was already an adult, large dog.","But Zhou Zehan was still a child. Even though he had been doing weight-bearing training all day recently, he was just stronger than an ordinary child.","Compared to a Tibetan Mastiff weighing over a hundred pounds, he definitely couldn't match its strength.","Da Huang considered itself an adult dog now, so it never listened to the commands of a child like Zhou Zehan.","At home, it only paid attention to the words of Si Nian, Zhou Yueshen, and Yaoyao.","Consequently, Second Child was dragged toward the direction of the Song family's house.","Second Child's shoe soles slipped, and the veins on his forehead bulged. Da Huang, we can't go over there. Mom said we can't go to crowded places.","The surrounding people immediately cleared a path when they saw such a huge dog approaching.","Oh my, isn't this the dog raised by the Zhou family?","Why was it let out? It's scaring people to death, oh my, quickly get out of the way.","Looking at the wide path cleared in the middle, Da Huang felt very prestigious, and its steps became even swifter.","Afraid that Da Huang would cause trouble, Second Child could only shout loudly in the direction of his home, Mom, Mom, Da Huang is going to cause trouble! Come save me quickly!","Si Nian was bathing Yaoyao in the bathroom and really hadn't noticed the commotion outside.","Hearing Second Child's voice, she hurriedly dried her daughter, called Eldest Child who was doing who knows what in the laboratory to dress her daughter, and ran outside.","Only then did she realize that many people were standing at the entrance of the Song house.","Seeing Da Huang walking straight into the Song house, she immediately scolded, Da Huang, sit down!","Da Huang's highly raised neck instantly shrank back, and it turned its head to look at its human mom.","It finally came to a stop.","Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief.","Da Huang rarely lost control. The first time was when it went into the mountains, bit a rabbit to death, and tasted blood.","But what was it this time?","She walked toward the Song family's house. There were many people around, making her inevitably feel a bit confused.","Second Child said to Da Huang very proudly, I told you to be obedient. Serves you right, doesn't it?","Da Huang let out two grunts from its throat.","Seeing Si Nian walking over, its tail wagged unconsciously.","Si Nian patted its head. Behave yourself.","Only then did she ask the people nearby what had happened.","The people around all knew Si Nian, so they immediately started recounting what had just occurred.","\"A woman came out of nowhere and pointed at Xiao Song, claiming she was a murderer. She even said a corpse was hidden in her house. Xiao Si, don't you think this is absurd?\"","Si Nian's eyes flickered. \"A woman?\"","\"Yes, the woman isn't very old, about your age. No, she looks a bit older. She came right up and said she knew the truth. I don't know where she popped out from. She looks very unfamiliar, like an outsider.\"","Second Child tugged at Si Nian's hem and said, \"Mom, it's that auntie who refused to marry Dad and ran away.\"","He thought for a moment and said, a bit uncertainly, \"Grandma seems to call her Sisi.\"","Si Nian was slightly stunned. \"Lin Sisi?\"","\"Yes!\" Second Child immediately said. \"That's the name.\"","Si Nian was surprised. Lin Sisi?","Why had Lin Sisi come to Beijing? Didn't she get into a local university and shouldn't she be studying there?","And she ran over here inexplicably, claiming Song Yanzhi was the murderer, and even knew there was a corpse hidden in her house?","She herself had known Song Zhaodi for so long and understood most of the situation, but it was all just speculation.","How could Lin Sisi know so clearly?","Just as Si Nian was pondering this, the plot of the novel suddenly popped into her memory.","That belonged to the later stages of the novel.","Lin Sisi followed Fu Yang to Beijing, resolutely ignoring the gazes of outsiders, declaring she wanted to do business and make money.","In this era, very few people her age dared to step out and do business.","Therefore, Lin Sisi's bold idea was not viewed favorably by many.","Even the Fu family didn't really support her doing business, but Lin Sisi had the persona of a strong female lead, so of course she had to do business.","And because she was the female lead, all sorts of noble benefactors and opportunities rushed to present themselves to her.","Perhaps she was already famous enough in her previous city, and there were no more face-slapping plots left to write, so she had to change maps and come to Beijing to do business, starting a new wave of face-slapping plots. Thus, when Lin Sisi arrived in Beijing, everyone looked down on her because of her young age.","However, Lin Sisi, relying on her massive female lead halo, easily got to know rich people. Then, the rich people went from looking down on her to being conquered by her female lead charm, opening up a bright path for doing business.","Of course, there were twists and turns. In the plot, an unsolved case occurred under a rich man's command, which Lin Sisi easily solved. In the end, she even made it onto all the major newspapers and became a celebrity in Beijing.","Ultimately, she returned home to fiercely slap the faces of the relatives who had looked down on her.","So, could this unsolved case be the one involving Song Zhaodi?","Si Nian hadn't seen Lin Sisi arrive here; her brain hadn't even considered this plotline at all.","Only now did she realize just how powerful the female lead was.","To think she could run over to Beijing to solve a case while studying in her hometown.","Truly worthy of being the female lead.","Si Nian was just sighing in admiration.","At this moment, Lin Sisi walked out of the house.","She had just heard Second Child's voice and felt it was somewhat familiar, thinking she had heard wrong.","But then she remembered that Si Nian was going to school in Beijing, so she ran out to take a look, not expecting it to actually be them.","She was very surprised. She didn't expect that in this life, Si Nian would also come here?","Even though she had already changed her fate, would she still encounter the things that were meant to happen?","She felt a lingering fear.","But on second thought, that house was still sealed off now, and according to her inquiries, this case hadn't been solved; it was still a cold case.","Then it seemed that the Si Nian of this life didn't have the ability to solve this case.","Perhaps this case was originally solved by Fu Yang, and she had just forcibly hyped it up to be her own doing?","Now without Fu Yang's help, she naturally didn't have this ability.","Thinking of this possibility, Lin Sisi breathed a sigh of relief and raised her eyebrows at Si Nian quite smugly.","What a pity, she wouldn't have the chance to get the courtyard house in this life.","This opportunity was now hers.","\"Sister Si Nian, what a coincidence. I didn't expect you to be here too?\"","Si Nian looked thoughtful. \"It is quite a coincidence. Traveling thousands of miles just to solve a case, you are quite impressive yourself.\"","Actually, Si Nian found it a bit strange, because normally Lin Sisi should still be in her hometown right now. Fu Yang had gone to the Northwest; the main storyline wasn't following the novel's development at all anymore.","But why had Lin Sisi still come to Beijing? Could it be specifically to solve this case?","Lin Sisi said, \"Just a coincidence. I just happened to run into this matter. I really can't stand these feudal superstitious things. Sister Si Nian, you've lived here for so long, haven't you noticed anything wrong either?\"","In her past life, Si Nian had portrayed herself as so capable and smart, praised by everyone.","Lin Sisi had thought she was so amazing.","Now it seemed she was nothing more than this?","Hearing this, Si Nian smiled.","She had indeed noticed, but unfortunately, she didn't want to bring trouble upon herself.","Speaking of which, Lin Sisi suddenly popping out to solve the case was actually a good thing for her.","Having someone else solve it without needing to lift a finger herself, allowing her to reap the benefits—why not?","Right now, she was also happy to just watch the show.","So she played dumb and said, \"No, how could I dare to meddle in such things.\"","Hearing her words, Lin Sisi became even more smug.","However, at this moment, the public security comrades walked out with dark expressions.","Obviously, they had found nothing.","Over the past few days, there had been continuous reports saying there was a corpse in this alley, each sounding more miraculous than the last.","So the public security comrades couldn't very well not come.","But returning empty-handed every time made them quite annoyed too.","Seeing the silent expressions of the several people, Lin Sisi felt a bit panicked in her heart.","\"I'm sorry, comrade. The public security comrades didn't find the corpse you mentioned in my house, which must disappoint you. Being falsely accused like this, I only hope the public security comrades can give me justice!\"","After saying this, Song Zhaodi covered her face and wiped her tears.","Everyone began to criticize Lin Sisi.","\"I told you so, how could Xiao Song have done such a thing.\"","\"Exactly, with her honest and simple nature, there's no way she could do something so terrible.\"","\"Xiao Song is someone who usually feeds stray cats and dogs when she sees them. To be framed like this is too much. She must be severely punished!\"","Everyone spoke out with righteous indignation.","An outsider inexplicably bringing the police to search someone's home and framing them—no one could stand by and watch that.","Lin Sisi's face flushed red as she argued, \"Everything I said is true! You definitely didn't search thoroughly enough. The corpse is absolutely inside her house!\"","The public security comrade, being doubted, said displeasedly, \"We searched inside and out and didn't find the corpse you mentioned. Are you questioning our search capabilities?\"","Lin Sisi was extremely anxious. In the news reports about this case, Si Nian hadn't explained it very clearly, only casually describing it, so she was certain it was in the Song household.","But as to exactly where, she didn't know either.","Refusing to give up, she said, \"You... search again! It has to be there!\"","Song Zhaodi said angrily, \"Who exactly are you? What grudge or enmity do I have against you that you want to frame me like this!\"","She glared furiously at Lin Sisi, her gaze looking as if she wanted to eat her alive.","Lin Sisi was frightened and almost didn't dare to speak.","After all, she had never truly come into contact with a murderer before; that kind of look was something she simply couldn't withstand right now.","Lin Sisi felt a sudden chill shoot up from the soles of her feet straight to the crown of her head, her scalp prickling with sheer terror.","In that split second, she realized that if Song Zhaodi was not brought to justice today, her life in Jing City would never be safe!","Even Si Nian had mentioned in her report that she had narrowly escaped injury because of this.","To think she had overlooked the danger and placed herself right under the nose of a murderer.","Just as Lin Sisi was at a loss for what to do, everyone suddenly heard a loud crash coming from inside the house.","Song Zhaodi's expression shifted drastically."]},{"number":424,"title":"Chapter 424: Find the Body","paragraphs":["\"What was that?\" the police asked, looking at Song Zhaodi with some suspicion.","Song Zhaodi forced a smile. \"It... it might be a jar. It's nothing.\"","\"Isn't your house empty? How could there be a noise like that?\"","Song Zhaodi's family only consisted of an elderly man on the verge of death, now paralyzed in bed and unable to move.","So the noise couldn't possibly have been made by him.","The police immediately led their men inside.","\"Mom, Da Huang is gone.\" Second Child had been focusing entirely on his mother, but upon hearing the noise and turning around, he noticed Da Huang was missing.","Startled, he quickly tugged at Si Nian.","Si Nian's heart skipped a beat. Could it be Da Huang?","She hurried in after them, only to see the group walking into the kitchen.","Song Zhaodi walked quickly at the front. As soon as she entered, she saw Si Nian's large dog had somehow gotten into her kitchen. In front of it was a shattered earthen jar scattered across the floor. Before she even had time to feel afraid, she heard the footsteps behind her and quickly bent down to pick up the pieces.","Several officers looked at the dust scattered all over the floor and asked in confusion, \"What is this?\"","\"This is medicinal powder I ground up for my father-in-law. An old traditional Chinese medicine doctor prescribed it. I ground some up in my spare time and kept it in here,\" Song Zhaodi said, pointing to the medicine on the stove that had been boiled countless times.","The group exchanged glances, sighing softly. With so much powder, how long must that have taken to grind?","When they searched earlier, they had seen Song Zhaodi's father-in-law. He was already breathing his last and probably wouldn't live much longer.","In this day and age, how many women would stay behind to dutifully care for their in-laws after their husband died?","They couldn't help but feel a bit of admiration for her.","It seemed they had misunderstood the situation.","Thinking this, the men prepared to leave.","Si Nian, following from behind, saw Da Huang and scolded him.","\"Da Huang, come here.\"","Da Huang, oblivious to the trouble he caused, wagged his tail and walked over to her. He had something in his mouth and offered it to her like a prize.","Confused, Si Nian reached out to take it. Upon closer inspection, it was actually a human finger bone!","\"Ah!\"","She let out a terrified scream, throwing the bone away as if she had been shocked by electricity.","She was trembling with fear!","The officers followed the trajectory, and once they saw clearly what it was, their expressions drastically changed.","...","Zhou Yueshen had just returned home when he noticed the commotion at the Song family's house.","He had just seen Lin Sisi hurriedly running away with her head down, and thought she had come to cause trouble for Si Nian again.","Now, just as he reached the door, he heard Si Nian's terrified scream coming from the Song house.","He immediately sprinted inside.","The Song family's kitchen was full of people. Song Zhaodi was surrounded by officers, while Si Nian stood by the door, her face deathly pale.","He strode forward, grasping her shoulders and looking her up and down. \"Nian Nian, what's wrong?\"","Si Nian's stiff body slumped into Zhou Yueshen's arms, her fingertips still trembling.","Zhou Yueshen watched the officers digging through the shattered jar to pull out fragments of bone, and instantly understood what was going on.","An officer walked over and said, \"This comrade must have been badly frightened. Are you her husband?\"","Judging by their body language, he had made an educated guess.","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly and asked, \"What happened?\"","The officer briefly explained the situation and said, \"This place is going to be cordoned off now. Outsiders aren't allowed in. You two should go back and rest. If we have any questions later, we'll come find you.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded.","He wrapped an arm around Si Nian and led her out.","He shot a cold, stern glare at Da Huang. \"Da Huang, go back.\"","Da Huang, still oblivious to what had happened, shivered in fear and quickly chased after them.","Only now did he realize he might have done something bad.","Zhou Yueshen guided Si Nian back home. The very first thing he did was take her to the bathroom and turn on the water to wash her hands.","The officer had just told him that she had touched a dead person's bone.","She was terrified.","Right now, her arms and legs were devoid of strength.","Zhou Yueshen lathered up some soap and gently rubbed her hands.","A dead person's bone, let alone Si Nian, even a grown man would be scared if he touched one.","Zhou Yueshen's expression was solemn, but his voice was extremely gentle. \"Don't be afraid. Let's go inside.\"","He wiped her hands clean while holding her in his arms to soothe her.","A bit of color returned to Si Nian's face, though her lips remained pale. Her heart was still pounding wildly, and her stomach was churning with a wave of nausea.","At this moment, it felt as if her lost soul had finally returned to her body.","She murmured a soft response and leaned against the man as they went into the room.","Zhou Zedong had heard the commotion outside. Coming out and seeing Si Nian's pale face, he immediately ran over and asked worriedly, \"Mom, what's wrong?\"","\"I'm fine.\" Si Nian shook her head. The discomfort in her heart had already dissipated quite a bit.","Perhaps having her family by her side gave her strength.","Zhou Yueshen half-carried her into the living room, sat her down on the sofa, and went to the kitchen to pour her a glass of water. He brought it to her lips. \"Drink some water.\"","Si Nian nodded and took a few sips from his hand.","Her heartbeat finally began to slow.","Just then, Second Child returned, pulling Da Huang along.","Second Child came running over with heavy footsteps. \"Mom, are you okay?\"","He didn't know what had happened earlier either; he had just heard Si Nian scream.","By the time he snapped out of it, the whole scene was in chaos, and he had been pushed out of the way.","Then his dad came running in from outside and carried his mom away.","He was still a bit dazed.","Da Huang hid behind him, taking tiny, tentative steps into the house. He kept shooting side-glances at the sofa, his hind legs trembling as he walked.","When Zhou Yueshen's gaze swept over him, the dog's legs shook even harder.","He could barely stand steady. His tail was tucked between his legs, and his ears were pinned flat against his head.","He held one front paw up, unsure whether to put it down or not, twitching it in the air every so often.","The sight was rather comical.","Si Nian had been quite angry, but seeing his terrified demeanor, she couldn't bring herself to stay mad.","She looked up at Zhou Yueshen; his expression was as dark as deep water.","Da Huang only dared to peek at his face out of the corner of his eye, too afraid to look at him directly.","\"I'm fine. Don't be like this, don't scare him.\" She gently tugged at Zhou Yueshen's hand.","Da Huang hadn't really done anything wrong, except for suddenly bringing her a finger bone. Truth be told, Si Nian had been frightened out of her wits at the time.","But thinking back on it now, he hadn't done it on purpose.","Dogs naturally had very sensitive noses; otherwise, military dogs wouldn't exist.","Si Nian just hadn't expected that Da Huang would actually find a corpse.","No wonder he kept trying to sneak into the Song family's house.","Zhou Yueshen withdrew his gaze and gave a soft hum of acknowledgment.","He lowered his eyes to meet hers. Sunlight danced in her eyes, making them look incredibly soft.","He held her just a little bit tighter.","\"It's alright now.\"","Si Nian nodded.","..."]},{"number":425,"title":"Chapter 425: The Mysterious Woman and the Big Yellow Dog","paragraphs":["Over the next few days, Song Zhaodi was taken away and detained.","Police tape was cordoned off around the entrance of the Song family's house, keeping outsiders at bay.","A few days later, the forensic results came out, confirming that the pile of ash was indeed the cremated remains of Song Zhaodi's husband, who had disappeared ten years ago.","Meanwhile, the police also detected numerous bone fragments and tissue inside the stone mill the Song family used to grind tofu.","The murder weapon was thus confirmed.","With both witness testimony and physical evidence present, Song Zhaodi finally confessed to the process of murdering her husband.","However, the police only found half of the ashes of such a large adult corpse.","The remaining half was missing. Upon interrogation, they discovered that Song Zhaodi had shockingly boiled it into medicine and fed it to her father-in-law.","As she said this, the seemingly honest and dutiful Song Zhaodi in the eyes of outsiders revealed a twisted, satisfied smile on her face.","This sent a shiver down the spines of even the most experienced police officers.","The decade-old missing person and murder case was finally solved.","Wang Ergou was successfully cleared of all charges. To compensate him for his ten years of wrongful imprisonment, the police department personally visited him to apologize and awarded him a substantial amount of compensation money.","Wang Ergou had been sneaking around the Song house for days, but he hadn't managed to find a single trace of the corpse.","He had just decided to throw in the towel and give up, and suddenly the case was solved?","His name was cleared, and he even received a massive payout.","He was completely dumbfounded.","He was just lying at home, and his innocence literally fell from the sky.","Then what was the point of all his hard work climbing walls earlier?","Wang Ergou didn't know whether to be happy or sad.","...","The news that Song Zhaodi was actually the murderer shocked and terrified the neighborhood.","The story instantly spread through every street and alley.","Because of her husband's disappearance, rumors had circulated that his soul was snatched away by a widow's ghost, which was why not many people lived in their alley.","This rumor had spread for ten years, becoming a classic tale everywhere. Whenever playful children refused to go home at night, adults would use this story to scare them, warning that if they didn't go home, the widow's ghost would catch them.","The children would be so terrified by the story that they wouldn't even dare to go out to use the bathroom at night.","It turned out it was all fake.","There were no ghosts or monsters at all; it was a murder committed by a human.","Song Zhaodi was sentenced to life imprisonment. Her father-in-law was supposed to be sent to live with relatives, but on the very day she was imprisoned, he suddenly died.","The relatives came, handled his funeral arrangements in passing, and then left.","Si Nian later heard that Song Zhaodi's parents-in-law had never treated her well. Because she couldn't bear children, they constantly pointed fingers and scolded her. So when their son had an affair, not only did they not object, but they fully supported it, saying that Song Zhaodi was worse than a widow.","To everyone else, it seemed like Song Zhaodi didn't take it to heart and wholeheartedly continued to care for them.","Who knew that someone who appeared so honest and simple on the surface could be so cruel and terrifying behind closed doors.","Of course, her being pushed to such an extreme was also largely due to the problems within her husband's family.","This incident naturally made it into the newspapers, but the only photo featured was a candid shot of Da Huang.","\"Famous Detective Da Huang and a Mysterious Woman Solve a Decade-Old Cold Case!\" These massive words were printed across the newspaper.","When Si Nian saw it, the corner of her mouth twitched.","Her dog, Da Huang, was in the newspaper.","As for the mysterious woman, Lin Sisi, she had run away so fast that the police didn't even have time to ask for her name.","Since no one knew her name, they could only refer to her as a mysterious woman.","Everyone said she was the incarnation of the widow coming to solve the case.","Lin Sisi had no idea about any of this. Fearing retaliation from Song Zhaodi, she had taken advantage of the moment the police and Song Zhaodi were distracted by the noise to slip away. She bought a train ticket overnight and fled, not even daring to continue her business.","Because she wasn't sure exactly where the supposed corpse was, and Song Zhaodi had looked completely unafraid of her, Lin Sisi was uncertain if things would play out exactly as they had in her previous life.","Plus, she had only read about it in the newspaper back then, which surely had discrepancies from the actual events, so she didn't dare to stick around.","She never imagined that by leaving, she would miss out on a chance to become famous.","However, her bad luck didn't end there. As soon as Lin Sisi arrived at her hometown's train station, she reached into her pocket, only to find it had been slashed. The thousands of yuan Zhang Cuimei had given her for business were gone.","Lin Sisi trembled with anger, almost coughing up blood.","Yet, the moment she got home, she saw the Beijing television station broadcasting the case.","Seeing the large words \"Mysterious Young Woman\" accompanied by a photo of Si Nian's dog, Lin Sisi almost fainted from fury.","\"It is understood that this case was solved by a young woman who seemingly fell from the sky. However, for unknown reasons, after the case was resolved, this person vanished without a trace, as if she had never appeared.\"","\"The police also awarded this Tibetan Mastiff the Best Search Award. This Mastiff, named Da Huang, has become the only Tibetan Mastiff in the country to receive a police dog medal...\"","\"Experts suggest that if Tibetan Mastiffs weren't so difficult to tame, they could potentially become police dogs...\"","Lin Sisi: \"...\"","So what was the point of her traveling all this way, spending so much on accommodation and transport, only to have her money stolen?","Her business venture failed, her school was urging her to attend classes, and when Zhang Cuimei saw her daughter return in such a sorry state, not only failing to get the goods but also having the money stolen,","she rolled her eyes and fainted from anger.","Lin Sisi's path to business had ended before it even began.","...","Because the case had such a huge impact, people thought the mysterious woman was some sort of incarnation. Da Huang also became a highly sought-after dog, and many families came out of admiration.","They even brought along various breeds of female dogs, expressing their desire to introduce a wife to Da Huang.","When Miao Chunhua heard the news, she also hurried over.","Si Nian happened to be rejecting a female guest who had shown up carrying a Pomeranian.","The woman strongly insisted on introducing her Pomeranian to be Da Huang's foreign bride.","Looking at the petite Pomeranian, Si Nian really didn't even have the energy to complain.","\"My Da Huang is still underage, I'm sorry.\"","She ignored the other party's expectant gaze and rejected her outright.","Introducing a dog wife was fine, but shouldn't they at least be comparable in size?","This size simply didn't match Da Huang at all.","Just imagining the scene made Si Nian feel like her eyes were burning.","However, the woman's dog seemed to really like Da Huang. Before even entering the house, it smelled Da Huang's canine charm, barked non-stop, and even jumped down from its owner to run inside.","There was no stopping it.","Si Nian was terrified.","Da Huang was very territorial; usually, any dog just passing by would be scared away by him.","Wasn't this little dog running inside just asking for a death wish?","To make matters worse, the woman's dog was in heat.","At this moment, it wasn't listening to anyone.","Da Huang looked at the small dog darting over, baring his teeth with a ferocious expression.","The little dog flirtatiously lay on the ground and rolled over to show its belly, but Da Huang didn't even spare it a glance.","Si Nian followed them inside and, seeing this, breathed a sigh of relief. Da Huang's behavior of not attacking females was very commendable.","If it had been a male dog, they probably would have started fighting long ago.","However, his low growl clearly indicated that he wouldn't let the other party get close.","Si Nian scolded, \"Da Huang, go back to your doghouse.\""]},{"number":426,"title":"Chapter 426: Attending a Banquet","paragraphs":["Da Huang had been happily sunbathing. Startled by the shout, he stood up feeling wronged and retreated into his little house.","This was the small wooden doghouse Zhou Yueshen had built over the past few days.","Because people kept bringing their dogs over, they were afraid of dogfights. That was why it was built.","Seeing Da Huang's figure, which was even larger than her own, the woman was completely stunned.","She had never seen such a huge dog.","Evidently, in the news reports, she had only seen Da Huang's bravery and handsomeness.","Only now did she realize that her Pomeranian and Da Huang were not a match at all.","For others, it might be a height difference, but for them, it was the difference between an adult and a nursing baby.","Thinking about how Si Nian had kept refusing, her face flushed with embarrassment, and she hurriedly picked up her dog and left.","Miao Chunhua followed her in and asked, What happened here?","Da Huang has become famous, and many people are asking to use him for breeding.","Oh, isn't that great? Has spring arrived for Da Huang? Miao Chunhua had visited once before, so she wasn't afraid of the dog.","If it hadn't been for Da Huang, her limited-edition bag and ID documents would have been stolen.","At the time, she thought Da Huang was incredibly handsome.","Seeing Da Huang so popular now, she actually felt quite proud.","Si Nian said helplessly, Sister Miao, what brings you here?","Miao Chunhua put away her teasing smile and said, I just finished my work and heard about what happened over here. I didn't expect things to turn out like this. It must have scared you, right?","She had heard everything; the murderer was right next door to Si Nian's house.","Originally, Lao Chen thought that since the house was in a good location, even though there had been a murder in the alley, it wasn't very close, so it wouldn't matter.","That was why he sold this house to them.","But who could have imagined that, by some twist of fate, they ended up living right next door to the actual murderer.","Anyone else would have been scared out of their wits upon finding out.","It was already a blessing that they hadn't gone looking for trouble with Lao Chen.","Naturally, she had to come over and check on them.","Holding several bags in her hands, she passed them to Si Nian. These are some things I picked up for you when I came back from Hong Kong. It's a bag, see if you like it. Consider it an apology gift for Lao Chen's improper handling of things.","Looking at the bag, Si Nian immediately recognized it as a Chanel.","She immediately refused, We were the ones who made the request. This location is very convenient for studying and working. We don't think there's anything bad about it. Besides, Boss Chen didn't know the inside story of this matter, so how could we blame him?","Back when they bought these dozen or so courtyard houses, Boss Chen had even sold them at a loss because of his relationship with Zhou Yueshen.","He had lost quite a bit of money himself.","Moreover, Si Nian knew the future market trends. For such a good deal, she was secretly laughing with joy.","How could she have the nerve to accept their gifts?","Miao Chunhua said, You're still being polite with me. Given our relationship, and the fact that your Da Huang helped me catch that thief last time, I haven't even had the chance to repay you yet. If you don't accept it, I'll be too embarrassed to visit your house in the future.","After saying that, she rummaged through the bags again. Oh right, I also bought a piece of clothing for Da Huang. I don't know if it will fit.","She unfolded the clothes and handed them to Si Nian. Si Nian took one look... it was Louis Vuitton.","...","To be honest, even in the future, she wouldn't be able to afford this brand.","Of course, she wouldn't be willing to splurge on wearing it now either.","Who would have thought that her dog would be wearing something she couldn't even afford herself.","...","Miao Chunhua knew the Zhou family had a few children, so she didn't just buy things for Da Huang. Since she didn't know the children very well, she just bought them some toys.","The two went into the house to chat.","Drinking the floral tea Si Nian had brewed, Miao Chunhua said composedly, Lao Chen is very happy. He said that since that house over there isn't a haunted murder house, it can finally be sold. I only just realized he still had such a house on his hands. Fortunately, he had some conscience and didn't sell that house to you guys too, keeping it for himself.","Maybe it can be demolished or something in the future, and he can recoup some of the costs.","But I was thinking, since the case is solved, can this house be put to use? Even though people can't live in it, it could be used for something else. I wanted to ask for your advice. What do you think would be good to do with it?","Si Nian thought for a moment. Although the rumors were gone, a house where someone had died definitely couldn't be lived in. It would indeed be a waste to just leave it there, so she said, I actually think you could build a temple. I've noticed people around here are quite superstitious. Building a temple to suppress the bad luck and burning some incense might stop people from being afraid.","Miao Chunhua was already quite superstitious herself. Hearing this, her eyes immediately lit up. Oh, why didn't I think of that? That's a great idea! Then I won't have to travel far to other temples in the future.","Whenever Miao Chunhua had an idea, she couldn't sit still. She downed her tea in one gulp and hurriedly took her leave to research how to build a temple.","Si Nian originally thought that Da Huang wouldn't be able to fit into the LV clothes.","Who knew that not long after, Da Huang would actually get a skin disease from the heat.","Si Nian took him to the vet. Because Da Huang's fur was too thick, making it difficult to apply the spray medication, the vet shaved him completely clean.","Now he only had fur left on his head and the tip of his tail, looking like a lion.","But he also looked very funny.","Feeling incredibly heartbroken for him, Si Nian put the LV clothes on him.","Da Huang was now a dog wearing designer brands.","Time flew by, and it was over a month later when Da Huang's fur grew back.","The weather had finally cooled down considerably.","Autumn in Jing City was exceptionally beautiful. The autumn wind rustled, and the yellowing maple leaves were as big as washbasins. The leaves blew all over the ground, setting off the old alleyways, looking as beautiful as a painting.","The widow's house from before had already been demolished, and a temple was currently being built there.","Miao Chunhua was the kind of person who acted immediately on what she said.","In the past, during the crackdown on feudal superstitions, doing something like this definitely wouldn't have been approved.","But now, after the reform and opening up, things had loosened up in all aspects. People wouldn't be so afraid that they didn't even dare to burn incense.","Of course, the most important thing was still the power of money and authority.","As long as these conditions were met, nothing was impossible.","Zhou Yueshen's current work involved a lot of contract negotiations, meetings, and social engagements.","It was then that Si Nian thought of a problem. Generally, for social engagements or attending banquets, one had to bring a female companion.","At least in the future, her colleagues, even if they didn't have one, would rent a companion to keep up appearances.","But Zhou Yueshen had never mentioned this matter.","Si Nian was just pondering what the older man meant by this.","When Zhou Yueshen returned, he inexplicably asked her if she wanted to dance.","Si Nian didn't have much interest in dancing, but she suddenly remembered how, during an intimate moment last month, this man had asked her if she knew how to dance.","She couldn't help but feel a bit more intrigued: Why do you ask?","Zhou Yueshen paused and said, There's a banquet. If you want to dance, I can take you.","He had attended seven or eight banquets this past month.","People often asked him why he didn't bring a female companion.","At first, because it was his first time dealing with such things, Zhou Yueshen didn't take it to heart.","Later, after learning that Si Nian knew how to dance, he did think about it, but then he considered that she still had to go to school and would be tired if she had to socialize with him at night.","So he didn't bring it up.","Today, Lao Chen and his wife had specifically asked him to bring Si Nian over to have fun.","That was why he thought to ask her if she wanted to go dancing.","\"Oh, you're only asking me now? Who did you dance with before?\"","Si Nian looked at him thoughtfully.","Zhou Yueshen paused and said in a low voice, \"No one.\"","Si Nian: \"No one what?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"I haven't danced with anyone else.\"","Si Nian raised an eyebrow. \"So at the banquets you attended before, no one asked you?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded, then shook his head.","Si Nian was puzzled. \"What does that mean?\"","Zhou Yueshen said, \"I didn't know them, so I refused.\"","Si Nian stroked her chin. \"Oh, so that means you would dance with them if you knew them?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","He had the feeling that whatever he said would be wrong.","Seeing him speechless, Si Nian stopped teasing him and asked curiously, \"You asked me to dance, but do you even know how?\"","She was actually a bit surprised. Although Zhou Yueshen was quite attentive, he had grown up in the countryside after all, so he shouldn't know how to do these things.","Unexpectedly, Zhou Yueshen replied, \"I do.\"","Si Nian was surprised. \"When did you learn?\"","Zhou Yueshen thought about it for a moment and frowned, as if it wasn't a very pleasant memory. He said quietly, \"In the past, when the army was running literacy campaigns, they often held social parties, and a lot of people would go dancing.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian suddenly felt a sour twinge of jealousy in her heart.","Oh, he said he rejected others, but in reality, he had already tasted better.","Fine, fine, fine, she had underestimated him.","\"Oh~\" she dragged out the syllable.","\"So you learned it a long time ago. I was about to say that if you didn't know how, I would teach you.\"","Zhou Yueshen said honestly, \"Yu Dong wasn't a good teacher. I can learn it again.\"","Si Nian thought she had misheard and asked uncertainly, \"Yu Dong taught you? You specifically asked him to teach you? Were you trying to show off in front of some girl?\"","Zhou Yueshen looked at her helplessly. \"Of course not.\"","Si Nian curled her lips. \"Then what was it?\"","Zhou Yueshen pursed his lips, paused for a moment, and then said, \"Yu Dong begged me on his knees to learn.\"","He had been very reluctant at the time, but Yu Dong had cried and begged him. Plus, the money offered was good, and Zhou Yueshen was indeed quite poor back then, so when he heard about it, he was naturally willing to help out.","Besides, his reputation was already pretty bad at the time, so he didn't care about these things.","Yu Dong was being pestered by a woman back then. It seemed he had run off to the army to escape a forced marriage by his family, but who knew the woman would chase him all the way there.","At that time, because Zhou Yueshen rarely interacted with women, there were some unsavory rumors about him, such as his roommates saying they were afraid of him, which resulted in him being assigned to a single dorm room.","This led many people to believe that his sexual orientation was different.","So, in order to make that so-called fiancée give up, Yu Dong begged him to help out by dancing with him.","Afterwards, the woman thought Yu Dong swung that way too and ran off in anger.","Yu Dong's feet were stomped on so badly by him that they swelled up, and it took two weeks of rest to recover.","Thousands of miles away, Yu Dong sneezed twice.","A sudden feeling of unease welled up inside him.","He had just packed up a lovely bento box and was about to ride his bicycle to deliver his newly developed lunch to Fu Qianqian.","But the moment he stepped out the door, he was blocked by a woman.","She glared at him furiously. \"Yu Dong, you liar! Didn't you say you liked men?!\"","Yu Dong: \"...\"","Back in Beijing.","When Si Nian heard that Yu Dong and Zhou Yueshen actually had such a past, she laughed until tears came to her eyes.","\"You were actually that kind of person in the past? Throwing away your dignity for money?\"","Zhou Yueshen used to think nothing of it, but recalling it now, he found it rather embarrassing.","Seeing Si Nian laughing so happily, a trace of awkwardness flashed across his face.","This was completely a dark chapter of his history.","If it wasn't to explain his innocence to Si Nian, he wouldn't have wanted to bring this up at all.","And yet Si Nian was laughing so joyfully.","Zhou Yueshen pinched her waist, his voice carrying a hint of danger. \"Is it funny?\"","Si Nian wiped away her tears of laughter while saying, \"Not funny, not funny.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","\"I'll deal with you tonight.\"","Since he already knew how to dance, there was naturally no need to learn.","Si Nian thought that since it was her first time attending a banquet with her man, she naturally had to dress up a bit so as not to embarrass him.","When she used to work, her company also frequently held banquets.","However, she didn't like dancing back then, though she did know a little about it.","Now, she went upstairs to rummage through her dresses. She needed something that wasn't too flashy, but also not too childish.","In the end, she chose a qipao with a slit.","The color was light, and the form-fitting design wasn't too tight, making it very comfortable to wear.","It wasn't too revealing either, making her look gentle and elegant.","Si Nian put it on and pinned her hair up.","With the addition of pearl earrings and a pearl necklace, the outfit looked exquisite and beautiful.","She rarely wore high heels, but this occasion required them to pull the look together.","She chose a pair of light-colored high heels to match.","Although she looked a bit more mature, she didn't look old.","Her aura, on the contrary, was very gentle and moving.","Si Nian also applied some light makeup.","With light makeup, the lipstick color needed to be darker to make her skin look good and glowing, without making people feel she was heavily painted.","When Si Nian carried her bag downstairs, the children were all stunned.","\"Mom, are you going out?\"","\"Mom, you look so beautiful today!\"","Si Nian smiled and pinched the children's cheeks. \"I look beautiful today, but not on other days?\"","\"You look beautiful on other days too, but today is a different kind of beautiful.\"","The second child struggled to describe it.","Si Nian burst into laughter.","Zhou Yueshen had also changed into a suit, carrying his jacket over his arm.","A few buttons at his collar were undone, revealing a patch of bronze skin.","Standing next to him, Si Nian looked even more radiantly fair.","Si Nian felt that one should find a partner like this, someone darker than oneself, to make oneself look fairer.","Whenever she stood next to Zhou Yueshen, she felt her skin was incredibly tender.","Seeing Zhou Yueshen staring at her, a flash of amazement in his eyes, she playfully spun around and asked, \"How is it? Can I hold my own?\"","Zhou Yueshen had actually been quite worried that Si Nian would wear one of her brightly stunning and sexy dresses.","Because on such occasions, many people's eyes would always linger on women.","It was repulsive.","So while he was worried, he didn't dare to suggest anything.","Now, seeing her dressed so gently yet elegantly.","The worry in his heart instantly eased.","\"Very beautiful, Niannian. It suits you very well.\"","Si Nian raised a smile and reached out her hand to him. \"Then Mr. Zhou, after you.\"","Zhou Yueshen raised his hand and intertwined his fingers with hers.","This banquet was held at the largest hotel in Beijing.","It was considered a top luxury hotel of this era.","By the time the two of them arrived, there were already many people.","Chen Nan and Miao Chunhua were at the door receiving guests.","Si Nian only then realized that today was the one-year anniversary of Chen Nan's company.","Seeing her arrive, Miao Chunhua immediately greeted her.","\"Sister, come quick! I was worried you wouldn't come. Little Zhou said you don't like these kinds of occasions.\"","Si Nian smiled awkwardly. Little Zhou hadn't told her about this at all.","She turned her head to look at the man beside her. \"Yes, my Little Zhou was worried that I'm too busy with my studies, so he didn't mention it much.\"","Zhou Yueshen, who had just been called Little Zhou: \"......\"","At this moment, a secretary wearing a red evening gown with her hair styled in large, bouncy curls walked over.","\"Mr. Zhou, you're here.\" As she spoke, she reached out to take his coat for him.","Si Nian cast a brief glance over.","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod but did not hand it to her. \"We are off the clock now, Secretary Chen. You are free to do as you please; you don't need to attend to me.\"","Secretary Chen paused, only then noticing Si Nian, who was talking with Miao Chunhua.","She did not look embarrassed at all. Giving a polite nod as a greeting, she took her leave first.","Si Nian withdrew her gaze.","Miao Chunhua, however, could not help but speak up."]},{"number":427,"title":"Chapter 427: The Dominant","paragraphs":["\"Isn't that Old Chen's former secretary, Chen Mi?\"","She stared at the other woman's slender back, her hot figure, and the alluring sway of her narrow waist as she walked, clicking her tongue a few times.","\"I thought she was fired, but to think she was actually assigned to your Zhou.\" Her voice carried a hint of displeasure.","If it weren't for the occasion, she probably would have picked a fight right then and there.","Si Nian withdrew her gaze and asked her, \"This secretary used to work for President Chen?\"","\"Yes, Old Chen really valued her. He said she was educated and talented. Although young, she isn't arrogant or rash, does her job well, and makes him look good when he takes her out. I was already very uncomfortable with it before.\"","Miao Chunhua had argued with Chen Nan about this matter quite a few times.","In the past, whenever Chen Nan attended banquets, he would take her along.","However, Miao Chunhua was a tough woman who wasn't very good at dancing, and she disliked the typical male dinner party antics, feeling that they were highly disrespectful to her.","So the two of them would always fight over this.","Later, when Chen Nan wanted to collaborate with foreigners and hired Chen Mi, he never took Miao Chunhua out to banquets again.","Miao Chunhua was a boss herself. Several times, people had told her they saw Chen Nan and his secretary coming and going together, looking very close, and warned her to be careful.","After all, Chen Mi was young, beautiful, had a great figure, and was well-educated.","What man wouldn't be tempted?","Miao Chunhua went back and fought with Chen Nan, demanding he replace her.","Chen Nan agreed verbally and changed his assistant.","Miao Chunhua actually thought he had fired her.","Who would have thought, he actually assigned her to Zhou Yueshen.","She was furious, and unable to hold back, she viciously pinched the man beside her.","Chen Nan's face twisted in pain.","\"What are you doing now?\"","\"Didn't you say Chen Mi had already resigned? What is the meaning of this?\"","Chen Nan froze for a moment. Recovering himself, his face darkened. \"Do you think an assistant like her is so easy to find? She's talented and speaks multiple foreign languages. She hasn't made any mistakes. If I fire her for no reason, what would people say?\"","\"She was working out perfectly well for me, but you insisted I replace her. Fine, I changed assistants and transferred her to work under Old Zhou. What are you still dissatisfied with?\"","Chen Nan felt he was being wronged. Talented people were hard to find, not to mention an assistant like Chen Mi, who was beautiful, good at socializing, and could hold her own at events—she was one in a hundred.","Having to replace someone and potentially getting someone incompetent, only to have to replace them again, was a huge hassle for him.","Besides, she hadn't done anything out of line. What had she ever done to Miao Chunhua to warrant such trouble?","Because of this incident, he had been mocked by outsiders as being henpecked, losing a lot of face in public.","Now that he had changed assistants, she was still causing trouble.","Women were truly too troublesome.","\"I don't care. That woman doesn't look like a good person at all. Aren't you just harming others by doing this?\"","Miao Chunhua felt psychologically uncomfortable just seeing Chen Mi. Her woman's sixth sense had always been very accurate.","Naturally, she trusted her intuition.","Hearing this, Chen Nan looked impatient. \"I think you're just jealous that she's younger and prettier than you. I really don't get why you women are so troublesome. Whenever you see a woman prettier than yourselves, your imaginations run wild, always suspecting this and that. Even if you aren't tired, I am! We'll talk about this later. I'm busy right now.\"","He waved his hand impatiently.","Although Miao Chunhua was a strong, independent woman who ran her own business and made her own money, being treated this way by her husband still made her eyes redden with unshed tears.","Watching this scene, Si Nian felt disgusted—disgusted with Chen Nan, of course.","He didn't think he was doing anything wrong, only feeling that others were being overly sensitive, completely ignoring his wife's inner feelings.","Chauvinistic men like him were simply among the types of men she hated the most.","She stepped forward to comfort Miao Chunhua, saying, \"I'm sorry, Sister Miao. I shouldn't have let you ask about this.\"","Miao Chunhua forced a smile. \"Not at all. It's just my big mouth. You didn't ask me to inquire for you; I just couldn't stand the sight of it. But this company was founded by Chen Nan, and I don't have much room to interfere. If anyone should be apologizing, it's me apologizing to you.\"","Chen Nan had caused them quite a bit of trouble, and Zhou Yueshen was currently even helping him expand his company.","If the relationship between this husband and wife was truly ruined because of that woman, her conscience would be uneasy for the rest of her life.","Working in this industry, Miao Chunhua had seen too many men and women like this. She knew very well how filthy their private relationships could be under the guise of a boss and secretary.","The women were up to no good, and the men were even worse.","Although Chen Nan hadn't done anything with the other party yet, she could already feel his impatience towards her.","The respect and cherishing he had for her when they first got together were long gone.","If it weren't for the fact that their children were already so old, she sometimes really wanted to cause a massive scene.","Si Nian shook her head.","Subconsciously, she looked over at Zhou Yueshen, who was talking to someone nearby.","His eyes were lowered, his side profile cold and handsome.","As the saying goes, clothes make the man. With Zhou Yueshen's current status, coupled with his attire and that cool, handsome face...","It was hard for him not to attract the attention of the opposite sex.","Although their relationship was still very good right now, and Zhou Yueshen treated her well...","They hadn't been married for long.","So many couples were deeply in love and incredibly sweet when they first got married.","But as time passed, people changed.","She didn't want that day to come, but Si Nian would never be arrogant enough to think she could change anything.","If a person was truly going to change, she wouldn't choose to compromise and suffer in silence.","In her eyes, love had never been her top priority.","Si Nian withdrew her gaze.","Just missing the glance Zhou Yueshen cast in her direction.","He paused; for a brief moment just now, his heart had skipped a beat.","For no apparent reason.","But looking at Si Nian, she was just talking with Miao Chunhua.","Nothing seemed different.","Zhou Yueshen frowned slightly, casually finished his conversation with the person beside him, and walked over.","His large hand naturally wrapped around her shoulder.","He asked softly, \"Are you hungry?\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"I'm okay.\"","Zhou Yueshen checked the time; it was about time.","\"Let's go inside and get something to eat first.\"","Si Nian nodded.","The group walked inside.","Si Nian was seated next to Miao Chunhua.","On the other side of Miao Chunhua was Chen Nan and his assistant.","His assistant was a man, also very young.","Zhou Yueshen sat beside Si Nian, and further down were Chen Mi and the other business partners.","Everyone was talking and laughing.","Many people already knew Chen Mi because she often accompanied them on trips.","However, it was Si Nian's first time meeting her.","She was beautiful, with bright, striking, and elegant facial features.","The qipao she wore gave her a gentle and refined temperament.","Miao Chunhua wore exquisite makeup and a fur coat; sitting together, the two of them looked like a noble lady and a wealthy young miss.","The people who usually stared at Chen Mi were now frequently casting their gazes upon Si Nian.","Chen Mi was already bright and beautiful enough.","But Si Nian's features were even more delicate and gorgeous than hers.","However, at these men's dinner tables, women were never the main subject.","It was mostly about work; in their eyes, women were nothing more than a decorative foil.","At this moment, people were raising their glasses to offer toasts. \"President Zhou, it's our first time meeting. Let me toast you.\"","Someone raised a glass to Zhou Yueshen.","Chen Mi immediately stood up and smiled softly, \"President Wang, our President Zhou is driving today, so it's not convenient for him to drink. I'll apologize on his behalf and drink this for him.\"","Zhou Yueshen frowned and was just about to speak up and stop her.","But Chen Mi cheerfully downed the drink first as a sign of respect.","It's true that many assistants are used to take the drinks for their bosses.","No one found it strange.","They immediately praised her as a reliable and sensible secretary.","Chen Mi smiled back politely.","She sat down after finishing the drink.","Seeing Si Nian staring at her, she smiled and said, \"Mrs. Zhou, please don't misunderstand. I just thought that President Zhou has been drinking a bit too much these past few days, so I stepped up to take the drink for him. I don't mean anything else.\"","These words made it sound as if Si Nian didn't care about Zhou Yueshen as much as she did. It implied that even though Si Nian knew Zhou Yueshen had been drinking at social events these past few days, she didn't know to step up and help, making her less considerate and sensible than the secretary.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow.","\"Thanks. I was just worrying about not finding anyone to take the drinks. I'm very happy that you could step up to help.\"","As if she couldn't understand the hidden meaning in Chen Mi's words, she said to Zhou Yueshen, \"This secretary of yours is not bad. She is quite caring. Since that's the case, let her drink all the remaining alcohol. Don't let her good intentions go to waste.\"","Zhou Yueshen paused.","Chen Mi was also stunned for a moment, and then cast a glance at Zhou Yueshen.","Patient and strong.","She seemed to expect Zhou Yueshen to say a word for her.","Unexpectedly, Zhou Yueshen nodded in agreement and said, \"Okay.\"","He didn't think much of it. Since the other party offered to help, then let her help.","He couldn't read any other meaning into it.","It was already hard enough to guess Si Nian's thoughts usually.","How could Zhou Yueshen be in the mood to guess another woman's thoughts?","Chen Mi froze.","Si Nian wanted to laugh.","Are you playing the 'domineering CEO falls in love with me' trope here?","Unfortunately, the male lead wasn't a domineering CEO, but a pig slaughterer from the village.","President Zhou wasn't abused by women since childhood like those domineering CEOs, nor did he have a sensitive heart like them.","He wouldn't be moved by such details either.","After speaking, Zhou Yueshen added, \"Secretary Chen, don't force yourself too much.\"","Chen Mi: \"...\"","Miao Chunhua watched this scene and chuckled inwardly.","It seemed that this Zhou Yueshen wasn't as shallow as her Old Chen.","She felt much more relieved.","This kind of social gathering was mostly about drinking; no one really touched the food.","Si Nian was busy eating, having a big crab one moment and grabbing a crayfish the next.","It looked like she was putting food into Zhou Yueshen's bowl, but in reality, it all went into her mouth.","Miao Chunhua, who was beside them, watched with envy.","The people around couldn't help but cast glances too.","They originally thought Si Nian was Chen Nan's daughter or something.","But looking at it now, something wasn't right.","As if just noticing her, someone asked, \"And who is this lady to President Zhou?\"","Zhou Yueshen lowered his head and slowly peeled a shrimp while answering, \"This is my wife, Si Nian.\"","Si Nian smiled politely.","Everyone looked at the high pile of crab and shrimp shells in front of the two.","Their mouths twitched.","Was she a starving ghost?","Despite thinking this, everyone seemed to understand.","So President Zhou had such a young and beautiful wife. No wonder he didn't even spare a glance at Assistant Chen next to him.","Coming back to their senses, the group enthusiastically offered toasts to Si Nian.","\"So it's Mrs. Zhou. Please forgive our lack of manners.\"","Si Nian raised her wine glass, but Zhou Yueshen took it from her. \"She's still young and can't drink. I'll drink for her.\"","After saying that, he downed it in one gulp.","Everyone looked at each other and teased, \"Is President Zhou not driving?\"","After speaking, they cast a meaningful glance at Chen Mi beside him.","Zhou Yueshen said calmly, \"Anyone can drive the car.\"","Hearing this, the crowd was filled with admiration again.","They continued to toast Si Nian one after another.","Zhou Yueshen drank them all without changing his expression.","Si Nian couldn't bear to watch anymore.","These people really loved to stir up trouble and watch the drama.","Fortunately, the dancing started at this moment.","Many people led their female companions to dance.","They hardly ate a few bites of food; they were all here for the dancing.","Si Nian didn't understand the hobbies of these rich people, but she respected them.","She had eaten and drunk to her heart's content and was quite satisfied. She sipped her tea while enjoying the dancing.","Miao Chunhua, who was beside her, saw Si Nian's status in the family and thought about how such a tough man like Zhou Yueshen was completely subdued by Si Nian.","She felt very envious in her heart.","Although in her eyes, Zhou Yueshen was also very formidable. When her husband mentioned him, his tone always carried admiration and a bit of respect, even though he was younger than her husband.","But his aura was very strong.","She heard that recently, when negotiating cooperations with him, basically no one dared to show him a bad attitude.","His imposing manner was right there, making people look up to him wherever he went.","And Si Nian was still young, even still in school, looking very gentle and soft.","Yet unexpectedly, such a tall and sturdy man had to bow his head before her.","She suddenly felt quite like a failure. Facing Chen Mi's provocation in the same way, she always panicked, questioned her husband immediately, and started a fight at the slightest disagreement.","But Si Nian, experiencing the same scene, was very calm and struck back effortlessly.","Miao Chunhua was extremely envious of her confidence and self-assurance.","Throughout this banquet, Si Nian had always been calm and composed.","Zhou Yueshen, on the other hand, was the passive one.","Thinking again about her own husband, it really was a case of no comparison, no pain.","Miao Chunhua suddenly felt very bored and quite disappointed.","Chen Nan had drunk a couple of ounces of liquor, and his face was completely red.","He came over to invite her to dance.","After all, she was his wife; of course, he couldn't go find someone else.","Miao Chunhua sized up her husband. Over ten years had passed, and he had lost his former handsome and delicate appearance. His face had grown broader, his skin was rough, his body had gained weight, and his hair was somewhat balding.","She suddenly felt a strong sense of disgust.","How could she let herself suffer grievances for such an ugly thing?","Although she was also getting older, she considered herself to be very well-maintained.","Thinking of how Si Nian acted in front of Zhou Yueshen.","She was clearly a princess, but she lived like a queen.","She instantly straightened her back.","She waved her hand in front of her nose in disgust.","\"Look at your dreadful appearance. Who would want to dance with you?\"","After saying that, she tucked her hair back, walked aside to find a young handsome guy, and went up to strike up a conversation.","The other party blushed red and reached out his hand to her.","Chen Nan shuddered, and his drunkenness faded by seventy percent.","Seeing his wife holding hands with another man and about to leave, he instantly burned with anger.","He rushed forward. \"What are you doing? Miao Chunhua, do you have no shame? Who allowed you to dance with someone else?\"","Miao Chunhua sneered, \"I have no shame? Why don't you look at yourself? Do you rarely dance with other women usually? What, you're the only one allowed to dance with others, but I can't? What kind of logic is that?\"","After saying that, she rolled her eyes, turned around, and stepped into the dance floor with the other man.","Chen Nan's face turned red and green, looking extremely ugly.","Si Nian watched this scene and couldn't help but want to laugh.","Serves him right.","Zhou Yueshen naturally noticed it too.","He withdrew his gaze and asked her, \"Want to dance?\"","Si Nian let out a burp. \"Sure, I ate too much. I need some exercise.\"","After saying that, she reached out her hand to Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Yueshen was very gentlemanly. He took her hand and stepped onto the dance floor.","Chen Mi watched this scene, her expression unreadable.","...","The banquet ended.","It was late at night.","It wasn't bad to occasionally savor a life of luxury and dissipation.","Zhou Yueshen had drunk quite a lot of alcohol.","But he seemed to be in good condition.","On the other hand, who knew how much Chen Mi had drunk. Right now, her face was completely red, and she couldn't even stand steadily.","Seeing the two about to leave, she hurriedly walked over and said, \"President Zhou, I'll help you find a car to go back.\"","After saying that, she took a few steps and was about to fall.","Before Si Nian could react, Zhou Yueshen pulled her aside to dodge.","Thud—","Chen Mi fell to the ground.","Hiss—","It looked painful just watching it.","She looked at Zhou Yueshen. \"It wouldn't have hurt to just help her up, right?\"","Zhou Yueshen said apologetically, \"I thought she was going to throw up.\"","Si Nian: \"...\""]},{"number":428,"title":"Chapter 428: Pregnancy","paragraphs":["Chen Mi probably felt it was just too embarrassing, so she pretended to be dead drunk and unconscious.","The two of them couldn't just leave her on the ground and walk away, so they had the hotel staff take her to a room to rest before hailing a car to head home.","Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen squeezed into the back seat. There were other people in the car, but since it was late, it was hard to find a taxi.","She sat on Zhou Yueshen's lap, nestled in his arms.","Starlight and city lights dotted the scenery outside. She raised her hand, looking at the diamond ring on her finger.","It sparkled beautifully under the passing lights. After admiring it for a while, she felt tired and rested her head against his chest. Zhou Yueshen kept an arm around her waist, occasionally casting his gaze down. Perhaps because he had been drinking, his eyes looked exceptionally gentle, and he would occasionally lower his head to nuzzle her hair. Si Nian looked up at him. She wasn't sure if it was because he had been so wonderful today, taking care of her the whole time they were out and giving her all his tenderness.","Because of that, she was actually in quite a good mood right now.","The socializing didn't even seem that boring anymore.","Zhou Yueshen looked down, meeting her gaze. \"Are you sleepy?\"","It was getting a bit late.","Si Nian shook her head and quietly looked at him for a moment.","He carried the mellow scent of red wine—not overpowering, just a faint, pleasant aroma.","His thin lips were pressed into a sexy curve, and she couldn't resist leaning up to kiss them.","One of her hands played with his large hand, gently rubbing the calluses on his palm.","Zhou Yueshen tightened his arm around her, his voice low and deep. \"Why are you being so clingy tonight?\"","Hearing this, Si Nian questioned him in return, \"Am I not usually clingy with you?\"","The corners of Zhou Yueshen's lips lifted slightly as he pressed her closer to his chest. The smell inside the car wasn't great, but she smelled wonderful—a faint scent of roses from the perfume he had gifted her previously.","Zhou Yueshen lost himself for a moment. Resting his chin on her shoulder and enveloping her completely in his arms, he said, \"Of course not.\"","The car could only drop them off outside; they had to walk the rest of the way into the alley themselves.","Si Nian hadn't actually fallen asleep, so she yawned and stepped out of the car.","Even though it was already quite late, there were still quite a few people on the street. Perhaps because it was Saturday, a group of young people came running over, laughing and shoving each other.","Si Nian got bumped into and almost fell over.","\"You bumped into someone, be careful,\" one of them joked.","They said to be careful, but they didn't sound the least bit apologetic.","The person who bumped into her was a young guy reeking of alcohol.","He wasn't very old.","The group consisted of both guys and girls.","They were probably afraid their school gates would close, so they were rushing back in a hurry.","Zhou Yueshen immediately reached out to protect Si Nian. \"Are you alright?\"","\"I'm fine.\"","Si Nian shook her head.","She glanced at the group of young people and realized there was a familiar face among them.","The person was hiding behind the guy who had spoken first. At first, Si Nian thought she was seeing things.","But after taking a closer look and confirming it was indeed Zhang Xue, she frowned.","Zhang Xue had clearly recognized her as well and was now hiding in the back, terrified of being spotted.","The guy who had bumped into her was originally grinning playfully, but when he turned and met Zhou Yueshen's sharp, cold eyes, he jumped in fright.","His wide grin instantly vanished, and he finally seemed to remember to apologize. \"S-sorry, I didn't mean to.\"","Zhou Yueshen withdrew his gaze and ignored him. Seeing that Si Nian was fine, he said, \"Let's go home.\"","Zhang Xue was a nervous wreck, her heart pounding wildly as she feared Si Nian had seen her.","To her surprise, Si Nian acted as if she hadn't noticed her at all and simply replied, \"Okay.\"","The couple walked toward the alley.","The rest of the group finally noticed Zhang Xue hiding in the back and began to tease her. \"Zhang Xue, what are you hiding for? Too shy to be seen?\"","\"Exactly! Brother Wang only introduced you to this job because he thinks you're pretty. You need to seize the opportunity.\"","Zhang Xue bit her lip and gave a soft sound of agreement.","Perhaps she had eaten too many crabs and crayfish, because as soon as Si Nian got home, she felt a dull, sinking ache in her abdomen.","She went to the bathroom, saw some blood, and assumed her period had started.","Come to think of it, her period was indeed late this month. It usually came on the twentieth, but this month it had been delayed by a week.","She washed up and went back to her room to lie down.","Zhou Yueshen went to take a shower as well.","The kids were already asleep, and the house was very quiet.","Zhou Yueshen came into the room after his shower. Seeing her furrowed brows and pale complexion, he went over and felt her forehead. \"What's wrong? Are you feeling unwell?\"","Si Nian felt an inexplicable sense of unease. But then she reasoned that she had simply eaten too much seafood and gotten bumped into earlier; it was nothing major and she should be fine.","It was just that her period felt a bit different this time around.","The pain felt strange, in a way she couldn't quite describe.","Her menstrual cycle would occasionally fluctuate due to various circumstances anyway, so she didn't think too much of it.","\"I probably just ate too much seafood. My stomach is a bit upset.\"","Seafood was considered a cold food, after all. Eating too much of it could indeed cause stomach aches.","She felt a pang of regret.","Zhou Yueshen thought back and realized that Si Nian had indeed eaten quite a lot.","But since she always loved eating those things at home, he hadn't thought much of it when he saw her eating so much earlier.","Si Nian's discomfort grew worse. In just a short amount of time, a cold sweat broke out on her forehead.","Zhou Yueshen noticed something was terribly wrong and immediately sat up to support her. \"Does it hurt a lot?\"","\"Mm... it hurts.\" Si Nian leaned against the headboard, gasping for breath. The discomfort in her lower abdomen was intensifying.","With every breath she took, a sharp, throbbing pain shot through her.","She had no idea what was happening to her.","The original owner's body had been well-nourished since childhood. Although she was sensitive to the cold, she only experienced severe period cramps if she caught a chill.","Usually, it was perfectly fine.","The pain this time was completely different from anything before.","Zhou Yueshen immediately grabbed a coat nearby, draped it over her shoulders, and scooped her up into his arms. \"I'm taking you to the hospital to get checked.\"","His face was tense and grim as he carried her out the door with long strides.","It was already very late, and there were barely any cars on the road.","They couldn't flag down a single car along the way.","Hearing Si Nian's occasional sharp gasps of pain in his arms, Zhou Yueshen's heart clenched tightly.","\"Just bear with it a little longer, we're almost there.\"","Zhou Yueshen moved incredibly fast, eventually breaking into a run. Si Nian felt the wind rushing against her face. She was sweating profusely from the pain and feeling dizzy.","But whenever a streetlamp flashed by, she could see the man's firm jawline. Sweat rolled down his cheeks and dripped onto her face.","He looked even paler and more terrible than she did.","Fortunately, the hospital wasn't far—only about a kilometer away.","Zhou Yueshen made it there in just a few minutes.","Although the temperature in Beijing had already dropped, Zhou Yueshen was burning hot.","His head was drenched in sweat, though it was hard to tell if it was from the heat of running or a cold sweat from panic.","Most of the hospital staff were off duty at this hour, leaving only a few on-call workers.","There was no need to queue. Seeing him rushing in carrying Si Nian, people immediately came forward to help.","Soon, the doctor's examination results were out.","\"Comrade Zhou, your wife is pregnant. She's currently at about four weeks. However, looking at her condition, there are signs of a threatened miscarriage. She needs to get plenty of proper rest. Please refrain from sexual intimacy and avoid any stimulating foods, such as anything spicy or cold.\"","The doctor explained the precautions to him while instructing him to go pay the fees and collect her medication.","But after the doctor finished speaking, the man standing before him still hadn't snapped out of his daze.","\"Comrade, did you hear what I said? Comrade?\"","It took several calls to snap Zhou Yueshen out of his daze. He stood blankly for two seconds, then nodded and turned away stiffly.","\"Hey, comrade, that's not the payment counter. You're going the wrong way.\"","As if he hadn't heard her, Zhou Yueshen walked faster and faster. He entered the hospital room, crouched down, and looked at Si Nian, whose face was still a bit pale on the bed.","His large hand subconsciously rested on her abdomen, his touch incredibly light.","As if he were afraid of crushing her.","His face still held a mix of disbelief and shock, because before they got married, they had discussed it and agreed not to have children.","They only wanted to raise the three existing children.","So even after getting married, Zhou Yueshen had always been very careful with contraception.","There had never been any accidents.","The only exception might have been the last time he lost control, but he had carefully helped Si Nian clean up afterward, and since it was her safe period, he thought everything would be fine.","He never expected that just this one accident would bring a new little life.","This was his and Si Nian's child.","His own flesh and blood.","This feeling was truly miraculous.","The doctor walked in and asked him to go pay the fees first, otherwise, she couldn't be admitted to the hospital.","Hearing this, Si Nian was also a bit stunned.","Compared to the pleasantly surprised Zhou Yueshen, she was mostly at a loss.","She had never thought about giving birth, having always planned to just be a painless stepmother.","But to her surprise, she was actually pregnant?","It came so suddenly, catching her completely off guard.","Zhou Yueshen looked at Si Nian's expression, only to see not a trace of joy or surprise on her face.","He paused, his attitude cautious. \"Nian Nian, the child... are you unhappy?\"","He remembered that Si Nian hadn't minded when he said he didn't want children back then.","At the time, Zhou Yueshen thought she was just saying that out of helplessness.","After all, in his mind, practically no family in this era didn't want children to carry on the family line.","But that was just an ideology passed down from the older generation.","He didn't believe everyone cared about such things. Naturally, Zhou Yueshen didn't value it that much either, otherwise he wouldn't have proposed the crazy idea of not having children.","He was even less willing to force this kind of thing onto Si Nian.","Si Nian couldn't articulate her thoughts. She didn't hate it, but she wasn't thrilled either.","Because having a child was never part of her life plan.","Yet it had come at such a wrong time.","She lowered her head and bit her lip. \"No, it's just that I'm not prepared, and I'm scared.\"","If you regret getting married, you can get a divorce, but if you regret having a child, you can't just put it back.","Although Si Nian considered Zhou Yueshen her closest person in this unfamiliar era, she couldn't bring herself to trust him completely with her entire being.","She was also worried that if she had a child and something unexpected happened later, or if they divorced, the child's situation would become difficult.","Si Nian was the type of person who wouldn't do something unless she was absolutely certain about it.","Zhou Yueshen held her hand. \"Don't be afraid. I'm right here with you. I will always stay by your side. You don't need to worry about anything; leave it all to me.\"","He wiped Si Nian's forehead, which was damp from the pain.","\"I...\" Si Nian opened her mouth with difficulty.","\"Let me think about it.\" She avoided Zhou Yueshen's gaze.","Afraid that one more look would soften her heart.","Zhou Yueshen's voice remained gentle, not pushing her for an answer.","\"Alright, take your time to think, there's no rush.\" He straightened up, intending to pay the fees first so Si Nian could stay in the hospital for observation for a few days.","After taking a few steps, he turned back, stepped forward, and softly reassured her, \"Don't be hard on yourself. No matter what you choose, I will respect your decision.\"","\"Nian Nian, in my heart, you always come first. Even a child cannot compare to you.\"","He bent down, wrapped his arm around her waist, and kissed her forehead.","Neither of them went home that night; Zhou Yueshen stayed with her in the hospital all night.","Si Nian had thought she would be too worried to sleep, but she had underestimated herself.","The moment she closed her eyes, she was fast asleep.","When she woke up the next day, her stomach no longer hurt.","Si Nian's condition had returned to normal, and she felt fine everywhere.","Zhou Yueshen called her school to ask for a leave of absence.","He had originally wanted her to stay in the hospital for a few days of observation.","But unexpectedly, the doctor came to check on her condition and said she could be discharged.","Zhou Yueshen repeatedly confirmed that she was fine before packing up their things and preparing to take Si Nian home.","She didn't know where he had found a car. He first helped Si Nian into the car and then fastened her seatbelt.","His gaze occasionally swept over her abdomen, his expression somewhat complex.","Si Nian's hand also unconsciously touched her very flat stomach, her expression similarly filled with countless thoughts.","She changed the subject and asked, \"When did you drive this car over?\"","She examined the car; it was quite new.","And very comfortable to sit in.","Zhou Yueshen stepped on the gas pedal, driving very slowly.","\"It's the car Chen Nan assigned to me before, but I didn't take it.\"","He knew very well that the more things he accepted from Chen Nan, the more favors he would have to do for him in the future, so he hadn't wanted these things.","They had a car at home, but because it was inconvenient to bring it to Beijing before, they had left it back in their hometown.","But now that Si Nian was pregnant, he didn't want an accident like last night's to happen again.","Although he could run fast, no matter how fast he was, how could he outrun a car? How could he get Si Nian to the hospital immediately?","So Zhou Yueshen had called someone today to drive the car over.","\"A car assigned by Chen Nan?\" Si Nian frowned. Her impression of this person wasn't very good.","It was undeniable that Chen Nan was a successful man.","But he was definitely not a good husband or a good man.","Zhou Yueshen spoke up to comfort her, \"We'll just use it a few times. In a couple of days, when your condition is better, we'll go buy one.\"","He had mentioned before that he wanted to buy her a nice car anyway.","Hearing this, Si Nian fell silent for a moment.","The better Zhou Yueshen treated her, the more guilty she felt.","Because yesterday, she had actually entertained the thought of not wanting his child.","But waking up today, she seemed to have figured things out.","She didn't know why.","Her heart suddenly became very peaceful.","She no longer felt the panic she had last night.","She tugged at the corner of the man's shirt beside her. Seeing him look over at her, she finally said, \"Zhou Yueshen, let's have the baby.\"","Zhou Yueshen almost couldn't stop himself from slamming on the brakes.","He hastily pulled the car over to the side of the road and stopped, his eyes filled with astonishment.","\"Nian Nian, have you thought it through?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Yes. Why, you don't look happy at all. Do you not want it?\"","After saying that, she frowned.","She couldn't bring herself to abort a child, which meant she had to take responsibility for this child's future.","But she also knew that Zhou Yueshen had once said he didn't want to have children.","At that time, his tone was firm, as if no one in this world could change his mind."]},{"number":429,"title":"Chapter 429: He Is Going to Be the Big Brother","paragraphs":["Si Nian originally thought it was because of the three children, but it was also very likely that Zhou Yueshen simply didn't want children himself.","If he didn't want the baby, what should she do?","\"Of course not!\" The heart that Zhou Yueshen had had in his throat all night instantly settled. He held Si Nian's hand tightly and said in a low voice, \"I am just so happy, Nian Nian. Thank you.\"","When he initially said he didn't want children, the three kids were part of the reason. After all, at that time, he had never imagined that he would come to know and fall in love with a woman.","In his mind, marriage was just about finding a partner to live with.","He didn't know that something like love would ever descend upon him.","He loved her, and he would love her child just the same.","It was the crystallization of the two of them; how could he possibly not want it?","Although the baby's arrival was unexpected.","To Zhou Yueshen, it was an equal surprise and joy.","Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief. Although the current situation was indeed not ideal, no one ever knew which would come first—tomorrow or an accident.","At the very least, she wasn't as opposed to having a child as she had imagined, or perhaps it was Zhou Yueshen who gave her the confidence.","The two of them returned home.","The kids at home woke up early in the morning and didn't see anyone, thinking the two had left them behind to go out and play.","They hadn't even realized that the couple hadn't come home last night.","As soon as the Second Child got up and saw his dad wasn't there, he said excitedly, \"Great! Dad isn't home, so I can rest today.\"","Whenever Zhou Yueshen was home, he had to practice throwing punches for half an hour every day.","The weather was hot, and the Second Child would be exhausted and dripping with sweat every time. He just wondered why he had been so foolish to insist on learning this; it was pure torture.","His older brother had it better. He only needed to cook every day, didn't have to suffer under the sun, and didn't get scolded by their dad.","Mom was the best; she never yelled at him.","Not like Dad.","However, there was one benefit: his strength had grown significantly.","So much so that when Zhou Zedong sent him to tie their little sister's hair, he accidentally pulled out a few strands of her hair.","Yaoyao pouted her lips and was about to cry, so he immediately hoisted his little sister onto his shoulders and gave her an airplane ride.","Yaoyao's attention was instantly diverted from crying, and the two siblings started giggling in the living room.","Zhou Zedong poked his head out of the kitchen and took a look, thinking he had heard wrong.","Seeing that his sister really wasn't crying, he turned back to the kitchen.","He grabbed a small stool nearby to stand on and reach the eggs in the cupboard.","He was already very good at cracking eggs with one hand. When he first started, he would get eggshells in the bowl, making him so embarrassed he wouldn't even lift his head.","Now, he used chopsticks to beat the eggs until frothy. Watching the flatbread in the pan puff up like a balloon, he poked a hole in it with his chopsticks and poured the egg liquid inside.","Two minutes later, an egg-filled pancake, the kind that was extremely popular at the elementary school gates, was fresh out of the pan.","Zhou Zedong continued with the same technique, making four in a row before carrying them out.","Seeing his sister holding her head with her hair still a messy nest, refusing to let their younger brother tie it, he frowned.","\"Little Han, what are you doing?\"","Seeing her older brother, Yaoyao immediately jumped off the sofa and hid behind him.","She refused to let her second brother touch her hair.","Zhou Zedong looked at his younger brother, who tilted his head, whistled, and said, \"I didn't do anything. It's just that our sister isn't listening.\"","He helplessly took the comb, sat to the side, and helped braid his sister's hair.","At this moment, Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen returned home.","The Second Child immediately dashed over like a gust of wind. \"Mom, Dad, where did you go to play?\"","After saying that, he was about to hug Si Nian's thigh, but Zhou Yueshen quickly blocked him.","\"Your mom has a little baby in her tummy now. You can't bump into her like this anymore, understand?\" Zhou Yueshen stopped his son's movement.","Si Nian had been bumped into last night. Although they weren't sure if her discomfort was caused by eating too much seafood or the bump, he had to be careful to prevent any more accidents.","Little Han froze. He knew what having a baby meant. The stepmother who had married his dad before wanted to have a baby with him, saying that if that happened, their dad wouldn't care about them anymore and might even kick them out because they weren't his biological children.","Thinking of this possibility, his smile stiffened. He pulled back, looked up at Si Nian, and watched her expression with anxiety.","\"It's fine, I'm not that fragile.\"","Although Little Han was not even nine years old yet, he was already sensible. He seemed carefree on the outside, but he was sensitive inside.","Si Nian was afraid he would misunderstand and think that because she and Zhou Yueshen were having a baby, they wouldn't want or love them anymore. So, she crouched down to be at eye level with the child. \"Little Han, Mom got sick last night and went to the hospital. I'm still not well and need Little Han to take care of me so I can get better.\"","Zhou Zehan immediately said nervously, \"Mom, are you okay now? Let me help you sit on the sofa. Don't move.\"","Saying that, he clumsily held Si Nian's hand as she stood up and carefully walked her toward the sofa. Seeing toys on the floor, he even ran ahead to pick them up and move them out of the way.","Si Nian sat on the sofa, smiling as she rubbed his head. \"Thank you for caring, Little Han. Mom is fine now.\"","Before Zhou Zehan could ask more, Zhou Yueshen walked over, gently nudged his son aside, sat next to Si Nian, and supported her.","Zhou Zehan pursed his lips. Normally, he would definitely squeeze in between them, but now that Mom had a little baby, he couldn't squish the baby. So, he decided to let his dad have his way today.","Zhou Zedong also processed the news, his face full of shock. Mom and Dad were really going to have their own child.","He had been a little worried at first, but seeing Mom's attitude toward his younger brother, he snapped out of it. Hiding the faint trace of guilt in his eyes, he stepped forward and said, \"Mom, I pan-fried some pancakes for you to eat.\"","\"Mom, do you want to eat some fruit?\"","\"Mom, let me go get the remote control for you. Don't get up.\"","The two boys busied themselves running around, washing fruit and turning on the TV.","Every now and then, they would glance at Si Nian's tummy.","Zhou Zehan thought that it would be great if it were a little sister. Then this sister could be his. Since Yaoyao preferred their oldest brother and didn't like him as much, he would finally have a sister of his own in the future.","Older brother gets one, and he gets one. It would be perfectly balanced.","Plus, this sister would be born to Mom, so she would definitely be just as pretty as Yaoyao!","His eyes instantly lit up. He carefully sat on the other side of Si Nian and asked her, \"Mom, Mom, when is the little sister coming out?\"","\"Hmm? Little sister?\" Si Nian almost didn't register the question, then said between tears and laughter, \"That will take a long time. And it might not be a little sister. What if it's a little brother?\"","\"A... a little brother?\" Zhou Zehan frowned in deep conflict, then furrowed his little brows and said, \"Can't it just be a sister? Of course! If it's a little brother, that's okay too. I'll take care of him as well.\"","If it were a younger brother, he could teach him how to box and take him out to play.","Then he would have someone to go running with him.","That didn't seem too bad either.","Zhou Zehan pictured the scene in his head and instantly grew happy.","Oh yeah, he was going to be a big brother too!"]},{"number":430,"title":"Chapter 430: Saving Money for Future Younger Brother","paragraphs":["Tomorrow he would go and share this good news with Jiang Jiu!","When it was time for bed at night, he dug out his piggy bank.","There were only a few bucks inside.","The money he had saved before had all been given to his mom.","Zhou Zedong returned to the room, saw his face full of worry, and asked, \"What are you doing?\"","\"Brother, can you lend me some money?\"","He knew his older brother must have saved a lot of money, because his brother didn't like eating snacks. He usually spent all his money buying snacks for himself, leaving very little behind.","His previous savings had been taken away by his brother, and now he was the poorest in the whole family.","Second Child felt so insecure.","Without money, he couldn't be the big boss, because following a big boss meant getting to eat and drink well, but he couldn't afford it.","Zhou Zedong frowned. \"What do you need money for?\"","\"I, I want to buy a present for my little brother.\"","\"Little brother?\" Zhou Zedong froze for a moment. After realizing he was talking about the little baby in Si Nian's belly, he paused.","How did he know it was a little brother?","He still preferred a little sister. Sisters were obedient, while brothers were clumsy and silly.","But it would be his own biological brother, so he couldn't exactly despise him.","Taking care of one little brother was already hard enough, let alone taking care of two.","Zhou Zedong hurriedly shook his head and said, \"I can lend it to you, but you have to do me a favor.\"","Zhou Zehan nodded eagerly.","Inside Si Nian's room, Yaoyao fell asleep listening to her mother tell a story.","Zhou Yueshen carried his daughter back to her room and covered her with a small quilt. After returning to their room, Zhou Yueshen pulled Si Nian onto his lap, gently poured out some of her skincare products, and rubbed them on her face. \"Don't go to school for the next few days. Rest at home for a couple of days.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian felt a bit helpless. \"I'm not that fragile, am I? Though I don't have many classes these next few days anyway.\"","Because she wasn't like other students who took every class available; she only majored in her own specialty, so her course load was indeed light.","Previously, Si Nian had thought that since she was in Beijing anyway, she would stay a bit longer if she could develop her career.","But now she was pregnant. It was fine for now, but once her belly grew bigger, it would be inconvenient.","It seemed she still needed to finish her studies as quickly as possible.","She had already been to college once before, so finishing in a year or two wouldn't be difficult.","Better to finish early and go back home to enjoy a relaxed life.","She basically understood the housing situation now, so all Si Nian needed to do was quietly wait for it to appreciate in value.","Zhou Yueshen and Chen Nan were doing business together, and it was also flourishing. Once they opened a branch company and returned to their city, everything would be just about perfect.","Zhou Yueshen nodded. In his eyes, there were too many students at the school who loved to roughhouse, and that group of people from last night also looked like students.","If an accident happened, it would be bad.","\"There are no streetlights around here, and it's not safe at night. From now on, wait for me to pick you up after class.\"","\"Won't that delay you too much? After all, your social engagements are all at night.\"","\"It's no problem. I can get away.\"","Si Nian nodded. She could tell that Zhou Yueshen cared very much about her and the baby; otherwise, he wouldn't go as far as picking her up after class. She wasn't a child, after all.","It really didn't seem like his usual steady and mature self.","\"In the future, don't tell the three children not to touch me in front of them. Even though I know you're worried about the kids bumping into me, it will scare them. Little Han and the others are sensitive inside. If you make them think you love your own baby more and don't love them, they will be sad.\"","Si Nian knew Zhou Yueshen didn't mean to do it; he was just being overly cautious. He also spoke rather bluntly, unlike others who would beat around the bush.","For a moment, he had neglected the feelings of the children.","Others might not know, but she was well aware of how sensitive the children were deep down.","Zhou Yueshen paused, then nodded and said okay.","The next day, Second Child went to school carrying a foam cooler.","As soon as class ended, he took it out and dug out a large pink popsicle to give to Jiang Jiu.","\"Xiaojiu, this is a big popsicle my brother made. I'll give you one, it's strawberry flavored.\"","His brother had said that if he helped sell the popsicles for three cents each, his brother would get two cents and he would get one cent.","This way, by the time his little brother was born, he would be able to save a lot, a lot of money.","Jiang Jiu looked at the strawberry-shaped popsicle in surprise, his eyes wide and round.","Just yesterday, his dad had bought him a big popsicle, but it was nothing like this one.","It wasn't as pretty as this one, and it didn't look as delicious.","\"Did big brother make this for me with his own hands?\"","Ever since he gave big brother the globe, big brother had been especially good to him.","Usually, when second brother asked for money, he wouldn't give it, but when big brother ran into him, he would buy him candy.","Thinking of this, Jiang Jiu was so moved that tears were about to come out.","\"Big brother is so nice. If only I were a girl.\"","Second Child didn't understand. \"Why?\"","\"If I were a girl, I could be big brother's wife, and then we would be one family!\"","Thinking about being able to eat big popsicles, Jiang Jiu had a look of longing on his face.","Second Child: \"...\"","Why did that sound so weird?","\"Oh right, Xiaojiu, let me tell you, I'm going to be a big brother.\"","\"Why?\"","\"Because my mom is going to give birth to a little brother for me.\"","\"Second brother's little brother is my little brother. Don't worry, second brother, I'll help you take care of him.\"","\"Of course, after all, we are the best friends in the world.\"","The two of them sat in their seats, each holding a popsicle and licking it.","While looking forward to their future life of raising a little brother.","The surrounding children stared straight at them when they saw this.","\"What is that? It looks so delicious.\"","Second Child introduced, \"This is a popsicle my big brother made. Jiang Jiu's is a strawberry popsicle, and mine is banana flavored.\"","Everyone was surprised. \"Do popsicles have this many flavors?\"","The big popsicles they bought outside were all just white, with no fruit flavors.","\"Of course, my brother invented this himself.\"","Second Child felt honored by association, his nose turning up to the sky as he opened his foam cooler and said, \"Look, there's also soda-flavored popsicles here, this one is watermelon-flavored, this one is mung bean-flavored. Right now there are only these five flavors.\"","\"Wow, this one even looks like it has watermelon seeds, it really looks like a watermelon. Can you share this with me?\"","The children opened their mouths wide.","\"Of course not, these are for sale. If you want to eat them, you have to pay. Fruit-flavored ones are three cents each.\"","\"Outside they only cost two cents,\" a child said, sniffing his runny nose.","\"Could the ones outside be as pretty and delicious as the ones my big brother makes?\" Zhou Zehan raised his chin.","Everyone looked at each other; what he said made sense.","\"If you don't want them, I'll close it. I still have to go out and sell them at noon later.\"","Big brother said to wait until it was time to sell before opening it, otherwise they would melt easily.","But Second Child really couldn't resist showing off, which was why he took them out to show everyone.","He immediately put the lid back on.","\"Don't do that Zhou Zehan, I want one, I want one, okay?\"","\"I want a watermelon-flavored one.\"","\"I want one too, I want the soda-flavored one.\"","\"...\"","Second Child was strong, but Zhou Zedong had only made twenty popsicles for him.","He was afraid he wouldn't be able to sell them all.","But unexpectedly, in just one morning, the foam cooler was empty.","The children each held a popsicle, slurping them until their mouths were covered in it.","\"It's so delicious, this is way better than the ones outside.\"","\"Yeah, second brother, will you have more tomorrow? I want another one tomorrow.\"","\"Tomorrow, I want the soda-flavored one.\"","\"I think watermelon tastes better.\"","\"Strawberry is obviously the best...\"","Second Child absentmindedly hummed in agreement while counting his money. He was grinning from ear to ear, completely unable to wipe the massive smile off his face.","At this rate, he and his little brother would definitely be the best of friends in the whole wide world!"]},{"number":431,"title":"Chapter 431: The Hypocrisy of Zhang Xue","paragraphs":["Si Nian rested at home for a few days. She could eat and drink well, and for the time being, she didn't feel anything unusual, as if her pregnancy was just a dream.","Because the children all had classes and she was too bored, she chose to return to school for classes after resting for a few days.","\"Sister Si Nian, have you been sick these past few days? Why haven't I seen you at school?\"","Seeing her, Liu Nana hurriedly waved.","Si Nian nodded, \"I was feeling a little unwell, but I'm fine now.\"","After speaking, she noticed that Zhang Xue was not around, and asked, \"Why is it just you?\"","That night, she had seen Zhang Xue with a group of unfamiliar men and women, seemingly going out to drink?","At the time, Zhang Xue pretended not to see her, and Si Nian didn't expose her.","But it felt a bit off.","However, she didn't want to meddle in other people's private affairs, so she hadn't taken it to heart.","\"Sigh, I was just about to tell you about this. Recently, Xiaoxue said she found a job and has been skipping classes and taking leaves all day to work. I really don't know what she's thinking.\"","She knew that Zhang Xue's family was not very well-off.","But it wasn't to the point where they couldn't get by. At this time, her studies should be the most important thing.","However, Zhang Xue might have seen Chen Haoran and the prosperity of the big city, so she cared more about saving face.","As soon as she arrived, she went to get her hair done, bought cosmetics and new clothes. Her family had just sent her living expenses for this month, and she had already spent it all.","It wasn't that Liu Nana hadn't tried to persuade her, but Zhang Xue wouldn't listen.","So she couldn't say much more.","Anyway, since starting college, she could feel that Zhang Xue had begun to change.","She couldn't quite put her finger on it, but she seemed somewhat vain.","Si Nian was puzzled: \"What about Chen Haoran? How are the two of them doing?\"","Chen Haoran's family was so rich; if he really had feelings for Zhang Xue, he shouldn't have let her mix with those people.","Liu Nana shook her head: \"I'm not sure either. Actually, in the beginning, Chen Haoran seemed quite enthusiastic about her, but he hasn't come to hang out with us for a while now. Rich people, you know, they have so many friends around them, how could they have time for us? Besides, we just met by chance, there's no real emotional foundation.\"","Si Nian nodded, thinking what she said made sense. With a family background like Chen Haoran's, they emphasized matching social status. Even if there was something between Zhang Xue and him, it would be hard for them to have a future. Besides, there was nothing concrete between them yet. Maybe it was just a bit of novelty at first, probably not even liking.","Zhang Xue was a bit awkward and petty, but it wasn't intolerable.","It was just that since Chen Haoran lost his initial interest, naturally he wouldn't continue pursuing her.","But while he didn't take it seriously, Zhang Xue very likely took it to heart.","Sigh, when a naive girl comes to the city, it's easiest for her to encounter this kind of playboy, giving her illusions and making her think she has a chance.","Before, when Chen Haoran was just a bit enthusiastic towards her, she could get so extremely jealous.","No wonder she was acting so crazy now.","Si Nian shook her head.","At noon, she went to the cafeteria to eat.","Seeing that the cafeteria had sweet pastries today, she was stunned for a moment.","They were exactly the same as the ones Zhang Xue had given her as an apology.","Chen Haoran popped up from out of nowhere, \"Sister, you finally came back to class. I heard the unsolved case in your hometown was resolved; you weren't scared, were you? You haven't come to class for so many days.\"","Si Nian glanced at him and said lightly, \"Not really, just some personal issues. I'm fine now.\"","\"Junior, is she your sister? She's really pretty.\"","Si Nian then noticed there was a woman beside him.","She was very beautiful.","No wonder Liu Nana said he stopped hanging out with them; it turned out he had a new flame.","Tsk, it seemed he had inherited a lot of his father's romantic and flirtatious nature.","\"Not my biological sister, just a relative, but calling her sister sounds nicer.\"","Chen Haoran smiled and said, \"By the way, Sister, where are Zhang Xue and the others? Why aren't they with you?\"","The girl next to him was getting food for him, and she asked him, \"Brother Hao, they have this dessert today. I remember it's your favorite, should I get more?\"","Chen Haoran gave a perfunctory reply.","Si Nian withdrew her gaze and said indifferently, \"I don't know, I'm rarely in the dorm.\"","\"True, I haven't really seen them these past few days either, and we had even talked about going out together.\"","Si Nian gave a cold response, walked to the side, and sat down to eat.","At this moment, Liu Nana arrived. Si Nian had saved a seat for her, and she sighed in relief: \"Thank goodness you saved a seat for me, Sister Si Nian, otherwise I might not have had a place to eat today.\"","She had just packed food for Zhang Xue and taken it back. Zhang Xue came back late at night and was still sleeping when she returned.","Not knowing what exactly she was doing, Liu Nana was quite worried. She got her food and sat next to Si Nian. Seeing Chen Haoran with a girl, she paused, then smiled and greeted, \"Chen Haoran, you're here too.\"","\"Yeah, why is it just you? Doesn't Zhang Xue usually hang out with you?\" Chen Haoran also seemed to notice something was wrong and asked in confusion.","\"She's resting in the dorm and didn't come out to eat. She looked listless, so I didn't wake her.\"","After Liu Nana finished speaking, she noticed the pastries placed next to him and smiled, \"Before, Xiaoxue said you loved these pastries, and I didn't believe it, but I didn't expect it to be true. That day she packed quite a lot and said she was going to give them to you.\"","\"Ah? When?\" Chen Haoran was a bit confused.","\"Not long ago.\"","Si Nian paused. She usually made pastries at home herself, and hadn't really noticed that the school had them too. So when Zhang Xue gave them to her at the time, she really thought Zhang Xue made them herself, and even took them back to keep. Although the taste was a bit too sweet and rich, not her preferred flavor, out of respect for the phrase \"made with my own hands,\" she still finished them.","\"I don't know, I never received any. You must have remembered wrong.\"","Chen Haoran shook his head.","Actually, that day he heard about Si Nian being misunderstood, and he had originally cleared things up with Zhang Xue.","Later, Zhang Xue wrote him a note, asking him to meet in the afternoon.","Chen Haoran was quite happy and went over early to find her.","But he saw Zhang Xue holding hands with a man. He didn't know what the other party was saying, maybe something like a confession. Her face was very red, and she neither agreed nor refused.","At that time, Chen Haoran felt it was quite meaningless.","So he just left.","At first, he did have a bit of affection for Zhang Xue. She had her things stolen on the train and bumped right into his arms. She dressed plainly, had big eyes and a small face, and was very cute, looking extremely innocent.","It made his heart itch.","So he had always helped them out later on.","He didn't blame her for the misunderstanding with Sister Si Nian either, after all, it was him who didn't explain clearly, and he was quite happy about it.","Who would have thought she was like this behind his back.","Liu Nana was also puzzled.","But there was no reason for Chen Haoran to lie about this.","Forget it, forget it, she wouldn't care anymore.","Si Nian didn't ask either, and they didn't mention Zhang Xue again.","Instead, Lu Yao came in to eat. As soon as she sat down, she noticed the group sitting nearby.","She paused, walked over, and handed an envelope to Si Nian, \"This is the translation fee you earned before. The English teacher saw you weren't here and asked me to give it to you.\"","Si Nian reached out to take it and thanked her.","Lu Yao didn't speak, walking to the side to sit down and eat.","These four people in the dorm were really quite strange.","Based on Zhang Xue's behavior, Si Nian would not interact with her much anymore."]},{"number":432,"title":"Chapter 432: Transition Chapter 02","paragraphs":["Originally, she thought it was reasonable for the other party to misunderstand, and once the apology was made, the matter should be dropped.","Only now did she realize that the pastries bought from the cafeteria were likely originally intended for Chen Haoran, yet they lied and claimed they were handmade specifically for her.","It had actually made her quite happy, and she had even felt a little embarrassed for thinking too poorly of them.","But now that Si Nian had come to her senses, she realized she had thought too highly of them.","She had no intention of playing out a palace drama with these roommates anymore. She decided to focus entirely on her children and her studies. She also explained her situation to her counselor. Knowing she was the top scorer in the entrance exams, the counselor was still very surprised to hear she wanted to graduate early and finish all her courses within two years.","The counselor even advised her that haste makes waste, telling her to take it slowly since studying cannot be rushed.","But this time, Si Nian did not listen to the advice.","Seeing that she had made up her mind, the teacher could not say much. After all, since the founding of their school, this kind of situation was not entirely unprecedented.","Let alone graduating early, there were even cases of students being specially admitted at the age of sixteen or seventeen and graduating in just a year or two.","So, she agreed to it.","After sorting things out at school, Si Nian contacted Miao Chunhua by phone, planning to invest in her new brand.","The last time Miao Chunhua saw her wearing a qipao, she thought it looked beautiful and mentioned her plan to create a traditional Chinese style brand.","She had invited Si Nian to join her before, but Si Nian had not agreed immediately.","She agreed now because she had confirmed that Miao Chunhua was a reliable person.","Besides, she was only investing; she wouldn't need to go to work in the future and could just collect dividends from home.","Si Nian was long tired of the nine-to-six job from her previous life.","In this life, she naturally didn't want to join any company right after graduation.","She had no ambition to fight her way through the corporate world to become a big boss.","What she envied more were the wealthy women who stayed at home, collected rent, and played mahjong.","Reborn into a new life, since she had the chance to slack off, why work hard?","Whoever wants to endure hardship can go ahead; anyway, she didn't want to anymore.","Miao Chunhua liked Si Nian very much and would occasionally send her some new arrivals.","Knowing that she didn't lack money and unsure of what to give her, Si Nian made some food and sent it over.","Miao Chunhua especially loved the dried radishes she pickled.","A box sent over would be finished by her in just a week.","Crisp and spicy, it was her absolute favorite flavor.","Speaking of the capital city, it had been a long time since she had eaten anything that suited her taste so perfectly.","Whenever Miao Chunhua was happy, she wanted to give gifts.","She sent gifts for everyone, from the adults to the children.","Even Da Huang had more clothes than he could wear, sporting a different LV piece every day without repeating.","When taken outside, people were no longer afraid of him; instead, they looked at him with envy.","Was this a dog?","This was clearly walking money.","However, Da Huang was too fierce, so no one dared to rob him.","As the weather turned cold, Zhou Zehan's business could no longer continue.","Because it was too cold, no one was eating popsicles anymore.","His face was full of sorrow; his piggy bank was almost full, but he hadn't expected the temperature to drop at this time.","He could only go to his older brother and ask if he could invent something to eat in the winter.","It is too cold in winter, and no one wants to leave the classroom. Selling just about anything would work.","Zhou Yuedong thought for a moment and said.","Making pancakes was too troublesome, and unlike popsicles, they couldn't be kept for a long time; they would taste bad if they got soggy.","Therefore, cooked food was not suitable.","After some thought, Zhou Zedong told him to just stock up on some popular small snacks to sell.","However, Zhou Zehan couldn't remember this job well, because once there were too many items, he couldn't keep track of the prices.","Everyone was afraid of the cold, but Zhou Zehan wasn't.","For the past half year, he had been exercising with his dad, even going for a run every morning.","He was used to it, so whenever people wanted something to eat, Zhou Zedong would have his younger brother deliver it to them without charging any extra fees.","They didn't have to go out, they could get food, and it was still at the original price.","Who wouldn't be willing?","The small snacks prepared by Zhou Zedong sold out in a single day.","Seeing him actually making money by selling snacks, Xiao Bowen really couldn't understand it. He remembered that the Zhou family was quite wealthy and used to live in a big house. Why did they still need to make money?","But seeing so many people buying things from Zhou Zedong, he began to feel a little envious.","Zhou Yuehan also ran around everywhere with Jiang Jiu trailing behind him like a little tail, making many people recognize him.","This candy is twenty cents a pack, and this biscuit is ten cents. That is thirty cents in total.","Jiang Jiu counted on his fingers to calculate, and Zhou Zehan immediately handed the biscuits and candy from his pocket to the customer.","Jiang Jiu was responsible for collecting the money.","They had barely taken a few steps with the money when a big fat boy blocked their way. Are you the ones stealing my family's business lately?","The other party looked at them down his nose.","The two exchanged a glance and took two steps back.","They finally got a clear look at the boy in front of them, who had beady eyes and a large, basin-like face.","He looked older than them.","Who are you? Second Child asked in confusion.","The boy pointed his thumb at himself. I am the little boss of the school tuck shop, Shi Xiang. There isn't anyone in this school who doesn't know me.","His tone was very proud.","Second Child and Jiang Jiu exchanged a glance.","What happens if we don't know you?","Impossible, there is no one in the school who doesn't know me!","The two said in bewilderment, But we really don't know you.","The other party flew into a rage out of humiliation. I am the little boss of the tuck shop. You have to know me, otherwise, when you go to my tuck shop in the future, I won't sell anything to you.","Oh. The two nodded carelessly and were about to leave.","They still had their next order to deliver.","As they walked, they couldn't help but complain, Jiu, did you hear that? His name is Poop Fragrance. How could anyone have such a name?","Jiang Jiu agreed, Yeah, his parents are so weird. He is so pitiful.","Hearing this, Shi Xiang's little face immediately dropped.","He looked incredibly foul.","What he hated the most was people calling him Poop Fragrance.","You guys aren't allowed to leave!","Poop... Fragrance classmate, is there anything else you need? Second Child looked at the other party in confusion.","Shi Xiang was so angry that the fat on his little face quivered. My surname is Shi, not Poop! You, you, you just wait! I am going to tell my parents right now that you are stealing our business, and I will have the teacher confiscate all your snacks!","The two exchanged a puzzled look.","Why? Did we offend you?","Hmph, as long as you know!","Second Child said, Then we will apologize to you. Can you not tell the teacher?","Shi Xiang: ...Fine, say you are sorry to me.","Second Child and Jiang Jiu: We are sorry. We shouldn't have gotten your name wrong and called you Poop Fragrance.","Shi Xiang: ...","The surrounding classmates burst into loud laughter.","Shi Xiang was so angry that his little face twisted. You guys, I am going back to tell my parents.","After saying that, he ran away crying.","Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu looked at each other, completely baffled.","They had already apologized, so how could he get even angrier?","He was so big, yet he was so petty.","The two shook their heads, turned around, and left.","Neither of them took this little interlude to heart, but they never expected that because of Shi Xiang, their business would no longer be able to continue."]},{"number":433,"title":"Chapter 433: I Am a Country Person","paragraphs":["Anyone who could open a tuck shop in a school had connections.","Zhou Zedong naturally thought of this possibility before starting this business, but he didn't expect it to happen so fast.","Seeing the teacher and the tuck shop staff march in to confiscate his things, Fang Bowen, who was standing to the side, was very worried. Although his relationship with Zhou Zedong wasn't that close, they had known each other the longest. Therefore, he was afraid they would be punished by the teacher. Sure enough, the teacher called their parents.","They were accused of neglecting their duties, not studying hard, and doing business in school instead.","Worried that something bad would happen, Fang Bowen immediately told Grandma Fang about this upon returning home.","Upon hearing this, Grandma Fang immediately became worried.","Is their family facing some difficulties? This school too, children doing a little business won't affect them. Why shouldn't they be allowed to do it? How petty!","Then, she added with some pride, This child is really amazing. He knows how to do business and make money at such a young age.","Fang Bowen was also envious. Why could Zhou Zedong always think of these things before he did?","Apart from studying every day, it seemed he couldn't think of anything else.","Even though others said he was very smart, a genius.","But Fang Bowen felt that he was incredibly stupid.","...","Late autumn in Beijing City was very cold, and the wind was exceptionally strong, strong enough to blow people away.","Because it was in the north, it was also very dry. If one didn't wear a mask and a hat, their skin could crack from the wind.","Si Nian didn't like going out much anymore.","Being two months pregnant, her belly had a slight curve and wasn't so flat anymore, but Si Nian still didn't feel any different.","Many times, she doubted if the doctor had made a mistake in the examination.","Because after getting pregnant, she had been worried that she would vomit, eat poorly, have no appetite, and so on.","But as it turned out, none of these situations occurred.","Zhou Yueshen bought her a classic Chevrolet sedan.","Since Si Nian was pregnant, he never let her drive. He drove her to and from school every day.","Everything had been peaceful until today, when she had just arrived home and was unexpectedly called in by the teacher.","The teacher said the two children were doing small business at school, which had affected school discipline, and so on. Anyway, it sounded quite serious.","The implication was that they needed to rush over there immediately.","However, it wasn't Si Nian's first time being called in as a parent. As long as it wasn't about fighting or getting injured, she could accept it.","It was just that she didn't expect the Eldest Child's business to grow so big that the tuck shop owner actually reported him.","The couple hurriedly rushed to the school, only to see the tuck shop's proprietress pointing at the two children and lecturing them.","How did your parents teach you? Doing such wicked things at such a young age. One look and I can tell you are outsiders!","Children in Beijing City were generally fair and tender, unlike these two children who were quite dark-skinned.","It was obvious at a glance that they weren't locals.","No wonder they would do such a thing.","The Second Child frowned and said, I am not an outsider!","Tuck shop proprietress: If you are not an outsider, then what are you?","The Second Child: I am a country bumpkin.","Tuck shop proprietress: ...","Everyone: ...","Zhou Yueshen & Si Nian: ...","...","Seeing that the parents of the two children had finally arrived, the homeroom teacher breathed a sigh of relief and hurriedly greeted them, You must be Little Dong and Little Han's parents. Please come in.","Seeing his parents arrive, the Second Child immediately ran over to hold Si Nian's hand and explained, Mom, my brother and I really didn't steal her business. It's just that everyone was too lazy to leave the classroom, so we helped deliver things.","He was afraid Si Nian would think he and his brother had caused trouble again.","Si Nian rubbed his head and told him not to worry.","Zhou Zedong stood there awkwardly. He had originally thought the matter would be over once the teacher confiscated their things and stopped them from doing business.","He didn't expect the tuck shop owner to insist on calling their parents.","Seeing a young couple, the tuck shop proprietress immediately raised her chin. You are the parents of these two children, right? How do you teach your kids? You look like decent people, yet you let your children do such immoral things.","For the past few days, she had been wondering why fewer people were coming to buy things.","But she hadn't thought much about it.","It wasn't until her son went home crying, saying someone was stealing their business, that she realized elementary school students were actually doing such a thing.","The proprietress was also quite shocked, and her shock was quickly followed by fury.","Because her son said that the snacks and candies those two children sold were cheaper than hers, and they even offered door-to-door delivery, which made everyone very happy.","If this continued, who would go to her shop to buy things in the future?","She had gone through a lot of trouble to open a tuck shop in the school just to make money from these kids.","Moreover, she sold things slightly more expensive than outside.","The children at this school all came from good backgrounds; none of them lacked money, so they bought from her to avoid the hassle.","After class every day, her business was exceptionally good.","No one cared if it was a penny or two more expensive.","But these two kids were suddenly selling things so cheaply and even delivering them. How could she tolerate this?","Si Nian waited for her to finish before asking, Does the school have a rule against children running small businesses?","The other party was stunned for a moment.","The homeroom teacher was also taken aback, then said awkwardly, Well, there is no such rule, but it is indeed not very appropriate.","Then may I ask if my children broke discipline or affected other students?","The homeroom teacher paused again and shook his head.","To be honest, because of what the two children were doing, it actually made things convenient for many students.","For example, if someone ran out of pens or notebooks, they would go and deliver them.","It saved a lot of time.","Everyone actively sought them out to buy things. However, such a situation had never occurred in the school before.","Si Nian said, Since they haven't, why can't my children run their own small business? I am very happy they have such ideas because they dare to do what others cannot. Furthermore, the two children make at most a few dimes or a dollar a day, and they have to work hard to deliver items to others in the freezing cold. While you sit in your tuck shop warming yourself by the fire and comfortably collecting money, they are doing the things you are unwilling to do. Yet you still think they stole your business. Don't you think you are being too harsh?","After hearing this, the proprietress's face pulled as long as an old cucumber. You are being unreasonable! I paid money to open this tuck shop. They don't pay a single cent, so what right do they have to do business here? If this isn't stealing my business, what is?","I didn't steal your business. The things I sell are completely different from yours, Zhou Zedong said.","I don't care anyway. You have affected my business and must compensate me for my losses over the past few days. Also, you must guarantee that you won't do business in the school anymore, or else this isn't over.","Little Dong, how much money have you made these past few days? Si Nian ignored her and asked Zhou Zedong.","Zhou Zedong pulled out a crumpled wad of cash from his pocket, along with some one and two-cent coins. In total, it added up to just over a dollar."]},{"number":434,"title":"Chapter 434: Letter","paragraphs":["\"Mom, this is all the money I've earned these past few days. If this grandma wants it, I'll compensate her with it. I will never do business at school again, nor will I deliver pens to classmates when they don't have any, or deliver toilet paper to them when they need to use the restroom. Since this old grandma is such a good person, she will definitely help deliver these things to everyone.\"","The shop proprietress, who had just been called \"old grandma,\" almost fainted from anger.","She wasn't even thirty yet; did this kid know how to speak properly?","\"You, you...\" She pointed a trembling finger at Zhou Zedong, furious.","Si Nian said, \"Do you see, comrade? This is the money my son has earned over the past few days. Since you claim he affected your business, we will compensate you.\"","Seeing this, the surrounding teachers couldn't help but look at the proprietress with disdain.","Seeing her make such a huge fuss, they really thought the child had stolen a massive amount of business from her.","It turned out to be just one yuan?","Who didn't know that her little shop here made over ten yuan a day?","Earning that much and still not being satisfied, to be so greedy as to snatch the little bit of pocket money a child earned—it was truly a disgrace to adults.","The proprietress was also dumbfounded. She had clearly heard her son say that their business was booming and everyone was buying from them.","How could they have only earned this little?","\"You're lying! How could you have only earned this much? I don't believe it. You must be searched!\"","Zhou Zedong lowered his head, pretending to wipe his eyes. \"I'm not lying. I sold things very cheaply, not expensive like the shop, so I didn't make much money. Teachers, please believe me. If you don't, you can ask my classmates.\"","Seeing him like this, several teachers felt incredibly heartbroken for him.","\"I know about this. Previously, Little Han even gave me a popsicle they made themselves. It was full of ingredients and cheap; everyone loves buying from him. It's not too much for a child to earn a penny from something they made with their own hands. If you ask me, some people shouldn't be too harsh. He's just a child.\"","\"That's right, Sister Liu. Why must you haggle over every ounce with a child? He only earned this little bit of pocket money; how could it affect you? You're really making a mountain out of a molehill. Besides, the child has already apologized. What more do you want?\"","\"If he gives you this one yuan, would you even have the nerve to take it?\"","If it weren't for the fact that the shop owner was a relative of the school's administration, they wouldn't have wanted to get involved in this matter at all.","With everyone chiming in one after another, it was clear that no one was on her side anymore.","The proprietress was choking with rage. \"How is one yuan not money? I'll take that one yuan all the same. Let's see if he ever dares to steal business from me at school again!\"","After she finished speaking, she snatched the money from Zhou Zedong's hand and stormed off in frustration.","The people around looked at her with contempt.","The teacher then apologized embarrassedly to Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen. \"I'm really sorry, I didn't expect things to turn out like this. Sorry to trouble you to make a trip here. It's not easy for the two children, but there's nothing we can do on the school's end. We can only let you suffer this grievance.\"","Si Nian shook her head. She felt that a matter that could be resolved with one yuan was no big deal.","As for her Eldest Child, others might not know, but how could she not know what he was really like?","This little sweet dumpling was actually quite cunning on the inside.","The couple led the children out of the school, and only then did Si Nian ask the Eldest Child, \"Little Dong, did you really only earn one yuan?\"","Zhou Zedong blinked and said, \"Mom, do you want to see?\"","Si Nian grew interested and nodded.","She watched as the child took a book out of his schoolbag and shook out the money hidden inside.","Si Nian looked at the thick stack of bills—there had to be at least twenty or thirty yuan.","Her: \"...\"","Good heavens, he's even more cunning than I thought.","She had thought that at most, this kid had only earned a dozen yuan or so.","No wonder he was targeted...","Zhou Yueshen withdrew his gaze with an unreadable expression and didn't say anything either.","\"Mom, Mom, I delivered them all. I ran around after every class, and everyone knows me,\" the Second Child said proudly.","Si Nian smiled and rubbed his head. \"Alright, alright, you're the best.\"","\"But you can't do business at school anymore. Don't look for trouble. Even though your dad and I fully support you doing what you want to do, the prerequisite is that you protect yourselves.\"","Zhou Zedong nodded.","\"Mom, don't worry, I won't do business inside the school anymore.\"","Since the other party wouldn't let him do business inside the school, he would just do it outside the school.","They couldn't possibly control what happens outside the school, right?","Si Nian smiled and nodded.","The family got into the car and happily returned home.","They happened to run into the postman delivering a package to them.","\"Is Comrade Si Nian here? There's a package for you.\"","\"I'm here.\"","Si Nian raised her hand to greet him, watching as the postman unloaded a large package from his bicycle.","Si Nian took one look and knew it was sent by her parents.","When she got pregnant, she had written a letter to her family to share the good news.","But because it was so far away, the delivery took a long time.","Her family was only just now replying.","They had also sent her quite a lot of food.","Zhou Yueshen hoisted the large woven bag onto his shoulder, and the family bustled into the house.","There was still sun during the day, so it wasn't too cold.","By the afternoon, however, only the howling north wind remained.","Actually, the temperature wasn't that low; it was mainly the wind chill.","Once the door was closed, the house immediately warmed up.","Si Nian pulled the letter out of the package and opened it to read.","It was in the handwriting of her younger brother, Lin Feng. Everyone else in the family was illiterate; only her two younger brothers went to school. Lin Feng was already in the fifth grade and could write most basic characters.","Si Nian had previously bought the two brothers many copybooks to practice their handwriting. Perhaps influenced by the Eldest Child, her brother practiced very seriously. Now, his handwriting was clean, neat, and very elegant.","Greetings upon opening this letter.","We have been apart for nearly four months. Sister, everything is fine at home, please do not worry.","Knowing that you are doing well in Beijing puts Mom and Dad at ease. We all really love the local specialties you sent back.","Mom and Dad heard that you really missed the hometown's cured meat, fish mint, and wild garlic, so my brother and I went and dug up a lot. We washed them clean and packed them for you. Mom said you can marinate them yourself and they'll be ready to eat after leaving them overnight.","My brother and I have finished all the copybooks you bought for us, but I will still practice my handwriting seriously. My brother and I will also study hard so that in the future, we can get into the best university just like you and bring honor to Mom and Dad.","By the way, Mom and Dad planted a lot of vegetables in your yard. They're growing very well, and we can't even finish eating them all. If it weren't for the long distance, we would have wanted to send some to you.","We heard that you're having a baby, sister. Mom and Dad want you not to overexert yourself and to rest well. My brother and I are also worried about you. You must take good care of your health and eat more meat to nourish your body. In the past, we were always reluctant to eat meat at home, but now that brother-in-law's family runs a pig farm, we have endless meat to eat every day. My brother and I have both grown a lot taller. The New Year is approaching, and Mom and Dad say they hope you can come home so we can celebrate together, but if it's inconvenient, you don't have to come. Finally, we hope everything goes smoothly for you in Beijing, and that you can return home soon for a reunion."]},{"number":435,"title":"Chapter 435: Heavy Taste","paragraphs":["Si Nian opened the bag. Inside was a smoked pig's trotter and a piece of bright red cured meat. The savory aroma wafted out as soon as she opened it. Beside it, a jar was filled to the brim with wild garlic and a large handful of fish mint.","In addition, there were some small sweaters, hats, scarves, and shoes hand-knitted by Mother Lin.","No wonder it was such a huge bundle.","Si Nian felt a rush of warmth in her heart as she distributed the hats, scarves, and shoes among the children.","Yaoyao received a small sweater.","Second Child got gloves.","Zhou Zedong's was a scarf.","Hers was a hat.","Zhou Yueshen received a pair of cloth shoes.","Even Da Huang got a little jacket.","Mother Lin had prepared something for everyone. No wonder it took her so long to write back.","The children were overjoyed to receive their new gifts. They put them on immediately and couldn't bear to take them off, even while eating.","Si Nian watched Zhou Yueshen try on his shoes, and to be honest, it looked a bit comical.","It was her first time seeing Zhou Yueshen wear this kind of cloth shoes.","He used to wear liberation shoes, and now that he was President Zhou, he wore leather shoes to match his status.","Suddenly changing into these shoes gave him a strong rustic vibe.","She covered her mouth and giggled.","As Zhou Yueshen inspected the shoes, he caught sight of her crinkled eyes in his peripheral vision and raised an eyebrow. What is it? Nothing, it looks great, Si Nian smiled.","Seeing her expression, Zhou Yueshen knew she was teasing him a bit, but he wasn't annoyed. He knew it looked strange wearing these shoes with his suit pants, but they were quite comfortable.","His mother-in-law had made these shoes for him; even if they were uncomfortable, he would still wear them.","So, ignoring Si Nian's irrepressible smile, Zhou Yueshen wore them into the kitchen to cook.","They had cured meat today, and Si Nian was craving it badly. She went into the kitchen to watch Zhou Yueshen scorch and clean the cured meat.","The sizzling fat was roasted out by the fire, filling the entire kitchen with a mouth-watering aroma.","Since getting pregnant, Si Nian's appetite had grown, and now her mouth was watering helplessly.","Her face clearly showed how much she wanted to eat it.","Seeing her adorable little expression, Zhou Yueshen found her endearing and sped up his scraping of the charred pork skin.","Si Nian couldn't stay idle. It had been a long time since she had been in the kitchen, as Zhou Yueshen wouldn't let her cook.","She took out the wild garlic to wash and asked the children to sort the fish mint.","Fish mint could be kept for quite a long time, and it still had its leaves attached.","Actually, the leaves of the fish mint were edible too, but the roots had many small fibrous hairs, making them tedious to sort.","If they had been removed before sending, it wouldn't be fresh upon arrival.","That was why they still had dirt on them.","The children gathered around the iron basin to sort the fish mint.","Yaoyao squeezed in too, getting the distinct smell all over herself.","People from their hometown loved eating this, and none of the children disliked it. As long as it was edible, they would stuff it into their mouths.","They especially loved fish mint; whenever they ate potatoes, they had to add some of it.","However, since coming to Beijing, they hadn't been able to eat it.","People here didn't eat these things at all.","The cured meat here was also different from what they had at home.","Today, they could finally enjoy it again.","Smelling the cured meat and sorting the fish mint, the children all drooled helplessly.","Si Nian washed the wild garlic clean and put it into a plastic bucket previously used for white sugar, marinating it with bird's eye chilies, ginger, garlic, and soy sauce.","Marinated this way, it would be crisp and appetizing. The ones soaked black by the soy sauce were especially flavorful and delicious, otherwise, it would have a slightly pungent taste.","Si Nian drooled while adding the seasonings.","She didn't even know she was such a gluttonous person.","In no time, the children brought in the cleaned fish mint.","Si Nian chopped it into small sections. She kept some aside and threw some into the pan to stir-fry with the cured meat that Zhou Yueshen was cooking.","The aroma was absolutely intoxicating.","She marinated the rest with seasonings.","With doubanjiang, bird's eye chilies, soy sauce, and cilantro added, it was simply invincible.","She picked up a little for Zhou Yueshen to taste, looking very proud. I didn't expect my cooking skills to still be this good after not cooking for two months.","Zhou Yueshen's eyes softened. Mhm, it's very good, but it's too spicy. You can't eat it.","Si Nian: ?","Afraid she might get angry, Zhou Yueshen explained, The doctor said you shouldn't eat food that's too spicy and stimulating.","Si Nian: ...","That was two months ago. How did he still remember?","The cured meat was done, and Zhou Yueshen had stir-fried a large plate of it. He also made a non-spicy tomato and egg stir-fry and shredded potatoes.","Si Nian felt miserable looking at it.","Zhou Yueshen, haven't you heard of a saying?","Zhou Yueshen: What saying?","Craving sour means a boy, craving spicy means a girl. Look at how much I like spicy food; it might be a girl.","She was smug. She was so pretty, and Zhou Yueshen was so handsome and tall. If they had a daughter, wouldn't she have incredible height and stunning looks?","As cute as Yaoyao and Little Douding?","Zhou Yueshen's eyes lit up. Then I'll let you have a little bit.","Si Nian smiled. Okay, I'll just eat a little bit. I'll be careful.","Zhou Yueshen helplessly rubbed her hair. His Niannian was truly like a child.","They had cured meat for dinner that night. Second Child competed with his dad to see who could eat more cured meat. Whoever ate the most would get to wash their feet with Mom.","Second Child naturally wanted to compete, eating until his mouth was dripping with grease.","Si Nian was impressed. For such a small child, his appetite was huge. He didn't even get sick of eating such large pieces of fatty meat.","He ate at least two large bowls of rice for every meal.","Originally, she had been a bit worried, but when they went for a check-up, the doctor said there was no problem. The doctor also said he was very healthy, significantly taller than his peers, and would be at least 185 cm tall in the future.","Furthermore, Second Child was even darker than his brother. Initially, Si Nian thought it was from being tanned when he was younger.","But after being in Beijing for so long, Second Child's skin was still a yellowish-dark tone.","She then realized that Zhou Yueshen's entire family was of the Yi ethnic minority.","Being Yi, it was possible to inherit this type of yellowish-dark skin.","It didn't look like a sunburn, which would be patchy, but rather a very even skin tone.","Second Child had bold facial features, handsome eyes and brows, and slightly naturally curly hair.","Si Nian couldn't even imagine how handsome this child would be when he grew up.","He would at least be on the level of a dark-skinned athletic student.","Zhou Yueshen's skin was more of a bronze color, but Si Nian felt that he also had some of those genetics.","Because the areas of his skin that hadn't seen the sun weren't white either.","After having a good meal, Si Nian also became picky.","One moment she wanted hot pot, the next she wanted stinky tofu, and then she said she wanted to eat luosifen.","Her taste buds had become even heavier than before.","Hot pot was fine; they could buy ingredients to make the broth.","But Zhou Yueshen truly didn't know where to find stinky tofu and whatever luosifen was.","He had heard of stinky tofu, but he had never even heard of luosifen.","He didn't know where Si Nian had heard of it either.","Yet Si Nian muttered about it every day, smacking her lips as she thought about it, looking as though she desperately wanted to eat it. Seeing this made his heart ache for her.","After asking around extensively, he finally found someone who went to Changsha for goods and would pass by that area, so he asked them to bring some over.","The stuff really stank. As soon as he opened the bag, Zhou Yueshen couldn't help but frown.","He knew Si Nian liked strong flavors, but he hadn't expected them to be this strong."]},{"number":436,"title":"Chapter 436: Bao Le Me Convenience Store","paragraphs":["The dark stinky tofu was still just a semi-finished product, and it wasn't clear how to cook it after buying it.","Si Nian had a very sharp sense of smell; the moment she caught a whiff, she knew it was exactly right.","She immediately opened the bag and took a deep breath, declaring that this was the authentic scent.","Zhou Yueshen's brows never once relaxed as he watched her.","How could such a sweet and soft girl like the smell of this?","\"Niannian, are you really going to eat this? I feel like this stuff has gone bad.\"","Zhou Yueshen was a bit worried, afraid it was unhealthy and would give her a stomachache.","Si Nian immediately hugged the bag to her chest, not disgusted in the slightest, and looked at him warily. \"It's edible, of course it's edible. It's just not cooked yet. Once it's done, it'll be delicious. This is a traditional craft, very healthy! This smell is what makes it authentic.\"","Her posture made it seem like if he dared to snatch it away, she would cut ties with him.","Zhou Yueshen felt helpless and could only coax her gently, \"Alright, you can eat it, but not too much.\"","Si Nian reluctantly agreed.","She felt Zhou Yueshen was making a fuss over nothing.","Although she knew there were many dietary restrictions during pregnancy, the doctor had also said that psychological happiness was the most important thing. She could eat whatever she wanted, as long as her body didn't feel unwell.","Thinking of the stinky tofu that smelled foul but tasted fragrant, with a slightly crispy exterior and a soft, savory interior...","She couldn't even talk about it without drooling.","Making stinky tofu wasn't too difficult. With the semi-finished product, the next steps were just frying it and making the seasoning.","Si Nian roughly remembered the recipe.","She immediately ran into the kitchen and soaked the stinky tofu in water.","Zhou Yueshen followed her in to help.","He asked her what to do.","Although it stank terribly, seeing Si Nian looking so incredibly expectant, Zhou Yueshen felt he could endure it.","Si Nian had him heat the oil to fry the stinky tofu while she prepared the seasoning.","During the frying process, it had to be constantly flipped to prevent burning; frying for four or five minutes would be enough.","Si Nian peeled a few cloves of garlic, minced them, and mixed a spicy sauce with bird's eye chili, stir-frying them until fragrant. The seasonings were limited, so she could only mix it according to her own taste.","Once Zhou Yueshen scooped out the stinky tofu, she immediately poked holes in them with chopsticks, poured in the soul-infused sauce, and then sprinkled some cilantro, chopped green onions, and fish mint to mix. Once every piece of tofu was soaked in the sauce, it was ready to eat.","...","At school, Second Child and Jiang Jiu ran to his older brother's class to hand over the money.","Originally, he thought that since the snack shop proprietress had caused trouble for them last time and forbidden them from selling, he wouldn't be able to make money anymore, but his brother said they would continue selling.","Although Second Child was a bit scared, money was the most important thing to him, so he continued to act as an errand boy every day.","Now that more and more people knew them, he ran all over the place as soon as class ended every day.","He was collecting more and more money too.","Right now, seeing his brother share the money with him, he grinned from ear to ear.","\"Big brother, shouldn't we give our little shop a name?\"","Today, when he passed by the snack shop, he took a glance at the Shi family's shop.","It was called \"Fragrant Eats Snack Shop.\"","He suddenly felt that they needed to pick a name for themselves too.","\"How about calling it Second Child's Snack Shop?\" he suggested narcissistically.","Zhou Zedong's mouth twitched, and he said without giving any face, \"That sounds awful.\"","Second Child said, \"I think it sounds great. What do you say, Xiaojiu?\"","Jiang Jiu agreed thoroughly, \"It sounds good, but can't you add my name?\"","Second Child felt torn. \"Wouldn't that be too long? Big brother, what do you think?\"","\"I don't think much of it.\"","\"Then what do you say we call it?\"","Zhou Zedong thought for a moment and said, \"Let's call it the 'Full Yet? Snack Shop'.\"","\"Offering the cheapest prices so everyone can eat their fill.\"","During this time, Zhou Zedong had observed that not everyone in the school was actually that rich.","There were still many people who couldn't afford things from the snack shop, often swallowing their saliva as they watched others eat snacks.","That scene was just like back at Xingfu Village Hope Primary School when his younger brother would watch others eating snacks.","That was why he sold things cheaply, so everyone could afford them.","Second Child's eyes lit up. \"Big brother, you're so smart.\"","Jiang Jiu also chimed in, \"Big brother is really smart.\"","Zhou Zedong couldn't be bothered with the two of them. He zipped up his schoolbag. \"Let's go pick up Yaoyao and head home.\"","Second Child and Jiang Jiu hurriedly followed, but the three of them had barely taken two steps when they were blocked.","It was their homeroom teacher and the proprietress of the snack shop.","The proprietress's face was pulled as long as an old cucumber.","\"You kids, stop right there!\"","She scolded loudly.","The group stopped in their tracks.","Seeing clearly who had come, Second Child and Jiang Jiu immediately hid behind Zhou Zedong.","\"We're doomed, we're doomed. The old grandma is here to cause trouble for us again, brother. What do we do?\"","Zhou Zedong didn't reply, but instead looked at the other party with a remarkably calm expression. \"Grandma, is there something you need us for?\"","Being called grandma again with double the impact, the proprietress was so angry that the fat on her face trembled.","Her family was prone to gaining weight; her son was plump and so was she, making her look like a wealthy madam.","It was no wonder the two of them still mistook her for a grandma.","\"You two, who let you continue selling things? Was the lesson you got last time not enough?\"","\"And how are you acting as a teacher? Didn't you promise me last time that you wouldn't let them steal my business? Do you still want your job?\" After saying this, still feeling aggrieved, she even blamed the homeroom teacher standing to the side.","The homeroom teacher's expression didn't look too good either as she asked, \"Little Dong, didn't we agree last time that you weren't allowed to sell things in school anymore? Why are you still disobeying?\"","Zhou Zedong said, \"Teacher, we didn't sell them in school.\"","\"You're still lying! My son saw it with his own eyes! To think you're still lying, how on earth did the adults teach you? You're full of nonsense!\"","\"Some classmates did indeed see you still selling. Little Dong, you cannot lie to your teacher!\" the homeroom teacher frowned and said.","Zhou Zedong had very good grades, and she valued this child highly.","But this kind of thing just had to happen.","Although his mother was right—it was truly admirable for a child to have ideas and the courage to act on them, knowing how to do business and make money at such a young age, and in this manner—she actually admired him quite a bit too.","But the snack shop proprietress happened to be petty and unhappy about it, leaving her caught in a dilemma.","On one hand, she didn't want to offend the other party and bring trouble upon herself.","On the other hand, she didn't want to unfairly blame her student.","Being a teacher was just too difficult.","Zhou Zedong said, \"Teacher, I really didn't sell them in school. I remembered everything you said last time. Since this grandma wouldn't let us sell in school, we thought we would go sell outside the school. It's just that some students don't want to go out, so we just delivered the items inside to them. Is it not allowed for us to help our classmates bring things in from outside the school?\"","As soon as these words came out, the homeroom teacher was stunned.","\"Is... is that so?\"","\"Yes, because we can't do business in school, I figured we would do it outside the school. This way, the old grandma can't still control us, right?\"","\"Teacher, we've already compromised this much, did we still do something wrong?\""]},{"number":437,"title":"Chapter 437: Covering Up for Someone's Faults","paragraphs":["He lowered his head, looking somewhat sad.","It was as if he had been pushed into a corner with no way out.","Seeing their usually tough oldest brother driven to such a state, Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu were also furious.","As soon as Zhou Zedong finished speaking, his younger brother's high-pitched scolding rang out.","\"You nasty crazy old hag, don't even think about extorting the money my brother and I earned. Our money is saved to buy gifts for our future little brother!\"","After Second Child finished scolding, Jiang Jiu also threw a tantrum: \"Oh heavens, are you going to let people do business in peace or not? This business is impossible to run! God, just take us away. If we can't make money, we'll all starve to death anyway.\"","Although Zhou Zedong was also angry, hearing his brother's and Jiang Jiu's scolding still made his mouth twitch uncontrollably.","After hearing this, the homeroom teacher immediately felt that the tuck shop owner's wife was completely out of her mind!","She knew these children were from out of town, from a relatively underdeveloped city. Just getting into this school was already not easy for them.","Earning money at such a young age to help out their family was supposed to be a very inspiring act.","Yet they were being targeted to such an extent. It was truly shameless and going way too far!","The tuck shop owner's wife was so angry that the veins on her forehead bulged, and she almost jumped up in rage.","\"You little brats, how dare you curse at me! Watch me teach you a good lesson today. You really don't know your place!\"","\"Hey, what do you think you're doing? If you lay a hand on them, I'll call the police!\"","The homeroom teacher quickly blocked the three children, saying with righteous indignation, \"And you call yourself an adult! To think you'd actually try to hit three children. Have you no shame?\"","\"Even if the Emperor of Heaven himself came today, these children have done nothing wrong! Report this if you have the guts. I'd like to see who is really the one going overboard here!\"","\"We teachers have all seen it with our own eyes. The two children were doing business outside and didn't affect you at all. On what grounds are you stopping them?\"","Seeing her take the children's side, the tuck shop owner's wife was half-dead with anger.","\"You... do you still want your job? Do you know who I am?\"","\"Bah, I don't care who you are, what does it have to do with me? You were about to hit the children in my class, and you still expect me to speak nicely to you? Even if you don't report this, I'm going to complain to the principal. I want to see which shameless person will stand by your side to bully a few children!\"","After saying that, she couldn't be bothered to pay any more attention to the furiously stomping owner's wife, and escorted the children out.","She also comforted them, telling them not to be afraid, and that if the owner's wife ever gave them trouble again, they should tell her!","At this moment, the homeroom teacher's sense of justice was overflowing. Let alone the tuck shop owner's wife, even if the Emperor of Heaven came down, he wouldn't be allowed to bully her students.","The children sweetly thanked her, which made her heart swell with joy, and she walked them out of the school with a gentle expression.","After picking up their younger sister, the children headed home.","Right after they left, a luxury car drove into the school.","The tuck shop owner's wife was furiously complaining to her husband, telling him to go to the principal and teach those kids a lesson, preferably by getting them expelled.","At this moment, her husband was complaining to the principal, saying that the children were ignorant and incompetent, and were selling junk food at school. Not only were they breaking discipline, but if someone got an upset stomach, the school would be held responsible.","Since he made it sound so serious, the principal couldn't help but pay some attention to it.","It was true that the school had never encountered such a situation before.","Just as he was about to leave it to him to issue a warning, he heard his assistant come in and anxiously say, \"Principal, Director Jiang is here.\"","The principal immediately stood up. \"Quick, invite her in.\"","Grandma Xiao was invited in by the bowing and scraping assistant.","\"Chairman Jiang, please, please have a seat. What brings you to the elementary school so suddenly today? Your presence brings light to our humble dwelling,\" the principal smiled.","\"Spare me the pleasantries,\" Grandma Xiao said, lifting her chin and sweeping a disdainful glance over them. \"I heard from my grandson that recently there are a few children doing business at school and breaking school rules? I came to ask how you are handling it.\"","The principal's heart immediately skipped a beat. Why would such a trivial matter cause a big shot from the Xiao family to make a special trip?","Could it be that it affected her grandson?","When her grandson enrolled this year, the Xiao family had donated an entire building to their school.","This was absolutely someone they could not afford to offend.","\"Yes, there is such a matter, but it has already been handled. We will warn the students, and this kind of thing will definitely not happen again in the future. Rest assured, it absolutely will not affect your grandson.\"","Grandma Xiao snorted coldly. \"Why warn them? Isn't it good for children to have such ideas? Do you think just burying their heads in books is the only good thing? I think your school's education is too rigid, causing children to be unable to freely do what they want, broaden their minds, and create opportunities. Is them earning a few bucks going to kill your school? On what grounds are you stopping them?\"","\"I have acquired your school's tuck shop. All the money earned from now on will be invested into these children as their tuition fees. You are not allowed to cause trouble for these children anymore.\"","\"Huh?\" The principal was dumbfounded.","The tuck shop owner, who had come to complain, was also dumbfounded.","......","\"Mom, we're back.\"","\"Auntie Si, I want to sleep with Second Brother today. Could you help me call my dad?\"","On such a cold day, the two children chased each other, walking into the house sweating profusely.","As a result, as soon as they entered the door, they smelled a pungent stench.","The two were stunned and immediately pinched their small noses.","What was going on? Did his mom spread manure on the vegetables she planted today?","\"Second Brother, why does your house smell so bad today?\"","Jiang Jiu's pretty and delicate little face scrunched up into a ball.","Second Child was even more exaggerated than him. He had been sensitive to smells since he was little. If someone's family was cooking meat, Second Child could smell it from far away.","Therefore, this smell was absolutely lethal to him.","He tilted his head to look for Da Huang, only to find that Da Huang had hidden in his own little doghouse and had even pulled the door shut.","Although it was very smelly, this was his home after all. A dog doesn't despise its home for being poor, and a person shouldn't despise their home for being smelly.","Second Child walked in, covering his nose.","He saw his dad sitting at the dining table, while his mom sat on the sofa. The two were sitting very far apart, as if they weren't familiar with each other.","Normally, his dad would always sit right next to his mom.","His dad's expression didn't look too good either, appearing a bit green.","But he remained silent, not saying a word.","Second Child found it very strange, but then he thought that since his dad wasn't sitting with his mom today, no one would fight with him for the spot.","He immediately ran over.","\"Mom, Mom, did you spread manure on the vegetables today?\"","Mom said she wanted to eat baby bok choy, so Dad got some foam boxes, filled them with soil, and scattered some seeds.","However, for the vegetables planted in the yard, Mom always let them grow on their own and never poured manure on them.","Only the ones planted in the fields would need that.","Si Nian turned her head to glance at Second Child, her eyes lighting up. \"Little Han is back. Quick, come here, Mom made something delicious for you, come have a taste.\""]},{"number":438,"title":"Chapter 438: Smells Stinky, Tastes Delicious","paragraphs":["Second Child's eyes lit up, and he ran over gleefully, \"Mom, what delicious food did you make?\"","The closer he got, the more he felt something was wrong. Why was there a growing stench?","It seemed like the smell was coming from his mom.","Second Child's footsteps slowed down.","He stared wide-eyed at the bowl his mom was holding; there seemed to be something black inside.","That was exactly where the stink was coming from.","\"Stinky tofu. You haven't heard of it, right? It's really delicious, come have a taste.\" Si Nian picked up a piece to feed him, then threw a sidelong glance at the older man sitting in the dining room, complaining unhappily, \"Hmph, it's obviously delicious, but your dad insists it's not. I spent so long making it.\"","Second Child originally wanted to refuse, but hearing that his mom had spent a long time making it, his body stiffened. \"Mom, do I really have to eat it? But how come it smells...\"","He didn't dare say it smelled stinky.","He was afraid his mom would get angry.","Si Nian smiled and said, \"It smells stinky, right? But that's okay. This thing smells bad but tastes amazing. Try it if you don't believe me.\"","Meeting his mom's eager and expectant gaze, Second Child couldn't bring himself to say no.","He opened his mouth with great difficulty. Never before had he felt that food was so hard to swallow, nor had he ever felt that eating was such a terrifying ordeal.","Seeing him eat it, Si Nian asked expectantly, \"How is it? Is it really good? It's not that stinky anymore, right?\"","Second Child chewed mechanically a few times and said, \"Mom, it seems like it doesn't smell as bad when you eat it gag... the taste is okay too gag...\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Zhou Zedong and Yaoyao also walked in, covering their noses. \"Dad, why does the house smell so bad? Did Da Huang poop inside?\"","Pinching her little nose, Yaoyao said, \"Shame on Da Huang~\"","Si Nian lost her appetite.","Looking at her whole family staring at her bowl with faces full of horror, she asked suspiciously, \"Is it really that stinky?\"","Everyone nodded in unison.","Si Nian's mouth twitched. Alright, she had just been saying that Zhou Yueshen was overreacting.","She hadn't expected them to genuinely be unable to handle the smell.","She had no choice but to find a place to store the leftover stinky tofu.","Then she opened the windows to ventilate the room.","She had originally wanted to eat luosifen too, but with her family reacting like this, she probably wouldn't be able to.","She also understood that some people just couldn't accept this kind of smell.","She just hadn't expected that not a single person in her family shared her palate.","Si Nian felt depressed, radiating a melancholic aura of being abandoned.","Perhaps being pregnant made her a bit sensitive.","Although the kids didn't quite understand why someone would eat something so smelly, seeing their mom sad, they hurried over to comfort her.","\"Mom, it's actually not that stinky. Eat it if you want to.\"","\"Yeah, even if it's stinky, as long as Mom likes it, then it's fragrant.\"","\"Don't worry, Mom. Even if you become stinky, you're still our mom.\"","Si Nian: \"...\" She felt even sadder qwq.","Zhou Yueshen looked at Si Nian, not knowing whether to laugh or cry. He shooed the kids away and coaxed her himself.","He told her she could eat whatever she wanted and didn't need to worry about them.","It wasn't going to kill anyone; it was just a little smell, nothing they couldn't endure.","Si Nian nodded repeatedly. Feeling supported, she gained some confidence. \"Then what if I want to eat luosifen, is that okay too?\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't know what luosifen was, but since she often mentioned it, she definitely liked it a lot, so he nodded and said yes.","Si Nian was instantly satisfied. She asked him to go buy river snails for her, saying she wanted to boil the broth herself.","She also added, \"Luosifen is a regional specialty, it's just that people don't know about it yet. These noodles are also famously known for smelling bad but tasting delicious. There might be a lot of people who can't stomach stinky tofu, but there are many who love eating luosifen. Men love it too. This time I'll make it myself, and you guys will definitely like it.\"","After saying that, she rubbed her hands together in anticipation.","Si Nian didn't have many hobbies; she just liked making good food.","Not to mention that she had been here for so long, and these things that were commonly eaten in the future couldn't be found in this era.","Thinking about making it with her own hands gave her a greater sense of accomplishment.","She felt very fulfilled in her heart.","Zhou Yueshen humored her with soft eyes, deciding that no matter how stinky it was this time, he would try it, since she was making it herself.","The stinky tofu had been processed before being brought over, and it already stank when it arrived.","So it wasn't a problem with Si Nian's cooking skills.","Si Nian's cooking was so good, this situation definitely wouldn't happen this time.","Harboring full confidence in his wife, Zhou Yueshen went to the seafood market to buy river snails the next day.","\"Mom, what is luosifen? It sounds so interesting.\"","\"Is it noodles boiled together with river snails?\"","\"Mom, when I was in the countryside, I went to pick up river snails with Shitou too, but we didn't dare eat them. I didn't expect them to be edible.\"","Si Nian smiled and said, \"Of course they are edible. There are many ways to cook river snails: spicy, garlic-flavored, and they can also be boiled into a broth to make luosifen. Luosifen isn't like the glass noodles here; it's made of rice noodles, which are very chewy.\"","Hearing her describe it like this, the kids couldn't help but gulp and say, \"Mom, then I want to eat two big bowls.\"","\"Okay!\"","Seeing them so supportive, Si Nian grew even more confident.","The deliciousness of luosifen mainly lies in its unique broth. The broth is simmered with river snails, sand ginger, star anise, cinnamon, cloves, and other spices.","Zhou Yueshen bought the things Si Nian needed, carefully cleaned the river snails, and then put them in the pot to stew.","Si Nian also pickled some sour bamboo shoots.","Smelling the broth, which didn't stink at all, Second Child felt relieved and said, \"Dad, smell it, it really doesn't stink at all. Mom didn't lie to us.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded.","Si Nian also made chili sauce and fried tofu skin. Seeing that the seasonings were about ready, she put the noodles in the pot to boil.","The kids gathered around, their faces full of anticipation.","The luosifen that Mom loved to eat so much was definitely going to be delicious.","Once they each scooped out their noodles, Si Nian brought out the sour bamboo shoots she had pickled in advance and said, \"Ta-da! This is the true soul of luosifen. It's sour, crispy, and especially delicious. But if you're worried about the strong taste, you don't have to add it.\"","Si Nian said.","Second Child looked at the sour bamboo shoots, his eyes lighting up. The fish mint, wild garlic, and dried radishes that Mom pickled were all especially sour, spicy, and refreshing. This would definitely be delicious too. He immediately ran over holding his bowl and said, \"Mom, Mom, I want some, I want some, give me a lot.\"","Si Nian raised an eyebrow. \"Are you sure? Aren't you afraid it'll stink?\"","\"I'm not afraid at all. This looks really delicious.\"","It wasn't like that stinky tofu he saw last time, which was all black and looked like it had gone bad.","Second Child was very confident.","Plus, Mom made this herself, so it definitely wouldn't taste bad.","Si Nian twisted off the lid, and a bizarre smell drifted out.","Second Child's expectant smile suddenly froze.","He leaned in uncertainly and sniffed the scent, \"Gag~\""]},{"number":439,"title":"Chapter 439: The First Year in the Capital","paragraphs":["A few children who were originally lining up to get more food instantly stopped in their tracks, turned their heads, and pretended not to see.","\"Dad, I think it tastes really good just like this.\"","Zhou Yueshen was silent for two seconds before replying, \"Yeah, let's just eat it like this.\"","Second Child's hand trembled, looking at his mother in horror.","Si Nian said helplessly, \"I told you that you wouldn't be able to stand it. If you don't like it, don't force yourself. Go eat, Mom won't force you to eat this.\"","She wasn't so unreasonable as to force the children to eat with her.","Actually, the sour bamboo shoots in luosifen shouldn't smell bad if soaked for a short time; she probably messed up a step somewhere.","However, even though it smelled, it didn't taste spoiled.","It was still edible.","Second Child glanced at her cautiously. \"Mom, aren't you angry?\"","Si Nian smiled gently. \"Why would Mom be angry? Mom is already very happy that Little Han could eat with me.\"","She reached out and rubbed her son's head. \"Go eat, it won't taste good if it gets dry later.\"","Second Child nodded heavily.","Si Nian served herself a little bit, not too much, just to taste it.","The smell of luosifen was very strong, the kind that wouldn't dissipate for days.","Although Si Nian really liked eating it, she also knew how lethal the smell was.","After eating, she went to brush her teeth and wash up.","But when they went to sleep at night and Zhou Yueshen held her, he could still faintly smell it.","The smelly month finally passed. Si Nian got tired of it after eating too much, and started preferring sour foods.","Zhou Yueshen thought of the saying she had mentioned about sour cravings meaning a boy and spicy meaning a girl, and could not help but worry.","Could it be that he was going to have another son?","He felt he already had enough sons; having a daughter would be best.","However, to his relief, Si Nian had not experienced any discomfort over the past three months. Her morning sickness was pitifully rare, and she ate a lot.","Perhaps due to the pregnancy, her figure became increasingly fuller. When Si Nian went to school, others even thought she had just gained weight.","Fortunately, she had a naturally small frame, so even if she gained weight, it wasn't obvious. She just seemed to glow with health, looking exceptionally radiant and comfortable.","Si Nian's belly wasn't very big these past few months, so she studied especially hard.","She wished she could finish all her studies this year.","When December arrived, it snowed heavily in Beijing.","Si Nian took a leave of absence in advance and finished her courses.","Because it was cold, she had Zhou Yueshen drive the children to and from school.","She stayed home to walk the dog and watch TV.","The only downside was that Zhou Yueshen, a native countryman, actually failed at growing vegetables. A few sparse seedlings came up, only to be eaten by bugs.","By the time Si Nian tried to save them, the weather turned cold, and they all froze to death.","The temperature in the north was much lower than in the south. Not to mention the sub-zero temperatures in winter, the wind was also strong.","Si Nian had never lived in such a cold place before, and being pregnant, she found it a bit hard to endure.","They started burning a foreign stove and honeycomb coal briquettes at home.","Only then did it warm up.","Naturally, they couldn't go back for the New Year this year.","Si Nian wrote a letter to her family telling them not to worry and that she would return during the summer vacation.","Being pregnant in the dead of winter and taking several children on a train was simply too much torture.","Her family sent them a lot of New Year goods again.","Miao Chunhua's shop had booming business right from the opening, and she had now opened several branch stores.","Hearing that Si Nian was pregnant, she made time to visit her, but in reality, it was to eat luosifen.","This time, Chen Nan and Chen Haoran came with her.","All of them came to eat the delicious food Si Nian made.","Previously, Si Nian had sent over a lot of pickled radishes and wild garlic, and occasionally made some pastries.","Chen Nan used to live in their hometown and was very fond of these flavors.","Chen Haoran liked sweet pastries, so the father and son both came over to mooch food and drinks.","Especially after Miao Chunhua heard on the phone that Si Nian had made luosifen and stinky tofu, she kept talking about it. She said that when she used to travel around, she had tasted Changsha stinky tofu with her parents and had also heard of luosifen.","Anyway, they were both very delicious.","Now that she finally had time to come over, the two men, whose ears had grown calluses from hearing about it so much, naturally came along with great expectations to taste it.","\"Hey, Little Dong and Little Han, are the luosifen and stinky tofu your mom makes really that delicious?\"","Chen Haoran saw the children building a snowman outside and asked curiously.","The children stopped what they were doing and asked him, \"Do you want to eat some?\"","Chen Haoran nodded. \"Yeah, we traveled all this way just to eat this stuff. Hearing my mom praise it to the heavens, I definitely have to try it.\"","The children exchanged glances. \"Are you really going to eat it?\"","Chen Haoran nodded. \"Why would I lie to you?\"","\"Then you must finish it all. Don't waste food, otherwise Mom will be unhappy,\" the children advised.","They looked at him with some pity.","Chen Haoran was confused. \"Why do you say that? Do you guys think it doesn't taste good?\"","\"Our opinion doesn't matter. Our mom thinks it's very delicious.\"","Chen Haoran looked at the children, feeling that they were acting very strangely.","Suddenly, he smelled something. It was stinky.","He looked around and saw Da Huang wearing an LV sweater. He paused, unzipped his jacket, and looked at his own sweater.","It was exactly the same?","The sweater his mom bought for him was exactly the same as the one Si Nian's dog was wearing?","Chen Haoran was dumbfounded.","When his mom said her friend's kid really liked it, could she have been talking about this dog?","Chen Haoran's face darkened. Just as he was about to go make a fuss, he suddenly felt the smell getting stronger.","\"Hey, Little Han, did your dog poop? Go scoop it up quickly, it stinks.","Such a big dog must poop a lot, no wonder it's so smelly.\"","Chen Haoran stood up, covering his nose.","Da Huang rolled his eyes at him, turned around, and continued sleeping with an unbothered expression.","Seeing that the children were ignoring him, Chen Haoran had to turn around and go inside the house first.","To his surprise, it smelled even worse inside.","\"Holy crap, sis, did your toilet explode?\"","Then he saw his mom walk out holding a bowl of food. She took a deep, intoxicated sniff and said, \"This smell, so fragrant, exactly like the legends!\"","\"Haoran, you're here. Go quickly and get some noodles, they won't taste good if they get soggy.\"","Chen Haoran looked at his mom in shock. She could actually eat in such a smelly environment?","His mom was truly a ruthless person.","He quickly covered his nose and walked toward the kitchen, intending to tell Si Nian to have someone deal with the smell right away.","However, upon entering the kitchen, he found it was even stinkier.","He looked up and saw Si Nian, looking as if she had no sense of smell, putting food into a bowl while smiling at him. \"I heard from your mom that you've been craving my luosifen for a long time. Hurry up and take it out to eat.\"","Only then did Chen Haoran realize that the stench seemed to be coming from her bowl.","\"?\"","Walking out with a bowl of noodles, looking like he had lost the will to live, Chen Haoran finally noticed that his dad and Zhou Yueshen were missing.","He asked, \"? Mom, where are my dad and Uncle Zhou?\"","His mom, slurping mouthfuls of the stinky noodles, replied without looking up, \"Your dad and your Uncle Zhou have business to discuss, they went to the study.\"","Chen Haoran: \"...\" Could it be that his dad had known all along, which was why he bolted so fast?","Good grief, even a vicious tiger wouldn't eat its own cubs. Why didn't his dad call for him?"]},{"number":440,"title":"Chapter 440: Slaughtering the Pig","paragraphs":["With tears in his eyes and under the urging gazes of his mother and Si Nian, Chen Haoran took a bite. With this one bite, he froze.","Why didn't it taste smelly at all?","The aroma of the chili oil and the rich broth that burst from the fried egg with a single bite completely stunned him.","This thing actually tasted incredibly delicious.","The rice noodles were smooth and chewy. The sour bamboo shoots smelled terrible, but tasted sour, crisp, and refreshing!","Every single topping inside was delicious.","However, he wasn't very good at handling spicy food. Si Nian had only added a little bit, but it was still spicy enough to make him gasp for air.","Despite the heat, he kept stuffing his mouth. On such a cold day, the food made him sweat profusely.","The children had originally wanted to come in and laugh at him, but they didn't expect to see him slurping the noodles in huge mouthfuls, completely unaffected by the smell.","The kids were stunned.","Admiration shone in their eyes.","Even now, they still weren't quite used to the smell of the sour bamboo shoots.","After finishing his bowl, Chen Haoran still didn't feel satisfied. He shamelessly went to Si Nian and asked if she could pack some sour bamboo shoots for him to take home.","Seeing that she had finally successfully recommended it to someone, Si Nian was happy and packed a generous amount for him.","She told him to come to her whenever he wanted more in the future.","Chen Haoran happily went home hugging half a bucket of sour bamboo shoots.","When the twelfth lunar month arrived, every household began slaughtering pigs, sheep, and chickens.","It snowed early in Jing City. The night before had been perfectly fine, but when they woke up the next day, heavy snow was falling like goose feathers outside.","As soon as they got up, they could see smoke rising from the chimneys of every house and hear the sounds of children playing.","It was the New Year, and the children of the neighbors had all returned for the holidays. Quite a few people had moved in recently as well. Although the rumors of ghosts and monsters here had only just been dispelled, the location was excellent and close to everything.","Moreover, because of the previous rumors, renting a house here was very cheap.","So, many people had moved over.","Si Nian was just thinking about taking the kids out to buy some down jackets because of the heavy snow when someone knocked on the front door.","Sister Si Nian, is your man at home? the person outside shouted while knocking.","Mom, I'll go open the door. Second Child, wearing only a sweater, ran out with thumping steps.","Afraid he would be cold, Si Nian wanted to tell him to put on a coat, but it was too late.","It was still snowing outside. The heavy snow had covered the doorway in a thick layer. A lot of snow had also accumulated on Da Huang's little doghouse and the nearby trees, making it look very beautiful.","Da Huang had half of its body hidden in the doghouse with its head sticking out. Fortunately, its fur grew quickly and was almost fully grown back. Tibetan Mastiffs naturally had very thick fur, so there was no need to worry about it getting cold.","Xiao Han, where are your parents? Are they home? the aunt outside asked.","Si Nian quickly responded, Aunt Wang, we're home. Do you need something from us?","Oh, thank goodness you're home. My family is slaughtering a pig today, but we don't have enough hands. I wanted to ask your man to help. They had passed by here before and encountered Zhou Yueshen a few times.","Although he was a southerner, he was tall and sturdy, and anyone could tell at a glance that he must be very strong.","Her family had raised a pig all year round, weighing about five hundred catties. Originally, they planned to drag it to the slaughterhouse and bring it back, but who knew that they would wake up today to heavy snow and blocked roads.","The car couldn't be driven out.","They had no choice but to slaughter it today.","After all, they had calculated an auspicious date for slaughtering the pig, and today was a good day for it.","Unfortunately, they didn't have enough people to help here.","She had run to several houses in a row and only found two helpers.","Passing by Si Nian's house, she remembered her man, so she hurriedly came to ask.","Hearing this, Si Nian raised an eyebrow. Slaughtering a pig?","When is it? My Lao Zhou isn't home, she said helplessly.","Tomorrow would work, or this afternoon. Zhou Yueshen usually came back early in the afternoons now.","That's a problem then. We had someone calculate the time for slaughtering the pig, and it has to be at ten o'clock. That's the best time.","Si Nian's mouth twitched.","Even slaughtering a pig required calculating an auspicious time. The older generation was indeed particular.","She said apologetically, Lao Zhou's company hasn't started the holidays yet, so he's still at work.","The other party immediately felt it was a pity. That's fine then. You should bring the kids to my house for the pig-slaughtering feast. It'll be lively today.","Si Nian felt a bit awkward. Although they would greet each other when they met, and the neighbors had visited her house before, they weren't really that familiar with each other.","Then she heard the other party say, All the neighbors are going. Don't be polite, everyone can get to know each other.","Hearing this, Si Nian found it hard to refuse.","She nodded and said, Alright, I'll change my clothes and head over later to help out.","Nowadays, slaughtering a pig was a major event, and many neighbors and relatives would go to help.","Since they had invited her, refusing would be quite disrespectful.","Actually, Si Nian quite liked this kind of lively atmosphere.","Beside her, Second Child was so excited he was beside himself. Mom, Mom, can I go too? I can help!","Yes, yes, we're all going. Hurry up and put on your coat, we can't have you catching a cold.","Si Nian patted his little head. This child really loved a bustling crowd. Even though his father used to slaughter pigs every day, he was still overjoyed to encounter such an event.","She smiled helplessly and went back into the house to find some thick clothes to wear. Just as she was saying she should call Zhou Yueshen to ask about his situation, the man strode in from outside, covered in snow.","Zhou Yueshen brushed the snow off his body. Seeing her and the children dressed to go out, he asked, Are you heading out?","Si Nian nodded, a bit surprised. Why are you back so early? I was just about to call you. Aunt Wang's family is slaughtering a pig today, and she just came over to see if you could help.","Zhou Yueshen explained, It suddenly started snowing heavily today, and the roads are blocked. Goods can't be sent out or brought in, so we got the day off.","That's perfect, let's go over together. You haven't slaughtered a pig in a long time, are you out of practice?","Zhou Yueshen didn't know whether to laugh or cry. No.","The snow was heavy outside, so Zhou Yueshen put a hat and scarf on her.","While extending her foot for the man to put on her snow boots, Si Nian said, I didn't expect it to snow so soon. Later, when the Wang family is done, let's take the kids to buy down jackets, otherwise it'll be too cold.","Zhou Yueshen finished putting on her shoes and nodded slightly, saying alright.","The children also put on their hats, earmuffs, and scarves.","The whole family was bundled up like little dumplings.","Especially Yaoyao. Perhaps because she had been eating so well, the little girl had plumped up quite a bit. Her little face was round and incredibly cute.","Right now, with fluffy earmuffs on her ears, a hat on her head, and a matching red scarf, her little face looked perfectly round and radiant, brimming with festive joy."]},{"number":441,"title":"Chapter 441: Slaughtering Pigs Doesn't Earn Much Money","paragraphs":["The whole family went out fully armed against the cold. Actually, it wasn't as cold as usual since it started snowing, though the biting wind was piercing; it was fine when the wind wasn't blowing.","As soon as they stepped out, the children started playing and chasing after each other.","They soon arrived at the Wang family's door.","The Wang family were Beijing locals. Although they weren't considered rich, owning their own house was quite impressive. It was said they had lived here for a very long time.","Because of this, they knew a lot of people. Si Nian originally thought there would just be a few relatives and friends, but she didn't expect it to look like a massive banquet.","Many people were standing at the main gate.","She was initially a bit embarrassed, but seeing so many people, that feeling vanished instantly.","Although there were many people, most were just there to join in the fun and eat the pig-slaughtering feast; few could actually help.","Many were public servants from various units; how could they possibly slaughter a pig?","At this moment, the Wang family was discussing who could lend a hand.","As the Zhou family approached, everyone immediately greeted them. Little Si's family is here! Sister Wang, her husband came too.","Because the case involving Song Zhaodi's family was accidentally solved by Da Huang, Si Nian's family had become quite famous in this alley.","Many people had heard the news and went to visit their Da Huang.","Right now, everyone had a very good impression of them.","Previously, due to rumors from ten years ago, everyone always felt this alley was eerie and dared not walk it at night.","Especially with Song Zhaodi's missing husband, it added a few more degrees of creepiness.","So, people felt the feng shui here was bad and unlucky. Some who cared deeply about these things had moved away.","Those who couldn't bear to leave stayed. Whenever they went out and chatted with others, someone would always ask, Your house is in that haunted alley, right?","Anyway, hearing that made them very uncomfortable.","But after this case was solved, no one talked about those things anymore. Some who had moved out even moved back, and more people started doing business in the alley, making it much livelier.","They felt this was all thanks to the Zhou family.","Aunt Wang hurried over to speak. Oh my, sister, isn't Comrade Zhou supposed to be at work? Why did you call him over?","She thought Si Nian had specially called him back because she asked for help, and felt extremely apologetic.","Si Nian said, No, sister. Old Zhou's company is on holiday. He came back right after you left, so I asked him to come over and help.","That's great! With your Old Zhou here, it will definitely be handled.","She smiled and welcomed them, Quick, come in and have a seat.","Si Nian led the curious children and followed her inside.","As soon as they entered, they saw a big black pig locked in an iron cage.","Brother, look, what kind of pig is this? Why is it black?","I've never seen a black pig.","Zhou Zedong said, I haven't seen one either. Although he hadn't seen one, he didn't show any surprise. He had read about black people in books. If there were black people, what was so strange about a black pig?","As soon as Zhou Yueshen went over, he was pulled aside to discuss how to slaughter the pig.","Seeing the group still looking unsure, Zhou Yueshen said in a low voice, I know how to slaughter it. Don't worry, it's fine.","The surrounding children gathered around, all wanting to watch the pig slaughter.","Second Child watched his father walk over with a knife and immediately said proudly, That's my dad, did you see? That's my dad. He's really good at slaughtering pigs. He used to run a pig farm, and our family has a hundred thousand pigs.","Si Nian had just taken a cup of hot water to drink. Hearing this, she almost choked.","Second Child, how are your boasts getting bigger and bigger?","She didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","Someone came over to talk to her. Watching Zhou Yueshen's clean and decisive knife work, they exclaimed, Sister, your man's movements are so neat and crisp! I thought it would be a huge hassle. In the past, when we had no other way, we always hired people from the slaughterhouse to do it.","Yeah, if we slaughter a pig in the future, could we invite your man?","Si Nian said, If he has time, sure.","That's a deal. We won't let your man work for free; we'll give him a big red envelope.","Aunt Wang had picked a specific time for the slaughter. Seeing Zhou Yueshen handle it so easily, she was overjoyed. She repeatedly pulled Si Nian aside to praise him, I really found the right person by asking your Old Zhou. My sons-in-law are completely useless at this; none of them dared to do it.","Hearing this, her two daughters standing nearby were displeased. What's so great about killing a pig? Any rough man can do it. My husband works in an office, how can they be compared?","Yeah, if I had married a pig butcher, you'd be mad to death.","The two of them had brought their husbands home for the pig slaughter, bustling about only to be criticized by their mother as useless.","Naturally, they had to defend their husbands.","Unexpectedly, Aunt Wang snorted coldly. Working in an office means you can't slaughter a pig? What kind of logic is that? If they are so delicate, why even come to help? Just now, when I asked someone to pick up the knife, not a single one was willing. They just pushed the responsibility back and forth. If Comrade Zhou hadn't come over, my schedule would have been delayed.","The two curled their lips. Only you would be so particular as to set a specific time to kill a pig.","Aunt Wang couldn't be bothered to argue with them and quickly thanked Si Nian.","Her two daughters had only been married for a year or two and were around eighteen or nineteen, but they looked about the same age as Si Nian.","Once their mother walked away, they couldn't help but speak up. You guys are from out of town, right? Was your husband a butcher back in your hometown?","Si Nian paused for a moment and said, Not exactly, he just killed a lot of pigs every day.","The two looked disdainful. Isn't that just like a butcher at a slaughterhouse? He probably doesn't make much money, right?","Si Nian glanced at them and said, It's alright.","The two thought she was just embarrassed to admit it, otherwise she wouldn't have come to drift in Beijing, so they said with faux pity, That must be pretty tough, right?","In this day and age, it's hard to get by if you only have brute strength and no brains. Although my husband isn't very physically strong, he does very well at his unit. Not only is the work easy, but the salary is also high.","Exactly. In the dead of winter, slaughtering pigs is freezing cold, and you can't even earn a few bucks.","Si Nian nodded in agreement. You're right.","The two laughed. So what does your husband do now that he's not killing pigs?","Si Nian said, He's a manager now.","Ah? The two froze, thinking they had heard wrong.","What did you just say? That man is a manager? Si Nian blinked and said slowly, Yes, is there a problem?","The two were dumbfounded. Wasn't he a pig butcher before? How did he become a manager? How is that possible? A pig butcher becoming a manager, I've truly never heard of such a rare thing.","Is it that strange? Slaughtering pigs was just his side job. His main profession is actually the boss of a pig farm.","The two of them: ...","Recovering their wits, they gave a dry laugh. You must be joking. If he really ran a pig farm at home and was a boss, why would he come all the way to Beijing?","Because I had to come here to study. He was worried, so he followed me.","Si Nian explained with great patience.","Study? The two exchanged glances and stared at her in astonishment. You, you're a student?","Yes.","Really? Which school are you at? the two asked suspiciously.","Beijing University.","The two of them: ..."]},{"number":442,"title":"Chapter 442: Preparing New Year Goods","paragraphs":["After Si Nian finished speaking, someone over there called her for help.","She didn't pay attention to the colorful expressions on the two women's faces and walked over.","The two waited for quite a while before they finally snapped out of it.","They felt Si Nian was just bragging.","\"She's a student at Jing University? Why do I find that so hard to believe?\"","\"Yeah, her kids are already so big.\"","\"And that husband of hers, that's even more exaggerated. A pig farm owner and a company manager? He looks like a rough man to me, how could he do that kind of brain work.\"","\"Exactly, I think she just makes things up as she goes.\"","\"Wang family, the Wang family's TV is here, come out and help move it.\"","Someone shouted outside.","The two women couldn't be bothered to think further and hurriedly said, \"Coming.\"","\"Mom, the TV we bought for you has arrived, call someone over to help.\"","Mother Wang nodded quickly and called her two sons-in-law over to help.","As it turned out, the two men didn't have much strength, and ultimately it was the deliverymen who helped carry it in.","Seeing the Wang family slaughtering a pig, the deliveryman let out an \"Oyo\": \"Slaughtering a pig, huh? How lively.\"","Mother Wang smiled and invited him to stay for a meal, \"You've worked really hard, sir, delivering our TV even in such heavy snow.\"","\"Of course, if the roads hadn't been closed in the morning, it would have been delivered much earlier. But we can only deliver within the city, we can't go anywhere outside.\"","The man wrote up the receipt and had them sign it. His gaze swept across the courtyard, and suddenly noticing something, his eyes fixed. He then uncertainly rubbed his eyes, and after making sure he hadn't seen wrong, he cried out in astonishment, \"President Zhou, what are you doing here?\"","Zhou Yueshen was currently scraping hair off the pig. Hearing the voice, he turned his head to look over.","He saw that it was exactly the deliveryman from his company.","He paused for a moment.","He handed the scraper in his hand to his eagerly watching youngest son on the side, stood up, and said, \"You haven't rested yet?\"","The man quickly smiled apologetically and said, \"The boss arranged it, saying to try and deliver all the goods that can be delivered within the city. Once we finish delivering today, we can rest. Oh my, I didn't expect to run into you here, President Zhou. Do you live around here too?\"","After saying that, he immediately offered a cigarette to Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Yueshen blocked it and didn't take it: \"My wife is pregnant, I've quit smoking.\"","The man immediately withdrew it in embarrassment, \"Look at me, I'm really sorry, President Zhou.\"","\"It's fine,\" Zhou Yueshen said. \"Go on with your work, and head home early to rest when you're done.\"","\"Aye~\" the man responded sweetly. Who said their President Zhou was unapproachable and scary as hell? He used to be terrified whenever he ran into him, but now that they actually spoke, he realized President Zhou wasn't fierce at all. He was actually quite nice. Just look, running such a huge company, yet here he is helping people slaughter pigs.","Bosses with such a human touch were rare nowadays.","After sending the man off, Zhou Yueshen turned back to continue his work.","The two Wang sisters were already standing there dumbfounded.","He... he really was a boss...","Thinking about how they had just mocked pig slaughterers in front of Si Nian as nothing special, and not comparable to their men who worked in state units.","The two sisters wished they could dig a hole and hide in it.","Zhou Yueshen turned his head. A group of kids was surrounding his youngest son, lining up to learn how to scrape pig hair.","Second Child scraped while teaching, \"I have experience with this. I used to watch my dad scrape pig hair all the time. It doesn't matter if you can't scrape it off; just scald it with boiling water, and it comes right off. Isn't it fun?\"","Everyone opened their mouths in a \"Wow\" expression, looking at him with admiration and envy.","\"Zhou Zehan, can you let me try too?\"","\"I really want to scrape pig hair too.\"","Zhou Yueshen's mouth twitched. He walked over, lifted his son off the ground, and seeing that he was covered in a smelly odor and his sleeves were wet, frowned and said, \"Go sit by the fire. If you catch a cold later, your mom will be angry.\"","Second Child reluctantly returned the scraper.","\"Second brother is stinky.\" Yaoyao saw him come back smelling awful and waved her hand in front of her nose in disgust.","Zhou Zehan pinched his dripping wet sleeve and secretly peeked at Si Nian. Seeing that she was busy helping and hadn't noticed him, he made a \"shh\" gesture to his sister.","A firewood fire was burning in the courtyard, and a group of people was gathered around it to keep warm.","It wasn't long before he was dried off.","At this moment, someone shouted, \"Opening the belly~\"","Zhou Zehan immediately squeezed over with a group of kids.","He looked proudly as his dad sliced open the pig's belly with a knife, constantly telling the people around him, \"Look, that's my dad. My dad can do anything.\"","Everyone looked at him with envy.","Zhou Yueshen was fast. After cleaning out the organs inside the pig's belly, he gripped the cleaver and dismantled the whole pig in a few swift strokes.","Every piece of meat was cut to the same size, and the ribs and trotters were all portioned perfectly.","Aunt Wang couldn't stop smiling at the sight.","He was so fast that before others had even finished cleaning, he had already finished chopping.","Si Nian helped with the cooking, and everyone shared a piping hot meal of fresh pork dishes.","When they finished, it was only twelve noon.","Aunt Wang stuffed a red envelope into her hands and gave her a piece of meat to take home.","Si Nian originally didn't want to accept it, but it was hard to refuse such great hospitality, so she eventually carried it home.","Zhou Yueshen didn't get his clothes dirty, but Second Child smelled entirely of raw meat.","The smell of black pigs was particularly strong. Ever since Si Nian got pregnant, her sense of smell had become very sensitive, making it hard not to notice.","Second Child thought he would be fine once his clothes dried by the fire, but when he raised his arm, there were still water stains, and it stank horribly.","Si Nian didn't blame him, knowing he enjoyed it. Since she was carrying things anyway and it wasn't convenient to go shopping, they went home first to change his clothes before the family set out to buy new ones.","At the mention of buying new clothes, the children grew excited.","Their current thick clothes were all brought over from their old hometown.","The temperature in their hometown wasn't as cold as it was here. Although these clothes weren't thin, they definitely couldn't withstand the temperatures here.","Second Child skipped and ran ahead. Having participated in the pig slaughter today, he was very thrilled. \"Mom, Mom, are we going to slaughter a pig at our house this year?\"","He asked with some anticipation.","No matter how fun it was at someone else's house, it couldn't compare to doing it at their own.","The last time their family slaughtered a pig was when Mom and Dad got married. At that time, he, Shitou, and a group of others skewed meat and roasted it to eat, and it was so delicious.","But this was someone else's house, and he was too embarrassed to ask for any.","So he felt it was a real pity.","Si Nian shook her head and said, \"We won't slaughter one this year. We wouldn't be able to finish it.\"","The main reason was that smoking meat here was too troublesome, and a whole pig was just too much; they definitely wouldn't be able to finish it.","It would be fine to just buy some outside for the New Year.","Seeing the look of pure disappointment written all over Zhou Zehan's face, she added, \"Wait until next New Year when we go back home, then we'll slaughter a pig.\"","\"Really?\"","Second Child asked expectantly.","\"If you don't believe me, ask your dad.\"","\"Dad, Dad, are we going to slaughter a pig next year?\"","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod. \"Yes.\"","\"Yay, that's great~\"","Amidst his cheerful laughter, the family arrived at the department store.","It wasn't cold inside the store, and because the New Year was approaching, it was very crowded.","Zhou Yueshen protectively shielded Si Nian and told the children to stay close.","The New Year period was when human traffickers were at their most rampant.","Si Nian took them to try on a few sets of down jackets. The down jackets were light, thin, yet warm, and the kids all really liked them.","\""]},{"number":443,"title":"Chapter 443: Cooking New Year's Eve Dinner","paragraphs":["Si Nian took them to try on a few down jackets. The jackets were light, thin, and warm, and the children all liked them very much.","\"Mom, Mom, these clothes are so light and comfortable to wear.\"","Second Child was so happy that he jumped up and down on the spot.","The heavy cotton-padded jackets they wore before were not only bulky but also restricted their movement.","Otherwise, his sleeves wouldn't have gotten wet.","\"As long as it's comfortable.\"","Si Nian smiled and went to pay with Zhou Yueshen.","After buying the jackets, they also got fleece-lined pants and snow boots for the children.","Upon hearing the price, Second Child lost his nerve and quickly changed his tune, \"Mom, actually, I think the big cotton-padded jackets are pretty good to wear too.\"","Si Nian smiled and rubbed his head. \"Don't worry, it's not like your dad can't afford it.\"","Now that their family's living conditions had improved so much, there was no need to pinch pennies over something like this.","Si Nian also bought a loose, long down jacket for herself so that even when her belly got bigger later on, she wouldn't feel restricted.","She could wear it all winter long.","She also picked out a black one for Zhou Yueshen.","The family bought quite a lot, carrying bags big and small. Fortunately, the children could carry their own things; otherwise, no matter how strong Zhou Yueshen was, he wouldn't have been able to carry it all.","On the way home, they saw someone setting up a stall selling fireworks and firecrackers.","The prices weren't very high.","These things would go up in price once the New Year arrived.","Seeing that the children couldn't take their eyes off them, Si Nian bought quite a few to save for the New Year.","After buying clothes, Zhou Yueshen went back out in the afternoon to buy New Year goods.","The family was very busy for several consecutive days.","On New Year's Eve, the children started nagging early in the morning about pasting up the spring couplets.","Si Nian also woke up early to make tangyuan and dumplings.","The fillings had been prepared in advance the night before.","Zhou Yueshen lit the honeycomb briquettes and a small brazier early in the morning.","As soon as you entered the living room, it was wonderfully warm.","Because it was too cold in the winter, the windows were sealed with plastic wrap to prevent the heat from escaping, keeping the house very cozy.","Si Nian only needed to wear a fluffy set of pajamas around the house.","She sat at the table wrapping dumplings and shaping tangyuan. They weren't the usual round tangyuan, but sweet dough drops that were a must-eat for the New Year in their hometown. She mixed the filling herself, which contained peanuts, sesame seeds, and white sugar, bursting with sweet juice with every bite.","Yaoyao pinched a piece of dough, trying to learn how to wrap it from her mother. After a long time, the dough was kneaded completely out of shape, and she still hadn't managed to wrap it.","Si Nian noticed that while this child was smart and learned things quickly, she just couldn't do this kind of manual work at all.","Perhaps she was simply born destined to enjoy a life of ease.","Looking at her daughter's rosy little face, Si Nian's eyes softened unconsciously.","Second Child came in from outside holding the spring couplets. \"Mom, Mom, where do we paste this?\"","Si Nian took a look and said, \"This is a paper cut, it goes on the window. And this 'Fortune' character goes on the front door, but it needs to be pasted upside down.\"","\"Why upside down? Won't we be unable to read the word then?\"","Despite having gone to school for a few years, Second Child, who still lacked any real cultural refinement, asked this soul-searching question.","Si Nian didn't know whether to laugh or cry. \"The word for 'upside down' sounds just like the word for 'arrive.' So 'Fortune upside down' means 'Fortune has arrived,' understand?\"","Second Child suddenly saw the light. \"I get it now, so that's what it means.\"","Since using tape didn't look nice, Zhou Yueshen also made some flour paste.","The two children couldn't reach, so naturally, he was the one to paste them.","Second Child was still standing there, bossing him around, \"It's crooked, it's crooked! Too high, too high! Dad is so clumsy!\"","When Zhou Yueshen was pasting the \"Fu\" character for good fortune, the little boy was afraid his dad wouldn't understand the reasoning, so he reminded him, \"Dad, this needs to be pasted upside down. Mom said pasting it upside down sounds like fortune has arrived.\"","Zhou Yueshen pinched his little face, which was red from the cold, and pasted the character properly.","Zhou Zedong, who was better at detailed work, was assembling lanterns on the side. Having finished, he brought them over, and Zhou Yueshen hung them by the door.","The festive red and the snow-covered courtyard formed an absolutely beautiful picture.","Looking at the finished work, Second Child nodded in satisfaction. \"I did a great job. I should set off a firecracker to celebrate.\"","Zhou Yueshen and Zhou Zedong thought to themselves that it seemed all he did was chatter non-stop.","Second Child didn't care what they thought. He immediately ran into the house, dug out his matchcrackers, and ran back out, announcing he was going to set them off.","Just as he struck one and tossed it, Chen Haoran walked out from around the corner carrying some things. As luck would have it, the firecracker landed right inside his clothes.","Chen Haoran said, \"Sister... huh, what's this?\"","He looked down; his clothes were smoking.","\"Ah—\"","In the courtyard, Second Child was made to stand in the corner as punishment.","Chen Haoran looked at the hole in his clothes, then at Second Child who was being punished, and laughed dryly. \"Um, it's fine, Sister Si Nian. Little Han didn't do it on purpose.\"","Si Nian frowned and said, \"Whether it was on purpose or not, this kind of behavior is wrong. It's a good thing it was you. If it were anyone else, they would have probably caused trouble for him by now.\"","Chen Haoran was speechless. What did she mean by 'it's a good thing it was him'?","Did it not matter just because it was him?","She should know that this new jacket of his was a limited edition that cost a lot of money.","He had worn it over today specifically to show it off.","Yet before he even stepped through the door, a hole had been blown into it.","But as it happened, he was the type of person who didn't like to hold grudges against children.","He took a deep breath. \"It's partly my fault for taking the shortcut, otherwise he wouldn't have missed seeing me.\"","He had taken the small path, thinking it would be closer.","Who knew that the moment he stepped out, a lit firecracker would end up in his arms.","Fortunately, this type of firecracker wasn't very powerful.","Thinking back on it, Chen Haoran still felt a lingering fear.","\"Little Han, hurry up and apologize to your Uncle Chen,\" Si Nian said, shooting the boy a look.","Uncle Chen Haoran was confused.","\"How did I become an uncle?\"","He was only about seven or eight years older than the kid, right?","Si Nian rolled her eyes at him. \"You call me sister, and he is my son. If he doesn't call you uncle, is he supposed to call you brother?\"","Chen Haoran's face twisted.","So no matter how they addressed each other, he was the one getting the short end of the stick?","\"Uncle Chen, I'm sorry. I didn't do it on purpose.\"","Second Child said obediently.","\"Oh, it's fine, it's fine. I don't blame you,\" Chen Haoran hurriedly said.","He actually quite liked younger siblings, especially Si Nian's youngest daughter, who was as round and cute as a little dumpling.","In previous years, when his parents asked him to deliver things to relatives, it was like asking for his life.","Today, he had volunteered to come over, saying he was delivering New Year's goods.","He was carrying quite a few large and small bags right now.","Si Nian hadn't expected someone to come pay New Year's greetings so early. She went back inside, prepared a red envelope, and handed it to Chen Haoran.","Seeing his dumbfounded expression, she smiled and said, \"It's from an elder, so don't be polite and just accept it.\"","Chen Haoran's mouth twitched.","Si Nian also went and cooked him a bowl of sweet dough drop soup. Chen Haoran felt that absolutely everything in the Zhou household was delicious.","Unlike his own home, where the New Year lacked any warmth or liveliness. They would either go to a hotel or have the nanny cook the meals.","Everything was pre-arranged, completely devoid of any New Year atmosphere.","Even when Si Nian asked him to stay for lunch, he declined.","He explained that he still had another house to visit.","Si Nian had no choice but to let him go.","Later that afternoon, Zhou Yueshen started preparing the food by slaughtering chickens, cleaning fish, and braising pork trotters, having also bought a good amount of seafood.","The whole family was bustling about, busy preparing the New Year's Eve dinner."]},{"number":444,"title":"Chapter 444: Chapter 441: Celebrating the New Year 01","paragraphs":["Since it was their first Chinese New Year in Beijing, Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen had prepared a lot of things.","They were incredibly busy right now.","The children were also very happy. This was their first time celebrating the New Year together as a complete family. Last year, they went to their grandmother's house, which was a different experience.","Si Nian cooked many home-style dishes, all of which were the children's favorites back in their hometown.","The large table was fully loaded with food.","Si Nian explained the auspicious meanings behind the dishes to the children. \"This is for abundance year after year, this is for great luck and prosperity, this is for rising higher every day, and this is for blooming wealth...\" She went through seven or eight dishes in a row. Seeing the children's fascinated expressions, Si Nian smiled and said, \"Hurry and ask your dad to get the firecrackers ready. We'll eat right after we set them off.\"","Second Child let out an excited howl and skipped outside to find his dad.","\"Dad, Dad! Mom says it's time to set off the firecrackers and eat!\"","He dragged Zhou Yueshen into the house from outside. Seeing his unhurried pace, the boy wished he could walk for him.","Second Child dug out the firecrackers they had bought in advance from the cabinet and handed them to him. \"Dad, you light them.\"","Mom had told him that he was still too young. Unlike small matchcrackers, these firecrackers were very powerful and shouldn't be lit by children.","So, he had to let his dad do it.","Zhou Yueshen reached out, took them, and walked outside.","Si Nian and the children followed him out.","By now, the sound of firecrackers going off could be heard everywhere, crackling and popping in a lively atmosphere.","It was finally their family's turn, and Second Child was so excited he was practically jumping.","\"Brother, Brother, look! Our family is setting off firecrackers.\"","\"Sister, Sister, come here quickly.\"","He helped cover Yaoyao's ears.","Zhou Yueshen lit the firecrackers. Soon, a series of deafening cracks and pops erupted at the doorway.","\"Aw, setting off firecrackers!\" Second Child cheered out loud.","Not to mention the excited boy, even Zhou Zedong, who was standing to the side, had a faint smile on his face.","Seeing her second brother so happy, Yaoyao jumped along with him and said in her milky voice, \"Setting off firecrackers!\"","It wasn't even six o'clock yet, but because it got dark early in the winter, it was already dusky outside.","After setting off the firecrackers, the family went inside.","The Spring Festival Gala was already broadcasting by now. Si Nian turned on the TV, and the festive programs of the Gala filled the screen.","They listened to the program while gathering around the table for their New Year's Eve dinner.","Second Child brought out the cola, poured himself a full glass first, and then filled everyone else's glasses.","This cola was expensive, unlike the cheap sodas sold on the street that would give you an upset stomach.","The children all loved it.","\"To celebrate our second New Year together as a family, and to being together and reunited every year from now on.\" Si Nian raised her glass, and the children immediately followed suit.","Zhou Yueshen looked at her with gentle eyes.","The family clinked glasses, and then the children buried their heads in their food.","Every time she watched the children eat, Si Nian felt her appetite grow because they ate with such relish.","It made her, who usually didn't have a big appetite, eat a little more.","After dinner, Si Nian dug red envelopes out of her pocket and handed them to the children.","\"This is Little Dong's, this is Little Han's, and this is your sister's. You can only open them when you go to bed later,\" Si Nian smiled mysteriously.","The children held their red envelopes excitedly, looking at each other.","Zhou Zedong said shyly, \"Thank you, Mom.\"","\"Mom, Mom, you are the best mom in the world,\" Second Child said super loudly.","\"Mom is the best,\" Yaoyao chimed in.","Si Nian patted their heads. The children's eyes then suddenly darted to Zhou Yueshen, who was sitting to the side.","Zhou Yueshen wasn't as particular and wouldn't create surprises like Si Nian. He simply pulled a wad of cash from his pocket, counted it, and handed them each two ten-yuan bills.","Second Child was just about to reach out and take it when Zhou Yueshen changed direction. Second Child watched helplessly as he handed the money to Si Nian instead. \"Let your mom hold onto it for you. She'll give it to you when you need it.\"","In this era, many working-class people only made about thirty yuan a month.","Keeping twenty yuan on a child was indeed unsafe.","Si Nian coughed. \"Right, it's not safe to keep so much money in your hands. Let Mom hold it for you, and tomorrow I'll take you to buy toys.\"","The children nodded in agreement. \"Then Mom can hold it.\"","\"Mom, I don't want toys. I want to save it to buy new clothes for my little brother,\" Second Child said.","Si Nian's heart warmed at his words. \"Okay, Mom will save it for you.\"","Zhou Yueshen then pulled a red box from his pocket. Si Nian took a look and saw the four characters for \"China Gold\" written on it.","She raised an eyebrow.","Zhou Yueshen coughed. Even though he had given her gifts many times before, he still felt a bit nervous, afraid she wouldn't like it.","But he had already bought all the rings, perfumes, jade bracelets, and pearl necklaces that Si Nian liked.","This time, he specifically asked Chen Nan what gifts his wife usually liked.","Chen Nan said his wife didn't have any other hobbies except buying gold. She would buy it even if she didn't wear it.","Only then did Zhou Yueshen remember that Si Nian didn't seem to buy much gold.","He bought her a gold bracelet and a gold lock.","\"Niannian, try it on and see if you like it.\" He handed it over to Si Nian.","Si Nian feigned a curious tone. \"What is this? Gold?\"","\"Yes, a bracelet and a gold lock. If you don't like them, you can go exchange them.\"","Si Nian was secretly delighted. Who wouldn't like gold? She opened it and saw a solid gold lock and a patterned bracelet.","They were quite heavy.","This must have cost a lot of money.","The patterns were delicate and quite beautiful.","She slipped the gold bracelet onto her wrist. With her fair skin, wearing the gold bracelet looked even better, making her appear very elegant and wealthy.","\"Help me put this on,\" she called out to Zhou Yueshen.","Zhou Yueshen stood up and put the necklace on her.","He even rubbed it with his hands to warm it up before putting it around her neck so it wouldn't be too cold.","Si Nian looked at herself in the mirror again and again, then turned to the children. \"Does it look good?\"","The children nodded. \"It looks good. Mom looks good in everything.\"","Thinking that today was New Year's Eve, Si Nian had specially changed her clothes and put on some makeup. The lipstick she applied gave her a very healthy and radiant complexion.","She had also put on the pearl necklace and rings she normally didn't wear.","Now, with the addition of the gold bracelet and gold necklace, she felt like she was covered in jewelry from head to toe.","Finding it a bit funny, she asked Zhou Yueshen to take them off and put them away for now.","Zhou Yueshen took them off and looked at her. \"Do you like them?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Of course I like them. They're very beautiful. Thank you, Zhou Yueshen.\"","Zhou Yueshen rubbed her head. \"No need to be so polite.\"","Si Nian took a red envelope out of her pocket and handed it to him. \"I originally thought that since all your money is with me, I would give you a big red envelope. After all, our Lao Zhou has been busy running around all day today and worked so hard. But seeing that you still have money to buy a gold necklace and a gold bracelet, I'm a bit embarrassed to even take out this little red envelope.\"","Zhou Yueshen was slightly stunned.","When he realized what she meant, he didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","How interesting. This was the first time someone had thought of giving him a red envelope."]},{"number":445,"title":"Chapter 445: Night Watch","paragraphs":["His Niannian was truly full of surprises.","He reached out and accepted it. \"Whether it's a little or a lot, it's the thought that counts, and your feelings are always worth showing.\" He held her hand and placed a gentle kiss on it.","The children looked away, unable to watch any longer.","Their dad and mom just couldn't sit together. Whenever they did, they would eventually start getting all lovey-dovey.","Eww~~~","After receiving their red envelopes, the children clamored to set off fireworks. Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen led them outside to do so.","Feeling too cold after the fireworks, Si Nian ran back inside to sit down. She covered herself with a small blanket, warmed herself by the small fire basin, and watched the Spring Festival Gala. Before long, the children ran back in, giggling and laughing, and snuggled up right next to her.","They said they wanted to stay up late to welcome the New Year.","Si Nian smiled and agreed.","The whole family sat on the sofa, planning to stay up for the night.","However, before it was even nine o'clock, their eyelids were already drooping one by one.","Yaoyao was the first to give in, falling asleep in her dad's arms.","Zhou Yueshen carried his daughter back to her room to sleep, then saw the Second Child resting against Si Nian's legs, sound asleep.","Despite his young age, he was snoring loud enough to shake the heavens.","Who knew when he had picked up such a bad habit.","Afraid the boy would catch a cold, he carried him to his room. The Second Child was still clutching his red envelope tightly, mumbling in his sleep, \"Hehehe, eating dumplings~~\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't know whether to laugh or cry. He pulled the blanket up to cover him, then went to tell his eldest son, whose head was bobbing with sleepiness, to go to bed.","Now, at last, only the two of them were left.","Pulling an all-nighter used to be nothing for Si Nian, but ever since she came to this era, her bad habit of staying up late had been completely cured. Now she was also feeling a bit sleepy and kept yawning.","Because of her pregnancy, she would sometimes get hungry in the middle of the night.","So she sent Zhou Yueshen off to get something to eat.","Zhou Yueshen went into the kitchen and boiled some dumplings. The two of them finished them off, taking turns feeding each other bite by bite.","They finally made it to midnight, but Si Nian was the first to succumb, falling completely asleep.","Helpless, Zhou Yueshen could only lean over, pick Si Nian up, carry her into the bedroom, and lay her on the bed to sleep.","Having gone to bed late the night before, Si Nian wanted to sleep in the next day. However, early in the morning, the crackling sounds of firecrackers echoed everywhere, making it hard for her to sleep in. She had no choice but to drag herself out of bed. They had made a lot of food yesterday, so today they just needed to stir-fry and heat up the leftovers, and it would be ready to eat.","Si Nian stubbornly dawdled in bed until mealtime before finally getting up.","Seeing that Si Nian was up, the children, accompanied by Da Huang, ran out covered in snow.","\"Mom, Happy New Year!\"","\"Good morning, Mom.\"","\"Woof, woof, woof~~\"","Si Nian smiled and said, \"Happy New Year.\"","The Second Child pulled at her, \"Mom, look quickly, we built a lot of snowmen.\"","Si Nian followed her son outside. A gust of cold wind made her shiver, completely driving away her sleepiness.","Several lopsided snowmen were piled up neatly at the door.","It was just that they didn't look very good.","The Second Child pointed to the two larger snowmen and introduced them to her, \"This is Dad, and this is Mom.\" He then pointed to the smaller snowmen next to them, \"This is Big Brother, me, and our little sister.\" Next to them was a shapeless lump. Si Nian asked curiously, \"What is this?\"","The Second Child said, \"Mom, this is Da Huang. Couldn't you tell?\"","Si Nian nearly choked on her own saliva and said, not knowing whether to laugh or cry, \"It does look quite like him.\"","The children immediately burst into happy laughter.","At that moment, some unknown child playing in a snowball fight outside threw a snowball that landed with a splat right on a snowman's head.","\"Ah, my head fell off!\" the Second Child exclaimed.","He immediately ran over angrily, standing in the yard to throw snowballs back at the people outside.","\"Brother, come help me! I can't beat them.\"","Zhou Zehan threw snowballs outward while turning his head to ask his older brother for help.","Unexpectedly, Zhou Zedong just turned and walked away.","Seeing that his brother had zero interest in participating, the Second Child got very angry and turned around to throw a snowball right at his brother's butt.","Zhou Zedong paused and immediately turned around.","The Second Child regretted it the moment he threw it, instantly putting on an 'I know I was wrong' expression.","But the very next second, his brother packed a snowball and hurled it at him.","The two brothers started pelting each other with snowballs in the yard.","Seeing this, Yaoyao also clumsily ran over, stepping through the snow. \"I want to play too! I want to play too, brothers!\"","\"Heave-ho—\" She threw a snowball, but it only flew about thirty centimeters before dropping, and the momentum caused her to fall flat on her bottom in the snow.","Si Nian couldn't stop laughing at the sight. She also picked up some snow and joined the children in their game.","As a result, with a splat, she threw one right onto Zhou Yueshen, who was just returning from outside.","Beside Zhou Yueshen were the members of the Chen family.","The Chen family had come early in the morning to pay a New Year's visit, but their car couldn't drive all the way in, so Zhou Yueshen had gone over to help them carry their things.","Now, covered in snow, he looked a bit comical.","Chen Nan stood to the side, wanting to laugh but feeling too embarrassed to do so.","Biting his lip, it was obvious he was trying very hard to suppress his smile.","Si Nian hadn't expected guests to arrive. She stood up straight, feeling a bit awkward. \"Uh, Brother Chen, Sister Miao, you're here too. Please, come in.\"","Miao Chunhua smiled and said, \"I was wondering why I could hear giggling from so far away. It turns out you guys were playing.\"","Si Nian scratched her head, only then remembering that she had been dragged out by her son before she even had a chance to wash her face.","Right now, her hair was a mess, and she was wearing thick pajamas, looking incredibly disheveled.","No wonder the family had such strange expressions when they walked in.","Zhou Yueshen ushered the guests into the house and put the things down. He walked up to Si Nian and asked, \"Why didn't you change your clothes? It's so cold outside.\"","He brushed off the snow sticking to Si Nian, afraid she would catch a cold.","Having packed several snowballs, Si Nian's hands were freezing and bright red. Zhou Yueshen took them in his palms and rubbed them to warm her up.","Si Nian felt a bit embarrassed. \"I'll go change my clothes. You go entertain the guests.\"","Zhou Yueshen murmured an agreement.","Si Nian went to change into a fresh outfit, tied her hair into a bun, and walked back out.","Only to see that Chen Haoran had already started a snowball fight with the children.","As an older kid, he surprisingly couldn't beat the younger ones and was currently being chased around by them.","Yaoyao trailed at the very back, her little face flushed red from running.","The others had already run several laps, and she still hadn't caught up.","Si Nian walked into the house and heard Chen Nan and Zhou Yueshen seemingly discussing something.","She didn't go over, only vaguely catching words like branch company and economic development.","Lately, these two were always discussing business.","Successful people really were different; they talked about work anytime and anywhere.","Just as Si Nian was about to enter the kitchen, Zhou Yueshen stopped talking, stood up, and followed her in.","Chen Nan watched this with great amusement. \"You really can't tell with Little Zhou, he's actually so henpecked.\"","Beside him, Miao Chunhua rolled her eyes at him. \"What do you mean henpecked? This is called doting on his wife.\"","Chen Nan curled his lip. Fine, ever since they met Si Nian, his wife spent all day comparing him to Little Zhou.","Anything he said was wrong.","Lately, he didn't dare say anything at all anyway.","The food had already been prepared and was currently covered with plates on the stove. The stove was still warm, so the dishes hadn't gotten cold.","Seeing him follow her in, Si Nian said, \"Why did you come in? I can handle this little bit of work myself.\"","In front of outsiders, Si Nian always made sure to give him face.","After all, even if Zhou Yueshen didn't think anything of it, some men would gossip behind his back.","Especially chauvinistic men like Chen Nan.","\"It's fine, Lao Chen doesn't care about this.\"","They had known each other for many years, so they didn't mind these little things.","Si Nian nodded at his words. Wondering what kind of business they were discussing, she asked curiously, \"Are you planning to expand the company? I just heard him mention something about wanting to open a branch.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded. \"I mentioned to him earlier that I wanted to open a branch back in our hometown. Our area is still relatively underdeveloped, after all, and many families can't afford these appliances, unlike here. Opening a factory there could really help boost the local economy. However, Lao Chen is a bit worried. Since the economy back home isn't very strong, he's concerned that the goods won't sell well.\""]},{"number":446,"title":"Chapter 446: Daughter or Son","paragraphs":["Zhou Yueshen had always wanted to return to his hometown, and the children were also more accustomed to life there. If the branch company could be opened there, he was confident he could make it big and successful. However, because some of their parts were imported, they were very expensive, and ordinary families simply couldn't afford them.","Even here in Beijing, the only ones willing to buy them were families with better financial conditions.","Making money was indeed profitable, but Zhou Yueshen wanted more to build a business that ordinary people could afford.","In this world, the poor still made up the majority.","The rural areas back home still only used black-and-white televisions.","Most could only afford radios.","Simply because color TVs were too expensive.","But as long as the price was affordable, there would definitely be many people willing to buy them.","It was just that there were no channels over there; they were basically all out-of-town merchants, which was why they were so expensive.","Zhou Yueshen said, I always feel that according to this development model, in the future, every household will definitely be able to afford these things.","Since that day will come eventually, it might as well start with me.","After hearing this, Si Nian looked at him in astonishment.","In the past, back in their hometown, their knowledge was indeed limited.","But after Zhou Yueshen came here, saw foreign products, secured partnerships, and experienced the rapid development of the company, he also foresaw the changes of the future.","That was why he had such thoughts.","Si Nian really admired these business people.","Their vision and intuition truly surpassed those of ordinary people.","While ordinary people were still hesitating about whether to start a small business, they had already taken a big step forward into the future.","She looked at Zhou Yueshen with admiration, suddenly feeling that his achievements in the novel were not without reason.","Seeing that she was silent, Zhou Yueshen turned his head to glance at her.","He saw Si Nian looking at him with a mix of surprise and adoration in her eyes.","Such a gaze made him slightly stunned.","Why are you looking at me like that?","Si Nian hadn't expected him to suddenly turn around; she immediately withdrew her gaze, blushing a little.","Having been married for so long, it was still quite embarrassing for her to stare blankly at this man.","I think you are quite amazing.","Zhou Yueshen raised an eyebrow. Aren't you worried I'll go bankrupt? With this kind of investment, one careless move could cost us everything.","That was why Chen Nan had been so hesitant.","Si Nian shook her head and said affirmatively, No, I believe in you.","As long as you do it, you will definitely succeed.","It wasn't just because of the plot, but rather Zhou Yueshen's steadiness and capability that made her firmly believe he could definitely do it.","Zhou Yueshen reached out and patted her head. Actually, let alone Chen Nan, when this idea popped into his head, he too had a moment of hesitation.","Because Chen Nan had said, if he failed, had he thought about the consequences?","The consequence, of course, was that his family would suffer hardships alongside him.","Perhaps even worse than before.","But Zhou Yueshen didn't feel that their past life was that bad. The reason for his hesitation was Si Nian, because he didn't want her to live a hard life with him.","Therefore, Zhou Yueshen was only discussing this matter with Chen Nan and hadn't told Si Nian.","He was afraid she would worry.","But to his surprise, upon hearing about this, not only was she not afraid, but she also fully supported him.","So this was what it felt like to be supported.","In the past, no one supported anything Zhou Yueshen did. When he wanted to retire from the military, his superiors disagreed; when he started a breeding farm, everyone was pessimistic about it.","But no matter what others thought or how they laughed at him, he never cared.","But Si Nian was the only exception; he cared too much.","Having a bond made him less decisive.","But even if she didn't want to, it didn't matter, because everything he did was to give her and the children a better life.","The two brought the dishes to the table, and Si Nian went out to call everyone in to eat.","Chen Haoran, a grown adult, couldn't even beat a few children, and right now his head and body were covered in snow.","The children giggled happily as they walked into the house.","Si Nian told them to wash their hands and eat, and only then did they remember it was time for dinner, obediently lining up to wash their hands.","Chen Haoran awkwardly shook the snow off his body. He was about to pull out a chair and sit down, but seeing that the children were so particular, he rubbed his nose and followed them in.","Miao Chunhua stood up to help. Si Nian had the children bring out cola and liquor. Zhou Yueshen and Chen Nan drank liquor, while the little ones drank cola.","Everyone sat down together. Chen Nan asked curiously, Isn't Sister Si pregnant? Why doesn't it show at all? She doesn't look like she's changed much.","Not only was there no change, but he also noticed that Si Nian had become even prettier.","Thinking back to the months his wife was pregnant, she was so tormented by their son that she couldn't eat and lost so much weight she hardly looked like herself.","How could there be such a big difference when both were pregnancies?","Si Nian replied, Maybe it's because I'm wearing thick clothes, so you can't tell. Besides, I'm only three months along, so it's normal that it's not obvious.","Do you know if it's a son or a daughter? he asked curiously.","He also knew that none of these three children were Zhou Yueshen's biological children, so he found it quite a pity.","But now that his wife was finally pregnant, he was extremely happy for him.","After all, no matter how close other people's children were, they weren't one's own flesh and blood.","Chen Nan still believed it was better to have a child of one's own.","I don't know. Si Nian shook her head; she hadn't paid attention to this matter.","Dad, why are you asking this? Chen Haoran asked in confusion.","You don't understand. Back when your mom was pregnant with you, she suffered a lot and her body changed completely. I was very worried at the time, but your grandmother said that sons make mothers ugly, so she was definitely carrying a boy. And indeed, your mom gave birth to you.","Your grandmother knows how to read these signs; they can tell if it's a boy or a girl. But looking at your Auntie Si's reaction, it seems like a daughter.","After speaking, he glanced at Zhou Yueshen.","Lao Chen? Are you serious? Nian Nian is pregnant with a daughter? Zhou Yueshen paused, his eyes showing a bit of pleasant surprise.","Mom, is there a little sister in your tummy?","The children looked over in pleasant surprise.","Chen Nan was dumbfounded.","In his opinion, having a son was essential for carrying on the family line and continuing the incense. Especially given Zhou Yueshen's age—he was already thirty-one or thirty-two—regardless of his capabilities, conceiving wasn't easy. Plus, with so many children already in the family, it would be best if the firstborn was a son, so there would be someone to inherit everything in the future. A woman giving birth to a son for her husband would also see her status rise and become more secure in their hometown.","If it was a daughter, she would eventually grow up and marry into another family.","Wouldn't all of Old Zhou's property go to these nephews then?","Although he was their adoptive father now, they weren't his biological children after all.","Chen Nan couldn't treat them as if they were his own flesh and blood.","Therefore, he assumed that Zhou Yueshen valued Si Nian so much because he wanted her to give him a son."]},{"number":447,"title":"Chapter 447: Someone Who Has Been Through It","paragraphs":["It wasn't that he looked down on these current children, but as someone who had been through it, and since Zhou Yueshen wasn't getting any younger, he felt the need to remind him.","Lest he regret it when it was too late.","Not to mention that human nature is unpredictable. Especially in a family like theirs, the children might be small and naive now, but once they grew up and had their own thoughts, seeing the family fortune, how could they not fight for it?","Once interests were involved, even the best relationships would become worthless.","But biological children were different; no matter what, they would remember that these were their parents and provide for them in their old age.","Among the bosses around him, whose family didn't have a few illegitimate children or siblings?","They all fought tooth and nail for money.","Logically speaking, a smart person like Zhou Yueshen shouldn't have missed this point. As a brother, he was genuinely thinking of him, not looking down on girls. But seeing the look of pleasant surprise on his face, it seemed a bit strange.","Could it be that he really wanted a daughter?","Seeing that the whole family's expressions were different from what he expected, he couldn't help but ask in confusion, \"Don't you guys want a son?\"","Si Nian corrected him, \"No, whether it's a boy or a girl, we are very happy. We don't care about that.\"","Hearing this, Chen Nan's eyes became a bit complicated, feeling that Si Nian was just comforting herself.","After all, women cared even more than men about whether they were pregnant with a daughter or a son. Everyone hoped for a son for their firstborn, and wanting a daughter later on was considered normal.","So he smiled and said, \"Yes, a son or a daughter is good, but you still have to have a son in the future.\" He reminded Zhou Yueshen.","Hearing this, Si Nian felt a bit disgusted.","Whether they would have more children in the future was a matter between husband and wife. What did Chen Nan mean by constantly asking this question?","Was he afraid that she couldn't give birth to a son to carry on Zhou Yueshen's family line?","Although she understood that men in this era valued these things, it was also true that it was unpleasant to hear.","She respected it, provided it didn't fall on her.","Zhou Yueshen said lightly, \"I'm perfectly happy with a daughter. Having a daughter is enough.\"","Having a child was not easy; it easily took a year. Not to mention the impact on Si Nian, seeing her uncomfortable sometimes made his heart ache.","If having a daughter really had less of an impact on her than having a boy, as he said, then he would be even more willing to have a daughter.","Chen Nan put on a caring appearance. You could say he lacked intelligence, yet his company was so big; you could say he was intelligent, yet he couldn't read the room at all.","Si Nian could roughly see through this person. In his eyes, women were just accessories. Being able to give birth to a son for him was good, and nothing else mattered. That was why he could casually say such pressure-inducing and uncomfortable things right in front of her.","Si Nian had never dared to agree with such people, and now she lost her good expression, saying indifferently, \"If you insist that I must give Lao Zhou a son, then I really can't do it. Otherwise, why don't you introduce someone to him? I think that Assistant Chen is pretty good.\"","\"Uh...\" Cold sweat slid down Chen Nan's forehead, and his face turned somewhat livid.","He really didn't think there was anything wrong with Secretary Chen. Why did these women all think this way?","Giving Secretary Chen to Zhou Yueshen wasn't to harm him; he just thought that since she had worked with him for so many years, she was experienced and could help him.","He still wanted to say something.","His wife beside him threw down her chopsticks, \"Chen Nan, are you done yet? Eat if you want, if not, get out of the way. Looking at you here is an eyesore and ruins my appetite.\"","In the past, during her first pregnancy, her parents-in-law gave her a lot of pressure, saying that the firstborn must be a son to be a good symbol, and whoever had a girl as their firstborn would never be able to have a son later, and so on.","It made her panic all day long and unable to eat. She was terrified of giving birth to a daughter and being looked down upon.","Her husband didn't stand on her side either. Although he was good to her, in this regard, he also sided with his parents.","He also thought she must give him a son.","That pregnancy tortured her so much that it left a shadow. Later, although she still wanted a daughter, out of a retaliatory mentality and the impact of the previous one, she wouldn't be willing to give birth even if they begged her.","That was why they only had Chen Haoran.","It was bad enough to apply that kind of thinking to herself, but now he was meddling in other people's business.","Thinking he was doing it for their own good.","Not reading their expressions at all.","Miao Chunhua felt ashamed of this husband from the bottom of her heart.","In her view, Si Nian's current state was very good. Whether it was a son or a daughter, as long as she didn't suffer, that was the best.","Chen Nan was given attitude by his wife, but he didn't dare to say much. He muttered a couple of sentences and looked at Zhou Yueshen, hoping he would speak up for him.","Unexpectedly, Zhou Yueshen said coldly, \"Lao Chen, I treat you as a friend, and I hope you respect my wife. If you don't even have basic respect for women, then we shouldn't interact in the future.\"","Chen Nan's face instantly turned ugly.","He finally realized that he had gone a bit too far. This kind of thing should be said in private, not face-to-face like this.","He was incredibly embarrassed.","This meal seemed a bit oppressive because of Chen Nan's words.","They finally finished dinner. The children stopped playing and helped clear the table, washing the dishes and wiping the table.","Knowing he was in the wrong, Chen Nan was too embarrassed to stay longer. He said a few words to Zhou Yueshen and took his leave.","Si Nian didn't really care what he said. Most people in this era were like this, and she could actually understand. Anyway, he wasn't her relative; what he said was just like a fart, gone once it passed.","Her mindset wasn't so poor that she would be sad over these words.","But seeing that the children didn't dare to go play, and Zhou Yueshen was staying by her side the whole time, carefully watching her expression...","She found it amusing.","\"Why are you all surrounding me? Not going out to play?\"","\"Mom, that uncle is bad. He said having a younger sister is bad.\"","The children were sensible now, so they naturally understood what the other party meant.","Back in the village, they had heard some adults say that girls were money-losers.","They only liked having sons.","They didn't expect it to be the same here.","Si Nian rubbed her son's head: \"That's because he doesn't have a daughter and doesn't know how wonderful daughters are, so he thinks daughters are bad. We won't stoop to his level.\"","Zhou Zehan nodded heavily.","Zhou Yueshen touched her belly and said in a deep voice, \"Nian Nian, don't feel pressured. I meant what I said, I like daughters.\"","Si Nian nodded, \"I know, I didn't take it to heart.\"","Actually, seeing Zhou Yueshen almost fall out with Chen Nan just now, she had been a bit worried.","Seeing that she truly wasn't sad, the big one and the little ones all breathed a sigh of relief.","No matter how comfortable the New Year days were, they passed quickly. In the blink of an eye, spring arrived.","Zhou Yueshen's plan received support. Now their factory was manufacturing an affordable electrical appliance, wanting to test the waters here first before expanding outward.","Zhou Yueshen didn't do his subsequent work at home, and he also changed to a male assistant.","Si Nian and the children soon started school. Her pregnancy was now showing. Although she did not mind it herself, it was annoying when people constantly asked about it. So, Si Nian made a point to wear looser clothes to hide it, heading straight home after classes.","But recently, perhaps because of her heavy course load, Si Nian felt as if something was weighing her down. Regardless, she was in a bad mood.","Especially since her belly had grown, Zhou Yueshen seemed to be intentionally keeping his distance from her, treating her like some fragile object.","Before, she used to complain that his body was too hot and did not want to snuggle close to him.","But now that he was not pressing up against her, she could not help but overthink.","She wondered if Zhou Yueshen was disgusted by her growing belly, her changing figure, and her fading beauty.","Women are incredibly sensitive when it comes to changes in their appearance and figures.","Especially someone as vain about her looks as Si Nian. A few months ago, she was still rejoicing and feeling lucky that she had not experienced any morning sickness.","But her belly grew just as it was supposed to, and her waist thickened significantly. For any girl, this was a massive blow.","She could no longer wear any of her old waist-cinching dresses.","She could not stop measuring her waist with her hands, fearing that after giving birth, her stomach would become wrinkled like some people's, never to return to how it used to be.","The more she thought about it, the more she regretted it.","That night, seeing Zhou Yueshen return and lie down next to her as usual without touching her, she could not help but shed tears.","Fortunately, Zhou Yueshen had sharp hearing. The moment she cried, he heard it. Startled, he quickly sat up and turned on the bedside lamp. Sure enough, seeing her twisted away from him with her back turned, her body trembling with each sob, he knew something was wrong.","He thought Si Nian was having stomach pains and anxiously asked if she was feeling unwell.","Hearing that his first concern was the baby again made Si Nian feel even worse. She felt he was being hypocritical. Someone used to say they did not want children, but now they talk about the baby every day.","He had been so firm about it back then that she really believed he did not want kids.","Sure enough, all men are the same.","Zhou Yueshen did not expect his words to stir up a hornet's nest. His usually steady gaze grew panicked. How could that be? I was just worried that your stomach was uncomfortable.","After saying that, he carefully lifted her into his arms, letting her sit on his lap while he wiped away her tears.","His rough fingers landed on Si Nian's increasingly tender and fair face; he did not even dare to apply any pressure.","Nian Nian, I am sorry, I did not mean it that way. Do not overthink it, okay?","Did someone bully you?","Si Nian turned her face away. Yes, someone bullied me.","Zhou Yueshen immediately frowned and said in a deep voice, Who? Someone from school?","Si Nian replied coldly, That person is far away on the horizon, yet right in front of my eyes.","Zhou Yueshen: ...","Influenced by hormones after getting pregnant, she had become a bit clingy, wanting to stick close to Zhou Yueshen from time to time.","But lately, after her belly had gotten slightly bigger, he had stayed far away from her.","This made Si Nian very angry.","Although she had heard that when a wife gets pregnant and gains weight, the husband might not say anything but would secretly feel disgusted. However, when this happened to her, she still found it unbearable.","Zhou Yueshen thought hard but truly could not figure out what he had done to make her angry.","But seeing that Si Nian's anger was genuine and not faked, his expression turned solemn. He wondered who had been badmouthing him in front of her. So, he took the initiative to admit his mistake. Yes, it is all my fault. I was wrong.","Si Nian: ... Why did that sound so off?","Did he really know what he did wrong?","Then tell me, what did you do wrong?","Zhou Yueshen: ...","Si Nian laughed out of anger and accused him, Fine, Zhou Yueshen. You have even learned how to brush people off now.","Zhou Yueshen's expression changed, his heart trembling. Nian Nian, do not think like that.","Seeing that he was genuinely frightened by her, Si Nian knew this man was completely straightforward, so she stopped teasing him. She said sullenly, I am your wife. Why are you keeping your distance from me lately? You have hurt my fragile little heart.","After saying that, she felt she was being a bit dramatic and turned her head away unnaturally.","Sometimes when she woke up and instinctively leaned into his embrace, she would find that he had retreated all the way to the edge of the bed.","Si Nian was furious.","At first, she did not think much of it, but as it happened more frequently, she could not help but overthink.","Hearing this, Zhou Yueshen froze for a moment, then did not know whether to laugh or cry. Just because of this?","He was built like a mountain, his whole body hard as a rock. After Si Nian got pregnant, she had become plumper, her skin tender and soft.","Normally, a slight bump would leave her bruised for days. She used to complain about how hard he was, saying it was uncomfortable to lean against him.","Therefore, Zhou Yueshen was worried about hurting her, which was why he had kept his distance.","He never expected that it would make her misunderstand and think he did not like her anymore.","Si Nian was indeed overthinking. Although her belly had grown, her limbs remained slender. It was just that she had become a bit fuller, and her old clothes no longer fit, giving her the illusion that her figure was ruined.","She and Zhou Yueshen had already decided that by June, she would take a leave of absence from school to stay home and give birth.","She could just make up the classes when she returned.","Anyway, she had already informed the school in advance.","But Si Nian never expected that something would happen at home."]},{"number":448,"title":"Chapter 448: The Big Brother's Car Accident, the Roommates with Their Own Agendas, and Xiao Bowen's Birthday Invitation","paragraphs":["Her parents called, hesitating and humming and hawing as they tried to borrow money from her.","Si Nian immediately knew something must have happened.","Because in all the time she had been married to Zhou Yueshen, her parents had never asked her for money.","For them to actually ask, it had to be something very serious.","Sure enough, under her pressing, her mother finally admitted over the phone, \"Your brother got into a car accident while trying to save someone. He needs a huge sum for surgery right now. We've emptied our pockets and still can't scrape enough together. We had no choice but to call you, otherwise I really didn't want to trouble you.\"","Lin's mother choked up as she spoke. Since her daughter was pregnant, she originally hadn't wanted to tell her about such things for fear of making her worry, especially since they lived so far apart.","But right now, her son desperately needed surgery. If they couldn't gather enough money and do the surgery soon, the doctor said he might end up disabled.","Lin's mother was truly out of options, which was why she had to ask her daughter for a loan.","Si Nian's face paled upon hearing this.","Because in the novel, her brother had indeed gotten into a car accident.","But she hadn't expected that even though she had changed some of the plot's direction and her brother no longer had to work as exhaustingly hard to make money as before, he would still end up in an accident.","And the situation was exactly the same as written in the novel.","She immediately said, \"Mom, what are you saying? That's my brother. You should have told me the moment it happened. Don't talk about troubling me.\"","After saying that, Si Nian didn't have time to ask for more details and immediately went out to wire the money herself.","In this era, things weren't as convenient as before, and it took a long time. Although one could use telegraphic transfers, or wire transfers for short, the transaction fees were high.","Right now, Si Nian couldn't care less about the high fees; she just needed to send the money back first.","In the novel, her brother ended up disabled precisely because his leg injury was severe and he didn't receive surgery in time.","If he had the surgery promptly, it could definitely be saved.","At the very least, he wouldn't become a disabled person at such a young age like in the novel.","With such a major crisis happening at home, Si Nian was truly worried.","But she couldn't just leave the children behind; they still had to go to school.","Zhou Yueshen had been busy with new electrical appliances lately and didn't have time to look after the children either.","Si Nian could only fret helplessly, planning to discuss the matter with him when he returned.","In the afternoon, when Zhou Yueshen came back with groceries, Si Nian told him about it.","Zhou Yueshen's expression grew solemn upon hearing the news. Seeing her distress, he said, \"Don't worry. I'll have Yu Dong find someone to go check on him. It will take time for the money you sent to arrive anyway. I'll ask him to front the money over there first, to ensure your brother gets treated in time.\"","As he spoke, he patted her head and went to call Yu Dong.","On the other end of the line, Yu Dong originally wanted to tease him for actually remembering his old brother-in-arms, but as soon as he heard about Si Nian's brother's accident, he turned serious.","He had spent time with Lin Xiao in the past, so they could be considered friends.","However, ever since he went back home to inherit the family business, they hadn't seen much of each other.","He hadn't expected such a massive incident to occur.","With Yu Dong's help, Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief.","She knew that although Yu Dong was often playful and not serious, he was absolutely diligent and reliable when it came to getting things done.","Zhou Yueshen comforted her, \"Rushing back now won't help matters. It's better to wait and see how the situation develops before making any plans.\"","If they rushed back in a panic, not to mention the children, they also couldn't just abandon their work here.","Besides, neither of them were doctors. If they went back, they could only wait around helplessly.","It was better to monitor the situation first.","If things didn't work out over there, they could always arrange for him to be transferred here for treatment.","Hearing him say this, Si Nian felt much more at ease and nodded in agreement.","Today, the children were once again dropped off by a luxury car.","Si Nian remembered this car; it belonged to the Xiao family. Xiao Bowen had visited her house before and had come over with the kids.","But why was it here again this time?","Looking through the car window, she saw Xiao Bowen's grandmother occasionally glancing back at the children with a loving gaze, which left her feeling somewhat puzzled.","For no particular reason, and considering their relationship with Xiao Bowen wasn't exceptionally close, this person was simply being too kind.","The children stepped out of the car.","\"How come you took Xiao Bowen's grandmother's car back again? Hurry up and thank her.\"","The children expressed their gratitude, \"Thank you, Grandma Xiao.\"","\"Oh, you're too polite, too polite. I was originally just taking Bowen home today, but I happened to run into the children, so I dropped them off along the way.\"","After Grandma Xiao finished speaking, she smiled at Si Nian and said, \"I heard all about the two children doing business from Bowen. Don't worry, I've already spoken to the principal about it. In the future, whatever ideas the kids have, just let them go ahead and do it. I'll take responsibility for them!\"","\"Yes, Mom, Mom! The teacher told us today too. From now on, my brother and I can do business at school, and no one will ever report us again.\"","Si Nian was slightly taken aback and asked in confusion, \"Madam Xiao, why are you helping us so much?\"","Grandma Xiao paused for a moment before realizing something. Her eyes flickered as she said, \"Oh, you forgot. When our Bowen was over at your place before, it was all thanks to your two children taking care of him. Now that you've come to our hometown, of course we have to repay you generously.\"","Si Nian paused, finally remembering this matter. Put that way, it did seem to make sense.","Then she heard the other party say, \"By the way, it will be our Bowen's birthday in a little while. His mother didn't raise him well, so he doesn't have many friends. He's only really familiar with your Xiaohan and Xiaodong, so I'd like to invite you to bring the two children over to celebrate his birthday.\"","Before she even finished speaking, Xiao Bowen's face turned red.","Si Nian initially wanted to refuse, but Second Child exclaimed in pleasant surprise, \"Really? Xiao Bowen, you're having a birthday too? Congratulations, and happy birthday to you!\"","\"Mom, do I need to get a gift for Xiao Bowen too?\"","Si Nian paused, thinking that Xiao Bowen was just like her two children. Perhaps this would be the first time someone celebrated his birthday for him.","She couldn't bear to refuse anymore.","She nodded and said, \"Of course.\"","Xiao Bowen's eyes lit up.","After seeing off the Xiao family, Si Nian led the children into the house.","She didn't tell them about Lin Xiao's situation, afraid that they would worry.","The children were actually quite fond of the Lin family.","Fortunately, the next day, news came from the Lin family saying that the surgery could proceed.","The doctor said there was a sixty percent chance of success.","That could be considered good news.","Si Nian also breathed a sigh of relief.","She hadn't been to school lately, and Liu Nana and the others were all worried that something might have happened to her.","After finding out that Chen Haoran was her relative, they even brought some fruit over to visit her.","Because Si Nian had taken a leave of absence due to illness, when they went to ask, the teacher just told them exactly that.","As a result, when they found Si Nian's house and she opened the door, they were all stunned.","Si Nian was actually sporting a large, pregnant belly.","They hadn't noticed it at all before.","\"You... this is...\" The group stared with their mouths wide open in shock.","Seeing the group of people, Si Nian was also slightly taken aback.","She immediately asked, \"Why are you guys here?\"","She was a bit confused.","Behind Liu Nana stood Zhang Xue and Lu Yao.","Si Nian could understand Zhang Xue and Liu Nana, but what was Lu Yao doing here?","Looking at the astonished gazes of the three, she didn't feel there was anything to hide.","After all, she hadn't been hiding it at home. With her belly getting so big, they would naturally know what was going on.","It was only natural that a sudden pregnancy would surprise them.","We... we noticed you hadn't been to school for a long time and got a bit worried. We asked the teacher and found out you were sick, so we got your address from Chen Haoran and came over to see you. We never expected that you're actually pregnant!","Si Nian nodded and said calmly, Yes, my husband and I have been married for two years, so it's normal to get pregnant. But it wasn't convenient to just say I was pregnant, so I asked for sick leave.","Then what about your studies... Surprisingly, what Lu Yao cared about was still Si Nian's academic progress.","But it made sense. After all, in her eyes, the English teacher was grooming Si Nian to become a diplomat.","The teacher had connections in that field, and it was said that she could introduce her students into it in the future.","That would save years of taking the long way around.","But such opportunities were rare, and Lu Yao's dream was also to become a diplomat, which was why she treated Si Nian as a rival and refused to let go of any chance.","Hearing that Si Nian was sick, she had been quite surprised, thinking that this meant Si Nian wouldn't have time to study.","When Liu Nana asked if she wanted to come visit together, she hesitated for a moment before tagging along.","She hadn't expected her to actually be pregnant.","However, Si Nian hadn't exactly kept her marriage a secret from them all along, so although they were a bit surprised, they quickly recovered.","Si Nian glanced at her and said, I can do my studying at home.","Lu Yao choked on her words.","Meanwhile, Zhang Xue's gaze constantly swept over her.","In the past, Si Nian had kept a low profile at school and was rarely seen wearing any accessories.","Because just the clothes she wore were things they couldn't afford.","But now she noticed that the items on Si Nian's ears, neck, and wrists were either gold or jade.","One look was enough to tell they were extremely expensive.","She had previously seen her taking a luxury car to school, and now seeing her wearing gold and silver at such a young age, she was almost certain that Si Nian's family was very wealthy.","Moreover, Chen Haoran had also mentioned that Si Nian was a relative of his.","Recently, she had learned from various people just how wealthy Chen Haoran's family was.","Thinking about how Chen Haoran was growing increasingly cold toward her, and hearing that quite a few other girls were showing interest in him, she felt a pang of regret. She shouldn't have been so reserved before; she should have taken the initiative when Chen Haoran was enthusiastic about her.","Now that Chen Haoran was acting cold toward her, no matter how hard she tried to dress up, she couldn't get him to give her a second glance. Zhang Xue knew she could no longer get close to him on her own.","So she thought of Si Nian. Hearing Chen Haoran say he had even visited Si Nian's house to pay New Year's respects, she figured that perhaps by building a good relationship with Si Nian, she could get in touch with him.","With Si Nian's help, surely Chen Haoran wouldn't reject her again, right?","Feeling her scrutinizing gaze, Si Nian looked back at her. Zhang Xue had changed so much over the past six months. Not only was she dressing much more provocatively, but she had also learned to apply makeup. Her makeup was a bit heavy, yet being on the thinner side, she gave off the feeling that she couldn't quite pull off such a look.","At first glance, it just looked like forced maturity.","Thinking back to when they first met half a year ago, when she wore her hair in braids and dressed somewhat conservatively, Si Nian couldn't help but sigh at how time could truly change a person.","Especially someone like Zhang Xue, who had just stepped into society and lacked experience.","Although she felt a bit lamentable, she didn't ask. Anyway, ever since the pastry incident, Si Nian had no intention of associating with her.","This time, she also hadn't expected these roommates, who usually harbored their own thoughts, to suddenly show up at her door.","It wasn't proper to keep them standing and talking at the door, so she led the three of them inside and poured them some tea.","The girls curiously looked around the house. The outside environment seemed average, as it was an old alleyway after all. To be honest, the path here had looked a bit rundown, and the houses were not only lower than the buildings outside but also felt oppressive.","But they hadn't expected the inside to be a completely different scene.","Wooden floors, leather sofas, a large television, a refrigerator...","These were things they had only ever seen on TV before.","Looks of amazement and envy flashed through their eyes.","They asked her when she would go back to school.","Si Nian replied, I'll wait until the baby is born. After all, it's not very convenient right now.","The girls thought it made sense. Seeing Si Nian get up to wash some fruit for them, Zhang Xue eagerly offered to help. Sister Niannian, the style of your house is so nice. It's beautiful.","Her words carried an obvious tone of flattery.","Si Nian paused and said indifferently, It's alright. Every household is about the same.","How can they compare to yours? I've heard all about it. You and Chen Haoran are relatives, and his family runs a factory selling expensive appliances like televisions. I'm so envious.","The admiration in her eyes didn't seem faked.","To be honest, among the three roommates, Si Nian had the best impression of Liu Nana, followed by Lu Yao, and she disliked Zhang Xue the most.","If it weren't for the fact that they had to see each other constantly at school, she wouldn't have even wanted to let her in today.","She could put on a polite front to host them, but she had no mood to play pretend besties with her.","I'm not too clear about that. I haven't known him as long as you guys have.","After saying that, without waiting for the other party to ask more, she walked out carrying the fruit.","Zhang Xue pursed her lips, feeling too embarrassed to ask further in front of Lu Yao and Liu Nana.","She could only sit down and join the others in asking about her health.","Si Nian answered each question but didn't initiate conversation.","The girls felt awkward staying too long. Liu Nana stood up first. Since you're fine, we can rest easy. We still have things to do at school, so we'll be leaving now.","Si Nian nodded and said, Sorry to trouble you all for coming to see me.","Don't be so polite, it's no big deal.","Liu Nana smiled. Lu Yao was merely curious about Si Nian's situation, and to be honest, she still felt a bit awkward in her heart, so she didn't ask anything.","Zhang Xue, on the other hand, was a bit reluctant to leave, seeming like she wanted to talk to Si Nian more.","She kept winking at her pointedly.","But Si Nian acted as if she were blind and simply couldn't see it. In the end, Zhang Xue had no choice but to helplessly follow the others back.","A few days later, her family called to tell them that her brother's surgery had finished successfully.","However, he might need a long time to recover.","Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief upon hearing this.","By the time she snapped back to reality, Second Child was already anxiously asking her what gift he should get for Xiao Bowen.","He repeatedly dug out two dollars from his piggy bank, only to stuff one dollar back in, asking Si Nian what he could buy with one dollar.","Seeing his stingy behavior, Si Nian laughed, Why are you only spending one dollar? It's not like you don't have money.","Second Child stiffened his neck and said, My money is being saved for my little sister and brother. I can't give it all to him.","Because he wasn't sure if it would be a brother or a sister, he always mentioned both.","He was terrified that leaving one out would be disrespectful to his future younger sibling.","Si Nian didn't know whether to laugh or cry at his words."]},{"number":449,"title":"Chapter 449: Hide and Seek","paragraphs":["These two children had already made quite a bit of money buying and selling things themselves. The other day, when she was changing the quilts, she packed it up, and it was quite heavy.","It was almost full.","Yet now, he was only willing to part with one note. It was easy to see how deep his love for his future little brother or sister was.","Si Nian felt a warm glow in her heart. Although these children weren't her biological ones, she felt they were even better than if they were.","Their transformation gave her a great sense of validation.","After all, she used to be an adult who hated bratty children.","Sometimes, just hearing children make a fuss would annoy her.","But the good behavior and understanding of these kids showed her that there are many, many good children in this world.","They needed someone to love them, and they knew how to cherish affection even at such a young age.","If you treated them well, they would want to repay you a hundredfold.","Such children were simply angels.","Just looking at him made Si Nian feel warm inside.","Very warm.","Si Nian said, \"If you are true friends, a birthday gift isn't about how much it costs, but the thought behind it.\"","\"As long as it's from you, even if it's not worth much, I believe Xiao Bowen will cherish it.\"","Second Child understood and nodded. He immediately stuffed his one-dollar note inside, then rummaged through a nearby cabinet until he found a stone.","He held it up to Si Nian and said, \"Mom, this is a stone I picked up by the stream in Xingfu Village. It can even sharpen knives. Sometimes when my pencil sharpener gets dull, I grind it a bit and it works great. I plan to give him a piece.\"","He thought to himself that this was something he was giving from the heart, and it didn't cost any money. It was the best of both worlds!","Si Nian didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","\"As long as you're happy.\"","On Fang Bowen's birthday, Si Nian led the three children over.","The car drove for about ten minutes before arriving at Fang Bowen's house.","Fang Bowen's house was very large, a European-style villa.","The surrounding houses were all similar villas, and just looking at them, you could tell the families were wealthy.","Si Nian wasn't someone who had never seen rich people before. After a brief moment of surprise, she took the hands of the curious children and walked in.","Although the house was big, besides a few maids, there was only Xiao Bowen and his grandmother.","The house felt large, empty, and lacking vitality.","There were some balloons and \"Happy Birthday\" signs pasted around.","It was obvious that the hosts also valued the child's birthday.","Right now, Grandma Xiao was helplessly talking to Xiao Bowen, who was wearing a little suit.","Xiao Bowen didn't seem very happy.","Seeing Si Nian and the others arrive, Grandma Xiao felt a bit embarrassed. \"I'm so sorry to let you see this joke.\"","\"What's wrong?\" Si Nian asked in confusion.","Grandma Xiao sighed helplessly, \"Bowen said he wants to make his own cake, but I don't know how to make one. I told him I'd have someone deliver one, but he wasn't happy. He said Xiao Dong and Xiao Han make their own cakes.\"","Si Nian paused for a moment after hearing this, then smiled helplessly. \"So he wants to make his own cake. Isn't that simple?\"","Xiao Bowen's face turned red. He had originally wanted to make a cake with Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan, but he didn't expect his grandmother to say that none of them knew how.","They had to buy one.","He didn't want a bought cake.","In the past, his mother always bought him cakes. He'd blow out the candles and eat it all by himself, which wasn't fun at all.","He wanted to have a different birthday, just like Eldest Child and Second Child.","\"Mom, Mom, I know how to make a cake! I'll make it with him,\" Second Child volunteered. Although he claimed to know how, he had only made one once, and he had even lost to his brother.","Si Nian smiled. \"Ms. Xiao, can we make it at your house? I know how to make a cake. It's very simple. If we have the tools, letting the kids make it themselves will be very fun.\"","She guessed that Xiao Bowen had seen Eldest Child and Second Child make their own cake for their birthday and wanted to try it too.","Grandma Xiao said, \"If you want to make it, that's easy. I'll call someone to bring the ingredients over right away. It's just that Bowen said he wanted me to teach him, and that's really hard for me.\"","Si Nian nodded, and soon someone brought the tools.","Si Nian went into the kitchen. Having money was great; the kitchen was even bigger than her living room.","It had areas for both Western and Chinese cuisine.","This was the 1980s, but Si Nian felt like she had returned to her own era.","For someone who loved to cook, a kitchen like this was simply fantastic.","Grandma Xiao hurried to have people help. She felt very embarrassed that Si Nian, who was pregnant, had to help teach her grandson how to make a cake.","Originally, she wasn't happy about letting the children hang around outsiders, but after observing for a while, she realized that Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen, this young couple, had indeed educated the children very well. No wonder Bowen always came back muttering about what the two brothers did today and what they were going to do tomorrow, every word filled with envy.","When she first found out about this, she only thought about how to get the child back.","But after being scolded by her son, she had let it go.","She didn't want to repeat the tragedy of her eldest son.","The more Grandma Xiao looked at Si Nian, the more she liked her. She even asked if she had any sisters she could introduce to her son.","Her son had been set up by Fang Hui back then, and she had come to their door with the child, trying to threaten them.","Grandma Xiao would never accept a woman like that as her daughter-in-law.","Even though her son now had a child, he had a stable job and the family was wealthy. If a girl was willing to marry him, they would definitely let her enjoy a good life.","It was just a bit of a compromise, having an adopted son.","Si Nian smiled. \"I only have one older brother and two younger brothers at home.\"","Grandma Xiao felt a bit disappointed upon hearing this.","The children were still talking over there. Second Child said, \"Xiao Bowen, this little bow tie of yours is so stylish. It looks just like the one my sister wears in her hair.\"","Xiao Bowen blushed and stammered, \"Idiot, this isn't a bow tie, it's a necktie. It's not the same as something as childish as a bow tie.\"","Yaoyao touched the bow in her hair and said in a childish voice, \"It looks exactly the same.\"","As they talked, Si Nian told them to go wash their hands.","At this moment, Jiang Jiu also arrived.","As soon as he entered, he let out an exaggerated \"Wow~\".","Hearing the sound, Second Child immediately shook the water off his hands and ran out, \"Xiao Jiu, over here!\"","Jiang Jiu, who had been brought by Jiang Wenqing, withdrew his gaze and, seeing Zhou Zehan, said in surprise, \"Second Brother, Second Brother, Xiao Bowen's house is so big! It's bigger than my house!\"","Second Child also said, \"It's my first time seeing such a big house too. I used to think the house in my hometown was the biggest, but I didn't expect Xiao Bowen's house to be bigger than mine.\"","After saying that, he pulled Jiang Jiu into the kitchen and said, \"Hurry up, we're going to make a cake! Do you still remember how to make it? You probably don't remember, haha, but I still do~\"","As he spoke, he was about to crack an egg into the bowl, shouting for Si Nian to watch him as he did it, \"Mom, Mom, look, I can crack an egg with one hand.\"","With a crack, he crushed the egg in his hand.","Second Child's face immediately turned red with embarrassment.","Si Nian said helplessly, \"You eat what you break. You can't waste food.\"","She didn't make fun of him, either.","The Second Child looked around at the other children. His older brother had already finished cracking the egg and was now rapidly beating it in a bowl with chopsticks, quickly turning the egg into a foamy mixture.","Xiao Bowen watched his brother and learned from him, mimicking his actions quite convincingly.","Looking at Jiang Jiu, he humbly asked his mother how to beat an egg.","Even their little sister was holding a small spoon, tapping away as she stirred the egg in her own bowl.","Of course, her mother had helped her crack the egg.","Yaoyao stirred for a long time but still couldn't break the yolk.","She was panting softly, looking so tired.","The Second Child was finally happy.","His sister was even worse at this than he was!","Si Nian taught the children how to make the cream and the cake base, and the rest was easy.","The kids each cut a small piece to decorate themselves.","Then, they had a competition to see who could finish first.","The ultimate winner, naturally, was the little culinary expert Zhou Zedong. Second place went to Xiao Bowen, third to Jiang Jiu, and fourth to Zhou Zehan.","There was no need to mention Yaoyao; her hands were covered in cream, and it was impossible to tell what she was trying to mold.","Xiao Bowen hadn't expected to actually make a cake himself. He was incredibly happy, his face beaming with joy.","He stood up straight with a proud little posture.","Plus, he had finished faster than Zhou Zehan and Jiang Jiu.","And this was his very first time making one!","Once the cakes were done, they had to wait until after dinner to eat them.","So, the children went off to play on their own.","Thinking that Xiao Bowen might like her cooking, Si Nian stayed in the kitchen to help.","After all, she didn't know what to get him for a present, so she figured she might as well help cook him a meal.","She let the children go play by themselves.","Xiao Bowen took them on a tour of his house. Every time they passed a painting, he would introduce it, saying it was from his grandfather's collection and very precious.","The others couldn't help but feel a bit puzzled. The Second Child was the first to ask, \"Your grandpa? How come I haven't seen your grandpa?\"","Xiao Bowen paused for a moment before replying, \"My grandpa is sick. He's lying in his room.\"","\"Then your grandpa is so pitiful,\" the Second Child immediately said sympathetically.","He didn't mean anything else by it; he just genuinely felt that being sick was pitiful.","Naturally, Xiao Bowen didn't mind.","As they wandered around, the Second Child and Jiang Jiu grew intrigued.","\"Xiao Bowen, your house is so big and has so many rooms. It's like a maze. Don't you ever get lost walking around in here?\"","\"Yeah, if we played hide-and-seek here, we'd definitely never be found. That would be so much fun.\"","Jiang Jiu chimed in.","Yaoyao also nodded her little head. \"Yeah, fun!\"","After saying that, she tugged on Zhou Zedong's hand. \"Brother, hide-and-seek!\"","Zhou Zedong frowned. \"This is someone else's house. We can't play hide-and-seek here; it's impolite.\"","To his surprise, Xiao Bowen's eyes lit up with interest. \"It's not that we can't play. Don't worry, hardly anyone lives here. You guys can run around these rooms all you want.\"","And so, the group of children started playing hide-and-seek on the second floor.","Yaoyao was too little and had to run along with her eldest brother.","Zhou Zedong's stamina wasn't the best, and carrying his sister, who had grown taller and chubbier, slowed him down significantly.","He swept his gaze around, noticed a room door that wasn't fully closed, and walked over to it.","Just as he opened the door, the Second Child called out from outside, \"Hide well, here I come!\"","Yaoyao covered her little mouth, blinking her eyes.","Zhou Zedong wasn't really interested in hide-and-seek, but his sister wanted to play, so he couldn't refuse.","As soon as he stepped inside, he smelled a strong scent of medicine.","He turned his head and, sure enough, saw someone lying in the bed.","Even as bold as he was, he was startled.","He was just about to leave when he suddenly noticed the person had tubes inserted into their face.","He immediately thought of the grandfather Xiao Bowen had mentioned.","Could it be this elderly man?","Driven by an inexplicable thought, he curiously walked over to take a look.","The old man was skin and bones. He must have been lying in bed for a very long time; the closer Zhou Zedong got, the stronger the smell became.","It was obvious that his life was being sustained by medication.","He thought to himself, perhaps this was what they called a vegetative state?","Zhou Zehan held his breath. For some unknown reason, the person before him gave him a very inexplicable feeling.","He couldn't quite put it into words.","His heart felt tight.","He was just about to quietly pull his sister away when she suddenly tugged at him. He tilted his head to look and saw her pointing at a large group photo on the bedside table, whispering in her milky voice, \"Brother, this is just like the one at our house.\"","Their mother had taken them to get a group photo taken before, and it was also framed and placed by the bed like this.","Thinking of those scenes, Zhou Zedong's face involuntarily softened.","He was just about to smile at his sister when his expression suddenly froze.","He abruptly grabbed the photo, making a loud noise because his movement was so forceful.","The Second Child, who was searching for them at the door, immediately pushed it open. \"I found you!\"","After he spoke, he saw his brother hiding something behind his back, staring at him with a dark expression, which gave him a fright.","Only then did he notice the old man lying in the bed.","He immediately covered his mouth in shock.","Oh no, had he disturbed Xiao Bowen's sick grandfather?","At that moment, someone called them downstairs to eat.","The children went downstairs and took their seats at the dining table.","The other children looked normal, with nothing strange about them.","Only Zhou Zedong remained silent, lost in thought.","But everyone was so happy right now that no one noticed.","Xiao Bowen's face was flushed red. He never expected that the hide-and-seek game he had once dismissed would be so thrilling to play right now.","He had run so fast, yet he was still caught by Zhou Zehan.","He thought that if there was a chance to play together again next time, he would definitely find a better place to hide.","Si Nian had made him a bowl of noodles. It was her signature clear broth noodles with lard, topped with a heart-shaped poached egg, looking absolutely delicious.","He immediately stood up and said, \"Thank you, Teacher Si.\"","\"You're welcome.\"","After everyone finished eating, it was finally time for cake.","Just after the candles were lit and he made his wish, he heard, \"Happy birthday, Xiao Bowen!\"","The children's smiling voices rang out, making Xiao Bowen's eyes widen as he stood frozen in place.","His eyes instantly turned red.","He had never had friends celebrate his birthday before.","It was so nice; having friends was truly wonderful!","\"Xiao Bowen, this is my birthday gift to you.\"","\"Xiao Bowen, this is from me.\"","\"Mine.\"","\"And me.\"","Yaoyao held up a milk candy and handed it to him.","Xiao Bowen, who was already on the verge of losing his composure, suddenly felt his eyes getting a little wet. He blinked hard to keep his tears from falling.","\"Grandma, my, my gifts.\" He held the gifts in his arms, at a loss as to where to put them.","\"Alright, alright, our Bowen has gifts too. Aren't you happy?\"","Xiao Bowen nodded heavily.","The children cheerfully sang the birthday song to him again.","Xiao Bowen carefully put the gifts away and then cut the cake for them.","Everyone ate until their faces were covered in it.","\"It's so delicious. This cream smells so good, Mom.\"","The Second Child was eating the cream in huge mouthfuls, which made Si Nian feel cloyed just watching him.","However, it was obvious that this cream wasn't cheap. She tasted a little bit; it was very fragrant and sweet. She couldn't blame the Second Child for thinking it tasted better than anything he had eaten before.","Although it didn't look very pretty, these were the ingredients, and no matter how ugly it looked, the taste would be the same.","Moreover, eating the cake they made themselves gave the children a great sense of accomplishment.","Xiao Bowen looked at Si Nian with admiration. He used to think that cake wasn't delicious at all and was just cold, but the one Auntie Si taught them to make was different. He had eaten so much of it. He really envied Eldest Child and Second Child for having such an amazing mother. But where was his own mother? She hadn't come to see him for a long time. He couldn't help but say, \"Teacher Si, it would be so great if you were my mom. I want to learn so many things from you.\"","Before Si Nian could speak, Second Child immediately swallowed the cake in his mouth, grabbed Si Nian's hand, and glared at Xiao Bowen, saying, \"No way! This is my mom, you can't steal her from us!\""]},{"number":450,"title":"Chapter 450: Discovery of Origin","paragraphs":["Before Si Nian could speak, Second Child immediately swallowed the cake in his mouth, grabbed Si Nian's hand, glared at Xiao Bowen, and said, \"No way.\" Hearing this, Xiao Bowen actually looked a bit regretful. He sighed and then said very reluctantly, \"Alright then, you guys have to treat Teacher Si well in the future.\"","His little expression left people not knowing whether to laugh or cry.","Only then did Second Child let go of her hand. He stiffened his neck and snorted, \"Of course.\" His small face tilted up with an expression of absolute certainty.","She rubbed the child's head, the corners of her mouth uncontrollably curving upward.","In the end, an entire cake was eaten completely clean by the children.","Normally, this kind of thing could be a bit too sweet and rich.","But the way Second Child ate it in big mouthfuls made it look incredibly appetizing.","Everyone was already full, but seeing him eat with such relish, they couldn't help but join in.","As a result, even the cream on the plates was scraped completely clean.","Si Nian thought to herself that if she took this child to a buffet in the future, they would definitely get their money's worth.","Thinking about this, she actually started to look forward to it.","The other children had eaten until their bellies were perfectly round. Seeing Second Child still stuffing snacks into his mouth, they could only look at him with envy.","\"Oh my, this child is eating so much. Be careful not to burst your belly,\" Grandma Xiao said with some concern.","Second Child poured a handful of small cookies into his mouth and said, \"I won't. I'm only seventy percent full. Mom said I can eat until I'm eighty percent full.\"","Grandma Xiao: \"...\"","Hearing this, Si Nian found it a bit amusing. Second Child's appetite was indeed twice that of other children. Because he was growing fast, running around everywhere every day, and getting a lot of exercise, his food intake was very large.","She was used to it herself, but outsiders probably found it a bit hard to accept.","Feeling a little embarrassed, she said, \"Alright, Xiao Han, eat a little less. If you eat too much, your tummy will hurt.\"","Remembering the time his tummy hurt before, Second Child was scared and immediately pulled back the hand that was reaching for more snacks.","After the gift-giving and cake-eating were over, Second Child actually started helping to clear the plates.","Xiao Bowen looked at him in confusion, \"Xiao... Zhou Zehan, what are you doing?\"","\"Helping clear the table. Don't you help with chores at home?\"","Xiao Bowen was a bit dazed, \"Y-yeah, I never clear things away at home. Grandma says I don't need to.\"","\"If I don't clear them, then my mom has to do one more thing, and that's too hard on her. Clearing plates isn't even as tiring as practicing boxing, so of course I have to do it.\"","Second Child didn't even lift his head as he clattered away, carrying the plates to the kitchen, and then ran back out to wipe the table.","He did these things so often at home that it had become a natural reflex for Second Child.","Seeing that no one was clearing the table after they finished the cake, he immediately took it upon himself to do it.","Hearing this, Xiao Bowen felt it made a lot of sense. In the past, his mother never let him do this kind of thing, nor did she let him enter the kitchen.","After coming to his grandma's house, there were many nannies, so they let him do it even less.","Every day, he just read books, did his homework, and played by himself.","He scratched his head and said, \"But my house has nannies.\"","Second Child suddenly realized, \"Ah, right, your house has nannies. Why am I clearing things for you?\"","He then remembered Grandma Liu, whom his dad had found for them before; she was mean and her cooking was terrible.","And yet, Xiao Bowen's family had several people like that.","He immediately cast a very pitiful look at Xiao Bowen.","Si Nian: \"...\"","Help, how did this child bring his diligence to someone else's house?","Seeing it was getting late, Si Nian hurried to lead the children home.","Grandma Xiao offered to have them driven back, but Si Nian declined, wanting to take the children for a stroll.","Jiang Wenqing had dropped her child off and hurriedly left again, saying she was letting Jiang Jiu go play at Si Nian's house.","So Si Nian took him along too.","After leaving the Xiao family's house, Si Nian finally said to Second Child, \"Xiao Han, in the future, don't touch other people's things when you're at their house, understand?\"","Second Child looked up at her, a bit nervous. \"Mom, did I do something wrong?\"","Jiang Jiu said, \"I know! Auntie is definitely afraid that Second Brother will sneak into the kitchen to eat things.\"","Every time Second Brother got greedy for food, he would sneak into the kitchen to find something to eat.","He had even taken him along to look before.","Zhou Zehan: \"...\"","Si Nian didn't know whether to laugh or cry. \"No, Mom is worried that you might accidentally break their plates, which wouldn't be good. Although wanting to help is a great thought, when we are at an outsider's home, we still need to maintain a little bit of boundaries, understand?\"","Second Child nodded and said obediently, \"Mom, I understand!\"","Si Nian patted his head and said to Zhou Zedong, \"Xiao Dong, let me hold your sister's hand. We will take the bus back in a bit.\"","After speaking, she heard no response. She turned her head in confusion, only to find Zhou Zedong following behind mechanically, seemingly unresponsive to her words.","Si Nian then realized something was wrong. Zhou Zedong usually didn't talk much at home. Today at Xiao Bowen's house, he had been very active in making the cake with everyone at first, and nothing seemed amiss. Later, while eating the meal and the cake, he hadn't spoken at all. Si Nian had assumed he was just too shy to sing the birthday song.","And that was why he had remained silent.","Now, seeing him spacing out, she became a little worried. \"Xiao Dong? What's wrong?\"","\"Brother, Brother, Mom is calling you!\"","Second Child also shouted loudly.","Zhou Zedong suddenly snapped back to reality and stopped in his tracks, startled. He looked up at his confused mother and brother, his eyes shifting before he said, \"Mom, what is it?\"","Si Nian frowned and instinctively reached out to feel his forehead, then touched her own. It didn't seem like anything was wrong. She couldn't help but look at him in confusion. \"Xiao Dong, what's the matter? Are you feeling unwell somewhere?\"","Zhou Zedong paused, then shook his head. \"Mom, I'm fine.\"","\"Brother, were you spacing out just now? Mom called you several times and you didn't react.\"","Second Child asked curiously.","\"Brother is ignoring Yaoyao. I don't want Brother, I want Mom.\" Yaoyao reached out for Si Nian to hold her hand.","She had been talking to her brother just now, but he hadn't answered her.","She looked at her brother aggrievedly.","Zhou Zedong said apologetically, \"Sorry, Yaoyao, Brother didn't mean to.\"","\"Xiao Dong, is there really nothing wrong?\"","Zhou Zedong shook his head. \"Mom, I'm fine.\"","Si Nian sensitively realized that something was off, but she couldn't put her finger on it for the moment. Seeing that he was unwilling to speak, she didn't force him.","The two children's business continued, but after the incident that happened before, even if the teacher allowed it at school, Zhou Zedong insisted on not doing it at school.","He even did business under the guise of helping bring things in for others from outside the school.","Not only that, when it was time to pay for study materials and various other fees, the teacher actually said that they didn't need to pay.","Saying that someone had already paid for them.","Second Child was very confused. When his dad drove to pick him up, he climbed into the passenger seat, pulled on his seatbelt, and asked Zhou Yueshen, \"Dad, today the teacher said we needed to pay the materials fee, but told us we didn't have to pay. Did you and Mom already pay for me and my brother in advance?\"","Zhou Yueshen froze for a moment, then said in a low voice, \"Not yet. Could it be that your mom paid it? Let's ask her when we get back.\"","Because he was mostly busy, it was Si Nian who took care of the children, so she handled a lot of these matters.","Zhou Yueshen truly didn't know about this matter.","After he finished speaking, he noticed that his eldest son hadn't gotten in the car. He turned his head to look at him, \"Xiaodong, what's wrong?\"","\"Dad, I'm going to the library. You guys go back first.\"","Zhou Zedong said as he closed the car door for his younger sister.","Zhou Yueshen paused for a moment, then nodded. \"Do you want Dad to come pick you up later?\"","He shook his head. \"I can go back by myself.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded and handed him some money. \"Buy whatever books you want and read them at home. Don't stay out too late.\"","Zhou Zedong gave a sound of agreement.","The Second Child's eyes turned red with envy as he watched his brother accept the bill expressionlessly.","He immediately grabbed his seatbelt and said, \"Dad, I suddenly want to go read books too.\"","Zhou Yueshen tapped him on the head. \"Sit properly.\"","The Second Child immediately behaved.","In his heart, however, he couldn't help but secretly criticize his brother. Hypocrite! When Mom offered him money, he never took it.","But when Dad gave him money, he accepted it right away.","His brother was too cunning.","Watching the car drive away, Zhou Zedong turned and walked to the school gate.","He deliberately stood in a specific spot.","Sure enough, Grandma Xiao got out of a car and spotted him immediately.","Her eyes lit up at once, and she approached with a smile. \"If it isn't Xiaodong! What are you doing here? Hurry and get in the car, Grandma will take you home.\"","Zhou Zedong's little face grew even colder, and his voice carried a hostile edge. \"You don't need to pretend anymore. I know who you are.\"","Grandma Xiao froze for a moment. \"Wh-what?\"","Previously, Zhou Zedong hadn't understood why Xiao Bowen's grandmother was so enthusiastic toward them. At the time, he just assumed it was because they had helped Xiao Bowen.","So, whenever she saw them, spoke to them warmly, and offered to buy snacks for his younger brother and sister, he hadn't said anything.","Later on, their act of selling things at school was reported by the tuck shop owner, who tried to stop them from continuing their business.","The tuck shop owner despised them so much and was the kind of person who would snatch away even a single dollar; it was impossible for him to suddenly change his tune and say they could get along peacefully.","Growing up, he had encountered too many people. He could tell what kind of person someone was with a single glance. He knew as clear as a mirror whether the owner would actually let them run their business.","Harboring doubts, he deliberately visited the tuck shop a few times, only to find that the original owner was gone.","This surprised him greatly. He didn't believe the school would kick the owner out just so the two brothers could do business.","And it was even more impossible for the owner to give up his business just because of them.","Not only had the owner been replaced, but the teachers also told them they could do whatever they wanted, which was already very strange.","Today, they were specifically kept behind and told that they didn't need to pay the material fees.","If he hadn't seen that photograph, Zhou Zedong might not have thought too deeply about it.","But now, he instantly understood exactly what was going on.","Zhou Zedong said expressionlessly, \"I saw it, that photograph. I've seen him before. When he came to our house, my mom would treat us well. My mom said he is my dad, but I don't want to acknowledge him.\"","Grandma Xiao's eyes widened in shock!","\"You, you went into your grandfather's room?\"","Zhou Zedong immediately retorted, \"That's not my grandfather. I don't have a grandfather!\"","His dad is Zhou Yueshen, and his mom is Si Nian.","He has no other relatives!","Grandma Xiao's face paled. \"Xiao, Xiaodong, listen to Grandma. I can explain this.\"","Zhou Zedong took a step back and said coldly, \"There's nothing to explain, and I don't want to listen. Right now, I only want to stay with my mom and dad. I don't want to acknowledge anyone else. I sought you out today to tell you not to target me and my younger brother and sister. We will never leave our mom and dad. And don't interfere in my and my brother's affairs anymore. We don't need your help or your pity.\"","Hearing this, Grandma Xiao's heart trembled. He had actually discovered that she was helping them behind the scenes?","This child was far too observant and sharp!","I-if he returned to the Xiao family, then...","Before her thought could settle, she met Zhou Zedong's resolute and cold eyes.","That fierce gaze, preferring to break rather than yield, frightened her.","It was exactly the same as the look her eldest son had when he wanted to leave for that woman all those years ago.","And because of that one time, she had forever lost her son and her husband.","This child was truly too much like his father.","Grandma Xiao's eyes reddened, and she choked up, \"Child, it was us who let you down back then.\"","Zhou Zedong didn't care at all. Looking at the tearful person in front of him, his attitude remained incredibly cold. He was very happy now with his younger brother and sister. He loved his current life, and he loved his mom and dad.","He didn't want anyone to come and destroy their family.","He knew Xiao Bowen's family was very rich, lived in a big house, and his grandmother was very powerful, able to have someone expelled from school with a single word.","Therefore, he was afraid, afraid that this person would snatch his younger siblings away and force them to separate.","Zhou Zedong didn't want such a thing to happen, so he had specially waited for Grandma Xiao today. No matter what she wanted to do, he had to tell her to give up on the idea completely.","She must not target them.","He had seen Xiao Bowen; ever since Xiao Bowen came back, he had never seen his mother.","After finishing his piece, Zhou Zedong, ignoring Grandma Fang, turned around with his schoolbag on his back and walked away.","Now that he knew about this, he would never interact with the Xiao family again. He even wanted to leave the capital, but relying solely on his current self, he couldn't do anything.","He also couldn't tell his mom and dad. He was terrified that if they found out their biological father was from the Xiao family, they would send them away.","Just thinking about this possibility drove Zhou Zedong crazy.","He would absolutely never leave.","He wanted to be with his family forever.","Grandma Xiao's face was filled with desolation. Looking at Zhou Zedong's resolute back, the sliver of hope she had kept hidden in her heart completely vanished.","She turned around, brimming with sorrow, only to suddenly meet her grandson's disappointed gaze.","Grandma Xiao froze, and in an instant, a chill ran through her heart.","C-could it be that all of this was orchestrated by little Bowen?","Indirectly telling her that the two brothers were being bullied, prompting her to step in and help.","Then, using his birthday as an excuse, inviting the children to the house so that Zhou Zedong would discover his grandfather.","That group photo was only kept in his grandfather's room.","Zhou Zedong was the person most likely to know what his biological father looked like. If someone suddenly helped him behind the scenes, with his personality, he would definitely get suspicious.","If that was truly the case, then this child was far too terrifying.","No, no, no, little Bowen didn't know about the two children's background.","Her son couldn't possibly have told him such a thing, right?","Thinking this, Grandma Xiao breathed a sigh of relief in her heart.","It seemed she was overthinking things.","Her grandson had just celebrated his ninth birthday; how could he possibly understand such complicated matters?"]},{"number":451,"title":"Chapter 451: The Lin Family Accident","paragraphs":["Whether that warning had taken effect or not, Zhou Zedong rarely ran into Grandma Xiao after that.","Most of the time, a driver would drop Xiao Bowen off at school.","The Zhou family also entered a peaceful period.","Si Nian's belly was getting bigger and bigger, and the children were all being very careful.","Yaoyao was no longer as clingy with Si Nian. In the past, she would constantly stick to Si Nian and want to sleep with her. Si Nian would coax her to sleep, and then Zhou Yueshen would carry the little dumpling back to her own room.","The little girl was forgetful; she would wake up and forget everything.","But now that her mother's belly was big, and seeing her father and brothers acting so cautiously, she understood. She knew her mother had a little brother or sister in her tummy, so she was careful too.","Si Nian was still woken up by her daughter for breakfast in the morning.","Her pregnancy was comfortable, partly because of her good health. She could eat and drink well, rarely experienced morning sickness, and her complexion was getting better and better.","Si Nian had initially been a little afraid, as some people had severe and frightening pregnancy symptoms.","Whenever she scrolled past those kinds of videos, she would instinctively skip them, not daring to watch.","When it came to her own turn, she would sometimes even get scared in her dreams.","But after getting used to it, it seemed like no big deal.","\"Mommy, older brother says it's time for breakfast,\" Yaoyao said, lifting her round little face as she saw her open the door. After speaking, she carefully touched Si Nian's belly and said in a milky voice, \"Good morning, little brother or sister. You have to grow up quickly today too.\"","Si Nian smiled and stroked her daughter's soft hair. \"Okay, let's go eat.\"","Yaoyao nodded and reached out to pull her.","At the dining table, Yaoyao sat down, put on her little bib by herself, and pushed the eggs toward her mother. \"Mommy, brother steamed eggs for you and me. They're delicious.\"","Second Child also came in yawning. Rubbing his eyes, he said, \"Mom, you woke up earlier than me today.\"","Si Nian laughed. \"You have the nerve to say that? If you don't eat soon, you'll be late.\"","The biggest symptom of her pregnancy was probably lethargy. She wanted to sleep as soon as she was full, and sleeping for over ten hours a day wasn't enough.","So she had been waking up late recently.","But because the children had to go to school, Si Nian still tried her best to wake up early and have breakfast with them.","After all, she didn't want to wait until the children left to eat a cold breakfast all by herself. That would be too pitiful.","Zhou Yueshen hadn't come home again last night; the man was simply too busy.","Whatever. Seeing a man every day could get annoying anyway; it was fine if he didn't come back.","Si Nian was clingy with Zhou Yueshen, but strictly at night.","As soon as day broke, she assumed her independent persona.","She was practically two different people during the day and at night.","She felt like pregnancy was making her a bit schizophrenic.","She couldn't finish that many eggs, so she scooped a large spoonful for each of her two sons. \"Next time, don't just steam eggs for me and your sister. You two should eat some too. You need more protein to grow fast.\"","Even though the family was wealthy now, the children still maintained their frugal habits.","Whenever Eldest Child cooked, he would always save the best for her and his sister.","He and his younger brother couldn't bear to eat it themselves.","Sometimes, if their sister couldn't finish, Second Child would take the leftovers and shovel them into his mouth.","It was quite heartbreaking to watch.","While frugality was a good thing, with their current living conditions, it was completely unnecessary.","They could eat whatever they wanted.","\"Mhm, Mom, it smells so good and tastes great, but it's not as good as yours,\" Second Child added at the end.","This wasn't the first time he had stepped on his brother to praise Si Nian.","Zhou Zedong was used to it and just glanced at him.","He decided that tomorrow morning, he wouldn't wake his brother up. He would let him be late and get punished by the teacher to stand in the corner.","Just as the family finished eating and was getting ready to leave, they heard the barking of Da Huang outside.","Zhou Yueshen was back.","Si Nian and the children, who were carrying their schoolbags, walked out the door and saw Zhou Yueshen pinching Da Huang's mouth, stuffing something inside.","Da Huang was behaving very obediently. Normally, it would turn its nose up at anything other than meat offered by others.","But when it came to whatever was in Zhou Yueshen's hand, Da Huang would obediently open its mouth even if it were poison.","After swallowing, it even seemed to think it was tasty, pawing at Zhou Yueshen's hand to see if there was more.","\"Dad, what yummy thing did you give Da Huang? I want some too.\" Second Child immediately trotted over and curiously patted Zhou Yueshen's pocket.","Zhou Yueshen clapped his hands to dust them off, glanced at his gluttonous youngest son, and said in a low voice, \"Dad gave Da Huang deworming medicine. Do you want to eat that too?\"","The little hand Second Child had just slipped into his pocket instantly froze.","He immediately took a few steps back, putting distance between himself and Da Huang. \"Da Huang has bugs? I know, Da Huang must have fleas, the jumping kind. I used to have them, and they would jump onto my brother too. I caught a lot back then and even kept them in a bottle, but they all died later.\"","Si Nian was speechless. Could he not describe it in such detail? She was truly terrified of those kinds of things, alright?","\"Da Huang is dirty. Only dirty things get fleas.\"","\"Sister, stay away from Da Huang, or they'll jump onto you.\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't know whether to laugh or cry. \"Alright, hurry up and get in the car. I'll drive you to school.\"","He had indeed heard that having a dog at home could be unhygienic, as dogs could get parasites which were bad for pregnant women. So, Zhou Yueshen had stayed up late last night finding someone to buy deworming medicine.","He heard it would work quickly once ingested.","That was why he fed it to Da Huang.","Actually, ever since Si Nian came to the family, she had paid special attention to Da Huang's hygiene.","Previously, because its fur was too thick and it got a skin disease, it had been shaved completely bald. The fur that had grown back now was yellow, shiny, and very flowy.","Passersby outside would praise its coat when they saw it.","But dogs ultimately lay and rubbed against the ground outside, so they definitely wouldn't be completely clean.","Second Child darted over to Si Nian's side and said, \"I'm not taking the car. I want to walk there with Mom.\"","Because Si Nian had said she wanted to go for a walk and drop them off at school along the way, he had specifically waited for his mother.","He didn't want to ride in the car with his dad; car rides were no fun.","Zhou Yueshen looked toward Si Nian. She had her hair pinned up and was wearing a loose dress. Even though her belly was already big, her limbs were still slender. Her skin was rosy, and her complexion looked exceptional, giving anyone who looked at her a feeling like a gentle spring breeze.","Her temperament was gentle, so all the children wanted to stick close to her.","Now that Si Nian was taking them to school, they were overjoyed.","He didn't dampen his son's spirits and said, \"Alright, we'll walk there.\"","After saying that, he stepped forward and let Si Nian link her arm through his.","Second Child was pushed aside and wasn't very happy about it. He immediately rushed to Si Nian's other side, grabbed her hand, and said, \"Mom, I'll go for a walk with you again when I get back this afternoon.\"","Si Nian smiled and said okay.","It wasn't far to walk from here to the school, just a ten-minute distance.","Watching the children enter the school, Si Nian finally looked at Zhou Yueshen. He looked to be in good shape.","She said, \"Aren't you tired? You didn't even go rest first when you got back. I could have just walked them here; it's not far anyway.\"","Zhou Yueshen said softly and gently, \"I'm not tired. I went to the factory last night. There was a problem with the goods, and we couldn't meet the shipping deadline, so everyone worked overtime for a long time. It was too late at night, and I was afraid of disturbing you, so I didn't come back. I slept at the factory for a few hours, and now I feel very refreshed.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian said enviously, \"You're so energetic after only sleeping for three or four hours a day. But now, I sleep for over ten hours a day and still can't get enough. I feel like my bones have gone soft from sleeping.\"","Zhou Yueshen looked at her lazy expression. In fact, sleeping too much wasn't very good for her health, but Si Nian was pregnant, so this situation was normal.","Seeing her slump completely beside him, he said in a deep voice, \"I'll give you a massage when we get home.\"","Perhaps because her belly was getting bigger, Si Nian walked slowly. Arm in arm with Zhou Yueshen, she got tired after just a short while.","The two stopped and started along the way. A walk that usually took just over ten minutes ended up taking half an hour before they reached home.","Upon arriving home, Si Nian lay down on the sofa and refused to move no matter what.","By the time Zhou Yueshen finished massaging her, Si Nian had fallen asleep again.","This situation continued for quite a long time.","Because Si Nian liked to go out for a walk every day, Zhou Yueshen would give her a massage after every bit of exercise.","He knew exactly how to adjust his strength, and Si Nian came to enjoy it more and more.","However, her days of enjoyment didn't last long. Just the day after receiving a letter saying her brother had been discharged from the hospital, a phone call came from her hometown.","But this time, the person calling wasn't a family member. Unless it was something very important, her family would usually write letters to them. After all, phone calls were too expensive, and they were more accustomed to writing letters.","The person calling was Yu Dong. His tone was very heavy, and as soon as he spoke, Si Nian's expression changed.","Si's Father and Zhang Cuimei had hired people to beat up her parents.","Her mother's head was busted, and her father's condition was even worse—his internal organs were ruptured, and his life was in danger.","Furthermore, this incident happened just yesterday when her eldest brother was discharged from the hospital.","The specific reason was that Lin Sisi had secretly taken money from the Lin family to pay for Lin Xiao's surgery, and it was said she took quite a lot.","But she hadn't told Si's Father.","By the time Si's Father discovered the money was missing, it was already too late. He believed that the Lin family had manipulated his daughter into secretly stealing money for them.","Originally, Si's Father was already frustrated and angry enough because of what happened with Si Nian.","A while ago, Lin Sisi had supposedly wanted to start a business. As a result, she took some money and made a trip, but she didn't get the goods and had three thousand yuan stolen from her. Although it wasn't Si's Father's money, but his wife's private savings, Si's Father was furious when he found out and raised his hand against Lin Sisi for the very first time.","Who knows what Lin Sisi was thinking; perhaps because she felt wronged in the Si family, she began to miss how good the Lin family had been to her.","On the day of Lin Xiao's accident, she immediately offered to help raise money.","The situation was too urgent at the time, and Father and Mother Lin had no other choice, so they accepted it. They had originally planned to pay Lin Sisi back once they got the money from their own daughter.","However, Lin Sisi refused to take it back no matter what, saying it was a small compensation to repay the Lin family and make up for her past mistakes.","Later, because they were too busy taking care of their son, Father and Mother Lin ended up neglecting the matter.","By the time they realized it, Si's Father and Mother Si had come looking for trouble.","Yet Lin Sisi herself was nowhere to be found.","With no one to help explain, the situation blew up even more.","By the time he received the news, Father Lin had already been sent to the hospital for emergency resuscitation.","So he immediately called the two of them.","The situation was critical. Si Nian was so shocked that she stumbled back two steps. Zhou Yueshen hurriedly stepped forward to support her.","Si Nian's vision darkened slightly. She hadn't expected Lin Sisi to be involved in this.","Because she wasn't in her hometown, her parents couldn't contact her immediately, which gave Lin Sisi a chance to exploit the situation.","Her parents were probably afraid she would be angry, so they hadn't mentioned it before.","But it ended up resulting in such a disastrous outcome.","Couldn't Lin Sisi, that menace, just stay far away from the Lin family?","She had given up the man to her and yielded the status of the Si family's young lady. If Lin Sisi just lived her life properly, she wouldn't have it bad at all.","Why did she still have to pop up from time to time to make her presence known?","Si Nian knew deeply that wherever the female lead was, there would inevitably be conflict.","But she never expected this conflict would fall upon her parents' heads.","Her parents had been desperate to save their son. At that time, if someone was willing to give them money, they definitely would have accepted it, regardless of who it was.","How could they have anticipated such consequences?","Zhou Yueshen, standing nearby, naturally heard it too, and his face darkened.","\"S-Sister-in-law, are you alright?\"","Yu Dong on the other end was a bit worried.","He had also heard that Si Nian was pregnant. Originally, Mother Lin hadn't let him tell Si Nian about this, afraid she would be too stimulated, especially since she was expecting.","But Yu Dong felt that such a major incident couldn't be kept from Si Nian. Otherwise, if something happened to her father, she would regret it for the rest of her life.","So he hurriedly called to explain the situation.","\"How is my dad's condition now?\"","Si Nian took a deep breath and asked.","\"He had emergency surgery last night. It was supposed to be over, but complications arose in the middle of the night. It's gotten worse now, and he's still in a coma. The doctors are preparing for a second surgery, b-but maybe...\"","Yu Dong didn't dare to say it out loud, because the doctor had already issued a critical condition notice.","Without a signature, they didn't dare perform the surgery.","Si Nian tilted her head and buried her face in Zhou Yueshen's embrace, not daring to listen any further.","Initially, she hadn't had much affection for the Lin family, but after spending time together, she had long since treated them as her own biological parents.","Although her parents were honest, simple, and easily deceived, they had never done anything bad. They devoted themselves entirely to their children, and even though she had only just returned to them, they had never mistreated her in the slightest.","They were still so young. After toiling for half their lives, they met with such an accident before they could even enjoy the filial piety of their children and grandchildren.","She found it hard to accept.","Si Nian couldn't help but start crying.","Zhou Yueshen held her in his arms, gently patting her back to comfort her. \"It's alright, Nian Nian. Dad will be fine.\"","Si Nian choked with sobs, unable to speak. As their biological daughter, she was far away in another land at this moment. In such a critical time, she couldn't be by her parents' side.","How could her heart not ache?","Zhou Yueshen also knew the situation was urgent. It wasn't about money anymore; his father-in-law was severely injured and his life was hanging by a thread.","They couldn't just sit and wait for death.","Seeing Si Nian unable to recover, her face covered in tears, his heart ached as if he were suffocating.","\"Let's go back. Let's go back and see them.\"","He suddenly spoke.","Si Nian froze for a moment and lifted her teary eyes. \"Then what about Little Dong and Little Han and the others?\"","She was currently pregnant and had three children to look after; it was practically impossible for her to leave.","Zhou Yueshen definitely wouldn't allow her to go back alone.","Zhou Yueshen said, \"I'll escort you back for a few days and then return. For these few days, we can just find someone to take them to and from school. Little Dong is no longer a child. If he knows about this, he will definitely stay at home nicely and take care of his younger brother and sister.\""]},{"number":452,"title":"Chapter 452: Chapter 449: Coming Home","paragraphs":["Si Nian was still worried, but she had no other choice at the moment. After thinking for a while, she said, \"I'll ask Sister Miao and Chen Haoran if they have time. I don't feel at ease leaving them with anyone else.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded, and Si Nian made the call.","When Sister Miao heard about the situation, she immediately offered to have her son come over and help.","Si Nian knew that Chen Haoran got along well with the children and would definitely take good care of them. This put her mind at ease a little.","With their plan settled, Zhou Yueshen started figuring out their travel arrangements.","Taking the train would take too long, and a bumpy car ride wouldn't be good for Si Nian, so Zhou Yueshen decided to buy plane tickets.","Plane tickets were very expensive in this era, but with their current financial situation, it wasn't something they couldn't afford.","The main advantage was speed; if they could get tickets, they would be home in no time.","However, buying plane tickets wasn't that simple. Once the decision was made, Zhou Yueshen headed out to take care of it.","Si Nian calmed herself down and tried to look on the bright side.","She had altered many of the novel's plotlines, but most of the destined events still occurred. Only the process was changed, leading to different outcomes.","Because of this, although Brother Lin's surgery was successful this time, the price paid was her parents getting beaten up.","In the novel, it seemed like the family overcame every crisis because of Lin Sisi, but in reality, all those problems were brought about by Lin Sisi in the first place.","After actually interacting with Lin Sisi, Si Nian realized that while it was true she created problems, it was equally true that she couldn't solve them.","The novel only positively depicted how she helped her family solve problems, making it seem like all the credit belonged to her, without ever emphasizing where the trouble originated.","That afternoon, Chen Haoran rushed over on his motorcycle.","He wore a thin leather jacket over a white shirt, a chain necklace around his neck, and sunglasses clipped to his head. He looked incredibly fashionable.","As soon as he parked, he strode into the house. \"Sis! Are you home, Sis? I'm here.\"","Si Nian walked out from inside. Seeing that he had arrived so quickly, she was a bit surprised. \"Are you done with classes?\"","Chen Haoran replied, \"I didn't have classes this afternoon, so I went out to hang out. My mom had someone tell me about your family's situation and asked me to help watch the kids for a few days, so I hurried right over. How about it? I'm pretty loyal, right?\"","Si Nian immediately smiled. \"It's a good thing you had the time, otherwise I really wouldn't be able to leave.\"","\"It's nothing. I was actually thinking of hiding out at your place for a few days anyway. My parents have been arguing every day lately, and it's so annoying I don't even want to go back. It's perfect that you guys won't be home. I promise I'll drop off and pick up the kids every single day.\"","Chen Haoran was actually quite happy about it.","He used to hate kids, but the Zhou family's children were obedient and fun to be around. The little sister looked like a little dumpling and was incredibly cute.","His long-held wish of having a younger sister was finally fulfilled.","For the sake of gaining a younger sister, he made a decision: from now on, he would call Si Nian 'Auntie'.","\"Auntie Si, you can go with peace of mind.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Although she couldn't quite keep up with the thought process of the young people of this era, Si Nian didn't have time to dwell on it. She still needed to go over some important instructions with Chen Haoran.","What reassured her was that, aside from the safety of picking them up and dropping them off, the children knew how to cook and do chores, so there wasn't too much to worry about.","Zhou Yueshen would escort her back and return first after a few days; after all, he couldn't be away from his company for too long.","As a daughter, if Si Nian didn't go back during such a crucial time, regardless of what others might say, she wouldn't be able to forgive herself.","Si Nian asked him if he knew how to drive, since picking the kids up every day was quite a hassle. \"If you know how to drive, you can take your Uncle Zhou's car to pick them up and save some time.\"","\"No need, I have my motorcycle. I'll just pick them up on that. Don't worry, Sis. Their elementary school is close to my school, so it's right on my way after class. You can go without worrying.\"","Si Nian nodded. She handed him a red envelope with some money, gave him a set of house keys, and said, \"Sorry for the trouble.\"","Chen Haoran told her not to mention it.","Zhou Yueshen went out to his workplace to get a letter of introduction. Taking a plane these days was very troublesome; whether it was for a business trip or any other reason, a letter of introduction was required.","Flying was considered a rather expensive luxury at the time. One's job position needed to reach a certain level, and a single plane ticket cost as much as many people's monthly salary. It wasn't like the future where everyone could fly and afford a ticket.","Furthermore, the approval process took time.","However, with Chen Nan's help, Zhou Yueshen didn't have to spend too much time on it.","Since not many people flew nowadays, there was no fear of tickets selling out. The main issue was the cumbersome process, which usually required lining up to buy tickets several days in advance.","Having connections through Chen Nan saved them a lot of time.","When the children returned, Si Nian gathered them together to tell them about the situation.","\"Mom is going away for a few days. I'll be back as soon as Grandpa is okay. You need to be good, go to school, do your homework, and wait for Brother Chen Haoran to pick you up after class, understand?\"","Hearing that their grandpa was sick, the children were all very worried.","They weren't little kids anymore, so they naturally understood the severity of the situation.","Although they really wanted to go with their mom, they knew that if Si Nian wasn't taking them back this time, she definitely had her reasons.","Holding back his disappointment and reluctance, the oldest said, \"Mom, don't worry. I'll watch over my younger brother and sister.\"","\"Mom, I'll be good and won't run around either. You have to take good care of yourself and come back soon.\"","Second Child had tears welling up in his eyes. Ever since Si Nian came to their family, apart from spending a few days at their grandma's house, she had always been by their side.","The sudden turn of events caught the children a bit off guard.","Yet they also knew this wasn't the time to be willful, so they held her hands and spoke with reluctance to see her go.","Si Nian patted the children's heads and said, \"Once Grandpa is okay, Mom will come right back. Don't worry.\"","The children nodded their little heads firmly.","After making two trips back and forth, Zhou Yueshen finally managed to buy the plane tickets for nine o'clock.","Early the next morning, Zhou Yueshen packed some of Si Nian's daily necessities, and they were ready to set off.","\"I'm leaving now. Go to school after you finish your breakfast, and if you miss Mom, just give me a call.\"","Even though long-distance calls were expensive, they weren't in a position where they couldn't afford them.","Standing at the door and looking at the three children, Si Nian suddenly realized that they had grown quite a bit. Back when she first arrived at the Zhou household, the three kids were like little beans—so skinny and small."]},{"number":453,"title":"Chapter 453: A Temporary Farewell","paragraphs":["Now they were all quite tall. Little Dong even reached her shoulders; he was a big boy now. A feeling of reluctance began to spread, and she found it hard to move her feet.","Indeed, when it came to affection, her feelings for the Zhou family were much deeper than those for the Lin family.","However, now was not the time to be willful.","Zhou Yueshen noticed her mood. He stepped forward, his long fingers tugging at her coat slightly before smoothing out her hair.","\"Don't worry, I'll have someone deliver food and drinks to them regularly. Once things settle down on your end, I'll go back and pick you up.\"","Si Nian nodded, holding the man's hand, and softly murmured, \"Mhm.\"","She looked at the children and opened her arms to them.","Tears shimmered in the children's eyes.","Second Child was the least able to control his emotions. His mouth turned down, his shoulders hitching as he tried hard to look up at the sky, terrified that he wouldn't be able to stop his tears from falling.","Their mother was going back to her hometown to see their grandpa. Except for the time she took his younger sister to their grandma's house, he had never been separated from her for this long.","Si Nian embraced the children and said, \"Stay safe at home. Don't slack off, and study hard. I'll be checking your homework when I get back.\"","Second Child nodded heavily and choked out, \"I will definitely do my homework well, Mom, and I will miss you.\"","Si Nian patted his back. \"Mom will miss you too.\"","She then looked at Zhou Zedong. He was holding back his emotions, not looking like he was about to cry like Second Child, but his disappointment was still visible.","Si Nian patted his head and said, \"Little Dong, with Mom and Dad not at home, it's up to you to take care of your younger brother and sister. As the older brother, you'll have to work a bit harder. When Mom comes back, I'll bring you a gift.\"","Zhou Zedong shook his head and said, \"Mom, I don't want a gift. This is what I should do. I just want you to come back soon.\"","Si Nian smiled and nodded. She then patted her daughter, who didn't quite understand farewells yet, hugged her, kissed her, and waved goodbye to the children.","Zhou Yueshen led her into the car, and the two headed to the airport together.","Airport procedures were complicated, so they arrived early to wait. Their boarding passes were filled out by hand, but there were people guiding them along the way. The plane was parked far away, requiring them to walk over and line up to board.","The plane had over forty seats, but there were only about ten people in the cabin, making the seating very spacious.","Si Nian had flown many times in the future, but this was her first time in this era.","People who flew nowadays were not ordinary folks. Shortly after boarding, the flight attendants handed out chewing gum, chocolates, and even cigarettes, along with various teas and souvenirs.","Taking this flight, Si Nian's pockets couldn't even hold everything.","At first, Zhou Yueshen was worried that Si Nian might be scared. After all, she was pregnant, and the turbulence during takeoff made many people uncomfortable.","But seeing her calm demeanor, he breathed a sigh of relief.","The plane took off smoothly. Si Nian had woken up early that morning, so she was feeling sleepy again.","Zhou Yueshen kept an eye on her expressions from time to time. Seeing she was tired, he let her lean against him to rest.","Si Nian fell asleep as soon as she closed her eyes. The plane was fast; it felt like she had just closed her eyes when Zhou Yueshen woke her up, saying they had arrived.","In an era where everything moved slowly, Si Nian experienced the fast-paced life of the future for the first time.","She yawned and got off the plane with Zhou Yueshen, taking their luggage.","It was only twelve noon. She had eaten quite a bit before sleeping, so she wasn't hungry yet.","As soon as they stepped off the plane, the refreshing and cool weather typical of the Yunnan-Guizhou-Sichuan region greeted them. Si Nian had worried this morning that it would be chilly here, so she wore a coat, which turned out to be perfect for the moment.","The two left the airport and immediately took a taxi to the city center hospital.","By the time they reached the hospital gates, it was already past two o'clock.","Many people were sitting outside the wards. Due to a lack of seats, everyone was sitting on the floor, and most looked exhausted.","Just as they found the ward, they saw her younger brother, Little Feng, holding a thermos and walking toward the room with a haggard face.","\"Little Feng,\" Si Nian called her brother's name.","Little Feng took a few more steps before reacting. He instinctively looked up, and upon seeing the two, he thought he was seeing things and blinked hard.","When he finally snapped back to reality, his eyes widened in pleasant surprise. \"Sis, Sis, you're back!\"","He ran toward Si Nian. The young boy who had been holding it together for so long seemed to lose all his strength in that moment; he just wanted to throw himself into his sister's arms and cry out all his grievances.","However, just as he got close, he realized his sister was pregnant and he couldn't do that.","He forced himself to stop, looking at Si Nian. Trying desperately to hold back his tears, he still choked up as he said, \"Sis, I missed you so much.\"","Si Nian patted his head. \"I missed you guys too.\"","\"Where is everyone?\"","\"How is Dad?\"","At the mention of this, Little Feng's earlier joy vanished instantly, and his face turned pale. \"Our little brother went to class. Eldest brother was discharged from the hospital but still can't get out of bed, so sister-in-law is taking care of him at home. Mom just went out with Uncle Yu Dong, so I'm here looking after Dad.\"","When speaking of their father, his voice choked up again. \"Sis, Dad will be okay, right? He coughed up blood again today. The doctors said his current condition makes surgery too dangerous right now, and Mom has to sign some kind of paper before they can do it. I don't really understand, but seeing Dad like this makes me so scared.\"","Si Nian's heart tightened. \"Don't be afraid. Take me to see him.\"","Little Feng nodded quickly and said, \"Okay, Dad will definitely be so happy to see you and brother-in-law. Maybe if he's happy, he'll get better.\"","He took Si Nian's hand. Though he was excited, he restrained himself and slowed his pace, leading Si Nian into the ward.","As soon as Si Nian entered the ward, she couldn't help but frown.","There were about six beds in the room. In addition to the beds being full, many people were sitting in the aisles, making it extremely crowded.","Seeing someone come in, a few people shifted over to let them pass.","Then they went back to talking and laughing, with some gossiping loudly. It was unbearably noisy.","In an environment like this, anyone would find it hard to sleep.","\"Dad, Dad, Sis and brother-in-law are back. Look!\" Little Feng excitedly pulled back the last curtain and spoke to the person lying inside.","Hearing this, Lin's father turned his head with difficulty to look their way.","Si Nian looked at her father on the bed. She had only been away for half a year, but he had lost a massive amount of weight. His cheeks were sunken, and there was white hair on his head.","During the New Year not long ago, her family had written letters telling her they were safe and sound, their words full of happiness.","How had so little time passed, yet he had wasted away like this?","Si Nian hurried forward in a few quick steps and grasped her father's hand, which was trembling with excitement.","\"Nian... Nian Nian, how come you're back?\"","Si Nian blinked hard and said in a hoarse voice, \"Dad, I came back to see you. Are you doing okay?\"","\"I'm fine, just a little cough. Your mother didn't believe me and insisted I come to the hospital. Why did you come back? Aren't you attending classes? The children... cough, cough...\"","Lin's father couldn't even finish his sentence before he started coughing violently.","Si Nian quickly said, \"Okay, I understand. Rest first. We can talk slowly when you're feeling better.\"","After she spoke, she urged him to close his eyes and rest. Lin's father listened to his daughter and immediately closed his eyes to rest.","Only then did Si Nian finally have a moment to ask her younger brother for the details of what had happened."]},{"number":454,"title":"Chapter 454: Suspecting Lin Sisi","paragraphs":["Lin Feng said he only found out his parents had been beaten when he got home from school in the afternoon. At that time, his mother had a head injury, and his father kept coughing throughout the night.","Initially, the two of them thought it was just some superficial wounds and didn't think much of it. Who knew that his father would start coughing up blood in the middle of the night? They rushed him to the hospital, and after an examination, they discovered he had internal bleeding.","He underwent surgery that very night. Originally, the surgery went quite smoothly, but an unexpected complication occurred in the middle of the night, and his condition had been worsening over the past two days.","Their older brother had just been discharged from the hospital when their parents met with such an incident. This was a massive blow to the two children.","Mentioning it, his eyes couldn't help but turn red, and his voice choked with emotion.","In the afternoon, Yu Dong and Lin's mother came over.","Upon seeing Si Nian, Lin's mother shed tears of excitement.","She hadn't expected her daughter to return so quickly. For some reason, seeing her daughter gave Lin's mother an inexplicable sense of reassurance, and her taut nerves finally relaxed.","Ever since her daughter returned home, the Lin family's luck had been consistently good, and their days had become increasingly prosperous.","Everyone said her daughter was their family's lucky star, and Lin's mother took great pride in this.","As long as her daughter was around, there was nothing that couldn't be resolved.","Lin's mother's condition wasn't much better than Lin's father's. She was already slender to begin with, but now, having been injured, not only was her face pale, but she had also grown incredibly emaciated.","It was obvious that she had worried her heart out over her husband and son.","There was a wound on her forehead, but it wasn't severe and had already scabbed over.","Mentioning her own injury, Lin's mother couldn't help but shed tears again. \"If your father hadn't been protecting me the whole time, he wouldn't have been hurt so badly.\"","Si Nian hurriedly comforted her, saying that everything would be alright.","Seeing the two of them, Yu Dong also said excitedly, \"Auntie Lin said you were a lucky star, Eldest Sister-in-law. I didn't believe it before, but right after you came back, the doctor I was trying to book an appointment with suddenly became available. I just told Auntie Lin the good news, and we're preparing the transfer paperwork now.\"","Yu Dong was also very happy to see them and smiled.","Hearing this news, Si Nian was also very happy and said gratefully, \"Thank you for the trouble, Yu Dong. None of us were at home. If you hadn't been here to help, I really wouldn't know what to do.\"","Yu Dong smiled and said, \"It's a small matter. In the past, the Boss helped me out a lot too. What is this little thing in comparison?\"","Zhou Yueshen also said, \"Thanks for your hard work.\"","Yu Dong actually felt a bit embarrassed.","They hadn't seen each other for half a year, and the Boss was actually being polite to him.","The group didn't have time to say much more and immediately went to process the hospital transfer.","Upon arriving at the appointed hospital, the hospital immediately arranged an examination for Lin's father's condition.","For some unknown reason, the originally oppressive and gloomy atmosphere instantly stabilized after Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen returned.","The doctor Yu Dong found was a specialist in this field. It was said that he was very famous in hepatobiliary surgery, and patients with liver hemorrhages all came to him for surgery.","Indeed, professionals did things professionally. After the examination, his expression was calm. \"The probability of a successful surgery is still quite high. If it hadn't been delayed, it wouldn't be this serious.\"","After speaking, he asked them to go pay the fees and prepare for the surgery.","Since Si Nian was pregnant, Yu Dong and Zhou Yueshen did all the running around.","With her daughter and son-in-law present, Lin's mother also relaxed completely.","In the evening, after the papers were signed, the surgery began.","Zhou Yueshen brought hot water from somewhere and poured a cup for Si Nian.","\"Are you tired?\" he asked, considering that Si Nian's stamina wasn't good right now, and she had been rushing about all day. She must be exhausted.","Si Nian nodded. She was tired, but it wasn't unbearable. She leaned on her man's shoulder while asking her mother about the whole story behind the incident.","Lin's mother was anxious at heart, and only when she heard her daughter did her attention shift. She said guiltily, \"It's all my fault. Your brother's accident happened so suddenly, and the doctor said he needed immediate surgery. We didn't have that much cash on hand at the time. Lin Sisi somehow got the news from somewhere and brought over two thousand yuan to help. Later, when Yu Dong came over to deliver money, I wanted to return it to her right away, but I couldn't find her. I had no choice but to find someone to send the money back to her. I thought everything would be fine once the money was returned, but I didn't expect the Si family to misunderstand, thinking we had manipulated Lin Sisi into taking their money for us, and then things turned out like this.\"","Lin's mother felt guilty bringing this up. At the time, her son's situation was critical. Although she knew she shouldn't have accepted the money, she had no other choice. Her daughter was out of town, and it would take time to wire money back. So she thought she would take it first for her son's emergency, and once her daughter's money arrived, it would be fine to return it.","Who knew she had thought too simply of the matter.","Hearing this, Si Nian's expression became a bit strange.","The last time she inexplicably ran off to Beijing to solve a case, Si Nian had already been somewhat suspicious.","This time, with her brother's accident, could Lin Sisi have predicted it in advance and prepared the money to come back?","This was just too much of a coincidence.","Recalling what had happened previously, Si Nian suddenly felt her scalp tingle.","It seemed as though every time a plot point occurred, Lin Sisi could predict it in advance.","But because she never managed to resolve things smoothly in the end, Si Nian hadn't thought much of it, assuming it was just following the original plot.","But at this moment, an unbelievable thought struck her.","Could it be that Lin Sisi, just like her, also knew what was going to happen in the future?","After all, if something like her transmigrating into a book could happen, why not something similar for Lin Sisi?","Speaking of which, the novel described Lin Sisi's journey to acknowledge her true family as very smooth, with the real daughter turning into a vicious supporting female character who served as her foil.","However, it never explained how Lin Sisi found out she was the biological child of the Si family. How did someone who had lived in the countryside for a long time know about something that neither family had discovered for over a decade?","The more she thought about it, the stranger it seemed.","Si Nian asked, \"Mom, how long after my brother's accident did Lin Sisi show up?\"","Lin's mother replied, \"It was the exact day of your brother's accident. We received the notice and rushed over, and she arrived right on our heels. When we heard the surgery would cost a lot of money, your father and I didn't know what to do, and she just took out the money to help us.\"","Lin's mother had been too panicked at the time, so she hadn't thought much about it.","Now that her daughter was asking about it, she suddenly felt that something wasn't quite right either.","After all, when their son had his accident, they hadn't told any outsiders. How could Lin Sisi have known so quickly, rushed over so coincidentally, and happened to have that much cash in hand?","The more Lin's mother thought about it, the uglier her expression became.","Although she didn't want to believe it, this matter was just too coincidental.","Seeing the gleam of suspicion surface in her eyes, Si Nian thought to herself that her guess was indeed correct.","No matter what, Lin Sisi definitely knew about her brother getting injured.","Although she didn't know if it was due to a female protagonist's halo or because she, like herself, knew the plot in advance.","But Si Nian felt that this matter was very likely inseparable from Lin Sisi.","\"When the Si family came knocking on our door, Lin Sisi didn't show up either, right?\"","Lin's mother nodded.","Si Nian asked again, \"You also found someone to send the money back, so you're sure it ended up in the Si family's hands, right?\"","Lin's mother said, \"Yes, it was exactly because we returned the money that they found out Lin Sisi gave us money to help out. They inexplicably claimed that we manipulated Lin Sisi into taking money from her home to empty out their Si family, and things like that.\"","Speaking of this, Lin's mother also found it strange. This time, Lin Sisi had brought the money over herself. They had never sought Lin Sisi out before, nor had they asked her for a single cent, so how were they suddenly accused of trying to bleed the Si family dry?","It was absolutely baffling.","They hadn't taken a single penny, yet they had suffered an inexplicable beating. Lin's mother felt they were simply too unlucky.","Whenever the Lin family got involved with Lin Sisi, nothing good ever came of it."]},{"number":455,"title":"Chapter 455: Encounter Again","paragraphs":["Si Nian nodded. Judging from how Lin Sisi had secretly taken the three thousand yuan and severely harmed the Lin family, she did not seem like someone who had any affection for the Lin family.","Let alone taking out so much money for his surgery.","However, she could not be entirely certain about such an unbelievable thing.","Si Nian said, \"We cannot just let this matter go. If we had asked Lin Sisi for the money, it would indeed be our problem. But it was Lin Sisi who brought the money to us, and you returned it to her immediately. There is no such thing as our Lin family inducing her to take the money. We must call the police. We cannot let you get beaten up for nothing.\"","Si's Father must have been provoked somehow to actually hire people to attack her parents. Although he was selfish, he would absolutely not do something like this unless pushed to the extreme.","Who knew what Lin Sisi had actually done to make the Si family do such a thing to the Lin family.","Si Nian's eyes were cold. \"As long as we call the police, even if Lin Sisi does not want to come forward to explain, she will have to stand up.\"","Lin's mother nodded, also feeling that she had done nothing wrong.","In the past, she would have preferred to turn big problems into small ones and small ones into nothing.","But this time, the Si family had truly gone too far!","The successive blows left Lin's mother with no time to care about the feelings of outsiders.","She did not want to cause a scene with others, but that did not mean their Lin family was easy to bully.","Thinking about it, she also felt that she really lacked assertiveness. If her daughter had not returned, she would still be panicking and at a loss right now.","Let alone calling the police.","\"Yes, call the police. We must call the police for this matter. The Si family is really too much!\"","Yu Dong, who was listening on the side, seemed to just realize it when Si Nian mentioned this matter, and immediately echoed her sentiments.","When this incident first happened, they were all so busy and overwhelmed that they never even thought about calling the police.","They just thought about waiting for Lin's father to recover before making any plans.","But if they waited until Lin's father was completely healed, calling the police would be completely useless.","Yu Dong immediately said he would go call the police.","The surgery took two hours and finally ended.","Lin's father was wheeled out. The doctor said the surgery was very successful and told them not to worry. The next step was hospitalization for recovery and observation. Tonight was relatively important; if everything was fine tonight, then he would be okay.","Everyone accompanied Lin's father in his ward. Zhou Yueshen, afraid that Si Nian would be sleepy, even paid for an extra bed for her to rest on the side.","The treatment at this hospital was quite expensive, so it was not like the city hospital where there was not even a place to sit.","Lin's father woke up after a short while. He was in a very good mood. When the doctor came to check on him, he said with a cheerful laugh, \"My daughter flew all the way from Beijing just to see me.\"","\"I don't feel any pain at all. I feel like I'm already cured and can be discharged right now.\"","This made everyone laugh heartily.","...","Lin Sisi had been very unlucky these past few days. That day, after she went to the hospital to deliver money for Lin Xiao's surgery, she actually saw an acquaintance.","Liu Dongdong.","She was holding a child.","Lin Sisi was stunned. She had never heard anything about Liu Dongdong getting married.","Previously, after suspecting that Liu Dongdong wanted to seduce Fu Yang, she had sent her away.","She thought that as long as Liu Dongdong could not come into contact with Fu Yang, nothing would happen.","So she stopped paying attention to this person.","Later, when the people in the family compound saw that Liu Dongdong was gone, they even asked her about it.","They told her a lot about how Liu Dongdong would run to the Fu family's house all day long while she was in prison.","She heard that when others brought food to Fu Yang, he never accepted it.","But he accepted everything Liu Dongdong brought.","Everyone originally thought that Fu Yang accepted it out of respect for the Si family.","But as such incidents became more frequent, some people began to grow suspicious.","After all, it was not proper for a young, unmarried girl like Liu Dongdong to run to a man's house all day.","Since Lin Sisi was not around at the time, many people did not say anything to her face, but privately they were all waiting to watch a good show.","As a result, not long after, Liu Dongdong left.","Only then did everyone bring this matter up to let Lin Sisi know.","Lin Sisi never expected that she had almost invited a wolf into her house.","She originally thought she had stopped it in time.","But unexpectedly, a year later, she actually saw Liu Dongdong in the hospital.","And she was even holding a child.","She did not know why at the time, but she felt a sudden wave of panic.","She immediately rushed to Xingfu Village to inquire about Liu Dongdong's situation.","However, this trip scared her half to death.","Not only was Liu Dongdong not married, but she had also never returned to Xingfu Village!","Then whose child was she holding?","Lin Sisi was extremely panicked. She did not even have time to go to school these past few days, spending all day tracking Liu Dongdong.","She was terrified that she would run away.","She did find the place where Liu Dongdong lived, but she heard no mention of her being married; she was raising the child alone.","Although Lin Sisi was not certain, she felt that Liu Dongdong was planning something.","However, before she could investigate further, the police found her and said that Lin Xiao's car accident was suspected to be intentional injury. The Lin family had called the police, and she was asked to cooperate with the investigation.","Lin Sisi was instantly dumbfounded.","Only then did she learn that her parents had actually hired people to beat up Lin's father and Lin's mother.","It turned out that when the Lin family tried to return the money to her, they could not find her, so they sent the money to the family compound.","Her parents thought the Lin family had gone behind their backs to induce her to take money to support the Lin family. Coupled with the previous incident where she lost three thousand yuan, her parents both believed she was instructed by the Lin family—that she had clearly taken the money to their home but lied and deceived them, saying it was stolen.","That was why so many things had happened.","The person investigating this case this time was still Captain Li.","Seeing Lin Sisi, he did not even bat an eyelid. \"I heard that right after Lin Xiao got into a car accident, you immediately went to the hospital with money for them. I would like to ask, Comrade Lin Sisi, where did you learn that he would get into a car accident?\"","Originally, when Lin Xiao got into the accident, the other party had already fled. The scene was chaotic at the time, and no one noticed the license plate number.","Even if they investigated, they would not be able to find anything.","At this moment, the hit-and-run driver still had not been found.","Everyone thought the Lin family would just have to accept their bad luck regarding this matter. Who knew that as soon as Si Nian returned and heard about it, she immediately began to suspect Lin Sisi.","When Captain Li heard it was Lin Sisi again, he immediately took over the case.","For no other reason.","Just because whenever there was a case involving Lin Sisi, the main culprit was bound to be her.","Lin Sisi: \"...\"","\"Captain Lin, you aren't suspecting me, are you?\"","Captain Li did not speak, but his eyes said it all.","Lin Sisi bit her lip and said, \"I just happened to pass by the hospital and ran into my adoptive parents, which is how I found out about this.\"","\"At the time, I was actually going to the hospital to visit a friend, but I didn't expect such a coincidence.\"","Captain Li withdrew his gaze, maintaining a businesslike attitude: \"A friend? What kind of friend requires you to bring two thousand yuan to visit?\""]},{"number":456,"title":"Chapter 456: Lin Sisi's Anger","paragraphs":["Lin Sisi's expression was very calm. After all, she had been in prison and had dealt with the police many times.","\"This is my private business, and I refuse to answer,\" Lin Sisi said. \"Since this involves my friend's privacy, I cannot tell you what happened to her, because it has nothing to do with my brother's car accident. If it hadn't been an emergency at the time, I wouldn't have just casually given the money to my adoptive mother. I just didn't expect that my good intentions would be maliciously speculated upon like this. Truly, no good deed goes unpunished.\"","Lin Sisi wore a bitterly disappointed expression. \"If you suspect me, please show the evidence, and I will naturally cooperate with the investigation. But if you wrong me and frame me without evidence, I, Lin Sisi, will not just let you bully me like this.\"","Captain Li fell silent for a moment. \"You are right. There is currently no evidence to charge you.\"","Lin Sisi breathed a sigh of relief, smiled, and stood up. \"In that case, I will take my leave.\"","\"I didn't say you could leave.\" Captain Li looked up and glanced at her. Seeing the displeasure on Lin Sisi's face, he looked at the chair, signaling for her to sit back down. \"Regarding the car accident, we indeed haven't found the hit-and-run driver, so we cannot determine whether it was an accident or intentional...\"","He said coldly, \"But there is one thing we can be sure of, and it is because of you.\"","\"What? I haven't been in contact with anyone recently. What did I do wrong now?\" Lin Sisi felt somewhat irritated.","Captain Li replied, \"Of course you did something wrong. Without your family's consent, you took a large sum of money to treat a friend, which by a twist of fate ended up with the Lin family. The Si family believed that the Lin family made you secretly take money from the Si family to support them, so they attacked the Lin couple, resulting in one minor external injury and one severe internal injury. It took two consecutive surgeries to save their lives, causing massive losses...\"","At this point, seeing Lin Sisi's ugly expression, he added, \"However, you disappeared during this time. Not only did you fail to explain the reason to the Si family, but you also let the Lin couple get beaten and only showed up now. If this matter isn't because of you, then tell me, who is it because of?\"","Lin Sisi looked awful. She hadn't expected the Lin family to return the money in the blink of an eye either!","Originally, she had secretly taken out these two thousand yuan, thinking that by helping save Lin Xiao, the Lin family would be grateful to her.","Perhaps they would even choose to forgive her for their previous frictions because of this.","She knew the Lin family's personalities very well.","She also knew that the Lin family would definitely ask Si Nian for help.","Si Nian was rich, but she was far away in another town. Even if she could wire the money back, it would certainly take a few days.","By then, the Lin family would return this sum of money to her.","That way, she could secretly put the money back. The Si family wouldn't find out, and the Lin family would be deeply grateful to her—the best of both worlds.","But because of Liu Dongdong's appearance, she had neglected this matter, and her plans couldn't keep up with the changes.","Not only did things not develop according to her ideas, but it also caused the two families to become enemies, resulting in such severe consequences.","But no matter what, Lin Sisi never expected that the Lin family would actually call the police.","She had originally thought she was only brought in to cooperate with the investigation because of the incident with Lin Xiao.","She hadn't expected it to actually be about the money.","Yes, she hadn't discussed the money with her family in advance, but didn't they realize that the Si family never wanted her to interact with their poor relatives in the first place, let alone take out so much money to help them?","If it weren't for her, how could their son have been able to undergo surgery? He might have even been kicked out by the hospital.","Now that their son was better and discharged, they actually called the police to sue her.","Sure enough, she had thought too highly of them!","Lin Sisi felt furious. At this moment, she had only learned from Captain Li that the Lin couple had been beaten, but she believed that it was probably just her father misunderstanding things and feeling unhappy, which led him to find someone to casually teach them a lesson.","It definitely wasn't as exaggerated as Captain Li made it out to be, otherwise, how would they still be in the mood to call the police?","The more Lin Sisi thought about it, the more she felt that the Lin family were truly ungrateful wretches.","She said agitatedly, \"Fine, it's all my fault then! If they were so capable, they shouldn't have accepted the money when their son had the car accident. Accepting the money on one hand and blaming me on the other—whatever I do is wrong. If I had known this would happen, I wouldn't have given the money. It serves them right if their son is crippled for life!\"","Lin Sisi said angrily.","Actually, ever since her time in prison, some plots completely different from her past life would inexplicably pop into her mind.","The Lin family was no longer that ordinary Lin family; they would become very wealthy in the future. Although her brother was disabled, he would be highly valued by a big boss and have a boundless future.","Her two younger brothers would also be quite successful and would follow her every lead.","Lin Sisi was, after all, someone who had been reborn. When such strange memories appeared, not only did she not feel afraid, but she was even a little excited.","She thought it was the butterfly effect triggered by her rebirth.","But these things had clearly actually happened, yet after she was reborn and came back, it was as if all the outcomes and directions had changed.","And in this life, she wasn't living much more comfortably than in her past life either.","In her past life, she had married Zhou Yueshen. She lacked neither food nor money, and she didn't have to manage the three children much. At first, everyone envied her. But as time went on, Lin Sisi grew tired of that kind of life, finding it very meaningless. She didn't want to live her whole life in that remote countryside, acting as a stepmother to a group of dirty, gloomy children.","Therefore, in this life, she schemed desperately, wanting to run to the city and live the glamorous, wealthy life that Si Nian had in her past life.","She had obviously worked so hard, and she couldn't understand why her life had still turned out like this.","Si's Father and Si's Mother no longer felt guilty toward her, Fu Yang didn't have her in his eyes, and the Lin family avoided her like the plague. Although she had gotten into a university, no one thought she was that amazing. Everyone was praising Si Nian's achievements. She was like an ugly duckling; no matter where she went, she was always an ugly duckling and would never shine brightly like a white swan.","Captain Li continued to ask calmly, \"Then why didn't you honestly tell your family the reason you took the money?\"","Lin Sisi: \"I...\"","\"Regardless, this matter started because of you. The Lin family has already filed a lawsuit against your parents for intentional assault. Since you are unwilling to speak, we can only resolve this through legal procedures.\"","Lin Sisi looked awful. \"What will happen if we go through legal procedures?\"","\"Your parents' crime of intentional assault caused severe injuries to the victims. Under normal circumstances, they would be sentenced to a fixed term of imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years. I remember your father still holds an official position. I don't know if he truly believes that because he is in a high position, no one would dare to sue him, or if there is another reason he did such a thing. But as long as the Lin family does not agree to settle, we will continue investigating.\"","After speaking, Captain Li no longer looked at her ugly expression. At the end of the day, even if they couldn't find out who the instigator of Lin Xiao's car accident was, the Si family was finished.","Lin Sisi was a bit panicked at first, but upon hearing Captain Li mention her father's status, she breathed a sigh of relief again.","Since her father dared to do such a thing, he definitely had a backup plan. After all, he wasn't the one who actually got his hands dirty. As long as he denied everything, the police couldn't touch him.","Furthermore, the Lin family had no power or influence in this area, so how could they possibly compete with the Si family?","The only person who could help, Zhou Yueshen, was far away in another city. No matter how formidable he was, his reach simply didn't extend this far.","At this thought, Lin Sisi's fears completely vanished."]},{"number":457,"title":"Chapter 457: Captain Li's Phone Call","paragraphs":["Thinking of this, Lin Sisi suddenly was not afraid anymore.","She swaggered out of the police station.","She believed the police had no evidence and were just questioning her.","Seeing her leave, Captain Li instructed his subordinates, Follow her for the next few days and find out who she frequently contacts.","Why? someone nearby asked. She was not the one who beat him up. Should we not be tracking her parents?","Captain Li rolled his eyes at him. Who asked you to look for the attackers? She was lying from the start. These days, an illness that costs two thousand yuan to treat is no minor ailment. Yet she turned around and gave all the money to the Lin family without leaving a single cent for that friend of hers. This excuse is far too far-fetched.","Based on his previous understanding of Lin Sisi, she would probably go look for this so-called friend to help prove her innocence.","As long as they followed Lin Sisi, found the friend she mentioned, and checked if that person was actually sick, they would have the evidence that Lin Sisi was lying.","And if she was lying, why did she lie? Was it to prove she was innocent? Or was it for something else?","Regardless, if someone said this matter had nothing to do with Lin Sisi, Captain Li would not believe it even if he were beaten to death.","Originally, the Si family must have also thought the Lin family would not dare report to the police and sue them.","That was why they dared to be so brazen. Now that a lawyer's letter had been sent, the Si family would definitely make a move.","Their first action would undoubtedly be to get rid of the people who carried out the assault.","As long as those people disappeared, even if it was known that they did the beating, the police would not be able to find any evidence.","Lin's father had a successful surgery. Si Nian could not sleep comfortably at the hospital, so the next day she was sent home by her mother to rest.","Returning home again and looking at the familiar, spacious street scenes and the tube-shaped apartment buildings, Si Nian felt a bit dazed. In truth, she had only been away in Beijing for a little over half a year.","Compared to the crowded hutongs, everywhere here was spacious, and the air felt much more pleasant.","Opening the door, the flowers, plants, and trees planted in the courtyard had grown quite a bit. There were also some cacti and succulents, all brought from their rural hometown by her two younger brothers. In their hometown, everyone would go up the mountain to dig them up for planting themselves, and there were plenty of cacti.","A square plot of land had been cleared in the courtyard, fully planted with green vegetables.","In the styrofoam boxes next to the wall, rows of green onions and cilantro were growing lush and green.","In the corner was the rose bush that Zhou Yueshen had previously broken. It had grown taller now, with thick, sturdy stems. It would probably bloom this year.","In the small fish pond to the side were the fry raised by Second Child. They had grown quite large by now, swimming lazily in the pool. They had fattened up by at least two sizes; who knew what they had been eating.","One had to admit, when it came to planting these flowers and trees, adults were much better at it.","The courtyard was kept very neat and clean. When Si Nian went to the Lin family before, she noticed that her parents' home was always swept spotless. If she had not transmigrated into this book, she would have thought her slight germaphobia was hereditary.","Zhou Yueshen, our courtyard is so beautiful, Si Nian tilted her head and spoke to him, feeling very happy. Little Han and the others will definitely be thrilled when they see it.","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod. A courtyard so full of life like this, not to mention the children, even he felt a sense of joy looking at it.","Inside the house, hearing the commotion, Lin Xiao and Zhou Suisui came out, pushing a wheelchair.","Seeing the two of them return, their faces filled with pleasant surprise. Niannian, brother-in-law, you are back!","Quick, come inside and have a seat.","The two of them had already known the good news when Lin's mother came back to report it the night before.","If it were not for the mobility issues and the need to keep watch at home, the couple would have loved nothing more than to rush straight to the hospital.","Seeing them actually back now, the reality of witnessing it with their own eyes still made them extremely excited.","Hurry in and sit. Little sister, your belly has gotten so big! Zhou Suisui hurriedly stepped forward to support Si Nian.","Si Nian quickly said, Sister-in-law, you do not need to be so polite. I am still very agile right now.","A hint of envy flickered in Zhou Suisui's eyes. What was an accident for Si Nian and her husband was something she desperately longed for.","Although her health was much better now than before, there was still no activity in her belly.","Seeing that Si Nian, who got married after her, already had such a big belly, she could not help but feel envious.","The group went into the house chatting and laughing. Because only Lin's mother was keeping watch at the hospital, Zhou Yueshen, after bringing Si Nian back, still had to head over to help.","After saying his goodbyes, he drove off.","Their car had been parked at the door the whole time and had not been driven much.","But perhaps because the Lin family frequently helped maintain it, it surprisingly had not accumulated any dust.","Si Nian entered their room. The Lin family had kept their room locked and had not let anyone in.","Pushing the door open, there was a faint smell of dust in the room. It was not severe, but Si Nian still dug out clean bedsheets.","Zhou Suisui came over to help her and took all the quilts and bedding upstairs to air them out in the sun to remove the smell.","To prevent them from being uncomfortable when sleeping at night.","Si Nian felt sleepy after tidying up and went to the room to catch up on some sleep.","When she woke up, her sister-in-law had slaughtered a chicken.","Her father's successful surgery, along with Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen's return, were both wonderful and joyous events for the Lin family.","Since Si Nian was pregnant, Zhou Suisui did not let her help.","A large pot of chicken soup was stewed. Si Nian drank some but felt a bit greasy, so she did not eat much.","Perhaps she was too tired from the day before, she felt sleepy again right after eating.","She slept straight through to the next morning. Si Nian even admired her own sleep quality.","Zhou Yueshen did not come back until the next day. Although her father had passed the critical period, he could not move yet and needed close, personal care.","Lin Xiao had mobility issues, Lin's mother did not have much strength, and the two children could not help much either.","As a result, all the tasks fell onto Zhou Yueshen.","Seeing him return from outside early in the morning, Si Nian's heart ached for him. You have worked so hard. You barely slept the night before last.","Because the hospital bed was not big, Zhou Yueshen was afraid of crowding her, so he had not slept much.","He did not come home all night yesterday either; it was truly exhausting.","Yet he never complained about anything.","Upon returning home, Si Nian went into the kitchen to heat up food for him.","Zhou Yueshen came in to help. He had a big appetite, and he polished off the entire pot Si Nian had cooked.","After eating, Si Nian glanced at her brother and sister-in-law talking on the sofa and waved at Zhou Yueshen. When he lowered his head slightly and leaned in, she stood on her tiptoes and whispered in his ear, I have not taken a bath in three days. I am scared to do it alone, help me.","Her belly was big, and Zhou Yueshen would not let her go into the bathroom alone, afraid she might slip and fall.","So he had always been helping her before.","With Zhou Yueshen away, Si Nian did not dare to do it.","Zhou Yueshen's Adam's apple bobbed as he lowered his voice, I will go draw the water for you.","Si Nian put her hands on her hips and said, Then after you draw the water, you have to wait outside. You cannot stare at me while I wash.","Can I not? Zhou Yueshen's lips curled up slightly, a smile lingering in his eyes.","Si Nian glared at him. I will call you when I am done washing.","After saying that, she was about to go upstairs.","In Beijing, their place only had one floor, so they did not have to climb stairs.","Seeing her step onto the stairs, Zhou Yueshen compromised and followed her up, holding her hand.","After escorting her upstairs, Zhou Yueshen went to the washroom to draw hot water. The bathing barrel was still there, but since the family usually went out to the public bathhouse, no one had used it.","He scrubbed it clean inside and out, filled it with hot water, and only then called Si Nian in.","In the end, halfway through her bath, Si Nian still ended up calling for him. With her long hair, it was too difficult to wash on her own, and since she couldn't bend over, she had no choice but to ask Zhou Yueshen for help.","Zhou Yueshen knew this would happen. Even though Si Nian refused to let him in every single time, she would always regret it later and give up her resistance.","After a nice, comfortable bath, Si Nian changed into her pajamas and lay back down.","Just as she was drifting off to sleep, a call came in from Captain Li."]},{"number":458,"title":"Chapter 458: Liu Dongdong's Conspiracy","paragraphs":["Captain Li informed them that the people who committed the assault had been found.","The Si family had also sent someone over, asking them to come by to discuss how the two families should resolve the matter.","Logically, Lin's father and Lin's mother should have been notified, but given their current condition, they were in no shape to handle it. Therefore, the responsibility fell on their son-in-law, Zhou Yueshen, to sort it out.","Their plainclothes officers had staked out the entrance of the family compound for a whole day and night before spotting Zhang Cuimei sneaking off to a secluded area while out grocery shopping, where she was seen talking to a group of people.","The funny thing was, Zhang Cuimei had tried to send the group away, but these local thugs were not so easily dismissed. They took the opportunity to extort her right then and there. Unable to tolerate such behavior, Zhang Cuimei immediately pointed her finger at their noses and began cursing them out.","Well, that did it. These men were not about to put up with that, so they promptly slapped Zhang Cuimei to the ground and even attempted to assault her.","Only then did Zhang Cuimei panic. She screamed like a slaughtered pig, alerting the trailing plainclothes officers, which was the only reason she managed to escape unscathed.","Now, the whole group had been taken to the police station for immediate questioning.","These thugs had loose lips and instantly confessed that Zhang Cuimei had paid them to beat the victims up, telling them that as long as they didn't kill anyone, anything goes.","That was why the Lin parents had ended up so severely injured.","Upon hearing this, Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen immediately drove to the police station to handle the situation.","Meanwhile, Lin Sisi blocked Liu Dongdong, who was just about to head out.","Seeing her, Liu Dongdong's expression didn't change in the slightest.","She had heard from others that Lin Sisi had been asking around about her over the past few days.","Now, facing Lin Sisi, her eyes flickered briefly, but she remained poised, showing little emotional shift.","Seeing that look in her eyes, Lin Sisi instantly felt provoked.","In the past, she had treated Liu Dongdong as a friend and never overthought things, simply assuming the woman was honest, simple-minded, and easy to manipulate.","But now she realized she had been far too naive.","Liu Dongdong not only had a child but was also still staying in the city. Lin Sisi didn't dare to think too deeply about what she was really plotting.","However, if this child had anything to do with Fu Yang, then she was truly doomed.","The Fu family had already been clamoring for a divorce. If Fu Yang hadn't suddenly been transferred away, she and Fu Yang probably would have divorced long ago and severed all ties.","Perhaps because Lin Sisi had experienced the future, she didn't want to have children so soon. Having a child would make it very troublesome for her to attend college and pursue other goals later on.","She wanted to be like Si Nian, waiting until she was successful in her career before considering a baby.","She had thought her incredibly independent and progressive mindset was the right way to go.","But now, she regretted it bitterly.","Back when Fu Yang was still in the family compound, she had plenty of opportunities to seek him out; the worst she would have had to do was be thick-skinned about it.","But to avoid coming off like the clingy Si Nian from the novel and risking his disgust, she had even asked Liu Dongdong to deliver food to him on her behalf.","As a result, she ended up having fewer opportunities to see Fu Yang than Liu Dongdong did.","It was exactly this that had given the other woman the chance to steal him away.","The more Lin Sisi thought about it, the angrier she became. She said coldly, \"Liu Dongdong, you deceived me so ruthlessly!\"","Liu Dongdong lowered her eyes and replied, \"Sisi, I don't understand what you're talking about.\"","Lin Sisi gritted her teeth. \"Whose child is this? Tell me the truth!\"","When she had managed to send Liu Dongdong away so easily back then, she thought it was because Liu Dongdong was scared.","Only now did she realize that it had all been calculated by Liu Dongdong.","If she had gotten pregnant right under her nose, Lin Sisi would have noticed long ago, and this child would never have been born.","She wasn't an idiot. The Fu family already disliked her and couldn't wait for a divorce. If a child were to appear now, even an illegitimate one, the Fu family would definitely take the child back.","And her, the lawful wife, would suffer the miserable fate of being kicked out. It wasn't impossible for Liu Dongdong to take her place.","The more she thought about it, the more furious she became. At this moment, Lin Sisi truly wished she could strangle her to death.","If she had known this would happen, she never would have helped Liu Dongdong leave the textile factory in the first place.","She had gone through so much trouble to return to the Si family and live such a good life. It was one thing to deal with Si Nian, but what right did Liu Dongdong have to fight her for it?","Liu Dongdong stayed silent for a moment before saying, \"It was an accident. I never wanted to ruin your marriage with Mr. Fu, otherwise I wouldn't have left back then.\"","After she finished, she added softly, \"Sisi, I have always seen you as my best friend and the person I am most grateful to, so I didn't want to hurt you.\"","\"This whole thing truly was an accident, but the child is innocent. How could I bring myself to harm him? I don't ask for your forgiveness; I only hope you can give me and my child a way to survive.\"","Lin Sisi's eyes turned red with fury. Although she had already guessed the gist of it, hearing her admit it in person made the anger in her heart impossible to contain.","At this moment, Lin Sisi didn't know what to do. She could scheme against Si Nian to take back everything that was hers.","But when it came to dealing with a third party who had ruined her marriage, she was completely at a loss.","Her only thought was that she couldn't let Liu Dongdong and this child stay here.","If only they could disappear forever...","The instant this thought popped into her head, Lin Sisi scared herself.","She hurriedly shook her head. When she had first been reborn, she had relied on the era's weak legal system to take that three thousand yuan without hesitation.","She thought she would never be discovered.","But in the end, it caused her to lose all face and even land in jail.","To this day, that incident kept her from holding her head up high in the family compound.","And even if she had such a thought, she wouldn't dare act on it.","In this moment, Lin Sisi understood that in this life, she could never be a resolute, independent, and strong career woman.","How could she possibly achieve in a second life what she had failed to do in her past life?","She had thought that being reborn made her invincible, that she could change so many things.","Only to find out that she had played a good hand of cards terribly.","Lin Sisi snapped back to reality, her entire back drenched in sweat. With a deathly pale face, she asked, \"What will it take for you to leave here and never show up again?\"","Liu Dongdong curled her lips into a slight smile and said, \"If you can guarantee the living expenses for my child and me, I can go anywhere. As you know, I can't work while taking care of a child. If I weren't truly out of options, I wouldn't have stayed here.\"","\"The Fu family definitely looks down on me. If they find out, at most they'll just take the child away, and when that happens, neither you nor I will have a good ending...\"","Lin Sisi took a deep breath, understanding perfectly.","She said in a deep voice, \"Fine, I agree. But in return, I need you to do one last thing for me.\"","Liu Dongdong smiled and agreed.","...","Lin Sisi returned home with a heavy heart. She had no idea where she was going to get the money for Liu Dongdong.","Previously, she had taken three thousand of her mother's secret savings, and later she secretly took two thousand from her father, which ultimately led to the Lin parents being beaten. Originally, by lending the money, she planned for the Lin family to be immensely grateful to her.","Now look what happened. Not only had she failed to salvage the relationship, but she had also completely turned the Lin family into her enemies.","The events of the past two years had caused her parents to completely lose any sense of guilt toward her.","At least her mother would still feel a little heartache for her.","But her father barely wanted anything to do with her anymore.","If she took money again and got caught, she would definitely be punished.","Yet, if she didn't get the money, Liu Dongdong wouldn't leave. And if Liu Dongdong showed up before the Fu family with the child, she would lose absolutely any chance of winning.","Though she didn't know whether she should trust Liu Dongdong, she had no other options left.","Lin Sisi's eyes hardened with resolve. As long as she hadn't divorced Fu Yang, her father wouldn't dare do anything to her.","She hurried home, only to discover that both her parents had been taken away by the police."]},{"number":459,"title":"Chapter 459: Lin Sisi Reunited","paragraphs":["She heard that many police officers had come and caused quite a scene. The people in the family compound were still talking about it.","Someone saw her return and shouted, \"Sisi, you're finally back! Hurry up and go to the police station. I heard your mom was beaten up, and your dad was arrested on suspicion of intentional assault.\"","Everyone was engaged in heated discussions.","They sounded worried, but their eyes were filled with the excitement of watching a good show.","Lin Sisi's mind buzzed.","It had only been a day; how could they have been arrested?","Did her parents fail to pay off those people?","Lin Sisi couldn't afford to overthink it and hurried toward the hospital.","However, right now she couldn't even afford taxi fare, so she could only brave the blazing sun and hurry toward the police station.","Fortunately, the police station wasn't too far away. Lin Sisi ran to the entrance of the station, her face covered in sweat.","Although she felt incredibly frustrated, she knew that as long as she got the money to send Liu Dongdong away, settled down, finished her studies, and waited for Fu Yang to return so she could give birth to their child, even if Liu Dongdong reappeared later, he wouldn't be able to threaten her position.","Even though she had been tortured miserably during this time, she was still better off than Si Nian. Zhou Yueshen didn't want children, which meant Si Nian would only ever be a stepmother for the rest of her life.","Right now, those kids were small and might still acknowledge her, but once they grew up and got married, who would provide for her? Her existence was no different from that of a nanny.","But she still had a chance. This minor setback wouldn't defeat her, Lin Sisi!","Lin Sisi encouraged herself. Just as she straightened her back, a black Santana drove past her.","She unconsciously stole a glance. The first time she rode in such a nice car was when she and Fu Yang went to Xingfu Village to find Si Nian and the others to take wedding photos.","That car belonged to Father Fu. Seeing that they were going to take wedding photos that day, he had specifically lent it to him so he could drive her there.","At that time, sitting in the car and passing through the streets, Lin Sisi could feel the envious gazes of the people around them. She felt like she was the moon surrounded by stars, a high and mighty young lady.","That was the kind of life she was meant to live.","But she had only ridden in it that one time, and she had never sat in such a luxury car again.","As Lin Sisi was looking on with envy, she saw the car stop at the entrance of the police station not far ahead of her.","She stopped in her tracks and watched curiously. What kind of wealthy person needed to come to the police station in person?","In this era, most people who could afford to drive this kind of car were big bosses.","Just as she was thinking this, a familiar tall figure stepped out of the car.","Lin Sisi looked closely, and her eyes widened.","Zhou... Zhou Yueshen?","How could it be? Didn't he go to Jing City with Si Nian?","After not seeing him for more than half a year, Zhou Yueshen had changed a bit. His facial features were deeper, but his overall aura had softened significantly. He no longer looked like the rough man who could scare children to tears just by walking through the village.","His temperament had become more restrained and settled.","Yet, he was also more handsome.","In the past, Lin Sisi didn't like rough men like Zhou Yueshen.","He was tall and sturdy, feeling like a bear.","He wore a torn tank top all year round, his skin was tanned dark by the sun, and his eyes carried a murderous look.","She had never thought Zhou Yueshen was good-looking.","So, the first time she saw Fu Yang, she was instantly captivated.","But now, after a long time apart, running into Zhou Yueshen again, he was no longer riding a vintage bicycle. Instead, he was driving a black Santana, wearing a gray shirt, tailored suit trousers, and leather shoes.","His hair was cut very short, clean and neat. His eyes were sharp, and his eyebrows looked as if they had been trimmed. His skin was still dark, but it was very clean.","His entire body exuded the cold, untamable, and unattainable aura of a mature man.","It seemed as if no one could ever tame him.","Lin Sisi stood frozen in place, forgetting to walk.","She had always believed that even if Zhou Yueshen opened a factory and became a boss, he would never compare to Fu Yang.","Because Fu Yang's starting point was his finish line.","Therefore, she rarely looked this man straight in the eye.","But seeing him again now, she didn't know if her taste had changed or what the reason was, she just felt that the current Zhou Yueshen was different. It was as if the uncrossable chasm between him and Fu Yang had vanished.","He didn't seem at all like the old, country bumpkin breeding farm boss in her memory.","In the moment she stared blankly, she saw the man walk to the passenger side, open the car door, bend his back, and reach his hand inside.","A slender, white hand reached out from within and was tightly grasped in the man's palm.","Then, a familiar figure entered her line of sight.","Zhou Yueshen carefully helped Si Nian, who had a large pregnant belly but was still stunningly beautiful, out of the car. His eyes were full of doting affection, treating her like a precious treasure.","Si Nian seemed to be complaining about something, but Lin Sisi couldn't hear a word.","She only felt as if she had been struck by lightning. Her blood ran cold, and she stood rigidly in place.","She watched in disbelief as the two walked into the police station. It wasn't until they disappeared from her sight that she snapped back to reality, as if she had been hit over the head with a club.","T-That was Si Nian?","Si Nian was pregnant?","H-How was that possible? Didn't Zhou Yueshen say he didn't want children?","In her past life, she had disdained Zhou Yueshen and looked down on him, so the two of them slept in separate rooms. Let alone being intimate with her, Zhou Yueshen rarely even spoke to her.","His silent nature made her despise him even more.","It also completely severed any thought she had of living a life with him.","But now, he and Si Nian were living a happy life completely different from hers.","Why?","Why did Si Nian deserve this?","Why was it that no matter who she was with, her final ending was always happy?","Lin Sisi was so jealous she was almost going mad.","She thought Si Nian's fate would definitely be more miserable than hers. Even if Zhou Yueshen liked her, she would never have children and could only be a nanny.","And Fu Yang merely disliked her temporarily. As long as she worked hard in the future, she wouldn't have to worry at all; she would definitely live better than Si Nian.","But she had exhausted her mind doing so much, and in the end, Si Nian was still living happily.","Zhou Yueshen was even driving a luxury car and wearing an expensive suit, looking every bit the successful man.","She clearly hadn't done anything...","The only one who had been working hard all along was clearly herself.","So why did her hard work go unrewarded, while Si Nian got everything she had ever dreamed of without having to do a thing?","...","\"Achoo~\"","As soon as Si Nian walked into the station, she sneezed twice in a row.","She rubbed her nose. \"Who is cursing me?\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't know whether to laugh or cry. \"Isn't it because you're cold?\"","He draped the shawl he was holding over her shoulders. \"Careful not to catch a cold.\"","Si Nian pursed her lips and said, \"It's definitely not a cold. I speak from experience. Usually, if I sneeze twice, it means someone is cursing me.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","The two entered the station together. At this moment, Si's Father and Zhang Cuimei were sitting there with ugly expressions on their faces.","Several people next to them were speaking heatedly, \"They gave us money and told us to do it! It has nothing to do with us. If you want to blame anyone, blame them.\""]},{"number":460,"title":"Chapter 460: No matter how she pretends, she is still a thief.","paragraphs":["Si's Father and Zhang Cuimei, whose face was half swollen, both looked rather displeased.","They had originally intended to use money to keep this group of people tight-lipped.","Who knew it would turn out like this? Not only did they fail to keep them quiet, but the men had confessed everything on their own before the police even asked.","However, besides looking awful, Si's Father's expression also held a trace of something strange.","Only Zhang Cuimei was cursing furiously.","Her husband had found these people; initially, she had merely given them money to get the job done.","Because of her husband's caution, Zhang Cuimei hadn't suspected anything, but she never expected the situation to escalate like this.","Just as she was about to speak, she suddenly saw Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen walk in.","The moment they saw the two enter, the couple was stunned.","\"Niannian?\" Si's Father stared at Si Nian in astonishment.","\"Didn't you go to Jing City for university?\"","He was startled when he noticed Si Nian's belly.","Zhang Cuimei's face turned even uglier. She had said that a cowardly and helpless family like the Lins would never dare to sue the Si family.","So it was Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen pulling the strings.","In the past, when these two were here, they had always opposed them.","Whether it was her daughter or herself, they had never won a single time.","Seeing the two of them return now, how could Zhang Cuimei not understand?","With a dark expression, she demanded, \"Was it you? Did you make the Lin family send us a lawyer's letter?\"","Si Nian couldn't be bothered to pretend with her and said, \"Yes, it was me.\"","Zhang Cuimei shot up to her feet. \"Well, aren't you something! You ungrateful wretch, you heartless thing! It was bad enough that you caused our Sisi to go to jail back then, and now you want to ruin us as a couple.\"","\"As expected, no one in the Lin family is any good. First, they took advantage of Sisi's soft heart to get money from her, and now they turn around and bite us back. Does your Lin family have any conscience left?!\"","Zhang Cuimei's eyes were red with fury as she cursed.","Si Nian wasn't angry; she said calmly, \"Auntie, it seems you really don't understand your own daughter.\"","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Your daughter stole three thousand yuan in bride price from the Lin family, saddling them with massive debt, and she never thought of helping them in the slightest. Why would you think that the current her would be willing to give the Lin family money?\"","\"Bah! What are you pretending for? Wasn't it you who made Sisi steal those two thousand yuan from her father?\"","Captain Li interrupted her, saying, \"Comrade Zhang, regarding this sum of money, we have already found out the reason. According to what Comrade Lin Sisi herself explained, she took those two thousand yuan to help a good friend in an emergency. She just happened to encounter Comrade Lin who was in a car accident, so she gave it to them first. It was not demanded by the Lin family.\"","\"Furthermore, the Lin family had someone return this money to you in full the very next day. If they were really using Lin Sisi to swindle money out of you two, why would they return the money at such a critical moment, causing you to misunderstand, and then take a beating? Do you think they are idiots?\"","Zhang Cuimei choked on her words.","\"No, impossible. This must be an act. Sisi gave them three thousand before, so how do you explain that three thousand?\"","\"My parents only received these two thousand; they never received any three thousand yuan.\"","Si Nian frowned. So Lin Sisi had also taken three thousand.","No wonder the Si family went crazy, even to the point of getting physical.","This Lin Sisi really spent money like water. She had stolen three thousand yuan in bride price from her family before without changing her expression or feeling any guilt.","Then she turned around and took five thousand yuan from the Si family.","It had only been a little over two years since she came back, right?","To be honest, Si Nian was starting to not understand what Lin Sisi was trying to do.","\"Who knows if they received it or not? Would they admit it if they did?\" Zhang Cuimei scoffed coldly.","\"You even made our Sisi say it was stolen by someone. Maybe this time, saying she was helping a friend was also nonsense you made her spout. Only your Lin family could come up with such a lame excuse.\"","\"Mom, stop talking,\" Lin Sisi suddenly walked in from outside.","She looked awful, wearing an expression of unspoken suffering.","As if she were holding something back.","\"Sisi, you came at the right time. Tell them, did the Lin family secretly ask you for money?\"","Lin Sisi lowered her eyes and said with a complicated expression, \"Mom, it was all my own wishful thinking. It has nothing to do with the Lin family. Let's just let this matter go, okay? At worst, at worst I'll go work part-time in the future and pay all the money back to you.\"","\"No matter what, the Lin family raised me for eighteen years. I don't want to fall out with them like this.\"","As she spoke, she began to sob sadly, as if she had truly suffered a great injury.","Seeing her daughter's pale face and helpless tone, Zhang Cuimei flew into a rage, convinced that the Lin family was secretly using the fact that they had raised her for eighteen years to threaten her.","Trembling with anger, she shouted, \"Did you hear that? This is how the Lin family threatens my daughter. They take the money and still make her speak up for them. It's too hateful! Exploiting a girl's kindness like this, has their conscience been eaten by dogs?\"","Si Nian couldn't be bothered to deal with her. Looking at Lin Sisi, she said, \"Lin Sisi, didn't you say this money was for your friend's emergency? How did it suddenly become for my parents? Do you not know how to speak, or are you confused? Your words aren't adding up. We aren't your mother; crying a couple of times won't make us feel sorry for you.\"","\"What more do you want? Just how much pain do you have to inflict on our Sisi before you let her go?\" Zhang Cuimei glared fiercely.","Si Nian said indifferently, \"Auntie, when she stole the three thousand yuan, you said the exact same thing to me, and you felt sorry for her just like this. But what was the result? No matter how much she pretends, isn't she still a thief?\"","Zhang Cuimei's face turned pale and green from the retort.","These words were practically rubbing salt in her wounds.","Lin Sisi's face also twisted slightly.","\"Whether she's lying or not, wouldn't we know if we just invite her friend over and ask?\"","Si Nian said calmly.","Lin Sisi silently lowered her head, biting her lip. \"Yes, I lied. I was just worried that my parents would blame the Lin family, so I lied. I just didn't want my adoptive parents to be dragged down because of me...\"","\"Sister Niannian, if you want to blame someone, blame me. It has nothing to do with my parents; it's all my fault alone.\"","Lin Sisi stepped forward, acting as if she were willing to bear all the consequences.","Seeing this made Zhang Cuimei's heart ache.","She was just about to start cursing again, but remembering Si Nian's words that no matter how much Lin Sisi pretended, she was still a thief, she hesitated.","At this moment, the expression on her daughter's face was exactly the same as when she was caught back then. In that one second of hesitation, Captain Li spoke up. \"Who says there isn't such a person? Our men who were following Comrade Lin Sisi found out that she has been frequently running to a certain place lately, and today she even spoke with a woman.\"","Lin Sisi's face instantly turned pale.","She... she was being followed?","And she had absolutely no idea?","She remembered how Captain Li had easily let her leave yesterday, thinking it was because the other party had no evidence and thus couldn't say much.","She never expected that they were actually plotting against her.","Lin Sisi looked awful, barely able to conceal the panic in her eyes.","At this moment, she wasn't panicking about the lie.","But about another, much more important matter.","If this blew up, that child...","However, before she could even open her mouth, Captain Li interjected, \"We've brought the person here. Let's all hear what Comrade Liu Dongdong has to say, shall we?\""]},{"number":461,"title":"Chapter 461: The Mantis Stalks the Cicada","paragraphs":["Lin Sisi's eyes widened. She turned her head abruptly, and the moment she saw Liu Dongdong, her breath hitched.","Zhang Cuimei also looked over in astonishment.","\"Dongdong? Didn't you go back to your hometown?\"","\"What's going on here?\" Zhang Cuimei asked in disbelief.","Liu Dongdong greeted her, \"Auntie Zhang, long time no see.\"","Zhang Cuimei's expression was a bit strange. Previously, Liu Dongdong had been doing a great job working for them, and she had really liked the girl. But after her daughter returned, some unpleasant things happened. When her daughter told Liu Dongdong to leave, Zhang Cuimei hadn't said anything to help her.","Seeing her again now, her eyes held a hint of guilt.","\"Repeat that again, why did Lin Sisi look for you?\"","Captain Li interrupted the two of them calmly.","Lin Sisi looked at Liu Dongdong in panic, almost forgetting to breathe.","Hadn't they agreed? She was supposed to find a place to hide immediately, not show up, and leave the city as soon as she got the money.","Was she tricked?","At the thought of this possibility, Lin Sisi's face instantly turned deathly pale.","However, realizing she had been deceived now was already too late.","Liu Dongdong said, \"I don't want to lie for her this time. Previously, because she helped me, I agreed to testify that she didn't steal that three thousand yuan. I considered her a friend at the time and didn't expect her to be that kind of person. Who knew it would end up harming me, making me unable to hold my head high when I returned to my village, and even causing my family to be ridiculed...\"","\"My trust and defense of her have harmed so many people. This time, the Lin family was hurt like this because of it, and my heart aches deeply. I originally wanted to persuade Sisi to tell the truth, but I didn't expect her to ask me to lie for her again this time.\"","\"I'm sorry, Sisi, I can't do it. I don't want to hurt people anymore.\"","\"I never asked you for two thousand yuan, yet you deliberately told me to hide and not come forward to explain, letting everyone misunderstand the Lin family. I don't understand why you wanted me to tell this lie to help you, but what you're doing is wrong.\"","Liu Dongdong condemned her with a look of disappointment.","Hearing these words, Lin Sisi was instantly dumbfounded.","\"So you two never actually bumped into each other at the hospital, right?\" Captain Li said.","Liu Dongdong nodded. \"That's right, I never ran into Lin Sisi at all.\"","\"Since Lin Sisi didn't go to the hospital to look for you and happen to run into the car accident, but was lying, then why did she arrive at the hospital the very moment the accident happened, and even had the money for the surgery prepared in advance?\"","Captain Li murmured, \"Could it be that you knew in advance that Brother Lin would have an accident, so you were staking out the place to offer help?\"","\"We checked. You had classes that day, but you took time off early and went back.\"","\"The reason you gave for your leave was that a family member was injured...\"","\"Lin Sisi, you really have the gift of foresight.\"","Si Nian narrowed her eyes. She had originally just been guessing.","But hearing Captain Li mention this, she couldn't help but feel suspicious.","She asked, \"Did Lin Sisi lose that three thousand yuan a few months ago?\"","Zhang Cuimei snapped out of her daze. \"How did you know?\"","Si Nian sneered. \"Of course I know. At that time, Lin Sisi traveled all the way to Beijing to solve a case. She suddenly led a bunch of police officers to the vicinity of my house, claiming someone had committed murder and hidden a corpse there. Later, because they couldn't find a body, she sneaked away.\"","\"Although I don't quite understand why she went all the way to Beijing, it probably wasn't just to solve a case, right? With that three thousand yuan, she couldn't possibly have spent nothing on her trip to Beijing, so how could it have fallen into my parents' hands?\"","Zhang Cuimei was dumbfounded. She had thought her daughter's claim about doing business was just a lie to get money to subsidize the Lin family.","So when Lin Sisi said the money was stolen, she hadn't believed it at all.","But to her surprise, she really went to Beijing?","Because she spent all the money and failed to do business, she lied about it being stolen?","\"In other words, the first time her three thousand yuan didn't go to my parents, and the second time it didn't either. Then on what grounds did your Si family hire people to beat up my parents?\"","Si Nian's eyes turned cold.","Zhang Cuimei immediately panicked. Realizing she might really have no more excuses, she had to look to her husband for help.","Unexpectedly, her husband suddenly spoke up, \"I disagreed with you doing this at the time. You insisted on helping Sisi teach them a lesson.\"","He sighed. \"Since both the witnesses and material evidence are here, we have nothing more to say. Punish us however we should be punished.\"","\"What?\" Zhang Cuimei was stunned. \"What are you saying? Are you crazy?\"","Suddenly realizing something, her eyes snapped wide open. \"You!\"","Si's Father interrupted her, \"I only knew you said you wanted to warn the Lin family, which is why I didn't stop you. I had no idea you would hire people to beat them up like this. You have truly disappointed me.\"","Zhang Cuimei's breathing grew rapid, her chest heaving violently. She pointed at his nose. \"It... it was clearly you who hired those people.\"","\"What are you talking about? You took the money and hired people to do the deed. What does that have to do with me? I never knew you had such a cruel heart!\"","Si's Father scolded.","\"Now that we're at the end of the line, are you still trying to shirk responsibility?\"","Si Nian watched this family with amusement as they pushed the blame back and forth.","\"It seems there's nothing left for us to do. We'll just leave it to however the court decides.\"","She couldn't even be bothered to deal with this hypocritical family anymore.","Instead, she cast a thoughtful glance at Liu Dongdong and Si's Father.","Come to think of it, there was something off about this matter. It was too easy.","It was as if Zhang Cuimei was deliberately called over, and then the other party acted to let the police find out.","The same went for Liu Dongdong, who had suddenly appeared.","It felt like it had been orchestrated by someone.","But obviously, the beneficiaries this time were neither them nor Lin Sisi.","It was Si's Father and Liu Dongdong.","It was just very strange. How did these two completely unrelated people suddenly and tacitly end up working together?","Si Nian felt very weirded out.","Next.","Because Lin Sisi might be the mastermind behind orchestrating the car crash, she was detained as a key suspect.","Meanwhile, Zhang Cuimei was also detained awaiting sentencing on suspicion of intentional injury.","Because Si's Father was unaware, and those thugs also insisted that Zhang Cuimei was the one giving orders, he was simply questioned about the details and then released.","Both Zhang Cuimei and her daughter Lin Sisi ended up in the police station.","Si's Father did not choose to help the two of them.","Instead, at this time, he righteously filed a divorce report with his superiors. Because Zhang Cuimei's situation was extremely severe, he didn't have to worry much about the divorce going through.","The Fu family also heard about Lin Sisi's matter. This time, they absolutely could not tolerate it and directly took charge, having their son and Lin Sisi—a married couple in name only—get divorced.","A few days passed, and Zhou Yueshen went back first.","Si Nian stayed home to help, afraid that Si's Father would stir up trouble again."]},{"number":462,"title":"Chapter 462: The End of Lin Sisi","paragraphs":["She and Zhou Yueshen both felt that this matter was highly likely manipulated behind the scenes by Si's Father.","Si's Father had wanted to divorce Zhang Cuimei for a while, but he had been pressured into holding back.","Now, this situation gave him a legitimate excuse.","She was also worried that the Lin family would be targeted for trouble.","So she stayed at home.","Zhou Yueshen couldn't be away from his company for too long, so he went back first to handle business. Furthermore, if he stayed away too long, Si Nian would worry about the children. Having him go back first gave her some peace of mind.","However, nothing happened to her next; instead, it was Lin Sisi who got into trouble.","Sure enough, following the police investigation, the abandoned hit-and-run vehicle was quickly found.","They originally thought the driver had fled, but unexpectedly, within a couple of days, the driver turned himself in.","The driver quickly confessed, claiming that Lin Sisi had paid him to help out. She told him to hit and run, promising to contact him later to hand over the money.","Who knew that after hiding for several days, he wouldn't hear a peep from Lin Sisi.","Thinking she was going to renege on the debt, he turned himself in out of anger.","Now Si Nian understood why Lin Sisi had taken so much money.","It turned out that besides paying for her brother's surgery, there was also the driver's fee.","But because she was detained, she had no way to get the money to him.","Instead, she got sued.","With both human witnesses and material evidence present against the mother and daughter, a prison sentence was inevitable.","On the day Lin Sisi was sentenced, Fu Yang returned.","He didn't come back specifically to visit Lin Sisi, but rather because he had earned merits after being away for half a year.","This time, he came back to bid farewell to his family.","Originally, he had just gone to temper himself, but after his experiences in the Northwest, Fu Yang realized just how blessed his previous life had been.","He found the true value of his identity there.","He just didn't expect that right upon his return, he would encounter Lin Sisi's downfall.","Hearing that Lin Sisi was going to prison again, Fu Yang was speechless.","He seriously suspected that because he had treated Si Nian so poorly in the past, heaven had arranged for such a woman to torment him.","This woman, Lin Sisi, had always been exceptionally good at courting disaster.","He actually used to think someone like her was better than Si Nian.","He couldn't even understand why he had inexplicably agreed to the marriage back then without putting up the slightest resistance.","Had his brain short-circuited?","Out of all the choices, he had picked the absolute worst.","Fu Yang's visit this time was to deliver the news of their divorce to Lin Sisi.","This was to prevent her from relentlessly pestering him once she got out of prison.","For some reason, he felt a sense of loss and regret in his heart, feeling that things shouldn't have turned out this way.","But having reached this point, there was no way to change anything.","Before Lin Sisi was sent away, she heard that someone had come to visit her.","She thought it was Si's Father and was thrilled.","She believed her father had abandoned Zhang Cuimei because he had no other choice.","But she herself could absolutely be saved.","After all, she was his only daughter. He could give up her mother, but he could never abandon her.","Lin Sisi didn't have much affection for Zhang Cuimei anyway, even disliking her a bit.","When she heard from Si's Father that it was Zhang Cuimei who hired someone to hurt the Lin family, she was furious.","If it weren't for her mother constantly ruining her good deeds, her plans would have succeeded long ago.","Frankly speaking, she ended up in this state all because of her mother.","Now, not only was her mother going to prison, but she had been dragged down and arrested too.","Lin Sisi was burning with anger.","But being angry right now was useless.","She only had one thought in her mind, and that was to get out.","She didn't want to go back into that cold, bleak prison cell.","However, Lin Sisi never expected that the visitor would actually be Fu Yang.","When she saw Fu Yang, she was completely stunned.","Then, a flash of pleasant surprise crossed her eyes. Brother Fu Yang, you're back. Are you here to help me?","Lin Sisi shed tears of excitement. Sob... I knew you couldn't bear to see me go to jail. I really didn't do this; you have to believe me.","Fu Yang listened quietly until she finished, then spoke in a deep voice, I came to inform you of something.","I'm sorry to give you this news in such a setting, but there are some things I don't want to leave tangled up forever.","Lin Sisi froze. Meeting his expressionless face, her heart leaped into her throat.","Fu Yang was even thinner than before, and his skin was tanned, matching the complexion of Zhou Yueshen, whom she had once looked down upon.","He was lean, and his face showed signs of weathering.","Yet he remained handsome and dashing.","It made it hard to look away.","This man was her husband by marriage. Even if it was in name only, Lin Sisi had always believed that she held at least a tiny place in Fu Yang's heart.","But now, the coldness and indifference on the man's face chilled her to the bone.","What, what do you mean?","Lin Sisi's mind was a mess, terrified of hearing from his mouth that she was being abandoned.","But Fu Yang felt no pity for her and said directly, I'm here to tell you about our divorce. Speaking of these past two years, I actually didn't want to hold you back. But your Si family has been uncooperative, causing this abnormal marriage to drag on for so long.","I once thought that being with you would be fine, but in reality, we aren't suitable. All this time, I have never felt a trace of affection for you. A loveless marriage has no need to continue.","I came here because I want you to know that I'm not choosing to divorce you because you're going to prison, but because... I don't like you at all.","Fu Yang calmly delivered the most cruel words.","Lin Sisi felt a loud rumble in her brain.","Her mind instantly went blank.","All the color drained from her face.","When she recovered, her eyes immediately turned red. She shook her head and said, No, you're lying. You used to be so good to me. Is it Liu Dongdong? Did Liu Dongdong secretly say something to your family behind my back, so you're divorcing me?","When she went to prison before, Fu Yang hadn't divorced her.","This time, he had specifically traveled all the way back from the Northwest. Lin Sisi didn't believe she had the power to make him return in person just for her.","There had to be another reason.","It could only be Liu Dongdong.","It could only be that child...","Lin Sisi's eyes were bloodshot.","She thought everything was under her control, but she never expected that she had been played for a fool by Liu Dongdong all along.","Come to think of it, she had been too naive. Although Liu Dongdong came from a poor background, she had a child, and a boy at that. Just relying on that child, her status would rise as the mother.","The Fu family already disliked her. With such a great opportunity, how could Liu Dongdong possibly miss it?","She had been too stupid, actually believing Liu Dongdong's nonsense and thinking she would really take the money and leave!","Lin Sisi was trembling all over with rage.","In this life, she had focused all her attention on targeting Si Nian.","But she never expected the mantis stalking the cicada to be unaware of the oriole behind.","In the end, Liu Dongdong had stolen everything from her.","Seeing her frantic state, Fu Yang frowned. What does this have to do with Liu Dongdong?","He was bewildered.","Liu Dongdong?","There seemed to be someone by that name.","Her cooking was pretty good. He didn't know where she learned her tricks, but she always made food similar to what Si Nian used to make and sent it to him.","Fu Yang originally wanted to refuse, but every time he tried, he would think of the scenes where Si Nian used to bring him things, only to be shut out and leave dejectedly.","Somehow, he just couldn't bring himself to be cruel."]},{"number":463,"title":"Chapter 463: Fu Qianqian and Yu Dong","paragraphs":["As for Liu Dongdong, he didn't even know what she looked like.","\"Are you still trying to hide it from me? Do you think I don't know? You always look down on me from your high horse, but how is Liu Dongdong any better than me? Why would you fancy her but completely ignore me? How am I inferior to her?\"","Lin Sisi accused him angrily.","\"You cheated during our marriage, and I didn't even make trouble for you, yet your Fu family was the first to accuse me. Yes, I made a mistake, but I've never done anything to wrong your family. Why are you treating me like this?\"","These words left Fu Yang completely baffled.","Looking at Lin Sisi's frantic expression, he asked in confusion, \"Where is this coming from? Although I don't like you, I haven't been in contact with any other women during this time. I live an upright life and have never done anything to wrong you.\"","If there was anyone he had wronged in this life, it was only Si Nian.","Lin Sisi wasn't even worth him doing something to wrong her.","Lin Sisi sneered, \"Do you dare to say that Liu Dongdong's child isn't yours? She has already admitted it, and you still want to hide it? What, are you worried I'll expose your scandal so you won't be able to hold your head up in the family compound?\"","Fu Yang: \"...Lin Sisi, is there something wrong with your head? I haven't even seen Liu Dongdong twice. How could I possibly have a child with her?\"","Speaking of which, he had heard over the past two days that Si's Father had adopted a child.","Rumors in the family compound said that because Si's Father had lost his daughter and had no heir, he had no choice but to adopt a child.","Could it be this?","Fu Yang's expression turned odd.","The complexity of this family was truly comparable to a battlefield.","He couldn't be bothered with Lin Sisi's stunned look and stood up to leave.","Lin Sisi was completely dumbfounded.","If that child wasn't Fu Yang's, then whose was it?","She clearly remembered that when Liu Dongdong visited her a year ago, she had ambiguous marks on her body.","At that time, Liu Dongdong said she had found a boyfriend.","But she had never seen such a person.","So Lin Sisi had been living in fear, thinking something had happened between her and Fu Yang.","But a proud man like Fu Yang wouldn't stoop to lying.","When he heard her mention the child, his face showed nothing but confusion.","And he genuinely seemed unfamiliar with Liu Dongdong.","Since he wasn't familiar with her, nothing could have happened between them.","Then Liu Dongdong's child really wasn't his?","But if it wasn't his, whose child was it?","Did Liu Dongdong say that simply to take revenge on her for driving her away back then?","As Lin Sisi stood there in a daze, she suddenly saw Zhang Cuimei being brought over. Zhang Cuimei looked blank and motionless.","Ever since she was arrested that day, her mental state hadn't been right.","It seemed someone had just gone to talk to her as well.","Upon seeing her now, the previously blank Zhang Cuimei suddenly rushed at her like a madwoman, \"Liars, you're all liars, hahaha, he has a son, he doesn't want you anymore, hahaha.\"","Lin Sisi was badly startled.","When she realized what was happening, she was utterly bewildered.","...","Si Nian didn't wait long enough for Si's Father to come looking for trouble, but instead heard the news that Si's Father had taken in an adopted son.","Fu Qianqian heard she was back and rushed over right after work.","After not seeing each other for over half a year, she had grown her hair out. She no longer looked like a tomboy; her hair reached her shoulders, making her look less boyish and more gentle.","She stuffed food into her mouth while saying, \"Some people say it's his illegitimate son from the outside. They say he deliberately sent his wife and daughter to prison this time just to bring the boy back. They say the child looks just like him, but who knows if it's true.\"","\"But everyone is just discussing it in private. On the surface, no one dares to say anything since there's no proof. Speaking of which, with his wife and daughter in prison for doing such things, he's left all alone as a loner. A lot of people actually feel sorry for him.\"","Si Nian cracked melon seeds and said, \"No need to doubt it, it definitely is.\"","Originally, she didn't quite understand why Si's Father would do this.","If he simply wanted a divorce, there was no need to push things to such extremes.","Now, Si Nian understood.","It turned out he had an illegitimate son.","Si's Father used this incident to not only get rid of his wife but also smoothly bring his illegitimate son home. She had to admit, his methods were truly brilliant.","Previously, Zhang Cuimei had refused to divorce, but now she had ended up in such a state.","Si Nian didn't know whether to feel sorry for her or think she deserved it.","Oh well, now that Si's Father had his own son, he probably wouldn't come knocking on her door to find fault anymore.","With Lin Sisi and Zhang Cuimei both in prison, no one would come to disturb the Lin family in the future either.","As for whatever mess the Si family made, Si Nian didn't care at all.","She glanced at Fu Qianqian and frowned, \"Have you noticed that you've gained weight?\"","Fu Qianqian's eating movements froze.","She touched her noticeably rounder face, \"Right? I said I got fat, but Yu Dong insisted I didn't.\"","Si Nian raised an eyebrow, \"I can tell you've been eating well with him.\"","Fu Qianqian said uncomfortably, \"What do you mean 'with him'? He's the one who insists on pestering me, researching new dishes all day and forcing me to taste them. Once I start eating, I can't stop. Now I get scared just seeing him.\"","Si Nian didn't know whether to laugh or cry, \"Isn't that great? You like to eat, and he likes to cook.\"","\"What's great about it? He made me fat. How am I supposed to date handsome guys in the future?\"","Si Nian could see she didn't entirely mean what she said.","\"Date who?\" Yu Dong popped out of nowhere, holding quite a bit of food in his hands.","\"Qianqian, I brought it over for you. Didn't you say you were too lazy to go over? From now on, I'll deliver it to you. This is a new dish I researched, I guarantee you'll like it.\"","Seeing him sweating profusely while carrying a bunch of food over, Fu Qianqian didn't give him a good look, \"Eat, eat, eat, that's all you know how to make me do every day. How am I supposed to find a boyfriend after I get fat? Even Si Nian said I gained weight. It's all your fault!\"","\"Did you get fat? I don't feel like you did.\"","Yu Dong looked her up and down, finding her cuter the more he looked.","Feeling quite a sense of accomplishment, he nodded in self-satisfaction as he watched her, \"Even if you get as fat as a pig, I'll still think you're beautiful.\"","Fu Qianqian: \"......\"","Si Nian: \"......\""]},{"number":464,"title":"Chapter 464: Three Siblings","paragraphs":["......","Ever since their parents returned to their hometown, Second Child had been unhappy, finding no joy in anything he did.","In the past, he would wake up every day to jog and practice martial arts. After finishing his routine, he could eat breakfast. Seeing him work so hard, his mother would rub his head, praise him, and tell him not to overtire himself.","She was never as heartless as their father.","His mother's praise was the motivation that kept him going every day.","But with their mother away from home and their father no longer managing him, Second Child suddenly lost all his drive.","He decided that he would definitely sleep in the next day and specifically instructed his older brother not to wake him up.","No one was going to stop him from sleeping in.","Then he collapsed onto the bed and went Zzzzzz...","Zhou Zedong shot him a glance and completely ignored him.","He pulled out a notebook and began to write.","He never used to take notes, but ever since he took an interest in research, he developed a habit of recording things.","At first, he only recorded research processes and results.","Later, when he started cooking with his mother, he also enjoyed writing down the recipes, the flavors of each dish, and everyone's feedback.","Eventually, this evolved into keeping a diary.","Every night before bed, he would first jot down the key events that had happened during the day.","Only after writing would he go to sleep.","With Mom and Dad away from home, he was now the eldest brother in the house, and he had to take good care of his younger brother and sister.","Although he had been angry at his brother earlier and planned not to wake him up so he would be late and punished by having to stand in class...","...he was also afraid his brother would be scolded by the teacher.","So, after thinking it over, Zhou Zedong decided to let him off the hook this time.","His brother said he didn't want to exercise and wanted to sleep in, but he wasn't going to let him get his way.","When Mom was home, his brother always loved to show off, and Mom liked him best.","Slacking off as soon as Mom was gone—such a brother was not a good brother.","He had to correct his brother's bad habit.","However, his younger sister didn't need to jog and exercise; she could sleep a little longer, and he would wake her up after making breakfast.","His sister liked egg pancakes and millet porridge. His brother said he wanted noodles and didn't like vegetables—so picky. Therefore, it was better to make what his sister liked.","For lunch, he would pick up his sister and they would eat at the cafeteria. In the afternoon, he would cook at home.","When Dad left, he gave him a hundred yuan. Tomorrow, he would give his sister fifty cents to buy candy, leaving ninety-nine yuan and fifty cents. In the afternoon, he would go buy some groceries...","After finishing his record of today's events and tomorrow's plans, Zhou Zedong got up, changed into his little pajamas, and lay down to sleep.","Halfway through his sleep, he climbed out of bed again, feeling worried.","His sister was sleeping over there all by herself, and Mom and Dad weren't home. What if she wanted to go to the bathroom at night but was too scared to get up?","Thinking of this, he immediately got up, put on his little slippers, and ran toward his sister's room. He would sleep with his sister tonight.","Anyway, if his brother wet the bed, he would have to wash his own sheets.","In the middle of the night, Zhou Zehan urgently needed to pee. He groggily climbed out of bed and called out to Zhou Zedong, Brother, come with me to the bathroom. I want to pee.","After calling out for a long time with no response, he reached out to feel the spot next to him, but it was empty.","Second Child jolted awake.","His brother had disappeared.","His brother had been taken away by ghosts.","Terrified, Second Child immediately pulled his feet back under the covers, squirming around on the bed. When he really couldn't hold it in any longer, he shivering grabbed a flashlight and went out to use the bathroom.","Spirits of heaven and earth, Brother, I didn't mean not to save you. If you're gone, please don't haunt me. I haven't lived long enough yet.","Don't worry, Brother, I'll help you be filial to Mom and Dad and take good care of our younger siblings. You can go in peace.","His little legs were trembling. Before he even reached the bathroom, he couldn't hold it anymore, so he hurriedly pulled down his pants and squatted in the courtyard to pee.","A cold gust of wind blew by, making his bare bottom feel chilly.","Without even having time to pull up his pants, he ran back to the room like the wind and immediately shrank under the covers.","He groggily fell asleep and even dreamed that his brother was captured by monsters.","Second Child was very sad. Even though his eldest brother always looked down on him and didn't like talking to him, no matter how bad he was, he was still his brother.","Without his brother in the future, the family would have to rely entirely on him.","Second Child cried sadly, and cried until he woke himself up.","He even forgot all about sleeping in.","The clock nearby showed the time was six in the morning.","Having been trained by his father for almost a year, he had already developed a biological clock.","Now, he woke up on his own right on time.","After finishing his morning run and returning, he suddenly remembered that his brother was gone. That meant he had to cook for his sister, otherwise she wouldn't have any food when she woke up.","He didn't know when Mom and Dad would come back. Even though they had just left, Second Child already missed his mother very much.","He felt as if he had matured in an instant, and immediately went thumping off to the kitchen to prepare a meal.","As a result, before he even stepped into the kitchen, he smelled a delicious aroma.","Second Child twitched his nose, thinking he was hallucinating.","He moved in the direction of the scent, only to see his brother, who had disappeared overnight, right there in the kitchen.","At this moment, he was wearing their mother's pink apron and frying pancakes.","The aroma wafting out was exactly the scent of egg pancakes.","Second Child was a bit dumbfounded. He stepped forward and suddenly pinched his brother's butt.","Zhou Zedong was so startled that he almost threw the pan out of his hands.","Why did you pinch me! He turned around to see his brother covered in sweat with an expression like he had seen a ghost, and asked with a frown.","Brother, are you real? Second Child's eyes widened when he heard the voice.","Was it not a hallucination born out of missing his brother too much?","Realizing this possibility, Second Child immediately threw himself into Zhou Zedong's arms and started crying, wiping all his tears and snot on his brother.","I woke up last night and didn't see you, and I even dreamed that you were taken away by ghosts. I was scared to death.","Zhou Zedong: .....","Chen Haoran walked through the door carrying food and immediately smelled a delicious aroma.","He almost thought Si Nian and the others had returned.","Entering the kitchen, he realized it was just the two little guys. The younger brother was hugging his older brother, crying his heart out. He was a bit bewildered.","Oh my, why did you two brothers come into the kitchen? Children shouldn't be in such a dangerous place. Hurry up and get out. Didn't I say I would bring your food over from now on?","He thought the two children had gotten hungry, ran to the kitchen to make food, and ended up getting hurt.","His heart leaped into his throat.","He couldn't mess up on his very first day of babysitting.","Wouldn't he be scolded to death when Si Nian came back?","I know how to cook myself, I don't need you to look after us, Zhou Zedong pushed his brother away. With practiced ease, he shook the egg pancake in the pan with one hand, then with a deft flick of his wrist, the fragrant pancake flipped in the air and landed perfectly back in the pan.","Just this one pan-tossing move was enough to dumbfound Chen Haoran, a man who had never done any household chores in his life.","He had just heard the crying and rushed in without stopping, not even noticing the aroma wafting through the house.","He had thought it was someone else cooking next door.","Now he noticed that in a bowl to the side sat four or five perfectly uniform, mouth-watering egg pancakes, and next to it was a small clay pot filled with softly simmered millet porridge.","After finishing the last large pancake, Zhou Zedong took out a small bowl, picked out some pickled radishes that Si Nian had prepared earlier from among the various jars and pots, and carried it out.","Chen Haoran stood rooted to the spot like a block of wood, holding a bag of breakfast, watching him bustle back and forth.","Zhou Zedong methodically cleaned up the kitchen, wiped the countertops spotless, and then dried his hands before going to the bedroom to wake his younger sister. He changed her into fresh clothes, tied her hair, and supervised her as she brushed her teeth and washed her face.","The entire routine took no more than seven or eight minutes.","Chen Haoran: \"...\"","He suddenly felt like a third wheel, completely redundant.","Last night, he had been worried about oversleeping today, so he dragged himself out of bed bright and early to buy breakfast for the kids, afraid they might go hungry.","He had been full of confidence, imagining that when he arrived, the kids would swarm around him with adoration and joy.","Who knew that upon his arrival, let alone swarming around him, they wouldn't even have the time to spare him a single glance.","Having finished all the morning preparations, Zhou Zedong saw him still standing there and asked in confusion, \"Brother Chen, is there something else?\"","Chen Haoran: \"...\"","He wanted to say yes, but he couldn't quite articulate what it was.","Oh right, what about the breakfast he bought?","He looked down at the large bag of breakfast food in his hand.","He fell into a spiral of self-doubt. Did these kids really need him?","Eating the breakfast made by a little kid, someone as confident as Chen Haoran felt a sense of inferiority for the very first time.","He made up his mind. In order to take better care of these children, he was going to move in!","After heading to school with a full stomach, Chen Haoran tossed the breakfast he had bought to a few of his friends.","They were quite touched. \"Wow, Brother Chen, how did you know I didn't eat breakfast?\"","\"Whoa, there's so much! What a feast!\"","\"Aren't these the buns from Yulongfang? I heard you can't even get them if you line up. Brother Chen is the best, so generous.\"","Chen Haoran picked his teeth, looking at them with a face full of disdain. \"Look at you all, acting like you've never seen good food. What I ate today was way better than this.\"","In the past, he always found it too troublesome and never ate breakfast at all.","Having eaten it today, his stomach felt incredibly comfortable, and he was in a great mood.","He wondered what else that kid could cook. It seemed he needed to go pick them up a bit earlier this evening.","With this thought in mind, he immediately turned down all sorts of invitations from his rowdy friends. As soon as his afternoon classes ended, he drove his motorcycle over early to pick up the kids.","Seeing the children walking out of the school, Chen Haoran smiled sweeter than a blooming flower.","The kids passing by looked at the motorcycle he was riding with envious eyes.","His motorcycle was a limited edition model. Its bright red body was incredibly eye-catching.","What kid wouldn't covet such a cool motorcycle?","Coupled with Chen Haoran's trendy outfit, his hair spiked up towards the sky and dyed blonde, rumored to be the exact same hairstyle as a certain Hong Kong celebrity.","He also wore stud earrings, had a pair of headphones hanging around his neck, and a pair of sunglasses resting on his head. He looked ridiculously stylish.","Since he was also quite good-looking, let alone the children, even passing teenagers and young girls couldn't help but cast envious and shy glances his way.","When the kids came out, this was the scene they saw.","Seeing the three siblings emerge, Chen Haoran lifted his chin. \"Little Dong, Little Han, I'm over here.\"","Zhou Zedong tilted his head and caught sight of the flamboyant Chen Haoran.","\"...\"","Second Child, on the other hand, let out an uncritical \"Wow!\" and said, \"What a beautiful motorcycle! Brother, I want to ride it too.\"","Thinking of motorcycles, he couldn't help but miss his dad's motorcycle back when they lived in Xingfu Village.","Back then, their dad would ride his motorcycle bright and early every morning to take him and his older brother to school. It was so cool.","All his friends at school envied him.","Second Child would walk with his back straight and tall every single day.","Later, they moved to the city. Although their lives had improved, he still deeply missed their time in Xingfu Village.","He broke into a run, rushing over to touch the bike here and there.","Seeing his delighted expression, Chen Haoran knew that riding this motorcycle here was definitely the right choice.","He jutted his chin out and asked, \"How about it? Is my ride cool or what?\"","Second Child nodded. \"So cool!\"","\"Want a ride?\"","\"Uh-huh!\"","\"Then I have to test you a bit. Do you notice anything different about me today?\"","Second Child's attention was finally drawn away from the bike. He looked up at Chen Haoran in confusion.","Chen Haoran lowered his head, thinking he looked extremely handsome, and asked Second Child, \"Do you see anything on my face?\"","Second Child frowned, stared carefully for a moment, and suddenly came to a realization. \"I see it.\"","The corners of Chen Haoran's mouth curled up. \"Say it out loud.\"","Second Child yelled at the top of his lungs, \"You have eye boogers!\"","Chen Haoran: \"...\"","Yaoyao came running over with pitter-patter steps, opening her big, beautiful eyes, and said, \"Second brother, let me see.\"","Then she said in an exaggerated tone, \"There really are eye boogers! Brother Chen is dirty, he doesn't wash his face. Yaoyao washes her face every single day.\"","After saying that, she proudly lifted her little chin.","Chen Haoran almost fell off the motorcycle.","Watching his younger brother and sister diligently searching for eye boogers on Chen Haoran's face, Zhou Zedong's mouth twitched.","It was simply too embarrassing to watch.","Was this guy their parents found really reliable?","With a heavy heart, Zhou Zedong went to the wet market to buy groceries.","He was already very familiar with this place.","Sometimes when they ran out of vegetables at home, his mother would ask him to come buy some.","As a result, whenever the vendors saw him, they would greet him warmly.","\"Little Dong, did your mom send you to buy groceries again?\"","\"My mom went back to our hometown, so I came to buy them myself.\"","Zhou Zedong replied politely while picking out fresh vegetables.","\"Oh my, how impressive.\"","Everyone smiled and praised him for being so sensible.","They said that knowing how to buy groceries and cook at such a young age meant he would be incredible when he grew up.","Whichever girl married him in the future would surely be blessed.","Chen Haoran's stylish motorcycle was ultimately reduced to a grocery transport vehicle, with a few large green onions tied to the back.","Yaoyao sat in the front, while the two brothers, Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan, sat in the back.","Despite his excellent driving skills, navigating through the crowded wet market made him sweat profusely.","Zhou Zedong was still very distrustful. \"Maybe we should just get off and walk.\"","Chen Haoran's face flushed bright red in embarrassment.","Zhang Xue was out doing things with a group of friends as usual, when someone nudged her. \"Hey, Xiaoxue, look quickly, isn't that Chen Haoran?\"","Zhang Xue looked over in surprise. Sure enough, there was Chen Haoran, who had been so stylish and cool that morning, causing a sensation at school with everyone wanting to ride on the back of his bike. Right now, he looked completely flustered, hauling three little kids around with a few large green onions hanging off the back of his motorcycle.","Before she could recover from her shock, someone asked in confusion, \"Didn't you say his family is really rich? He doesn't look like he has a lot of money right now.\"","\"Yeah, what kind of rich person has to buy their own groceries? Also, doesn't he have a bit too many siblings?\"","Zhang Xue was also puzzled in her heart. Why would Chen Haoran be taking care of Si Nian's children?","No wonder he left right after school every day recently; she heard he wasn't even going out to play anymore.","Thinking about how Si Nian was pregnant, could he be specially helping Si Nian take care of the kids?","If she managed to build a good relationship with Si Nian, she would definitely be able to interact with him more.","Zhang Xue felt a surge of excitement. Watching the motorcycle approach, she immediately tidied her hair. Everyone around her nudged her frantically, their gazes filled with teasing ambiguity.","Zhang Xue felt a bit shy.","Seeing him get closer, she was just about to open her mouth to say hello, but who would have expected Chen Haoran to speed off on his motorcycle without even looking back.","He hadn't seen her at all."]},{"number":465,"title":"Chapter 465: Homecoming","paragraphs":["Her smile froze instantly.","\"Hey, what's going on? Why didn't he say hello to you? Aren't you good friends?\"","\"Yeah, I even heard people say he was pursuing you,\" everyone asked in confusion.","Zhang Xue's face didn't look too good. Hearing this, she forced a smile and said, \"M-maybe there were too many people and he didn't notice?\"","Everyone looked at each other.","He had just ridden his motorcycle right past their faces. If he couldn't see them, he was either blind or they just weren't close at all.","The way everyone looked at Zhang Xue became a bit strange.","After all, Zhang Xue often mentioned in front of them that she knew Chen Haoran, and boasted about how rich his family was because they ran a company.","Anyway, he was a young master from a wealthy family in Jing City.","They didn't quite believe it at first, but after noticing that Chen Haoran frequently switched between different motorcycles and always wore famous designer brands, they had to believe it.","You have to know that nowadays, a motorcycle costs around ten thousand yuan.","A household with ten thousand yuan was already considered very wealthy where they came from.","Plus, Zhang Xue and Chen Haoran seemed to have a pretty good relationship before and were often seen walking together, so they thought there was something going on between them.","Therefore, they had been very flattering towards Zhang Xue.","But now, watching him pass right in front of them without even sparing a glance...","They couldn't help but overthink it.","Could it be that their relationship wasn't as good as Zhang Xue claimed at all?","Looking at everyone's strange and suspicious gazes, Zhang Xue bit her lip, feeling somewhat embarrassed.","They all looked as if she had been lying.","But she hadn't lied! Chen Haoran had indeed been very enthusiastic towards her before.","He just gave her hope, only to disappoint her.","But no matter what, they were acquaintances. Was it really necessary to not even say hello when they saw each other?","Zhang Xue always felt as if someone had been speaking ill of her behind her back.","That was why Chen Haoran's attitude towards her had suddenly changed so drastically.","She bit her lip, and for some reason, Si Nian's face popped into her mind.","Because only Si Nian had had friction with her.","And she was the only one who had a relatively good relationship with Chen Haoran.","Coupled with the fact that Chen Haoran had started acting cold to her right around the time she misunderstood his relationship with Si Nian, it was really hard for her not to overthink.","...","If Chen Haoran knew that just because he hadn't noticed Zhang Xue, she had conjured up such a massive dramatic plot in her head, he would definitely look up at the sky in sheer speechlessness.","Because taking three little kids through a crowded vegetable market...","Making it out safely was already a great achievement for him.","How could he possibly notice who was standing nearby?","At this moment, even if his own mother stood in front of him, he would only be able to focus on the road ahead and look after the three kids around him.","After one trip, his back was covered in cold sweat.","Grocery shopping was truly not easy at all.","As the saying goes, practice makes perfect.","To ensure the vegetables were fresh, Eldest Child always calculated the number of people before cooking and buying groceries.","He bought just enough to finish without wasting any, which meant they had to go shopping every day.","After running around for a few days, Chen Haoran became thoroughly familiar with the vegetable market.","He also got to know the routes well.","Every day, he was the most proactive about going grocery shopping.","He didn't even go out when his friends asked him to hang out.","Zhang Xue had also asked people to look for him several times, saying she had something to talk to him about.","But by now, Chen Haoran had long lost any good impression of Zhang Xue, so naturally, he didn't plan on interacting with her.","Thus, he didn't take it to heart.","He thought these happy days would last for a long time—if not a month, then at least ten days.","However, a week later, the children's father appeared at the door.","Zhou Yueshen entered the house carrying some local specialties and gifts he had brought back from his hometown.","Chen Haoran slurped the ramen made by Eldest Child, feeling incredibly guilty.","After all, aside from helping buy groceries these past few days, he hadn't done anything else.","He was supposed to be here to take care of the kids, but in the end, he became the one being taken care of.","Not to mention, this kid's cooking skills were excellent; everything he made was delicious.","In just a few days, Chen Haoran felt like he had gained a layer of fat.","After eating his fill, he could even take Da Huang out for a walk.","What boy wouldn't like such a handsome, fierce dog?","Not to mention, Da Huang was a Tibetan Mastiff that could afford to wear LV.","Every time he walked the dog, he felt extremely proud.","Before he could react, the kids beside him dropped their chopsticks and sprinted outside.","Mom is back! Mom, Mom!","Several excited cheers rang out.","Zhou Yueshen paused his steps and said in a low, gentle voice, Your mom isn't back yet. She has to stay at home for a while longer.","Hearing this, the excited children instantly stopped in their tracks. Their smiles froze, and when they realized what he meant, their eyes widened. Mom isn't back? Only Dad came back?","Zhou Yueshen gave a slight nod. Mom still needs to stay there to keep your grandma and grandpa company for a few days. Once I finish my work here, I'll go back and pick her up.","The children were still not very happy, and Second Child was even more suspicious: Dad, did you really not have a fight with Mom and leave her in our hometown?","Yaoyao also widened her eyes. Dad is bad!","Not to mention his younger siblings, even Zhou Zedong couldn't help but cast a suspicious glance at his dad.","After all, Mom was pregnant now. Given how much Dad cared about Mom, how could he possibly let her stay in their hometown alone while he came back by himself?","Zhou Yueshen was slightly taken aback, then didn't know whether to laugh or cry. What nonsense are you talking about? Mom really needs to keep your grandma and grandpa company.","This time, it was truly because their family members were either sick or injured, so it wasn't appropriate for them to leave so soon.","The main reason was that the matters on the Si family's side hadn't fully settled down yet.","To avoid any other situations from occurring, Si Nian suggested staying a few extra days.","She asked him to come back first.","Hearing this, the children breathed a sigh of relief.","That was fine then. As long as they hadn't argued.","Otherwise, if Mom didn't come back, what would they do?","The children had just gotten a complete family and had only just begun to live happily with their family members. If Mom fought and wanted to divorce Dad, they would be doomed.","Maybe Mom would marry someone else in the future, take care of other people's children, and quickly forget about them.","Just thinking about this possibility, the children suddenly felt a wave of sorrow rise in their hearts.","Remembering something, Zhou Yueshen dug out a letter from his bag and handed it to the kids. This is a letter your mom wrote to you. It contains what she wants to say to you.","The children took it, and it was indeed their mom's handwriting.","Because Mom's handwriting was so beautiful, they could recognize it at a glance.","Mom wrote that Grandma and Grandpa were sick and needed taking care of, so she had to stay there for a while longer. If there was anything they wanted to eat or have, they could call her.","She told them not to worry about her, to study hard, and that she would be back soon.","She had written a long, flowing letter, entirely filled with words of care for the children.","The kids gathered around to read it and finally felt at ease.","Zhou Yueshen looked at his ignored self and said helplessly, Are you relieved now?","We're relieved, Dad. But you need to hurry up and work so you can bring Mom and our little sibling back quickly.","Yeah, without me, Mom will be lonely over there by herself.","Zhou Yueshen sighed and said okay.","Only then were the children satisfied.","Time passed quickly. Over the following month, Lin Sisi and Zhang Yanmei were sentenced to three and five years in prison, respectively.","The sentences were so long because the injuries sustained by the Lin family's eldest brother and Father Lin were severe, coupled with the fact that the two women had hired thugs to carry out the attack, making the circumstances particularly grave.","It really went to show that they were mother and daughter; their ways of doing things were exactly the same.","Though the mother and daughter were promptly locked up, the Si family was significantly affected by the fallout.","This was especially true because, as family members of a government cadre, repeatedly committing such scandalous acts was highly frowned upon.","The atmosphere in the family compound grew tense. People were forbidden from discussing these matters, and anyone caught gossiping would be forced to write a formal self-criticism.","There were even investigators coming and going specifically to conduct random checks on the backgrounds and identities of the family members, reviewing household registers, and so on.","Since Si Nian had moved away a long time ago, she remained unaffected by all this.","Instead, a slight hiccup occurred regarding Father Si's adoption of a child.","Because Father Si couldn't look after the adopted baby himself, he hired a nanny.","As it happened, this nanny was the older sister who had previously substituted for Liu Dongdong to take care of him.","Father Si's explanation was that he originally wanted to ask Liu Dongdong for help, but since she had found a job, she was unavailable, so she introduced her sister to help out instead.","Of course, no one really believed this excuse, but it wasn't their place to say anything.","The investigators also discovered that Liu Dongdong's sister had actually been divorced twice.","This revelation put everyone's minds at ease.","Even if Father Si really had something going on with her, marriage would be impossible.","After all, not only had she been divorced twice, but rumor had it that the reason was her inability to have children.","Back then, Zhang Cuimei was despised by her in-laws precisely because she couldn't give birth to a son.","Now, she had even been abandoned by her husband.","Therefore, everyone believed that Father Si would definitely not take a fancy to someone with such a background.","Although Si Nian wasn't living at the family compound, the incident had such a huge impact that the military arranged for representatives to visit and console her parents, checking on their injuries.","They also took the initiative to ensure the Si family cooperated with paying compensation.","This time, Father Si raised no objections.","Si Nian also heard about the Si family's situation from these visitors.","She heard that Father Si doted on the child, caring for him as if he were his own flesh and blood.","Every day after work, he would go straight home and stroll around the compound carrying the baby.","It seemed he had absolutely no intention of bothering them anymore.","Father Lin was finally discharged from the hospital. Si Nian genuinely missed her children; she had originally planned to stay for ten days or half a month at most, but a whole month had somehow slipped by.","During this time, the children called her often, telling her that their dad dropped them off at school every day. However, Brother Chen still hadn't gone home; he came over for free meals every day, insisting he wouldn't leave until she returned.","They urged her to hurry back.","Si Nian packed her things and prepared to say goodbye to her parents.","Seeing her growing belly, her parents initially wanted her to stay and give birth there before going back.","That way, they could also take care of her during her postpartum confinement.","But then they considered that their hometown was full of drama and trouble. With Zhou Yueshen not around, they could barely protect themselves, let alone their daughter.","So, they agreed to let her go back.","Si Nian took the train back this time. It was the off-season, so it wasn't crowded.","She bought a sleeper ticket and secretly headed back.","Zhou Yueshen had told her to let him know in advance so he could pick her up, but Si Nian felt that was too much trouble.","Not only would the round trip take a long time, but it would also cause unnecessary delays.","It was better to just go back on her own.","She had planned to rush home and give the children and her older man a surprise, but just as she reached the door, she ran into an uninvited guest."]},{"number":466,"title":"Chapter 466: Zhang Xue Borrows Money (Supplement 4000 Characters)","paragraphs":["The other person was holding a bag, standing at the door.","She seemed somewhat hesitant.","Si Nian almost didn't recognize her.","\"Zhang Xue?\" she called out uncertainly.","Zhang Xue was startled and quickly turned around. Seeing Si Nian standing behind her carrying some things, she was surprised. \"Sister Si Nian, you're home?\"","Si Nian frowned and asked, \"I just got back. What are you doing standing at my door? Do you need something?\"","Zhang Xue smiled enthusiastically, \"I came to bring you a gift.\"","Speaking of it, her tone carried a hint of smugness.","She handed over the luxury brand bag she was holding. \"I recently found a gig, and now I'm my own boss doing business. This is a very popular skincare cream from Hong Kong. It's a big brand. I heard you mention before that your skin gets dry here, so I wanted to give you a bottle to try.\"","\"If it works well, you can help introduce some customers to me. I'm giving it to you for free, I'm quite a loyal friend, right?\"","She had a patronizing attitude, as if Si Nian had just scored a huge bargain.","Si Nian glanced at the logo on the bag and raised an eyebrow. It really was the name of a major brand.","However, it was so obviously fake at first glance that it made her cringe, especially since she was currently using this exact cream herself.","She looked at Zhang Xue's expression, remained silent for a moment, and then said, \"You're selling this now?\"","Zhang Xue nodded, \"Yeah, I'm selling it pretty well. Everyone likes it, and it's much cheaper to buy it from me, otherwise it's very expensive, and you can't even buy it easily. This is stock sent over from Hong Kong, and I use it myself too.\"","\"No need, I'm pregnant right now and can't use skincare products casually. You should keep it for yourself.\"","Si Nian lacked interest and didn't accept it.","She knew perfectly well whether Zhang Xue liked her or not.","Suddenly bringing her a gift out of nowhere.","That could only mean she was offering unsolicited flattery for ulterior motives.","Zhang Xue's smile stiffened. She had invested quite a bit to give Si Nian such an expensive bottle of face cream. Did she know how much this bottle cost, and she actually didn't want it?","Si Nian didn't look at her ugly expression, but said lightly and distantly, \"Do you have anything else?\"","Zhang Xue's face looked awful, but thinking of something, she held it in and forced a smile, \"Sister Si Nian, actually there's one more thing. I wanted to ask for your help.\"","Si Nian paused. So she had guessed right?","She was getting a bit impatient. \"Look at my current state, how can I help you?\"","Zhang Xue said, \"Don't worry, it's not a big favor. I just want to borrow some money from you. My goods have been selling really well lately, but I'm just a bit short on capital to get more stock. It just so happens that a large batch of goods is coming from over there this week. You also know it's not easy for us to get goods from Hong Kong, so this time I want to keep a bit more to sell slowly, and when the time comes, you...\"","\"I can't help you,\" Si Nian interrupted her.","\"Why? It's not like I won't pay you back. You're so rich, it shouldn't matter to borrow a little, right?\"","Zhang Xue was a bit agitated and very uncomprehending.","They had known each other for so long, and she wasn't even willing to lend a little money?","Sure enough, what people said about the richer you are, the stingier you get was true.","Actually, she came today wanting to borrow money from Chen Haoran. After all, among the people she knew, only Chen Haoran and Si Nian were wealthy enough to help her.","It just so happened that she thought she'd visit Si Nian this time, so gritting her teeth, she even brought her a bottle of face cream.","Who knew she wouldn't give her any face at all.","It was truly embarrassing for her.","\"There's no other reason, I'm just not lending it. I advise you best not to do this...\"","Si Nian just wanted to tell her these were fake goods and advise her not to do it, but who knew Zhang Xue would react like a cat whose tail had been stepped on, exploding instantly and interrupting her excitedly.","\"If you won't lend it, then don't, is it necessary to say that? Even advising me not to do it, you all just can't stand seeing me make money, right?\"","\"Liu Nana is like this too, and so are you. You're both women, why is your jealousy so heavy?\"","Si Nian: \"...?\"","After Zhang Xue finished speaking angrily, she said coldly, \"Forget it, forget it, the worst comes to worst I just won't borrow from you, to avoid having to look at your sour faces.\"","After saying that, she turned and left with a cold face, carrying her things.","Si Nian looked up at the sky speechlessly; this person was way too sensitive.","It wasn't that she was worried about Zhang Xue failing in business and being deceived.","She was worried about the people who would be deceived by her, which was why she tried to advise Zhang Xue.","But since she wouldn't listen, Si Nian couldn't be bothered to care.","Si Nian carried her things into the house.","As soon as she entered the yard, Da Huang stood up, wagging its tail.","It barked a few times at her.","It seemed that even though she had been away for over a month, Da Huang hadn't forgotten her.","Si Nian smiled and rubbed Da Huang's dog head, patted its head, and walked inside.","She saw Chen Haoran and the children sitting in a row on the sofa watching cartoons.","Her mouth twitched.","Zhou Yuesheng had been back for so long, and Chen Haoran still hadn't left?","She thought the children were just complaining about Chen Haoran, but she didn't expect him to actually be squatting at her house?","Si Nian coughed.","The children all turned their heads at the same time.","Then they instantly exploded with excitement.","\"Mom! Mom is back!\"","Second Child jumped up high on the spot and rushed over from the sofa, half running and half jumping.","\"Eldest brother, Mom is back!\"","He ran over in a few steps and hugged Si Nian's arm, wagging his imaginary tail like a little puppy, looking up at her with sparkling eyes. \"Mom, I scored seventy points on my test a few days ago!\"","Looking at the children, Si Nian's eyes and brows unconsciously softened. Hearing this, she immediately smiled gently, \"Our Little Han is getting more and more amazing.\"","Although Zhou Zedong was also very happy, he wasn't like his younger brother. Hearing this, he glanced at his brother and suppressed his excitement to say to Si Nian, \"Mom, I took the test too.\"","\"How did Little Dong do?\"","\"Same as always, full marks,\" Zhou Zedong said.","After saying that, he lowered his head shyly, his ears turning a bit red.","Then he looked up at Si Nian again, his eyes seemingly waiting for something.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow and smiled.","\"You are all amazing! Mom feels so relieved. Mom is so tired, Little Han help me put the bag to the side.\"","Si Nian hadn't brought many things, just carrying a bag and a purse.","Mainly because she was pregnant and couldn't carry much, and she hadn't brought back the clothes she took with her.","But the things in the bag were treasures that had to be brought back.","These were some wild mushrooms she had asked people to buy while she was staying at home during this time.","It was currently mushroom foraging season over there.","They made a particularly delicious soup.","So she had gathered a bagful and brought them over to eat.","Second Child immediately started rummaging through it curiously.","Chen Haoran also leaned over, \"What is this?\"","He curiously pulled out a bag of mushrooms still covered in dirt, strangely shaped, having never seen mushrooms like this before.","Si Nian glanced at them and said, \"These are wild mountain mushrooms from our hometown. I brought them over to make soup; the soup will be very fresh.\"","\"Wow, that sounds delicious!\"","\"Mom, I'll go cook.\"","Zhou Zedong also came over, his eyes lighting up.","He hadn't cooked mushrooms before.","\"I'll go help you cook,\" Chen Haoran offered immediately. Usually, when he came here, there was no work for him to do, and he was feeling a bit guilty about it. Hearing that this was for stewing soup, he thought it must be very simple.","Although he didn't know how to cook, he had learned quite a bit following Zhou Zedong recently.","Stewing soup would be a piece of cake.","With that, he immediately took the ingredients and headed to the kitchen to help.","Si Nian was a bit tired. After sitting on the train for a day and a night, she smelled like the train all over.","She immediately went upstairs to wash up and change into clean clothes.","After taking a shower and changing clothes, Si Nian smelled a delicious aroma coming from the kitchen.","She was actually feeling a bit hungry.","She went into the kitchen to help.","Thinking that the Eldest Child had never cooked mushrooms before, she was afraid he wouldn't know how, so she had to go keep an eye on things.","After all, these were wild mushrooms. Although they were edible, they could not be eaten raw and had to be cooked thoroughly.","Otherwise, they could cause poisoning.","Just as Si Nian was about to remind them, she heard Chen Haoran's voice coming from the kitchen: \"Mmm, these mushrooms are really delicious, so smooth, tender, and juicy.\"","As he spoke, he picked up another piece with his chopsticks and put it in his mouth.","Si Nian: \"...\"","\"Sister, you're here. Your mushrooms are so fresh and delicious! Where can I buy them? I want to buy some to take back for my family to try.\"","Chen Haoran asked while still chewing on the mushrooms.","Si Nian was silent for a moment before asking, \"How long have these mushrooms been in the pot?\"","The Eldest Child was busy washing side dishes nearby. Hearing this, he looked up at Si Nian: \"Mom, are you hungry? They just went into the pot a little while ago. Wait a moment, I'll be done soon.\"","\"Little Dong, you didn't eat any, did you?\"","Si Nian looked at him with concern.","Zhou Zedong paused for a moment, then shook his head and said, \"I didn't eat any. Only Brother Chen ate some.\"","After speaking, he looked at Chen Haoran.","Chen Haoran's hand, which was about to sneak another piece, paused. He tilted his head in confusion and asked, \"What's wrong, Sister? Aren't these meant to be stewed and eaten?\"","Hearing that the Eldest Child hadn't eaten any, Si Nian breathed a sigh of relief, then said, \"They are meant to be eaten, yes, but this thing must be boiled for fifteen to twenty minutes before it can be eaten, otherwise it might cause poisoning...\"","Chen Haoran's mouth froze open, and the mushroom in his hand dropped to the floor with a splat.","\"What?\"","Thinking he had misheard, he asked again.","Si Nian patiently repeated, \"They will cause poisoning.\"","Chen Haoran looked at the Eldest Child washing vegetables nearby, then at Si Nian's pitying gaze, and was dumbfounded.","\"Why didn't you say so earlier?\"","\"I forgot.\"","Si Nian touched her nose awkwardly.","\"Mom, is the poisoning going to be very serious?\"","Zhou Zedong frowned and asked.","\"It might be, but it might not be. I'm not entirely sure either, I've just heard about it.\"","Si Nian always cooked them thoroughly at home before eating, so she hadn't experienced it herself.","She said uncertainly, \"Maybe it will just cause dizziness, nausea, hallucinations, or something like that?\"","Zhou Zedong breathed a sigh of relief. \"That's not too bad.\"","Acting like a little adult, he patted the stiff Chen Haoran: \"Brother Chen, don't worry, you won't die.\"","Chen Haoran: \"...\"","Couldn't he say something a bit more comforting?","\"Then what should I do now?\"","He only cared about this question right now.","Even if he wouldn't die, being poisoned wasn't a good thing, right?","Si Nian checked the time and said, \"It's best to go to the hospital to get it checked out. If there's really a problem, you can get treated in time.\"","Chen Haoran was speechless. In the end, he could only ride his bike to the hospital with a dark face.","There was no other way. This family consisted of the weak and the young. Could he really count on them to take him to the hospital if something happened to him?","\"Mom, once they're cooked thoroughly, they won't cause poisoning?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Stew them for a bit longer.\"","When Zhou Yueshen came back in the evening and saw that Si Nian had returned, he was completely silent for a full thirty seconds.","Si Nian stared back at him for a while, blinked, and said, \"Why aren't you saying anything? Are you not happy that I'm back?\"","Zhou Yueshen took a deep breath, looking a bit angry. \"Didn't we agree that I would go pick you up?\"","Although he had been busy recently, he had been calling her hometown every few days to check on Si Nian's situation.","Knowing that her father had been discharged from the hospital, he had planned to go pick her up.","But Si Nian said she wanted to stay a few more days.","He didn't say much about it.","As a result, the person who told him she was going to stay a few more days the day before yesterday appeared at home today.","Zhou Yueshen wasn't angry that she didn't tell him; he was just too worried about her traveling alone.","\"I figured you're so busy every day, and having to take time off to pick me up would be too much trouble. I'm just pregnant, it's not like I can't take care of myself. I came back on my own to give you a surprise.\"","She became unhappy: \"You're even giving me an attitude. People always say absence makes the heart grow fonder, but look at you.\"","After speaking, she started to feel sad.","She sat to the side, turned her body away, and gave him the cold shoulder.","Zhou Yueshen immediately regretted his attitude just now. He knew she was emotionally sensitive right now, yet his tone had been harsh.","Great, now he had really upset her.","Zhou Yueshen touched his nose and had no choice but to step forward and properly apologize.","\"Nian Nian, I didn't mean it that way. I was just worried that it wasn't safe for you to be alone.\"","Zhou Yueshen gently stroked Si Nian's hair. Under the dim yellow light, his features were indescribably soft, and in the quiet room, only his gentle, magnetic voice could be heard.","Si Nian also knew she was in the wrong. She was just worried that if she told Zhou Yueshen she wanted to come back, he would rush over to pick her up without even sleeping.","That was why she decided to come back alone.","She wasn't a child, after all.","Seeing the man giving her a way out, she immediately said, \"I just didn't want you to have to run around so much. I feel bad for you, and you're still not happy about it.\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't know whether to laugh or cry. \"I know, but you are more important to me.\"","Si Nian felt a sweet warmth in her heart, and the corners of her mouth couldn't help but turn up.","Being with a man like Zhou Yueshen, it was really hard to feel depressed.","Then she heard Zhou Yueshen say, \"I have to go back to the company in a bit. I originally planned to come back and see the children, but I didn't expect you to be back too.\"","He frowned, resting his chin on the top of Si Nian's head, not really wanting to leave.","They hadn't seen each other for a long time, and he had been thinking about her constantly.","If he hadn't been absolutely unable to get away, he wouldn't have let her stay in her hometown alone.","Zhou Yueshen never knew he was such a sentimental person.","\"It's so late, and you still have to go work?\"","Si Nian leaned against the older man's solid and gentle chest, not wanting him to go either.","When she was in her hometown, she always woke up in the middle of the night without her older man to pull up the covers for her and hold her.","Habit is a scary thing.","If her dad hadn't been in the hospital for so long, she would have wanted to come back much earlier.","Zhou Yueshen sighed softly. \"Chen Nan's son had an accident, and he went back, so I have to go hold a meeting.\"","Mentioning this, he also remembered that when Si Nian was in her hometown, she would take the children up the mountain to pick mushrooms herself, so he reminded her, \"In the future, when we eat mushrooms, remember to cook them for a longer time, understand?\"","He heard that Chen Nan's son got poisoned from eating wild mushrooms.","Apparently, he stuffed them into his mouth before they were fully cooked, which caused the accident.","He was worried Si Nian didn't know about this.","Si Nian paused and said guiltily, \"He ate them at our house.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\""]},{"number":467,"title":"Chapter 467: Joyride","paragraphs":["He didn't really want to go to the company originally, but now it seemed he had no choice but to go.","Zhou Yueshen felt a bit helpless, but he also knew that Si Nian was a food lover, so bringing back wild mushrooms from her hometown wasn't anything strange.","He just didn't expect that Chen Haoran would accidentally eat them.","However, as long as the toxicity wasn't high, it shouldn't be too serious.","Si Nian knew much more about ingredients than he did, and she wouldn't put herself at risk.","So they were definitely edible.","Then the only possible reason for Chen Haoran's poisoning was that they weren't cooked thoroughly.","After talking with Si Nian for a while and telling her not to worry, Zhou Yueshen hurried to the company.","Chen Haoran's condition indeed wasn't serious; he just suffered from vomiting and diarrhea, and recovered after resting in bed for a night.","The very next day, he ran over excitedly to ask if there were any left.","Si Nian asked him, \"Aren't you afraid of getting poisoned?\"","Chen Haoran stiffened his neck and said, \"How can we blame the mushrooms? If anyone is to blame, it's me for not cooking them properly.\"","Si Nian sighed helplessly and let him go to the kitchen to eat by himself.","Chen Haoran walked out holding a bowl of mushroom noodles, sat naturally on the threshold, spread his legs, and slurped the noodles.","He had absolutely no care for his image anymore.","Who knew what he had gone through at her place during this time.","Si Nian then remembered Zhang Xue asking her to borrow money.","She asked Chen Haoran if Zhang Xue had tried to borrow money from him.","After all, given Zhang Xue's situation, the only relatively wealthy people she knew were Si Nian herself and Chen Haoran.","Si Nian was reminding Chen Haoran not to lend money to her.","After all, Zhang Xue was selling fake goods. If something went wrong, Chen Haoran would be dragged into it too.","After hearing this, Chen Haoran also had a complicated expression. \"I was wondering why she seemed like a completely different person. She's actually selling those things? Is she that short on money?\"","Although there were some students at school trying to do business and find ways to make money right now,","and quite a few were looking for opportunistic shortcuts,","he never would have expected this from Zhang Xue.","He would occasionally bump into her. The current Zhang Xue wore heavy makeup, styled her hair, and dressed herself up to look very mature every day.","She looked completely different from the innocent and green girl he first met.","It was just that Chen Haoran thought it was normal for girls to love beauty, so he didn't pay it much attention.","He didn't expect that not only was she selling goods now, but she was also borrowing money from Si Nian.","\"Don't worry, Sis. I basically don't interact with her anymore.\"","Speaking of which, Chen Haoran felt a bit uncomfortable.","He didn't know who spread the rumor that he was pursuing Zhang Xue. It made everyone nudge him whenever they saw her.","Although he did have a good impression of Zhang Xue at first, he automatically distanced himself after discovering her interacting with other men.","They barely saw each other twice a month, so how could such news be spread?","Did Sis Si Nian think the same way, which was why she specifically reminded him?","\"Sis, you don't think I'm the type with more money than sense, do you?\"","Si Nian: \"If you want to think that way, there's nothing I can do.\"","Chen Haoran: \"?\" He knew it!","Despite saying this, Chen Haoran was still a bit worried that Zhang Xue would actually come to borrow money from him.","After all, he was a nice guy who didn't know how to refuse people. If Zhang Xue really used their past connection to borrow money, he would be in trouble.","He didn't like to meddle in other people's business; whatever Zhang Xue did was her own affair.","He also didn't want to advise her, because he was afraid that his well-intentioned advice would make Zhang Xue mistakenly think he was interested in her, which would be troublesome.","To avoid this kind of trouble, Chen Haoran specifically took a few days off.","He claimed he got food poisoning from eating mushrooms and needed a month to recover.","He wasn't exactly lying; he really was poisoned, but he recovered in one night and ate them again the very next day.","Brave Chenchen fears no difficulties.","Zhang Xue indeed went looking for him, only to hear that Chen Haoran was sick and had taken a leave of absence.","And this leave was for a whole month.","She gritted her teeth. Left with no other choice, she could only borrow from a loan shark under the coaxing of her friend.","Loan sharks were rampant in the 1980s. With an imperfect financial system, private loan sharks became the choice of many people.","And college students were one of their major targets.","Especially someone like Zhang Xue, who knew nothing and just blindly rushed forward.","She figured that since the profit from selling face cream was so high, as long as she got a batch of goods, she could pay all the money back.","Hearing that the interest would be much lower through a friend's introduction, she gritted her teeth and followed along.","Time flew by, and in the blink of an eye, the weather in Jing City grew hot.","Since they were on the first floor, there were simply too many mosquitoes.","Si Nian was a mosquito magnet; even buying mosquito repellent incense was useless.","Seeing that she got several new large mosquito bites on her arms every day, Zhou Yueshen found a pile of mugwort from who knows where, lit it, and fumigated every room in the house.","He didn't even spare the bathroom and the yard.","For this reason, Zhou Yueshen also weeded the yard.","Right now, he was leading the children to pull weeds in the yard.","These weeds grew fast, sprouting wherever there was soil. Also, under the tree, because a light was installed, the mosquitoes underneath would swarm densely every night when the light turned on.","To make matters worse, the weather was hot, and wearing long sleeves was unbearable.","Not to mention Si Nian, the children were bitten terribly.","Only Zhou Yueshen, perhaps due to his thick skin, was completely unaffected.","As soon as Chen Haoran came in and saw the family weeding to repel mosquitoes, he immediately and enthusiastically came over to help.","The Zhou household had now become his second home. Using the favor of having helped Si Nian take care of the children before, he came over to mooch meals every few days.","He didn't feel embarrassed about it at all.","Seeing Si Nian spraying mosquito repellent on the children, he leaned in as well, \"Sis, spray some on me too.\"","Si Nian rolled her eyes at him. \"Do you think you're a child? Spray it yourself.\"","After saying that, she tossed him a bottle, telling him not to slack off and hurry up to help.","Chen Haoran didn't get angry and helped clear the weeds in the yard.","Seeing that Zhou Yueshen had no intention of leaving, he felt it wasn't appropriate to stay too long.","He didn't know why, but even though this Uncle Zhou looked so young, standing in front of him brought a pressure even greater than facing his own old man.","So he usually came over when Zhou Yueshen wasn't home.","It just so happened that Zhou Yueshen was basically busy during the day.","He didn't expect to run into him by coincidence today, which made him feel a bit too embarrassed to mooch a meal.","After thinking it over, he found a way out for himself.","\"Little Han, let's go, I'll take you bike riding.\"","Zhou Zehan immediately said happily, \"Okay!\"","Only after he spoke did he realize that both his mom and dad were there. In the past, when he went bike riding with brother Chen Haoran, his parents hadn't been home.","He subconsciously looked at Si Nian's expression, gazing at her: \"Mom, can I go?\"","Figuring there was nothing much going on at home anyway, Si Nian nodded in agreement. \"Go ahead. Come back before dark, and don't play for too long, understood?\"","Second Child immediately nodded, then asked Zhou Zedong and his sister, \"Brother, do you want to go? Sister, do you want to go?\"","Zhou Zedong shook his head and refused, \"No.\"","\"If Big Brother isn't going, Yaoyao isn't going either. Yaoyao wants to keep Mom company.\"","Because Yaoyao had been separated from Si Nian for a while, she was very clingy to Si Nian these days and insisted on sleeping with her at night.","Si Nian's heart ached for the little girl, so she placed her in the middle of the bed every day.","Yaoyao was so tiny and had gotten a bit chubbier; she was soft and squishy, making her very comfortable to hug.","Si Nian gently touched the little dumpling's head and said, \"Yaoyao won't go, or she'll catch a cold from the wind later.\"","Second Child was a little disappointed, but the thought of riding a motorcycle made him happy again.","He left with Chen Haoran immediately.","Chen Haoran hoisted the little guy onto the motorcycle and drove out to cruise the streets.","The big one and the small one lost track of time while playing. By the time they realized it, it was almost dark.","Moreover, Chen Haoran had forgotten to get gas. He also hadn't expected Zhou Yueshen to be home this time, which led to the two of them running out of gas halfway and having to push the bike home.","They were as miserable on the way back as they had been happy on the way out.","Just as they reached the alley, they were blocked by several fierce-looking men.","These people were even holding sticks.","They looked like they were looking for trouble.","Both of them stopped in their tracks in unison. They looked left and right, and after confirming there was no one else around, their expressions changed.","\"Brother Chen Haoran, did you offend someone?\"","Chen Haoran was also trying hard to think, did he offend someone?","But other than being a bit of a delinquent in high school, he rarely got into fights after starting college.","Besides, this group of people looked completely unfamiliar.","He was a bit unsure at the moment.","But now wasn't the time to think about this. With so many people, even though he knew how to fight, he had a little guy with him.","Having to protect Second Child while dealing with so many people, he really had no confidence.","He took two steps back, shielding Second Child behind him.","He said seriously, \"Little Han, there's another way out if you turn right at the back. Run, quickly.\"","After speaking, he heard no response. Thinking Second Child was unwilling to leave, he added, \"Don't worry, I'll be fine. I used to be a tyrant at school...\"","He felt a bit touched. \"Although I'm very happy that you want to stay with me, I don't want anything to happen to you...\"","After saying this, he was moved by his own words and turned his head to tell the boy to hurry up and leave.","A gust of wind blew past...","There was no one behind him.","Chen Haoran: \"? Where is he?\"","Behind the corner of a wall not far away, Second Child poked his little head out, clenching his fists to cheer him on. \"Brother Chen Haoran, I'm going to find the police uncle first. Hang in there!!\"","After saying that, he ran away without a trace.","\"Go after that kid,\" one of the men over there suddenly spoke.","Chen Haoran couldn't care less about his twitching mouth and hurriedly blocked them. \"Hey, what do you want to do? You won't even let a kid off? Don't go too far. If you have a problem, come at me!\"","The men exchanged glances, their faces gloomy. \"We aren't here to look for trouble either, but if you call the police, we won't be polite.\"","\"What do you mean? Who exactly are you?\" Chen Haoran frowned.","\"I shouldn't have offended you guys, right?\"","\"You didn't offend us, but your chick did. She borrowed a thousand yuan from Brother Qiang, and now with interest, she owes us ten thousand. But she's hiding in the school and won't come out. We can't find her, and we heard her boyfriend's family is rich and runs a company, so we came to find you...\"","\"If you don't pay this money back, don't blame us for forcing you to pay.\"","Chen Haoran's face sank. \"What boyfriend? How come I don't know when I got a girlfriend?\"","Thinking of something, his expression suddenly changed. He said coldly, \"Are you talking about Zhang Xue? I'm not dating her. You've got the wrong person!\"","The men exchanged glances, thinking he was lying because he didn't want to help pay back the money. Disdain flashed in their eyes as they said, \"Do you think we're stupid? Zhang Xue's friends all said you have a good relationship with her. Just the bike you're pushing is worth more than ten thousand, right? If you cooperate and mortgage this bike to us, we'll let this matter go. Otherwise...\"","A fierce light flashed in their eyes.","Chen Haoran's face darkened. This bike was a motorcycle his dad ordered from abroad for his eighteenth birthday. Let alone ten thousand, you might not even be able to buy it for a hundred thousand.","These people really dared to dream!","\"You're ugly, but you dream beautifully. I already said I have nothing to do with Zhang Xue. Why the hell should I help her pay back the money!\"","A wave of impatience appeared on Chen Haoran's face.","He had worried that Zhang Xue would ask him to borrow money, but he didn't expect that although she didn't borrow from him, she borrowed from loan sharks.","She was truly crazy!","She was someone who got into a prestigious university after all. How could she do something so stupid?","\"Since you won't cooperate, don't blame us for forcing you to cooperate.\"","The men exchanged glances and stepped forward to rob him.","This was an alley, and it was getting a bit dark now, so there was hardly anyone walking by.","These people dared to be loan sharks, so naturally, they were extremely audacious.","They came over holding their sticks.","They weren't fools either. They could tell at a glance that Chen Haoran's motorcycle was expensive. Since it was hard to get the money back from Zhang Xue, they might as well take this bike as collateral.","Even if she didn't pay it back later, they wouldn't lose out.","Although Chen Haoran was decent at fighting, two fists ultimately couldn't match four hands. Plus, the other side had weapons, so he was soon injured.","Seeing his beloved little motorcycle about to be snatched away, Chen Haoran's eyes turned red.","He cursed, \"Fuck!\"","The other party was just about to get on the bike and ride away, looking quite happy. \"I've never ridden such a nice bike before!\"","\"Look quickly, it has gold trim. Could this be real gold?\"","\"Fuck, who exactly is this kid to be so rich?\"","\"Who cares who he is? Hurry up and drive away. Don't linger.\"","The guy examined it for a long time before realizing it was out of gas.","He cursed, \"No wonder it wouldn't start. It's out of gas.\"","\"Bro, his clothes seem to be some kind of LV, you know, that foreign luxury brand? It's super expensive. I like it.\"","Someone else eyed the clothes on Chen Haoran's body, then noticed the watch on his wrist, which clearly looked valuable. They immediately became jealous.","They stepped forward to snatch it.","Chen Haoran was furious, but having taken a few heavy blows with the sticks, he was dizzy and could barely stand.","At this moment, he could only watch helplessly as they robbed him of both his bike and his clothes. Right now, he really wished he could tear Zhang Xue into pieces.","Just as he was feeling utterly aggrieved, a crisp, childish voice came from behind.","\"Dad, it's right there. That's where Brother Chen Haoran was cornered.\"","Zhou Yueshen was just about to leave the house when he was pulled over by his son, who had sprinted all the way home.","Second Child originally intended to find a police uncle, but after running out, he realized the police station wasn't as close as his own home.","Remembering that his dad was home today, he hurried back to find him.","His dad was amazing; no one in the village ever dared to fight him.","The bad uncle who had harassed his mom before was beaten up terribly by his dad.","Now coming back and seeing Chen Haoran lying on the ground like a dead dog, his clothes half stripped and his body bloody and miserable, he was terrified.","He hurriedly ran over. \"Brother Chen Haoran! You bad guys, you're not allowed to hit Brother Chen Haoran.\"","Chen Haoran felt so incredibly touched, his eyes brimming with hot tears, but worrying that the child might get hurt by coming over, he immediately shouted loudly, \"Little Han, don't come over. It's dangerous here.\"","Second Child ran so fast that he reached them before he could even finish his sentence. Before he even had the chance to bend down and help him up, he was suddenly hoisted into the air.","\"Oh? You little brat actually dared to bring someone back with you?\"","The man looked at Second Child with a hint of amusement.","Second Child kicked his little legs in the air, staring wide-eyed right back at the man.","\"Bad guy, let me go, or I will beat you up!\"","\"Hahaha!\" The man burst into roaring laughter, completely amused.","\"Did you guys hear that? He says he is going to beat me up. Come on, come on, hit me, I will let you hit me...\"","The man leaned his face in provocatively.","The crowd of men around them joined in the laughter.","Before their laughter could even fade, Second Child threw a punch right into the face leaning toward him.","Thump—a heavy, muffled sound rang out."]},{"number":468,"title":"Chapter 468: Deceived","paragraphs":["The man's face caved in at a speed visible to the naked eye.","He froze for a full dozen seconds until some warm, wet liquid gushed out from his nose.","Only then did he let out a terrified shriek, \"Ah—!\"","Second Child was released. Seeing the man bleeding, he was terrified. He had only punched him lightly; how could there be so much blood?","He hurriedly ran to hide behind Zhou Yueshen, whispering nervously, \"Dad, I didn't mean to. He told me to hit him.\"","It was his first time hitting someone, and he was very scared, but he had just been so angry.","These bad guys had beaten Brother Chen Haoran so badly, and he had merely given the man one punch.","But Second Child hadn't expected this person to be so fragile. Why was he bleeding?","Having done such a bad thing for the first time, fear crept up on him in hindsight.","Zhou Yueshen patted his son's shoulder with his large hand and said in a deep voice, \"Don't be afraid, but you can't be so impulsive next time.\"","He knew at a glance that these people were up to no good. Second Child usually had the best relationship with Chen Haoran, so it was normal for him to be angry seeing him beaten like this.","But he hadn't expected that after hitting someone, the boy would scare himself.","Zhou Yueshen's eyes showed a hint of helplessness.","He really didn't want to get physical either. He glanced at Chen Haoran and said coldly, \"Are you going to the police station yourselves, or should I take you there?\"","The group of men hadn't yet recovered from the sight of their companion being punched bloody by a little kid when they heard this.","Their faces immediately darkened.","In their line of work, being threatened was the biggest taboo.","Other people would turn and run when they saw them.","Who would just come up and threaten to call the police like this?","Wasn't this guy an idiot?","Although the man in front of them looked tall and burly, they had the advantage in numbers and weapons in their hands, so naturally, they weren't afraid.","\"You've got some nerve. Do you know who we are? You want to call the cops? Watch me break your legs, let's see you call them then.\"","The leading man stepped forward with a stick and swung it right at Zhou Yueshen's head.","\"Dad!\" Second Child was terrified and let out a scream.","The next second, he was so shocked he lost his voice.","He saw his dad simply raise a hand and block the heavy blow of the stick.","It was as if the opponent hadn't used any force at all.","The man was also stunned, not expecting him to block it so casually. Annoyance flashed in his eyes, and he pulled hard to yank it back.","But no matter how hard he pulled, the stick remained entirely motionless in the man's grip.","Instead, he found himself sticking his butt out, kicking backward with all his might, his face flushed red.","The scene was incredibly comical.","Zhou Yueshen twisted his wrist. The man only felt a tremendous force strike his hand, causing him to let go instantly. Before he could react, the rather crude wooden stick that had been in his hands suddenly felt like an iron rod, swinging toward him with a biting gust of wind.","The man was frightened out of his wits. In the face of absolute power, he actually forgot to dodge.","The strong wind blew against his face, bringing a stinging sensation.","By the time he regained his senses, the stick he had used to strike others was pressing right against his own head.","If this blow had landed, wouldn't his skull have been split open?","The man slumped to the ground, his legs turning to jelly from the sheer terror.","The people around them were also dumbfounded.","When they realized what had happened, their expressions changed completely.","They weren't fools, and it wasn't like they had never seen a trained fighter.","Bangzi was usually the bravest and fiercest fighter among them.","Yet right now, he was so scared he was paralyzed on the ground, unable to move.","It was clear how terrifying that scene just now had been.","Even they had been scared silly. The speed at which the man swung the stick was too fast; it wasn't their kind of wild flailing, but a strike that could genuinely kill someone.","Seeing the man walking toward them, the group swallowed hard and backed away a few steps.","\"Um... let's talk this out calmly, comrade. We just wanted Chen Haoran to pay back the money.\"","\"Yeah, it's only right to pay off your debts.\"","Before they could even finish speaking, Zhou Yueshen swung the stick, knocking the few men to the ground in just two or three strikes.","Cries of pain echoed all around.","Ten or so minutes later, the police arrived and took the group away.","Chen Haoran was injured, but it wasn't serious. He had just taken a few hits from the sticks, leaving him with some superficial wounds.","These people had ultimately just been trying to scare him; they didn't actually dare to take things too far.","Si Nian sat on the sofa eating pastries and fruit, her expression unreadable.","Zhou Yueshen took Chen Haoran to the hospital, while Second Child went home.","At this moment, he was sitting as quiet as a mouse beside Si Nian, doing his homework. His eyes couldn't help but dart toward the snacks and pastries on the table. He swallowed his saliva and continued writing.","For the first time, he felt that doing homework next to his mother was a terrifying thing.","Because he had lost track of time playing with Brother Chen Haoran, got into trouble, and ended up in a fight, his mother had kept a dark face ever since hearing about it and ordered him to do his homework.","She also strictly forbade him from going out to play with Chen Haoran for the next few days.","Second Child was a little scared.","Even during dinner, he couldn't help but check Si Nian's expression.","Si Nian lifted her eyes and asked him, \"Little Han, what are you looking at me for?\"","Zhou Zehan gulped. \"Mom, are you... are you mad at me?\"","Si Nian simply put down her chopsticks and asked, \"Why would I be mad at you?\"","Zhou Zehan bit his lip. \"I... I got into a fight.\"","He had promised his mother before that he would never fight and make her angry again.","But today he was just too angry.","Si Nian said, \"Is that it?\"","A flash of confusion appeared in Second Child's eyes.","What else was there besides that?","He thought hard about it but couldn't figure it out, so he helplessly looked toward his older brother for help.","Zhou Zedong frowned and didn't speak either.","His younger brother was too playful and deserved to be taught a lesson by their mother.","So, he simply ignored him.","Second Child lost his appetite entirely and only knew how to apologize. \"Mom, I was wrong. I'll never fight again.\"","Si Nian said, \"You don't even know what you did wrong. Is there any use in apologizing like this?\"","Seeing his little eyes turn red, Si Nian's heart softened a bit. This child was always so careless, and having encountered such an incident just now, he had probably long forgotten her instructions.","Although she felt soft-hearted, Si Nian kept a stern face and said deeply, \"What did Mom say when you went out with Chen Haoran?\"","Second Child held back his tears and suddenly remembered something, his eyes widening. \"Mom told me not to play too late and to come home before dark.\"","\"Mom, I was wrong.\"","\"I won't stay out playing for so long anymore.\"","\"Mom, please don't be angry. I'll go stand in the corner right now...\"","After saying this, he put down his chopsticks and ran to the wall, standing straight against it for his punishment.","His eye sockets were red, but he tried very hard to keep his tears from falling.","Usually, when he did something wrong or slacked off, his dad would make him stand in the corner.","Seeing him like this, Si Nian found it both exasperating and amusing.","\"Finish eating before you stand.\" It would be a good way to digest his food anyway.","Si Nian didn't spoil him either. If he did something wrong, he should be punished; otherwise, he wouldn't learn his lesson.","Though she loved the children dearly, she didn't want to spoil them.","Right now, they were young enough to be obedient, but once they reached their rebellious phase, it would be easy for them to go astray.","Good habits need to be cultivated from a young age.","As for the matter with Chen Haoran, Si Nian felt quite speechless about it.","She had originally thought it was a romantic encounter, but it turned out to be a rotten one.","Zhang Xue wasn't very old, but she certainly had a lot of nerve. To think she actually dared to borrow from loan sharks.","Sure enough, she was still young and hadn't yet experienced the harsh beatings of society.","Poor Chen Haoran, getting dragged down into this mess.","Fortunately, it hadn't involved her, otherwise she absolutely would not have let Zhang Xue off the hook.","Si Nian had told Chen Haoran to call the police. For the past few days, Zhang Xue had been hiding out at school, too afraid to go outside, even wearing a mask to class.","Even Liu Nana noticed something was wrong and asked her what was going on.","Just a while ago, she had seen Zhang Xue showing off about helping people sell things and making money.","She bragged around school all day. Many people heard she was making money and wanted her to show them the ropes.","Zhang Xue had become quite famous back then.","Liu Nana, however, always felt the money came too easily and was somewhat worried.","In private, she had even advised her to be careful.","After all, pies don't just fall from the sky.","But Zhang Xue was dismissive, thinking Liu Nana was just jealous that she was making money.","Because Liu Nana's family was better off, even though the two were good friends, Zhang Xue had never lived as comfortably as Liu Nana since they were kids.","After coming to the city to study, this gap became even more obvious.","Liu Nana never lacked living expenses, unlike her, who had to call home every time to ask for money.","Her family favored boys over girls. Even though she had gotten into college, they were harsh on her, giving her only five yuan a month for living expenses, whereas Liu Nana got ten yuan.","Zhang Xue also loved to look good. After seeing the refined and beautiful college students in the city, how could she stand her own rustic appearance?","But to change that, this little bit of money was definitely not enough. So, introduced by a suitor, she met some people in business.","Now she was following them, selling things.","She made a lot of money the first time, and Zhang Xue let it go to her head.","When Liu Nana advised her, Zhang Xue naturally assumed she couldn't stand seeing her do better.","Originally, she had wanted to bring Liu Nana in to make money together.","But seeing her attitude, Zhang Xue decided not to take her along.","But Zhang Xue never expected the unexpected to happen so quickly.","She had just brought back a batch of goods when the school issued an announcement, posted right on the bulletin board at the main gate.","It stated that a group of people selling counterfeit goods had been reported. Rumor had it that many students were scammed into joining and even took out high-interest loans to buy large quantities of these fake goods. The case was now under investigation, and everyone was warned to be careful and not to buy such-and-such products...","And the photo attached was the exact product she was selling.","Their tactic was to first pretend to be students buying products from other students, marketing it as an easy way to make money so they could taste the sweetness of success. Then, they lured them with the promise of big profits into borrowing from loan sharks to buy the fake goods.","After many students bought the fakes, they realized no one was buying them at all.","This led to an inability to repay the money, being hounded by loan sharks, and even having to sell themselves to pay off debts.","Because this case involved a large number of people, the city had already organized special investigators who were currently questioning people at the school.","Zhang Xue had only sensed something was wrong after she got the goods.","The people who used to come in groups to buy face cream from her suddenly seemed to have vanished.","Once she brought in the new stock, no one came to buy from her.","Having invested thousands into it without being able to sell a single bottle, she was dumbfounded.","Those classmates who had enthusiastically wanted to make money with her were now coming back to cause trouble, demanding refunds.","Because they couldn't sell anything at all.","Some even said her products were fakes, citing the school's announcement, and were too afraid to sell them.","Only then did Zhang Xue find out about the whole thing.","A few days later, while Zhang Xue was in a state of panic, the loan sharks came knocking.","She was terrified, deeply afraid she would end up like those other college students, dragged off to sell her body to pay off the debt. So, no matter who called for her, she hid in the dorm, not daring to go out.","Fortunately, these people didn't have the guts to enter the school to look for her.","This allowed Zhang Xue to breathe a sigh of relief.","She just wanted to quickly find someone to sell the goods to, and then go home to hide for a while.","But no one wanted them even at a low resale price. People simply didn't buy this brand from her, much less spend money on it; those with money had their own channels.","Zhang Xue couldn't sit still anymore. Hearing Liu Nana's question, it was as if she finally remembered she had this good friend, and she pleaded for help, \"Nana, do you have any money? Lend me a little, I want to go home for a trip.\"","Liu Nana was stunned for a moment and asked her, \"Why are you going home?\"","Zhang Xue's eyes looked guilty as she said, \"Something happened to my parents, I want to go back and check on them.\"","Liu Nana frowned, \"Didn't you make money? Why do you need to borrow from me?\"","Not long ago, Zhang Xue was always bragging about how much money she had made.","She had also deliberately distanced herself; even a fool like Liu Nana had noticed.","She felt very uncomfortable about it, but considering they had known each other for years, she didn't say anything.","Yet now she was asking to borrow money.","Zhang Xue immediately explained, \"Isn't it because I used it all to get goods to sell? My cash flow just hasn't recovered yet. Don't worry, I'll pay you back as soon as I return.\"","Seeing her face full of anxiety, which didn't seem fake, Liu Nana found it hard to refuse and asked, \"How much do you need?\"","If her parents were really sick and she didn't help out, it really wouldn't be justifiable.","As she said this, Lu Yao, who was reading a book nearby, tilted her head and glanced at her.","Her eyes held an unreadable expression.","\"Not much, just lend me thirty. I know you have a habit of saving money...\" Zhang Xue's eyes lit up with pleasant surprise as she hurried to say.","Liu Nana's expression changed instantly. \"Thirty! Since when does a bus ticket cost that much? You're not lying to me, are you?\"","She could lend her money for a ticket, but if she was going to use it to buy more goods, Liu Nana was unwilling.","She immediately refused, \"I don't have that much!\"","Zhang Xue's face, which had just brightened, instantly turned ugly. \"Come on, Nana, we've known each other for over a decade, and you won't even lend me thirty bucks? Have you forgotten how I always took care of you when we were in school? And now you doubt me? This is really heartbreaking!\"","\"I just wanted to buy some medicine from here to take back to my parents, and you actually think of me like this!\"","Her face was full of disappointment.","At these words, Liu Nana was speechless.","It was true that back in high school, it was always Zhang Xue who hung out with her. They were inseparable and promised to be good sisters for life.","Seeing her like this now, she immediately said, \"It's not like that, Xiaoxue, don't be mad. I'll lend it to you.\"","She had actually saved a few dozen yuan, keeping it for future use.","But with Zhang Xue in such a rush, she didn't know what else to do.","\"Wait here, I'll go get the money for you.\"","Zhang Xue was finally satisfied and smiled, \"Nana, you're the one who treats me the best!\"","Lu Yao slammed her book down with a smack.","\"Liu Nana, I advise you not to lend it to her.\"","Liu Nana froze and looked at her in confusion, \"What's wrong?\"","\"Are you blind? Did you not see the bulletin board outside the school saying that many college students have been scammed recently? If I remember correctly, the pile of goods shoved onto Zhang Xue's bed is the exact fake merchandise the school warned about!\"","She originally hadn't wanted to meddle, but she hadn't expected Liu Nana to be so foolish.","To not even notice that something was wrong.","Lately, Zhang Xue had been acting like a thief. If she hadn't wanted to avoid being a busybody, she would have reported Zhang Xue a long time ago.","Zhang Xue's face paled. \"Y-you're talking nonsense! Mine isn't a fake!\"","\"You know perfectly well whether it's real or not.\"","\"Nana, do you believe her or me?\" Zhang Xue demanded angrily.","Hearing this, Liu Nana's suspicions were aroused. She asked, \"Xiaoxue, tell me the truth. Were you really scammed?\"","No wonder she had been holed up in the dorm lately, refusing to go out whenever Nana asked, and even wearing a mask to class.","She had assumed Zhang Xue was just feeling under the weather.","Now, Nana's expression turned grim.","Realizing she had been exposed, Zhang Xue panicked. Flustered and angry, she snapped, \"That's a load of nonsense! You just don't want to lend me the money. Why make up so many excuses?\"","With that, she spun around in a huff, yanked the door open, and prepared to storm out.","To her surprise, several police officers were standing right outside. Seeing her emerge, one of them spoke up, \"Hello, we are the police. Is Zhang Xue here? Please come with us...\""]},{"number":469,"title":"Chapter 469: Going into Labor","paragraphs":["Chen Haoran followed behind, pointing angrily at Zhang Xue and shouting loudly, \"Officer, it's her!\"","The male police officer, who was not much older than Chen Haoran, was speechless.","Chen Haoran was furious. He never expected Zhang Xue to be so shameless as to tell outsiders that they were dating.","He had lost all his dignity that evening.","Looking back, he wanted to kill her.","So when Si Nian suggested that he better call the police, he didn't hesitate at all and immediately reported it.","Seeing Chen Haoran with his face still wrapped in gauze, Zhang Xue was instantly stunned.","Liu Nana also ran over. Seeing the police, she was equally confused and asked, \"What exactly is going on? Even if she bought fake goods, it shouldn't warrant the police showing up at her door, right?\"","After all, they were childhood friends, and her eyes were full of worry at this moment.","They had played together since childhood, made wishes together, and worked hard together.","They had finally gone through all the hardships to reach their dream university.","But it was only their first year, and so many things had already happened.","Liu Nana stood frozen, not quite understanding why things had turned out this way.","\"Buying fake goods? So you borrowed from loan sharks just to buy those skincare products?\"","The police officers immediately exchanged a look. When they received Chen Haoran's report, they only heard him say that a student had borrowed from loan sharks and lied about him being her boyfriend, causing him to be harassed by the loan sharks.","So they only thought this girl had borrowed money from loan sharks, not knowing the reason why.","But hearing Liu Nana mention it now, they immediately connected it to the recent string of cases involving female students being scammed into buying fake goods.","The culprit had not yet been found.","They didn't expect that someone from a prestigious school like Jingda University could also be scammed.","It was truly surprising.","Zhang Xue's face flushed bright red, but in front of Chen Haoran, she still refused to admit that she had done something so stupid. She argued, \"I wasn't scammed. The person who introduced me is my friend. We've known each other for almost a year; he wouldn't lie to me.\"","When Zhang Xue was feeling emotionally vulnerable because of Chen Haoran, it was this person who stepped up to comfort and help her.","He liked her unconditionally.","If it weren't for the fact that his family background and looks were not as good as Chen Haoran's, perhaps they would have been together by now.","Actually, Zhang Xue had a good impression of him, but having seen someone better, she felt he was lacking in comparison and could never quite get past that hurdle in her heart.","Because of this, she felt very guilty towards that boy and refused to believe he would deceive her.","Even if it was a scam, it must have been someone else who tricked him.","There was no way he would deceive her!","The police officers exchanged glances, having never seen a victim defend their scammer before. They said solemnly, \"All the students scammed in this case were tricked by their own friends.\"","\"The perpetrators approach you as friends, gain your trust over time, and then slowly lure you into these schemes. Most of these girls unknowingly showed signs of needing money. In other words, you were targeted by this group from the very beginning.\"","Zhang Xue's face instantly turned deathly pale.","It was true. During that time, in order to show off in front of Chen Haoran, she spent a lot of money and overdrew her funds. She didn't even have money to eat at the cafeteria and often went hungry or ate very little.","That was when he noticed her, and they slowly got to know each other.","Hearing this, Chen Haoran was utterly speechless.","He couldn't care less why Zhang Xue was scammed.","All he knew was that he had been beaten up for no reason by a group of people who not only tried to steal his motorcycle but also almost stripped him of his clothes.","\"Let's go down to the station. I want to see how you explain this.\"","Ultimately, Zhang Xue was taken away for investigation.","Because she had dragged Chen Haoran into this, she was required to compensate him and apologize.","Chen Haoran didn't intend to send her to jail over this, but she had to learn her lesson. He had made it clear before; aside from a brief initial attraction and helping her out, he had never done anything to cause misunderstandings. They had barely interacted in the past six months, yet who knew Zhang Xue would go around spouting such nonsense.","If he didn't force her to give up, he might be dragged down again in the future.","Besides, Zhang Xue's outcome was already miserable enough.","Soon, the news of Zhang Xue's arrest became widely known.","Those who had been coaxed into spending money because of her couldn't get their money back. Once they confirmed Zhang Xue had been peddling fake goods, their parents all rushed to report her for fraud.","Due to the severity of the situation, the school ordered Zhang Xue to pay compensation, apologize, and recorded a major demerit on her file.","This meant she might not graduate smoothly, and even if she did, her future prospects would be severely impacted, to the point where she might not even find a job.","However, this wasn't the worst part. Because the matter had blown up, Zhang Xue's family found out and scolded her harshly, telling her she was better off dead.","They stopped answering her phone calls.","As a student unable to produce the money, she had lost all face at school and lived in constant fear of being taken away by loan sharks.","Under such extreme mental pressure and dual blows, Zhang Xue actually chose to commit suicide.","Although she was saved, she was sent home by the school due to her unstable emotional state.","It seemed as though the incident had suddenly come to an end.","People at school stopped bringing it up, and Liu Nana became withdrawn.","When Chen Haoran heard the news, he also felt a lot of psychological pressure.","Although he believed he hadn't done anything wrong, he still felt regret.","He regretted getting involved with Zhang Xue in the first place, because if it weren't for him, she might not have ended up like this.","By the time Si Nian heard about the incident, quite some time had passed.","She remained silent for a long time after hearing it, not expecting things to turn out this way.","In the future, there would actually be many students like Zhang Xue who went astray due to vanity.","But Si Nian didn't feel sorry for Zhang Xue, because when she had tried to warn her earlier, Zhang Xue thought she was just jealous of her success.","One could only say that pitiful people often have their own hateful traits.","Si Nian stopped paying attention to the matter.","Chen Haoran, on the other hand, became much more mature and steady, and no longer liked to flirt with girls.","It seemed the incident had cast a considerable shadow over him, turning the prodigal son around.","Given his track record of getting poisoned by wild mushrooms one moment and getting beaten up the next.","Chen Nan planned to send him to learn some martial arts from Zhou Yueshen.","He knew that Zhou Yueshen used to be able to take down a whole regiment in the army with just his fists.","He was practically invincible throughout the army.","Hearing that his son also practiced martial arts every day, he immediately introduced his own son to him.","It just so happened that Zhou Yueshen's wife was about to give birth, so he gave him some time off, doing him a favor.","Zhou Yueshen didn't have any objections. Second Child was practicing alone without a companion anyway, so it was fine if he came.","In front of him, Chen Haoran was like a mouse meeting a cat, meek and submissive.","He had seen it with his own eyes that day; this Uncle Zhou had easily sent that group of armed thugs flying with just a few moves.","At that time, he was completely dumbfounded. As someone who previously thought he was a fierce fighter, witnessing the other party's skills made him realize his own martial arts were merely amateurish.","Just thinking back on it was enough to make him blush.","So much so that his form of address for Si Nian went from Sister to Auntie and finally to Master's Wife.","He even became Second Child's junior martial brother.","Hey, hey, hey, can you still hold on? It's only been ten minutes and you already can't hold your squat. Don't make me look down on you.","Early this morning, Chen Haoran came over to exercise and was told by Zhou Yueshen to practice the horse stance in the courtyard.","After squatting for about ten minutes, this guy's legs were shaking like a sieve.","Si Nian sat on a chair to the side cracking melon seeds like it was none of her business, casually supervising the training of the adult and the child.","This had already become her favorite way to pass the time during her pregnancy.","Just watching Chen Haoran, a big 1.8-meter-tall man, keeping his head down and squatting in a horse stance next to Second Child to train his lower body foundation every day, she couldn't help but find it hilarious.","Today was Sunday, and on Sundays, his and Second Child's training would be doubled.","Because Second Child was still young, he couldn't be over-trained for fear it would stunt his growth, so his training intensity was not very high.","But Chen Haoran was different. He was already an adult, so naturally, he had to be trained ruthlessly. Otherwise, with a training intensity like Second Child's, it probably wouldn't yield any results for three to five years.","Yaoyao, the Little Tuanzi, was quietly and obediently playing with the small shovel and chili seeds Si Nian had bought for her yesterday.","They didn't actually learn much at her kindergarten usually; it was mostly just for play. Occasionally, the teacher would assign a task, and this time the task was for the parents to help them plant vegetables. If they successfully grew them, they would get a little red flower.","Yaoyao told Si Nian about this as soon as she got home. In her limited memories, she knew that both her eldest and second brothers really liked little red flowers, and they could get little red flowers both at school and at home.","Little red flowers could be exchanged for gifts.","However, Yaoyao had only ever received little red flowers at home, never from a teacher.","So as soon as she got home, she pulled Si Nian along, wanting to plant little vegetables.","She had planted vegetables with Si Nian before, so she still had some impression of how to do it.","Right now, she was busy sorting her seeds, occasionally looking up at the adult and child in the courtyard before retracting her gaze to continue her work.","Early this morning, Zhou Yueshen had been sent out by Si Nian to dig up some mud for their daughter.","Chen Haoran held it in, his face flushed red.","He had never exercised growing up, and he was actually quite a restless person with little patience.","Running was alright, but making him do push-ups and horse stances was asking for his life.","He wanted to stand up and take a rest, but he was afraid Si Nian would tattle on him.","He knew very well that this woman had been treating him as her source of entertainment these past few days.","As soon as Master Zhou returned, she would eagerly go over and tattle, saying he was slacking off.","It left him trembling with fear.","Right now, he naturally knew that Si Nian was just waiting to see him get taught a lesson.","He didn't know what he had done to offend her.","Chen Haoran gritted his teeth, holding on entirely out of sheer stubbornness.","The stubbornness of absolutely not letting Si Nian enjoy a good show!","Si Nian truly hadn't expected Chen Haoran to actually persevere. By the time the session ended, he hadn't slacked off at all. When it was over, he immediately collapsed onto the ground, gasping for air, tired as a dog.","She yawned in disappointment, stood up, and just as she was about to go into the house to get something to eat, she heard Yaoyao speak up in confusion, Mommy, pants are wet.","She froze for a moment, glanced down, and immediately stopped in her tracks, her expression turning slightly stiff.","Was she about to give birth?","But wasn't it not yet her due date?","Since getting pregnant, Si Nian hadn't felt any major discomfort.","The only major change was feeling that her belly had grown bigger.","Her physical constitution was good, and with Zhou Yueshen taking care of her, her pregnancy had been a breeze.","So she didn't have a very real sense of it.","This was the first time she stood stiffly in place for a long time, until even Chen Haoran noticed something was wrong.","What are you standing there blankly for? Holy crap! What happened?","Before he could finish his sentence, he saw that Si Nian's pants were wet.","He was startled and rushed over, ignoring his weak legs.","He wasn't a fool; he knew that in this situation, Si Nian was definitely about to give birth.","He heard her due date was next week, so his dad had even specially given Master Zhou time off.","The price was taking him on as an apprentice.","What do we do? What do we do? I don't know how, I don't know how to deliver a baby...","Before Si Nian could even speak, Chen Haoran had already lost his head.","Black lines formed on Si Nian's forehead. Who wants you to deliver my baby? Take me to the hospital.","She frowned. Zhou Yueshen hadn't been gone for long, and there was no soil nearby, so she didn't know where he had gone to dig.","She couldn't wait for him right now.","Even though she was the one who sent him out, not having her man by her side at such an important moment actually made her feel a bit upset and aggrieved.","We have a car at home. The car keys are on the table in the house. You should know how to drive, right?","Xiao Han, go inside and help Mommy get her bag. Everything we need is in there.","Si Nian admired herself; at this moment, her mind was quite calm. Even though she had a due date, Zhou Yueshen had packed everything in advance out of fear of unexpected situations.","Just in case of an emergency.","Now it was finally coming in handy.","Second Child stood there blankly for a long time before realizing that his mother was about to give birth to a younger brother or sister. He was stunned for a moment before snapping back to reality and sprinting into the house.","He nearly tripped over the threshold.","Si Nian turned to look at her daughter, who was staring at her in bewilderment, still clutching her little shovel. Yaoyao, you and your second brother stay home and be good. Later, when Daddy comes back, tell him we went to the hospital and have him go to the hospital to find Mommy, okay?","Your eldest brother isn't home, so you and your second brother shouldn't run around.","Zhou Zedong had carried his schoolbag and gone to the library to read early in the morning.","He basically spent all his days off immersed in the library.","Because it wasn't very convenient to borrow books and bring them home to read.","Si Nian hadn't expected that at this critical moment, the two most reliable males in the family would both be absent.","Yaoyao nodded hurriedly, gripping her little shovel tightly. Mommy, I'll wait for Daddy!","Second Child had already run back carrying Si Nian's bag. Chen Haoran supported Si Nian as she got into the car. As soon as Si Nian bent over, she could feel discomfort and a cramping pain.","However, Chen Haoran was panicking. He usually loved riding motorcycles and rarely drove cars; he had only driven his dad's car out of curiosity when he was younger.","His driving skills were not good at all.","Now that he was in the car, he was completely bewildered and didn't know what to do.","Si Nian hissed in pain several times. Seeing him sitting there blankly, too nervous to tell anything apart.","He was just a reckless kid after all. She gritted her teeth and said, Alright, get out. I'll drive.","It was only a five-minute drive from here.","She had never been in a car driven by Chen Haoran, and to be honest, Si Nian was a bit worried.","To prevent any accidents, she hurriedly supported herself and got out of the car.","Sure enough, at crucial moments, she could only rely on herself.","Chen Haoran got out looking crestfallen and worried to death. What do we do, what do we do? Can you drive? Are you in a lot of pain...","His incessant chattering was too annoying. Si Nian scolded, Shut up and get in the car quickly.","She could feel her own condition; it wasn't too intense yet, and she knew she could still hold on, but if they delayed any further, she wouldn't be sure if she could make it.","Si Nian had secretly driven Zhou Yueshen's car before, so naturally, she knew how to drive.","After all, she was someone who had lived through two lifetimes; her mentality was far more mature than that of her peers.","She got into the car, stepped on the clutch, and shifted gears in one seamless motion, leaving Chen Haoran completely dumbfounded in the passenger seat.","He had never imagined that a woman who was about to go into labor could drive with such calm precision.","The car quickly arrived at the hospital entrance.","Perhaps he was simply too nervous, but Chen Haoran fell flat on his face as he stumbled out of the car.","When he turned around, he saw Si Nian turn off the ignition and brace herself as she stepped out, staring at him with a look of utter disdain.","Chen Haoran's face flushed a deep, embarrassed red.","He then watched as Si Nian found a doctor and calmly announced that she was going into labor. The doctor took one quick look and urgently ordered, Her water broke! Hurry, bring a gurney over!","As Si Nian was helped onto the bed, she didn't forget to hand her bag to the doctor, mentioning that her money and identification were inside so they could help process her admission paperwork.","Clearly, she had realized that a guy like Chen Haoran was completely useless to rely on.","Meanwhile, Zhou Yueshen had just returned home carrying a woven sack of dirt when the two children rushed over, grabbing him and dragging him back out toward the hospital.","They shouted in a panic, Dad, hurry to the hospital and check on Mom! Mom is having the baby!","Zhou Yueshen's hand trembled, and the heavy sack dropped to the ground with a thud."]},{"number":470,"title":"Chapter 470: The father and son are all about ignoring each other.","paragraphs":["As soon as the car stopped at the hospital entrance, Zhou Yueshen scooped up the two children and quickly strode into the hospital.","Just as he found the direction of the delivery room, he collided head-on with Chen Haoran.","Chen Haoran was knocked flying. Since his legs were already a bit weak, he ended up sitting on the ground with two streams of blood running down his nose.","Ouch, which blind... Master Zhou! Master, you're here! Boohoo, you're finally here! Hurry, come with me, the master's wife is waiting for you!","He didn't dare call Si Nian Sister in front of Zhou Yueshen. Seeing him, it was as if he had instantly found his pillar of support. He casually wiped the blood from his nose and hurriedly led him to the delivery room.","Chen Haoran was still chattering away, There is not a single sound from inside, I am scared to death!","Zhou Yueshen's eyes turned cold as he shot him a glance. Chen Haoran finally realized he shouldn't be saying such inauspicious things and quickly covered his mouth.","Zhou Yueshen didn't speak. He just stared motionlessly at the three red words In Surgery. If it weren't for the excessive force and stiffness in the way he held his son's and daughter's hands, probably no one would have noticed anything unusual about him.","It was not easy for women to give birth. In the past, in the countryside, many women ruined their health due to difficult labor.","Therefore, during Si Nian's pregnancy, Zhou Yueshen had always taken extremely careful care of her.","He tried his best to keep her from suffering. Fortunately, Si Nian had a good constitution. Aside from being emotionally sensitive during her pregnancy, no accidents had occurred.","But now that she was about to give birth, a profound sense of reality finally hit him. His heart couldn't stop pounding wildly, not out of excitement or joy, but a certain kind of fear.","A fear he dared not think too deeply about. Zhou Yueshen closed his eyes and took a deep breath, just to keep his body from being so stiff.","He let go of the two children's hands, took a big stride forward, and was about to go in.","Chen Haoran hurriedly reminded him, You can't go in, Master. The doctor said you can't go in.","Zhou Yueshen paused. He tried hard to listen for any sound inside, but it was terrifyingly quiet.","In the past, when a sister-in-law in their military unit gave birth, she screamed for a whole day and night until she finally lost her voice and almost didn't make it.","He was very worried. Was Si Nian in so much pain that she didn't even have the strength to cry out?","Meanwhile, inside the delivery room, Si Nian was half-lying on the hospital bed. To be honest, she was dumbfounded. She had just entered the delivery room and lain down for a short while when the doctor said the baby was coming and told her to push.","It hurt a bit, but not enough to make her scream. Si Nian had originally come in expecting immense pain and had fully prepared herself mentally.","But she never expected to be the lucky one.","She had heard that nine out of ten childbirths were agonizingly painful.","Yet unexpectedly, she turned out to be the exception who didn't experience that extreme pain.","While Si Nian was lost in thought, she heard the doctor say loudly, I see the head, push harder!","She immediately snapped back to reality and quickly pushed. A tearing pain almost made her cry out, and then she heard the doctor's voice, He is out, he is out! Congratulations, it is a boy!","Si Nian had long prepared herself mentally; she would love the baby whether it was a boy or a girl.","Hearing this, she immediately took a moment to look up. The baby was being held by the doctor, so she couldn't see clearly. She still had the strength to ask, Doctor, why isn't he crying?","After ensuring the baby's health was good, the doctor patted the baby twice. The baby cried a few times symbolically and then quieted down again in a very good state. The doctor breathed a sigh of relief and smiled at Si Nian, It is fine, he cried. It is normal, although his crying was a bit perfunctory. He is still whimpering after crying, very cute. I haven't delivered such a chubby and cute little baby in many years.","Si Nian's mouth twitched. She thought to herself that after being smacked, how could the baby not whimper?","However, hearing the cry put her mind at ease.","Most newborns were wrinkled and looked like little old men, but Si Nian's baby had very elastic skin, which was truly surprising.","Right after giving birth, she heard the nurse say, Comrade Si, your husband has rushed over. He really has good luck. He just got here, and you gave birth. Do you need me to call him in?","Hearing this, Si Nian was displeased. What do you mean he has good luck? It is not like he is the one giving birth.","At such a crucial moment as her giving birth, that older man only arrived after she was done.","Although she hadn't expected to give birth so quickly either, Si Nian still felt a bit wronged.","Ever since she got pregnant, she had constantly dreamed of the childbirth scene.","She had always imagined her man staying right by her side, but imagination was just a beautiful ideal.","Si Nian firmly refused to mention the fact that she was the one who had sent him out to dig mud.","She deliberately wanted to let her older man panic outside for a while, to make him anxious.","Just as she told the nurse to ignore him, the delivery room door was suddenly pushed open.","Zhou Yueshen had good ears. He had heard the baby's two cries. He walked in with a terrible expression on his face, Nian...","Before he could finish his sentence, Zhou Yueshen met the eyes of Si Nian, who was half-leaning on the bed telling the nurse not to tell him and let him worry for a bit.","...This little rascal.","Meeting the man's deep gaze, Si Nian suddenly felt guilty.","Ouch, I suddenly feel so uncomfortable. I need to lie down to get better.","She held her forehead and lay down, pretending to sleep.","Footsteps sounded behind her. Zhou Yueshen pulled her hand and held it tightly in his, saying, Don't be angry, it is my fault. I shouldn't have gone out.","Although Zhou Yueshen also didn't expect it to go so smoothly, he still felt extremely guilty for not being by his wife's side at this critical moment.","Causing her to harbor resentment.","Si Nian had originally wanted to pretend to sleep, but hearing these words, she suddenly felt aggrieved. She said in a hoarse voice, You weren't home, I was scared to death.","Zhou Yueshen said, I know, it is all my fault. I will definitely stay home and accompany you from now on.","Si Nian saw that his head was covered in sweat and his clothes were soaked.","She also knew that the man must have rushed over in a great hurry. He hadn't even changed his shoes and was still wearing his slippers from home.","Seeing that his arms holding hers were tense, with veins popping out.","She knew that the man had been frightened too.","A man as mature and steady as him could also lose control because of her.","Si Nian felt genuinely warm inside. Perhaps she really loved this man so much that she thought everything about him was good and couldn't bear to blame him.","Even when she was angry, she would immediately become happy as soon as he admitted his mistake. She never knew she was such an easily satisfied person.","Or perhaps, when you meet the right person, you really do become hopelessly romantic.","She had seen too much falsehood and had never held any expectations for love.","Her mindset had always been that if a relationship works, fine; if not, forget it. She was determined never to put love first.","But Zhou Yueshen broke her prejudice against this relationship.","He let her know that there really was someone who would always dote on her and give to her without expecting anything in return.","At this moment, Si Nian didn't know what the future would be like or if he would change.","But she only knew that she was truly happy right now.","Cherish the present!","Si Nian blinked hard and reached out her arms toward Zhou Yueshen.","She said in a muffled voice, I want a hug.","The tension in Zhou Yueshen's brow relaxed. He immediately bent down and pulled her into his arms, his thin lips lightly pecking hers. Be good, it is all over now.","The nurse behind them, holding the baby and having tried multiple times to get the father to take a look at his child: ......","Si Nian was moved to a different ward. As coincidence would have it, there were a lot of people giving birth today, and the hospital had no empty private rooms left, so they placed her in a double room.","Zhou Yueshen carried Si Nian to the ward. Leaning against the man's chest, she felt an unprecedented sense of comfort and relaxation.","After this extreme relaxation, a wave of exhaustion washed over her.","Zhou Yueshen laid her down on the bed, pulled up the covers, and gently patted her back with his large hand.","Si Nian blinked, let out a yawn, and asked the man, Where are Yaoyao and Little Han?","Zhou Yueshen replied in a low voice, They just went to fetch some hot water with Chen Haoran.","Just as he spoke, Chen Haoran came over carrying the hot water, accompanied by the two children.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at them and whispered, Keep your voices down.","The adult and the two little ones immediately slowed their pace and walked in carefully.","Seeing Si Nian tilting her head to look at them, not yet asleep, the two children couldn't hold back anymore. They immediately ran over, clinging to the edge of the bed and looking at her. Mom, Mom, are you okay?","Mom, does it hurt?","Before the two children could even finish speaking, their little eyes turned red.","They had been terrified just now, deeply worried that something bad might happen to Si Nian.","Seeing her lying safely on the bed now, they felt both happy and lingering fear.","Si Nian smiled and rubbed the two children's heads. Mom is fine, it doesn't hurt anymore.","Mom, don't have any more babies for Dad in the future. Having babies is so scary.","When the two children were waiting outside earlier, they hadn't heard Si Nian's voice, but they had heard the miserable screams of a woman in another delivery room.","The screams were absolutely heart-wrenching.","Just now, when they passed by on their way back from fetching hot water, that woman was still screaming.","The two children were completely stunned with fear.","It was Chen Haoran who hurriedly used the excuse of fetching hot water to lead the two children away.","He was afraid they would be traumatized.","Hearing this, Si Nian didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at his son, withdrew his gaze, and looked down at Si Nian, adjusting her blanket. Alright, don't disturb your mother. She is very tired and needs to rest.","Okay then. Mom, rest quickly, we will stay right here with you.","Second Child mimicked his father's actions, reaching out his little hand to gently pat Si Nian, looking as though he was trying to coax her to sleep.","Yaoyao stayed close to her second brother, sitting obediently by the side.","Chen Haoran stood to the side, looking at the father and children gathered around the bed coaxing Si Nian to sleep, feeling that something wasn't quite right.","After pausing for a good while, he finally realized what it was and asked with wide eyes, Where is the baby?","At this exclamation, the adult and the two little ones all turned to look at him.","Their expressions were even more bewildered than his. Right, where was the baby?","Dad, where is our little brother or sister?","Dad, little brother or sister?","The two children looked at their father.","Zhou Yueshen's expression stiffened.","Fortunately, a nurse came over carrying the baby at that moment, letting out an exaggerated sigh. What kind of father are you, not even wanting your own child.","Zhou Yueshen stiffly stood up straight and looked at the baby the nurse had brought over.","The baby had been washed clean and wrapped in a small blanket by the nurse, currently sleeping soundly with closed eyes.","This father and son duo seemed to specialize in completely ignoring each other.","The nurse handed the baby to him and said, I'm still busy. You family members need to take good care of the baby yourselves, don't go forgetting the child again.","Although the nurse was teasing, she was actually quite envious of Si Nian.","Having worked here for five or six years, she had seen plenty of families who excitedly swarmed around the newborn baby, while the woman who had just given birth was left without a single word of concern.","Seeing a man who cared only about his woman to the point of completely forgetting about the baby was truly a rare sight for her.","Zhou Yueshen stiffly took the baby. Seeing his awkwardness, the nurse wanted to laugh. You already have so many children, how come you don't even know how to hold a baby?","After saying that, she carefully taught Zhou Yueshen how to hold the infant.","Once the nurse left, Second Child, who had been curiously watching and learning from the side, immediately stood on his tiptoes and reached out his hands. Dad, let me hold him.","Zhou Yueshen frowned at the sight of him. You are still too small, you can't hold him.","Second Child immediately replied, I know how to hold him, I just learned how.","Zhou Yueshen's movements were stiff; the little bundle in his arms was simply too fragile. There was no way he would dare hand the baby over to his careless son.","So he said in a deep voice, Wait until your little brother is a bit older, then you can hold him.","Second Child was very disappointed. He pouted, looked up at his little brother's sweetly sleeping face, then tilted his head to look at his mother on the bed, before twisting around and running back.","Then you hold little brother yourself, I'm going to stay with Mom.","Zhou Yueshen...","Dad, I want to see little brother. Yaoyao struggled on her tiptoes but still couldn't see, anxiously tugging at Zhou Yueshen's pant leg.","Zhou Yueshen snapped back to reality and crouched down to let his daughter take a look.","Although the baby had just been born, he was round and chubby, his little mouth pursed tight, looking incredibly adorable.","This was his own child.","Zhou Yueshen had originally thought he would never have a biological child in his lifetime.","He used to think it didn't matter at all.","He hadn't even understood why some families would argue and fight just to have a child, treating it as an absolute necessity.","But at this moment, looking at his son's adorable sleeping face, his hardened heart completely melted into a puddle.","Perhaps this was the significance of a blood connection.","The hospital bed wasn't large, so Zhou Yueshen had Chen Haoran go find a crib. He laid the baby down to sleep, then sat back down beside Si Nian, gazing blankly at her sleeping face.","Si Nian's cheeks were flushed, and she looked like she was sleeping very comfortably.","The baby beside her slept in the exact same manner.","His eyes were gentle. Just as he reached out to brush the stray hairs from her forehead, another pregnant woman was wheeled in.","Immediately, a cacophony of chattering voices rang out.","It was unbearably noisy.","Zhou Yueshen frowned and glanced over, seeing the woman lying on the hospital bed looking completely exhausted, her face deathly pale.","Meanwhile, the middle-aged woman who had followed her in was still chattering and scolding, You useless thing, another daughter. You've already given birth to three daughters, what use are you?","A man standing nearby was smoking a cigarette and said gloomily, Mom, stop talking.","His complexion was clearly not very good either.","The two children, who had been leaning against the edge of the bed and were about to fall asleep, were woken up by the noise.","They rubbed their eyes in confusion and looked over.","But they saw that their father had already stood up, his deep voice interrupting the group's chatter as he said, Please keep your voices down, do not disturb my wife's rest.","After speaking, his gaze fell on the man puffing away on his cigarette. Please take your smoking outside.","The man was already irritated because his wife had just given birth to yet another daughter.","Hearing this, his face immediately darkened. Who the hell do you think you are? What gives you the right to tell me what to do? I'll smoke wherever I damn well please!","Before he could even finish his sentence, Zhou Yueshen strode forward and grabbed him by the collar.","Before the man could even react, he was lifted up and thrown right out of the ward.","He was burned by his cigarette butt and finally snapped back to reality. He looked up angrily, only to meet a pair of ruthless, icy eyes.","Can't you understand human speech?","The man's face instantly flushed red, and he couldn't utter a single word.","Before he could even open his mouth, his mother rushed out in a flurry. \"Oh, you shameless thing! What gives you the right to lecture my son? So what if his smoking bothers you? If you have such a big problem with it, move to another room yourself! It's not like your family owns this hospital ward!\""]},{"number":471,"title":"Chapter 471: Sinister Premonition","paragraphs":["She pointed at Zhou Yueshen's nose and cursed loudly.","She didn't care at all that this was a hospital; this whole family lacked basic manners.","The son was smoking, and his mother was making an unbearable racket at the top of her lungs.","It really was true that birds of a feather flock together.","Inside the room, Si Nian, who hadn't been asleep for long, was woken up by the noise.","She frowned and asked, \"What's going on? Why is it so loud?\"","Chen Haoran whispered, \"Master got into an argument with another family. That man was smoking, and his mother came in making a huge fuss. Master couldn't stand it and told him to smoke outside, but he didn't get physical...\"","Si Nian said with a headache, \"Why can't we have any peace even in the hospital?\"","To be honest, hospital conditions nowadays were not very good.","This kind of central hospital was even worse. Everyone rushed here, and it was packed to capacity every single day.","Many people were crammed seven or eight to a ward.","When going through the admission procedures, she had made sure to ask the doctor in advance to assign her a room with as few people as possible.","She was just worried it would be too noisy.","She hadn't expected it to still be this noisy with only two patients in the room.","Not to mention the noise, the other party was swaggering around smoking right in the ward.","This seriously crossed Si Nian's bottom line.","It wasn't that she couldn't accept men smoking, but to smoke so brazenly in a place where smoking was prohibited, completely disregarding the feelings of a pregnant woman—how was that any different from being human trash?","As if sensing something, Zhou Yueshen glanced toward the room and met Si Nian's eyes.","Seeing that she had been woken up, his expression turned even uglier.","He couldn't be bothered to argue with women, especially unreasonable ones like her.","He simply reached out, grabbed the man by the collar, and strode out.","If he could solve it with action, he absolutely wouldn't waste breath talking.","The man was terrified, thinking Zhou Yueshen was actually going to beat him up, and begged for mercy the entire way.","He wasn't stupid. How could his frail, 1.7-meter frame compare to the tall, muscular man in front of him?","Yet, his mother didn't think the situation was big enough.","She followed along, cursing the whole time.","It was as if she was afraid the man wouldn't get beaten up.","Zhou Yueshen's face was cold and dark. People looked at them along the way, but no one dared to stop him.","The man watched helplessly as the crowd parted to make way for them.","\"...\"","He was dragged and tossed outside the security room at the entrance.","The two security guards, who were sipping tea and cracking sunflower seeds, didn't even notice him until Zhou Yueshen knocked on the door.","They shuddered in fright, hurriedly standing up to ask what was going on.","Zhou Yueshen pointed at the pathetic-looking man on the ground and said, \"He was smoking in the hospital ward and making a loud racket, disturbing my wife's rest.\"","The two guards froze for a moment, then came to their senses. Standing up straight, they said angrily, \"Nonsense! How can anyone smoke in a hospital ward?\"","\"Didn't you see the hospital's no-smoking signs, kid? Get over here!\"","The two guards pulled the dumbfounded man over.","The woman, who had followed them panting and still cursing Zhou Yueshen, saw her son being dragged away again. Forgetting about giving Zhou Yueshen trouble, she ran over to them.","She pointed at the two guards and started cursing at them.","Zhou Yueshen couldn't be bothered with her. After returning to the hospital, he asked to change wards.","However, they informed him that there were no vacant wards left.","Hearing that his wife had a natural delivery, they told him she could be discharged after a day or two of observation.","They asked him to bear with it, as it was peak time at the hospital, and having a double room was already very good.","Zhou Yueshen frowned and returned to the ward. Seeing Si Nian looking at him eagerly, he restrained the coldness in his eyes, stepped forward, and touched her forehead. \"Sorry for waking you up.\"","Si Nian shook her head. \"It's not your fault. How did it go?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"I handed him over to security to deal with. If he makes noise again, I won't hold back.\"","\"Can't we switch to a private room, Master?\" Chen Haoran asked.","Zhou Yueshen shook his head.","Si Nian also guessed that Zhou Yueshen must have asked and found out there were no rooms left.","If there were, the hospital would have arranged it for her when she first went through the admission procedures.","After all, it wasn't like she didn't have money.","Chen Haoran felt awkward; no one paid him any attention.","\"Mom, when can we go home? I don't want you to stay here.\"","Second Child said unhappily.","Si Nian smiled and said, \"We should be able to go home tomorrow or the day after. Just bear with it for a bit.\"","Second Child nodded at this, then eagerly ran over to look at his little brother. \"Mom, little brother is a lazy little pig. The noise didn't even wake him up.\"","Mom had been woken up, but his little brother was still sleeping.","Si Nian tilted her head to look at the baby, still feeling a bit surreal.","She had actually given birth to a child. Although it was a son and not the daughter she had imagined, Si Nian was still quite happy.","She said to Zhou Yueshen, \"Bring him over for me to see.\"","Zhou Yueshen carefully picked up the little milk dumpling, not daring to use too much force. He slowed his steps and held his breath as he placed the baby next to Si Nian.","Looking at her son, who wasn't crying or fussing but just focused on sleeping, Si Nian found it amusing.","\"He really is sleeping soundly. That's good.\"","She reached out and poked her son's little cheek. The baby smacked his lips and even nuzzled against her hand.","Si Nian widened her eyes, a wave of pleasant surprise washing over her. She immediately looked up at Zhou Yueshen. \"Did you see that? He nuzzled me.\"","\"Like a little kitten.\"","Zhou Yueshen didn't know whether to laugh or cry. What kind of description was that?","He didn't know that Si Nian used to have a cat. Their son's movement was just like her little cat's, incredibly cute.","What Si Nian feared most was a noisy child, but from birth until now, he had only given a couple of symbolic cries and had been very quiet ever since.","It seemed this child was as steady as his father.","That was really nice.","The family looked warmly at the baby, making the woman to the side seem exceptionally lonely.","Only when she heard them mention a son did she helplessly turn her head to glance at the family, asking, \"Comrade, did you give birth to a son?\"","Si Nian tilted her head to look at her. The woman looked very pathetic, her face deathly pale, and she was currently staring at Si Nian with envy.","Hearing her tone, Si Nian guessed that this woman must have given birth to a daughter.","Otherwise, she wouldn't have asked like that out of the blue.","She nodded slightly and said yes.","Sure enough, the other party became even more envious.","She sighed, \"I really envy you. You already have sons and you gave birth to another son. Do you have any secret recipe over there?\"","She assumed that Second Child and Yaoyao were both Si Nian's children. Although Si Nian looked very young, she had heard them call her Mom.","Si Nian fell silent for a moment before saying, \"Sorry, I don't.\"","She couldn't change the patriarchal mindset of this era that favored boys over girls, but she wasn't going to offer any comfort or advice either.","Respecting other people's destinies was Si Nian's rule of survival.","The woman sighed again. \"My husband went overboard just now. I hope you aren't angry and won't hold it against him. He was just upset inside. Who can blame him, since I gave birth to three girls in a row?\"","\"Before the birth, we hired a spirit medium to read my fortune. We spent a lot of money and I drank a lot of medicine. They said this pregnancy would definitely be a son, which is why my mother-in-law was willing to spend money to put me in a good ward, just waiting for me to give birth to a son. Who knew it would be another daughter...\"","Perhaps because no one had talked to her and it had been building up inside, she started talking to Si Nian as if she were talking to herself, pouring out her grievances.","Si Nian could hear the disgust in her tone.","If even she despised it herself, what right did she have to blame her husband and mother-in-law?","She said indifferently, \"I didn't ask.\"","When others were perfectly happy, bringing up such negative things—could she really expect them to sympathize with her?","It wasn't that Si Nian couldn't listen, but she simply disliked hearing others pour out their grievances.","Not to mention she didn't even know the woman.","Spreading negative energy when someone else was in a good mood.","Did she want others to be just as unhappy as she was?","And she even had the nerve to say not to blame her husband.","She had just given birth and was already being despised by her mother-in-law, while her husband smoked. She herself felt it was wrong, yet she told others not to blame him?","There was truly nothing pitiable about a person like that.","The words the woman was about to say came to an abrupt halt, and her expression turned somewhat awkward.","...","Inside the library.","Zhou Zedong was reading a book, but for some reason, he started to feel restless.","Usually, on his days off, he could stay cooped up in the library all day.","But today, he just couldn't focus on the words.","He kept feeling as if something was about to happen.","Even Xiao Bowen, who was beside him, noticed his absent-mindedness.","He asked in confusion, \"Zhou Zedong, what's wrong with you?\"","Zhou Zedong frowned, simply closed his book, and said, \"I don't want to read anymore. I'm going home. You can read by yourself.\"","Because Xiao Bowen also liked coming to the library, the two of them frequently ran into each other here.","After all, they had helped celebrate his birthday before, so Zhou Zedong wasn't as cold to Xiao Bowen as he used to be. Seeing him come over and sit next to him, he just quietly read his book without disturbing him.","So he let his little actions slide.","This situation had lasted for a long time, so both of them had tacitly accepted each other's presence.","Every weekend, Xiao Bowen would come over early in the morning to save the best seat for him.","When he saw him arrive, he would start reading.","Normally, Zhou Zedong could not be disturbed when he was reading.","But today, he had been frowning the whole time, and after only a few hours, he was already leaving.","Xiao Bowen couldn't read anymore either. He quickly closed his book, stood up, and said, \"I want to go too. I want to go to your house and play with Little Han.\"","After he finished speaking, he looked at Zhou Zedong nervously, afraid of being rejected.","Actually, every time he came over on the weekend and saw Zhou Zedong going home, he really wanted to tell him that he wanted to go over too.","But he could never bring himself to say it.","Ever since Zhou Zedong had a talk with his grandmother last time, he was somehow a little afraid of him.","Afraid that he would get angry.","That's right, he had intentionally guided Zhou Zedong and the others to his house to celebrate his birthday, wanting him to discover that they were actually brothers.","He didn't want to force Zhou Zedong and the others to come back; he just wanted to have siblings.","Even just one would be fine. He didn't want to be alone all the time; it was too lonely.","But he hadn't expected Zhou Zedong to hate his grandmother so much that he wouldn't even let her interact with them anymore.","Now Xiao Bowen didn't have an excuse to go play with them either.","He could only use coming to the library as an excuse to be with him.","Only in this way could he feel a little less lonely.","Usually, they could sit there all day.","Today, since Zhou Zedong was leaving, he couldn't sit still either.","Zhou Zedong paused and glanced at him.","\"Suit yourself.\"","Xiao Bowen was immediately pleasantly surprised. He hurriedly stuffed his notebook into his backpack and trotted after him.","Just as they left, a sneaky-looking woman walked in.","Her face didn't look too good.","Just as she was about to leave, she suddenly stepped on something on the ground.","She looked down and saw a photograph.","The woman bent down to pick it up and saw a familiar face.","She paused, and then her expression turned extremely ugly."]},{"number":472,"title":"Chapter 472: Lied","paragraphs":["......","Zhou Zedong usually walked over, as it only took about ten minutes.","But the sun was blazing hot today. As soon as he stepped out of the library, a wave of stifling heat rushed over him, making his already restless mood even more irritable.","He got on the bus, and Xiao Bowen followed him up. Having never taken a bus before, Xiao Bowen stood there looking a bit dazed.","Normally, his grandmother would have someone pick him up and drop him off for school, and even in the past when he lived with his mother, he never had to squeeze onto a public bus.","Zhou Zedong walked over and sat down, only to notice that the other boy was still standing there blankly, not knowing what to do.","He paused, then got up, walked back, and paid the fare for him, saying, In the future, if you want to take the bus, you need to prepare small change or coins first.","Xiao Bowen was just starting to feel touched when he heard him add, You have to pay me back.","Xiao Bowen: ......","When Zhou Zedong returned home, he found the front door wide open, yet the house was completely silent.","Feeling a bit confused, he quickly ran inside.","Da Huang was still sleeping under the shade of the tree, but the courtyard was empty. There was only the lounge chair left at the door that hadn't been moved inside, along with some mud from a snakeskin bag spilled on the ground, and the foam boxes his sister had prepared for planting vegetables.","The entire courtyard was so quiet that only his breathing could be heard.","He ran around inside and out but didn't see anyone. Just then, a passerby saw him and asked in surprise, Oh my, Little Dong, you're still at home? I heard your younger brother and sister say your mother is about to give birth. Didn't you go with them?","Zhou Zedong froze for a moment, and his expression drastically changed. My mom is giving birth?","Yes, only your younger brother and sister were home at the time. Later, your dad seemed to have come back and took them over. I thought you had gone there long ago.","The person sighed repeatedly.","Zhou Zedong didn't have time to say more and hurriedly rushed in the direction of the hospital. After running just a few steps, he thought of something, turned around, and ran back into the house to grab the baby supplies his dad had bought in advance, just in case.","As expected, his parents must have left in a great hurry, leaving behind all the formula and clothes.","Zhou Zedong packed everything into bags and hurried toward the hospital carrying two large bags of supplies.","Xiao Bowen followed behind with a bewildered look on his face. What, Teacher Si was about to have a baby?","The last time he saw Teacher Si was on his birthday, and he hadn't noticed at all.","It hadn't been that long, and she was already giving birth?","Didn't that mean they were going to have another younger brother or sister?","He was both surprised and envious as he watched Zhou Zedong run off without looking back, and he hurried to follow and see for himself.","However, Xiao Bowen had barely taken two steps when someone grabbed him.","He jumped in fright and was instinctively about to scream when he heard a familiar voice ring out, Bowen, it's Mom. It's Mom!","Xiao Bowen froze for a second, then abruptly looked up at the person.","Seeing Fang Hui standing behind him, looking even thinner than before and somewhat disheveled, dressed very poorly, his eyes instantly widened. Mom?","Fang Hui didn't have time to catch up with her son. In truth, she had been back for a while, but due to threats from the Xiao family, she hadn't dared to look for him.","But he was her own flesh and blood after all. Having been separated for so long, how could Fang Hui not miss him?","So during this time, she had been secretly following her son. But she never expected to see him reading together with Zhou Zedong today.","The two seemed to be on very good terms.","Fang Hui's face had darkened with anger at the time, because in her view, if it weren't for Si Nian being so petty and vindictive, she wouldn't have been pushed out by her company as a scapegoat over that reporting incident and sent to prison.","Now that she had finally managed to come back, she held onto a sliver of hope in her heart.","After all, her son had already been acknowledged and taken back by the Xiao family.","Although the Xiao family was powerful and influential, their lineage was thin. There were originally only two brothers; the eldest died young, and the second was unmarried. The only heir left was her son.","Therefore, Fang Hui felt that it didn't matter if the Xiao family disliked her now. As long as she waited for her son to grow up and gain authority, she would eventually be able to enter their doors.","But she hadn't expected to run into her son being so friendly with the son of the woman she hated the most.","It left a bitter taste in her mouth. Her former desire to control her son instantly surged up, and she wished she could step forward and teach him a good lesson, forbidding him from playing with Zhou Zedong.","However, before she could go over and make trouble, the boy suddenly had to leave in a hurry.","Fang Hui accidentally picked up a photo that had fallen out of her son's book, catching sight of a familiar man's face.","However, her attention was quickly drawn to the man beside him.","It was truly because that person's face looked far too much like Zhou Zedong's.","They were practically carved from the same mold.","Making it hard for her to ignore even if she wanted to.","Recalling how that man had inexplicably sent her to the Yunnan-Guizhou-Sichuan region and even rented a house for her right next door to the Zhou family, she couldn't help but overthink things.","So she hurriedly followed them.","Looking at her son's pleasantly surprised expression, she gripped his shoulders and asked, Bowen, tell Mom, does Zhou Zedong have some sort of relationship with the Xiao family?","Fang Hui's mind was in turmoil. Although she had interacted with that man, she had only heard that he had a brother who died young. Hearing that the brother had never married, she had always felt secretly pleased with herself.","That way, as long as she married into the family, her son would be the sole heir to the Xiao family.","But she had forgotten that even though his brother hadn't married, it was entirely possible that he had a child.","If the Xiao family had another child, her son's future status would definitely be affected.","Not to mention, the other party would be his eldest brother's child.","Even if her son was acknowledged first, according to seniority, he would still have to step back in line.","She was so worried that she didn't even notice the smile disappearing from her son's face. Seeing him stay silent, she anxiously urged, Why aren't you speaking? Quickly tell Mom, do you know something?","Xiao Bowen's face looked awful. Looking at Fang Hui's frantic expression, he couldn't help but recall the times when he lived with her, when she wouldn't let him do anything except study.","Just thinking about his past life made him feel a wave of suffocation.","He didn't quite understand why his mother was asking this, but he knew very well that he absolutely could not tell her.","He had a feeling that if he told her, he and Zhou Zedong would never be able to be friends again.","His mother didn't like Zhou Zedong and his family, and she might forbid him from playing with them in the future.","He pursed his lips and said, I don't know.","Fang Hui's expression turned even uglier.","If it had just been a suspicion at first, now she was almost certain.","Because her son had actually lied to her!","......","Zhou Zedong was in such a panic at this moment that he almost got hit by a car, completely failing to notice that Xiao Bowen hadn't followed him.","He rushed to the hospital in a hurry, standing on his tiptoes at the front desk to ask which room Si Nian was in.","Seeing a child in such a panicked state, the receptionist thought something terrible had happened to his family. Telling him not to panic, she checked for him and then said, Si Nian, right? She's in Room 301.","As soon as her voice fell, Zhou Zedong had already turned around and sprinted off without looking back.","Meanwhile, on the third floor.","The loud wailing of a baby was so noisy that Si Nian couldn't sleep at all.","It wasn't her baby crying, but the other woman's baby.","It seemed to be hungry, but the woman looked malnourished. After nursing for a bit, her milk ran out.","The hungry baby wailed loudly.","She cried her heart out. At first, the woman tried to comfort her, but then grew annoyed and simply ignored her altogether.","The crying woke up the son lying nearby.","He didn't cry either, just blinked his eyes and looked at Si Nian.","His little mouth smacked. Even though he wasn't crying, Si Nian could just feel that he was hungry.","She felt a bit awkward. Looking at the people sitting around her, she still couldn't bring herself to pull open her clothes and feed the baby like the other woman had just done.","So she tugged at the older man beside her.","Zhou Yueshen was also frowning at the noise of the crying baby.","Tugged by Si Nian, he turned to look at her and asked gently, Niannian, what's wrong? Are you hungry?","Si Nian shook her head. I'm not hungry, but your son is.","She pointed at the little bean staring at her eagerly. Surprisingly, this child didn't cry when he was hungry. She recalled that when he was just born, he only cried out twice, then slept all the way until being woken up just now.","Zhou Yueshen stayed silent for a second, then looked at his wife again.","Si Nian shot him a look.","Zhou Yueshen finally snapped out of it. He stood up and said, Xiao Chen, take Yaoyao, Little Han, and the others to get something to eat. Thanks for your hard work.","Chen Haoran was still sitting there looking bewildered. He still hadn't fully processed the reality of the situation.","The reality that a child had actually been born.","Just three hours ago, he was miserably doing horse stance squats in the Zhou family courtyard.","Three hours later, there was a newborn baby beside them.","And he was the one who had rushed them here.","Now that he came to his senses, he realized it was already noon.","He quickly patted his head, stood up, and took the two children to buy food.","Once they left, Zhou Yueshen closed the door and stepped forward to help her.","Si Nian had never breastfed before, but the baby seemed to know how to do it naturally. As soon as she opened her clothes, he nuzzled his head in and began nursing with smacking sounds.","Si Nian felt a bit strange. Seeing Zhou Yueshen staring at her blankly, she blushed and turned her body away.","You go outside too.","Zhou Yueshen rubbed his nose and walked out.","The other baby smelled the milk and cried even louder.","Si Nian had a headache from the noise and said to the woman beside her, Why don't you get her some formula?","The woman said dryly, Formula? How could we afford such a precious thing.","They had rushed over today, and by the time they arrived, there were no normal wards left.","She had delivered her first two children at home. Because her mother-in-law thought this one was a son, she had specially brought her to the hospital. Even though it was a double ward, she hadn't complained about the cost.","Who knew it would turn out to be a girl.","At this point, let alone formula, it was questionable whether they would even keep the child.","If she had known it was a girl, she wouldn't have planned to keep her.","The woman's face was ashen.","She would rather this child had never been born, let alone buy formula for her.","Her existence would only make it harder for her to hold her head up in her in-laws' family.","Her future days would only be harder.","Si Nian was momentarily speechless.","At this moment, someone knocked on the ward door, and Zhou Zedong walked in, sweating profusely and carrying things.","Mom, are you okay?","He had run over. Because it was hard to catch a cab at noon, and carrying so many things, his hands were red.","He headed straight for the ward. Seeing Si Nian lying on the bed, he immediately ran over with a tense little face.","Little Dong? Why are you here too?","Si Nian was a bit surprised to see him. The eldest boy usually went to the library and wouldn't come home until six in the evening.","Why did he come back so early today?","I went home and heard the grandma next door say you were going into labor, so I hurried over.","Zhou Zedong's gaze fell on the little milk dumpling in Si Nian's arms. The little guy was round and chubby. Having eaten his fill, he closed his eyes and fell asleep again, looking incredibly cute and pretty.","He stared blankly for a moment.","Is this... a little sister?","Si Nian burst out laughing. Not a sister, a little brother.","Zhou Zedong: ......","Si Nian looked at the things he was carrying. They were all items Zhou Yueshen had bought in advance—clothes, blankets, shoes, some small toys, formula, and baby bottles. They had everything.","But they were all pink.","Because she had come so hurriedly, she hadn't brought them, and Zhou Yueshen probably forgot too.","She didn't expect the eldest boy to remember to bring these things over at a time like this.","He was even more reliable than his father.","Seeing his red, chafed hands, Si Nian felt a pang of heartache and quickly told him to set them aside.","The woman saw them carrying so many things, which obviously weren't cheap, and her eyes grew red with envy.","The formula seemed as if it were free, carried in several large cans.","Seeing that Si Nian's husband wasn't around, she looked at her crying daughter and couldn't help but say, Comrade, could you lend me a little bit of that formula?"]},{"number":473,"title":"Chapter 473: Want to Open Up","paragraphs":["Si Nian: \"?\"","Just a moment ago, when told to go prepare some, she had claimed she couldn't afford formula.","If she couldn't afford it, how could she afford to borrow it?","Zhou Zedong wiped his sweat. Hearing the voice, he turned his head to glance at the other party.","Only then did he notice a woman lying on the adjacent bed. Next to her, a baby was crying weakly.","He hadn't even noticed them earlier.","He looked at the woman, then at Si Nian, and asked, \"Mom, do you know each other?\"","Si Nian withdrew her gaze and chuckled at her son's question. \"No, I don't.\"","Zhou Zedong's hand paused as he reached for the formula, and he pulled it back. \"Then why is she trying to borrow formula from you?\"","He had brought the formula for his younger sis... no, younger brother. The books he read said that mothers might not have milk right after giving birth, so to prevent the baby from going hungry, formula needed to be prepared in advance.","Because he was worried the baby would be hungry, he made sure to bring everything over.","His little brother hadn't even had any yet, so how could he let someone else drink it?","Zhou Zedong's words made the woman flush with embarrassment, her face turning beet red.","She immediately defended herself, \"It's just because I didn't prepare any. I won't borrow much, just enough for today. It's not a lot. We're all in the same ward, isn't it good to help each other out? At worst, I'll just buy some and return it to you later.\"","She felt that since they were both women, helping each other out was no big deal.","Besides, she wasn't asking for much. If her daughter wasn't being so noisy, she wouldn't have wanted to borrow from anyone in the first place.","Si Nian nodded in agreement. \"You're right.\"","The woman's eyes lit up. \"Really?\"","Si Nian gave a slight nod and said to her son, \"Little Dong, just give her a whole can.\"","The woman's eyes widened in pleasant surprise. \"T-this is too much, isn't it? Oh my, you're too kind...\"","Such high-quality formula, she really hit the jackpot.","She never expected this woman to be so generous.","Zhou Zedong didn't say another word. He took out a can of formula, walked over, and handed it to the woman.","\"Thank you, little one. You and your mom are such good people. May good people be blessed with peace.\"","Zhou Zedong looked at her calmly. \"You're welcome, auntie. This can is eight yuan. Just give me the money, and it will save you a trip out to buy it.\"","The woman's excitedly outstretched hand froze, and her voice pitched up. \"What? Eight yuan?\"","Zhou Zedong looked at her strangely. \"What else? Didn't you say you wanted to borrow it? We're giving it to you, so you just need to pay for it directly. That way, you won't have to go out of your way to buy it tomorrow. Did you actually expect us to give it to you for free?\"","The woman's expression turned ugly. \"I don't even need that much.\"","Zhou Zedong showed a look of disdain. \"Even a child knows that free lunches don't fall from the sky. Why would you think we'd just give it to you for free?\"","The woman's face immediately turned pale and green.","It was bad enough being lectured, but to be lectured by a child!","Flying into a humiliated rage, she snapped, \"Then just lend me a little bit.\"","\"You still have to pay for a little bit. If you can't afford it, I can give you fifty cents' worth.\"","\"What? Fifty cents for just a little bit? Why don't you go rob someone! Unbelievable. This is the first time I've met such stingy people. It's one thing for the adult to be cheap, but even the child is a miser.\"","She cursed and grumbled.","Zhou Zedong's little face darkened. \"Yes, we are stingy, but we are only stingy to strangers. Unlike you, who is even stingy to your own child.\"","After he finished speaking, he turned back to look at Si Nian and asked, \"Mom, don't you agree? She's so stingy. She won't even spend fifty cents to buy formula for her own child, yet she calls us stingy. She's so weird.\"","Si Nian's eyes curved into a smile, her previously annoyed mood instantly lifting. \"You're right. What right does someone who is stingy to her own child have to call others stingy?\"","\"Just ignore her.\"","Even if she were willing to give her some formula for the baby now.","What about tomorrow? And the day after?","She could help once, but she couldn't help for a lifetime.","So there was no need to invite trouble.","If the other party wanted formula, fine, then pay up.","Zhou Yueshen had bought the best formula available; a single can cost eight yuan.","She wasn't a fool. Why would she give it to a stranger she didn't know and would likely never see again?","Zhou Zedong carried the formula back.","Zhou Yueshen walked in carrying food. He saw that Si Nian had already finished feeding the little one and was talking to their eldest son.","\"Mom, what do you want to eat? I'll make it for you tonight.\"","Si Nian: \"I want to eat something spicy. My mouth feels tasteless, it's so uncomfortable.\"","Zhou Zedong furrowed his little brows and said, \"But you can't eat spicy food right after giving birth.\"","Si Nian said with a miserable face, \"Mom understands the logic, but my mouth just can't resist.\"","Zhou Zedong comforted her, \"Mom, it's okay. You can eat some in a few days when you feel better, but you can only have a little bit.\"","He had read in the library that a mother could eat it forty-eight hours after giving birth, but only a tiny bit. If she was breastfeeding, she definitely couldn't eat it, as it would affect the baby.","But since Mom wanted to eat it, the little brother would just have to drink formula.","Besides, they had bought so much formula, it shouldn't go to waste.","If Mom couldn't eat delicious food, she would be unhappy.","Zhou Yueshen: \"......\"","Why did he feel like someone had stolen his lines?","He had just bought food and returned, thinking that Si Nian definitely wouldn't like the hospital food.","It was too bland.","But the doctor had instructed that she couldn't eat spicy or stimulating food right after giving birth.","She could only eat light, mild dishes.","He had already figured out how to comfort Si Nian.","But before he could even utter his prepared speech, his son stole his thunder.","Furthermore, he had planned to cook for her himself tomorrow.","But his son's cooking skills were currently even better than his own...","Si Nian would definitely prefer eating what their son made.","Zhou Yueshen: \".......\"","He coughed softly, stepped forward, and said, \"Nian Nian, eat something.\"","Si Nian looked at the plain, watery food and sure enough, put on a miserable expression.","Zhou Yueshen was just about to speak when he heard his son say, \"Mom, this doesn't taste as good as what I make.\"","Si Nian immediately agreed, \"Of course, our Little Dong's cooking skills are good enough to be a head chef.\"","Her attention was diverted, and she ate while smiling, but stopped after just a few bites.","Zhou Yueshen coaxed her into taking a few more bites. Seeing that she really didn't want any more, he quickly scarfed down the rest himself and threw the containers in the trash.","The next day, after a check-up confirmed everything was fine, Si Nian was discharged from the hospital.","The woman in the adjacent bed watched as she happily carried her son away, and a wave of sorrow welled up in her heart.","Ever since her husband and mother-in-law left, they hadn't returned.","She secretly turned her head away to wipe her tears, only to feel her daughter's tiny hand grasp hers.","Her daughter was wrinkled and not pretty at all. She had seen Si Nian's son; he was fair and chubby, a clear sign that the mother was well-nourished during pregnancy.","But no matter how good he was, he belonged to someone else. Yesterday, because the pregnant woman in the same ward had given birth to a son, she had been full of resentment toward her own daughter, not even wanting to spare her a second glance.","Yet now, in her most difficult moment, the only one by her side was this little girl.","Even though she hadn't wanted her, the baby was completely oblivious, and looking up at her, actually smiled.","A deep wave of guilt suddenly washed over the woman, and overcome with sorrow, she pulled her daughter into her arms and burst into tears."]},{"number":474,"title":"Chapter 474: My Brother Is Not Stinky","paragraphs":["...","When Si Nian returned home, Zhou Zedong went straight into the kitchen.","Because from last night until now, she hadn't eaten anything.","When Zhou Yueshen walked into the kitchen to help, his son was already flipping through a cookbook for pregnant women.","Zhou Yueshen: \".......\"","He walked out, wanting to help change the baby's diaper, only to find the Second Child holding a diaper and gesturing at his son.","Zhou Yueshen: \"......\"","He walked around in a circle and returned to the room, thinking that Si Nian definitely wanted to change into clean clothes.","But as soon as he entered, he saw his daughter sticking her bottom out, half her body inside the wardrobe rummaging around, asking in a milky voice, \"Mommy, is it this one?\"","Si Nian smiled and said, \"Yes, that's the one.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"......\"","This home felt so unfamiliar.","...","That night, Si Nian suffered from clogged milk ducts.","Little Tuanzi puffed out his cheeks and sucked hard but couldn't get anything out. He was about to fall asleep but opened his eyes again, looking at his mother blankly, not understanding why the milk was gone.","Si Nian felt pain from the sucking and frowned. She had been leaking milk earlier, so her supply was plentiful.","But she hadn't expected to get a clogged duct. Now she felt uncomfortably engorged, and it was even starting to hurt.","The doctor had mentioned this condition, but there were too many instructions at the time, and she couldn't remember clearly.","She could only look for Zhou Yueshen and ask him what to do.","Zhou Yueshen's voice was a bit dry: \"It needs to be unclogged. It's okay, I'll help you.\"","Si Nian was still a bit suspicious. \"Can you do it?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"?......\"","Sure enough, listening to the doctor was the right choice. After a night of hard work from Zhou Yueshen, their son finally got to eat.","Zhou Yueshen also found his sense of presence in this home.","The next day, he and Si Nian named the baby. Because they weren't sure of the gender beforehand, they hadn't chosen a name in advance.","Now, after a family discussion, the name was finalized.","It was Zhou Zeyi.","Choosing one and staying true to the end.","Logically speaking, the nickname should have been Third Brother.","However, because of their sworn brother Little Jiang Jiu, they changed it to Little Four.","Si Nian also loved the child Jiang Jiu very much, so she had no objections.","Second Child, however, was acting smug.","Because he had always been a younger brother to others, he felt it wasn't very impressive.","Although Jiang Jiu was Third Brother, he was the same age as him after all, and he was someone else's child. Although he often considered himself an older brother, he still couldn't show off his authority like a real older brother.","Now that he had his own younger brother, he was thrilled.","Imitating how his older brother used to take care of them, he wiped Little Four's bottom and dressed him every day.","Yaoyao, on the other hand, liked to give her younger brother all sorts of cute little items, like small hair clips, little rubber bands, bows, and such.","They were all her favorite things.","In the blink of an eye, about ten days passed. Because Si Nian was doing her postpartum confinement, she couldn't bathe or wash her hair. Although she loved cleanliness and found it unbearable, she also knew that catching a cold during confinement would be bad for her. For the sake of her future health, being a little dirty wasn't something she couldn't endure.","But while she could accept it herself, she didn't want Zhou Yueshen to have to accept it. It was fine if she was dirty on her own, but it made her uncomfortable to have her man lying next to her, holding a dirty her.","Because she hadn't bathed, coupled with the hot weather and the inability to use a fan, Si Nian felt she reeked of milk and sweat. Her hair, which was thick to begin with, was greasy and knotted.","She had never been so unkempt.","Moreover, because she had too much milk, she would often get clogged ducts, which was incredibly painful.","She would wake up from the pain in the middle of the night, look at her man, and whimper. Upon hearing her voice, Zhou Yueshen would get up to help massage and unclog her ducts, and Si Nian would groan softly before falling back asleep.","After unclogging the milk, he had to change his son's diaper and coax him to sleep.","Only after taking good care of the mother and son would he lie down, getting up early the next morning to prepare formula for his son.","After all, making Si Nian get up so early every day to breastfeed was quite a cruel thing for her.","By the time Si Nian woke up, their son had already eaten and drank his fill and was sleeping sweetly.","Over the past half month, the baby had barely cried.","As soon as he let out a peep, the several males in the family would immediately run over.","They would coax him back to happiness in no time.","As a result, Si Nian didn't feel the hardships of raising a child at all.","In the past, to win over the children, she had racked her brains to make delicious food for them, trying her best to bring them back to a normal life.","Now, it could be considered that she was getting her reward.","The whole family was happy.","The unhappy one was Xiao Bowen. Ever since his mother returned, she would keep an eye on him from time to time and seek him out in private.","It made him very afraid, and he didn't even dare to go play at the Zhou family's house anymore.","Another unhappy one was Jiang Jiu. Someone was trying to matchmake for his father, and he didn't want a stranger to be his mother. Lately, he had been keeping a close eye on his dad, terrified that he would be snatched away.","Watching Zhou Zedong and his brother rush home without stopping the moment class ended, saying they wanted to help their mother take care of their younger brother.","The two children sighed at the same time.","Then, they exchanged a glance.","\"Why are you sighing?\" Jiang Jiu asked.","\"Could it be that you also want to go play at Second Brother's house?\"","Xiao Bowen blushed, \"I don't want to go at all.\"","\"I want to go,\" Jiang Jiu said honestly. \"I want to go see what the little brother looks like. Second Brother said that from now on, I am Little Four's older brother.\"","Hearing this, Xiao Bowen disagreed, \"You aren't his relative, why are you his older brother?\"","His tone was full of sourness.","Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan were his older brothers.","So wasn't their younger brother his younger brother too?","Jiang Jiu said, \"Because we made a sworn brotherhood like in the Peach Garden.\"","After speaking, he saw the person running far away without waiting for him to hesitate. After thinking it over, he hurriedly chased after him, \"Wait for me, Second Brother, I'll go with you to see the little brother.\"","Seeing him run off, Xiao Bowen pursed his lips and said, \"It's not safe for you to go alone, I'll accompany you!\"","After saying that, regardless of whether the other heard it or not, he chased after him.","After Zhou Zedong returned home, he went into the kitchen to cook.","Second Child went over to change his younger brother's diaper.","Jiang Jiu and Xiao Bowen brought their heads close, staring curiously at Zhou Zeyi.","Jiang Jiu: \"Wow, he's so chubby.\"","Xiao Bowen wrinkled his nose: \"He's so stinky.\"","Zhou Zehan immediately said, \"My little brother is not stinky! Is your poop fragrant?\"","He said that, but he was obviously smoked out so much that he couldn't even keep his eyes open.","Wrinkling his little nose, he changed the diaper while saying to his older brother who had just come out of the kitchen, \"Brother, little brother really is a bit stinky today.\"","Zhou Zedong glanced at him and said, \"You used to be even stinkier than him.\"","\"You used to just poop directly in your pants.\"","Jiang Jiu & Xiao Bowen simultaneously distanced themselves from Zhou Zehan.","Zhou Zehan: \"...\"","Si Nian sat on the sofa, watching the several children circling around her son, not knowing whether to laugh or cry.","Thinking of something, she asked, \"Little Jiu, Bowen, did you tell your families that you were coming here?\"","The two guys who had been staring at Little Tuanzi finally snapped back to reality, their expressions suddenly changing.","Seeing their expressions, Si Nian knew they hadn't.","She smiled and said, \"It's alright, I'll just give your families a call to let them know.\"","After saying that, she stood up.","Just then, she heard Da Huang barking outside the door."]},{"number":475,"title":"Chapter 475: Behind the Funding","paragraphs":["She turned her head and looked toward the door.","A woman in high heels walked into the courtyard.","Her eyes were full of arrogance.","Fang Hui had lived next door to the Zhou family for quite some time, so she knew very well that the Zhou family's dog was always chained up with an iron chain as thick as an arm.","Although it looked terrifying, as long as she didn't get close, she would be fine.","Therefore, she walked through the gate quite boldly.","Si Nian was slightly taken aback when she saw Fang Hui.","She then put away her smile.","Although Fang Hui had been detained, the time had long passed.","It wasn't strange for her to appear here.","After all, she was Xiao Bowen's mother.","Was she here to look for Xiao Bowen?","In the past, Fang Hui wouldn't let her son play with Xiao Bowen.","Si Nian hadn't seen this person in a long time. Judging by the Xiao family's attitude, they probably didn't like her.","Now that they had brought their grandson back, logically speaking, they wouldn't want him to have contact with her.","After all, the child's father had seen with his own eyes what Fang Hui had done to Xiao Bowen before.","Seeing her suddenly appear here, Si Nian couldn't help but overthink.","\"It's been a while, Teacher Si, and your life is truly getting better and better.\" Fang Hui scrutinized the brand-new courtyard with critical eyes, her words sour with jealousy.","She knew that Si Nian had become the top scorer in the exams, but shortly after, she herself was detained because of that incident.","She hadn't expected Si Nian to come to Jing City for university.","Even less did she expect her whole family to follow along.","If it were in the past, Fang Hui might have just felt a little uncomfortable in her heart.","But now, her heart was full of a sense of crisis.","No matter how rich the Zhou family was, they merely ran a pig farm, vulgar and unsightly.","How could they compare to a century-old prominent family like the Xiao family?","Not to mention, the Xiao family had power and influence.","As long as she outlived that old woman and could marry into the family, she would be a wealthy young madam, enjoying endless wealth and glory.","But once the Xiao family found out about the existence of those two children, her son's position would be in jeopardy.","At this moment, Fang Hui only wished that this family would disappear from the world forever.","\"Thank you for the compliment. However, Comrade Fang doesn't seem as glamorous as before. I remember you used to be the most particular about rules, but now you don't even know the basic courtesy of knocking before entering someone else's house.\"","\"Fortunately, our Da Huang is tied up today. If you had come on any normal day, I couldn't guarantee that you'd walk out of here in one piece.\"","Si Nian didn't like Fang Hui, nor did she want to invite trouble.","Usually, when she had nothing to do, she would let Da Huang loose to stroll around the courtyard on its own.","Recently, because she was in postpartum confinement and couldn't go out often, she had chained Da Huang up, afraid it might run outside.","Otherwise, if a stranger suddenly barged in, Da Huang would likely pounce on them directly.","Si Nian absolutely loathed people who asked for trouble and dragged others down with them, so her tone was entirely unceremonious and carried a hint of mockery.","Fang Hui's face darkened a bit. She knew Si Nian didn't want to interact with her. In the past, because she feared this dog, she had never stepped into the Zhou family's house.","But things were different now.","For the sake of her son's future and prospects, nothing could make her afraid.","\"Hehe, it's just been a long time, and I was too happy. Teacher Si wouldn't hold such a trivial matter against me, would you?\"","\"Speaking of which, I'm quite surprised. It's one thing for you to come to Jing City for university, but why drag your whole family along? You brought all the kids over, don't you find it troublesome? I've never even seen the biological parents of these children; don't they mind?\"","Si Nian narrowed her eyes.","Why would someone like Fang Hui, who only cared about her own interests, inexplicably ask about the children's biological parents?","Catching her suspicious gaze, Fang Hui immediately said, \"Don't misunderstand. I heard you've given birth. Since you have your own child now, you'll definitely have to send these kids back, right? You can't possibly plan on raising someone else's children for the rest of your life?\"","As soon as she said this, the faces of the children immediately fell.","At the same time, a flash of panic appeared in their eyes as they subconsciously looked at Si Nian's expression.","The first woman their father married had said something similar before: as long as she had her own children, she definitely wouldn't want them.","Now, Mom had her own child...","Before Si Nian could speak, Xiao Bowen spoke up.","Others might not understand what his mother meant by this, but he did.","His mother had asked that day if Zhou Zhedong and the others had any relationship with the Xiao family.","He felt back then that he shouldn't tell her this secret.","So he kept quiet. Recently, Fang Hui had been coming to look for him often, and he had thought she simply missed him and wanted to see him.","But he never expected that she was actually doing it because of this matter.","Xiao Bowen's expression was exceedingly grim.","He had a premonition that his mother was going to destroy their current stable life.","In fact, during the time Fang Hui was away, Xiao Bowen had roughly guessed what had happened.","Although his father and grandmother both kept it from him and never mentioned his mother.","But Xiao Bowen wasn't a fool.","He might be young, but he understood everything.","He knew his father didn't like his mother.","He also knew his mother had done bad things.","\"Mom, stop talking.\"","Interrupted, Fang Hui finally noticed that her son was looking at her with a face full of disappointment and anger.","Her heart skipped a beat.","It felt as if her thoughts had been seen through by her son, but she also felt it was impossible since her son was still so young.","Si Nian withdrew her gaze, \"Why are you asking this? Does it have anything to do with you?\"","Fang Hui shouldn't be the kind of person who would be interested in the biological parents of these children.","Not to mention that she had previously shown behavior indicating she didn't like these children at all.","So how could she possibly ask about such a thing?","Thinking about it now, she couldn't help but feel that Fang Hui knew something she didn't.","And it was something related to the children.","Fang Hui stared at her for a good while, confirming that she wasn't playing dumb, before smiling, \"It's nothing, I was just curious and asking. Teacher Si, don't overthink it.\"","\"Bowen, let's go home.\"","After she finished speaking, she looked at her son.","Xiao Bowen's small face was tense, and he didn't move.","Fang Hui's face darkened a bit more.","In the past, her son would never dare to show her such an attitude!","She didn't know how the Xiao family was raising him.","Now he was being disobedient.","Feeling Si Nian's mocking gaze, her face instantly fell. Putting on her former strict attitude, she said in a deep voice, \"Be obedient! What's this about running to other people's houses all day? How did I teach you before?\"","She still had some things to ask her son.","Xiao Bowen bit his lip and tightly gripped his backpack straps.","He glanced at Si Nian, withdrew his gaze, and was about to leave with his backpack.","He didn't want to cause trouble for the Zhou family, but then he heard Si Nian say in a deep voice, \"Bowen, I've already called your grandmother to come pick you up. If you leave with your mother now, your grandmother might worry about you later.\"","As soon as she said this, before Xiao Bowen could speak, Fang Hui blew up first, her face looking awful. \"You...\"","\"What about me?\" Si Nian looked back at Fang Hui calmly. Although she knew Fang Hui probably wouldn't hurt Xiao Bowen, looking at Fang Hui's expression, she figured she wouldn't just let her son leave her like this and would definitely think of something.","And her only avenue for that was Xiao Bowen.","Si Nian did not want to meddle in other people's business, but she could not bear to let Xiao Bowen go through what had happened before all over again.","Although not having a mother might make him sad.","But returning to the extremely oppressive life of the past, would that not be a kind of torture too?","At least the current Xiao Bowen had his father and grandmother to care for and love him, giving him freedom and space, and letting him live like an ordinary child.","Compared to when he was with Fang Hui, the child had become much more cheerful.","Si Nian hoped he could keep going like this, without having his worldview distorted by Fang Hui.","Hearing that Grandma Xiao might be coming to pick up the child, Fang Hui looked as terrified as a mouse meeting a cat.","Although she was very angry, she was also afraid of running into Madam Xiao.","Madam Xiao was a very terrifying person, ruthless and decisive; after her husband and son passed away, she was able to support the Xiao family all by herself.","She was a very famous, strong businesswoman.","If she knew she had come back and was in contact with her son, her future days could be well imagined.","Fang Hui was not afraid of Si Nian, but she was terrified of Grandma Xiao, and she immediately wanted to leave in a panic.","\"Forget it, I suddenly remembered I have something to do. Bowen, you can go back with your grandmother later. Remember to study hard and be a good boy. Mom will come to see you when she has time.\"","After saying that, she turned and strode away.","Xiao Bowen looked at Si Nian and said, \"Teacher Si, did you lie to my mom?\"","Si Nian looked down at him. \"Are you mad at your teacher?\"","Xiao Bowen shook his head. He was not angry; he was happy.","Happy that Teacher Si would actually lie to protect him.","He clearly saw that Teacher Si had not even had the chance to call his grandmother yet.","Teacher Si was such a good person, no wonder Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan did not want to leave her.","If it were him, he would not want to leave either.","Si Nian called Grandma Xiao. It was getting late, and Fang Hui's appearance had disrupted the family's rhythm.","Grandma Xiao picked up her grandson, and Si Nian told her about Fang Hui. She frowned, but was not very surprised.","Si Nian did not say much else, as this was their own family matter. After saying their goodbyes.","The car slowly drove away from the Zhou family, and Grandma Xiao finally withdrew her gaze.","She asked her grandson softly and gently, \"Bowen, your mother came to find you?\"","Xiao Bowen nodded and gave an \"Mm.\"","Grandma Xiao felt a bit guilty and said, \"Your parents' situation is a bit complicated. You don't understand it yet, but rest assured, we won't stop you from seeing her.\"","The premise was that Fang Hui did not cause trouble.","Otherwise, she had plenty of ways to make her leave her grandson.","If it were not for her feeling sorry that her grandson was too young and might find it hard to accept leaving his mother, there was no way she could have come back.","Xiao Bowen nodded and said, \"I know, Grandma.\"","Grandma Xiao patted his head in relief, but then heard her grandson say, \"It's just that Mom was so strange this time. She kept asking me about Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan, and this time she even followed me to Teacher Si's house, asking her about Zhou Zedong's biological parents...\"","He mumbled to himself, as if he did not see Grandma Xiao's stiff expression.","\"And what did you say?\" Grandma Xiao's paused hand fell on her grandson again.","Xiao Bowen said innocently, \"I didn't say anything, because Mom never liked me playing with those brothers in the past.\"","Grandma Xiao's expression looked thoughtful.","She smiled on the surface, but her heart had already sunk to the bottom.","...","When Zhou Yueshen returned, Si Nian brought up this matter.","\"It's been so long since Fang Hui had her accident before she came back. Logically speaking, her first priority should have been to look for her son, but she inexplicably asked about Little Dong and Little Han's biological parents. I think she's very strange.\"","Si Nian leaned against the man's shoulder, holding their son and breastfeeding him while asking.","Zhou Yueshen frowned. \"Speaking of those two children, when I thought about going to pay their tuition for the second half of the semester today, the school told me someone had sponsored their tuition...\"","Although in this school, the Zhou family was indeed not considered rich, they were definitely not poor either.","It was just that maybe when they first transferred here, the two children seemed out of place.","Before, Si Nian used to pay for these things, but now that she was pregnant and had given birth, she did not have time to manage the children. Zhou Yueshen was worried he would forget about it, so when he dropped the children off at school today, he thought about paying in advance to save trouble.","But he was told he did not need to pay.","This surprised him a bit.","Because Si Nian had not mentioned this to him either.","Hearing this, Si Nian was also very surprised. \"When did this happen?\"","\"Someone sponsored them over half a year ago, that's what the school said, but the material fees still need to be paid by ourselves. Because the other party didn't want to reveal their name and just wanted to do a good deed, they didn't tell them.\"","Such a good thing, to outsiders, was like a pie falling from the sky.","But Zhou Yueshen never believed such things would fall on him.","So he always maintained a skeptical attitude in his heart.","And he had thought about coming back to ask Si Nian.","Si Nian felt even more confused. Could there really be someone who does good deeds without leaving a name?","If it were not for what happened today, she might not have thought much of it.","After all, in a school like that, Little Dong and Little Han's conditions might indeed not be as good as the other children.","But now, she felt really weird about it.","She always felt like she had overlooked something.","Zhou Yueshen told her not to worry, they would ask about the situation later, and if something was really wrong, they would just refuse the other party's sponsorship.","Anyway, they were not short of this little bit of money.","The two did not have time to say more before the baby suddenly threw up milk.","He threw up all over her.","Instantly, a smell of milk filled her nasal cavity.","Si Nian was a germaphobe and immediately frowned.","Although she had not washed her hair recently, she would wipe her body with a hot towel every day and change her clothes daily.","What she feared the most was the baby throwing up milk.","Because once he threw up, she would smell, and she would have to change clothes again.","Zhou Yueshen did not have time to say more and hurriedly took the baby.","He changed the baby's clothes, and the small basin was filled with a pile of clothes again.","Si Nian's and the baby's.","They had to be changed every day.","It was hot here, and if they did not change the baby's dirty clothes, he would stink.","After wiping the baby's face and changing his clothes, when he went back, Si Nian was sitting there changing into her pajamas.","Zhou Yueshen's gaze swept over, he stopped in his tracks, and did not make a sound."]},{"number":476,"title":"Chapter 476: The Suppression and Grandma Xiao's Worries and the Stubborn Woman","paragraphs":["There was a sudden knock on the bedroom door.","Zhou Zedong's voice rang out, \"Mom, I cooked some noodles.\"","Because Si Nian was breastfeeding, she ate a lot every day and sometimes woke up hungry in the middle of the night.","So she would have a midnight snack.","The Eldest Child, learning from who knows where, made all sorts of different foods every day. Si Nian didn't eat much, but she would always take a few bites to taste it.","Whatever she couldn't finish went to Zhou Yueshen.","Today, she only took two bites before she didn't want any more. She mainly just wanted a taste. Si Nian had no desire to gain weight during her postpartum confinement; losing weight later would be too difficult.","Therefore, she didn't eat too much, stopping when she was seventy percent full.","Zhou Yueshen took the noodles but didn't even have time to eat before their son started crying again.","Whenever Si Nian wasn't around, for some unknown reason, the baby was especially prone to crying and had to be held and coaxed.","Just now, Si Nian had stepped out to brush her teeth and wash her face. Unable to see his mother, he started to wail.","No matter how Zhou Yueshen held him, he wouldn't stop.","Zhou Yueshen had little experience caring for children. His greatest concession when his son cried was to hold him and pat his back.","If you expected him to speak and coax the baby, that was impossible.","So when Si Nian came out, she saw him holding their son stiffly. The big one and the little one were in their own worlds: you cry your way, I'll hold you my way.","Completely disconnected from each other.","Si Nian was utterly amused.","\"Give him to me and hurry up and eat. The noodles will get clumpy and taste bad if you wait.\"","The moment Si Nian took her son, he immediately stopped crying.","Only then did Zhou Yueshen have time to eat his noodles.","The noodles had clumped together. There hadn't been much to begin with, but now they had swelled to fill the entire bowl.","He slurped the noodles in large mouthfuls. He was usually quite casual about eating, and although he didn't smack his lips, the noise still disturbed Si Nian.","Si Nian looked up at him. Zhou Yueshen paused and asked, \"Do you want some more?\"","Si Nian replied, \"You make it look really appetizing when you eat.\"","Zhou Yueshen was speechless.","By the time he returned from finishing his meal, Si Nian was already lying down, holding the baby.","Zhou Yueshen lightened his footsteps. First, he washed and hung up the clothes for the mother and son, then took a shower himself. Only after that did he get into bed, gently move his son aside, and pull Si Nian into his arms to sleep.","Since getting pregnant, Si Nian had filled out quite a bit.","Holding her felt soft and sweet-smelling.","Having abstained for several months, the man would often get aroused.","But he acted as if he felt nothing, purely holding Si Nian as they rested.","However, during this period, Si Nian was such a light sleeper that the slightest movement would wake her. As soon as the man approached, she immediately frowned and opened her eyes.","It was already hot, and she had a burning-hot man pressed tightly against her back.","It was hard for Si Nian not to wake up.","The moment she opened her eyes, she found herself nestled in the man's embrace, a wall of heat radiating endless warmth from behind her.","Sitting on the bed late at night, he massaged her. Si Nian herself blushed furiously, but thinking about doing it herself seemed too awkward, so it was better to let him help.","As a result, every morning when she woke up, she could feel Zhou Yueshen's vigorous morning arousal.","Si Nian admitted that she had a bit of a lustful mind, but she wouldn't go too far.","Just to make breastfeeding easier, she changed into light, thin pajamas every night, her fair skin dazzlingly white.","Their skin pressed together.","Although they couldn't be fully intimate, it didn't mean they couldn't kiss.","Even though she couldn't go all the way, it didn't mean she couldn't have some fun, right?","With overwhelming lust, Si Nian immediately said, \"What I mean is, it's not like there aren't other ways.\"","She had no idea that this suggestion would make her regret it.","Right now, she was still feeling smug, just wanting to see Zhou Yueshen blush or make a fool of himself.","This could be considered one of Si Nian's few wicked hobbies.","This older man remained completely unruffled no matter what happened.","Sometimes Si Nian found this annoying; she wanted to see Zhou Yueshen lose control.","To prove her importance in his heart.","Perhaps a life that was too peaceful and happy occasionally needed a little thrill.","\"Has it been too long?\"","Si Nian was speechless. Where did this man get the nerve to boast about himself like that?","This was a provocation, an absolute provocation!","If she admitted it now, wouldn't he be insufferably smug in the future?","She had previously thought he was lacking stamina; she couldn't let him wipe away that past humiliation right here and now.","So Si Nian gritted her teeth and feigned calmness, saying, \"It was alright.\"","Hmph! She couldn't let a man get too arrogant!","\"Are you really not tired?\"","Si Nian replied, \"...Heh, it wasn't that long, what's there to be tired about.\"","Seeing that her entire body was limp and soft, with only her mouth remaining stubborn, Zhou Yueshen let out a helpless, low chuckle.","Si Nian, however, felt she was being mocked. After all, she was the one who suggested it first, yet she was also the first one who couldn't hold on.","She was flustered and exasperated.","Zhou Yueshen went to take another shower. When he returned and looked at his wife sleeping deeply from exhaustion, he felt both amused and slightly guilty.","She was the one who made the suggestion, and she was the one who regretted it in the end.","How could she be so cute.","He also blamed himself for not refusing, which caused her to become so exhausted. A woman who recently gave birth already had trouble sleeping.","Zhou Yueshen felt a bit of regret and decided he must be firmer in the future.","...","Once Si Nian's postpartum confinement was over, it meant she could no longer rest. Catching up on her junior and senior year university knowledge in advance could not be delayed.","As for the children, they naturally had to ask what exactly was going on.","Although Zhou Yueshen had inquired about it, the school kept stating that the sponsor was unwilling to reveal their name.","To prevent any trouble, Si Nian requested the school to reject the sponsor's financial aid.","She hoped that if the other party wanted to sponsor someone, they would sponsor students who were in greater need of help.","They were not short of money themselves and had no need to occupy such a valuable spot.","Si Nian didn't want to take advantage of the situation.","Surprisingly, ever since Fang Hui's last visit, Si Nian had always assumed she would show up again. However, after picking up and dropping off the children a few times, she noticed that people from the Xiao family were staking out the school gates early every day, as if trying to prevent something.","Fang Hui never appeared again either.","Her suspicions from that day seemed to be just her overthinking.","Grandma Xiao naturally also heard about Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen rejecting her financial sponsorship for the two children.","The school hadn't dared to say anything at first, thinking that free benefits should never be turned down. Even though the Zhou family might be puzzled, they surely wouldn't refuse such a good thing.","But unexpectedly, it wasn't long before Si Nian came to decline the sponsorship.","Left with no choice, they could only inform Grandma Xiao.","Grandma Xiao didn't know if the Zhou family had grown suspicious or if there was another reason.","Not being able to help the children made her feel terrible.","She had originally thought that even if she couldn't take the children back with her, she could at least compensate them.","But she never expected that such a simple wish would be so difficult to fulfill.","Yet she couldn't voice her troubles. After all, Zhou Zedong had already warned her not to disturb their family's life.","She had spent most of her life being resented by her sons. Her second son disliked her, and because of the incident with the eldest son of the Xiao family, her youngest son even spitefully refused to listen to her and get married or have children.","This was what led to the Xiao family's current situation, with all their descendants scattered outside.","Perhaps this was heaven's punishment for her past selfishness.","To avoid having her grandchildren resent her as well, Grandma Xiao could only try her best to minimize her presence and silently care for them behind the scenes.","Although she had no intention of fighting for custody of the children, they were still descendants of the Xiao family, and she hoped that one day they would return to inherit the Xiao family legacy.","Right now, the children didn't understand how massive the Xiao family's assets were and only focused on their current happy lives. She, too, just hoped the children would live well.","Therefore, she could leave them undisturbed for now.","Once they grew up and learned of their innate advantages, she believed they certainly wouldn't refuse.","However, Fang Hui's appearance disrupted Grandma Xiao's plans.","If Zhou Yueshen's family found out about this, she worried that the couple would take the children away just to stay out of the conflict.","The children saw them as their pillars of support and definitely wouldn't stay behind.","Grandma Xiao had been restless and uneasy for a long time.","Especially after the school informed her of the incident, she was afraid that something amiss would be noticed. Even more so, she worried about Fang Hui's underhanded tricks, so she had to resolve this trouble as quickly as possible.","Originally, considering that she was the mother of her grandson, as long as she behaved, there would be nothing to worry about.","But a greedy and selfish woman like Fang Hui had previously used the grandson as leverage to boss her son around. He had almost agreed to marry her. If it hadn't been for a trip to the remote southwestern regions, which allowed her son to see through her true nature, she might have actually become her daughter-in-law.","Now that she knew that besides Bowen, the eldest son of the Xiao family had three other children living out in the world, Grandma Xiao dared not imagine what Fang Hui might do to consolidate her own son's position.","Even though people had already been sent to protect the children.","Grandma Xiao knew that dealing with Fang Hui was the most crucial priority right now.","Sure enough, under Grandma Xiao's surveillance recently, Fang Hui pretended to know nothing. In reality, she had long been secretly investigating the circumstances of the eldest son of the Xiao family from back then, trying to find out why he had died.","This matter had caused quite a stir back then, so she could find out about it very easily.","Especially the fact that the eldest son of the Xiao family had been sent far away to the countryside for his safety due to family connections. The place he was sent to was the remote countryside of the southwest, away from all the disputes.","This already proved why those children were left without parents.","However, before she could even make a move, Grandma Xiao's suppression came crashing down on her."]},{"number":477,"title":"Chapter 477: Not Entirely Impossible","paragraphs":["At first, she simply couldn't find a job, hitting a wall at every turn.","Then, even her landlord deliberately raised the rent to drive her away.","Fang Hui knew that Grandma Xiao must be targeting her behind the scenes. She gnashed her teeth in hatred, but didn't know what to do.","She came from a poor background, and in order to enter the circle of the wealthy, she had even cut off contact with her hometown.","She had suffered untold hardships just to return to Beijing.","She didn't have much money left on hand. She originally wanted to settle down here temporarily and wait for her son to secure his position in the Xiao family.","However, the cost of living here was not low, and she was used to living a good life. It is easy to go from frugality to luxury, but hard to go from luxury to frugality.","Naturally, she was unwilling to live in an old, shabby, and small place, let alone one far from the city center.","All her money went into renting an apartment.","Fortunately, she still had some old friends here who lent her a little money, allowing her to gain a foothold.","But she never expected that just as she had finally stabilized, Grandma Xiao would suppress her.","She wanted to make it impossible for her to survive in this city.","During this time, she clearly felt that Grandma Xiao had sent people to keep an eye on her son, preventing her from getting anywhere near him.","Having lost contact with her son, she could only find ways to secretly investigate what had happened back then.","Now she was certain that those children belonged to the Xiao family and had evidence. Although the existence of these children posed a great threat to her.","But indirectly, it also meant she held the lifeline of the Xiao family, didn't it?","However, now she couldn't find a job, had no place to live, and couldn't even solve her basic needs for food and clothing. Driven into a corner with no way to retreat, she had no choice but to use this matter to threaten Grandma Xiao.","This was also her last bargaining chip to negotiate with the Xiao family.","Fang Hui thought Grandma Xiao still didn't know that these children were the Xiao family's offspring, so she was very arrogant and went directly to Grandma Xiao for a negotiation.","She had another idea, an idea that would make the Zhou family's children hate the Xiao family.","The children were still young and ignorant. Once they knew that their biological father was driven to death by Grandma Xiao, which led to them becoming orphans, they would definitely harbor hatred.","In addition, if Grandma Xiao knew these children belonged to the Xiao family, she would definitely fight for them.","Someone like Si Nian, combined with the children's dependence on her, would be even less likely to be willing to separate.","When the time came, she might even leave Beijing to protect the children.","After all, here, the Zhou family definitely had no way to shake the Xiao family.","She had interacted with those children; they practically followed Si Nian's every lead.","But they were cold and ruthless to outsiders, especially the eldest child of the Zhou family, Zhou Zedong. The few times she had bumped into him before, meeting his gaze, Fang Hui found it terrifying.","Such a child could not possibly forgive Grandma Xiao.","Thinking of this method, she could both threaten Grandma Xiao and make the children hate her bitterly. Perhaps it would even make Si Nian take the children away, and then she could stay with peace of mind!","The more Fang Hui thought about it, the more excited she became.","It was as if she had been injected with adrenaline.","She waited at the school gate to catch Grandma Xiao, who was sending the child to the library, and took the initiative to propose a talk.","Grandma Xiao didn't know what tricks she was hiding, but it wasn't appropriate to lose her temper in front of her grandson, so she had to agree.","Xiao Bowen watched the two secretly crossing swords. For some reason, he felt that his mother seeking out his grandmother must be related to the Zhou family.","He restrained his gaze and parted ways with the two under the pretext of going to read.","Then he carried his schoolbag and went to the Si family's house.","Si Nian was just about to take the children out to buy summer clothes. Little Four was tied to the back of Second Child, who was running very fast. Little Four was amused and giggled, thinking his brother was playing with him.","He almost bumped into the approaching Xiao Bowen.","Seeing Xiao Bowen, Si Nian was taken aback for a moment.","\"Bowen, why did you come over by yourself?\"","Xiao Bowen held his backpack straps, pursed his lips, and whispered, \"Teacher Si, I want to buy a book, but I didn't bring any money. Can you take me to buy it? I'll have Grandma return the money to you tomorrow.\"","His expression was conflicted and troubled.","Si Nian paused, thinking to herself, this child came all the way to find her just to buy a book?","She laughed helplessly and said, \"How much is it? I'll give it to you.\"","\"It's just a book, no need to pay it back. Consider it a gift from your teacher.\"","But Xiao Bowen pursed his lips and after a long while said, \"Can you go with me?\"","A strange look flashed in Si Nian's eyes, but she thought Xiao Bowen just didn't want to be alone.","He seemed to really like going to the library to read with Eldest Child, and occasionally he would come over to play, but every time he had to find an excuse for himself.","It seemed that only in this way could he feel at ease staying.","Because she had told Eldest Child earlier today that she was taking his younger siblings to buy clothes in the afternoon and asked him to come back early, Eldest Child hadn't gone to the library. So, being bored alone, he found such an excuse?","Si Nian didn't think much of it. It was on the way anyway, so she nodded, \"Alright, I'll take you to buy it, but go home early after buying it, don't let your grandmother worry.\"","Xiao Bowen nodded, and then led them all the way to the library they often visited.","Meanwhile, in the rest area below the library, Grandma Xiao and Fang Hui were confronting each other.","After Grandma Xiao sat down, she looked at Fang Hui. Her eyes held a hint of smugness, though it was unclear what exactly she was being smug about.","Her look of a petty person flush with success made her very uncomfortable.","Her second son was also foolish to have provoked such a woman.","\"Speak, what exactly do you want to do? If you want to marry my son, then don't even think about it. Unless I die, you will never enter the Xiao family's door in this lifetime.\"","\"Madam Xiao, why are you so aggressive? I'm not here to bring that up. However, I'm sure you will be very interested in what I have to say.\"","\"What is it?\" Grandma Xiao frowned.","Fang Hui smiled, \"I heard that your eldest son passed away in a car accident back then, right?\"","Grandma Xiao's face instantly darkened.","Smart as she was, she immediately understood what Fang Hui was trying to do.","Her eyes grew cold, and she simply stopped talking.","Letting her continue.","Fang Hui saw her ugly expression, thought she had hit the mark, and immediately felt pleased with herself.","She continued, \"Although I don't know what caused that accident, I think it must have something to do with you, Madam.\"","\"What exactly are you trying to say?\" Grandma Xiao interrupted her impatiently.","\"Actually, following your son's arrangement this time, I took a trip to Yungui Sichuan City and discovered some incredible things. I don't know if you are aware of them...\"","She took out that group photo from her bag. \"I saw a few children who look very much like Big Brother Xiao, and they live right next door to me. Speaking of which, these children have had a miserable life. They are raised by their uncle and have a stepmother. Living under someone else's roof, their life is difficult. Perhaps they don't even know that their father has already...\"","Grandma Xiao's face instantly turned incredibly ugly.","\"Coincidentally, after I came back, I also found these children here. However, their stepmother is a snob. If she knew the children's background, I'm afraid she wouldn't let the matter rest... Sigh, seeing that the Xiao family only has Bowen as an heir, it's truly pitiful, so I came to tell you immediately after finding out about this.\"","She spoke in a tone as if everything she did was for the sake of the Xiao family.","After all, only by letting Grandma Xiao see how generous and selfless she was would the old lady stop having such a huge problem with her.","As for those children, they were still so young and their biological parents were dead. Even if they really returned to the Xiao family, they would have no one to rely on.","Once Grandma Xiao passed away, what could those orphaned kids possibly use to fight her for the inheritance?","By doing Grandma Xiao a favor now, she could get the old lady to have a massive falling out with Si Nian over the custody of the children. That was the outcome she wanted to see the most.","The more Fang Hui thought about it, the more smug she felt.","Grandma Xiao looked at the overly clever Fang Hui, a cold sneer surfacing in her eyes.","She pretty much figured out the little schemes running through Fang Hui's mind.","However, the stupidity of this woman exceeded her imagination. Did Fang Hui really not know that she had already been in contact with Si Nian and already knew the children belonged to the Xiao family?","She had assumed her grandson had already told Fang Hui about these things.","But unexpectedly, Fang Hui only knew about the children's relationship with the Xiao family and was completely oblivious to everything else.","And here she was, shamelessly badmouthing Si Nian.","After learning about the children's situation, she had secretly investigated it long ago. Si Nian's relationship with the children was as close as if they were her own flesh and blood.","The children were exceptionally fond of her and intimate with her, to the point where Grandma Xiao couldn't bear to tear them apart.","Coupled with Zhou Zedong's warning to her, even she didn't dare to make threats.","Yet Fang Hui was actually trying to sow discord.","If she hadn't known about these matters beforehand, Fang Hui might have actually succeeded.","Grandma Xiao sneered, Is that so? According to what you're saying, she definitely won't easily return the Xiao family's children to me?","Xiao Bowen led Si Nian over, then asked Zhou Zedong to take her to the resting area to wait for him while he went upstairs to get the books.","Zhou Zedong gave him a weird look, but seeing that Si Nian was indeed sweating profusely from the heat, he hurriedly pulled her toward the resting area.","He came here often and was very familiar with the place.","But to his surprise, just as they walked over, he heard a familiar voice.","Of course. You have no idea how snobbish their stepmother is. If she finds out about their connection to the Xiao family, she definitely won't let the children come back so easily. At the very least, she'll try to scam a massive sum of money out of the Xiao family.","He looked up and saw that it was Xiao Bowen's mother talking with Grandma Xiao.","Although Si Nian noticed it too, she didn't immediately react.","But Zhou Zedong's expression instantly turned ugly.","However, the other party hadn't noticed them yet and continued speaking.","Grandma Xiao's furious voice rang out, Enough! Do you take me for a fool? I've known what kind of person Comrade Si is for a long time. You still want to smear her reputation in front of me? Don't think I don't know what you're plotting!","If Comrade Si is willing to let the two children come back, even if she empties out our Xiao family, I would be happy to let her! I don't need you scheming and plotting here!","Grandma Xiao liked Si Nian very much and couldn't stand seeing Fang Hui smear her like this. Her face was dark and gloomy.","Fang Hui was startled, and her expression quickly turned sour.","Just as she was about to say something, she noticed Si Nian and her son.","Her gaze shifted, and she mocked directly, You might be willing, but it depends on whether she is! Since you know her personality and her relationship with the children, you should be well aware that she couldn't possibly bear to return the children to you!","Grandma Xiao noticed the strange look in her eyes and immediately turned around.","Seeing her eldest grandson's ugly expression and the astonished Si Nian, she was also stunned.","Si Nian was totally dumbfounded.","She only just realized that her appearance here was no coincidence.","Some of her previous doubts instantly made sense at this moment.","After the initial shock, she quickly regained her composure.","It was a novel, after all. Things like the mystery of the children's birth were essential plot points; there was nothing to be surprised about.","What Si Nian hadn't expected, however, was that the children's background would be so massive.","After just a few seconds of being stunned, Grandma Xiao had already stood up in a panic, hurriedly explaining, It's not like that, Nian Nian. I have no intention of forcing the children back to the Xiao family. Please don't misunderstand!","Si Nian said with a weird expression, I was wondering why your attitude toward the children earlier and the baffling anonymous financial aid they received at school felt a bit off. Now it all makes sense.","It was you working behind the scenes, right?","Grandma Xiao nodded with a pale face. Yes, but I meant no harm. I just wanted to give the children a little bit of compensation. It is our Xiao family that let them down, and I don't expect their forgiveness. I just hope you don't misunderstand. I don't want to separate you and force the children to come back.","She was terrified that Si Nian would misunderstand and actually take the children away.","Si Nian said, Of course I can't bear to be separated from the children.","Fang Hui immediately sneered, See, I was right! How could she possibly return the children to you!","Grandma Xiao's face turned pale.","Si Nian glanced at the smug Fang Hui and said, Of course. It hasn't been easy for me. I've shed so much sweat and earned so much money just to raise these children to this age. How could I let them go back so easily, only to call someone else grandma the moment they meet? This is clearly my grandma!","Grandma Xiao: ......","Fang Hui: .......","Beside them, Zhou Zedong almost dropped the things in his hands, staring at Si Nian in astonishment.","Grandma Xiao was the first to react, asking in surprise, Nian Nian, what do you mean?","Si Nian smiled. Grandma Xiao... oh wait, Auntie. This chance to get filthy rich... oh wait, you don't need to worry about my thoughts at all. I would be more than happy to let the children inherit the Xiao family's fortune.","Of course, if the children want to live with me now, they will live with me. I won't stop them from interacting with the Xiao family in the future. It'll be the same when they grow up and inherit the fortune. You wouldn't mind that, right?","The matters of the previous generation have nothing to do with the children. I don't want to dig into it, and I hope they won't dwell on it either. Living our own lives well right now is the most important thing.","Little Dong, do you want to give up this chance to get filthy rich?","Si Nian's eyes sparkled with golden light.","Zhou Zedong: ......","If he didn't have to leave his mom and could still inherit a million-dollar fortune... it seemed like it wasn't a bad idea.","He immediately shook his head."]},{"number":478,"title":"Chapter 478: Little Boss Is Quite the Businessman","paragraphs":["Fang Hui: \"......\"","Si Nian saw her son's reaction and nodded in satisfaction. As expected of the child she raised, he was indeed on the same front as her.","Grandma Xiao's jaw dropped in shock, and she asked in disbelief, \"R-really?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Of course it's true. You can rest assured handing over the Xiao family's property to him. Our Eldest Child is very good at doing business.\"","Si Nian felt a sense of pride as she spoke.","The Eldest Child had a talent for business since he was young.","Although she only knew that the Xiao family was very rich and hadn't paid attention to what they actually did, Si Nian believed that nothing could stump her son.","Inheriting property without the parents having to work hard for it—this was an overwhelming amount of wealth no matter who it happened to.","Si Nian didn't quite understand why Grandma Xiao would think they were unwilling to return the children.","Did they have a grudge against money?","Zhou Zedong was a little dumbfounded. Hearing his mother promoting and praising him so vigorously, his expression was blank.","So in his mother's eyes, he was such an amazing person?","His eyes lit up.","He didn't look at all like the cold and ruthless person he was when he went to see Grandma Xiao back then.","Grandma Xiao clutched her chest; the excessive surprise and stimulation made her a little breathless.","For a moment, she was filled with mixed feelings of grief and joy.","Meanwhile, Fang Hui, who was standing to the side, was dumbfounded.","At this moment, Xiao Bowen, who couldn't stay upstairs any longer, ran down anxiously. He actually regretted it a little, very afraid that Teacher Si would be angry if she heard his mother and grandmother talking.","He was also afraid that she would see through his petty thoughts, think he was a dishonest child, hate him in the future, and never let him play with Zhou Zedong and the others again.","After some struggle and regret, he planned to find Si Nian and apologize.","But he didn't expect to see Teacher Si smiling in a scene where everyone was happy.","Zhou Zedong's eyes and brows were also soft, without the coldness from the last time he talked with his grandmother in private.","Xiao Bowen stared blankly for a long time.","He didn't quite understand why something that sounded so complicated and troublesome from his grandmother and mother's mouths became so simple and clear when it came to Teacher Si.","After Si Nian finished speaking, she even took the initiative to invite Grandma Xiao to buy clothes, saying that the weather was hot and she planned to buy clothes for the children.","Grandma Xiao was flattered and interpreted it as Si Nian giving her a chance to personally buy clothes for her grandchildren as compensation, which was simply what she dreamed of doing.","Because she had no way to compensate her grandsons, she could only secretly sponsor and protect them behind the scenes.","But as their biological grandmother, how could she not want to personally buy some clothes and gifts for the children?","Grandma Xiao was moved to tears.","She wished she could treat Si Nian as her own daughter.","At this moment, she didn't care whether Fang Hui was there or not. With such a reasonable child like Si Nian, even if Fang Hui wanted to belittle her, it would be impossible.","She grabbed her bag and said she would take them to the department store.","Fang Hui came back to her senses, her nose twisted in anger.","\"Wait, Mrs. Xiao, are you going to believe her so easily?\"","Grandma Xiao turned her head, her face turning cold as fast as flipping a page in a book. \"Do you think everyone is as scheming as you? Niannian, don't overthink it. All those bad things she said about you just now, I treated them like a fart and didn't take them to heart at all. Auntie sees very clearly what kind of person you are.\"","\"It was Auntie who thought too much before. I never dared to admit this matter, and I did those things secretly, causing you to misunderstand. I had no malicious intent.\"","Seeing her two completely different attitudes towards herself and Si Nian, Fang Hui's face turned pale and green.","Si Nian glanced at Fang Hui's pale and green face and said, \"It's fine. To be frank, I really have to thank Comrade Fang for speaking out about this today and letting me know. Otherwise, my child would have had to struggle for another ten or twenty years.\"","She spoke in a tone of taking advantage and still acting innocent.","Hearing this, Fang Hui was fuming with anger and almost fainted.","Then she thought about the three children returning home. Where would her son's status in the Xiao family be then?","She said anxiously, \"No, Mrs. Xiao, you can't be so biased. Bowen is also your grandson!\"","Grandma Xiao snorted coldly from her nostrils. \"I don't need you to teach me what to do! If you still want to stay in Beijing, you'd better not make trouble for the Zhou family in the future, otherwise I'll be the first to not let you off!\"","She originally didn't want to keep Fang Hui here, just worried that she would expose this matter.","But now it seemed that the other party didn't care at all. It was she who thought too much, and Grandma Xiao's heart relaxed.","She dropped those words and, no longer caring about Fang Hui's expression, left with Si Nian and the children.","The matter with Fang Hui came to an end. Si Nian didn't spend a single cent but bought a large pile of clothes and toys for the children. Although she didn't experience the life of a rich second generation, her children did (envious.jpg).","Although she said that, Si Nian was mostly acting out of shock over this matter and deliberately mocking Fang Hui. After all, she saw things thoroughly. After knowing the children's background and hearing Fang Hui's words, she knew exactly what Fang Hui wanted to do.","Doing this not only protected the children but also angered her to death. It was the best of both worlds, so why not do it?","As for what happened between the children's parents and the Xiao family before, because she didn't know, she didn't comment much.","At the very least, Grandma Xiao wouldn't hurt the children, and that was the most important thing right now.","The rest was up to Zhou Yueshen's opinion.","Her agreement didn't mean Zhou Yueshen agreed. After all, this matter also involved Zhou Yueshen's sister.","She had heard that his sister's death back then was inextricably linked to the children's father.","If he hated the other party, then it was normal for him to be unwilling to accept it.","When Zhou Yueshen heard about this, his expression was indescribably strange.","He didn't expect that the matter he had been having people investigate for so many years had only yielded the word \"Beijing.\"","But he didn't expect it to be exposed by his wife so coincidentally.","Si Nian looked at her new clothes in fascination. These clothes were made of fine fabrics. For a woman like her who had just given birth and urgently needed maintenance, she liked them very much, especially since the weather was hot and they were comfortable to wear.","They were simply too friendly to her.","But this kind of silk fabric was expensive. Even as a little rich woman, she only occasionally splurged on it.","She wouldn't be too willing to spend the money.","But Grandma Xiao pulled her along and bought them without hesitation.","She didn't look at the price at all, saying it was to thank them for taking care of the children all these years.","Although Si Nian felt quite embarrassed, she also felt that there was nothing unacceptable about this. She had indeed raised the children to be decent, sensible, and family-oriented!","One had to know that the three children in the novel all had miserable ends.","This was what she deserved!","So while talking to Zhou Yueshen about this, she held the new clothes and gestured them against her body, finally saying, \"If you have any objections in your heart, then I can only return all the clothes.\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","Why did it seem like he was going to be the bad guy?","Was he such an unreasonable person?","As for the love and hate between his sister and that man, Zhou Yueshen was in no mood to care. Something Si Nian said was very right: respect the fate of others.","Whatever he did, as long as it benefited the children, it was a good thing.","Since Si Nian had already said that the other party meant the children no harm, that was enough.","At the very least, the kids could stay here. If they struggled to make a living when they grew up, they could always come back home to inherit the family fortune.","It wasn't a bad path to take.","After all, if someone was wealthy from a young age, who would want to work their fingers to the bone from dawn till dusk?","Ever since he found out that Zhou Zedong and the others were willing to come home, Xiao Bowen would call out, \"Big Brother!\" whenever he saw him.","Faced with Zhou Zedong's peculiar gaze, Xiao Bowen felt a bit nervous, but he lied without batting an eye, \"Grandma said you're the oldest in the family, so I have to call you Big Brother from now on!\"","Zhou Zedong didn't like being called Big Brother by outsiders, but when he thought about the massive fortune he was going to inherit, it suddenly didn't seem so unbearable.","So, he couldn't be bothered to correct him.","He had already made up his mind. In the future, he would leave his father's pig farm to Xiao Han and his father's new company to his youngest brother. Between the three brothers, they would definitely earn more than enough to provide for their mother and sister.","That way, he wouldn't have to bother with those petty businesses anymore.","With his newly freed-up time, Zhou Zedong chose to participate in math competitions and delve into some research.","He knew that only by becoming truly exceptional could he secure the very best in the future."]},{"number":479,"title":"Chapter 479: A Qualified Factory Manager","paragraphs":["It was a long time later when Second Child finally learned of his older brother's arrangements.","He had noticed his brother secretly writing things every night.","He thought his brother was secretly working hard behind his back to amaze everyone.","Who knew that upon opening it, he would see densely packed diary entries.","There were so many words that it made his head ache just looking at them.","So he just flipped through it casually and spotted some key words.","He also got a rough idea of what his brother was writing about.","They were divided into three categories.","1. Research.","2. Food.","3. Future plans.","It was quite clear and straightforward.","Zhou Zedong didn't hide it either; he just left it on the desk after writing every day, so Second Child could read it whenever he wanted.","He probably didn't expect someone like Second Child, who hated studying, to actually open it.","Seeing his brother write that he would leave the pig farm and their dad's company to him and their younger brother, while he alone would bear the immense pressure of the Xiao family.","Second Child was incredibly moved.","His older brother was really looking out for him. He knew he liked the pig farm the most, so he gave it to him.","While he himself would go inherit the property of that father they didn't even know.","He didn't want a stranger's property anyway.","Seeing that his eldest brother was preparing to inherit property, Second Child decided he couldn't just go on like this either.","He had to train hard so he could become a qualified pig slaughterer in the future.","Thus, Second Child went to find Zhou Yueshen, who was working, and said in an earnest, studious tone, Dad, I want to slaughter pigs!","Zhou Yueshen, who had just taken a sip of tea, choked.","Zhou Yueshen asked, Why do you suddenly want to slaughter pigs?","Second Child replied seriously and solemnly, Because Eldest Brother is going to inherit a stranger's property, and our younger brother is still too small. This family can only rely on me to inherit your pig farm. If I don't learn how to slaughter pigs from you now, how will I inherit the farm and become a qualified factory manager in the future?","Zhou Yueshen, ?","Don't worry, Dad. I will definitely study hard this time.","Seeing his dad stay silent, Second Child thought he was doubting his past unreliability, so he immediately promised, I will work hard at slaughtering pigs and won't slack off. I'll make sure you and Mom always have pork to eat.","You're still so young, why did you suddenly think about inheriting Dad's pig farm? Zhou Yueshen asked.","Because Mom said good children need to start from a young age, Second Child said, sticking his neck out righteously.","The entire room fell silent for a good while.","After waiting a long time, Zhou Yueshen finally spoke, Alright, when you come home for the holidays, I'll take you to practice.","Second Child jumped up in excitement, Yay! I'm going to be the boss of a pig farm!","He ran out skipping and jumping. Zhou Yueshen shook his head helplessly, not knowing whether to laugh or cry.","Si Nian was busy with her studies and had no idea what the father and son were planning.","Because of her heavy workload, she originally wanted to go home for the summer vacation but didn't have the time.","It wasn't that Si Nian didn't want to go; it was just that there was an extra child at home, and she had to catch up on four years of university knowledge. Although she had graduated once before, there was still a huge difference in the knowledge between the two eras. The only easy part was that this major came naturally to her.","If her teachers hadn't been so strict about it, she could have finished her studies in a year.","She thought about finishing her studies as soon as possible and then returning to her hometown to retire.","As a corporate slave who worked early mornings in the future world, her only wish was nothing more than early retirement. Whether it was playing mahjong or square dancing, it was all the life Si Nian dreamed of.","So she resisted the urge to go home and managed to finish her sophomore and junior year courses no matter what.","But while imagination is beautiful, reality is somewhat cruel.","Because in the blink of an eye, Eldest Child was already in the sixth grade. If they went back home, he would have to transfer schools again.","The hometown definitely didn't have as rich learning resources as here, and the education was relatively backward.","Si Nian was very worried that running back and forth like this would affect her son.","Speaking of which, after all this time, Second Child had been changed a lot by her. But it could also be that he was naturally optimistic, so he could make friends wherever he went.","However, Eldest Child always kept to himself, whether back in their hometown or after coming to Beijing.","Even if his classmates wanted to interact with him, they couldn't. He was simply too exclusive and didn't give any outsider a chance to get close to him.","The only one who could walk beside him was Xiao Bowen, and that was only because the two families now had this connection.","Si Nian was quite heartbroken at first, always hoping that Eldest Child could live a normal life. She wondered if he couldn't make friends because of past influences.","But after spending more time with him, she realized she was wrong. It wasn't that Eldest Child couldn't make friends; he was just naturally independent and didn't like being around outsiders.","Aside from studying and researching his family, he had absolutely no interest in those things.","In other words, he didn't crave friendship.","However, in this era, the less you needed these things and the more independent and aloof you were, the more mysterious you appeared.","In the sixth grade, Eldest Child suddenly shot up in height.","He suddenly grew to 165 centimeters.","Si Nian looked at her suddenly taller son, feeling a bit bewildered.","Eldest Child didn't gain weight no matter what he ate. Unlike the sturdy Second Child, his figure was rather lean and his skin wasn't fair. But as he grew, his facial features became particularly distinct.","His brows and eyes were somewhat similar to Zhou Yueshen's, sharp yet with an added touch of refinement.","The only other person Si Nian had seen with this kind of aura was Xiao Bowen's father previously.","Due to long hours of reading and doing research, Eldest Child became nearsighted.","Si Nian took him to get glasses.","The moment the child put on his glasses and spoke to her, Si Nian was stunned.","The gentleness and restraint revealed in his speech displayed a unique, refined temperament.","It was as if she could see the scene of the future grand villain wearing a white lab coat, his fragmented hair slightly messy. His words would always be gentle and elegant, but his actions would be ruthless and cold. He would have an unknown darkness in his heart, making everyone keep their distance.","Si Nian swallowed hard.","Eldest Child took off his glasses in confusion and asked, Mom, what's wrong?","Without his glasses, he lost a bit of that maturity and showed more respect and gentleness toward his mother.","Si Nian hesitated to speak, then sighed deeply, Little Dong, you've grown up.","Zhou Zedong was baffled, but thinking about how everyone said he had grown taller when school started this year, he couldn't help but feel secretly delighted, Mom, have I grown taller?","Because his younger brother had grown so fast before, it put a lot of pressure on him.","Actually, when he was in the fifth grade, Eldest Child didn't really like eating eggs and drinking milk anymore.","But remembering what his mom had said, he started eating them again during the winter break.","He didn't know if it was just psychological, but he felt like he was shooting up in height.","He was still taller than his brother.","But he never expected that he would become nearsighted.","At first, he just noticed that he couldn't see things clearly from a distance.","Later, it gradually became more obvious.","He was a little scared, knowing he was definitely nearsighted.","He hadn't paid attention to this kind of thing before, but he had seen classmates wearing glasses.","Yet he hadn't paid attention to himself. It was one thing to constantly immerse himself in the library, but he also liked to write in his diary and do research under a desk lamp when he went home at night.","By the time he realized it, it was already too late.","He didn't really like wearing glasses, and they felt a bit uncomfortable.","But when he wore them, everything was incredibly clear.","He could even see the spots on other people's faces clearly; it felt like everyone around him had gotten uglier.","But when he looked at his mother again, she was just as beautiful as ever, which he found really strange.","Si Nian took him to measure his height and was surprised to find out, \"You've grown another two centimeters. I remember you were only 162 centimeters a few months ago.\"","Now he was already 165.","And he was only in the sixth grade.","It seemed his nutrition had caught up. The Eldest Child, who was only a little over 170 centimeters in his previous life, might actually grow to be over 180 in this one.","Si Nian was happy too. Who wouldn't want their eldest son to be tall and handsome?","Putting on glasses in just the sixth grade, she could already vaguely see the sharp brilliance this child would have when he grew up.","Not to mention how stunning he would be when he truly came of age.","Si Nian suddenly had a strong urge to document this. She planned to take the Eldest Child to a photo studio for some pictures right after getting his glasses fitted.","Seeing how good his brother looked in glasses, the Second Child wanted to wear them too.","He hurriedly clamored for Zhou Zedong to let him try them on.","Zhou Zedong handed them over. The moment they went on his face, he immediately felt dizzy and his vision blurred. \"Ah, this thing is so weird! My head spins when I wear it.\"","He quickly took them off, a look of horror on his face.","He looked at his brother in disbelief, unable to understand why he would wear something so uncomfortable.","\"Little guy, you can't just wear these glasses casually. Since you're not nearsighted, wearing them is bad for your eyes, so it's best not to try. If you want to wear glasses, you need to get tested first to check your prescription, and then get fitted with the right lenses. That way, you won't feel dizzy. Do you want to take a test?\"","The Second Child seemed to half-understand.","But upon hearing that he needed to be tested, he shook his head like a rattle drum.","He definitely didn't want to wear such a terrifying thing.","His poor brother, having to wear such dizzying glasses all the time.","Zhou Zehan cast a pitying glance at his older brother.","After getting the glasses, the family went to the photo studio.","Unfortunately, Zhou Yueshen had to work and couldn't come to take photos during the day, so the group photos only featured Si Nian and the children.","The poor old man.","When Si Nian returned home, she found that people from their hometown had sent them letters again.","Besides the letters from the family, there was also a letter from Shitou to Zhou Zehan.","Shitou was now in the second grade too and knew how to write. Although he substituted many words with pinyin, it was still readable. Zhou Zehan didn't mind; after all, he and Shitou were in the same boat, so neither could judge the other.","In the letter, Shitou mostly wrote about how he was now in the second grade at the town center school above Xingfu Village. He had originally attended school in the village, but his grandmother sent him to the town so he could get a better education.","In town he had seen a lot of the world and had now become the boss of his class group. He boasted that no one in the class could beat him in a fight and that everyone wanted to follow him. His words carried the distinct flavor of a troublemaker...","He also said that when the Second Child returned, they would be bosses together.","The Second Child was no longer interested in this sort of thing. He used to want to be a boss too, but Mom said fighting was wrong.","So he didn't want Shitou to become a bad kid who loved to fight either. They both needed to be good kids so that Mom would always love them.","Therefore, he advised Shitou, writing that he practiced martial arts, exercised, and ran with his dad every day. His teacher had said he could become a star athlete and win glory for the country, or he could join the army when he grew up to defend the nation.","When he went back home, he would inherit his dad's pig farm and become an outstanding pig farm manager just like his dad.","He told Shitou to exercise well too, so that when he returned, they could run the pig farm together. He would let Shitou be the second-in-command of the farm, and they would make money together.","He felt that Shitou would definitely be a great helper. With Shitou's help, his pig farm might even become bigger than his dad's.","By then, he would be the proudest cub in the whole family.","As he wrote, the Second Child broke into a beaming, joyful smile.","He seemed to envision his status in the family skyrocketing.","After sending the letter out, he looked forward to Shitou's reply, hoping he would agree to the proposal.","Meanwhile, at a certain town center elementary school, Shitou also received the Second Child's letter."]},{"number":480,"title":"Chapter 480: The world is finally quiet","paragraphs":["Shitou has grown up quite a bit by now. His skin was very dark, but his eyes were strikingly bright. His small face had developed, and he sported a square crew cut. With thick, bushy eyebrows, he gave off an air of naughty rebelliousness.","He was at that playful age. Even though he had handsome features, anyone could tell at a glance that he was a little rascal.","Shitou used to attend school in the village, but ever since his second brother and the others left, he had become much more bored.","Later, after he was sent to the town, the local kids looked down on him for being a country bumpkin and bullied him.","Unlike Second Child and the others, who had grown fearful from being bullied since childhood, Shitou was an only child doted on by his grandparents. He had a fierce temper. If someone bullied him, he wouldn't just take it; he would fight back, often ending up with his face covered in scratches.","Eventually, the children from the village banded together to form a small group, and the town kids no longer dared to bully them.","They even called them little hooligans.","\"This is a letter from my second brother. You guys probably don't know him, but he's the son of the pig farm manager in our village. And he is in a big city now, the kind of big city you see on TV. You guys have never seen that, right?\"","Having a second brother who had seen the world made Shitou feel incredibly proud.","Seeing everyone's envious gazes, he opened the letter, and the other kids immediately gathered around.","After reading the letter, everyone's expressions turned somewhat sour.","\"Are we bad guys for doing this?\"","Shitou immediately explained, \"My second brother just said that fighting is wrong. He didn't say we are bad kids for fighting. I think my second brother is right. I'm not going to fight anymore.\"","The others were speechless. One of them asked in confusion, \"But they were the ones who bullied us first, so we just fought back. What's wrong with that?\"","Shitou rolled his eyes and said, \"Anyway, I plan to listen to my second brother. When he comes back, I can be the second boss. I don't care what you do.\"","\"If you guys keep fighting, I won't play with you anymore.\"","Even though he was afraid of being bullied, since his second brother said so, it had to be right.","Besides, fighting would only make him a gang leader, but not fighting could make him a boss!","Hearing this, the others immediately grew anxious.","They quickly leaned in and said, \"Don't do that, Brother Shitou. We'll stop fighting, okay? Can you talk to your second brother and let us work at his pig farm in the future?\"","\"Yeah, I'm really good at gathering pigweed.\"","Soon after.","Second Child received Shitou's reply.","Shitou said he wouldn't fight anymore and would work hard to build his strength so he could help him butcher pigs.","He also asked if he could bring all his underlings over to help out together.","Second Child's business empire was beginning to take shape.","Si Nian also wrote letters to her family.","At the same time, she received a letter from Fu Qianqian.","In the letter, Fu Qianqian mentioned that she had been invited to be a host for the Yun-Gui-Chuan Municipal TV Station.","Originally, she was someone who couldn't even secure a job as a broadcaster, but after Si Nian sold her the job, her life had been on an upward trajectory.","It all started when Si Nian helped her with an elementary school English speech. Word had it that the parents spread her reputation so miraculously that the school invited her back every year to host or participate in various events.","After doing this several times, she became famous.","Fu Qianqian's English was originally just average, nowhere near as good as Si Nian's.","To avoid messing up those events, she started working hard and studying on her own.","In the end, not only did she host successfully, but she also gained a little fame and made it into the newspaper.","Later, their city decided to establish a news television station.","Because of her outstanding performances, Fu Qianqian was invited to be the news anchor for the city.","Since a TV host needed to have a good aura, be fluent in both Chinese and English, and because she was already an experienced broadcaster, the higher-ups offered her a very high salary.","Fu Qianqian was naturally overjoyed. She had achieved success in both her career and her studies. She even mentioned that, barring any accidents, Si Nian would be seeing her on TV from now on.","She said she was very nervous, afraid she wouldn't do a good job, and was also a bit reluctant to give up her broadcasting job, hoping Si Nian could give her some guidance.","Most importantly, going to the TV station required them to have an elegant, simple, and capable aura. She had looked at the TV stations in Beijing and noticed that the hosts all had short hair.","She didn't want short hair because she had previously been told she looked like a man with short hair, which was why she still couldn't find a boyfriend.","Torn between her career and finding a partner, she didn't know what to do.","In response, Si Nian told her to go for it boldly. A broadcaster had nowhere near the upward mobility of a TV host. Besides, as televisions became more widespread in the future, fewer and fewer people would use radios, and many companies would face layoffs or bankruptcy.","But being a TV host was an enduring profession.","As for the short hair, Si Nian suggested she could use a wig. After all, even Si Nian herself couldn't bear to cut her hair when she gave birth and did her postpartum confinement, so she naturally understood Fu Qianqian's feelings.","Although she didn't quite understand why Yu Dong hadn't managed to woo her yet, to be honest, Si Nian didn't like playing matchmaker or setting people up.","She felt that if two people truly liked each other, they would eventually get together.","If one party wasn't interested, forcing them together would only make things strained. If conflicts arose later, she would end up being the bad guy.","So, she neither meddled nor pointed it out.","Finally, she added a sentence at the end: I definitely won't be watching you; it would burn my eyes.","Having gained the approval of her former rival, Fu Qianqian naturally felt a surge of confidence.","Seeing Si Nian's last sentence about not watching and saying it would burn her eyes, she got exasperated, which only strengthened her resolve to become a host. She thought to herself: It's your loss if you don't watch!","On the day Fu Qianqian took her post, Yu Dong hurried home early in the morning and dragged his parents over to watch the news broadcast.","His family didn't know what was going on. When their son tuned in to the station, they said in surprise, \"I didn't expect our city to have its own news broadcast now.\"","\"It's developing so fast!\"","\"I have to say, this girl looks really heroic and spirited.\"","Yu Dong jutted out his chin and nodded repeatedly, \"Right? Right? Right?\"","How could the person he had his eyes on be bad?","...","While he was happy on his end, Si Nian was dealing with a headache on hers.","Her son was only in the sixth grade, yet someone had already slipped him a love letter.","Eldest Child originally wanted to throw it away, but he felt it would be impolite. After thinking it over, he brought it to Si Nian to ask what to do.","He had never encountered a situation like this before.","Thus, Si Nian laid eyes on a love letter that she hadn't even received back in her own youth.","And it was from a sixth-grade girl.","The handwriting was delicate and elegant, clearly belonging to an excellent student.","The letter was written as a poem.","It was even Xu Zhimo's \"I Wait For You.\"","\"I look at the dusk outside the window as if looking into the future; my heart has deafened my hearing. Why haven't you come yet? I hope for a blossom to bloom in every second. I wait for your footsteps, your laughter, your face, your soft hair, waiting for everything about you; hoping to wither away in every second—where are you? I want you, I want...\"","Si Nian: \"?\" She couldn't read any further.","After reading about Xu Zhimo's life, she remembered cursing the whole time she had to memorize his texts back in the day.","Now, reading this letter, it just felt full of scumbag vibes.","But the other party obviously didn't know that Xu Zhimo was a passionate playboy, and seemed to have deeply projected themselves into the role.","Only in the sixth grade and already so skilled at this.","What would happen when she grew up?","Si Nian's mouth twitched, feeling both amused and helpless.","She finally understood how adults used to feel when they watched them date in the past.","It was probably both an eyesore and hilarious.","\"Xiaodong, do you know this girl? Are you close?\"","Si Nian asked him.","The Eldest Child frowned and shook his head, \"I don't know her, I don't even know what she looks like.\"","Si Nian thought: What a classic case of unrequited love.","She sighed, \"Since you don't even know her, just pretend you never received it. You are still young, and dating right now is not appropriate.\"","Zhou Zedong asked blankly, \"Then what should I do, Mom?\"","Si Nian replied, \"You're right to ask Mom about this. Back in the day, when Mom was your age, the boys chasing me could form a line around the school, but I didn't fancy a single one of them and rejected them all directly. If you don't know her, just ignore her. When the other party sees you're not paying attention, she'll know to back off. If she doesn't back off and still looks for you, just reject her directly, understand?\"","Zhou Zedong nodded and said, \"I understand.\"","\"Then Mom, I'm going out to study.\"","Si Nian knew he was preparing for his middle school entrance exams, so his study pressure had increased. A good middle school was very important. Although she didn't have overly high demands on the children herself, the Eldest Child's pride wouldn't allow him to do poorly.","Si Nian didn't say much else, only telling him not to work too hard.","Right after sending her son out, she saw Zhou Yueshen walk in.","Over the past few years, the man had become more mature than before. He had grown accustomed to wearing suits, and although he no longer had a buzz cut, his current hairstyle was also very clean and sharp, adding a bit of a mature and steady masculine aura to him.","Since Zhou Yueshen stopped butchering pigs, the fierce aura around him wasn't as heavy anymore.","He had become much more reserved.","His beard was shaved very clean. Because Si Nian was refined and often kept an eye on him, let alone growing a beard, even his face had to be kept spotless.","The skincare products she couldn't finish using were rubbed onto the man's face, to the point that Zhou Yueshen's skin was actually better than before.","Meeting the man's gaze at this moment, Si Nian's eyes inexplicably showed a bit of a guilty conscience, though she couldn't say why.","She immediately stood up with an expression that screamed she was hiding something: \"I suddenly remembered I have an appointment with Sister Miao. I'm heading out first.\"","Before she could walk out, she was pulled into the man's embrace. His voice was deep and pleasant: \"The boys chasing you could form a line around the school?\"","Si Nian laughed awkwardly: \"Hahaha, I wasn't lying, that was the truth.\"","Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly, but his voice carried a hint of jealousy, \"Our Niannian is so pretty, it's no wonder you've been so well-loved since you were little.\"","\"Of course, just look at who I am.\" Si Nian was still quite smug.","Seeing her triumphant look, Zhou Yueshen felt that the Second Child's increasingly confident demeanor nowadays was definitely learned from her.","They were simply cut from the same cloth.","He felt both love and exasperation watching her, which ultimately turned into a sigh of regret: \"I wasn't a part of your past.\"","When he met Si Nian, he was already quite old.","He only knew her in her full bloom.","But he never knew what she looked like as a budding flower.","Zhou Yueshen suddenly felt a bit jealous of Fu Yang.","Such a wonderful girl had been right in front of his eyes, yet he hadn't cherished her.","He felt heartache for Si Nian but also felt fortunate.","Because if Fu Yang hadn't personally pushed her away, how would it have ever been his turn to hold her in his arms?","Zhou Yueshen held Si Nian in his arms, his eyes full of doting warmth and love.","Si Nian heard the regret in his words. She turned around, hooked her arms around the man's neck, stood on her tiptoes, and pecked his thin lips, \"It's okay, having you in my future is enough.\"","Speaking of which, she was a bit curious about Zhou Yueshen's past and asked him, \"Tell me about when you were little. What were you like as a child?\"","Zhou Yueshen thought carefully, frowned, and said in a low voice, \"It's better if you don't know.\"","\"Why? Is there something shameful? Or were there many girls chasing you, and you're afraid I'll be jealous?\" Si Nian asked suspiciously.","Zhou Yueshen was so handsome; he must have been as brilliant and eye-catching as the Eldest Child when he was young.","If the Eldest Child was already like this in the sixth grade, let alone Zhou Yueshen.","Plus, there was that military beauty who remained unmarried for years because of him.","It showed his extraordinary charm.","Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly, \"You think too highly of me.\"","He sighed: \"If you had seen me back then, you probably wouldn't have even given me a second glance.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian became even more curious: \"Why? Why?\"","Zhou Yueshen saw her intense curiosity but found it hard to bring up. Back then, his family was pitifully poor. He always wore ill-fitting clothes with patches on the butt, and he was laughed at wherever he went.","At that time, due to the poor conditions at home, he was always like a little mud monkey. At night, he could fall asleep even if he slept in the cow shed.","How could he let the neat freak Si Nian know about such a version of himself?","Seeing her still looking at him with eyes full of curiosity, Zhou Yueshen simply lowered his head and blocked her lips.","The world was finally quiet."]},{"number":481,"title":"Chapter 481: Ending and Beginning","paragraphs":["By the time Si Nian came back to her senses, she realized she was already sitting in the man's lap. Zhou Yueshen was a large man, and she looked like a small ball in his arms. He could completely envelop her. Zhou Yueshen held her with one hand and picked up an English book on the side to read with the other.","\"I plan to part ways with Chen Nan.\"","Zhou Yueshen's voice was deep. \"The market here is saturated. There is no room for advancement if I stay here. The main reason is that we have some disagreements.\"","He told Si Nian this not to make her worry, but just to explain the current situation to her.","To tell her his future plans.","When he mentioned their disagreement, his eyes darkened slightly.","Si Nian's heart skipped a beat. \"You two had a falling out.\"","She had always felt that doing business with others was not a very good idea. No matter how good the relationship was, once interests were involved, it would definitely be easy to have a falling out.","Therefore, when Miao Chunhua invited her to do clothing business together, Si Nian did not agree.","Instead, she chose to invest and take dividends directly.","She also didn't want to interfere with Miao Chunhua's business, much less offer any suggestions, lest they disagree and create a rift.","Just sitting at home and taking dividends was good enough.","Zhou Yueshen and Chen Nan had also been cooperating for over three years.","Things had always been pretty good.","Now Chen Nan's room for advancement was huge, and it was already the largest appliance company in the capital.","Business was booming.","\"It's not a falling out, just a disagreement. He wants to do imports and expand the business overseas.\"","Zhou Yueshen's voice was cold.","Chen Nan had high standards but little practical ability, and he looked down on the consumption of ordinary people. So when Zhou Yueshen proposed doing mass-market business, although he didn't say anything, he felt that it lowered the brand's grade.","He felt there was no need to make cheap goods and always wanted to make high-end appliances.","This also led to the current appliances being expensive, which ordinary families couldn't afford at all.","But the rich people's market was not infinite either, so he had plans to go overseas.","He wanted to be a big international brand.","Zhou Yueshen didn't think there was anything wrong with his idea. Everyone wants to move up, and wanting fame is also good for their brand.","But what he had always wanted to do was a mass-market brand.","So the final result of the discussion was to split the shares. He would start his own company to make his own mass-market brand.","Chen Nan would make his high-end brand.","Neither of them was the type to have a falling out over a disagreement, but their ideas had already dictated that their futures would not go down the same path.","Chen Nan didn't understand why Zhou Yueshen didn't like running to the city or going abroad.","He only focused on returning to their remote hometown.","He felt the development there was too poor, and simply not many people could afford such expensive big brands.","That's why he advised Zhou Yueshen to follow him.","But Zhou Yueshen didn't listen, and he couldn't do anything about it.","He thought Zhou Yueshen hadn't tasted hardship yet, and worried about dragging down his brand's reputation, which was why they were splitting up.","Si Nian, however, agreed with Zhou Yueshen, saying, \"I think this is good too. Although you make money following him, you are always working for someone else. It's better to do it yourself.\"","It was understandable to want to make a big brand now, but Si Nian believed that in the future, generally everyone would be able to afford these things, so Zhou Yueshen's decision was right.","The price might indeed not compare to theirs, but the market of ordinary people was much larger.","She thought Zhou Yueshen's idea was very good.","Actually, he had mentioned it before, but because of Chen Nan's disagreement, it had never materialized.","But now that they were separated, there was no need to worry about this kind of problem anymore.","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly, but thinking that his withdrawal meant he had to leave, his brows and eyes showed a bit more helplessness.","\"I have to go back first. Yu Dong has already found a venue for me, and I need to go make a decision.\"","Si Nian didn't expect him to be so quick. Feeling reluctant to part, she hurriedly hugged his neck: \"Then you're leaving again?\"","Originally, because of work, he didn't have much time to come back every day.","Now he was leaving again.","If he left, who would get up in the middle of the night to wake their son up to pee?","Si Nian's face was full of sorrow.","Little Four was already two years old, but he still couldn't wake up on his own in the middle of the night and would wet the bed.","So every night, he had to be woken up to go to the toilet before they could sleep.","Zhou Yueshen hummed in agreement. \"Yes, I'll go buy tickets tomorrow.\"","\"Once things are settled at home, I'll bring you all back.\"","\"You still have classes. I plan to take Little Four back and let Mom take care of him.\"","\"He's a boy, no need to raise him too delicately. It's good to be independent from a young age, we can't keep him by our side all the time.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian also felt it made sense and nodded. \"Then I have to speed up my progress. I plan to go back to our hometown for my internship in my senior year, and just come back for graduation.\"","The couple made their decision, and Zhou Yueshen began to pack his things to leave.","Hearing that their father was going back to their hometown and taking their younger brother away, the older children all showed concern in their eyes.","But upon hearing that their mother was staying and only their father was leaving, they were instantly relieved.","They also wished Zhou Yueshen and their little brother a safe journey.","Little Four was still a bit confused, thinking his dad was taking him out to play, and giggled.","Si Nian put his little backpack on him and told him to listen to his dad while outside. Little Four nodded obediently before she let him go.","She was actually a bit reluctant to part, but thinking that she would be able to go home before long, Si Nian also felt quite happy in her heart.","To tell the truth, she also missed life in Xingfu Village. Although life was better now, the children had to study and she had to go to school. Truthfully, with everyone busy with their own things, it wasn't as carefree as before.","But she also knew that choosing to take the university entrance exam was not a bad thing for her. Only by making herself excellent could she have confidence in the future. The benefits outweighed the losses.","Zhou Yueshen bought tickets for the morning. Little Four could already walk on his own, but he didn't walk fast. Being led into the train by his dad, he finally realized something was wrong and tried to let go of his hand to go in Si Nian's direction.","Zhou Yueshen held onto him. People were coming and going, and the child was small; he could easily fall if they weren't careful.","Seeing that he wouldn't let go, Little Four got anxious. When he got anxious, he couldn't speak smoothly.","He pointed at Si Nian and his older brother and sister with one hand, babbling to indicate that they hadn't gotten on yet.","Zhou Yueshen lifted him into his arms and hugged him, saying in a low voice, \"Mom and your brother and sister aren't going. We're going back first, and we'll come pick them up in a while. Be good.\"","Even his coaxing was stiff.","Watching the train doors close, Little Four cried out of anger.","\"Bad Dada, I don't want to go with you, I want Mama, Mama waahhh...\" He sat tiny in his seat, sobbing.","He didn't like crying loudly and rarely cried at home. He was only crying now because he was forcibly taken away by his dad, and he couldn't help it.","While wiping his tears, he complained about Zhou Yueshen separating him from his mom.","Seeing her son leave, Si Nian was also very reluctant.","But thinking that she had to attend classes and couldn't always be at home to take care of him, she couldn't bring herself to ask him to stay.","\"Mom, when is little brother coming back?\" Second Child asked with a sad expression.","\"Your little brother won't be coming back for now, but we will go back. Once your dad settles things down over there, we'll return to our hometown.\"","Everything had been discussed and settled with the Xiao family. The children would stay with her for now, and after they turned eighteen, they could make their own choices.","So, returning home when the time came wouldn't be a problem.","Perhaps Grandma Xiao felt guilty about what happened to the children's parents, so she didn't visit them often, but she never fell short in providing for them.","Hearing that they could also go back home, the children were very happy.","After all, they had familiar faces waiting for them in their hometown.","Having seen the bustling outside world, they ultimately felt that there was no place like home.","After sending off the older man and the little one, Si Nian finally had some free time.","Without her youngest son around, she actually didn't have much to do.","The Eldest Child was busy studying and researching every day.","The Second Child spent all day working out and exercising.","Yaoyao was now in the first grade. Because she had been learning alongside her brothers since she was little, the first-grade curriculum was incredibly easy for her, and she became the class monitor right after starting school.","She was also great at drawing. Having loved to doodle since she was a toddler, she showed a lot of talent in this area.","Si Nian enrolled her in an art class.","Yaoyao would go to her art class every day after regular school.","Since it was near the library, Zhou Zedong would drop his sister off at her class after his own school ended, and then head to the library to read.","Once his sister's class was over, he would pick her up and take her home.","For convenience, Si Nian bought a bicycle for each of the three children.","Zhou Zedong's was black, Zhou Zehan's was red, and Yaoyao's was pink.","Yaoyao was now a very cheerful girl. As she grew, her little face wasn't as round anymore; it had developed into a classic oval shape with graceful willow-leaf eyebrows and beautiful upward-slanting eyes. Si Nian thought that when she grew up, she would be a stunning beauty like Liu Yifei.","Therefore, she especially loved dressing her daughter up and buying her little dresses.","To accommodate this, a separate room in the house was dedicated as a walk-in closet for her and her daughter, while Zhou Yueshen and the boys only took up a single small wardrobe.","After settling the children, Si Nian went to the university to attend her classes.","She rarely came back to campus for classes nowadays because she couldn't easily step away from taking care of her son.","She only returned to submit her thesis. Unlike in the future where one could type on a computer, she had to write it all by hand, which took her quite a long time.","Her professor was still urging her to become a diplomat, even mentioning that the university could recommend her and she could start her internship the following year.","Si Nian took the university entrance exam primarily to get her diploma, figuring it would come in handy someday in the future.","She certainly hadn't done it to become a corporate slave.","So she refused on the spot, stating that she wanted to return to her hometown to develop her career and wouldn't be staying in the city.","She thought she might become an English teacher back home. Not only would she have fewer classes to teach, but she could also help improve the rural education in their area.","It would be her way of making a contribution to the people of this era, ensuring her trip to this time wasn't in vain.","Since she no longer needed to work desperately to make money, Si Nian only planned to do what she truly wanted.","Hearing this, her English professor once again adopted a tone of frustration over her wasted potential.","Lu Yao walked in just in time to hear the professor trying to persuade her.","She bit her lip. Even though she had been studying under the professor for so long, he had never offered to recommend her for any positions.","Yet Si Nian did nothing, and the professor practically begged her every single time.","The opportunities Si Nian casually dismissed were things Lu Yao couldn't even reach.","She used to feel resentful, but her professor wasn't one to offer comforting words; he simply told her that this was the gap between her and Si Nian.","Over the years, Lu Yao had gotten used to it. She handed in her thesis and left the office together with Si Nian.","Completely baffled, she asked her, Why would you turn down such a great opportunity from the professor? I really don't understand.","Si Nian replied indifferently, Isn't that a good thing? It means one less competitor for you.","Lu Yao bit her lip and said, I did plan to compete with you in the past, but I've let that go now. The professor also said my personality isn't suited for a diplomat; I'm too eager for quick success.","Si Nian looked at her in surprise. I never thought I'd see the day you actually self-reflect.","Lu Yao's mouth twitched. Si Nian's words were as infuriating as ever, but she knew that was just how straightforward she was, never beating around the bush. Although annoying, it was the truth.","So she continued, I plan to apply to study abroad next year. I want to further my education and get a master's degree.","Si Nian agreed, That's not a bad idea. I think it's very doable.","Seeing her approval, the lingering hesitation in Lu Yao's mind instantly cleared up. She smiled and said, If you say so, then I feel much more confident about it.","...","After finishing his book and seeing that it was about time, Zhou Zedong went to the art class to pick up his sister.","There were many children coming to learn drawing, of all different ages.","Just as he reached the classroom door, he saw a little boy with a greasy, heart-shaped shaved haircut leaning extremely close to his sister, whispering who knew what.","Zhou Zedong's face instantly darkened."]},{"number":482,"title":"Chapter 482: Boys and Girls","paragraphs":["Tall, with aloof facial features, his upright posture and aura instantly caught everyone's attention.","Yaoyao had been attending classes for a few days, and everyone was already quite familiar with Zhou Zedong.","Because he was the one who came to drop off and pick up Yaoyao from class every day.","He even carried her backpack for her and treated her exceptionally well.","Everyone was envious of Yaoyao for having such a great older brother.","Some little girls even blinked their eyes, staring unblinkingly at Zhou Zedong.","Zhou Zedong strode forward and said in a low voice to his sister, \"Yaoyao, it's time to go home.\"","Yaoyao tilted her head and blinked at her brother.","\"But brother, I haven't finished drawing yet.\"","She pointed at her drawing with a fair, chubby little finger.","The little kid beside her, sporting a heart-shaped hairstyle, also tilted their head to look at Zhou Zedong. Zhou Zedong's previously indifferent expression faltered for a moment.","The other child had large, rolling eyes and exquisite, beautiful features, looking just like a doll-like little girl.","The words of urging that reached Zhou Zedong's lips took a turn, and his eyes softened a bit. \"Then draw for a little while longer. I'll wait for you.\"","Although he didn't quite understand why a girl would have such a comical hairstyle, since she wasn't a boy, it wasn't a big deal.","Zhou Zedong was originally watching his sister draw, but he unconsciously found himself drawn to the little bald kid next to her. Her hair was just too eye-catching. As he watched, he surprisingly discovered that this child's drawing skills were extremely high.","Even better than his sister, who had loved drawing since she was a toddler.","Although Yaoyao had loved doodling since she was young, she hadn't received formal training, so her technique was quite disorganized and her basic skills were not solid.","But the girl next to her, who looked to be about the same age, drew with effortless ease and possessed amazing drawing skills.","She taught Yaoyao techniques as she drew. Yaoyao was smart to begin with, so she learned them right away.","The two children were immersed in their drawing and momentarily forgot about the time.","Not wanting to disturb them, Zhou Zedong just waited quietly behind them.","By the time they finished drawing, it was getting rather late.","Yaoyao stretched and waved her little hand to say goodbye to the other child.","Zhou Zedong watched as the other child carried their drawing board and got on the bus alone. He withdrew his gaze. \"Let's go, time to head home. Mom will be worried if it gets too late.\"","Yaoyao nodded. As she pedaled her little bicycle, she said, \"Big brother, did you see? Isn't Brother Xie Xian really amazing at drawing?\"","Zhou Zedong's foot slipped on his bike pedal, a rare look of astonishment appearing on his face. \"? Brother?\"","Yaoyao nodded her little head and said, \"Yeah, Brother Xie Xian.\"","Zhou Zedong: \"? Wasn't that a girl?\"","Yaoyao giggled, her eyes curving into crescents. \"How could he be a girl? Brother Xie Xian has a little bird.\"","Zhou Zedong: \"......\"","When he realized what she meant, his face instantly darkened.","He stopped to scold his sister, \"Who taught you to say that?\"","Yaoyao was startled by his sudden change in attitude and felt a bit scared. \"Be-because I thought Xie Xian was a big sister at first too. When I called him big sister, he got angry and said he was a big brother. So I asked him how he could prove he was a big brother, and he said he could show me his little bird.\"","Zhou Zedong's face turned livid. \"Did you look?\"","Yaoyao shook her head. \"I didn't look. Mom said we can't look at other people's private parts.\"","Zhou Zedong breathed a sigh of relief, but his face remained gloomy.","Because he had thought the other party was a girl. After all, the kid was just too adorable and beautiful. Plus, being a child, he hadn't thought much of it.","Who knew it was actually a boy!","When he saw that hairstyle back then, he shouldn't have doubted his initial suspicion!","Upon returning home, Zhou Zedong went straight to the kitchen to cook, minding his own business, while Yaoyao followed him like a little tail.","Thinking about what had just happened, Zhou Zedong was still angry. Even though he knew his sister didn't understand, he didn't want to talk to her at the moment.","He had to make her realize the seriousness of the matter so she wouldn't be taken advantage of by boys in the future.","Seeing her brother's cold face, Yaoyao felt wronged, and her eyes unconsciously turned red. When Si Nian returned, she was also full of sorrow, her little face drooping.","Si Nian noticed her condition and asked what was wrong.","Yaoyao's little face scrunched up as she said heavily, \"Mom, I made a mistake and made my brother angry.\"","Si Nian found it amusing. She turned to look at her daughter. \"Made a mistake? Tell Mom about it.\"","Seeing that her mom didn't seem angry, Yaoyao grew bolder and reached out to hug Si Nian's arm.","She told her about the little boy in class wanting to show her his little bird.","Si Nian took a sip of tea and instantly sprayed it out.","Her expression immediately changed, and she asked in a deep voice, \"Who showed it to you?\"","\"Mom, I didn't look. I just thought he was a girl, and he said he was a boy and wanted to prove it to me. But before he even pulled his pants down, I believed him. Mom said we can't just take our pants off outside, it's shameful.\"","Si Nian's mouth twitched. Although it was an accident, considering the child wasn't that young anymore, she immediately put on a stern face to lecture her: \"You are a girl, you absolutely cannot look at a boy's private parts. If he wants to show you, you must refuse, do you understand?\"","Seeing that she was also angry, Yaoyao's eyes grew redder. She hugged Si Nian and said, \"I... I know I was wrong, Mom. I shouldn't have suspected he was lying to me just because he looked like a girl, and I shouldn't have asked him to prove it.\"","Because the other party was so good at drawing, Yaoyao was completely won over by his skills the moment she went over. She originally thought he was a boy, but looking at his face, he seemed like a girl, so she just asked him whether he was a boy or a girl.","Then he got angry and said he was a boy. Yaoyao thought he was tricking her because he was exceptionally pretty.","Who knew that upon a single disagreement, the other party would try to pull down his pants to show her.","Si Nian smiled. This little one clearly knew where she went wrong. It seemed the child was growing up; now she didn't even need much prompting to know her mistakes.","Si Nian reached out and vigorously rubbed her daughter's head. \"We'll let it slide this time. In the future, you must never doubt others like that. Not only can you not look, but such behavior will also hurt other people's self-esteem, understand?\"","Si Nian knew that some children were so pretty it was hard to tell their gender, but she didn't think it could be that exaggerated. It was just because the children were young that they couldn't distinguish it.","Seeing that her mom wasn't angry, Yaoyao immediately nodded vigorously. \"I understand, Mom. I'll apologize to him tomorrow.\"","Si Nian told her to go wash her hands for dinner. During dinner, she asked Zhou Zedong about the matter.","Mainly, she wanted to tell him not to be angry with his sister. When he kept a straight face, the little girl had to watch his expression even while eating.","It was quite pitiful.","Hearing her bring this up, Zhou Zedong furrowed his brows slightly, looking very much like a little adult.","He said seriously, \"I know, Mom. This matter isn't my sister's fault either, because I didn't realize it at the time.\"","To put it bluntly, he was just angry at himself.","If even he couldn't tell, how could his sister not misunderstand?","Second Child shoveled rice into his mouth and asked curiously, \"Big brother, what are you talking about? What's not sister's fault?\"","\"Is it really that exaggerated?\" Si Nian was very surprised. It was one thing for her daughter not to be able to tell, but her son couldn't tell the difference either?","Is there really someone who looks so much like a girl despite being a boy?","Zhou Zedong recalled, \"Yeah, just as pretty as his sister.\"","However, his facial features were a bit more defined, delicate, and petite.","It wasn't as if he had never seen girls with short hair before; he had even seen some with shaved heads, so he hadn't thought much of it at the time.","Second Child strained his ears to listen and asked, \"What? What is it?\""]},{"number":483,"title":"Chapter 483: The Precocious Second Youngest","paragraphs":["Zhou Zedong thought for a moment and added, \"His drawing skills are very high.\"","Si Nian was surprised.","For the Eldest Child to say something like this, the kid must truly be extraordinary.","\"It seems I'll have to take a look when I have time. I'll go pick up your sister tomorrow.\"","Si Nian planned to pick up her daughter herself the next day to see for herself.","It wasn't that she was overwhelmingly curious, but her daughter was close to the boy, and his behavior of pulling down his pants to prove himself was honestly a bit startling.","Si Nian felt she needed to see exactly what kind of person he was.","The Second Child had been trying to chime in for ages, but his brother completely ignored him.","He curled his lips and immediately said, \"I'll go with Mom!\"","He really wanted to see what kind of person could be as pretty as his sister but still be a boy.","The next day, as soon as Si Nian went over to pick up the kids, she heard her son exclaim, \"So cool! Mom, that's so cool. I want a hairstyle like that too.\"","Si Nian tilted her head to look and saw a child with a heart shaved into his hair, standing with his back to them, talking to a teacher.","Because of his height, they could easily see the prominent heart shape on his head.","Si Nian was speechless. Wasn't this the heart-shaped haircut that many kids loved back when she was little?","So someone was already at the cutting edge of fashion this long ago?","Seeing the Second Child's amazed and longing expression, the corners of Si Nian's mouth twitched.","It was cute enough for a little kid to have this haircut.","But the Second Child was already in third grade, soon to be fourth, and he was quite a big boy. If he got that haircut, it would be an absolute eyesore.","The teacher talking to the little boy seemed to notice their gaze and turned her head to look over.","Spotting Si Nian, her eyes immediately lit up.","\"Comrade Si, you're here too. What a coincidence. I actually wanted to talk to you about something. I was planning to do a home visit this afternoon, but I didn't expect to run into you here.\"","Si Nian nodded slightly and asked, \"What is it you need to see me about, teacher?\"","The teacher smiled, \"Well, there's an upcoming national children's traditional Chinese painting competition. We have two spots from our side, and I'd like to select Yaoyao to participate. I wanted to ask for your opinion and see if you agree.\"","After saying that, she remembered something and added, \"Don't worry, we will cover the food and accommodation. You might just need to prepare some daily necessities for her. The competition itself lasts one day, but since it's not held locally, it might require a two-day stay. The venue is in the mountain city, which takes about five or six hours by bus.\"","Si Nian frowned. It was certainly a good thing to participate in a competition; it was very important for a child's awareness and engagement.","But the child was still so young.","Si Nian thought for a moment and said, \"I'll ask my daughter. If she wants to go, then she can go.\"","She couldn't put too much pressure on the child.","Speaking of which, the child had only been enrolled for a few days.","Why did the teacher choose her so quickly?","As Si Nian was puzzling over this, she turned her head and noticed a round little head staring at her with a pair of beautiful peach-blossom eyes.","There was a hint of curiosity in his gaze.","Suddenly making eye contact with such a face, Si Nian was stunned for a good moment.","The child was simply too pretty. He was more delicate and good-looking than any child she had ever seen, yet he was sporting that tacky heart-shaped haircut, which made for a truly eccentric combination.","However, because his features were so outstanding, even that haircut somehow looked pleasing to the eye.","Si Nian examined him, and he examined her right back.","His calmness surprised her immensely.","Si Nian quickly recovered, wondering if this was the boy Yaoyao had mentioned yesterday.","Before she could say a word, the Second Child next to her stepped forward, blushing. Eyes wide, he said, \"Little sister, you are so pretty. As pretty as my mom.\"","Before he even finished his sentence, he started scratching his head in a goofy manner, blushing and giggling foolishly.","Si Nian was speechless. She had never felt the Second Child to be so cheesy before.","The boy, however, simply withdrew his gaze as if used to this. He ignored the goofy, sturdy kid in front of him and said to Si Nian, \"You don't look alike.\"","Si Nian was confused and asked, \"What doesn't look alike?\"","\"You are Yaoyao's mom, but you don't look like her at all.\"","His voice was a bit childish but carried a hint of aloofness. Si Nian couldn't quite understand why a child with such a temperament would pull down his pants for a girl just to prove himself.","Hearing this, she found it both funny and exasperating. \"Of course we don't look alike. Didn't Yaoyao tell you that I'm her stepmother?\"","She tapped her chin thoughtfully for a moment and said, \"Have you heard the story of Snow White? I'm like the stepmother in Snow White.\"","The little guy's pretty face changed, and the way he looked at her became unfriendly.","Si Nian found it highly amusing.","Having satisfied her curiosity, Si Nian needed to get ready for her daughter's competition.","Because they would be away for two days and needed to stay overnight, even though the school covered the expenses, the child was too young for her to feel at ease letting her go alone.","So she packed her daughter's clothes the night before. The next day, she took a leave of absence from work and prepared to set off with her daughter.","A bus was waiting at the school gate. She heard that once registered, the bus would go around picking people up for the competition. There were many children from the city participating, so when Si Nian arrived, the bus was already filled with quite a few children and parents.","She held her daughter's hand, telling her to stay close. Just as they went to find a seat, she saw the pretty boy from yesterday sitting alone. Unlike everyone else, there was no adult beside him.","Seeing Yaoyao, he shifted over and moved to the inside seat, clearly offering the spot to her.","The teacher stood up from the back and said with a smile, \"Mother Si, you can sit here.\"","\"Xie Xian and Yaoyao are the closest, let them sit together.\"","Si Nian nodded. She took out her daughter's small bag and the pastries her son had woken up early to make for her. \"Yaoyao, remember to share with your little friend, okay?\"","She had noticed that not only did this child not have a parent with him, but he was also wearing the same clothes as yesterday. He was just carrying a backpack with empty hands, probably having brought nothing else.","It would be a bus ride of several hours; he would definitely get hungry.","Yaoyao nodded her little head.","The teacher beside them retracted her gaze and sighed, \"It's a good thing you were willing to come, Mother Si. Otherwise, I would really worry about not being able to keep an eye on both kids by myself.\"","Si Nian asked, \"The child's parents didn't come?\"","The teacher lowered her voice, \"Xie Xian's family situation is a bit complicated. His mother works as a dancer. You know, in a dance hall. She spends her days intoxicated and dreaming, where would she find the time to take him to a competition? I went to look for her the day before, but couldn't find anyone.\"","She sighed endlessly as she spoke, feeling a bit heartbroken. \"It's a pity that Xie Xian has such great talent but ended up with a mother like that. I don't even know if he'll be able to continue learning painting with me next year.\"","Xie Xian's family had money, but his mother completely ignored him. When she was in a better mood, the teacher only had to mention it, and she would readily pay the tuition.","When she was in a bad mood, even saying one word would make her impatient.","The more Si Nian listened, the more familiar it sounded.","Xie Xian?","A mother from a dance hall?","Isn't this the name of the male star who became one of the Four Heavenly Kings of the entertainment industry later in the novel?","Because of his androgynous beauty, he once took the country by storm and was affectionately known as the Pretty Boy.","He even became the youngest Best Actor winner thanks to a movie called Break of Dawn.","Although the novel definitely exaggerated things, seeing such a face in real life, Si Nian had to admit that the novel's description was actually quite conservative.","It was just a pity that at the peak of his popularity, it was dug up that his mother was a notorious dance hostess who had not only done many illegal things but also ruined other people's families.","Dragged into the mud just as he became famous, his personality changed drastically. He began operating on the edge of the law and was eventually arrested.","If one were to ask how Si Nian knew this, it was because this person was assigned to the same prison cell as the Eldest Child.","The Eldest Child had quite a lot of screen time in the novel. After all, as the main villain, the book described him seeing Xie Xian being bullied in prison for looking too feminine.","It was he who stepped in to help him.","As for the reason for helping him, it was because of his sister who had passed away early in his life.","Zhou Zedong said that his sister didn't like to talk since she was little, and just like Xie Xian, she liked to express herself through drawing, doodling wherever she went.","He felt that Xie Xian was just like his sister.","Seeing Xie Xian being bullied reminded him of his sister, who had committed suicide because she was bullied.","That was why he helped him.","In the end, Zhou Zedong was transferred away for research, leaving only Xie Xian behind.","Ultimately, Xie Xian died too.","He committed suicide, just like his sister.","Zhou Zedong always kept this person in his memory.","When Si Nian read this part, she just skimmed over it because she didn't like depressing plots.","She never expected that, after all the twists and turns, she would actually run into him.","She knew that every encounter was by no means a coincidence.","It must be a ripple effect caused by her altering the plot.","In this life, the children were all living happily, which almost made her forget what they had gone through in the original book.","Because they had never seen the light, their world in the novel was completely dark.","The same went for the people around them.","But this time, Si Nian felt that everything would definitely be different.","She looked at her daughter. Yaoyao was pinching a small pastry from a little box and handing it to him, smiling sweetly and adorably: \"For you.\"","......","At the same time, at school, the Second Child was cupping his little face, looking completely lovestruck.","Jiang Jiu leaned his head over in confusion and asked, \"Second Brother, why do you keep spacing out?\"","The Second Child: \"I think I'm in love.\"","Jiang Jiu: \"?\""]},{"number":484,"title":"Chapter 484: During the Competition","paragraphs":["\"What does falling in love mean?\"","Jiang Jiu looked completely bewildered.","\"It means meeting someone you like.\"","Second Child used to think that when he grew up and got a wife, he would be like his dad and marry a girl as beautiful as his mom.","But he had never met anyone as pretty as his mother before.","So he had never known what that felt like.","Now he knew.","Jiang Jiu asked, \"Ah? Second Brother, are you getting married?\"","Second Child almost choked on his own saliva. He quickly covered Jiang Jiu's mouth and whispered, \"Don't talk nonsense, it's still way too early for that.\"","\"How is it early? I heard people say that dating means you're going to get married.\"","Because previously, someone tried to set his dad up on a date, saying they wanted to find him a stepmother to take care of him.","His dad refused.","Because he didn't like her.","If Second Brother liked someone, didn't that mean he was going to get married?","Jiang Jiu's imagination ran wild for a moment, and he started to feel sad.","If Second Brother got married, wouldn't that mean no one would play with him anymore?","So he said rather sadly, \"Second Brother, please don't forget me when you get married.\"","Although Zhou Zehan felt this was weird, he couldn't quite put his finger on why. Hearing these words, he nodded blankly. \"I won't forget you.\"","Meanwhile, on the bus, Xie Xian, who was sitting next to Yaoyao, sneezed twice in a row.","The teacher quickly asked with concern, \"Are you okay, Little Xian? The temperature here is colder than in the city. Be careful not to catch a cold.\"","After all, if he got sick, it would affect his performance in the competition.","Xie Xian nodded and didn't say anything.","It was already two o'clock in the afternoon when the bus arrived at the mountain city.","It was actually raining in the mountain city, and the air was a bit damp and cold.","Si Nian took Yaoyao's jacket out of her bag and put it on the drowsy little girl.","Beside them, Xie Xian looked out at the gloomy weather, frowning his little brows, not knowing what he was thinking about.","He looked preoccupied.","The teacher said worriedly, \"Why is it raining? What bad luck. Little Xian, did you really not bring a single jacket? What should we do?\"","Si Nian looked at his short sleeves.","She dug out another jacket from her bag and handed it over. \"Teacher, please put this on him. It's cold outside, and we don't want him to catch a cold.\"","Although it was a girl's jacket, the two children were about the same age, so it shouldn't be too small.","The teacher thanked her, \"Thank you so much, Mother Si. If it weren't for you, I wouldn't know what to do.\"","She quickly put the jacket on Xie Xian.","A faint fragrance entered his nose. Xie Xian twitched his nose, looked up at the front, and saw Si Nian leading Yaoyao off the bus.","He lowered his eyes, pursed his lips, and touched the clothes with his small hand.","The teacher took them to check in. Since Xie Xian didn't have any family members with him, the teacher shared a room with him, while Si Nian shared a room with her daughter.","The hotels in this era were not terrible, but they weren't great either, carrying a dusty smell.","Si Nian took out disposable bed sheets and made the bed before letting her daughter go to sleep.","Since they were only staying for one night, they just made do. She wasn't a picky person anyway.","She merely instructed and taught her daughter that in the future, when a girl is away from home, she should bring her own personal items and not use the hotel's toiletries, as they were dirty and had been used by many strangers.","Having lived with her since she was little, Yaoyao also knew the importance of cleanliness and immediately nodded to show she understood.","During dinner, the teacher brought Xie Xian over to discuss the details of tomorrow's competition. Because the topics would be given on the spot, no one knew what they would have to draw tomorrow.","She just told the two children not to be nervous and to perform normally as they usually did.","It wouldn't matter even if they didn't win a prize.","It was the participation that counted.","The two children were not nervous at all. Although Yaoyao had never competed herself, her older brother had many competitions of all sizes every year, and even her second brother, despite his poor grades, excelled in sports and frequently participated in various athletic events.","Since they were in the same school, she often went to the venues to cheer him on.","Seeing her second brother's high spirits when he won medals, Yaoyao believed that competing was a very interesting thing.","So not only was she not nervous, but she was also looking forward to it very much.","As for Xie Xian, he cared even less. This was not his first time participating in a competition, and he had always come in first before.","This kind of competition had long lost its challenge for him.","If the teacher hadn't mentioned that Yaoyao would also be competing, he wouldn't have come here behind his mother's back.","The next day, the competition was held as scheduled.","Si Nian took her daughter to line up to enter the venue.","They were not allowed inside the competition area and could only wait outside.","After watching her daughter go in, she found a seat and sat down.","The teacher next to her also walked over and sighed.","Si Nian said, \"Although my Yaoyao has loved learning to draw since she was little, she just draws freely and her foundation isn't very good. Teacher, how did you come up with the idea of letting Yaoyao participate in the competition?\"","The teacher was stunned for a moment. Indeed, Yaoyao hadn't been in their class for long. Logically speaking, for such a competition, she should have chosen a child with more stable skills.","She felt a bit awkward, thinking that Mother Si was truly too sharp.","She felt somewhat embarrassed.","Sure enough, Si Nian looked at her and asked, \"Is it because of that boy?\"","The teacher said apologetically, \"I'm sorry, Mother Si, I didn't mean to use Yaoyao. I did consider Yaoyao because her drawings amazed me. I think she is a child with excellent talent and is absolutely qualified to participate in such a competition. But what you said is also right, her foundational skills are not yet perfected, which is why I was torn.\"","\"Originally, I thought it would be fine just to have Little Xian participate, but he refused. I accidentally mentioned Yaoyao, and he asked me if Yaoyao was participating. When I said yes, he immediately agreed.\"","\"I figured it's probably because no one else is willing to play with him. Only Yaoyao doesn't care about his looks, which made him feel warmth, and that's why he acted this way and chose to participate together with Yaoyao. I meant no harm, and I hope you won't be angry.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"It's fine, it's also a test for Yaoyao.\"","It was true. With such stunning beauty, being called a pretty boy since he was little, he received not only marvels at his appearance but mostly attacks.","They called him a sissy, saying he didn't fit the mighty and domineering identity of a man.","Si Nian could imagine what kind of environment this child had grown up in.","She understood even more why he went and got such an ugly haircut.","The competition ended quickly. As soon as Yaoyao came out, Si Nian saw Xie Xian following closely behind.","\"How was it?\" Si Nian withdrew her gaze and asked her daughter.","Yaoyao said happily, \"It was so fun, Mom! I've never seen so many people who can draw. Everyone is so amazing.\"","Her eyes were filled with excitement. In the past, she was the only one around who knew how to draw, and she couldn't find anyone to discuss it with.","Later, after her mother sent her to learn drawing, she met Xie Xian. Xie Xian was incredibly good at drawing, which immediately caught her attention.","Now, seeing hundreds of students sitting together drawing, that kind of scene was a very novel experience for Yaoyao.","She felt her blood boiling with excitement.","She thought that her second brother must have felt exactly the same way during his competitions.","Si Nian smiled and rubbed her head, As long as you like it. If you enjoy it, you can participate in more competitions in the future. Not only will you meet more people, but you'll also get to see grander scenes.","Si Nian recalled that in the novel, Yaoyao couldn't speak, so she liked to express her inner feelings through drawing. However, because no one in the countryside understood art, she was left to immerse herself in her own world alone, gradually falling into depression.","But things were different now. Yaoyao had a cheerful personality. Not only was she unafraid of interacting with strangers, but she had also met more and more like-minded friends.","Si Nian hoped she would grow up bright and generous.","Only by experiencing better things and grander scenes from a young age would she avoid being easily deceived when she grew up.","In the afternoon, the results were announced.","The first place went to Xie Xian; his artwork was even purchased by an art gallery as a collectible.","His first-place win was truly well-deserved.","Yaoyao won fifth place, though it was quite controversial. On one hand, her foundation was weak and her lines were messy; on the other hand, her imagination was astonishing, and her artwork had a unique artistic conception. Several judges strongly vouched for her, which secured her the fifth place.","Yaoyao hadn't expected to win an award at all and was completely dazed.","Mom, I won an award! I won an award too! Coming back to her senses, she exclaimed and turned to happily hug Si Nian beside her.","Si Nian was also a bit surprised, not expecting her daughter to actually win. She smiled and said, Mom saw it. Go claim your prize, and after you get it, we'll go home and tell your brothers.","Yaoyao nodded and went up to the stage to receive her award.","Out of a total of ten awards, their group took two.","The teacher was grinning from ear to ear with joy.","On the way back, the teacher insisted on treating them to a meal.","Si Nian declined, explaining that she had two children waiting for her at home, leaving the teacher with no choice but to accept.","Seeing Si Nian leading Yaoyao into the car, Xie Xian then spoke up, I'm not going either.","He immediately followed them.","Oh, my little ancestor, if you're not going, then you're not going, but wait for your teacher!","After saying that, the teacher hurried after them.","The journey back took another five hours, and Si Nian's bottom ached from sitting.","By the time they finally reached the city, it was already getting late, and the parents led their children back to their respective homes.","Si Nian was also preparing to head home with her daughter when she was called to a stop.","She turned around and saw it was Xie Xian. Holding the clothes in his hands, he said with a complex expression, Thank you for the clothes.","Si Nian smiled, reaching out to take them, and said, You're welcome. We'll be heading back now, you should go home early too. Yaoyao, say goodbye to your friend Xiao Xian.","Bye bye Xiao Xian, see you tomorrow.","Xie Xian looked at her and nodded.","Only after the two had walked away did he withdraw his gaze and turn to leave.","Yaoyao originally wanted to show off her trophy.","But unexpectedly, when she got home, both her eldest brother and second brother were already asleep.","Even Da Huang only left its butt sticking out.","Her face was full of disappointment. Seeing the letdown written all over her little face, Si Nian said, Let's give Dad a call, he shouldn't be asleep yet.","Zhou Yueshen had returned to their hometown, and there was a phone at home there. Si Nian didn't write letters anymore. In the past, her family worried about phone bills and always wrote to her; she felt it had a sense of ceremony and wrote back in kind.","But when there were important matters, a phone call was still necessary.","Yaoyao's eyes lit up, and she immediately pattered over to call her dad.","Sure enough, the call connected quickly. Her eyes sparkled as she said loudly, Dad, I participated in a drawing competition and got a certificate!","On the other end, hearing his daughter's voice, Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly, his tone gentle, It's Yaoyao. You won an award? That's amazing. Where is your mom?","Mom went to take a shower. Are you and little brother doing well? When are you coming back?","Just as Zhou Yueshen was about to say something, someone tugged at his pant leg.","He looked down. His son, who had gone to bed early but hadn't fallen asleep, was wearing little pajamas and staring with bright eyes at... the phone in his hand.","Mama?","Zhou Yueshen shook his head, No.","The little guy immediately let go.","Zhou Yueshen: ...It's your sister.","His hands grabbed on again: Listen, I want to listen.","Seeing that his dad wouldn't give it to him, he yelled loudly, Sister, help! Smelly Papa is trying to tear us apart, you're going to lose your cute and obedient little brother, boo hoo hoo~","Zhou Yueshen: ...","Ever since bringing his youngest son back to their hometown without telling him beforehand, the little boy's resentment towards him had grown deeper by the day.","He handed the phone to him, and the little guy, with tears and snot running down his face, complained to his sister.","It was as if Zhou Yueshen wasn't his father, but a kidnapper who had abducted him.","They talked for at least half an hour. Seeing that he had stopped crying, Zhou Yueshen finally spoke, Are you happy now?","The little guy then felt a bit guilty, stiffening his little neck and saying, I, I'm not happy at all. Mama, sister, brother, and Da Huang aren't here...","At the thought that out of the whole family, he was the only one stuck with his dad, the little guy felt a wave of sorrow and cried sadly, Boo hoo hoo, I miss Mama so much.","Zhou Yueshen had a massive headache. He scooped up his son and coaxed, Your mom will be back very soon. Stop crying, a true man bleeds but doesn't weep.","Really? The little guy looked at his dad suspiciously.","Zhou Yueshen nodded, Why would I lie to you? Go to sleep.","Then let's pinky promise.","He held out his little pinky finger.","Zhou Yueshen's mouth twitched, but he had no choice but to play along.","He finally managed to send the little guy to his room, but just as he was about to leave, he was pulled back again.","Little Tuanzi pouted and said aggrievedly, Mama used to tell me a story every day...","Zhou Yueshen: ...","...","Ever since Second Child saw his dream hairstyle, he had been obsessing over it.","When the holidays finally approached, he clamored for Si Nian to take him to get a haircut.","Seeing that he truly liked it, Si Nian, although barely able to hold back from criticizing her son's taste, figured he was just a kid and his happiness was what mattered most. So, she agreed, taking him to get the exact same style before the winter break.","Afterwards, when they went to school together, Eldest Child refused to walk with him, finding it too embarrassing.","But Second Child felt great about himself, still believing he looked incredibly handsome.","Si Nian was busy writing her thesis and forgot to call home for several days.","As a result, just as she finished her work, a call came from home saying that something had happened."]},{"number":485,"title":"Chapter 485: Such a Filthy Insult","paragraphs":["Her family's Little Four suddenly got a fever, vomiting and having diarrhea.","He wasn't getting any better and cried for his mom every day.","Si Nian's heart clenched when she heard this.","She immediately went to the school to ask for leave, planning to go home early to check on him.","Who knew that after she had packed all her things, Zhou Yueshen called her in the afternoon, telling her not to worry. He said the child was fine, just had a slight cough, and the fever had broken the same day; it was all an act.","Her mother saw how pitifully her son missed his mom, so she helped him lie, hoping to get Si Nian to come back earlier.","Si Nian was furious upon hearing this. She originally wanted Zhou Yueshen to teach their son a good lesson, but thinking about how the child hadn't seen her in so long, she felt that he wasn't entirely to blame.","He just used the wrong method, causing her so much worry.","True, the child had been with her since he was a baby. Now suddenly taken back to their hometown by his father, in an unfamiliar place with unfamiliar people, she couldn't blame him too much.","Si Nian sighed and said to Zhou Yueshen, \"I originally planned to bring the kids back together during the holidays. When I got the call today, I was so worried that I asked the teacher for leave. I figured it wouldn't be long until the holidays anyway, so going back early would be fine. I didn't expect it to be a lie.\"","Her mother was the same, corrupted by the boy, actually telling such a lie to deceive her.","Si Nian felt a headache coming on.","Before having her own biological child, she raised the three little ones very casually and never worried much.","Only after having her own son did she realize that being a mother was truly not easy.","After all, when she took over the three children, they were already older and sensible.","Even though Yaoyao was small, she didn't cry or make a fuss.","But her son was different; he grew up in a happy and perfect family from a young age.","Naturally, he couldn't handle sudden separations.","He had a father and a mother, so he felt he could cry and throw tantrums.","Unlike the other kids, who wouldn't say a word even if they were sad, just bottling it up inside.","The contrast at this moment was so obvious.","Si Nian thought to herself: It's better to be a stepmother.","Ultimately, she decided to wait until the kids had their summer vacation before going back.","Before the summer vacation arrived, the school suddenly organized swimming training sessions.","Worried that some children might sneak out to play in the water during the hot summer and have accidents, the school made it mandatory to teach the kids how to swim.","In past years, many children drowned during the summer holidays, making this an issue parents cared deeply about.","However, a fee was required.","After all, the swimming coaches weren't teaching for free.","The parents of most boys paid the fee, but only a minority of girls' parents did.","Since girls weren't as playful as boys and wouldn't strip down to swim outside, parents felt they could save a good amount of money.","But Si Nian believed that both boys and girls needed to learn.","Learning to swim was a good thing; she fully supported the school in this regard.","After all, something that didn't cost much to learn at school would cost a lot more to learn in the future.","So, she paid for all three of her children.","Si Nian wasn't sure about the coaches' skill levels, but she felt that learning to swim was still somewhat dangerous.","Since the children were still young, she went over personally to keep an eye on them so she could rescue them in time if any accidents happened.","She wasn't the only one; many parents showed up.","Boys made up eighty percent of the swimming participants, while girls were only twenty percent.","Most girls felt quite shy, as the swimsuits were thin.","But there were also some who were quite confident and natural, not feeling embarrassed at all.","The school's swimming pool was super large and looked quite old; it was probably built a long time ago.","Looking at it, she couldn't help but sigh. In her past life, she only had a swimming pool in high school, yet in this era, primary schools already had them.","Regional development truly varied drastically. Things that people here experienced in the 1980s, she only saw in the 1990s.","Si Nian led the kids to change clothes. Yaoyao wore her swimsuit, her chubby little rolls squeezing out. Frowning her small brows, she said, \"Mom, it's a bit small.\"","The Second Child laughed at his sister, \"I told you to eat less just now but you didn't listen. Now your flab is showing, isn't it?\"","After saying that, he looked around and didn't see the pretty little girl who was with his sister before. He hurriedly asked, \"Yaoyao, didn't your desk mate, the little girl, come?\"","Yaoyao asked, baffled, \"What little girl?\"","\"The one who is super pretty, as pretty as Mom, the little girl with the heart?\"","Little girl with the heart?","Yaoyao thought carefully, and a familiar figure popped into her mind, but it wasn't a girl. She shook her head and said, \"That's not the little girl with the heart, that's the little boy with the heart. Second brother is so silly, you couldn't even tell.\"","\"Impossible, how could a boy be that pretty,\" the Second Child said, waving his hand with a laugh.","But as he spoke, he suddenly realized something was wrong.","Wait, could that pretty little girl be the boy who looked like a girl that his brother mentioned?","The Second Child: \"?\"","Crash, something seemed to fall to the ground and shatter into pieces.","Oh, it was the Second Child's broken heart.","The coaches for each class were different, so everyone was separated.","Si Nian instructed the Eldest Child to keep an eye on the Second Child. This wasn't like their usual sports; they couldn't just jump into the water casually.","She then led her daughter to the other side.","The first graders learned even less. Because people felt the children were too young and didn't need to learn, there were only seven or eight kids from each class.","Right now, they were all gathered together, a group of little kids earnestly listening to the coach teach swimming knowledge.","Although they didn't fully understand, it didn't stop them from finding it fun.","The originally heartbroken Second Child immediately forgot his sorrow upon hearing they would go into the water to swim. He raised his hand and asked the teacher, \"Teacher, is swimming just doing what a frog does?\"","The teacher replied, \"That's breaststroke. It only looks simple, but it's actually not easy. However, it's a relatively easy stroke to pick up. If you learn it earnestly, it will definitely come in handy someday.\"","\"Of course! This is just teaching you the methods, giving you an emergency survival skill in case of danger. It doesn't mean you can go swimming anywhere once you learn it. The water outside is not like a swimming pool; it's full of danger. Everyone must remember, absolutely no swimming in the wild!\"","The students looked at each other and nodded in unison.","The Second Child originally wanted to show off how he had been playing in the water since he was little, but hearing the teacher say it was wrong, he immediately shut his mouth in fright.","So he had been doing bad things since he was a kid.","Good thing he didn't say it out loud, otherwise, if Mom found out, she would definitely be angry.","He covered his mouth.","\"You're the sports committee member, right? Do you know how to swim? What are you usually good at?\" The teacher looked at the Second Child, who was a head taller than the other kids.","He had long heard that this kid was the school's star athlete.","Looking at his physique now, the teacher couldn't help but nod.","The Second Child immediately said, \"Teacher, the thing I'm worst at is swimming!\"","The teacher smiled and patted his head. Seeing his haircut, he found it amusing again. He covered the corner of his mouth with his hand, stifled a laugh with a cough, and said, \"Alright, then I'll teach you. Everyone, watch closely.\"","He taught the Second Child hand-in-hand. The Second Child's face was written with agony. Was swimming really this hard to learn? If he had known it was this difficult, he wouldn't have pretended he didn't know how.","If he had known swimming was this hard before, he definitely wouldn't have been able to learn it.","Just as he was thinking this, a conflict broke out somewhere over there, and a child lost their footing and fell into the water.","The teacher jumped in fright. Just as he was about to rush over to save the drowning child, the kid beside him suddenly slipped away like a loach, paddling through the water toward them at an incredible speed.","Logically speaking, the dog paddle is the slowest swimming stroke.","But this child swam very fast. By the time anyone reacted, he had already grabbed the crying, breathless child and hauled him up onto dry land.","Everyone gathered around. Fortunately, the child had only choked on a little water and was otherwise fine.","By the time Si Nian heard the commotion and came over, the child had already been taken away.","She only heard from bystanders that a child had fallen into the water while playing, and another child had saved him.","Speaking of that child, everyone got excited.","\"Did you see? That child has a huge heart shape shaved on his head, it's so cute.\"","\"What a kindhearted child, and with such good taste. When I get home, I'm going to get my son a haircut like that too.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","She looked up and saw Second Child scratching the back of his head, talking to the teacher.","The heart on his head was particularly conspicuous and prominent.","The teacher had a wooden expression. \"Didn't you say you didn't know how to swim?\"","Second Child replied, \"Teacher, I said I was worst at it, not that I didn't know how.\"","Teacher: \"...\"","\"Then where did you learn the dog paddle? Did a coach at an outside swimming pool teach you? It looks pretty standard to me.\"","Second Child shook his head and said, \"I learned it from my family's Da Huang.\"","In the past, it wasn't convenient to bathe at home. Second Child thought Da Huang was stinky, so occasionally, when the weather was nice, he would drag him to the river in the village to wash. That was exactly how Da Huang swam.","He just copied him for a bit, and surprisingly, it actually worked.","He learned it in no time.","So whenever he had free time, he used to love sneaking off to catch fish and shrimp.","Teacher: \"Da Huang?\"","Second Child: \"Yeah, Da Huang is my family's dog. He's known how to swim since he was a puppy. He didn't even have to learn, he's super awesome.\"","In his heart, he couldn't help but grumble: learning to swim from Da Huang was so easy. Da Huang didn't say a single word, and he learned it.","The teacher had just talked for ages and had only managed to confuse him.","It really made him want to pull his hair out.","Hearing that a dog had taught him, the teacher's mouth twitched.","He didn't want to speak anymore.","Since he knew how to swim and clearly went into the water often, the teacher let him go play on his own and pulled the other children back to continue the lesson.","Second Child was bored, so he started swimming by himself.","His head stayed above the water, so he didn't need to take breaths. He paddled with his limbs, moving forward at a slower pace, looking very leisurely.","It just looked a bit comical.","Everyone was full of envy, but someone also mocked him: \"What's the big deal? This kind of dog paddle is the easiest. He looks just like a dog, it's hilarious.\"","Just as those words were spoken, Second Child suddenly leaned back, raised one arm, kicked his legs, and started swimming backward. It was actually the backstroke.","The kid who had just spoken opened his mouth but made no sound.","A group of children gathered around, clamoring for Zhou Zehan to help teach them.","Second Child was very interested. He immediately demonstrated and said, \"Look, this is super easy. You'll get it just by watching. I'll show you.\"","Everyone nodded at once. Second Child demonstrated by swimming a lap and came back to look at the crowd. The crowd was still a bit bewildered. \"Why aren't I moving?\"","\"Yeah, is it really done like this?\"","\"It's exactly like this. Watch again.\"","Second Child demonstrated two more times in a row. Seeing that everyone still looked totally confused, he furrowed his little brows and said in disgust, \"How are you guys dumber than me? I only watched my dog swim once, and I learned it.\"","The crowd: \"...\" It felt like a really dirty insult."]},{"number":486,"title":"Chapter 486: Chapter 483: Going Home","paragraphs":["Si Nian took a moment to glance over there and saw that everyone was studying earnestly.","Looking at the first-grade side, some children had already started having water fights.","Only a few students were seriously learning.","After the swimming training classes were over, the summer vacation arrived as scheduled.","Jiang Jiu still hadn't figured out how to swim.","His athletic talent wasn't very good; although he had been learning for several days, he still didn't dare to swim alone.","He had heard from Second Child that he had been swimming in the river in their hometown of Xingfu Village since he was little, and Da Huang also swam there, which made him extremely envious.","These past few days, he had been running to the Zhou family's house all day long, just wanting to see if he could learn a little from Da Huang and Second Child. He also wanted to invite Second Child to go out and learn swimming together during the summer vacation.","Seeing his son so interested in swimming, Jiang Wenqing specially signed him up for a summer training class.","But he didn't know that Second Child was going back to his hometown this summer.","He clamored for Second Child to accompany him.","Second Child felt that he already knew how to swim and there was no need to learn again, but he couldn't refuse his good brother, so the two children went to ask Si Nian about this matter.","Si Nian was currently figuring out what things to take back. Since they were taking the train, it was naturally better to travel light.","They had everything at home, so they didn't need to buy too much. She mainly wanted to bring some Beijing specialties back for her family.","Hearing Second Child say he wanted to learn swimming with Jiang Jiu, she paused for a moment, then smiled and said, \"That won't work. In a couple of days, when your school goes on holiday, we are heading back to our hometown.\"","Second Child didn't really want to leave yet. Before they went home, he had been longing to go back, but now that they were really leaving, he felt reluctant. Because Jiang Jiu had already said he was going to learn swimming, which meant he definitely couldn't go back with them.","So he looked at Si Nian and said, \"Mom, do we have to go home immediately when the holiday starts? Can't we stay for a few more days? I want to teach Little Jiu how to swim.\"","It wasn't that Si Nian didn't want to stay, but there was still Little Four at home eagerly waiting for her to return. Moreover, she had already bought the train tickets in advance, and if she returned them now, she wouldn't be able to buy new ones.","Because it was summer vacation, tickets were already hard to come by.","Otherwise, for such a simple request, she would definitely have agreed.","\"If you want to stay, then you'll be home alone. You can play for a few more days and stay at Grandma Xiao's house, or you can go to your Uncle Chen's place. When your dad comes back in a while, you can go back with him.\"","Upon hearing this, Second Child immediately refused. He quickly reached out and hugged Si Nian's arm, \"No, if Mom goes back, I'm going back too. I don't want to leave Mom.\"","Si Nian reached out and rubbed his head, \"Alright then, take advantage of these two days and quickly take Little Jiu out to play.\"","Second Child hurriedly pulled Jiang Jiu away to learn swimming.","He also stated that he must teach him how to swim before he went back.","He even instructed Jiang Jiu that when he wasn't around, he absolutely must not go out to play in the water with other children.","Previously, when they were learning to swim, the teacher was worried they would go wild swimming outside after they learned, so he showed them many examples of accidents.","Second Child was terrified after watching them.","He thought to himself that he was really lucky in the past, and anyway, he would absolutely never go into the water alone in the future.","Now, naturally, he was also worried that Jiang Jiu would run off to play by himself after learning.","Anyway, without himself watching by the side, he didn't feel at ease.","Hearing that he was leaving as soon as the holiday started, Jiang Jiu felt very reluctant. While freeloading a meal at the Zhou family's house, he couldn't help but ask Si Nian, \"Auntie Si, can't you really stay and play for a few more days?\"","Si Nian smiled and said, \"Because Auntie has already bought the tickets in advance, we must go back. Otherwise, you can come with us to play at Auntie's house. Going back to our hometown to learn with Second Child is the same.\"","Jiang Jiu was used to playing with Second Child, so naturally, he didn't want them to leave. Hearing this, his eyes immediately lit up, and he nodded vigorously, \"I'll go, I'll go.\"","He completely forgot that he had already asked his dad to sign him up for a swimming class.","When Jiang Wenqing came over to pick him up and heard about this, he originally wanted to refuse. But thinking about how busy he was with research, his son would be alone during the summer vacation. Usually, at home, he played with Second Child and the other children. If they all left now, his son would be incredibly lonely.","He also thought about how his parents missed their grandson, so it would be better to let him stay in their hometown for a while. When he was free later, he could just go and pick him up.","Anyway, his research always had him running between the two places.","Si Nian was also worried he wouldn't agree, so she said, \"Zhou Yuesheng might also come back in a while. If you're worried, you can just have him bring Little Jiu back along the way.\"","Jiang Wenqing looked helplessly at his happy son and said, \"Then you're not going to learn swimming?\"","\"I want to, of course I want to. I'll learn with Second Brother when I go home. Second Brother's home doesn't charge money to learn swimming, Da Huang will teach me.\"","Jiang Jiu said.","\"Second Brother said Da Huang teaches fast.\"","Jiang Wenqing: \".......\"","His son was over ten years old, how could he still be so foolish.","However, he was always reluctant to refuse his son's requests. His happiness was the most important thing to him.","So he nodded and said, \"Alright then, I'll have to trouble Comrade Si. I'm really embarrassed to always have you help me take care of my Little Jiu.\"","Si Nian raised an eyebrow, \"Still being polite with me? Back then, when my kids were coming over to study, Jiang Jiu couldn't bear to part with them and even wanted to run away from home to follow them. Could I just leave him behind and ignore him?\"","\"It's just that tickets might be hard to buy. Right now, there are probably only standing tickets left. See if you can buy one. If you can, he can go with us. I bought a sleeper ticket, so he can sleep with Second Child then.\"","Jiang Wenqing nodded. Hearing that tickets might be sold out, Jiang Jiu hurriedly pulled his dad to go buy a ticket.","Jiang Wenqing didn't want to seek special privileges either, so he bought a ticket at a high price from some scalpers.","Now all the children were happy.","They were happy, but Xiao Bowen wasn't happy.","Because he couldn't find an excuse, and he actually really wanted to go together too.","If you asked him why he knew the Zhou family was leaving, it was actually quite obvious.","Because these past few days, his grandma had been preparing every day, saying that Teacher Si was going home and she needed to buy more gifts for the children to take back.","He was even the one who went with her to buy them.","Of course he knew.","Unfortunately, he wasn't like Jiang Jiu, who dared to act spoiled with Teacher Si.","Otherwise, Xiao Bowen thought, if he also wanted to go, his grandma would definitely agree too. She was very supportive of him playing with Second Child and the others.","It was just that he was too proud to ask for help and suffered in silence, simply unable to open his mouth.","Chen Haoran originally came to freeload a meal, but seeing that everyone was packing up to leave, his jaw almost dropped in shock.","\"What, you're going back to your hometown? Why didn't you tell me in advance?\"","His dad had been clamoring to have him go learn at the company recently, and Chen Haoran was annoyed to death by it. He finally found time to come over, only to find they were leaving.","Si Nian took a moment to glance at him and said, \"It's the holidays, of course we're going back to our hometown.\"","Chen Haoran gasped, his tone full of sadness, \"Then what am I going to do?\"","After saying that, seeing Si Nian shake her head and not bother with him, he hurriedly followed after her, \"You're leaving, and I won't even be able to find an excuse to slack off.\"","That is right, every time his dad wanted him to do something, he would use the excuse that he had to go over to the Zhou family's house to help take care of the kids.","Since his mom was on such good terms with Si Nian now, and had previously told him not to run around when he was free but instead go help watch the kids, his dad had taken note of it.","He did not know when it started, but his dad had become especially afraid of his mom.","In the past, they used to argue, and his dad would stand his ground with a straight back.","Now, however, he was unilaterally crushed by his mom. No matter the issue, his dad was always the first to bow down and apologize.","Anyway, she was not to be provoked; at the mere mention of her, he would not dare utter a word.","This gave Chen Haoran an opportunity to slack off.","He never wanted to follow his dad into business in the first place, so naturally, he planned to run off to the Zhou house as soon as the holidays started.","Hearing that Master Zhou had returned to his hometown for business, he no longer had to worry about being called out for training the moment he arrived.","What a rare and leisurely time.","But in the end, it was stripped away just like that.","No way, he could not stay here all alone and miserable.","He said seriously, \"How about I go with you guys?\"","Si Nian finally stopped what she was doing and gave him an odd look. \"Do you still think you are a child? I don't have time to look after you.\"","It made sense for Jiang Jiu to go along, because his hometown was there and his grandparents were around, so it was reassuring.","But why would a big guy like Chen Haoran tag along?","Chen Haoran immediately stiffened his neck and argued, \"Who needs you to look after me? I can work too, okay? Let me go with you, I would be perfectly happy to just tag along and enjoy the good food.\"","Si Nian rolled her eyes at him. \"I cannot make that decision. Ask your master.\"","Bringing a guy her own age back home would probably scare her family to death.","Si Nian did not want to cause trouble for herself either.","She knew that once Zhou Yueshen was brought up, Chen Haoran would definitely back down. After all, when he was learning boxing from Zhou Yueshen a couple of years ago, his legs would tremble just at the sight of the man.","After that, the number of times he visited her house visibly decreased.","Who knew that that very afternoon, Chen Haoran would show up carrying a suitcase and grinning from ear to ear.","\"Sister, my master agreed, and my parents agreed to let me go too. I have even bought my ticket. Tomorrow morning, I will be on the same bus as you guys.\"","Si Nian: \"?\"","\"Your master agreed?\"","Chen Haoran could not stop smiling, his eyes shining with a clear yet foolish light."]},{"number":487,"title":"Chapter 487: Going to Help Kill the Pig","paragraphs":["Si Nian thought that if he really followed Zhou Yueshen to work, this halo would probably disappear very soon.","\"Yeah, I told my dad I wanted to intern at my master's company. My dad called my master, and he agreed.\"","Si Nian: \"...\"","Traveling all the way to their hometown to intern, the young master really knew how to experience life.","\"Can you still buy tickets now?\"","\"I got them. My dad bought them from someone at a high price. It's a sleeper ticket.\"","\"Originally, my dad said he would buy me a plane ticket, but I didn't want to. I wanted to go with you guys.\"","Si Nian: ? If you didn't want it, you could have given it to me!","Showing off his wealth, he was definitely showing off his wealth!","She shook her head. Forget it, since Zhou Yueshen had already agreed, she had nothing more to say.","Chen Haoran was going down to the countryside, and he was so excited that he couldn't sleep all night.","Early the next morning, Grandma Xiao brought Xiao Bowen to see them off, bringing along many gifts.","Just as Si Nian was about to refuse, saying she couldn't carry them all, Grandma Xiao said, \"I figured you wouldn't be able to carry them all, and it's inconvenient for you to travel with so many children, so I had someone airfreight them over. They should arrive today.\"","Si Nian: \"...Then I won't be polite.\"","Seeing the children wearing matching clothes and carrying backpacks, Xiao Bowen couldn't help but feel envious.","At this moment, he finally understood that even if he joined them, he would always be an outsider.","Arriving at the train station, the family lined up to board the train like a mother hen leading her chicks.","\"Brother Chen, are you really going to work at my family's company?\"","Knowing that Chen Haoran was going to work at his dad's company, Second Child suddenly put on airs.","\"Yeah, what's up?\" Chen Haoran asked, raising an eyebrow.","\"Then why didn't you tell me first?\" he said.","\"If you had told me first, I definitely would have found a good position for you in advance.\"","Chen Haoran was a bit confused. \"Tell you? You'd find me a good position? Hahaha, Xiaohan, you must be joking with me.\"","\"I'm not joking, I'm serious. Don't you know that I'm going to inherit all my dad's property? I'm going back home this time to study hard at the factory so I can be the boss in the future. Don't underestimate me because I'm young; I have a lot of say at home. My dad agrees to whatever I say.\"","As he spoke, he unconsciously straightened his back.","Chen Haoran was amused and laughed out loud. \"Alright then, I didn't expect my little brother to be a boss. Then tell me, what can I do?\"","\"You can come with me to scrape pig hair. Let me tell you, scraping pig hair is the easiest. It's fun and not tiring. It's the simplest job. I'm pretty loyal, right?\" Second Child immediately thought of him.","Although there was quite an age gap between him and Chen Haoran, in Second Child's eyes, age wasn't an issue and height wasn't a distance. He and Brother Chen had gone through life and death together, so naturally, he couldn't treat him poorly.","Chen Haoran laughed even louder after hearing this. He had long heard that the Zhou family had a large breeding farm in their hometown, but he hadn't expected Second Child to be talking about this.","\"Alright, I'll definitely learn well.\"","He said that, but in his heart, he thought that no matter what, he would at least get a job as a secretary or assistant. After all, he was a student at Jing University. How could he possibly go scrape pig hair? Hilarious.","...","It was already the evening of the second day when they arrived in the Yunnan-Guizhou-Sichuan region.","Zhou Yueshen drove a minivan to pick up the whole carload of people.","As soon as she got off the train, Si Nian saw the older man waiting outside, with a little pendant hanging onto his leg.","\"Mama!\"","As soon as he saw them, Little Four immediately ran over on his short little legs.","Si Nian smiled and bent down to pick up her son, only to find that he had gotten heavier.","She ground her teeth. This brat, all that talk about having a hard time was just him tricking her.","She had thought this child missed his mother so much that he couldn't eat or sleep, that he had gotten sick, and if not haggard, he should have at least lost a few pounds from starvation. But he actually got fatter?","Si Nian pinched her son's chubby cheek. \"Didn't you say you were sick?\"","Little Four's excited expression immediately turned weak. He dramatically covered his mouth with his little hand, coughed twice, hugged Si Nian's neck, and said, \"Mama, actually, I haven't completely recovered yet.\"","Looking at this little drama king, Si Nian felt both helpless and amused.","How did he not inherit any of his father's steadiness at all?","Chen Haoran immediately took out two thick red envelopes and handed them over. \"Little Four, these are red envelopes from your Uncle Chen and Auntie.\"","Little Four looked at Si Nian. Since Si Nian didn't refuse, he immediately and happily reached out to take them. No child would be unhappy to receive red envelopes, and right now he was dancing with joy, holding the envelopes up to play with.","After playing for a while, he handed the red envelopes to Si Nian.","The little guy looked at Si Nian and said, \"Mama, this is for you to buy clothes to wear.\"","\"When I have money in the future, I'll buy Mama a gold bracelet.\"","The little guy didn't know what things were valuable, but during this time, Zhou Yueshen would take him around to socialize, and he saw many aunties with golden things hanging around their necks, on their ears, and on their hands.","He asked his dad what they were, and his dad said it was gold.","Seeing that everyone liked to wear it, he thought gold was the best thing, so he earnestly wanted to buy it for his mama.","Si Nian beamed with joy upon hearing this. \"Alright, I'll wait for you to buy it for me.\"","Second Child immediately squeezed in and said anxiously, \"Mom, didn't we agree that I would buy it for you?\"","Little Four said in a milky voice, \"Second Brother, I said it first.\"","Second Child was furious. \"I clearly said it first. You weren't even born yet when I said it.\"","Seeing that the two brothers were about to argue, Si Nian immediately said, \"Okay, okay, can't you both buy it?\"","Second Child said, \"That's more like it.\"","Little Four loved fighting with him for favor the most.","He always loved to act spoiled with their mom.","Hmph!","Zhou Zedong had already reached the point where he disdained fighting with his two younger brothers. He didn't speak, but he would take action.","Anyway, he would definitely be the first to have the money to buy gold for their mom.","Zhou Yueshen stepped forward and lifted his son down. He was already so big, yet he still wanted his mom to hold him all day.","Seeing the exhaustion written on Si Nian's face, his heart ached a little.","The two hadn't seen each other for a long time and had missed each other dearly. He picked up the things next to Si Nian and said softly, \"It's too late, let's go back and rest first.\"","Si Nian nodded slightly. \"Let's go, let's go. The kids are tired too.\"","On the way back, Si Nian sat in the back with the little ones, while Chen Haoran sat in the front.","Rubbing his hands together with some excitement, he said, \"Master, when do I start work, and what will I be doing? I actually don't have much experience, but don't worry, I will definitely learn well and won't embarrass you.\"","Zhou Yueshen glanced at him and said, \"Tomorrow, someone will take you to the breeding farm.\"","\"Ah? To the breeding farm? Not to your new company?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"Your dad said to let you go to the breeding farm to temper yourself.\"","Chen Haoran looked a bit sheepish, but thinking that the breeding farm wasn't bad either, he asked, \"Am I going to be an assistant or...?\"","Zhou Yueshen: \"You're going to help slaughter pigs.\"","Chen Haoran: \"?\""]},{"number":488,"title":"Chapter 488: The New Factory","paragraphs":["When they arrived home, the family was still waiting for them to have dinner.","Seeing them return, Si Nian's parents each held a child by the hand, grinning from ear to ear.","After such a long time, their daughter and son-in-law were finally planning to return to their hometown to build their careers.","This meant the whole family could be reunited, no longer having to spend more time apart than together.","Father and Mother Lin were getting older, especially Father Lin, whose mobility was limited. He usually had to stay at home and couldn't help out much.","They really wanted to enjoy the blessings of having their children and grandchildren around.","Now, their wishes were finally fulfilled.","Grandpa and Grandma Jiang were also waiting. Since their own grandson had returned, they naturally had to come over to welcome him.","Si Nian said helplessly, \"Didn't I tell you to go to bed early? You just had to wait up for us.\"","Everyone had jobs to do. Her mother and sister-in-law had recently opened a small shop in the city, specializing in selling braised food.","They had to get up very early to work every day.","Seeing the whole family stay up just to wait for them made Si Nian feel a bit guilty.","Mother Lin smiled and said, \"It's fine, it's fine. At worst, we'll just open the shop a little later tomorrow.\"","Si Nian felt helpless but couldn't say much more.","Truthfully, they were exhausted from the journey and didn't have much of an appetite. The children were also drowsy.","Even though they had been sleeping on the train all day, the fatigue of traveling still weighed heavily on them.","After everyone finished eating, the children were sent to wash up and go to bed early.","Si Nian also returned to her room. It had clearly been tidied up; the bedding was brand new, and everything was spotlessly clean.","Little Four tugged at her. His eyelids were drooping, but he forced himself to stay awake, saying in a milky voice, \"Mommy, tell me a story tonight.\"","Si Nian smiled and agreed, telling him to get into bed first while she went to wash up.","But by the time she came out, the little guy was already snoring softly.","She pulled the blanket up for her son, then got up and went out the door to look downstairs.","Several men were still drinking and chatting.","Chen Haoran was pulled into the group and couldn't get away. His face was flushed bright red as he started bragging about his past exploits again.","As if sensing her gaze, Zhou Yueshen turned his head toward the second floor.","Their eyes met.","He set down his wine glass, stood up, and said, \"You guys keep drinking.\"","Si Nian had just stepped back into her room when the man followed closely behind.","\"Why aren't you asleep yet?\" Zhou Yueshen's voice was gentle.","Si Nian replied, \"I'm going to sleep right now. I just went to see if you guys were done drinking. You should go to bed early too, don't stay up playing with them.\"","Starting a company was inherently a time-consuming and exhausting endeavor. Zhou Yueshen was incredibly busy, and Si Nian hoped he would get more rest.","In the past, when she watched him work from dawn to dusk, she only admired his strong physical stamina.","But now, her heart ached for him. She didn't want him to only get a few hours of sleep every day.","Health was the most important thing.","Hearing this, Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly, reached out his large hand to pat her head, and said, \"Alright.\"","Si Nian yawned and got into bed first. \"How are things going at the factory?\"","\"Everything is basically set up. We've been gradually bringing in parts for trial runs recently.\"","\"Is it easy to hire workers?\" Si Nian asked.","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly. \"Not difficult.\"","Si Nian thought about it and agreed. After all, in this era, as long as the pay was good, nothing was too difficult.","As for the appliances, they were just assembled piece by piece from various parts. Each person only needed to learn one step, so it wasn't particularly hard.","With a day or two of training, they could easily pick it up.","Si Nian felt relieved.","A new electrical appliance factory had suddenly opened in the city, and its scale was quite large, which immediately attracted many people to apply for jobs.","In fact, the appliances in their city were basically all shipped in from other places to be sold.","Because of the long-distance transportation, travel expenses, and labor costs, coupled with the fact that appliances were inherently expensive, even a standard black-and-white TV could sell for around 500 yuan.","Color TVs cost over a thousand, and imported ones were even more expensive.","Because of this, not many people could afford them.","But the demand was quite high. Even if people couldn't afford them, rarity increased their value, and everyone wanted one.","So now that an appliance factory had suddenly opened, people were naturally incredibly curious, and many were watching closely.","Over the past two years, as more and more people started doing business, the city's economy had begun to develop rapidly.","Many had already realized that working a regular job would never make them rich.","As a result, an increasing number of middle-class families joined the ranks of business owners. Although some failed and lost everything, far more people made a fortune, making the temptation even greater.","It was in this era that many ordinary people changed their lives and embarked on the path to wealth relying simply on their boldness.","People no longer ostracized self-employed individuals like they did a few years ago; in fact, many even started to envy them.","Of course, the majority still believed that having an iron rice bowl—a stable, state-assigned job—was the most respectable and important thing.","Father Si was exactly this kind of person.","It wasn't that he wanted to change careers, but rather that he had reached the end of his service term yet still had no opportunity for promotion.","Due to the fallout from Zhang Cuimei and his daughter going to prison, he had been implicated.","He had been on the verge of a promotion, something that had seemed well within his grasp, but due to various unforeseen events, it had fallen through.","In the end, he remained stuck in his current position.","Seeing the end of his service term approaching, he was extremely panicked.","He didn't want to transfer to civilian work; to him, that would be far too humiliating.","He had always imagined that even if he couldn't become a commander, he would at least be a regiment commander.","If his son inherited his legacy, his life would be considered glorious.","But he never expected that ever since his biological daughter was swapped back, his life plans would be completely derailed.","Even though he had worked diligently and cautiously over the past few years, ensuring no one could find fault with him, he could only watch helplessly as younger men were promoted over him. Father Si saw it all, and he hated it in his heart.","He even felt like he couldn't hold his head up high anymore.","Back in the day, because his younger daughter was engaged to the Fu family from a young age, everyone in the military respected him.","Yet now, he had fallen to such a state.","Father Si seemed to have aged several years, his hair turning white.","Just as he was getting a headache over this matter, he heard the news that Zhou Yueshen had opened an appliance factory and was recruiting talent.","Father Si's eyes lit up. He thought to himself that with his rank, he should at least be given a manager position if he went over there.","Besides, they were considered acquaintances.","Although things had gotten quite ugly a few years ago, he reasoned that it was mostly his wife and daughter causing the trouble; he hadn't said much himself.","So, it shouldn't have anything to do with him.","At his age, transferring to civilian work and finding a job wasn't easy anymore.","Father Si looked down on ordinary jobs, while the truly good workplaces looked down on him.","Now that his adopted daughter's husband had opened a factory, he immediately felt he had found his new direction in life.","Early the next morning after he arrived, Chen Haoran was led to the pig farm by Second Child.","Seeing the piglets grunting and clamoring for food at the farm, Chen Haoran felt his vision go dark.","After feeding the piglets, he was dragged off to watch people slaughter pigs.","A massive stench hit him in the face, and he almost threw up.","The piles of pig hair on the ground, the group of shirtless, burly men gutting the pigs, and the floor covered with freshly scraped pig carcasses all left Chen Haoran feeling completely disoriented in the wind.","He didn't know who had stuffed a pig-shaving knife into his hand.","Then he was pulled down to squat in front of a fat pig.","\"It's very simple, you'll learn it just by looking at it once,\" Second Child, who was beside him, taught earnestly.","The foul stench of pig hair rushed into his nose. Chen Haoran suddenly snapped back to his senses, almost throwing the dirty pig-shaving knife out of his hand.","However, at this moment, everyone was burying their heads in hard work, and absolutely no one noticed his expression.","Chen Haoran looked at everyone in horror, and then his gaze landed on Second Child beside him. Wearing a small apron, he was half-squatting, scraping pig hair with a serious look in his eyes.","He froze.","His outstretched hand stiffened.","Second Child could endure this hardship, but he couldn't?","If word of this got out, wouldn't he be laughed to death?","Especially Si Nian. If she found out, she would definitely laugh at him to death.","Although it was a bit smelly, it wasn't unacceptable.","Besides, Second Child said that butchering pigs only required working for the morning, and then they could rest.","Because they only needed to provide fresh pork every morning.","They could spend the whole afternoon playing.","Having successfully convinced himself, Chen Haoran finally started learning to scrape pig hair with Second Child.","Not to mention, it was surprisingly fun.","It came off with a single scrape, giving him the feeling of playing house when he was a kid.","The two guys scraped with increasing enthusiasm. In no time, they had scraped several pigs completely clean.","In the morning, Si Nian ate scallion oil noodles with home-grown baby bok choy.","The scallion oil was freshly fried by her mother early this morning. The soy sauce itself was salty, so with just a few extra ingredients and a few boiled baby bok choy, it was very refreshing.","Perhaps it was because she was back home, her appetite had improved a lot, and she finished a large bowl.","Just as she finished eating, Second Child and Chen Haoran returned, reeking of a foul smell.","The adult and the child were discussing something, obviously both very happy.","The moment they entered the house and smelled the aroma, the two guys immediately ran over.","\"What are we eating today? It smells so good!\"","Looking at the glossy noodles in Si Nian's bowl, Chen Haoran couldn't help but swallow his saliva.","The delicious food was one of the reasons why he wanted to tag along so badly.","After all, as long as he followed Si Nian, there would never be a day of bad food.","Si Nian held her bowl and leaned away, saying in disgust, \"You guys go take a shower and wash up first, you stink. Come down to eat after you're clean.\"","The two of them finally lowered their heads to smell themselves, but they couldn't smell it.","However, thinking about how they had just been scraping pig hair, there definitely had to be a smell.","There is a kind of smell that you can't smell yourself, but others find incredibly stinky.","The two guys went to take a shower in disgrace.","By the time they came downstairs, Si Nian had already thrown noodles into the pot and told them to scoop it out themselves.","After eating, Chen Haoran suggested going to Zhou Yueshen's company to have a look.","Si Nian was also quite curious in her heart. Since she had nothing to do at home anyway, she planned to take the children to visit their old father's company.","Little Four was very excited, because when Zhou Yueshen brought him back previously, he took him running back and forth every day.","The little guy already knew the way.","He even wanted to help guide them.","The family now had three vehicles. One was a sedan, a Santana that was the first car Zhou Yueshen bought. The second was a van that he used for hauling goods, which he had already driven away.","The third was a tricycle, which her mother and sister-in-law used every day to transport braised food.","Because Chen Haoran was completely useless when Si Nian was giving birth, even forgetting how to drive—a memory that made him wake up in shame in the middle of the night—he had started practicing his driving skills hard after returning and even got his driver's license.","Now, acting as the driver, he was very steady.","Following Little Four's directions, the family arrived at the factory.","The factory was converted from a bankrupt textile mill, so it wasn't exactly new. It was located outside the city, which wasn't very convenient.","However, in order not to disturb the residents, factories were generally opened in more remote areas.","Following a straight line from here was Zhou Yueshen's pig farm.","Chen Haoran and Second Child had passed by it in the morning, but they hadn't paid attention.","It was too early then, and there was hardly anyone on the road.","But now there were many people. A long line of people was already queuing up for interviews at the factory gate.","A few desks were placed at the entrance, and someone was registering people at the front.","There were even people pushing carts over to do small business.","\"So many people,\" Second Child opened his mouth wide.","He showed an expression of someone who hadn't seen much of the world.","Si Nian was also a bit surprised.","Just as she was feeling curious, a conflict suddenly broke out in front of them."]},{"number":489,"title":"Chapter 489: Familiar Faces","paragraphs":["The car couldn't get through, so Chen Haoran had to stop. He rolled down the window and popped his head out to ask what was going on.","\"I heard it's the boss's relative who came to discuss something with him, but the boss isn't here right now. They asked him to wait, but he wasn't happy about it, so a fight broke out.\"","\"The boss's relative?\" Chen Haoran turned his head to look at Si Nian. \"A relative of yours?\"","Si Nian frowned. Her family didn't have any relatives in the city. Zhou Yueshen had always been a bit of a lone wolf; he had friends and brothers, but very few relatives ever came knocking.","Where did this relative come from?","\"Let's get out and take a look,\" Si Nian said.","She took the children's hands and got out of the car. Chen Haoran found a place to park and then squeezed his way into the crowd.","They saw Si's Father, dressed in a formal suit and looking thoroughly displeased, shouting, \"How many times do I have to tell you? I already said I'm the adoptive father of your boss's wife! Why can't you understand plain human speech? Even if he isn't here, you should let me go into his office to sit and wait. What kind of logic is it to block someone outside!\"","The two burly security guards looked very troubled by his words. \"Our boss said that non-company personnel are not allowed to enter.\"","Their factory had only been open for a short time, and many people had their eyes on it.","A few days ago, someone had even tried to sneak in and steal materials.","How could they dare let a stranger in?","More importantly, their boss hadn't mentioned that his father-in-law was coming today.","If he had, they naturally wouldn't have stopped him.","As luck would have it, the boss had gone out.","There were already a lot of people around, and now they were all gathering to watch the commotion.","Seeing that these people were impervious to both coaxing and threats, Si's Father felt he had completely lost face and was furious.","He pointed at the two guards and spat, \"You... just you wait! Offend me, and you can forget about keeping your jobs.\"","Just as he laid down this harsh threat, he turned around and met Si Nian's half-smiling face.","Si's Father was startled at first, but once he reacted, his face instantly filled with pleasant surprise. \"Nian Nian, you're here too! Perfect timing. Hurry up and tell these two—aren't I your adoptive father!\"","\"Mama, who ith he?\" Little Four, with a milk candy stuffed in his cheek, tilted his head up and asked Si Nian in confusion.","When the two guards at the gate saw Little Four, their expressions instantly changed.","They might not recognize others, but Little Four used to be brought to the factory every day by their boss.","They heard he was his youngest son.","Everyone was very familiar with him.","Now hearing him call her Mama, wasn't this bright and beautiful woman standing before them their boss's wife?","The man next to her also seemed to know her.","The two guards suddenly felt a wave of panic.","A boss's wife who could make the boss bring their son to work every day was no ordinary person in their eyes.","Everyone was whispering privately about whether the boss was afraid of his wife.","Otherwise, for a grown man to take care of a child all day, even bringing him to gatherings, it was just too pitiful.","For a moment, the two large men were at a loss for what to do.","Unexpectedly, at this moment, Si Nian put on a confused expression. \"Yeah, who is he? I don't know him.\"","The smile on Si's Father's face instantly froze. \"Wh-what did you say? Nian Nian, I'm your father! Have you forgotten?\"","Si Nian immediately replied, \"My dad is at home. Don't go around falsely claiming relatives. How could I have two fathers? Do you think I'm a gullible three-year-old?\"","After Si Nian finished speaking, she looked down and asked the children, \"Do you have a grandpa like this?\"","The children exchanged glances, shook their heads, and said in unison, \"No.\"","Someone in the surrounding crowd burst out laughing.","Si's Father flushed a deep red, pointing a trembling finger at Si Nian. \"Y-you won't even acknowledge your adoptive father? You are simply rebellious and unfilial!\"","\"I don't know what you're talking about, old comrade. Do you need me to take you to the hospital for a check-up?\"","Seeing the increasingly bizarre looks the people around him were giving him, Si's Father's expression turned ugly.","\"You... you just wait! You unfilial daughter! I'm going to report you.\" Humiliated and enraged, he flung his hand and stormed off.","\"So he wasn't your father after all. That really scared me, thank goodness.\"","\"Ma'am, are you here to see the boss?\" The two guards stepped forward.","Si Nian said, \"No, I just came to take a look. Don't mind me, just go about your business. But remember, if anyone comes trying to falsely claim to be a relative next time, just throw them out directly. No need to be polite to them.\"","Si Nian didn't even know where Si's Father got the audacity to try and claim ties with her.","Back when Zhang Cuimei and Lin Sisi went to prison, she guessed this old geezer had definitely played a part in pulling the strings. But those two were indeed foolish, getting caught with both witnesses and material evidence. Si's Father, on the other hand, got off easy and shook them both off.","Si Nian actually didn't want to meddle in the Si family's affairs. Anyway, Zhang Cuimei and Lin Sisi were both in prison. If Si's Father cared about his reputation at all, he should just live a good life with his so-called adopted son, instead of choosing to provoke the Zhou family again.","Coming to their door time and time again—did he really think she was a soft persimmon easy to squish, believing that because they raised the original owner of her body for eighteen years, he could use it to blackmail her forever?","Unfortunately for him, she wasn't the original owner, and she didn't care about his moral kidnapping in the slightest.","In the past, she had at least left them a bit of face.","But now, Si Nian couldn't even be bothered to humor them.","Ever since the Si family made a move against her parents, she had decided that she would never be polite to them again.","The factory buildings Zhou Yueshen rented this time were all four stories high. Inside each floor were assembly line-style workstations. Some people were still undergoing training, while others had already started working.","The first floor was for warehouse assembly and packaging, where some people were boxing things up inside.","Si Nian just stood outside the window looking in, without entering.","The children similarly clung to the window to peek inside.","After looking, they went up to the second floor. The second and third floors were for parts and the assembly line, and there was an elevator to send the finished products directly to the first floor for packaging.","The fourth floor housed the offices for administrative staff and the technical personnel responsible for product quality inspections. Zhou Yueshen's office was also here.","Si Nian didn't go in either; she didn't know anyone there anyway.","The group went downstairs and walked towards the back, where there were surprisingly staff dormitories. The first floor was the cafeteria.","There was an empty room to the side that hadn't been utilized yet. The area by the door was very spacious, with nothing in it.","Si Nian looked around and felt it was quite a waste.","A large factory, besides having a cafeteria, definitely needed some other entertainment facilities.","Only then could they retain their employees.","After surveying the environment, Si Nian planned to make a proposal to Zhou Yueshen.","It was just about noon, and they could already smell the delicious aroma of the chef cooking.","Si Nian led the children inside. She was just about to ask how to purchase meals here when she saw Yu Dong in the back kitchen, dictating orders like a general.","It turned out that because his family ran a restaurant, he had been called over by Zhou Yueshen to help manage the kitchen's menu.","Of course, he only wrote the menus, trying his best to make the cafeteria food tasty and ensuring it didn't repeat every day.","Long time no see, Yu Dong had matured quite a bit.","He had to be at least twenty-six or twenty-seven by now.","She wondered how things were developing between him and Fu Qianqian.","Si Nian was just about to greet him when Chen Haoran approached, drawn by the smell. \"Brother, when is food being served?\"","Chen Haoran went to his dad's company and hardly did any work, but he certainly freeloaded a lot of meals.","Now, as soon as he arrived at the cafeteria and smelled the aroma, he instantly felt hungry.","So, with his natural familiarity, he immediately stepped forward.","Yu Dong tilted his head over, glanced at him, didn't recognize him, and frowned: \"Who are you? It's not even time to get off work yet, why are you here to eat?\"","Before he could finish speaking, a crisp voice rang out, \"Uncle Yu! It's me!\"","Only then did Yu Dong notice a few children clinging to the side.","He could only see the Second Child, who had grown quite a bit taller, the Eldest Child with his usual calm expression, and Yaoyao, who was sporting two little pigtails and a pair of beautiful, curious large eyes. His eyes widened: \"Xiaodong, Xiaohan, Yaoyao?\"","\"You've all grown so big?\"","\"Oh my, Xiaohan, your hairstyle is really... trendy!\"","Yu Dong walked out, looking at the kids who were almost up to his shoulders now, feeling overjoyed.","Putting an arm around each of them, he said, \"Good heavens, what brings you here all of a sudden? Did your dad bring you?\"","\"No, Mom brought us.\"","Yu Dong then finally noticed Si Nian standing in the back. He exclaimed, \"Sister-in-law!\"","Si Nian nodded, \"Long time no see.\"","\"Yeah, ever since you went to Beijing, we've rarely seen each other. Sigh... and who might this be?\"","Yu Dong led them to sit at a table, poured them some water, and only then noticed Chen Haoran standing to the side.","He had thought he was just a newly hired worker.","He didn't expect him to be with Si Nian's family.","\"This is Chen Haoran, the son of a friend of mine.\"","\"Right, Brother Haoran, this is my Uncle Yu.\"","\"Brother Haoran?\" Yu Dong chuckled. \"Are you in the same generation as Xiaohan?\"","Wouldn't that mean he'd have to call him 'Uncle' too?","Chen Haoran immediately glared at the Second Child, feeling like he had lost entirely too much face. \"You talk too much.\"","Just because his generational seniority was lower than their mother's, he had already been made fun of many times.","Now another guy in his twenties popped out with a higher seniority than him.","Wouldn't it be a total joke if he had to call him 'Uncle' too?","\"Don't mind him,\" Si Nian said. \"We originally just wanted to come see how much lunch costs here, but I didn't expect you to be here. In that case, we might as well eat before leaving. It's been a long time since I had your cooking; let me see if your culinary skills have improved.\"","At the mention of this, Yu Dong became confident. His hard work over the past few years, researching all kinds of delicacies every day just to please Fu Qianqian, and occasionally even going out for advanced culinary training—those tens of thousands of yuan in tuition fees were not spent in vain.","Being able to work in their boss's factory meant that the meals they got to eat in the future would all be of five-star quality.","As he spoke, he couldn't help but brag a little, \"As the saying goes, to keep a person, you have to keep their stomach. If the food is good, they'll never want to leave our factory.\"","He had also made significant contributions to his boss's factory.","\"Oh.\" Si Nian gave him a look. \"Then did you manage to keep Fu Qianqian?\"","Yu Dong: \"...\"","Seeing his expression, Si Nian knew the two of them hadn't worked out yet. No wonder they weren't the male and female leads; if the main characters acted like this, they would have been scolded to death by readers long ago.","At a glance, it was obvious they were only cut out to be supporting characters.","\"Sister-in-law, I feel like I still have to rely on you. Now that you're back, do you have time to help me set up a date?\"","Because Fu Qianqian had become a television host and had strict requirements for appearing on camera, she was now basically unwilling to come eat at his place.","If one were to talk about the specific reason, it wasn't because she hated him.","She was just afraid that once she started eating, she wouldn't be able to stop.","Even when Yu Dong went to look for her, she would hide.","Yu Dong suspected that she had a boyfriend and was tired of him, so she didn't want to talk to him anymore.","He had originally prepared to confess his feelings, but Fu Qianqian's sudden change in attitude made him instantly lose his courage.","Si Nian was silent for a moment.","Then she patted his shoulder in silent comfort.","Yu Dong: \"...\"","Everyone ate in the cafeteria, and just as they finished and were getting ready to leave, the clock struck twelve.","The workers all came running over, their footsteps thudding heavily, to line up for food.","Just as Si Nian walked out, two women came running toward her.","The other party quickly made eye contact with her, then lowered her head and ran into the cafeteria.","Si Nian, however, stopped in her tracks and looked closely.","But in that brief moment, a large crowd of workers squeezed in like a horde of starving ghosts.","She couldn't get a clear look, so she had no choice but to grab the children and hurry out first.","On the way back, Si Nian fell into deep thought.","If she wasn't mistaken just now, was that girl... Liu Dongdong?"]},{"number":490,"title":"Chapter 490: The Good Boss with a Cold Face and a Warm Heart","paragraphs":["She had already found it strange. The fact that Zhou Yueshen opened a factory was only known to their family and a few of his brothers.","Zhou Yueshen definitely wasn't the type to go around broadcasting that he had started a company.","Their family wasn't in the countryside anymore, and they didn't know many people here. Their relationship with the Si family was already as incompatible as fire and water, making it even more impossible for them to be the ones to tell him.","The people in the factory basically didn't know the Si family.","So even though a factory had opened here, probably very few people knew whose company it actually was.","Yet Si's Father was able to come straight over.","She certainly didn't think Si's Father was someone with nothing better to do than snoop around to see what Zhou Yueshen was up to.","Now Liu Dongdong had appeared in Zhou Yueshen's factory, and it looked like she was an employee.","Then it was very obvious.","It was just that Si Nian didn't quite understand why Liu Dongdong would think of coming to work at Zhou Yueshen's factory.","Didn't she feel awkward?","She used to be on Lin Sisi's side. Even though she was just putting on an act with Lin Sisi, they had still met before.","To show up here now as if it were the most natural thing in the world truly made her a piece of work.","Even if she wasn't embarrassed, Si Nian felt embarrassed for her.","Si Nian thought carefully about Liu Dongdong's fate in the novel.","In the end, she failed to destroy the marriage of the male and female leads, was suppressed to the point where she couldn't survive in the city, and eventually left.","Because her character was written off, it was unclear what she actually went on to do.","So Si Nian didn't know what happened to this person later on either.","But no matter what, she wouldn't just let someone as scheming as Liu Dongdong stay in Zhou Yueshen's factory.","Who knew what this woman was plotting next?","Lin's mother came back very early today and bought a lot of groceries, saying she wanted to make dumplings for them.","Her sister-in-law was watching the shop alone.","Her oldest brother and sister-in-law had moved out a long time ago. They didn't live here with her parents, saying they felt bad staying for so long, so they moved out a couple of years ago after her brother's leg recovered.","The two of them rented a place right above the shop, which was very convenient for business.","Her two younger brothers stayed in the dormitories at school.","Although Si Nian felt it didn't matter, the Lin family was worried that outsiders would gossip and say awful things like the wife's whole family was taking over the daughter and son-in-law's home.","So the sons only came over to visit occasionally during holidays.","Sometimes they would also have them go back to their hometown.","Now that it was summer vacation, the two younger brothers had already returned to their hometown to look after the house.","As Lin's mother made dumplings and saw Si Nian coming over to help, she mentioned, \"If I had known you were coming back so soon, I would have told your brothers to wait a bit before going back. They've been asking when you would return for a long time.\"","Si Nian thought about how, even though they could call, her brothers were still used to writing her letters frequently. She missed them a bit too.","\"I also want to go back to our hometown for a visit. It's been a long time since I went back. I don't even know if the house is still livable.\"","Thinking back to when she first transmigrated and went straight to the Zhou family, she hadn't expected time to pass so quickly. In the blink of an eye, several years had already gone by.","After moving to the city, she rarely went back.","Now that she had time, she naturally had to go back and take a look, as well as thank Aunt Zhang for helping her look after the house.","However, she still needed to talk to Zhou Yueshen about this.","Lin's mother said, \"You should go back and take a look. It just so happens your dad also misses our hometown every day, and I was thinking about whether we should go back during this time. Since you mentioned it, we can all go together.\"","Si Nian nodded, then heard her add, \"But your brother and sister-in-law probably won't be able to go. Someone has to keep an eye on the shop. We can't just leave your sister-in-law here alone, and if we close the shop, she definitely wouldn't be able to bear it.\"","Si Nian said, \"It's fine. My sister-in-law and the others live right here; they can go home whenever they want. It's not like she has to accompany me just because we're going.\"","Lin's mother smiled in agreement and added, \"Your oldest brother and sister-in-law have saved up quite a bit of money over these years. Renting a house is always inconvenient. I think it would be better for them to buy a house; it will be more convenient when they have children in the future.\"","\"You mentioned it to me before, but the family didn't have much money, and buying a house is no small matter, so I never brought it up. A while ago, I mentioned it to your sister-in-law and the others, and they also thought it was feasible.\"","\"Your dad and I also have some savings on hand. We can't afford to buy a house, but building a two-story house back in our hometown is doable. We can't have you going back to our hometown without even a place to sleep.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Alright. Since you'll definitely want to retire in our hometown in the future anyway, let's build it there. It's quiet for retirement.\"","Lin's mother smiled happily.","When Zhou Yueshen returned that night, he smelled of alcohol. Si Nian knew he must have been out socializing.","\"You're not asleep yet?\" Zhou Yueshen paused in surprise when he saw her.","Si Nian nodded. \"I have something to tell you.\"","She stood up and said, \"You probably didn't eat much. I'll go boil a bowl of dumplings for you. Mom and I made them this afternoon.\"","How could Zhou Yueshen let her cook for him? He followed her. \"I'll do it.\"","\"Yu Dong said you went to the factory during the day? Why didn't you tell me?\" he turned his head to ask Si Nian while boiling water.","Si Nian took a bowl and prepared the soup base for him.","Hearing this, she nodded. \"I originally wanted to go for a tour, but I didn't expect you to be out. We just walked around on our own, grabbed a free meal at the cafeteria, and left.\"","Zhou Yueshen chuckled. \"Did Xiao Ze show you the way?\"","Si Nian replied, \"Yeah. Don't underestimate Little Four just because he's small; his memory is actually very good.\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded slightly. \"That must have been hard on him.\"","\"Today, Si's Father went to your factory and caused a scene.\" Si Nian frowned as she brought this up. \"Did anyone tell you?\"","Zhou Yueshen frowned. \"The security guard mentioned it briefly. He said it was someone falsely claiming to be a relative, and he was driven away.\"","Si Nian immediately smiled. \"Isn't it exactly falsely claiming to be a relative? Even though he raised me for eighteen years, whatever I owed the Si family has long been repaid. After doing such terrible things to my parents before, a normal person wouldn't have the nerve to show up in front of us again. He sure is shameless.\"","Zhou Yueshen remained silent for a moment.","\"But how did he know I opened this factory?\"","\"I was just about to talk to you about that.\"","Si Nian hadn't expected him to hit the nail on the head so quickly. She sneered, \"I was eating in your cafeteria today, and guess who I saw? Liu Dongdong. You remember her, right? The woman who testified for Lin Sisi when she stole money. She is actually working at your factory.\"","She had a look of utter disbelief. Had Liu Dongdong been secretly keeping an eye on them all along?","Otherwise, how could she have already become an employee before Zhou Yueshen had even publicized the company?","Zhou Yueshen narrowed his eyes slightly. \"I contacted Village Chief Huo before and mentioned that if anyone from the village wanted to find work in the city, they could come and try. The villagers probably spread the word.\"","Although Zhou Yueshen disliked some people in the village, he still wanted to help drive the development of his hometown.","While many people went to work at his breeding farm, most were men. After all, working on a breeding farm required older people who could endure hardship.","But for manufacturing these electrical appliances, the requirements weren't as high. As long as a person was a bit quick-witted, they could do it. This could also provide jobs and accommodation for many housewives who otherwise couldn't work. It would improve their family conditions while allowing him to recruit workers, making it a win-win situation.","Zhou Yueshen was well aware that this would also easily attract slackers and opportunists."]},{"number":491,"title":"Chapter 491: Tumor","paragraphs":["For many whose training wasn't up to par, he simply sent them back. After all, it was agreed beforehand that training was required, and they could come back if they were willing.","It was probably word of mouth in the village that spread to other villages.","Naturally, if people from other villages wanted to come, Zhou Yueshen didn't stop them.","This was what gave Liu Dongdong an opportunity to take advantage of.","If she just came to work peacefully, it wouldn't be a big deal.","But the moment she turned around, she notified Si's Father. Knowing the situation between them and the Si family and still doing this, one could imagine how scheming this woman was.","Zhou Yueshen certainly couldn't tolerate such a toxic presence in the company.","Hearing him say this, Si Nian understood.","Si Nian: I don't think we can keep this person.","Looking up, she met Zhou Yueshen's eyes. The couple happened to share the exact same view.","Immediately, they both couldn't help but laugh.","Why are you laughing? Si Nian nudged him after laughing.","Zhou Yueshen glanced at her, I was thinking the exact same thing. Great minds think alike.","Si Nian couldn't help but laugh again, You wish. It's cooked, hurry up and eat!","Zhou Yueshen turned around to scoop up the dumplings.","She then added: By the way, we're going back to our hometown for a trip in the next couple of days. Are you coming?","After scooping them out, Zhou Yueshen followed her out, I might not have time these next two days, but in a couple of days is fine. I need to personally inspect the first batch of goods. If we go back, we can bring a few machines for the village chief, Aunt Zhang, and everyone at the breeding farm to try out, as a way to thank them for their help over the years.","Si Nian thought it was a good idea. Zhou Yueshen was a generous man, giving away such expensive things just like that. But thinking about it, Aunt Zhang had watched over their house for so many years and frequently went to clean it. If they didn't have a good relationship, would people be so thoughtful to them?","Moreover, the village chief. Although Zhou Yueshen had given him shares, the old village chief wasn't greedy and dedicated himself to helping manage the business. After so many years, there wasn't a hint of failure, showing he had really put his heart into it.","The other people at the breeding farm had all worked with Zhou Yueshen for a long time.","As the boss, it was nothing for Zhou Yueshen to hand out some benefits.","Thinking this way, Si Nian truly felt that Zhou Yueshen was a good boss with a cold exterior but a warm heart.","If she had met a boss like this in her era, she would have been secretly thrilled.","How could it have felt like going to prison every day?","Si Nian even felt a bit envious of his subordinates.","...","On the other hand, after suffering a loss, Si's Father was so angry that he drank outside.","It was already very late when he returned.","His stomach was rumbling with hunger, so he immediately knocked on the bedroom door and said displeased: Why are you sleeping so early? Get up and cook me a bowl of noodles.","A woman with a curvy figure walked out of the room, seemingly a bit annoyed: What are you doing? Our son just fell asleep. I have to take him to the hospital tomorrow, so I don't have time to deal with you. Can't you get something to eat yourself?","After saying that, she slammed the door shut with a bang.","It was obvious that she had been spoiled by Si's Father over the past two years.","Because it was rare for Si's Father to have a son, he treated him like a precious jewel.","Naturally, the woman also gained confidence.","When she first came over, everything was agreed upon nicely, but humans are greedy creatures. Being without a proper title or status, only able to be called a nanny to outsiders, and even having people secretly call her indecent because of her way of dressing, she had long been unable to stand it.","Not wanting to live like this anymore, she was very anxious for Si's Father to give her a proper status, at least so her life wouldn't be so difficult.","But Si's Father always kept his mouth shut about it. With her own thoughts brewing, she naturally wouldn't behave obediently anymore.","Si's Father was furious and was about to knock on the door again, but worried about waking up his sickly son, he held back.","Ever since the son was sent over, his health had never been very good, and he was always in and out of the hospital.","Because of Lin Sisi, he had already spent a lot of money.","Now with a son full of illnesses, Si's Father finally experienced the difficulty of raising children.","So this was also why he was very anxious, wanting to find a suitable job quickly before retiring from the military.","Otherwise, he really didn't know what this family of theirs would do.","Because everyone thought he would definitely be promoted, the family's old house had long been divided up without a share for him.","In other words, if he had no job and no money, life would be incredibly difficult.","To make matters worse, he had lost face at the Zhou family's factory today.","Si's Father was very unhappy in his heart.","He couldn't help but think of his old mother's suggestion again. After divorcing Zhang Cuimei, he hadn't remarried, not only because he was afraid of people gossiping. It was more because, deep down, he still looked down on the mother of his son, a country woman who had already been married twice.","Although she was good-looking and sensible, Si's Father still felt she wasn't good enough for him.","Seeing him remain single, his mother was naturally anxious and had privately introduced him to a few women with better conditions.","He actually had some thoughts about it himself; after all, only a well-matched wife could be of help to him.","Look at the current one, unwilling to even cook a bowl of noodles when her man comes home drunk. She was truly too petty.","Si's Father calculated in his mind.","...","Meanwhile, thinking that there were still two days before going back, Si Nian planned to ask Lin's mother to buy some gifts to bring back for everyone.","Since Zhou Yueshen had taken the lead in giving gifts, she, as his wife, couldn't go empty-handed.","As for carrying the things, that would definitely be left to Chen Haoran and the children.","Poor Chen Haoran was woken up by Second Child at five in the morning to ride a bicycle to the breeding farm to slaughter pigs. He was busy until ten o'clock before coming back, and just as his head hit the pillow to sleep, he was called up to go shopping.","It was only when his hands were full of things that he realized what he was doing.","His face turned green.","He was supposed to come and experience life.","Why did it feel like being a nanny for the Zhou family!","Second Child, on the other hand, was very happy. Going back to their hometown meant he could go play with Shitou. His plan that had been in the works for years could finally be implemented, and he couldn't be more excited.","He even specifically pulled Jiang Jiu aside and told him that he would take him to learn swimming when they went to the countryside.","There was a small stream in their hometown. By blocking it with stones, a natural swimming pool would appear.","Moreover, it wasn't deep, making it very safe.","It was much more fun than a regular swimming pool.","When he and Shitou were younger, whenever they were free, they liked to run over and play. Not only could they play in the water, but they could also catch loaches, small crabs, tiny shrimp, and collect river snails.","Although they were small, they were very delicious.","Recalling this, Second Child talked endlessly.","Even though he was carrying quite a few bags large and small, he wasn't tired at all, as if he had an endless supply of energy.","Si Nian went to the company with Zhou Yueshen, intending to deal with Liu Dongdong.","Just as she followed her husband into the company, she clearly felt people's strange gazes.","As soon as they walked past, a group of people immediately started whispering.","Did you hear? That's the boss's wife of our factory.","I knew that already. I heard she pretended not to know her former adoptive father yesterday and even chased him away...","Aren't they on bad terms? I heard back in the countryside that the two families don't get along.","No matter how bad it is, she shouldn't act like that. The grace of upbringing is greater than the heavens. Tell me, is someone who doesn't even have filial piety still human?"]},{"number":492,"title":"Chapter 492: Final Chapter 01","paragraphs":["These people didn't really know the true relationship between the two families. They just heard the rumors, which spread from one person to ten, and ten to a hundred, with each version becoming more outrageous than the last.","In this day and age, filial piety meant everything.","No matter how bad one's parents might be, they were still the ones who raised and nurtured them.","Even if you didn't like them, you had to endure it and be filial.","It was incredibly rare to see someone completely disown their parents.","Let alone refusing to help or acknowledge them when you had money. What was the difference between that and an animal?","They also thought about how young this woman was. Previously, she had left the children for the boss to take care of, while no one knew what she was doing herself.","Everyone felt that this was not the behavior of a virtuous wife and loving mother at all.","How did such a good man like Boss Zhou end up with a wife like her?","She might look young and beautiful, but to them, she was just an empty vase with no inner substance, which made them look down on her.","Si Nian didn't hear any of this, but Fu Qianqian, who arrived right after her, heard it all.","Originally, she had gone to the Zhou residence to find Si Nian today. Having finally gotten a day off, she had hurried over to show off.","Unexpectedly, the children told her that Si Nian had gone to the company with Zhou Yueshen.","Only then did she remember Yu Dong briefly mentioning this matter before.","After asking for the address, she rushed over.","Her main reason was to see what kind of company it was.","Perhaps she could even introduce someone to interview them and help advertise their company.","After all, her current network was nothing to scoff at; she knew people from every newspaper, as well as various reporters and editors-in-chief.","Of course, the prerequisite for her recommendation was to first see if their factory met the standards.","Although she was good friends with Si Nian, she wasn't very familiar with Zhou Yueshen. She only knew that he used to run a breeding farm and later went to Beijing to do business.","He had only returned this year to expand his business here.","She had to be sure it was an ethical company before recommending it to anyone.","Otherwise, if she recommended it and people found it lacking, it would just cause trouble.","She was someone who sided with reason over personal relationships.","She had come over full of curiosity. Just as she saw Si Nian going upstairs and was about to chase after her to say hello, she heard these people turn around and start gossiping about Si Nian.","And the things they said were getting uglier and uglier.","She had no idea what had happened.","She originally wanted to step forward and confront them directly, but after a second thought, she suppressed her anger, walked up, and asked, \"Are you talking about the boss's wife of this company?\"","The group was startled and turned to look at her.","Someone exclaimed, \"Oh my, aren't you that TV host?\"","\"Yes, yes, I remember! Your name is Fu Qianqian, right? I've seen you on TV!\"","\"Goodness, this is my first time seeing someone from TV in real life. Are my eyes playing tricks on me?\"","Fu Qianqian tugged at the corners of her lips. \"You're right, I am Fu Qianqian. I heard a large electronics company opened here and attracted a lot of people, so I wanted to come over and interview the folks here. I just heard you mention that the boss's wife is unfilial. Did something happen?\"","As soon as they heard her ask, everyone immediately started chiming in, talking over one another about what happened yesterday.","They were absolutely filled with righteous indignation.","After listening, Fu Qianqian understood. It turned out that Father Si had come looking for Si Nian. Although they didn't know the reason, Si Nian refused to acknowledge him and had him chased away, which led to the rumors spreading like this.","However, she was a bit puzzled. \"How do you know he is the boss's wife's adoptive father? Maybe he's actually a fake?\"","\"Oh, how could it be fake? It was all said by people from their home village. It is the absolute truth. Why would they lie to us?\"","\"People from their home village?\"","\"Yes, anyway, the rumors spread from their side. Otherwise, would we just make things up? How does the saying go? Where there is smoke, there is fire. If she really had not done anything, would people be talking about her like this?\"","Fu Qianqian's lips twitched into a faint smile. \"That makes sense.\"","Seeing how easy she was to talk to, the group immediately smiled and asked, \"Are you here for an interview? Is our company going to be famous?\"","\"Yeah, it looks like we made the right choice coming here. I was a bit worried about job security, but if even a TV host is here for an interview, this place must be rock solid.\"","Fu Qianqian replied, \"I am not here for an interview.\"","They exchanged glances, full of confusion. \"But you just said you were here to visit someone. If you are not here to interview our boss, who are you looking for?\"","Fu Qianqian said, \"I am here to see your boss's wife.\"","\"Huh? Her? What do you want with her?\"","Fu Qianqian smiled, though her smile carried a hint of schadenfreude. \"To catch up, of course. I forgot to mention earlier, but she and I went to elementary school together...\"","The crowd was speechless.","Fu Qianqian continued, \"Do not worry, I will pass along everything you just said to your boss's wife, word for word.\"","She sighed. \"I do not know who fed you all these stories, but I think that person must really hate you. Gossiping about the boss's wife—it is obvious they want you to lose your jobs. If you know what is good for you, you will pack your things and leave now. Otherwise, it is going to be pretty humiliating when you get fired.\"","Their faces flushed red with a mix of shock and fear. \"No, you cannot do that! We were not lying!\"","\"How were you not lying? Si Nian and I grew up together. Do you not think I know what kind of person she is better than you do? Back then, her foster parents sold her off to a country man to take their biological daughter's place in an arranged marriage. Afterward, those same foster parents hired thugs to beat her brother and parents so badly they all ended up in the hospital. They were issued multiple critical condition notices. She was devastated. How could she possibly still associate with people like that? You started badmouthing her without knowing anything. Do you really think you are in the right?\"","Having finished her lecture, Fu Qianqian let out a cold snort and walked away.","She had to go find Si Nian and tell her all about this.","If it were not for her, Si Nian would have been dragged through the mud.","It was entirely thanks to her that Si Nian's reputation was saved.","Zhou Yueshen had a meeting first thing in the morning. He brewed some floral tea, left it on the desk, and headed out.","He had told her to wait a bit and to drink the tea if she got thirsty, as he did not have much else around the office.","The floral tea was actually brought over by Si Nian that morning.","Si Nian had mentioned her ideas to him yesterday, so he had the purchasing agent come over bright and early.","He told her to just let the agent know whatever she needed.","The company's basic infrastructure was still somewhat incomplete.","Even though it was already operational, Si Nian felt it still needed some improvements.","Pointing to the open area outside the cafeteria, she said, \"We can put up two basketball hoops here and make it a basketball court. We can put two ping-pong tables on the side. And what is this room used for?\"","The agent immediately and respectfully replied, \"Ma'am, this room is still empty. We have not figured out what to do with it yet.\"","\"That is perfect. Let us turn it into a convenience store. We can sell water, sports equipment, and daily necessities. It will be convenient. I noticed it is not very easy to buy things around here. If the company has its own store, everyone will not have to travel far to get what they need.\"","The purchasing agent nodded repeatedly. \"You're absolutely right, ma'am. I was just looking at that empty space and wondering if I should ask the boss to put something there. Doing exactly as you suggested will put it to perfect use.\"","Si Nian nodded. \"I just happened to notice it and casually mentioned it. If your boss agreed, then go ahead and do it. It's empty anyway, and such a large space shouldn't go to waste.\"","Just as she finished speaking, someone else came in.","It was Zhou Yueshen's assistant. \"Boss's wife, here is the company roster the boss asked me to bring you.\"","Si Nian coughed into her fist. Being called \"boss's wife\" over and over again was really going to her head.","She dismissed the two men to go about their work and opened the roster to take a look.","Zhou Yueshen's factory now had over two hundred employees—a modest scale, neither too big nor too small.","Currently, only two assembly lines were running.","The personnel for each department were listed separately.","Si Nian skipped right past the assembly line workers, figuring that someone who had worked in a place like the Si household would never settle for a lesser job.","Let alone someone like Liu Dongdong, who was desperately trying to climb the social ladder.","Sure enough, she eventually found Liu Dongdong's name under the Human Resources department.","How did she manage to get into HR?","She remembered that Liu Dongdong didn't have much of an educational background.","Looking further down the line, Si Nian was surprised to discover that Liu Dongdong's educational background was listed as a technical school graduate.","No wonder she was able to enter this department.","Si Nian was astonished. Liu Dongdong really kept her talents well-hidden.","To think that in the years since leaving the Si family, instead of returning to her village or choosing another path, she had actually gone to a technical school.","It was indeed a solid way out. Si Nian actually quite admired women like her—low-key, capable of independent thought, and highly proactive.","Yet, of all the places she could have gone, she just had to come here.","Si Nian didn't believe for a second that Father Si coming here to ask Zhou Yueshen for backdoor favors had nothing to do with her.","As she was lost in thought, Fu Qianqian arrived.","Si Nian assumed she was looking for Zhou Yueshen and had her shown in.","Instead, she was greeted by the sight of Fu Qianqian in high heels, dressed like an elite, powerful businesswoman.","Fu Qianqian had not only matured but also lost weight. Paired with her professional attire and high heels, her tall figure exuded a commanding presence.","Si Nian raised an eyebrow. \"What brings you here?\"","Fu Qianqian let out a cold snort, her sophisticated aura instantly vanishing the moment she opened her mouth. With a scolding tone, she said, \"If I didn't come, you wouldn't even know how people are badmouthing you behind your back.\"","\"Badmouthing me?\" Si Nian asked in confusion. \"Who's badmouthing me?\"","\"Who else? The people in your man's factory!\" Fu Qianqian rolled her eyes at her. \"I mean, it's not like you're some horribly wicked person, so how come you get cursed at wherever you go? Are you really that easy to hate?\"","Si Nian replied, \"...You're a pretty good person too, it's just a shame you have a mouth.\"","Fu Qianqian retorted, \"Oh, don't say that. I make my living with this mouth.\"","Seeing that Si Nian didn't seem to care much, she recounted what had just happened downstairs.","It wasn't that she deliberately wanted to make her feel bad; she just felt that some things were better known than ignored.","Otherwise, treating those people like good employees and being nice to them in the future just wouldn't be worth it.","After listening, Si Nian fell silent for a moment. \"Did the people from our village spread it? That's certainly possible.\"","\"You know how it is. There are so many people in the village, it's impossible for all of them to be on good terms with me.\"","\"Even so, they shouldn't act like that! Coming to work at your family's factory while cursing you behind your back—trying to have their cake and eat it too. People like that shouldn't be kept around!\"","Fu Qianqian absolutely despised people who talked behind others' backs.","Not to mention she is still working in their factory; it is the textbook definition of biting the hand that feeds you.","Si Nian nodded and asked, \"Do you remember Liu Dongdong?\"","Fu Qianqian froze for a moment, then nodded. \"Of course. When my brother was still around, she used to come over to our house all the time. Later, I heard Lin Sisi drove her away, but I am not too sure about what happened after that.\"","Si Nian said, \"She is working in Zhou Yueshen's factory right now.\"","\"What?\" Fu Qianqian's eyes widened in sheer disbelief. \"No way?\"","Si Nian handed her the roster to look at. \"And she is in the recruitment department, no less. She probably went off to a technical school over the last few years, which is why she hasn't been around much. This year, Zhou Yueshen opened up a factory, and word likely reached her ears through the villagers, so she came running. I was originally wondering how the Si family knew Zhou Yueshen was the boss here, but the moment I saw her, it all made sense.\"","Fu Qianqian immediately caught on. \"So you are saying it is highly likely that she was the one who intentionally spread those nasty rumors about you?\"","\"Nine times out of ten. After all, other than her, there probably isn't anyone who hates me enough to go out of their way to badmouth me.\"","Si Nian had just returned, and yesterday was only her first day at the factory.","Since she hadn't been back to her hometown for many years, even the locals might not necessarily recognize her right away.","Let alone gossip about her behind her back.","This Liu Dongdong was truly a malicious troublemaker.","\"But you never even offended her, so why is she targeting you?\"","Fu Qianqian couldn't understand it.","Si Nian stroked her chin and said narcissistically, \"Probably because I am just too beautiful.\"","Fu Qianqian was speechless. Did she really have no other reason besides that? The last time Lin Sisi pulled a stunt like this, she seemed to have said the exact same thing.","Fu Qianqian seriously suspected that this woman just loved tooting her own horn!","She snorted in frustration. \"...Can't you just fire her?\"","Si Nian replied, \"She signed a contract. Do you think we can just fire her on a whim?\"","\"Then what should we do? Regardless, I think there is something super creepy about this Liu Dongdong. I didn't like her back when she was with the Si family, and I hate her even more now. Seriously, why does she always hover around you and Lin Sisi?\"","Fu Qianqian gave an exaggerated shudder.","Si Nian's eyes darted thoughtfully. \"Do you remember who those people from earlier were?\"","Fu Qianqian nodded. \"I remember what they look like.\"","\"Good. I will have someone call them over.\"","\"Why call them over?\"","\"Since they were merely the ones spreading the gossip, if things go south, they will definitely go looking for trouble with the source of the rumor.\"","Fu Qianqian looked bewildered. \"But I asked them, and they didn't know exactly who started it either.\"","Si Nian smiled. \"That is exactly why they need us to guide them. As far as they are concerned right now, the culprit can be anyone, as long as it absolutely isn't them.\""]},{"number":493,"title":"Chapter 493: Killing Through Subterfuge","paragraphs":["Lunchtime.","Everyone was rushing toward the cafeteria, eager to be first.","Ever since they heard that the cafeteria chef used to work at a high-end restaurant and that the meals were incredibly cheap, basically everyone chose to eat there for lunch.","After all, who wouldn't want to take advantage of delicious, inexpensive food prepared by a master chef?","Why bother wasting time and energy going home to cook? A busy morning was exhausting enough, and eating at the cafeteria left them with time to rest.","Because of this, the cafeteria was exceptionally crowded right now.","In just one morning, people had begun bringing in and setting up ping-pong tables and basketball backboards.","A group of men gathered around, reluctant to leave; they even stood outside holding their lunch trays just to watch.","Clearly, seeing this equipment had reignited their long-dormant passion for sports.","Smiles beamed across everyone's faces.","However, at that moment, Liu Dongdong looked rather nervous.","A woman beside her noticed something was off and asked in confusion, \"Dongdong, what's wrong with you? You've been distracted all morning.\"","\"Hey, did you hear? The boss's wife came with the boss today, and they were even holding hands. It's so enviable. But I heard her reputation isn't very good... I wonder if it's true.\"","\"Don't say that, or you might get called in for questioning by upper management,\" someone nearby shushed her and quietly warned. \"This morning, a few older women from the assembly line got called in, apparently because they were spreading rumors everywhere...\"","\"Ah, really? Is this whole thing true or false? I heard it came from the people in their village. Dongdong, aren't you from around their hometown? Do you know what's going on?\"","Liu Dongdong forced a smile. Seeing Si Nian arrive today had actually panicked her quite a bit. She wasn't sure if Si Nian had spotted her yesterday; she hadn't expected to run into her so coincidentally.","But she had only taken one glance before hurrying away.","This incident left her feeling deeply uneasy, and she hadn't slept a wink last night.","Hearing bright and early this morning that Si Nian had come to the company only made her more anxious.","She wondered if Si Nian had come to cause trouble for her.","After all, regarding the incident where Si's Father came to make a scene, she worried that Si Nian might guess she had something to do with it.","Si Nian wasn't someone easily fooled like Lin Sisi.","That was what terrified her the most.","After spending the morning in fear and trepidation, she breathed a sigh of relief when she heard that management had sought out others instead of her.","She figured Si Nian probably hadn't seen her.","There were so many people eating at the time, and Si Nian had her child with her. Even if she had glanced her way, they hadn't seen each other in years, so she probably wouldn't have recognized her so quickly.","If she had been spotted, how could they not have called her over?","Still, to keep a low profile, she replied, \"I'm not really sure. After all, I'm just from the neighboring village. The people from their own village would probably know better.\"","With her saying that, the group couldn't press further, no matter how curious they were.","Subconsciously, they all assumed the rumors must have been spread by the people from her village.","Who knew that just as this thought arose, a bowl of hot soup would come splashing in their direction.","\"Ah!\" Liu Dongdong screamed as she took the brunt of the splash.","Everyone was stunned. Before they could react, several older women charged over and grabbed Liu Dongdong by the hair. \"You little bitch! So you were the one spreading rumors, trying to get us fired, weren't you! You black-hearted wretch, you'll get your karma sooner or later!\"","\"Watch me teach you a lesson, you damn girl!\"","Slap! Slap! Two hard slaps left Liu Dongdong dizzy and seeing stars.","Seeing someone getting beaten, the bystanders cried out in shock and hurried forward to break up the fight.","The cafeteria was packed, and seeing this scene, everyone crowded around, asking what was going on.","\"Hey, ladies, how can you hit someone!\"","\"This is too much. Whatever the issue is, you can talk it out.\"","A few of Liu Dongdong's colleagues rushed up to intervene.","But how could a few young women possibly overpower a group of furious, aggrieved older women?","The older women shouted angrily, \"How are we being too much? She almost got us fired! Why shouldn't we teach her a lesson!\"","\"Exactly! If it weren't for her rotten mouth spreading rumors everywhere, would we have misunderstood the boss's wife and been called in for questioning by management?\"","\"We got fined, yet the main culprit gets to sit here eating comfortably! How is that fair!\"","Hearing this, the crowd gasped in surprise.","\"They couldn't be talking about the boss's wife kicking out her adoptive father yesterday, could they?\"","\"Yes, yes, yes. It sounded pretty harsh, but I asked the people from Xingfu Village, and they said the boss's wife used to be horribly bullied by her adoptive family, which is why she cut ties with them. I didn't expect it to blow up like this.\"","The onlookers began to chatter animatedly.","A few of her colleagues flushed red, looking at Liu Dongdong in disbelief. \"Dongdong, didn't you just say that the people from their village said it themselves? It has nothing to do with you, right? Hurry up and explain it to them.\"","\"Yeah, you're not that kind of person.\"","Someone from Xingfu Village heard this and immediately jumped up in anger. \"What nonsense! Everyone in our village has a great relationship with Boss Zhou's family. When they got married, the whole village attended. We've met the boss's wife, so how could we possibly gossip about her!\"","\"Oh, Liu Dongdong? I was wondering why that name sounded so familiar! So it's you! I heard that when Lin Sisi stole three thousand yuan, you even testified for her, only for everyone to find out she was the thief! I was wondering where you ran off to—turns out you sneaked into our factory to ruin things for people here!\"","\"And you actually tried to frame the people of Xingfu Village! Are you looking for a death wish?\"","A group of people from Xingfu Village glared at her fiercely!","Now, Liu Dongdong had truly incurred public wrath.","Her colleagues were dumbfounded hearing this.","So that was the truth.","They remembered what Liu Dongdong had just told them—that she wasn't sure and that the people from Xingfu Village must have spread it themselves.","Everyone's expressions instantly darkened.","It turned out she was a thief crying 'catch the thief' all along!","What kind of good person would testify for a thief anyway!","Before the crowd could even process their shock, the factory management arrived.","Yu Dong walked at the forefront.","Liu Dongdong was covered in soup and looked completely wretched, her face deathly pale. Being rather petite with a small frame, she looked somewhat pitiful.","However, Yu Dong, leading the group, kept a cold expression. \"So you are Liu Dongdong. Hearing about you really doesn't compare to seeing you in person. Please come with us.\"","Seeing that the factory management had arrived, the crowd didn't dare to cause any more trouble and quickly made way.","Liu Dongdong was taken away.","Her final fate would undoubtedly be termination.","Everyone felt she deserved it and found it immensely satisfying.","Liu Dongdong had violated her company contract by privately causing trouble, spreading rumors, and inciting internal conflict within the company.","It was only natural that she be fired.","It also served as a warning to anyone else who might spread rumors.","And Si Nian hadn't even needed to show her face for the matter to be perfectly resolved.","Not only did they catch Liu Dongdong violating the contract stipulations, but they also amplified the incident of her spreading rumors.","As a result, everyone found out that Liu Dongdong was the one spreading the rumor, and he ended up offending the entire group of employees from Xingfu Village.","Originally, the core of the issue was people criticizing Si Nian for driving away her adoptive father.","But now, the focus had shifted. It became a scandal about Liu Dongdong spreading false rumors and framing the people from Xingfu Village.","What was once a personal matter between two individuals had escalated into a bitter conflict between two villages.","Now, Liu Dongdong had not only alienated the company but also made an enemy out of everyone from Xingfu Village.","Fu Qianqian had initially been puzzled. Zhou Yueshen could have simply stepped in and fired the man. Why did Si Nian have to make things so complicated?","Now she understood.","This was the classic strategy of borrowing a knife to kill someone.","Si Nian: Couldn't you use a better phrase to describe it?","She was clearly just giving him a taste of his own medicine.","Liu Dongdong had brought this upon himself.","Regardless of how you looked at it, Fu Qianqian felt that Si Nian was a truly terrifying person.","Thank goodness they were no longer enemies."]},{"number":494,"title":"Chapter 494: Return to Village Visit","paragraphs":["Liu Dongdong never expected that after surviving for hundreds of chapters by Lin Sisi's side, fancying herself clever enough to play the Si family for fools, she wouldn't even last two chapters against Si Nian before being written off.","She was still in a state of utter bewilderment.","They had hotpot for dinner. It had to be said that hotpot was best enjoyed with a large family sitting around together. It was fragrant and spicy, complete with the beef tripe Mother Lin had bought and cleaned early that morning.","The texture was fresh, tender, and crisp.","The children ate to their hearts' content. As they ate, they chattered away to Si Nian about going shopping with their grandmother earlier in the day, their lively voices filling the room.","Looking at the cheerful children, Si Nian's heart softened unconsciously. When she turned her gaze to Zhou Yueshen, her face held a touch more gentleness. What time are we leaving tomorrow?","Around nine. We'll head back early. I have to return in the evening, but you all can stay and play in our hometown for a few more days. Zhou Yueshen still had that serious, dedicated, and meticulous demeanor he showed at work.","But he was different from before; he would now make time for his family.","This time, he didn't actually need to go back in person.","But she said she wanted to go, so he was willing to accompany her.","Because as long as he was there, even if he didn't say a word, the children were happy just seeing him.","Zhou Yueshen didn't mind making a couple of extra trips either.","Si Nian smiled and nodded, then looked at the kids who were still talking non-stop. Alright, alright, I know all about it now. Hurry up and eat. After you finish, rest for a bit and then go to bed. Dad said we have to get up early tomorrow. If anyone can't wake up, we won't call them. They can stay here and watch the house all by themselves.","The children instantly zipped their lips and began racing to see who could eat the fastest.","Si Nian shook her head helplessly.","They had bought a lot of things, and with such a large family, taking a taxi was inconvenient, so they simply decided to drive back themselves.","Father Lin drove a tricycle himself, and right now he was driving his beat-up tricycle to transport Da Huang and some goods.","The children wanted to ride with him, but Da Huang was big now, and with all the cargo, there was no room for them.","They could only watch enviously as Da Huang lay in the back, wagging its tail as they drove off.","Meanwhile, they had to squeeze into the crowded little car.","Zhou Yueshen placed the inspected products into the truck bed, and the family got into the car to head home.","Chen Haoran had heard that the Zhou family came from the countryside.","But he figured that no matter how rural it was, they couldn't be too poor.","It wasn't until he watched helplessly as the car entered the deep mountains, where there wasn't a single household or person in sight, surrounded by mountains on all sides, that he fell silent.","Having lived in a magnificent home since childhood, the poorest people he had ever seen were just the students from less privileged families at school.","This was his very first time truly entering a remote rural village.","After winding past mountain after mountain, they finally saw some yellow mud houses and thatched cottages, along with dirty children herding cows by the roadside, looking at them with curiosity.","Some other regions had developed quickly, and many rural families already had small flat-roofed houses, or at the very least, tile-roofed houses.","He had only ever seen these kinds of mud houses and thatched cottages in books.","And those were documentary photos from the sixties and seventies.","Perhaps he was just too sentimental, but he felt a bit distressed.","Second Child in the passenger seat saw his red eyes and asked in confusion, Brother Haoran, why are you crying?","Chen Haoran replied, I'm not crying. I just got some sand in my eye.","Second Child looked around at the tightly closed car windows...","Soon, after the car navigated eighteen bends on the mountain road, making even Chen Haoran, who considered himself an experienced driver, feel weak in the knees, they finally reached a bright, open road.","He was surprised to find that this road was different from the others.","Everywhere else had been muddy dirt roads, but upon driving over, it had actually turned into a concrete road.","Although it wasn't perfectly smooth, it was much easier to drive on.","However, looking at the various forks in the road, only this particular path was this nice; the other roads were as terrible as ever.","The car soon arrived at a beautifully scenic mountain village.","At a glance, he saw the main gate of Xingfu Village. The three large characters for Xingfu Village were carved into a stone beside the gate, and several peach trees were planted nearby.","The roads leading inside were all paved with smooth concrete.","Moreover, the village had none of the thatched cottages or mud houses they had seen earlier.","Many of the homes were built with blue bricks and ceramic tiles, or were small flat-roofed houses with whitewashed walls, looking as if they were decades ahead of their time.","Chen Haoran remained silent for a long while. After confirming that this was indeed his master's hometown, he suddenly understood.","Previously, when he heard that there were many people from Zhou Yueshen's village working in his company, he hadn't quite understood it.","He figured that with so many people in the city, it should be very easy to recruit employees at that salary.","He didn't understand why he would bring villagers all the way over to work.","But now, seeing the conditions of these homes, what was there left to question?","His master wasn't like his own father, who only wanted to make money for himself and get rich in secret.","He was an open-minded and broad-hearted man.","He hadn't forgotten his hometown after striking it rich.","Instead, he worked hard to change and drive the local economy.","That was how today came to be.","He felt an immense sense of admiration in his heart.","They hadn't driven much further before they saw a large crowd waiting at the village entrance.","Boss Zhou was back, and almost everyone in the village had come out.","Everyone's faces beamed with smiles and excitement. Children chattered and played, all wanting to catch a glimpse of the big boss from their village.","Village Chief Huo looked incredibly spirited. He used to need a walking stick, but he didn't need it anymore. As the saying goes, rural folks lack nothing but money.","Now that they had money, ninety-eight percent of their life problems and worries were solved. Seeing his village repeatedly selected as the top among the ten major economic villages, a model village, and himself as an honorary village chief... his back no longer ached and his legs no longer hurt.","Now that the most accomplished man in the village had returned, he naturally had to lead everyone to welcome him.","He had somehow found a piece of red cloth from somewhere, on which was written with a brush: Welcome our Factory Manager Zhou and his family on their honorable return to the village! Thank you for contributing your strength to the development of our hometown. Wishing you smooth work and a happy family!","Seeing this grand display, Si Nian burst into a giggle and tilted her head to look at her husband.","Zhou Yueshen remained expressionless. What is it?","Si Nian shook her head. Nothing, they set it up quite nicely.","Zhou Yueshen sighed helplessly and stopped the car.","He had only given the village chief a brief heads-up about his return.","He hadn't expected so many people.","Boss Zhou, welcome home! Hurry, come to my house for a meal. I've already set up the banquet. We won't go home until we're drunk today.","Village Chief Huo held the sign in his hands, smiling so widely his face wrinkled like a chrysanthemum.","Zhou Yueshen said in a low voice, Thank you, but I have to rush back to the company this afternoon, so I can't drink.","Village Chief Huo's face was full of regret, but he still said, That's fine, that's fine. Work is important.","Having no other choice, the family went to the village chief's house to eat.","Back when he opened the pig farm, everyone had been enthusiastic, but not to this extent.","Now, as soon as they arrived, the men surrounded Zhou Yueshen, the women surrounded Si Nian, and their children were swarmed by a group of village kids.","Even Chen Haoran found himself surrounded in the center by a group of young, pretty girls.","He didn't even dare to move a muscle, only looking helplessly toward the children for help.","But when he turned his head, he saw Second Child was also surrounded by a group of little girls.","\"Wow, your hair looks so good!\"","\"It's so unique.\"","Second Child: \"Hehehe.\"","Chen Haoran: \"...\"","Fortunately, it was soon time to eat. Everyone was busy digging into their food, so they finally stopped crowding around, though they still had to sit at the same table.","Shitou, who had specially washed his hair, came over carrying his little sister. His sister had just been born a couple of years ago and was about the same age as Little Four.","Her name was Little Yuanzi. Little Yuanzi didn't know them and curiously stared wide-eyed at Little Four, who stared right back.","Shitou stared at the heart shape on his second brother's head in amazement and couldn't help but ask Second Child, \"Second Brother, how did you get your hair like that?\"","Second Child told Shitou, \"My mom took me to get it cut. A lot of people outside are getting this haircut; it's super popular.\"","Shitou didn't understand what \"popular\" meant, but he found it very interesting and asked in wonder, \"Are all the boys outside wearing this hairstyle?\"","\"Yeah. Not only is it fresh and cool, but it's also easy to wash. One wipe and it's dry. It's super comfortable.\"","Hearing this, Shitou was instantly filled with envy and couldn't help asking Second Child, \"Then can Auntie give me the same haircut?\"","Before Second Child could say anything, Si Nian came over holding a bowl to feed Little Four. Shitou immediately lunged over, hugged Si Nian, and cried out, \"Auntie, Auntie, I want the same hairstyle as Second Brother!\"","Si Nian looked at the neat and proper Shitou in surprise. Hearing his request, she immediately burst into laughter, reached out to rub Shitou's head, and said, \"Alright, alright, tomorrow Auntie will take you to get the exact same one.\"","Shitou cheered, and the children gathered around, chattering away once more.","After finally finishing the meal, Si Nian could at last head back home.","The house was still relatively clean, but the courtyard was empty and bare. The vegetables planted before had died off. Seeing them dried up, Aunt Zhang had cleared them out, leaving the area completely bare now.","The inside of the house was swept clean, but there was still a lingering smell of dust.","Si Nian dug out the cleaning tools, preparing to do a thorough sweep.","The children didn't just run off to play; seeing her cleaning the house, they quickly came in to help.","While the whole family was bustling about, people from the neighboring village who heard the commotion also came over carrying baskets.","Some came hoping to ask for a favor to get their own family members a job at the company.","Others came to apologize.","The one apologizing was, naturally, Liu Dongdong's mother.","The things her daughter had done at the factory had been spread back by the people of Xingfu Village just last night. Now, the relationship between the two villages was as incompatible as fire and water."]},{"number":495,"title":"Chapter 495: How Can We Be Stuck Together Every Day","paragraphs":["Si Nian heard a knock on the door and looked over.","A group of people was standing nervously at the door.","Looking at them, Si Nian felt a headache coming on.","Her whole family had just arrived home; couldn't they let her rest for a moment?","In the past, what she feared most was social pleasantries. If she didn't like someone, she would just ignore them and pretend not to see them.","It didn't matter when she was alone, but now that she had a family, she had reservations. To avoid gossip, whenever people threw all sorts of questions at her, she followed the rule of not slapping a smiling face and responded politely.","However, when there were too many people like this, it became quite annoying.","Si Nian also knew that this was just how things were in the countryside. Acquaintances were everywhere, and you saw them all the time, so she maintained the utmost politeness.","She wanted to prevent rumors from spreading that she was acting arrogant just because her husband was making money and had started a company.","She might not care if she heard it herself, but if Zhou Yueshen and the children heard it, they would be so angry.","She put down the broom, told the children to clean up their own rooms, and walked over.","When the group saw her, their eyes lit up like zombies seeing meat.","\"Uncles and aunties, what can I do for you?\"","Looking at the things they were carrying, Si Nian thought to herself that no matter how good they were, she couldn't accept them.","Accepting them meant owing a favor.","\"Oh my, you must be Niannian. Do you remember me, auntie? When you were brought over from the Lin family, I even went to help.\"","Dark lines formed on Si Nian's forehead. So many people had helped at her wedding; how could she possibly remember them all?","But she kept a smile on her face. \"Then when your family hosts a banquet in the future, I'll definitely go help.\"","She deflected the issue effortlessly, neither saying she remembered nor that she didn't. Either way, since they had helped her, she would certainly return the favor when their family had a happy occasion.","When rural families hosted wedding banquets, practically everyone in the village who was somewhat familiar went to help anyway.","It was nothing unusual.","The woman smiled from ear to ear. Being given such face by the boss's wife made her feel extremely proud.","\"I'm sorry, but my family is currently cleaning up. We haven't been back in many years, and the house is messy and covered in dust. I shouldn't let you come in and get dusty, so if you have anything to say, let's just talk here.\"","Seeing her outfit, everyone understood and didn't mind. They immediately asked, \"We heard from people in your village that your man opened a factory in the city? The wages are high, and room and board are included?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"Yes.\"","\"Oh my, what wonderful news! Are you still hiring? My child dropped out of junior high and is just idling at home. It'd be perfect for him to go up and work.\"","Si Nian was speechless. \"Auntie, a junior high student isn't eighteen yet, right? We can't hire anyone under eighteen; it's a state regulation.\"","\"Oh, whatever regulations those are, as long as no one says anything, who would know? Let me tell you, my kid is so hardworking, blah blah blah...\"","Si Nian smiled. \"We are all law-abiding citizens. Are you trying to induce us to break the law? Old Zhou's company just opened, and you want to send a minor in. Even if you and I don't say anything, other people aren't blind; they can tell if someone is of age or not. Once reported, the whole company will suffer. At that time, let alone your son, all the employees would probably lose their jobs. Who would take responsibility then?\"","Hearing this, everyone's expressions changed, and they hurriedly said, \"Yes, exactly! Sister Shi, really, how old is your son that you insist on sending him to their company!\"","\"Wouldn't it be fine to just find some technical skill for him to learn outside? Those private masters taking apprentices outside are fine, but a big company is different!\"","The woman called Sister Shi mumbled for a moment and whispered, \"It's not as serious as all that.\"","Si Nian's expression was indifferent, but she remained polite. \"Then you can try sending him to someone else's company and see if they'll take him.\"","Sister Shi looked embarrassed. If she could get him in somewhere else, would she have traveled all the way to Xingfu Village to bring gifts and beg for help?","\"Does anyone else have anything? If not, I need to get back to cleaning.\" Si Nian didn't want to entertain the group any longer.","Everyone knew this wasn't a good time to talk. They figured they should first get her to accept the gifts and then slowly bring up their requests later.","But thinking about Si Nian's attitude just now, they felt she must still be angry. After all, someone from their village had done such an outrageous thing.","Today, everyone had sneaked over while the villagers of Xingfu Village were at the village chief's house celebrating.","Otherwise, if they were seen, they would surely be mocked.","So they hurriedly nudged a woman in the middle, signaling her to apologize quickly.","\"Dongdong's mom, didn't you want to apologize? Hurry up and speak.\"","The middle-aged woman in the center, carrying a basket of eggs, looked uneasy. Pushed forward, she wore an embarrassed expression. \"Comrade Si, we've all heard about what happened with my Dongdong. I'm so sorry. Please don't take it to heart; I've already taught her a harsh lesson.\"","Si Nian continued to smile. \"There's no need. Your daughter has already received the punishment she deserved, and I haven't taken it to heart.\"","\"Oh my, Comrade Niannian is truly magnanimous!\"","\"Yes, yes. Not only is she beautiful, but she also has a kind heart.\"","Seeing her smiling the whole time, everyone thought Si Nian really didn't care about the trouble Liu Dongdong had caused, and they couldn't help but feel happy.","Dongdong's mom also felt a surge of joy and hurriedly said, \"Yes, yes, Dongdong was wrong, and the punishment is right. But this job position shouldn't be wasted, right? My Chunni is also in the city; how about letting her take over the spot?\"","She knew that her daughter's position was different from ordinary ones; she had only managed to pass the interview after attending a technical school.","Ordinary people couldn't get it at all.","The salary was also higher than average.","Naturally, she couldn't bear to lose it.","She had also heard about city people buying and selling jobs. She was counting on her two daughters to subsidize the household expenses. Since Dongdong couldn't do it anymore, she would just let her older sister Chunni do it. It was all the same anyway.","Thinking of this, she looked at Si Nian a bit nervously, afraid that she still held a grudge and would refuse.","Unexpectedly, Si Nian was exceptionally accommodating: \"Sure, just go for an interview.\"","She froze for a moment, then reacted and quickly said, \"Why does she still need to interview? Didn't Dongdong already interview?\"","Si Nian nodded. \"She did interview, but she was fired for violating company regulations. Being fired means the company no longer has a position for her, so how could we let someone else just take it? Of course, if you want someone else to go, it's not impossible; they just need to go for an interview.\"","Dongdong's mom was dumbfounded. \"Why an interview again? Will Chunni be able to pass?\"","\"Go back and ask Liu Dongdong. I don't know much about the company; she should know best how she passed her interview.\"","Everyone else also hurried forward to ask if their sons could go.","Si Nian told them to go interview for themselves as well.","Anyway, Zhou Yueshen had mentioned that anyone who wanted to work should go for an interview. Whether they passed or not was their own problem.","Everyone thanked her profusely and hurriedly tried to shove their gifts at her.","Si Nian didn't accept them, pretending not to see. \"Sorry, I still have to work. The house is a mess and there's nowhere to put things, so please keep them for yourselves to eat.\"","The crowd bowed and thanked her. Seeing this, Dongdong's mom grew anxious and hurriedly said, \"Then... then what about my Chunni?\"","Si Nian thought to herself, what does your Chunni's situation have to do with me?","However, a thought occurred to her, and she paused.","Seeing her remain silent, Liu Dongdong's mother thought she had softened and hurriedly said, \"I'm so pitiful. My son is a disappointment, so her father and I have to rely on our two daughters to subsidize us. Now that Dongdong has done something stupid, I accept it. But could you please do me a favor and let my Chunni work in your company? Whatever conditions you have, we can negotiate.\"","Hearing this, everyone felt contempt in their hearts.","They were already furious enough that Liu Dongdong's actions had caused them to be targeted by the people of Xingfu Village.","Let alone Si Nian.","How could she have the nerve to ask someone to squeeze her eldest daughter in at a time like this?","She really was thick-skinned enough.","Si Nian remained silent for a while before saying, \"Auntie, are your family's conditions really that bad? But I heard that your eldest daughter is enjoying a good life in the family compound. Her man has a government job. Rather than joining my small company, it would be better for her to ask her man to arrange a secure, golden-bowl job for her. Maybe she could even bring you to the city to enjoy a good life too.\"","Si Nian wasn't sure if Liu Dongdong's mother knew about this.","But she had heard about this family's situation before.","Liu Chunni had married two men in the past, but in the end, she was driven away for unknown reasons.","She wasn't entirely clear on the details, but she could roughly guess that Liu Dongdong had used his sister to seduce Father Si.","She didn't know what kind of person Liu Chunni was, but being able to have an affair with a married man already proved that neither the man nor the woman was any good.","The last time Father Si went to Zhou Yueshen's company to cause trouble, Si Nian felt infuriated.","Now it was time to find something for him and these two sisters to do.","To save them from constantly scheming against her all day long.","But Si Nian believed that since Liu Dongdong's mother didn't know about this, it meant that Liu Chunni and Father Si definitely had no intention of getting married yet.","Sure enough, she revealed a surprised expression: \"You're talking about my Chunni?\"","\"Yes, right in the house where Liu Dongdong previously worked as a nanny. Didn't she tell you?\"","\"I only heard from a friend in the family compound who mentioned that she takes a child out for a walk every day, but I don't know if she married into the family. Anyway, she is living a pretty good life. You say your family is having a hard time, which I don't think should be the case. But maybe my friend saw it wrong, you should ask her yourself.\"","After saying that, she ignored the shocked crowd and turned around to get busy with her work.","\"Chunni is living a good life in the city? Real or fake?\"","\"She hasn't been back for years, right? I thought she was too embarrassed to return, but to think she's doing so well?\"","\"And a child? When did that happen?\"","\"The man even has a government job! When did she get married? Dongdong's mom, how come we've never heard you mention it?\"","Liu Dongdong's mother was stunned for a long time. When she reacted, a momentary gloom flashed across her eyes.","She then smiled: \"I had heard about it before, but I wasn't too clear. Oh my, I'll go check. If it's true, I'll definitely tell everyone.\"","Having said that, she couldn't care less about work anymore. She hurriedly went home to find the village chief to make a phone call and ask about the situation.","Goodness, those two wretched girls had deceived her so miserably!","They called all day crying about being poor, saying how hard life was, and even said that once she settled down in the factory, she would bring her brother and the others in to work.","Thinking that since she worked in the HR department, squeezing people into the factory would surely be easy, Mother Liu was overjoyed and gave her whatever she asked for.","She told everyone she met that her daughter was successful.","As a result, it had only been a few days, and she was kicked out of the company, implicating her as well, having the village chief come to her door to demand she apologize in person.","It was already embarrassing enough.","Yet here she was, left behind to wipe their messes.","Those two sisters had it good, living luxuriously in the city!","And after so long, they never even mentioned it!","Fine, she was going to go see exactly what those two had been doing behind her back!","Although she was very angry in her heart, she thought that if her daughter really found someone with a government job and married into the city...","Wouldn't their family be rich then?","Maybe they could even buy a house in the city for her son.","The more she thought about it, the more excited she became. Mother Liu couldn't sit still for another moment and immediately went to town to catch a bus to the city.","At noon, Zhou Yueshen returned.","The house had already been cleaned.","After finishing his meal, he was pulled by Village Chief Huo to visit the factory.","The hospitality was hard to refuse, and indeed, it had been many years since he last came back.","Entering the house and seeing it spotless, the children had already run out to play, leaving only Si Nian fiddling with the cups on the coffee table.","He stepped forward quickly, \"Where are Second Child and the others?\"","\"I asked them to go call my brother and the others over to play. Xiaodong is watching them, don't worry.\"","Si Nian tilted her head to look at him, \"Leaving already?\"","Zhou Yueshen nodded and stepped forward to help her dry a few washed cups. Flower tea had already been brewed on the side, steaming, and the petals floating inside the glass and porcelain looked very beautiful.","He gave a soft sound of agreement and said, \"I'll try my best to come back tonight.\"","Si Nian paused and said, \"Don't come.\"","Zhou Yueshen glanced at her in surprise, then chuckled softly, \"You don't want me to come?\"","Si Nian shook her head, \"I just think it's too tiring to drive back and forth all day. It's not very close, and we'll just head back after playing for a few days.\"","After saying that, she paused for a moment and said slowly, \"How can we stick together every single day?\"","Although she said that, in her heart, she definitely wanted Zhou Yueshen to stay with her.","It was just that Si Nian also knew he had his own work and career. Being able to spare time to look after them was already doing very well.","To do everything perfectly, where in the world was there such a good thing?","Earning money to support the family on one hand, while also taking care of everyone's emotions on the other.","It would be very tiring.","Seeing her stubbornness, Zhou Yueshen knew she was just feeling bad for him. He pulled her into his arms, lowered his head, and kissed her on the lips, \"What if I want to stick to you, is that not allowed?\""]},{"number":496,"title":"Chapter 496: Section 493: Sometimes a Woman Being Too Charming Is Also a Fault","paragraphs":["Si Nian blinked her eyes, and after a long while, she sighed helplessly, \"Sometimes a woman being too attractive is also a fault.\"","Zhou Yueshan: \"...\"","Give her a little sunshine and she really shines.","He looked down at her. Si Nian's mouth was slightly turned up, with a little smugness in her eyes. She said she was helpless, but she was already proud.","If she had a tail, it would definitely be sticking up.","He really loved her charming look.","The two embraced, enjoying this moment of peace without the children.","........................","The children came back sweating profusely from playing. Zhou Yueshan had already left, and the children asked where their father was.","Si Nian said, \"Your father went back early, he couldn't wait for you to finish playing.\"","\"Sister!\"","\"Sis!\"","Two children about the same height as Zhou Zedong and Zhou Zehan walked in with bright eyes.","They came in one after the other, sweating profusely.","Seeing her, they were very excited.","They couldn't suppress their smiles.","Si Nian also smiled, \"Xiao Feng, Xiao Yu, long time no see. How are your studies?\"","Well, adults are indeed all the same; the first question is always about studies.","Lin Feng generously said, \"Not bad, better than before.\"","When he studied in the countryside before, he always heard others say how good the city was.","They always said that children in the city were smarter than them, so more of them got into college, while they couldn't.","But Lin Feng was stubborn at that time. He felt that city people and country people were all human, so why couldn't they compare with them?","He felt that as long as he studied hard, he could definitely catch up with or even surpass them.","He always had this kind of spirit in his heart.","But when he went to the city, this spirit was suddenly punctured.","He was one of the top students in his class.","But in the city, he couldn't even be considered excellent, only average.","He had never even heard of the things those people had learned.","Even though they used the same textbooks, they just knew more than him.","Later, he had to admit why they could go to college.","The educational ability and environment were completely incomparable to what they had in the countryside.","It's not looking down on the countryside; it's just that reality is so cruel.","Now he had settled down, and after experiencing the family changes caused by the accidents of his parents and brother, he had become much more mature and steady.","He could compare with Zhou Zedong.","Naturally, his academic performance was also much better than before.","Not to mention catching up with a talented player like Zhou Zedong, he was also one of the best in the class.","But his younger brother Xiao Yu was different.","When he heard the question about his grades, he felt a huge headache.","He hemmed and hawed, \"It's, it's okay.\"","Obviously, he was afraid of losing face.","That look was exactly the same as when Second Child felt guilty.","Si Nian didn't ask much. She smiled and patted the heads of the two children, took out two red envelopes from her pocket, and handed them to them: \"Your brother-in-law gave these to you. He had something to do at the company today and left early. He couldn't say hello to you before leaving, so he gave you two red envelopes as an apology.\"","Lin Feng immediately declined, \"No, we can't accept it.\"","Lin Yu's eyes were shining, and his face was written with the words \"I want it,\" but he didn't dare to say it out loud.","Si Nian smiled. They were really two treasures. She saw the shadows of Eldest Child and Second Child in them.","Does that mean she has successfully turned two misguided children into normal people?","Xiao Feng and Xiao Yu grew up in love. Although they were ordinary, that was what normal people should look like.","\"Take it. Don't be polite with your brother-in-law, otherwise, why does he make so much money?\"","The two children then accepted it.","Lin Feng was still a little blushing, while Lin Yu couldn't help but carefully feel how thick it was with his hands.","The next day, Si Nian took Shitou to get a haircut.","Jiang Jiu also clamored to get a haircut.","Si Nian didn't dare to cut his hair, afraid that the two elders would be angry when they saw it, so she didn't agree.","Jiang Jiu was also an obedient person. If she didn't agree, he wouldn't cut it.","He didn't dare to be disobedient.","But the little guy was still listless.","Seeing that he seemed to be in a bad mood, Si Nian was a little worried. As a result, when she looked down and saw him looking at a certain place, she followed his gaze and saw that it was Second Child and Shitou getting their hair cut. Because the barber hadn't done this kind of style before, he had to compare it while cutting.","So Second Child went over to sit as a model.","The two children hadn't seen each other for a long time, and they had endless topics to talk about, with smiles on their faces.","Jiang Jiu just stared, and there seemed to be some disappointment in his eyes.","Si Nian was stunned for a moment, and then realized what was going on.","Jiang Jiu was not from here. Except for his family, he was not familiar with anyone else.","He originally thought he had the best relationship with his second brother.","But after coming back, he found out that he was just one of the people Second Child had a good relationship with.","The two of them talked about their past and future, and he couldn't get a word in.","No wonder he was anxious to get his hair cut when he saw Shitou getting his hair cut.","He had never thought about getting his hair cut before.","This child has a sense of crisis.","Afraid that his good friend would be taken away.","Si Nian actually understood this feeling. In the past, when she had friends, seeing her good friends suddenly talking selflessly with others and ignoring her, she would also feel jealous.","Si Nian was just about to say something to comfort the little guy.","The little guy suddenly tilted his head and walked away.","She didn't know whether to laugh or cry. Looking at Second Child now, she suddenly felt that he was a bit of a scumbag.","That kind of feeling of \"when the ex appears, the current one will definitely lose.\"","Si Nian was amused by her own thoughts.","But no matter what, she still had to give Second Child a hint. Jiang Jiu followed him from far away, which was very loyal.","How could he ignore him?","Although she also understood that he hadn't seen Shitou for a long time and had a lot to say.","Si Nian sighed.","After getting their hair cut, they bought some fruits and snacks, and the whole family went back.","It was noon, and everyone was sweating profusely.","Looking at Jiang Jiu sitting listlessly on the sofa, Si Nian suddenly regretted letting the child come along.","Just as she was about to pull Second Child over to teach him a lesson, she saw him running in anxiously, \"Xiao Jiu, Xiao Jiu, why are you sitting here?\"","Jiang Jiu tilted his head and looked at him carrying a bag with clothes in a hurry, feeling a little confused.","\"What's wrong, second brother?\"","\"Didn't I say I'd take you to learn swimming? It's so hot today, we can just go learn.\"","Jiang Jiu really forgot the pain after the scar healed, and immediately stood up excitedly, \"Then are we going now? Do I need to change clothes?\"","Second Child lifted the bag and smiled, \"I've already packed it for you. Let's go.\"","Jiang Jiu immediately ran over.","Si Nian was a little worried. She didn't know about Second Child's past, but she also knew that wild water was dangerous.","She immediately said, \"Wait, I'll go with you.\"","It was a hot day, and it would be nice to go out to the river and play in the water.","Si Nian had a lot of procedures to go out. She couldn't find the sunblock, umbrella, and mat, but she dug out the old bed sheets, took out the fruits and watermelon she bought from the refrigerator, put them in a basket, and followed them.","Zhou Zedong, Lin Feng, and Lin Yu were originally looking at the children outside the door, holding a book in their hands.","Seeing her setup, he immediately followed: \"Mom, I'm going with you guys.\"","Second Child was quick to speak: \"Didn't you just tell my brother you weren't going when he asked you?\"","He received a glare from his brother.","\"Sis, where are you guys going?\" Lin Feng asked, holding Little Yuanzi with one hand and pulling Little Four with the other, following behind Si Nian.","His face was full of confusion.","Si Nian replied, \"Going to the stream to play in the water.\"","Hearing this, the corners of Lin Feng's mouth twitched.","How old was his sister, and she still liked playing in the water?","Wasn't that something only children played with?","He had long passed that age.","But seeing everyone going, it seemed quite fun, so he led the two children and followed behind.","Lin Yu carried a basket of things and curled her lip as she watched Second Child and the others walking ahead, discussing learning how to swim.","Si Nian led Da Huang. This guy had been living too comfortably in the city and had gained quite a bit of weight.","Si Nian also felt it was time for it to lose weight.","This guy had very thick fur, and whenever it got hot, its tongue would hang out. Going to play in the water would be good for it.","Yaoyao followed beside them and said, \"Mom, I want to learn how to swim too.\"","Because they were still too young, it was hard to teach them, so basically none of the first-grade children had learned how.","Si Nian did not dare let her get into the water. The boys would be playing and roughhousing, and if they got carried away and did not notice her, it would be too dangerous.","She did not agree: \"Wait until next time we come back, I'll buy you a swimming ring and then you can learn. Today, you can only play with the water on the side.\"","Little Four waited until his sister finished speaking before opening his mouth, \"Mommy, I...\"","Before he could finish, Si Nian said, \"No!\"","Little Four: \"...\"","Zhou Zedong was no longer reading his book at this moment, but he did not put it away and was still holding it. Hearing this, he said, \"Mom, it's fine, I'll watch them.\"","Hearing this, Si Nian immediately smiled: \"Then playing for a bit is not entirely out of the question.\"","The whole family arrived at the stream. She had to admit that an unpolluted environment was simply beautiful. Green mountains and clear waters, the stream rolling along. It had not rained recently, so the water was not deep, remaining clear and clean.","The grass by the roadside was lush and green, and various flowers and plants grew abundantly.","Si Nian spread out a bedsheet under a tree as a mat and placed the fruits on it.","The children were already helping each other take off their clothes and change into their swimsuits.","Finding a flat spot, the children used Shitou to build a small pool. Since the water could not flow down, it gathered up.","Getting into the water in this weather was quite nice. Si Nian watched them, moved over as well, and dipped her feet in.","A rush of coolness shot straight to the top of her head.","The children had already jumped into the water and started playing.","Si Nian squinted her eyes to enjoy the breeze while telling them to be careful and watch out for the Shitou. She also did not let them take off their shoes, afraid there might be glass.","The children all had sandals, so there was no worry about getting them wet.","At this moment, they were kicking their legs in the pool, swimming like little frogs.","Da Huang also jumped in after them.","But because it was too heavy, it could not float.","It only vaguely realized that it was no longer the youthful and energetic little puppy from back then.","Now it weighed over a hundred jin, and this small pool could only bear the weight of a few children.","Da Huang walked around in the water out of boredom. Suddenly, fierce dog barking sounded from the roadside.","It immediately looked over.","No matter what animal it was, they all had territorial awareness. Once out of their territory, they would be alert, and upon encountering their own kind, they would size each other up.","Hearing the barks, Da Huang immediately became alert.","But tilting its head, it saw a small, multi-colored dog.","Its two ears were floppy, and right now its legs were trembling as it barked wildly.","Obviously, it had never seen such a large dog before and was scared silly.","Si Nian was attracted by the fierce barking. She turned her head to look and saw Da Huang staring from a distance at a little puppy. It seemed the dog was terrified, its legs went soft, and it dared not move.","A woman had a rope tied around its neck and was also extremely frightened.","Worried that Da Huang would be provoked, Si Nian hurriedly got up, ran over, and scolded, \"Da Huang, go back.\"","Da Huang squatted for a moment, then turned around and went back into the water.","Si Nian walked over and apologized embarrassedly, \"Sorry to have scared you.\"","\"Oh my, you really scared me to death. I've never seen such a big dog.\"","The other party was holding a piece of meat and did not recognize her. Si Nian figured she must be from another village.","Otherwise, the villagers would all know Da Huang, after all, there was only one Tibetan Mastiff in this village.","Si Nian's eyelids twitched, \"Are you here to buy meat?\"","The woman patted her chest and said, \"Yes, I originally came over to pick up the dog. Since I happened to pass by the breeding farm here, I bought a piece of meat and asked them to help me butcher this dog, but they refused. Don't you think they are being unreasonable? Isn't it just a simple favor?\"","Si Nian paused for a moment, \"Butcher it?\"","She knew that some people ate dog meat, and she had not paid much attention to it before, but after raising Da Huang, it became somewhat hard for her to accept...","Not to mention this dog looked so small, how much meat could it possibly yield?","\"Exactly. There's no use keeping it. I originally wanted to sell it, but its coat has too many colors. People said it's not purebred, just a mutt, and they didn't want it. So I thought I'd butcher it to get a couple of meals out of it.\"","Si Nian did not even want to listen to her anymore; her scalp felt numb.","\"How about this, you sell it to me?\"","She looked down and examined the dog. The dog's face had three colors: white, black, and yellow.","It was indeed multi-colored, but she thought it looked quite pretty. It was just too dirty. With many colors to begin with, adding dirt naturally made it look unappealing.","It was still very small, probably only four or five months old.","Si Nian was not very knowledgeable about dog breeds either.","She only knew there was a type of cat called a calico cat, considered a great beauty in the cat world, and this coloration was basically always female, something you could come by but not seek out.","She had heard that in the animal world, the more colorful, the better looking.","She raised an eyebrow: \"Is this dog male or female?\"","Hearing that she wanted to buy it, the other party smiled like a blooming flower: \"Female! When she has litters in the future, you can sell the puppies too!\"","Si Nian smiled. Just now when Da Huang was staring at it, maybe it wasn't trying to hurt the dog, but perhaps it was attracted by its beauty?","The other party only asked for two yuan. It seemed that in their eyes, dogs were not worth much, and being able to sell it was already a good thing.","She smiled, clutching the money, and left.","The dog looked at her curiously, her figure reflected in its large, wet eyes.","Almost sensing that she would not hurt it, it actually started wagging its tail.","Si Nian clicked her tongue, led it over, and gave it some watermelon to eat.","Da Huang was the first to come over.","Si Nian temporarily called it Xiao Hua. Xiao Hua was very afraid of Da Huang. Perhaps because it had never seen such a large dog, its legs trembled as soon as it saw Da Huang.","Si Nian did not dare let the two dogs get close either, telling Da Huang to go to the side.","Da Huang had truly matured. It did not bark or make a fuss, just crawled under a nearby tree and occasionally glanced over.","The children were soon attracted to Xiao Hua. Xiao Hua was still small, skinny, did not look very pretty, and smelled stinky.","The children pulled it to take a bath, and it was not afraid.","It took several washes before it was clean, and finally, its original coat colors could be seen.","After drying off, its fur puffed out a bit, and being too skinny, it still did not look great.","Sure enough, among all living creatures except humans, being a little chubby looked better.","Si Nian felt that it would probably look better in the future.","Although she still didn't look very pretty right now, seeing how Da Huang kept trying to rub against her, it was obvious that in the dog's eyes, she was a slender and stunning beauty.","Si Nian didn't stay at home for too long either. Treating it as a vacation, she relaxed for a few days and then headed back.","Chen Haoran had been at the breeding farm these past few days. When he heard they were leaving, he was actually reluctant to go.","Wearing a pair of rubber boots and a tank top, his hair was a mess, and he hadn't even shaved the stubble on his chin.","He no longer looked anything like the young master of a wealthy family.","Si Nian was even a little worried about whether his parents would be angry when they got back.","............................","Barely two days after she returned home, Fu Qianqian came looking for her.","She rushed over in a flurry, looking exactly like someone bursting with juicy gossip.","Wearing a mysterious expression, she wasn't in a rush to speak after arriving. Instead, she sat there calmly sipping her tea.","Seeing that she was waiting to be asked, Si Nian played along, \"Did something happen in the Si family again?\"","\"Of course!\" Fu Qianqian said immediately. \"And it's a big one!\""]},{"number":497,"title":"Chapter 497: Yu Dong and Fu Qianqian (Complete)","paragraphs":["Before Si Nian could even speak, she excitedly began to chatter.","It turned out that a couple of days ago, the Si family was preparing to introduce a blind date to Si's Father. Word was that she was a teacher, a highly sought-after profession.","Si's Father even took her to visit the family compound, and guess what happened?","They ran right into Liu Dongdong's mother.","At the time, Liu Dongdong's mother was outside saying she was looking for her daughter. The family compound wasn't a place just anyone could enter, so naturally, the guards wouldn't let her in when she approached.","Who would have thought that Liu Dongdong's mother would throw her weight around, claiming her daughter was a military officer's wife inside and threatening to report the guard if he didn't let her in.","Hearing this, the guard thought he had misremembered the residents and quickly asked for the name.","Liu Dongdong's mother gave the name Liu Chunni.","Upon hearing the name, the guard hurriedly checked the registry.","As a result, he didn't find any officer's wife by that name, but he did find an exact match for the registered name of the Si family's nanny.","He then asked Liu Dongdong's mother if she was mistaken—her daughter was indeed inside, but she was working as a nanny for someone's child.","As soon as Liu Dongdong's mother heard this, she became anxious.","Refusing to believe it, she started throwing a massive tantrum.","Right at that moment, Si's Father brought his blind date over for a tour.","They bumped into Liu Dongdong's mother. Somehow, Liu Dongdong's mother recognized him as Si Nian's adoptive father and asked for his help.","But as luck would have it, Si's Father had no idea she was Liu Dongdong's mother.","He thought she was someone from Si Nian's hometown.","Then the guard immediately chimed in, \"Yes, yes, Liu Chunni works at Deputy Battalion Commander Si's house. You should talk to him and see if there's a misunderstanding. Comrade Liu Chunni is just a nanny; I've never heard of her being married.\"","Now both of them were completely dumbfounded.","Liu Dongdong's mother quickly reacted. Assuming her daughter had given birth to Si's Father's child and that he was now out looking for other women, she furiously caused a huge scene.","She demanded that he give her daughter an explanation!","No one knew which child belonged to Si's Father, but with this uproar, he couldn't have washed himself clean even if he jumped into the Yellow River.","At this point, the blind date was also utterly bewildered.","Once she processed what was happening, the blind date ran off with a dark expression on her face.","Although Si's Father vehemently denied it, the incident still caused such a stir that everyone in the family compound knew about it.","The higher-ups even began to suspect that his initial adoption of the child was a cover-up for an illegitimate son.","Considering his ex-wife Zhang Cuimei and Lin Sisi had just gone to prison, and immediately after he brought back an illegitimate child, everyone found it terrifying when they thought deeply about it.","Si's Father had been suspended for investigation over the past two days.","After all, for a deputy battalion commander, having a chaotic personal life was a very serious matter.","Not to mention, it had caused such a massive scandal.","Now everyone was spreading rumors that the child was born to him and Liu Chunni.","They said he first brought his illegitimate child home, and then brought the child's mother over under the guise of being a nanny.","This way, after ten or twenty years when he retired, he could legitimately marry her.","But ironically, Si's Father was too ambitious for his own good and actually started going on blind dates with others.","Fu Qianqian poured herself another cup of tea, feeling her mouth go dry from all the talking.","As soon as she heard the news, she immediately came over to share it with Si Nian.","She was gloating uncontrollably in her heart.","She thought about how the Si family had been living perfectly well before, yet they insisted on driving Si Nian away—and not just driving her away, but doing it in such an extreme manner.","Well, look at them now. They got their karma.","She didn't feel sorry for them at all.","After all, things like infidelity and illegitimate children were inherently despicable.","As she spoke, she suddenly added mysteriously, \"My brother is coming back today.\"","\"I wonder how he'll feel when he finds out his former father-in-law's family has turned out like this.\"","Si Nian just gave a noncommittal \"Mhm.\"","Although she had only been guessing before, it seemed her thoughts were pretty much spot on.","As for Fu Yang, if he hadn't been mentioned, she would have forgotten him completely.","When Fu Qianqian brought him up, Si Nian's expression didn't change much.","Seeing her calm demeanor, Fu Qianqian sighed again.","She felt bad for her brother.","But then again, he deserved it.","Thinking that Si Nian was about to graduate, Fu Qianqian wanted to recommend her to her own workplace.","She said that since Si Nian was beautiful and elegant, she would definitely be an even more popular host than herself.","Si Nian had no interest in being a host and shook her head.","Fu Qianqian had been looking forward to them working and getting off work together. Seeing her refuse, she grew anxious: \"You're about to graduate, what do you plan to do?\"","Si Nian replied, \"I plan to invest.\"","\"Invest?\" Fu Qianqian didn't quite understand; she had never done it anyway.","Although she desired career success more than others, she had never thought about going into business herself; she only wanted to shine in her own industry.","Hearing Si Nian mention investing, she worried: \"Isn't investing like doing business? It's very dangerous. I heard nine out of ten investments fail.\"","She wasn't clear on the details herself, but hadn't she at least seen others do it?","More and more people had been doing business in recent years because those who made money a few years ago were pulling others in to invest.","So many people chose to change careers, only to end up losing everything and going bankrupt.","Fu Qianqian felt that people who could get into college and secure a government job weren't necessarily cut out for business.","On the contrary, those who couldn't get into college and spent years hustling in society were often the successful ones.","Anyway, she would never do it.","Si Nian said, \"I'm not the one running the business; I'm just investing. Investing has risks, but it depends on whether the other party is reliable. If they are reliable, you make money; if not, you lose. It mainly depends on them. Of course, you can't put all your focus on one person. Cast a wide net, and one is bound to hit.\"","Fu Qianqian half-understood, \"In short, you just don't want to get a regular job, right?\"","Si Nian said, \"If I wanted a regular job, I wouldn't have sold my position to you.\"","What was the ultimate goal of working hard to make money? To be rich and slack off.","She already had the money to slack off, so why work so hard?","Was she that bored?","Life is meant to be enjoyed.","Of course, everyone's pursuits are different.","Si Nian wouldn't force her own views on others.","Anyway, she would avoid the daily grind of a regular job at all costs.","Besides investing in Sister Miao's clothing brand, she could use her investment returns to buy houses and land.","Although it didn't seem very useful now, once the real estate boom hit in the 90s, her returns would roll in.","Fu Qianqian understood and didn't ask further. Come to think of it, if someone had money, why would they go to work?","Speaking of which, she felt a bit melancholic. Although her career was on the rise and gave her a great sense of accomplishment, she had also lost a lot of joy.","For example, she couldn't eat or drink freely because she had to maintain her figure; she couldn't keep her hair too long because it made wearing wigs difficult.","And she had to wear mature makeup, and so on.","She sighed, \"Anyway, I still envy you.\"","Back when they were still in the family compound, she envied Si Nian for being better, prettier, and more capable than her.","Later, when Si Nian was driven away, she thought Si Nian would have a miserable life.","She used to wake up laughing in the middle of the night.","But as it turned out, Si Nian was living even better.","It was truly frustrating.","Si Nian said, \"You can live very well too. Don't restrict yourself too much.\"","Fu Qianqian said, \"I always feel like my life is missing something.\"","Si Nian had a sudden thought, \"Is it because you haven't dated anyone?\"","Fu Qianqian's face flushed red: \"Who, who hasn't dated? I've dated eight or ten guys by now, haha. My romantic history is way richer than yours.\"","Si Nian gave her a faint, knowing smile.","Knowing she couldn't hide it anymore, Fu Qianqian deflated. \"Actually, my mom has been looking for matches for me too, but I just don't find any of them pleasing to the eye. No matter how I look at them, it's just uncomfortable, and I don't feel a thing. Aren't we all about free love nowadays?\"","\"With no feelings at all, I just feel like I can't get married like that.\"","Actually, in the past, she wouldn't have minded the lack of feelings. As long as they weren't too ugly, it was just about living life together anyway. That was how people from the older generation did it—no real feelings, and looks didn't matter much. Family background was king. Once married, feelings would naturally develop over time.","She used to think the same way.","But after seeing how happily Si Nian was living, she felt that she should at least find someone as handsome as her husband.","What would be the point of settling for someone both ugly and poor?","Hearing her out, Si Nian could only think that indeed, the onlookers see clearly while those involved are blind.","\"Don't you have someone exactly like that right by your side?\"","\"Me? Where?\"","\"Yu Dong. He's good-looking, has a good family background, and a great personality.\"","Si Nian thought to herself that if she pointed it out like this and Fu Qianqian still didn't like him, then she wouldn't support Yu Dong continuing to pursue her either.","Some things just can't be forced.","Fu Qianqian's eyes widened. She wanted to retort, but the words died on her lips.","Now that she mentioned it, it seemed true. Yu Dong was a really nice guy, but she had never thought of him in that way.","Because he was friends with Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen, she had naturally just treated him as a friend.","When Yu Dong used to invite her out to eat and asked her to help him taste-test various dishes, she had felt really happy. Having all sorts of delicious food every day made everyone envy her.","But eventually, eating all that food made her gain weight.","That scared her. She started turning Yu Dong down and didn't dare to eat anymore. After that, she was even afraid to see him, terrified he would ask her to go eat again. She was someone with weak willpower to begin with.","So they hadn't seen each other in a long time. If Si Nian hadn't brought him up, she might have forgotten about him entirely.","With Si Nian saying this, she suddenly felt as if the empty spot in her heart had been found.","She had always thought that feeling of loss came from no longer being able to eat freely and enjoy delicious food like she used to.","But now she suddenly realized that she hadn't just lost the food.","She opened her mouth but couldn't speak for a long time.","She wanted to argue, but couldn't.","There really wasn't a single bad thing about Yu Dong.","But having known each other for so many years, why hadn't anything developed between them?","She thought for a moment and stammered out an excuse, \"He... I remember he has a fiancée. How could I have designs on him?\"","She remembered going over once and seeing a woman making a scene at the door.","She claimed to be Yu Dong's fiancée.","She had originally gone there to eat, but after that, she didn't really dare to go anymore.","After all, if he had a fiancée, she was afraid people would gossip if she kept running over there.","\"Fiancée?\" Si Nian seemed to recall Yu Dong mentioning this issue. \"So, if he didn't have a fiancée, you would be interested?\"","Fu Qianqian's face flushed red. \"What nonsense are you spouting?\"","Si Nian tsked a few times.","People in this era were indeed mostly very shy about romance.","If Fu Qianqian were asked to take the initiative like she did, it would probably kill her.","True, they lived in different eras.","It was definitely different.","She remembered how her own initiative back then had completely captivated her older man, making him run home all day.","Si Nian looked proud, completely forgetting the time she was so scared by her older man that she ran back to her maiden home.","The situation with those two now was that neither dared to take the initiative, but they both had feelings for each other.","\"Anyway, I'll just say this. Yu Dong isn't getting any younger. He did have a fiancée, but I don't think it worked out. If it was going to happen, they would have gotten married years ago.\"","Fu Qianqian's eyes flickered.","Si Nian said, \"Over all these years, have you ever seen him be so enthusiastic toward anyone else? Spending all day researching so many foods, what do you think he was doing it for?\"","Fu Qianqian replied, \"Wasn't it for his family's restaurant?\"","Si Nian scoffed, \"Come on. He used to run around the breeding farms with Zhou Yueshen all day. When did he ever care about the restaurant's survival? Even if he inherited the family business, it's not up to the young master himself to come up with dishes. What are the hired chefs for? How many bosses have you seen personally cooking in the kitchen?\"","Fu Qianqian's heart pounded wildly.","Hearing this, her state of mind instantly changed.","Thinking of Yu Dong's enthusiasm in the past, a sudden rush of heat rushed to her head.","Si Nian knew when to stop. \"Anyway, he's persisted for so many years. To say he has no feelings would be a lie. But even the most passionate person will eventually give up if they see no hope as time passes. A one-sided effort with no response is exhausting. If you truly have no feelings for him, you don't need to hide from him. Just tell him directly. I believe he's not the type to pester you.\"","Upon hearing this, Fu Qianqian immediately panicked.","She returned home in a daze, her mind completely elsewhere.","She didn't even notice the man standing at the door.","\"Fu Qianqian, are you blind? Are your eyes just for show?\" Fu Yang scolded after she bumped into him.","Fu Qianqian jolted and snapped back to reality. Seeing who it was, she shouted loudly, \"Brother! You're back!\"","Fu Yang snorted coldly, his voice hard. \"I've been standing here for ages, and you only just saw me?\"","Fu Qianqian laughed awkwardly and looked Fu Yang up and down.","After not seeing him for a few years, Fu Yang had become much tougher. His skin was tanned, and his gaze was sharp. She was startled; sure enough, after spending a few years out in the world, his aura was completely different.","She chuckled, \"Brother, you're finally back. Now Mom and Dad definitely won't rush me to find a partner.\"","Fu Yang: \"...\"","Watching him walk inside, Fu Qianqian dropped her smile, a faint sense of disappointment in her eyes.","Some things don't feel like anything until they are pointed out, and once they are, everything becomes a mess.","But she also knew that Si Nian was right.","She wasn't stupid. How could she not see how good Yu Dong had been to her?","Fu Yang's return this time wasn't just to visit his family; it was also to say goodbye.","He had previously planned to leave the city entirely and settle in the remote Northwest.","Of course, he would come back in the future, but his visits would become increasingly rare.","When Fu's parents heard this news, they both fell silent.","But in the end, they didn't say anything more.","Because their control and their planning of his life had ruined half of their son's life.","They shouldn't interfere with his future anymore.","Even if they couldn't bear to let him go.","___________________","When Yu Dong received Fu Qianqian's call, he was incredibly flattered.","Over the years, Fu Qianqian had gotten busier with work, and the time they spent seeing each other had grown less and less.","Sometimes he doubted whether his persistence was right or wrong. He thought about confessing his feelings but didn't dare, terrified that Fu Qianqian only saw him as a friend and that they wouldn't even be able to remain friends in the end.","So he had always carefully maintained the delicate relationship between the two of them.","Just when he was on the verge of giving up, feeling like he shouldn't keep acting this way, Fu Qianqian actually called to invite him to watch a movie.","Yu Dong was stunned.","At the entrance of a newly opened movie theater, it was said that this theater was opened by foreigners and the facilities were much better than those outside.","Si Nian was holding Little Four by the hand, and Little Four was clutching a cotton candy.","Her bag was being carried by Zhou Yueshen.","She watched as Fu Qianqian came over after buying popcorn, dark lines forming on her forehead.","\"You two are on a date, so why did you invite us over?\"","Fu Qianqian blushed. \"Wh-what date? We just haven't hung out in a long time. Everyone was free, so I just asked you to come watch a movie with us.\"","Si Nian rolled her eyes so hard they almost got stuck in the back of her head.","Soon, Yu Dong rushed over, sweating profusely.","It was obvious he had dressed up for the occasion; he had even styled his hair.","Si Nian winced playfully at the cheesy display. She linked arms with the expressionless Zhou Yueshen and said, \"Let's go in first.\"","Zhou Yueshen seemed to half-understand, probably figuring out what was going on, but he didn't say anything. He just gave a grunt of agreement. It had been a long time since he watched a movie with Si Nian, though he had come in such a hurry that he hadn't even changed his clothes.","The couple took the kids and went inside, instantly leaving only Fu Qianqian and Yu Dong behind.","The two of them awkwardly looked everywhere—up at the sky, down at the ground—anywhere but into each other's eyes.","Yu Dong was holding a bag behind his back. He probably realized that today was his last chance.","He nervously handed it to Fu Qianqian. \"This... is for you.\"","Fu Qianqian's heart pounded wildly and her face flushed red. She initially wanted to refuse, but thinking of something, she reached out and took it, whispering, \"Thank you.\"","Then, silence fell again.","\"Come on, let's go inside. It's going to start soon.\"","Yu Dong was older and more mature, after all. Seeing her accept the gift, he somewhat understood what it meant and took the initiative to speak.","The two walked inside. By now, the movie had already started, and the theater was pitch black.","Fu Qianqian had dressed up specifically for today and was wearing high heels. She walked behind him somewhat uneasily, terrified of making a fool of herself.","Just as she was following him cautiously, the back of her hand suddenly felt warm. A large, warm hand had grabbed hers.","Like she had been electrocuted, Fu Qianqian's reflexes kicked in faster than her conscious mind. She lifted her foot and kicked.","Crash!","The lights came on.","Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen looked over at the same time.","Only to see one person standing frozen at the top of the stairs, and the other having rolled all the way to the bottom.","Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen: \"...\"","When Fu Qianqian realized what happened, she was completely stunned.","Naturally, this movie outing ended with Yu Dong fracturing his leg and being sent to the hospital.","No one got to watch the movie.","Waiting outside, Fu Qianqian's eyes grew red.","She felt she had gone too far. Even if he had grabbed her hand, there was no need for her to overreact like that.","Si Nian didn't know what to say; she wasn't good at comforting people.","She patted her on the shoulder. \"Yu Dong won't blame you, but no matter what, you need to go apologize.\"","Inside the hospital room, Yu Dong lay there looking utterly dejected. His hair, previously held in place by hair gel, now hung messily over his forehead.","Zhou Yueshen stood silently by his side.","He didn't quite understand what had happened between the two, nor did he ask.","After a long while, Yu Dong finally let out a sigh. \"Maybe we really just aren't right for each other.\"","Zhou Yueshen said, \"If you have something to say, talk it out properly.\"","With that, he left.","Fu Qianqian came in.","Her eyes were red.","Yu Dong was just thinking about making things clear. If Fu Qianqian really didn't like him, then they should just drop it.","But seeing her eyes so red, his heart instantly softened.","\"Why are you crying? I only fractured a bone, it's not like my leg was amputated.\"","He still had the mood to joke around.","But Fu Qianqian was in no mood for jokes. Thinking back on it, she wished she could give herself a hard slap across the face.","Hearing him say this now made her feel even worse.","\"I'm sorry, I didn't mean to do it.\"","Yu Dong replied, \"No, no, it's my fault. If I hadn't grabbed you, you wouldn't have gotten angry.\"","Fu Qianqian shook her head. \"I wasn't angry. I wasn't mad at all, I was just...\"","She had just been startled. She was already feeling nervous and flustered about the situation between them, and she hadn't expected Yu Dong to suddenly grab her hand.","Come to think of it, it wasn't like he hadn't held her hand before.","Why was she so easily triggered this time?","\"You weren't angry?\" Yu Dong's heart skipped a beat, and he looked at her. \"Then... do you hate me?\"","\"Of course not!\" Fu Qianqian quickly shook her head.","Yu Dong felt a wave of relief, but still asked in disappointment, \"Then why? It can't be that you think my hands are dirty, right?\"","Fu Qianqian shook her head like a rattle drum. \"No, it's not that, it's not.\"","She couldn't quite explain the reason, so she could only keep repeating that it wasn't what he thought.","Seeing Yu Dong lower his head, his face full of defeat, she reached out and grabbed his hand to prove that she really wasn't disgusted by him.","\"Look, I don't mind you at all.\"","Yu Dong let out a chuckle. He turned his hand over to clasp hers, his eyes gentle. \"Silly girl.\""]},{"number":498,"title":"Chapter 498: You Can Come If You Want","paragraphs":["Having facilitated a good match, Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen stopped interfering in the affairs between the two of them.","First, they couldn't intervene even if they wanted to. Once the two broke the ice, their relationship developed so fast that it wasn't long before they heard a marriage proposal was on the way.","The speed was truly astonishing.","But Si Nian also knew that Yu Dong was not young, and his family must be anxious.","She heard that a few years ago, his fiancée had come to his door to fulfill their marriage agreement.","They called her a fiancée, but it was actually just a verbal agreement between the adults.","At that time, Yu Dong was entirely focused on pursuing Fu Qianqian and studying recipes, so he directly made it clear to the other party that he didn't like her, wouldn't marry her, and wouldn't be forced by his family.","The other party probably saw his firmness, felt disheartened, and quickly turned and left.","It was said that she was about the same age as Fu Qianqian.","Si Nian sighed, feeling it was quite pitiful. After all, in this era, how many women clung to a marriage verbally arranged since childhood, devoted half their lives to it, only to end up with nothing.","She thought of the original owner of her body, who was the same. She didn't particularly like Fu Yang at first, nor did she feel she had to have him, but it was just arranged by their families.","In her mindset, this was the person she would spend her life with when she grew up, so she had to treat him well.","However, deep affection is often betrayed.","Summer vacation always passed quickly.","Zhou Yueshen's factory had officially become busy, and he was rushed off his feet every day.","Si Nian handled the transfer procedures for the children, bringing them back to study.","After all, this was their hometown, and being together as a family was more important than anything else.","They were still young. Although the Xiao family was over there, Si Nian wasn't very comfortable letting them go over at such a young age.","Zhou Yueshen, on the other hand, felt it didn't matter. He believed the two children were grown up and should be left to roam free.","Whatever happens is their own fate.","He received a fierce glare from Si Nian.","A happy childhood is the most important thing.","Zhou Yueshen didn't dare to make suggestions, afraid she would get angry. He saw how well Si Nian treated the children and felt happy in his heart.","But this also reminded Si Nian to proactively ask the children what they thought.","Especially the Eldest Child and the Second Child.","The Second Child, of course, wanted to be with his parents. Although he had grown a lot, he was very clingy to Si Nian. Upon hearing he had to go to school in Beijing by himself, he shook his head like a rattle.","He said if he left, no one would look after Little Four.","His sister would be lonely too.","His mother would definitely miss him every day.","Si Nian couldn't help but laugh as she watched him constantly praise himself.","She knew the Second Child definitely didn't want to go over by himself.","The Second Child also thought about what would happen to his pig farm if he left.","Zhou Zedong was more stable. Upon hearing this question, he thought deeply for a long time before saying, \"Mom, I won't go back now. After I take the college entrance examination, I will get into the same university as you, and I will go back by myself.\"","Si Nian was taken aback and looked at him. Then she heard him say, \"Uncle Jiang is working at the research institute over there now, and I also want to go take a look.\"","After all, he was just playing around at home and didn't touch upon any professional things.","Zhou Zedong had lost interest; he wanted to come into contact with more things, those researches he had never seen in reality.","Previously, when Uncle Jiang gave him a globe, he thought Uncle Jiang could definitely show him more.","If possible, when he reached the age, he wanted to give it a try.","Now he was still young, and his studies were the priority.","He wasn't the kind of person who wanted to reach the sky in a single bound. By planning slowly and filling it in step by step, his life would slide along the trajectory he desired.","Si Nian thought about it and felt it was fine, so she agreed.","As for herself, she went back alone for a trip.","She didn't expect everyone to stay while she had to go back.","Si Nian felt sad and needed the older man's comfort.","She was held and coaxed by Zhou Yueshen for a long time that night.","The next day, she felt regretful and ashamed when she went out!","But she still couldn't bear to leave, comforting herself that she was an adult. It was the final days of her senior year, there were no classes, and she just needed to go back to submit a thesis or something before she could leave.","After returning to Beijing, she told her teacher that she would work right after graduation and wouldn't come back for the graduation ceremony, hoping the teacher could mail her diploma back to her.","The teacher saw that she really had no intention of working in the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and gave up, not persuading her anymore.","Speaking of which, Si Nian had been a very obedient student over the years, doing whatever she was told. Although she wasn't proactive, she always did her best every time. She was beautiful but very low-key. Over the years, surprisingly few people in the class had spoken to her.","The teacher had originally worried if Si Nian was a bit autistic or something.","But turning around and seeing her smiling and walking out of the school hand in hand with a man, she felt she had overthought it.","Si Nian stayed in Beijing alone for about a week.","She suddenly felt life was hopeless.","When she had nothing to do, she would call home.","Of course, when facing the children, she always smiled. When Little Four cried and complained that his dad scolded him, she had to comfort the children one by one, saying she would teach him a lesson when she got back.","Zhou Yueshen worked during the day, so they always called at night.","After finishing her thesis, Si Nian took a shower and looked at the empty house, feeling a chill in her heart.","So, the former her lived in such an environment.","But at that time, she was surrounded by the sounds of children playing and the man's low laughter.","Everything seemed so beautiful.","Now it was terrifyingly desolate.","She lay on the sofa, waiting for the nightly call.","Usually, Zhou Yueshen would call her when he got home. Because he worked overtime at night, they set the time for ten o'clock.","In this era, mobile phones were not common, and there were few of them. It wasn't that they didn't exist, but they were like antiques, expensive, and a brick phone was completely useless.","They couldn't make video calls or chat all the time.","Si Nian had never felt the days were so hard to endure.","But she told herself that for her university diploma, all this was worth it.","As soon as it passed ten o'clock, Si Nian immediately got up and walked over to the phone.","Her eyes stared blankly.","She felt she looked like a hungry wolf.","If Zhou Yueshen were here, he would have been eaten by her.","One minute, two minutes, three minutes, there was still no movement on the other end.","Si Nian went from initial confusion to calmness, and then pressed her brows.","Maybe he was busy. After all, sometimes he had to socialize. She felt a bit disappointed and went back to her room.","Just as she lay down, the phone rang.","She jolted and ran downstairs.","She answered the phone.","A man's deep voice came from the other end.","\"Hello? Nian Nian.\"","Si Nian's eyes reddened, and she instantly felt extremely wronged. \"Why are you calling so late? I was about to go to sleep.\"","\"Sorry, I just got back. I originally thought about not disturbing your rest, but I was worried you were waiting.\"","\"Who's waiting? I was already asleep, okay?\" Si Nian said stubbornly.","The man remained silent for a while. \"Can I come pick you up in a few days?\"","Si Nian blinked. \"Come if you want to.\"","\"Do you want me to come?\""]},{"number":499,"title":"Chapter 499: Tonight Only Them","paragraphs":["Her heart skipped a beat. \"If I didn't want you to, would you just not come?\"","She was going to be mad! If this older man dared to say he wasn't coming, she would be furious!","Zhou Yueshen chuckled softly. \"No, I have to come.\"","Si Nian was both annoyed and exasperated. \"You're still laughing. I'm mad.\"","\"Niannian, I miss you so much.\"","Si Nian paused, suddenly at a loss for words.","After a long while, with red eyes and a crying tone, she finally said, \"I miss you too. I want you to come right now.\"","There was a long silence on the other end of the line.","\"Wait for me.\"","Zhou Yueshen arrived the very next afternoon.","When Si Nian walked out of the school and saw her man standing at the gates, she was stunned, thinking her eyes were playing tricks on her.","After all, transportation wasn't very advanced nowadays. Taking the train took ages, and plane tickets were hard to buy and required advance booking. So how did he get here?","She stood in a daze for quite a while, even reaching up to rub her eyes to see if she was mistaken.","Naturally, Zhou Yueshen spotted her too. Seeing her reaction, he didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","Did this silly girl think she was hallucinating?","He called out, \"Niannian, come here.\"","Si Nian finally snapped out of it.","Her eyes widened, and she rushed over to him. \"How did you get here?\"","\"You wanted me to, so I came.\" Zhou Yueshen reached out to pull her into his arms, gently patting her head.","Si Nian's eyes instantly welled up. \"Did you drive here last night?\"","Although driving was slightly faster than the train, it still took almost a whole day and night.","When he said to wait for him last night, Si Nian thought he meant in a few days.","She never expected that he would set off the very same night.","To arrive so quickly, he must have started driving right after they hung up.","\"Mhm.\" He just hummed, a casual, indifferent hum.","As if there was nothing extraordinary about it at all.","Si Nian, however, was both touched and angry. \"Why were you so impulsive? It's so dangerous to drive alone!\"","\"It's not dangerous.\"","Back in his army days, he frequently drove through the night. He had driven for days and nights on end, so this was nothing to him.","Si Nian sighed, feeling her heart swell to the brim. She knew it was filled with joy and excitement.","Seeing his travel-worn appearance, she couldn't bear to blame him anymore. If she hadn't cried and told him how much she missed him last night, he wouldn't have been so impulsive.","When they got home, Zhou Yueshen parked his car at the door, and Si Nian told him to go take a shower.","Then, she went to the kitchen to cook him some noodles.","Having a man in the house brought so much more life to it. Looking at the dusty car parked outside, Si Nian felt both moved and amused.","Her waist tightened as the man's hands wrapped around her from behind, his chin resting on top of her head.","Si Nian set the noodles aside and turned around. \"Eat your noodles first.\"","Zhou Yueshen lowered his head and kissed her delicate face. \"I don't want to eat noodles right now.\"","Si Nian blinked. She naturally understood what he meant, but she played dumb. \"Then what do you want to eat?\"","\"Will you give me whatever I want to eat?\"","\"Mhm, whatever you want.\"","Zhou Yueshen's dark eyes deepened as he lowered his head and captured her lips.","Zhou Yueshen stayed for two days. By then, Si Nian had finally finished her work. She carried her packed belongings, which weren't much—mostly books she had accumulated over her years at the school. She couldn't bear to throw them away and planned to bring them back for Eldest Child to read.","Getting into the car, Si Nian prepared to leave, feeling a bit sentimental. Her years in Beijing felt like a dream.","She looked at Zhou Yueshen's car and asked, \"What about our car? Are we leaving it here?\"","Zhou Yueshen replied, \"I'll hire someone to drive it back.\"","Si Nian immediately brightened up.","This car was the Chevrolet Zhou Yueshen had given her, the second vehicle she had ever owned in her life.","The first one was a bicycle.","There was no way she could just leave it here.","Cars were incredibly expensive in this day and age.","But truth be told, Si Nian had hardly ever driven it herself.","After all, she had a driver now, so why would she need to drive?","Her eyes darted playfully. Under Zhou Yueshen's confused gaze, she got into the back seat.","Zhou Yueshen began to wonder if he had done something to make her angry.","Instead, Si Nian quipped, \"Bosses always sit in the back. Master Zhou, please drive.\"","Zhou Yueshen paused for a second before letting out a helpless, amused laugh. \"Alright, Boss Si.\"","Si Nian was happy, but then a wave of melancholy hit her. \"We're really leaving.\"","Looking at the bustling traffic outside, a subtle feeling welled up in Zhou Yueshen's heart too.","Back then, he had unhesitatingly left everything behind, bringing his whole family and Si Nian to Beijing to build a life.","Looking back now, even he was a little surprised.","It turned out there really was someone he couldn't let go of, even for a moment.","\"We can come back whenever you want. We have a house here, so it's convenient,\" Zhou Yueshen comforted her.","Si Nian thought about it and realized he was right. Getting excited, she leaned forward against the front seat and said, \"Right now we have trains and planes. Even though it's not very convenient, I believe that one day, there will definitely be faster and easier ways to travel. We won't have to buy plane tickets weeks in advance. We'll be able to leave whenever we want and arrive in just a few hours. Don't you think so?\"","Zhou Yueshen listened quietly. Imagining such a scenario in his mind, he nodded in agreement. \"There will be.\"","They still had children at home. Although Eldest Child and Second Child had grown quite a bit, parents could never completely stop worrying.","However, they hadn't managed to get train tickets for that day, only for early the next morning. So, Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen simply found a hotel near the train station to rest for the night.","Beijing was as muggy and crowded as ever, especially around the train station. Whenever there was a holiday, it was a sea of people.","Since they had money now, they naturally stayed in a more expensive hotel that looked relatively clean.","But the only amenity was a fan.","Si Nian turned on the fan and pointed it right at her face. Zhou Yueshen walked out after taking a shower. Seeing this, he stepped forward, moved the fan a bit further away, and said, \"Don't blow it directly at your head, it'll give you a headache.\"","Si Nian watched him fresh out of the shower, shirtless and wearing only a pair of boxer shorts.","She smiled.","This man was getting more and more uninhibited. In the past, he always kept himself tightly covered up.","At most, he would wear a tank top.","She reached out to touch his pectoral muscles. They were cool to the touch from the shower, and with the breeze from the fan, it felt incredibly comfortable.","\"I wonder if Little Four has been crying for his mom.\"","She let out a comfortable sigh, thinking about how Little Four was probably throwing a tantrum since she wasn't home.","After saying that, she turned to blame Zhou Yueshen. \"Are you mean to him?\"","Because Little Four spent all day with his dad, yet she never heard him say he missed his dad.","Zhou Yueshen reached out and pinned down her wandering hand.","\"What do you consider mean?\"","Although sometimes he did bring Little Four along to social engagements. In the past, there were always women trying to approach him, but ever since Little Four started tagging along, the little guy had acted as quite the shield.","Because he was often busy late into the night, the little guy would just tilt his head and fall asleep on the sofa or a chair.","Suddenly, he felt a bit guilty.","Seeing Si Nian's suspicious gaze, he coughed softly. \"Of course not.\"","With that, not giving Si Nian a chance to respond, he pulled her into his arms, lowered his head to kiss her, and his hands grew increasingly bold.","Vaguely, Si Nian thought she heard him whisper something in the heat of passion. She couldn't hear it clearly and wanted to ask, but the man gave her no chance.","Tonight, once again, it was just the two of them..."]},{"number":500,"title":"Chapter 500: Chapter 497: Fu Yang's Farewell","paragraphs":["The incident involving the Si family caused a massive uproar in the military compound.","Si's Father was already nearing retirement, and with such a scandal breaking out, he naturally ended up in a miserable state.","In truth, he could no longer stay there anyway. Not only was it a total humiliation, but he also had to endure people pointing fingers at him behind his back every single day.","Si's Father sat in his house, which was a complete mess.","No one was there to clean it up.","After his matchmaking affair blew up, the other party completely cut ties with him.","It also offended Liu Chunni. Coupled with the gossip from the people in the military compound, the heartless woman feared she would be dragged down with him. So, while he was overwhelmed with trouble, she secretly ran away with the child.","In the end, Si's Father was left completely alone. Overnight, his hair turned white, making him look as if he had aged more than a decade.","He couldn't figure it out. How did an originally happy family end up like this?","Perhaps everything started when they swapped Si Nian away.","Maybe it was the sins they committed for their biological daughter, scheming against the child they had raised for over a decade, that brought upon them continuous retribution ever since.","He schemed against her while also feeling indignant, thinking that since he had painstakingly raised her for over a dozen years, why would she disregard him just because of this little matter?","His initial guilt had turned into resentment.","But after losing everything, Si's Father was utterly bewildered.","It seemed he finally realized that everything was his own fault.","He complained that Si Nian didn't respect him after she left, but thinking back, she was quite polite to their family at the beginning. She respectfully called him dad and occasionally made his heart ache for her.","But what did he do later? He increasingly disregarded his own dignity, making more and more excessive demands, constantly oppressing her for Sisi's sake.","In the end, the look in Si Nian's eyes when she looked at him grew colder and colder, right up until the time he hired someone to hurt her parents.","He hadn't even realized his mistake then, shamelessly going to her door to demand that Si Nian and Zhou Yueshen arrange a job for him.","Ultimately, it led to this miserable end.","He thought Si Nian was too ruthless, but looking back at himself, was he any better?","Overjoyed upon hearing about the existence of a son and thinking he finally had an heir, he could no longer tolerate his wife and daughter, growing endlessly tired of them.","He even personally sent them to prison.","When it came to cruelty, who could compare to him?","At this moment, Si's Father finally remembered Zhang Cuimei's goodness.","Back when the family was plagued by frequent troubles, even when his scandalous affair with Liu Chunni was exposed, Zhang Cuimei never left him.","Yet he made mistakes without realizing them, erring again and again.","When things finally fell apart, his wife was still trying to protect him and their daughter.","But he became the final straw that broke the camel's back.","That night, Si's Father thought about many, many things.","He didn't go looking for Liu Chunni again. He knew very well what she valued in him, but now he had absolutely nothing.","Si's Father left the family compound, and no one ever saw him again.","When Si Nian heard the news, she couldn't quite describe how she felt.","Thinking back, at the very beginning, Si's Father did feel indebted to her. Although he was selfish, without Lin Sisi's manipulation, he wouldn't have gone to such extremes.","The beginning of it all was because of those two, Lin Sisi and Liu Dongdong.","Since leaving their company, Liu Dongdong had disappeared.","Si Nian didn't know where she went either, and there was no news of her returning home.","She was probably afraid of the humiliation if she went back.","However, with a degree, she should be able to find a good job in the future.","That is, if she could just behave herself.","Si Nian no longer wanted to think about the affairs of these outsiders.","As long as they didn't offend her, she didn't care what they did.","Fu Qianqian and Yu Dong's relationship was developing rapidly. She claimed it was because her brother was leaving, and she at least wanted to let him know that he was the only single dog left.","She heard that Fu Yang was going to settle in the Northwest, which meant he would rarely come back in the future.","But no matter what, he was still her brother. Fu Qianqian was very reluctant to see him go and didn't want him to be alone for the rest of his life.","So she advised him, Brother, I won't be picky anymore. Whether it's Lin Sisi or Liu Dongdong, if you really like them, you can marry whoever you want. I just hope you won't always be alone in the future; it's quite pitiful.","Her way of comforting people was always so ambiguous that it made people want to beat her up.","If Fu Qianqian were a younger brother, she probably would have been beaten by Fu Yang from childhood to adulthood.","But she just had to be a girl. Even as Fu Yang's face darkened, seeing her red-rimmed eyes made him soft-hearted.","What Liu Dongdong, Lin Sisi? They have nothing to do with me. Stop talking nonsense.","Tch, you're still pretending. I heard that you and Liu Dongdong had a little indescribable encounter before, and it was because of this incident that Lin Sisi drove Liu Dongdong away back then.","The love triangle between Lin Sisi, Liu Dongdong, and her brother had become a must-discuss gossip topic after meals in their compound.","Some people said that the current situation of Si's Father's family was all Liu Dongdong's revenge.","Fu Yang's face darkened. He didn't know what behavior of his had caused such a misunderstanding. He hadn't even seen Liu Dongdong a few times; how could he possibly like her.","If he fell for someone that easily, back then he wouldn't have...","Fu Yang clenched his fists.","You're overthinking it. I have absolutely nothing to do with her. To be honest, he couldn't even remember what Liu Dongdong looked like anymore. He only vaguely recalled that her hairstyle and clothing were somewhat similar to Si Nian's, but he couldn't remember her face at all.","That's good. I was terrified that, just like the Si family, some woman would suddenly bring a child back and claim it's yours.","Fu Yang's mouth twitched again, and he growled a warning, Fu Qianqian, what kind of person do you take me for?","Fu Qianqian didn't dare say more.","She knew that her brother probably wasn't that kind of person.","To be honest, with Liu Dongdong's deep schemes, she was even worse than Lin Sisi.","Sure enough, one shouldn't be too picky, or the choices just get worse.","She shivered. Anyway, as long as it had nothing to do with her brother, she felt relieved.","Fu Yang left.","What does his leaving have to do with me?","Si Nian looked at Fu Qianqian in confusion.","Fu Qianqian was just feeling sentimental, but upon hearing this, she suddenly felt bored. Makes sense.","Even though so much time had passed, she always felt that Si Nian should still have a tiny spot in her heart for her brother, or at least feel a bit sentimental.","What a pity, she underestimated Si Nian.","In fact, if there was even the slightest bit of lingering affection, she felt her brother wouldn't be so miserable.","But thinking about it, Si Nian was living a comfortable life now; why would she dwell on the past?","Wasn't bringing him up just needlessly causing her displeasure?","What a sin, what a sin.","She then asked Si Nian what date would be best if she and Yu Dong were to get married.","Si Nian was utterly exasperated and said, Shouldn't you ask your family elders about this? If I suggest something, I'm afraid they might take issue with it.","Not to mention, she didn't even know how to pick an auspicious date.","Fu Qianqian held her face and giggled foolishly, That's true.","Looking at her sweet expression, Si Nian thought to herself that love really could make a person foolish.","She used to be such a rational person, entirely focused on her career, but look at her now—she couldn't go ten sentences without mentioning Yu Dong.","When she married Zhou Yueshen back then, she didn't seem to have such an exaggerated reaction."]}]);
